hemo:5000026 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000012 ;
    rdfs:label "Absolute risk estimation function"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-FN-AR-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6000058,
        hemo:6000059,
        hemo:6000060 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6000058,
        hemo:6000059 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6000060 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Maps the number of people who have a new event during a stated period, and the number at risk at the start of that period, to the probability of the event over the period. The result is a risk, tied to the length of the period, not a rate per unit of time. Moving a risk to a different period, such as a model cycle, goes through a rate and is covered on the Transition Probability page." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absolute risk estimation function" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r(E,N) = R" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-FN-AR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absolute-risk-estimation-function" .

hemo:5000030 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000012 ;
    rdfs:label "15D index score function"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-FN-15D-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 false ;
    hemo:9000008 "Maps a respondent's levels on the 15 dimensions of the 15D, each with 5 ordinal levels, to a single index on a 0 to 1 scale, where 0 is being dead and 1 is no problems on any dimension. The index is a preference-based utility that can weight survival in QALY calculations." ;
    hemo:9000009 "15D index score function" ;
    hemo:9000014 "s(x_1,...,x_15) = v_H" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-FN-15D-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "15d-index-score-function" .

hemo:5000082 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000012 ;
    rdfs:label "Cohort simulation of a state-transition model"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-FN-CSIM-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 false ;
    hemo:9000008 "Maps a starting distribution of the cohort across health states, the transition matrix for each cycle, the reward per cycle in each state, the discount factors and a within-cycle counting rule to the expected total cost, life years or QALYs per person. The cycle-by-cycle trace m_(t+1) = m_t P_t is the cohort state update of the Markov Model page, which gives it in its time-homogeneous form s_(t+1) = s_t P (HE-FM-MM-001); here P_t may vary from cycle to cycle, and the update is not restated. Because each state is homogeneous, the proportion in a state equals the probability that one member of the cohort is in it, so the accumulated rewards are expected values per person. Two existing formulae check a run: the area under an exponential survival curve over one interval (HE-FM-BTH-001) gives a continuous-time benchmark for counting rules, and the fundamental matrix (HE-FM-ABS-001) gives the totals of a run to absorption counted at the start of each cycle." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cohort simulation of a state-transition model" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m_(t+1) = m_t P_t; Y = sum_(t=0)^T w_t delta_t m_t r" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-FN-CSIM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cohort-simulation-of-a-state-transition-model" .

hemo:5000119 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000012 ;
    rdfs:label "Matrix root of an annual transition matrix for a shorter model cycle"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-FN-TMAT-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 false ;
    hemo:9000008 "Converts a transition matrix estimated over one interval into the matrix for a cycle n times shorter by taking the n-th root of the whole matrix, so that n short cycles reproduce the original matrix, including movements through intermediate states within the interval. Cohort propagation with a matrix is HE-FM-MM-001, the matrix exponential of a rate matrix HE-CF-CONT-001, competing exits HE-FM-TP-004 and cell-by-cell rescaling of a single probability HE-FM-TP-003. Notation follows the Transition Matrix article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Matrix root of an annual transition matrix for a shorter model cycle" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P^(1/n) = V * D^(1/n) * V^(-1); (P^(1/n))^n = P" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-FN-TMAT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "matrix-root-of-an-annual-transition-matrix-for-a-shorter-model-cycle" .

hemo:5000127 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000012 ;
    rdfs:label "Incremental utility-cost function as the inverse of an incremental cost-utility ratio"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-FN-ICUR-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6000207,
        hemo:6000208,
        hemo:6000209 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6000207,
        hemo:6000208 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6000209 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Maps the incremental QALYs and the incremental cost of an intervention against one comparator to the QALYs gained per one million units of net expenditure, the form New Zealand's PHARMAC prefers to the cost per QALY. The incremental cost-utility ratio itself, ICUR = Delta_C / Delta_QALY, is HE-FM-CUA-001 and the general two-option ratio is HE-FM-ICER-001. Checks against a threshold use the incremental net monetary benefit HE-FM-NMB-002 or the incremental net health benefit HE-FM-CET-002. Notation follows the Incremental Cost-Utility Ratio article, which writes the QALY difference as Delta_Q." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Incremental utility-cost function as the inverse of an incremental cost-utility ratio" ;
    hemo:9000014 "g(Delta_Q,Delta_C) = IUCR" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-FN-ICUR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "incremental-utility-cost-function-as-the-inverse-of-an-incremental-cost-utility-ratio" .

hemo:5000128 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000012 ;
    rdfs:label "Per-trial risk ratio input function for a pairwise meta-analysis of head-to-head trials"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-FN-PWMA-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6000210,
        hemo:6000211,
        hemo:6000212,
        hemo:6000213,
        hemo:6000214,
        hemo:6000215,
        hemo:6000216 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6000210,
        hemo:6000211,
        hemo:6000212,
        hemo:6000213 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6000214,
        hemo:6000215,
        hemo:6000216 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Maps the event counts and arm sizes of one head-to-head trial of drug A against drug B to the risk ratio, its natural log and the variance of that log, the per-trial inputs that an inverse-variance pairwise meta-analysis of a dichotomous outcome pools. The pooling steps are existing records: the fixed-effect estimate HE-FM-ADMA-001, Cochran's Q HE-FM-ADMA-002, I-squared HE-FM-ADMA-003, the DerSimonian and Laird between-study variance HE-FM-ADMA-004 and the random-effects mean HE-FM-ADMA-005, all run in one pass by HE-CF-ADMA-001 with each trial's standard error taken as the square root of v. Applying the pooled risk ratio to a baseline risk from another source in an economic model is HE-FM-ARR-002. Notation follows the Pairwise Meta-Analysis article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Per-trial risk ratio input function for a pairwise meta-analysis of head-to-head trials" ;
    hemo:9000014 "g(a, n1, c, n2) = (RR, y, v)" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-FN-PWMA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "per-trial-risk-ratio-input-function-for-a-pairwise-meta-analysis-of-head-to-head-trials" .

hemo:5000152 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000012 ;
    rdfs:label "Interim value of information function for the stop or continue decision in an ongoing trial"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-FN-AVOI-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
