hemo:7000134 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Rates follow the governing reference case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The selected cost and outcome rates, whether equal or different, come from the applicable current institutional guidance." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rates follow the governing reference case" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rates-follow-the-governing-reference-case" .

hemo:7000135 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Comparable timing"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Cost and outcome streams use explicit timing conventions applied consistently across the alternatives being compared." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Comparable timing" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "comparable-timing" .

hemo:7000136 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Discount costs and outcomes separately"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000191 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Use separate named rate cells so the model remains valid when cost and outcome rates differ." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discount costs and outcomes separately" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discount-costs-and-outcomes-separately" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Cost/(1+CostRate)^Year; =Outcome/(1+OutcomeRate)^Year" .

hemo:7000137 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal-rate equivalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Set the cost and outcome rates equal. Expected result: equal timing receives the same discount factor in both streams." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal-rate equivalence" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-rate-equivalence" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1/(1+CostRate)^Year=1/(1+OutcomeRate)^Year" .

hemo:7000138 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Rate-source check"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Compare both base-case rates with the named current guidance. Expected result: exact agreement or a documented justified exception." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rate-source check" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rate-source-check" .

hemo:7000139 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Differential discounting in year 10"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A £10,000 cost and 1 QALY in year 10 have present values of £7,440.94 and 0.8617 QALYs when costs are discounted at an illustrative 3% and outcomes at 1.5%." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Differential discounting in year 10" ;
    hemo:9000014 "T = 10; t = 10; C_t = 10000; E_t = 1; r_C = 0.03; r_E = 0.015; PV_C = 7440.94; PV_E = 0.8617" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "differential-discounting-in-year-10" .

hemo:7000140 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One comparator and two mutually exclusive options"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The formula compares the evaluated intervention with one clearly identified comparator. When three or more mutually exclusive options are relevant, dominated options are removed and sequential ICERs are calculated between adjacent options on the frontier, as set out on the cost-effectiveness analysis page." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One comparator and two mutually exclusive options" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ICER-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-comparator-and-two-mutually-exclusive-options" .

hemo:7000141 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Consistent analytical basis for the ICER"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Costs and effects of both options refer to the same population, perspective, time horizon, price year and discounting approach, and the numerator and denominator both take the intervention minus the comparator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Consistent analytical basis for the ICER" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ICER-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "consistent-analytical-basis-for-the-icer" .

hemo:7000142 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Ratio of expected values"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The ratio is formed from expected incremental cost and expected incremental effect, as NICE requires, and not by averaging ratios calculated for individual simulations or patients." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ratio of expected values" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ICER-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ratio-of-expected-values" .

hemo:7000143 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive incremental effect for threshold comparison"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The ICER is compared with a threshold in the usual direction, as cost per unit of effect gained, only when E_1 minus E_0 is greater than zero. When the difference is negative the ratio is the saving per unit of effect forgone and the threshold comparison reverses, and when it equals zero no ratio is calculated." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive incremental effect for threshold comparison" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ICER-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-incremental-effect-for-threshold-comparison" .

hemo:7000144 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Quadrant identified before interpretation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The signs of incremental cost and incremental effect are examined before the ratio is read. An intervention that is less costly and more effective dominates, one that is more costly and less effective is dominated, and in neither case is the ratio compared with a threshold." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Quadrant identified before interpretation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ICER-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "quadrant-identified-before-interpretation" .

hemo:7000145 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Calculate a pairwise ICER"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000192 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel divides incremental cost by incremental effect using named ranges and returns #N/A when the two expected effects are equal. The sign of the effect difference is checked separately before the result is interpreted." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Calculate a pairwise ICER" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ICER-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "calculate-a-pairwise-icer" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(InterventionEffect<>ComparatorEffect,(InterventionCost-ComparatorCost)/(InterventionEffect-ComparatorEffect),NA())" .

hemo:7000146 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Label the cost-effectiveness-plane position"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000192 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel labels the position of the comparison from incremental cost and incremental effect before the ratio is read. Results with one difference equal to zero are classified as dominance, consistent with the inclusive dominance rule." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Label the cost-effectiveness-plane position" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ICER-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "label-the-cost-effectiveness-plane-position" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(AND(IncrementalCost=0,IncrementalEffect=0),\"No difference\",IF(AND(IncrementalCost>0,IncrementalEffect>0),\"North-east: compare ICER with threshold\",IF(AND(IncrementalCost<0,IncrementalEffect<0),\"South-west: saving per unit of effect forgone\",IF(AND(IncrementalCost<=0,IncrementalEffect>=0),\"Intervention dominates\",\"Intervention is dominated\"))))" .

hemo:7000147 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Incremental effect sign check"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Test whether the intervention produces more expected health effect than the comparator. Expected result: TRUE, so the ICER reads as cost per unit of effect gained. FALSE means the ratio is either a saving per unit forgone or undefined." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Incremental effect sign check" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ICER-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "incremental-effect-sign-check" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=InterventionEffect-ComparatorEffect>0" .

hemo:7000148 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "ICER reconciliation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Multiply the ICER by the incremental effect and compare the product with the incremental cost. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE reveals a formula that subtracts in inconsistent directions or reads the wrong cells." ;
    hemo:9000009 "ICER reconciliation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ICER-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "icer-reconciliation" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ICER*(InterventionEffect-ComparatorEffect)-(InterventionCost-ComparatorCost))<0.01" .

hemo:7000149 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement with incremental net monetary benefit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a positive incremental effect, test whether an ICER at or below the threshold coincides with non-negative incremental net monetary benefit. Expected result: TRUE. With a negative incremental effect the result is FALSE, which shows the south-west reversal of the threshold rule." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Agreement with incremental net monetary benefit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ICER-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "agreement-with-incremental-net-monetary-benefit" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(ICER<=Threshold)=(Threshold*(InterventionEffect-ComparatorEffect)-(InterventionCost-ComparatorCost)>=0)" .

hemo:7000150 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "North-east quadrant, cost per QALY gained"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000151,
        hemo:7000152,
        hemo:7000153,
        hemo:7000154 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000155 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A new medicine costs £18,000 per patient and produces 4.5 QALYs, while current care costs £12,000 and produces 4.2 QALYs. Incremental cost is £6,000 and incremental effect is 0.3 QALYs, so the ICER is £20,000 per QALY gained. Because the incremental effect is positive the ratio can be compared with a threshold, and it lies below the lower end of the NICE range of £25,000 to £35,000 per QALY gained. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "North-east quadrant: cost per QALY gained" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_1 = 18000; C_0 = 12000; E_1 = 4.5; E_0 = 4.2; ICER = 20000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ICER-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "north-east-quadrant-cost-per-qaly-gained" .

hemo:7000151 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "C_1 in the test North-east quadrant, cost per QALY gained"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000559 ;
    rheo:2000001 18000.0 .

hemo:7000152 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "C_0 in the test North-east quadrant, cost per QALY gained"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000560 ;
    rheo:2000001 12000.0 .

hemo:7000153 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "E_1 in the test North-east quadrant, cost per QALY gained"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000561 ;
    rheo:2000001 4.5 .

hemo:7000154 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "E_0 in the test North-east quadrant, cost per QALY gained"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000562 ;
    rheo:2000001 4.2 .

hemo:7000155 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "ICER in the test North-east quadrant, cost per QALY gained"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000563 ;
    rheo:2000001 20000.0 .

hemo:7000156 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "South-west quadrant, saving per QALY forgone"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000157,
        hemo:7000158,
        hemo:7000159,
        hemo:7000160 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000161 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A cheaper option costs £9,000 and produces 4.0 QALYs, against current care at £12,000 and 4.2 QALYs. Incremental cost is minus £3,000 and incremental effect is minus 0.2 QALYs, so the ratio is £15,000. Because the incremental effect is negative, the ratio is the saving per QALY forgone. At any threshold from £25,000 to £35,000 per QALY the saving is too small to justify the health lost, so a ratio below the threshold counts against the cheaper option. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "South-west quadrant: saving per QALY forgone" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_1 = 9000; C_0 = 12000; E_1 = 4.0; E_0 = 4.2; ICER = 15000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ICER-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "south-west-quadrant-saving-per-qaly-forgone" .

hemo:7000157 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "C_1 in the test South-west quadrant, saving per QALY forgone"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000559 ;
    rheo:2000001 9000.0 .

hemo:7000158 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "C_0 in the test South-west quadrant, saving per QALY forgone"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000560 ;
    rheo:2000001 12000.0 .

hemo:7000159 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "E_1 in the test South-west quadrant, saving per QALY forgone"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000561 ;
    rheo:2000001 4.0 .

hemo:7000160 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "E_0 in the test South-west quadrant, saving per QALY forgone"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000562 ;
    rheo:2000001 4.2 .

hemo:7000161 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "ICER in the test South-west quadrant, saving per QALY forgone"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000563 ;
    rheo:2000001 15000.0 .

hemo:7000162 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Utility constant within each period"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each period carries one utility value. Health that changes within a period needs shorter periods or the area-under-the-curve form with interpolation between observations." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Utility constant within each period" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-QALY-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "utility-constant-within-each-period" .

hemo:7000163 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Common anchors and one value set"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every utility value uses the same instrument and value set, anchored at 1 for full health and 0 for dead, across all periods and all options compared. NICE notes that different methods and instruments produce different utility values that cannot always be compared." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Common anchors and one value set" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-QALY-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "common-anchors-and-one-value-set" .

hemo:7000164 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Durations in years ending at death"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Durations are expressed in years, so months and days are converted, and they cover only time alive. No period after death contributes to the total." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Durations in years ending at death" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-QALY-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "durations-in-years-ending-at-death" .

hemo:7000165 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Preference conditions of the QALY model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Multiplying utility by time relies on conditions on preferences; NICE gives constant proportional trade-off and additive independence between health states as examples and expects evidence to be produced if they are inappropriate in a particular case." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Preference conditions of the QALY model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-QALY-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "preference-conditions-of-the-qaly-model" .

hemo:7000166 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounting applied after the calculation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The formula gives undiscounted QALYs. Where guidance requires discounting, each period's QALYs are discounted to the reference time with the present-value formula on the discount-rate page, at 3.5% a year in the NICE reference case, with a stated timing convention." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounting applied after the calculation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-QALY-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounting-applied-after-the-calculation" .

hemo:7000167 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Sum utility-weighted durations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000193 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel multiplies each period's utility by its duration in years and adds the products. Durations recorded in months are divided by 12 first." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sum utility-weighted durations" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-QALY-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sum-utility-weighted-durations" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(Utilities,DurationsYears)" .

hemo:7000168 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Utility range check"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Confirm that no utility exceeds 1 and none falls below the lowest value in the value set used. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Utility range check" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-QALY-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "utility-range-check" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(MAX(Utilities)<=1,MIN(Utilities)>=ValueSetMinimum)" .

hemo:7000169 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Duration reconciliation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Compare the sum of the period durations with the time alive within the horizon, in years. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE points to unconverted months or days, gaps or overlaps between periods, or periods after death." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Duration reconciliation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-QALY-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "duration-reconciliation" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUM(DurationsYears)-YearsAlive)<0.0001" .

hemo:7000170 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two six-month periods"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000171,
        hemo:7000172,
        hemo:7000173 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000174 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A person spends six months at utility 0.60 and six months at utility 0.80. Each period is 0.5 years, so the periods contribute 0.30 and 0.40 QALYs, giving 0.70 QALYs over the year. The result is 0.70 quality-adjusted life years, not 0.70 calendar years." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two six-month periods" ;
    hemo:9000014 "T = 2; u_t = [0.60,0.80]; d_t = [0.5,0.5]; QALY = 0.70" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-QALY-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-six-month-periods" .

hemo:7000171 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "T in the test Two six-month periods"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000566 ;
    rheo:2000001 2.0 .

hemo:7000172 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "u_t in the test Two six-month periods"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000564 ;
    hemo:9000014 "[0.6, 0.8]" .

hemo:7000173 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "d_t in the test Two six-month periods"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000565 ;
    hemo:9000014 "[0.5, 0.5]" .

hemo:7000174 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "QALY in the test Two six-month periods"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000567 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.7 .

hemo:7000175 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "A period in a state worse than dead"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000176,
        hemo:7000177,
        hemo:7000178 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000179 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.0005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A person spends one year at utility 0.70, three months (0.25 years) in a state valued at minus 0.20 under the value set used, and nine months (0.75 years) at utility 0.50. The contributions are 0.70, minus 0.05 and 0.375 QALYs, giving 1.025 QALYs. The negative value is retained and lowers the total. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "A period in a state worse than dead" ;
    hemo:9000014 "T = 3; u_t = [0.70,-0.20,0.50]; d_t = [1,0.25,0.75]; QALY = 1.025" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-QALY-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "a-period-in-a-state-worse-than-dead" .

hemo:7000176 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "T in the test A period in a state worse than dead"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000566 ;
    rheo:2000001 3.0 .

hemo:7000177 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "u_t in the test A period in a state worse than dead"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000564 ;
    hemo:9000014 "[0.7, -0.2, 0.5]" .

hemo:7000178 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "d_t in the test A period in a state worse than dead"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000565 ;
    hemo:9000014 "[1.0, 0.25, 0.75]" .

hemo:7000179 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "QALY in the test A period in a state worse than dead"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000567 ;
    rheo:2000001 1.025 .

hemo:7000180 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Linear change between observations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Utility moves in a straight line between consecutive measurements. Other interpolation rules can give different totals, so the rule is stated and tested in sensitivity analysis." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Linear change between observations" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-QALY-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "linear-change-between-observations" .

hemo:7000181 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Contiguous intervals"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The end observation of each interval is the start observation of the next, and together the intervals cover the follow-up period without gaps or overlaps." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Contiguous intervals" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-QALY-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "contiguous-intervals" .

hemo:7000182 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Baseline utility controlled in trial comparisons"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Baseline utility contributes to the area and is often imbalanced between trial arms, so incremental QALYs are estimated with adjustment for baseline utility, for example by regression." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Baseline utility controlled in trial comparisons" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-QALY-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "baseline-utility-controlled-in-trial-comparisons" .

hemo:7000183 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Trapezoidal QALYs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000194 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel averages the start and end utility of each interval, multiplies by the interval length in years and adds the products." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Trapezoidal QALYs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-QALY-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "trapezoidal-qalys" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT((StartUtilities+EndUtilities)/2,IntervalYears)" .

hemo:7000184 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuity check"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With start utilities in column B and end utilities in column C from row 2, compare each interval's start utility with the end utility of the interval before it by filling the formula down from row 3. Expected result: TRUE on every row." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuity check" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-QALY-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuity-check" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=B3=C2" .

hemo:7000185 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Area bounds check"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Confirm that the area lies between the lowest and highest observed utility multiplied by the total follow-up in years. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Area bounds check" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-QALY-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "area-bounds-check" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(QALYAUC>=MIN(StartUtilities,EndUtilities)*SUM(IntervalYears),QALYAUC<=MAX(StartUtilities,EndUtilities)*SUM(IntervalYears))" .

hemo:7000186 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three observations over one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000187,
        hemo:7000188,
        hemo:7000189,
        hemo:7000190 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000191 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.0005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Utility is 0.50 at baseline, 0.70 at six months and 0.80 at twelve months. The first interval contributes the mean of 0.50 and 0.70 multiplied by 0.5 years, which is 0.30 QALYs, and the second contributes the mean of 0.70 and 0.80 multiplied by 0.5 years, which is 0.375 QALYs. The total is 0.675 QALYs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three observations over one year" ;
    hemo:9000014 "T = 2; u_start_t = [0.50,0.70]; u_end_t = [0.70,0.80]; d_t = [0.5,0.5]; QALY_AUC = 0.675" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-QALY-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-observations-over-one-year" .

hemo:7000187 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "T in the test Three observations over one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000571 ;
    rheo:2000001 2.0 .

hemo:7000188 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "u_start_t in the test Three observations over one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000568 ;
    hemo:9000014 "[0.5, 0.7]" .

hemo:7000189 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "u_end_t in the test Three observations over one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000569 ;
    hemo:9000014 "[0.7, 0.8]" .

hemo:7000190 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "d_t in the test Three observations over one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000570 ;
    hemo:9000014 "[0.5, 0.5]" .

hemo:7000191 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "QALY_AUC in the test Three observations over one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000572 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.675 .

hemo:7000192 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Stated threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The value of lambda is stated with its currency, price year, outcome unit and source, because NMB and the ranking of options depend on it. The NICE manual asks for net health benefits at £25,000 and £35,000 per QALY and allows net monetary benefits to be shown alongside." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Stated threshold" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMB-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "stated-threshold" .

hemo:7000193 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Common analytical basis for every option"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every option's NMB uses the same population, perspective, time horizon, price basis and discounting, and uses the option's own expected totals rather than values incremental to another option." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Common analytical basis for every option" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMB-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "common-analytical-basis-for-every-option" .

hemo:7000194 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Calculate option-level NMB"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000195 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel values expected health at the threshold and subtracts expected cost. The threshold sits in one named cell so that results can be recalculated at other values." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Calculate option-level NMB" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-NMB-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "calculate-option-level-nmb" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Threshold*ExpectedEffect-ExpectedCost" .

hemo:7000195 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Recalculation at a second threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Calculate NMB at two thresholds. Expected result: TRUE, because the change in NMB equals the change in threshold multiplied by the expected effect. FALSE shows that the cost term has been scaled by the threshold or the effect omitted." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Recalculation at a second threshold" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-NMB-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "recalculation-at-a-second-threshold" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((NMBAtThreshold2-NMBAtThreshold1)-(Threshold2-Threshold1)*ExpectedEffect)<0.01" .

hemo:7000196 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "New intervention at £20,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000197,
        hemo:7000198,
        hemo:7000199 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000200 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A new intervention has an expected cost of £14,000 and 4.80 expected QALYs per patient. At an illustrative threshold of £20,000 per QALY its health is valued at £96,000, so its NMB is £82,000 per patient. Current care, at £10,000 and 4.50 QALYs, has an NMB of £80,000 at the same threshold." ;
    hemo:9000009 "New intervention at £20,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 20000; E_j = 4.80; C_j = 14000; NMB_j = 82000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-NMB-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "new-intervention-at-20-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7000197 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "lambda in the test New intervention at £20,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000573 ;
    rheo:2000001 20000.0 .

hemo:7000198 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "E_j in the test New intervention at £20,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000574 ;
    rheo:2000001 4.8 .

hemo:7000199 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "C_j in the test New intervention at £20,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000575 ;
    rheo:2000001 14000.0 .

hemo:7000200 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "NMB_j in the test New intervention at £20,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000576 ;
    rheo:2000001 82000.0 .

hemo:7000201 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Consistent subtraction direction for INMB"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Delta_E and Delta_C both take the intervention minus the comparator, so INMB equals the intervention's NMB minus the comparator's NMB." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Consistent subtraction direction for INMB" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMB-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "consistent-subtraction-direction-for-inmb" .

hemo:7000202 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Equivalence with the ICER rule"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "When Delta_E is greater than zero, INMB is positive exactly when the ICER is below lambda. When Delta_E is negative the ICER rule reverses while the INMB rule does not, and when Delta_E equals zero only INMB is defined." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equivalence with the ICER rule" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMB-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equivalence-with-the-icer-rule" .

hemo:7000203 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Calculate incremental NMB"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000196 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel values the incremental effect at the threshold and subtracts the incremental cost." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Calculate incremental NMB" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-NMB-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "calculate-incremental-nmb" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Threshold*IncrementalEffect-IncrementalCost" .

hemo:7000204 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Difference-of-NMB reconciliation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Subtract the comparator's option-level NMB from the intervention's and compare the result with INMB. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Difference-of-NMB reconciliation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-NMB-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "difference-of-nmb-reconciliation" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(INMB-(NMBIntervention-NMBComparator))<0.01" .

hemo:7000205 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement with the ICER rule"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a positive incremental effect, test whether a positive INMB coincides with an ICER below the threshold. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Agreement with the ICER rule" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-NMB-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "agreement-with-the-icer-rule" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(IncrementalEffect>0,(INMB>0)=(IncrementalCost/IncrementalEffect<Threshold),\"Not applicable\")" .

hemo:7000206 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive INMB at £20,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000207,
        hemo:7000208,
        hemo:7000209 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000210 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Incremental cost is £4,000 and incremental effect is 0.30 QALYs. At £20,000 per QALY the INMB is £2,000, the difference between the option-level NMBs of £82,000 and £80,000. The ICER of about £13,333 per QALY is below £20,000, so both rules favour the intervention. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive INMB at £20,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 20000; Delta_E = 0.30; Delta_C = 4000; INMB = 2000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-NMB-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-inmb-at-20-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7000207 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "lambda in the test Positive INMB at £20,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000577 ;
    rheo:2000001 20000.0 .

hemo:7000208 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_E in the test Positive INMB at £20,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000578 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.3 .

hemo:7000209 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_C in the test Positive INMB at £20,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000579 ;
    rheo:2000001 4000.0 .

hemo:7000210 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "INMB in the test Positive INMB at £20,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000580 ;
    rheo:2000001 2000.0 .

hemo:7000211 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Negative INMB at a lower threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000212,
        hemo:7000213,
        hemo:7000214 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000215 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At an illustrative threshold of £10,000 per QALY the same comparison gives an INMB of minus £1,000, so current care has the higher NMB. The INMB changes sign at about £13,333 per QALY, the ICER." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Negative INMB at a lower threshold" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 10000; Delta_E = 0.30; Delta_C = 4000; INMB = -1000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-NMB-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "negative-inmb-at-a-lower-threshold" .

hemo:7000212 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "lambda in the test Negative INMB at a lower threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000577 ;
    rheo:2000001 10000.0 .

hemo:7000213 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_E in the test Negative INMB at a lower threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000578 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.3 .

hemo:7000214 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_C in the test Negative INMB at a lower threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000579 ;
    rheo:2000001 4000.0 .

hemo:7000215 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "INMB in the test Negative INMB at a lower threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000580 ;
    rheo:2000001 -1000.0 .

hemo:7000216 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Complete set of mutually exclusive options"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "J contains every relevant option, and each is evaluated on the same basis. Leaving out an option can change which option has the highest NMB." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Complete set of mutually exclusive options" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMB-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "complete-set-of-mutually-exclusive-options" .

hemo:7000217 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected net benefit under uncertainty"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Under probabilistic analysis the rule uses expected NMB, the mean across simulations, and not the probability that each option has the highest NMB." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected net benefit under uncertainty" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMB-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-net-benefit-under-uncertainty" .

hemo:7000218 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Return the highest-NMB option"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000197 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel returns the option name with the highest NMB and flags a tie when more than one option shares the maximum." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Return the highest-NMB option" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-NMB-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "return-the-highest-nmb-option" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(COUNTIF(NMBValues,MAX(NMBValues))>1,\"Equal highest NMB\",INDEX(OptionNames,MATCH(MAX(NMBValues),NMBValues,0)))" .

hemo:7000219 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Maximum reconciliation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Look up the NMB of the selected option and compare it with the largest value in NMBValues. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Maximum reconciliation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-NMB-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "maximum-reconciliation" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=INDEX(NMBValues,MATCH(SelectedOption,OptionNames,0))=MAX(NMBValues)" .

hemo:7000220 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Four options at £20,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Options A to D have expected costs of £10,000, £13,000, £18,000 and £22,000 and 4.0, 4.3, 4.5 and 4.8 expected QALYs. At £20,000 per QALY their NMBs are £70,000, £73,000, £72,000 and £74,000, so option D, the fourth, is selected. Option C, which is extendedly dominated, is not selected at this or any other threshold. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Four options at £20,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "J = [1,2,3,4]; lambda = 20000; E_j = [4.0,4.3,4.5,4.8]; C_j = [10000,13000,18000,22000]; j* = 4" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-NMB-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "four-options-at-20-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7000221 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Inclusive treatment of ties"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Equal cost with greater effect, or equal effect with lower cost, counts as dominance because the tied option can be discarded with no loss at any threshold. Identical cost and effect is not dominance. The tie case is ordinary dominance and is not called weak dominance, a term some texts use for extended dominance." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Inclusive treatment of ties" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DOM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "inclusive-treatment-of-ties" .

hemo:7000222 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Consistent subtraction direction for dominance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both differences take the intervention minus the comparator. The intervention is dominated when the rule holds for the comparator, that is with the signs of both differences reversed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Consistent subtraction direction for dominance" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DOM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "consistent-subtraction-direction-for-dominance" .

hemo:7000223 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected values on a common basis"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The classification uses expected costs and effects for the same population, perspective, time horizon and outcome measure. The share of probabilistic simulations in which an option dominates describes uncertainty and is not the decision rule." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected values on a common basis" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DOM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-values-on-a-common-basis" .

hemo:7000224 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Classify a two-option comparison"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000198 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel classifies the intervention as dominant, dominated or neither from named incremental values. Rounding the incremental values first keeps the equality branches meaningful when model outputs carry tiny numerical differences." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Classify a two-option comparison" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DOM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "classify-a-two-option-comparison" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(AND(IncrementalCost<=0,IncrementalEffect>=0,OR(IncrementalCost<0,IncrementalEffect>0)),\"Dominant\",IF(AND(IncrementalCost>=0,IncrementalEffect<=0,OR(IncrementalCost>0,IncrementalEffect<0)),\"Dominated\",\"No dominance\"))" .

hemo:7000225 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Net-benefit consistency"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a comparison classified as dominant, test incremental net monetary benefit at a threshold of 0 and at a high threshold such as £100,000 per unit of effect. Expected result: TRUE. Because incremental net monetary benefit rises with the threshold when Delta_E is non-negative, it is then non-negative at every threshold; FALSE indicates a sign or subtraction error." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net-benefit consistency" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DOM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-benefit-consistency" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(0*IncrementalEffect-IncrementalCost>=0,100000*IncrementalEffect-IncrementalCost>=0)" .

hemo:7000226 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Tie-boundary check"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Enter an incremental cost of 0 with a positive incremental effect in the classification formula. Expected result: Dominant. Any other label shows that the formula requires both differences to be strict." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Tie-boundary check" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DOM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "tie-boundary-check" .

hemo:7000227 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cheaper and more effective treatment"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "The tie tolerances are 0, as the module's formula has them, added by HEMO as inputs."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000228,
        hemo:7000229,
        hemo:7007504,
        hemo:7007505 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000230 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A new treatment costs £7,500 per patient and produces 4.8 QALYs, while current care costs £10,000 and produces 4.2 QALYs. Incremental cost is minus £2,500 and incremental effect is 0.6 QALYs, so the new treatment dominates and no threshold comparison is needed. Its incremental net monetary benefit is £2,500 plus 0.6 times the threshold, which is £14,500 at £20,000 per QALY and positive at every non-negative threshold. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cheaper and more effective treatment" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = -2500; Delta_E = 0.6; DOM = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cheaper-and-more-effective-treatment" .

hemo:7000228 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_C in the test Cheaper and more effective treatment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000586 ;
    rheo:2000001 -2500.0 .

hemo:7000229 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_E in the test Cheaper and more effective treatment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000587 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.6 .

hemo:7000230 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "DOM in the test Cheaper and more effective treatment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000588 ;
    rheo:2000001 1.0 .

hemo:7000231 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal cost with greater effect"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "The tie tolerances are 0, as the module's formula has them, added by HEMO as inputs."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000232,
        hemo:7000233,
        hemo:7007506,
        hemo:7007507 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000234 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An intervention costs the same as current care and produces 0.2 more QALYs. Incremental cost is zero, so a rule requiring both differences to be strict would leave the result unclassified; the inclusive rule classifies the intervention as dominant." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal cost with greater effect" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = 0; Delta_E = 0.2; DOM = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-cost-with-greater-effect" .

hemo:7000232 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_C in the test Equal cost with greater effect"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000586 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.0 .

hemo:7000233 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_E in the test Equal cost with greater effect"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000587 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.2 .

hemo:7000234 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "DOM in the test Equal cost with greater effect"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000588 ;
    rheo:2000001 1.0 .

hemo:7000235 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Trade-off rather than dominance"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "The tie tolerances are 0, as the module's formula has them, added by HEMO as inputs."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000236,
        hemo:7000237,
        hemo:7007508,
        hemo:7007509 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000238 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An intervention costs £4,000 more and produces 0.30 more QALYs. Neither option dominates, so the comparison needs a threshold, through the ICER or net monetary benefit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Trade-off rather than dominance" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = 4000; Delta_E = 0.30; DOM = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "trade-off-rather-than-dominance" .

hemo:7000236 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_C in the test Trade-off rather than dominance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000586 ;
    rheo:2000001 4000.0 .

hemo:7000237 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_E in the test Trade-off rather than dominance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000587 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.3 .

hemo:7000238 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "DOM in the test Trade-off rather than dominance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000588 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.0 .

hemo:7000239 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Exact duplicates handled separately"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Options with identical expected cost and effect do not dominate each other under the rule, so duplicates are merged or one is retained before the screen." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exact duplicates handled separately" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DOM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exact-duplicates-handled-separately" .

hemo:7000240 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Screen before sequential ratios"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The screen runs on expected values before sequential ICERs are calculated and before extended dominance is checked, and it is repeated whenever an option is added." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Screen before sequential ratios" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DOM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "screen-before-sequential-ratios" .

hemo:7000241 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Flag dominated options in a table"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000199 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With expected costs in B2:B10 and expected effects in C2:C10, the formula in row 2, filled down, counts options that cost no more and produce no less, then removes those identical to the option itself. A remaining count above zero means the option is dominated." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Flag dominated options in a table" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DOM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "flag-dominated-options-in-a-table" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(COUNTIFS($B$2:$B$10,\"<=\"&B2,$C$2:$C$10,\">=\"&C2)-COUNTIFS($B$2:$B$10,B2,$C$2:$C$10,C2)>0,\"Dominated\",\"Not dominated\")" .

hemo:7000242 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Frontier order check"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "After the screen, sort the retained options by cost, with costs in column B and effects in column C from row 2, and fill the formula down from row 3. Expected result: TRUE on every row. FALSE shows a retained option with no more cost or no more effect than a cheaper one, which the screen should have flagged." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Frontier order check" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DOM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "frontier-order-check" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(B3>B2,C3>C2)" .

hemo:7000243 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Five options with one dominated"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Five options cost £10,000, £13,000, £20,000, £18,000 and £22,000 and produce 4.0, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5 and 4.8 life years. The third option, at £20,000 and 4.4 life years, is dominated by the fourth, which costs £2,000 less and produces 0.1 more life years. The figures are illustrative and match the example on the cost-effectiveness analysis page." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Five options with one dominated" ;
    hemo:9000014 "J = 5; C_j = [10000,13000,20000,18000,22000]; E_j = [4.0,4.3,4.4,4.5,4.8]; C_k = 20000; E_k = 4.4; DOM_k = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "five-options-with-one-dominated" .

hemo:7000244 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Dominance through a tie in cost"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Two options each cost £13,000, one producing 4.3 QALYs and the other 4.1 QALYs, alongside a £10,000 option producing 4.0 QALYs. The option producing 4.1 QALYs is dominated because another option costs no more and produces more health." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Dominance through a tie in cost" ;
    hemo:9000014 "J = 3; C_j = [10000,13000,13000]; E_j = [4.0,4.3,4.1]; C_k = 13000; E_k = 4.1; DOM_k = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "dominance-through-a-tie-in-cost" .

hemo:7000245 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Dominated options removed first"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The three options remain after dominated options, including ties, have been removed, so expected cost and expected effect both rise from L to M to H and both denominators are positive." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Dominated options removed first" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EXD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "dominated-options-removed-first" .

hemo:7000246 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Adjacent options, recalculated after each removal"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "L, M and H are consecutive in the current ordering by expected effect. After any removal, adjacency changes, the sequential ICERs are recalculated and the check is repeated until the ICERs rise with effect." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Adjacent options, recalculated after each removal" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EXD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "adjacent-options-recalculated-after-each-removal" .

hemo:7000247 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal sequential ratios"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "When D_M equals 0, the two sequential ICERs are equal and M lies on the straight line joining L and H, so it is not treated as extendedly dominated." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal sequential ratios" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EXD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-sequential-ratios" .

hemo:7000248 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Flag an extendedly dominated middle option"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000200 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel calculates D_M, the sequential ICER into the middle option minus the sequential ICER out of it, using named cells for the three adjacent options, and flags the middle option when D_M is greater than 0." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Flag an extendedly dominated middle option" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EXD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "flag-an-extendedly-dominated-middle-option" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF((MiddleCost-LowerCost)/(MiddleEffect-LowerEffect)-(HigherCost-MiddleCost)/(HigherEffect-MiddleEffect)>0,\"Extendedly dominated\",\"Retain\")" .

hemo:7000249 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Rising ICER check on the final frontier"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the final sequential ICERs in column F from row 3, compare each with the next by filling the formula down to the second-last option. Expected result: TRUE on every row. FALSE shows that an extendedly dominated option remains." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rising ICER check on the final frontier" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EXD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rising-icer-check-on-the-final-frontier" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=F3<=F4" .

hemo:7000250 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Net monetary benefit cross-check"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At any stated threshold, calculate net monetary benefit for L, M and H. Expected result: TRUE whenever D_M is greater than 0, because the net monetary benefit of the middle option is then below the larger of its two neighbours at every threshold." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net monetary benefit cross-check" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EXD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-monetary-benefit-cross-check" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MiddleNMB<MAX(LowerNMB,HigherNMB)" .

hemo:7000251 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Middle option extendedly dominated"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Three options cost £13,000, £18,000 and £22,000 and produce 4.3, 4.5 and 4.8 QALYs. The sequential ICER into the middle option is £25,000 per QALY and the next is about £13,333 per QALY, so D_M is about £11,667 per QALY. Because D_M is greater than 0, the middle option is extendedly dominated. The figures are illustrative and match options B, C and D in the article's four-option example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Middle option extendedly dominated" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_L = 13000; E_L = 4.3; C_M = 18000; E_M = 4.5; C_H = 22000; E_H = 4.8; D_M = 11666.67" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EXD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "middle-option-extendedly-dominated" .

hemo:7000252 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Frontier after recalculation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With option C removed, A, B and D are consecutive. A costs £10,000 for 4.0 QALYs, B £13,000 for 4.3 and D £22,000 for 4.8. The ICER from A to B is £10,000 per QALY and from B to D is £18,000, so D_M is minus £8,000 per QALY. Because D_M is not greater than 0, B is retained and A, B and D form the frontier." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Frontier after recalculation" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_L = 10000; E_L = 4.0; C_M = 13000; E_M = 4.3; C_H = 22000; E_H = 4.8; D_M = -8000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EXD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "frontier-after-recalculation" .

hemo:7000253 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Proportional blending"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Expected costs and effects of the blend are the population-share weighted averages of those of L and H, with E_L below E_M and E_M below E_H so that p lies between 0 and 1. The blend is a geometric device; the recommendation is L or H, whichever has the higher net monetary benefit at the threshold." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Proportional blending" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EXD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "proportional-blending" .

hemo:7000254 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Saving from the matching blend"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000201 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel calculates the blend share, the blend cost and the saving against the middle option in one formula using named cells." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Saving from the matching blend" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EXD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "saving-from-the-matching-blend" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MiddleCost-(LowerCost+(MiddleEffect-LowerEffect)/(HigherEffect-LowerEffect)*(HigherCost-LowerCost))" .

hemo:7000255 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement with the ICER condition"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Compare the sign of the blend saving with the sequential ICER condition for the same three options. Expected result: TRUE, because a positive saving occurs exactly when D_M, the ICER into M minus the ICER out of M, is greater than 0." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Agreement with the ICER condition" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EXD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "agreement-with-the-icer-condition" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(BlendSaving>0)=((MiddleCost-LowerCost)/(MiddleEffect-LowerEffect)>(HigherCost-MiddleCost)/(HigherEffect-MiddleEffect))" .

hemo:7000256 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Blend of the neighbours matching the middle option"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For options costing £13,000, £18,000 and £22,000 with 4.3, 4.5 and 4.8 QALYs, giving 40% of the population the most effective option and 60% the least effective one produces 4.5 QALYs at £16,600. The blend saves £1,400 against the middle option for the same health, so the middle option lies above the line joining its neighbours." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Blend of the neighbours matching the middle option" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_L = 13000; E_L = 4.3; C_M = 18000; E_M = 4.5; C_H = 22000; E_H = 4.8; p = 0.40; C_mix = 16600; S_mix = 1400" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EXD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "blend-of-the-neighbours-matching-the-middle-option" .

hemo:7000257 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Paired incremental results from one probabilistic analysis"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Delta_E_i and Delta_C_i come from the same simulation, in which every uncertain parameter is sampled from a distribution representing current evidence. Sampling costs and effects separately would discard their correlation and distort the curve." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Paired incremental results from one probabilistic analysis" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CEAC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "paired-incremental-results-from-one-probabilistic-analysis" .

hemo:7000258 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Sign of incremental net monetary benefit classifies each draw"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A draw favours the intervention when lambda times Delta_E_i minus Delta_C_i is greater than zero. This rule is correct in all four quadrants of the cost-effectiveness plane, including south-west draws, where the intervention is favoured only when the saving per unit of effect forgone exceeds lambda." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sign of incremental net monetary benefit classifies each draw" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CEAC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sign-of-incremental-net-monetary-benefit-classifies-each-draw" .

hemo:7000259 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Probability conditional on the represented uncertainty"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Reading the proportion as the probability of cost-effectiveness treats the model parameters as uncertain quantities with distributions, as probabilistic sensitivity analysis does. The value reflects only the uncertainty in the model: parameters held fixed and structural alternatives not modelled do not appear in it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Probability conditional on the represented uncertainty" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CEAC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "probability-conditional-on-the-represented-uncertainty" .

hemo:7000260 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-option CEAC in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000202 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With simulated incremental effects in the named range IncEffect and incremental costs in IncCost, one row per simulation, SUMPRODUCT counts the draws with positive incremental net monetary benefit at the threshold in the named cell Threshold and divides by the number of simulations." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-option CEAC in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CEAC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-option-ceac-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(--(Threshold*IncEffect-IncCost>0))/ROWS(IncEffect)" .

hemo:7000261 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "CEAC values across a threshold range"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000202 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With threshold values in column H from row 2, the formula in I2, filled down, returns the CEAC at each threshold from the same simulations. Column H against column I is then plotted as an XY scatter chart with lines, with the vertical axis fixed from 0 to 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "CEAC values across a threshold range" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CEAC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ceac-values-across-a-threshold-range" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(--($H2*IncEffect-IncCost>0))/ROWS(IncEffect)" .

hemo:7000262 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Zero-threshold end point"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At a threshold of 0, count the draws with positive incremental net monetary benefit and compare the count with the number of draws in which the intervention costs less. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that the classification uses something other than the sign of incremental net monetary benefit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Zero-threshold end point" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CEAC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "zero-threshold-end-point" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(--(0*IncEffect-IncCost>0))=COUNTIF(IncCost,\"<0\")" .

hemo:7000263 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Five simulations at £30,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Five illustrative simulations give incremental effects of 0.40, 0.25, 0.10, 0.30 and minus 0.05 QALYs and incremental costs of £6,000, £9,000, £5,000, £4,000 and minus £3,000. At £30,000 per QALY the incremental net monetary benefits are £6,000, minus £1,500, minus £2,000, £5,000 and £1,500, so three of the five are positive and the CEAC is 0.6. The fifth draw lies in the south-west quadrant with a ratio of £60,000 per QALY forgone and counts in favour of the intervention, because the saving per QALY forgone exceeds the threshold. A real analysis would use thousands of simulations." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Five simulations at £30,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 30000; N = 5; Delta_E_i = [0.40,0.25,0.10,0.30,-0.05]; Delta_C_i = [6000,9000,5000,4000,-3000]; CEAC = 0.6" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CEAC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "five-simulations-at-30-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7000264 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same simulations at a zero threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At a threshold of zero, health effects receive no monetary value, so a draw favours the intervention only when it saves money. Only the fifth draw does, so the curve starts at 0.2 rather than at zero. As the threshold grows very large, the curve approaches the share of draws with a health gain, here 0.8, so it need not reach 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same simulations at a zero threshold" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 0; N = 5; Delta_E_i = [0.40,0.25,0.10,0.30,-0.05]; Delta_C_i = [6000,9000,5000,4000,-3000]; CEAC = 0.2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CEAC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-simulations-at-a-zero-threshold" .

hemo:7000265 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Every option evaluated in the same simulations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "All options are run with the same parameter draw in each simulation, so NMBmax_i compares options under the same state of the world and the correlation between their net benefits is preserved." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Every option evaluated in the same simulations" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CEAC-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "every-option-evaluated-in-the-same-simulations" .

hemo:7000266 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Complete set of options"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The probabilities depend on every option included. Adding or removing an option can change every CEAC value, so all probabilities are recalculated whenever the set of options changes." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Complete set of options" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CEAC-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "complete-set-of-options" .

hemo:7000267 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Share of draws won by one option"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000203 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With each option's net monetary benefit in adjacent columns B to D, one row per simulation, a helper column RowMax holds =MAX(B2:D2) filled down. The formula then returns the share of rows in which the option in the named range OptionNMB equals the row maximum." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Share of draws won by one option" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CEAC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "share-of-draws-won-by-one-option" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(--(OptionNMB=RowMax))/ROWS(OptionNMB)" .

hemo:7000268 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Multi-option probabilities sum to one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Add the CEAC values of all options at one threshold. Expected result: TRUE when no draw has a tie for the highest net monetary benefit. FALSE shows an omitted option, inconsistent draws or ties credited to more than one option." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Multi-option probabilities sum to one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CEAC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "multi-option-probabilities-sum-to-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUM(CEACValues)-1)<0.000001" .

hemo:7000269 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two options with the most frequent winner not preferred"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At one stated threshold, option A has net monetary benefits of £10,000, £12,000, £9,000, £11,000 and £8,000 in five illustrative simulations, and option B has £10,200, £12,300, £9,100, £11,400 and £3,000. A has the highest value only in the fifth draw, so its CEAC is 0.2 and B's is 0.8. The figures match the article's worked example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two options with the most frequent winner not preferred" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N = 5; NMB_ij = [10000,12000,9000,11000,8000]; NMBmax_i = [10200,12300,9100,11400,8000]; CEAC_j = 0.2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CEAC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-options-with-the-most-frequent-winner-not-preferred" .

hemo:7000270 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Frontier and CEACs from the same simulations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "ENB_j and CEAC_j are calculated from the same draws at the same threshold, so the frontier switches between options at the threshold where the expected net monetary benefits cross, which need not be where the curves cross." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Frontier and CEACs from the same simulations" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CEAC-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "frontier-and-ceacs-from-the-same-simulations" .

hemo:7000271 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Frontier value at one threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000204 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With CEAC values in the named range CEACValues and expected net monetary benefits in ENBValues, both listed in the same option order, Excel returns the CEAC of the option with the highest expected net monetary benefit. The error probability is 1 minus this cell." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Frontier value at one threshold" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CEAC-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "frontier-value-at-one-threshold" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=INDEX(CEACValues,MATCH(MAX(ENBValues),ENBValues,0))" .

hemo:7000272 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Frontier never above the highest curve"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Compare the frontier value with the highest CEAC at the same threshold. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that the frontier has been read from a different threshold or from different simulations." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Frontier never above the highest curve" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CEAC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "frontier-never-above-the-highest-curve" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CEAF<=MAX(CEACValues)" .

hemo:7000273 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Frontier below the other option's curve"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the two-option example, option A has an expected net monetary benefit of £10,000 and option B £9,200, so A, the first option, is chosen. The frontier takes A's CEAC of 0.2, below B's 0.8, and the error probability is 0.8. B wins four draws by between £100 and £400 but loses one by £5,000, so its frequent small gains do not outweigh the single large loss." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Frontier below the other option's curve" ;
    hemo:9000014 "CEAC_j = [0.2,0.8]; ENB_j = [10000,9200]; j* = 1; CEAF = 0.2; P_err = 0.8" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CEAC-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "frontier-below-the-other-option-s-curve" .

hemo:7000274 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same parameter draw for every option"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "In each simulation every option is evaluated with the same draw of the uncertain parameters. This keeps the correlation between the options' net benefits, on which the probability of cost-effectiveness and value of information depend, and reduces the Monte Carlo error in the difference between options." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same parameter draw for every option" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ENB-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-parameter-draw-for-every-option" .

hemo:7000275 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Distributions that represent the evidence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each uncertain parameter is sampled from a distribution chosen to represent the available evidence, not chosen arbitrarily, as the NICE manual requires. The mean is only as good as those distributions and the model structure." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Distributions that represent the evidence" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ENB-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "distributions-that-represent-the-evidence" .

hemo:7000276 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Enough simulations for a stable mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "N is large enough for Monte Carlo error to be small relative to the differences between options. When two options have close expected net benefits, a small number of simulations can reverse their ranking by chance." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Enough simulations for a stable mean" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ENB-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "enough-simulations-for-a-stable-mean" .

hemo:7000277 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Adoption follows the highest mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The option with the highest ENB_j at the stated threshold is adopted on current evidence, whether or not the difference is statistically significant. This is the maximum net monetary benefit rule on the net monetary benefit page applied to simulation means; the spread of net benefit informs the separate question of whether more evidence is worth acquiring." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Adoption follows the highest mean" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ENB-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "adoption-follows-the-highest-mean" .

hemo:7000278 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected NMB from a simulation table"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000205 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With simulated effects of one option in the named range SimEffects and its simulated costs in SimCosts, one row per simulation, Excel averages the net monetary benefit at the threshold in the named cell Threshold." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected NMB from a simulation table" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ENB-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-nmb-from-a-simulation-table" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(Threshold*SimEffects-SimCosts)/ROWS(SimEffects)" .

hemo:7000279 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Linearity reconciliation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Compare the mean of the simulated net monetary benefits with the threshold times the mean effect minus the mean cost. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows blank or text cells treated differently in the two calculations, or effects and costs taken from ranges of different length." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Linearity reconciliation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ENB-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "linearity-reconciliation" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(Threshold*SimEffects-SimCosts)/ROWS(SimEffects)-(Threshold*AVERAGE(SimEffects)-AVERAGE(SimCosts)))<0.01" .

hemo:7000280 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Probabilistic mean against a deterministic run"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Compare ENB_j with the net monetary benefit from one deterministic run at the mean inputs. Expected result for a model that is linear in its parameters: TRUE. FALSE in a Markov or survival model is expected and shows why the probabilistic mean is used for the preferred estimate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Probabilistic mean against a deterministic run" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ENB-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "probabilistic-mean-against-a-deterministic-run" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ExpectedNMB-DeterministicNMB)<0.01" .

hemo:7000281 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard care over five simulations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Standard care A is evaluated at £25,000 per QALY in five illustrative, equally likely simulations with QALYs of 6.00, 5.80, 6.20, 5.60 and 5.90 and costs of £12,000, £11,000, £13,000, £12,000 and £12,000. Its net monetary benefits are £138,000, £134,000, £142,000, £128,000 and £135,500, with a mean of £135,500. The figures match the article's worked example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standard care over five simulations" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 25000; N = 5; E_jn = [6.00,5.80,6.20,5.60,5.90]; C_jn = [12000,11000,13000,12000,12000]; ENB_j = 135500" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ENB-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standard-care-over-five-simulations" .

hemo:7000282 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "New treatment over the same simulations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "New treatment B, in the same five simulations, has QALYs of 6.20, 6.04, 6.48, 6.20 and 6.70 and costs of £21,000, £20,000, £22,000, £19,000 and £20,000. Its expected net monetary benefit is £137,700, £2,200 per patient more than A, so B is adopted. A has the higher net benefit in three of the five simulations, but B loses by small amounts and wins by large ones." ;
    hemo:9000009 "New treatment over the same simulations" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 25000; N = 5; E_jn = [6.20,6.04,6.48,6.20,6.70]; C_jn = [21000,20000,22000,19000,20000]; ENB_j = 137700" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ENB-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "new-treatment-over-the-same-simulations" .

hemo:7000283 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Cost expressed as health forgone"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "C_jn divided by lambda is the health expected to be given up elsewhere when lambda reflects the opportunity cost of spending, as set out on the cost-effectiveness threshold page. Lambda is greater than zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cost expressed as health forgone" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ENB-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cost-expressed-as-health-forgone" .

hemo:7000284 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected net health benefit from a simulation table"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000206 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel subtracts the mean simulated cost divided by the threshold from the mean simulated effect, using the same named ranges as the monetary form." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected net health benefit from a simulation table" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ENB-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-net-health-benefit-from-a-simulation-table" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AVERAGE(SimEffects)-AVERAGE(SimCosts)/Threshold" .

hemo:7000285 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement with expected net monetary benefit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Multiply the expected net health benefit by the threshold and compare it with the expected net monetary benefit from the same simulations. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a different threshold or a different set of draws in the two calculations." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Agreement with expected net monetary benefit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ENB-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "agreement-with-expected-net-monetary-benefit" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ExpectedNHB*Threshold-ExpectedNMB)<0.01" .

hemo:7000286 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard care in health units"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Using the same five simulations and a threshold of £25,000 per QALY, standard care A has net health benefits of 5.52, 5.36, 5.68, 5.12 and 5.42 QALYs, with a mean of 5.42 QALYs, which is £135,500 divided by £25,000." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standard care in health units" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 25000; N = 5; E_jn = [6.00,5.80,6.20,5.60,5.90]; C_jn = [12000,11000,13000,12000,12000]; ENHB_j = 5.42" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ENB-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standard-care-in-health-units" .

hemo:7000287 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "New treatment in health units"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "New treatment B has a mean net health benefit of 5.508 QALYs at £25,000 per QALY, 0.088 QALYs per patient more than A, the same ranking as in monetary units. At £35,000 per QALY the values are about 5.557 QALYs for A and 5.741 QALYs for B." ;
    hemo:9000009 "New treatment in health units" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 25000; N = 5; E_jn = [6.20,6.04,6.48,6.20,6.70]; C_jn = [21000,20000,22000,19000,20000]; ENHB_j = 5.508" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ENB-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "new-treatment-in-health-units" .

hemo:7000288 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Order of expectation and maximisation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "With perfect information the choice can differ in each draw, so the maximum is taken inside the average. On current information one option is chosen for all draws, so the average is taken first and the maximum second. EVPI is therefore zero or positive, and zero only when the same option is best in every draw." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Order of expectation and maximisation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-VOI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "order-of-expectation-and-maximisation" .

hemo:7000289 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Net benefit on a stated basis"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every draw's net benefit uses the same threshold, population, perspective and time horizon as the adoption decision, and NBmax_s and ENB_cur come from the same set of draws." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net benefit on a stated basis" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-VOI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-benefit-on-a-stated-basis" .

hemo:7000290 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Only represented uncertainty is valued"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "EVPI values resolution of the uncertainty in the probabilistic model. Parameters held fixed and structural alternatives that are not parameterised contribute nothing, so an incomplete uncertainty model understates the value of information." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Only represented uncertainty is valued" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-VOI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "only-represented-uncertainty-is-valued" .

hemo:7000291 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "EVPI from a table of draws"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000207 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With each option's net benefit in adjacent columns B to D, one row per draw, a helper column RowMax holds =MAX(B2:D2) filled down and a helper row ColMeans holds the mean of each option's column. Excel subtracts the largest column mean from the mean of the row maxima." ;
    hemo:9000009 "EVPI from a table of draws" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-VOI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "evpi-from-a-table-of-draws" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AVERAGE(RowMax)-MAX(ColMeans)" .

hemo:7000292 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Non-negative EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Test whether the mean of the row maxima is at least the largest column mean. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that the order of averaging and maximisation has been reversed or that the two terms use different draws." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Non-negative EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-VOI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "non-negative-evpi" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AVERAGE(RowMax)-MAX(ColMeans)>=0" .

hemo:7000293 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two equally likely states"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000294,
        hemo:7000295,
        hemo:7000296 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000297 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Strategy A has a net monetary benefit of £1,000 in state 1 and £200 in state 2, and strategy B £600 and £800, each state having probability 0.5. The best values are £1,000 and £800, with a mean of £900. On current information B is chosen, with expected net monetary benefit £700, so EVPI is £200 per patient. The figures match the article's worked example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two equally likely states" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S = 2; NBmax_s = [1000,800]; ENB_cur = 700; EVPI = 200" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-VOI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-equally-likely-states" .

