hemo:7000303 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Stated timing and horizon"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The first period is t equal to 0 and is not discounted; if the first cohort is to be discounted, t starts at 1. The time horizon stands in for future changes in technologies, prices and evidence, so it is stated and justified." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Stated timing and horizon" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-VOI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "stated-timing-and-horizon" .

hemo:7000304 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Only people who can benefit are counted"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "N_t excludes people whose treatment is decided before new evidence could be available, and it can be reduced for incomplete adoption. Per-person EVPI is assumed to apply unchanged to every period." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Only people who can benefit are counted" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-VOI-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "only-people-who-can-benefit-are-counted" .

hemo:7000305 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Population EVPI from a period table"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000208 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the numbers of people in the named range Population, the period times in Period and the discount rate in Rate, SUMPRODUCT discounts each cohort and Excel multiplies the total by per-person EVPI." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Population EVPI from a period table" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-VOI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "population-evpi-from-a-period-table" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EVPI*SUMPRODUCT(Population/(1+Rate)^Period)" .

hemo:7000306 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted population bound"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Compare population EVPI with per-person EVPI multiplied by the undiscounted number of people. Expected result: TRUE for a non-negative rate. FALSE shows a rate entered as a whole number, such as 3.5 for 3.5%, or periods before time zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted population bound" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-VOI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-population-bound" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PopulationEVPI<=EVPI*SUM(Population)" .

hemo:7000307 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "1,000 people a year for five years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000308,
        hemo:7000309,
        hemo:7000310,
        hemo:7000311,
        hemo:7000312 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000313 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Per-person EVPI is £200, and 1,000 people a year face the decision for five years, from t equal to 0 to 4, with future cohorts discounted at an illustrative 3.5% a year. The discounted population is about 4,673 people, so population EVPI is about £934,616. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "1,000 people a year for five years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "EVPI = 200; T = 4; t = [0,1,2,3,4]; N_t = [1000,1000,1000,1000,1000]; r = 0.035; EVPI_pop = 934615.84" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-VOI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "1-000-people-a-year-for-five-years" .

