hemo:7000321 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Conditional expectation estimated adequately"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The inner expectation is estimated by nested simulation or by regression of net benefit on phi, as in the generalised additive model and Gaussian process methods. With few inner draws the maximisation biases a nested estimate upwards." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Conditional expectation estimated adequately" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-VOI-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "conditional-expectation-estimated-adequately" .

hemo:7000322 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Ordering with EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "EVPPI lies between zero and the EVPI for all parameters, apart from small violations caused by numerical error. Parameters are grouped by the research question that could inform them." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ordering with EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-VOI-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ordering-with-evpi" .

hemo:7000323 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "EVPPI for a discrete parameter"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000209 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With draws in rows, the value of phi in the named range PhiGroup and the net benefits of options A and B in NB_A and NB_B, the formula in I2, filled down beside the distinct phi values in column H, returns the best conditional mean. For phi values with equal numbers of draws, EVPPI is then =AVERAGE(I2:I3)-MAX(AVERAGE(NB_A),AVERAGE(NB_B))." ;
    hemo:9000009 "EVPPI for a discrete parameter" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-VOI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "evppi-for-a-discrete-parameter" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MAX(AVERAGEIFS(NB_A,PhiGroup,H2),AVERAGEIFS(NB_B,PhiGroup,H2))" .

hemo:7000324 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "EVPPI within EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Compare EVPPI with EVPI from the same draws, allowing a stated Monte Carlo tolerance. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an inner expectation estimated with too few draws or a maximum taken inside the inner average." ;
    hemo:9000009 "EVPPI within EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-VOI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "evppi-within-evpi" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EVPPI<=EVPI+Tolerance" .

hemo:7000325 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Four equally likely draws with two parameters"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Parameter phi takes values 1 or 2 and psi takes values 1 or 2, independently and with equal probability. Options A and B have net benefits of £1,000 and £600 at phi 1 and psi 1, £600 and £800 at phi 1 and psi 2, £200 and £800 at phi 2 and psi 1, and £200 and £600 at phi 2 and psi 2. Knowing phi, A is chosen at phi 1 with a mean of £800 and B at phi 2 with a mean of £700, an average of £750. On current information B is chosen with £700, so EVPPI for phi is £50, half the EVPI of £100 for both parameters." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Four equally likely draws with two parameters" ;
    hemo:9000014 "phi = [1,1,2,2]; psi = [1,2,1,2]; NB_d = [[1000,600],[600,800],[200,800],[200,600]]; EVPPI_phi = 50" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-VOI-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "four-equally-likely-draws-with-two-parameters" .

hemo:7000326 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Other inputs held at base case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each endpoint run changes only input j and the quantities calculated from it, and the base case is restored between runs, so every bar is traceable to two model runs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Other inputs held at base case" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-OWSA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "other-inputs-held-at-base-case" .

hemo:7000327 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Defensible ranges on the estimation scale"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The lower and upper values come from the evidence, for example a 95% confidence interval on the scale on which the parameter was estimated. The ranking reflects range width as much as the model, and an arbitrary percentage range measures sensitivity but not uncertainty." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Defensible ranges on the estimation scale" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-OWSA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "defensible-ranges-on-the-estimation-scale" .

hemo:7000328 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Endpoints recorded rather than inferred"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The lower input value does not necessarily give the lower output, so both input endpoints and their outputs are stored with the swing." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Endpoints recorded rather than inferred" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-OWSA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "endpoints-recorded-rather-than-inferred" .

hemo:7000329 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Swing of one input"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000210 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel takes the absolute difference between the stored outputs of the two endpoint runs for one input." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Swing of one input" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-OWSA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "swing-of-one-input" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(HighInputOutput-LowInputOutput)" .

hemo:7000330 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Order inputs for the tornado diagram"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000210 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In Excel 365, SORTBY returns the results table in descending order of swing, keeping each input's label, endpoints and outputs on the same row." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Order inputs for the tornado diagram" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-OWSA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "order-inputs-for-the-tornado-diagram" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SORTBY(OWSATable,SwingColumn,-1)" .

hemo:7000331 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Base-to-base reproduction"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Run the model with input j set to its base-case value. Expected result: TRUE, the output reproduces the locked base case. FALSE shows that another input was changed or not restored." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Base-to-base reproduction" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-OWSA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "base-to-base-reproduction" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(BaseRerunOutput-BaseCaseOutput)<0.000001" .

hemo:7000332 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Widest bar at the top"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "After sorting, compare the first swing with the largest swing in the table. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows ranking by the width of the input range rather than by the output swing." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Widest bar at the top" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-OWSA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "widest-bar-at-the-top" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=INDEX(SortedSwing,1)=MAX(SwingColumn)" .

hemo:7000333 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Relative risk bar for the fictional drug Quintavel"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the illustrative Quintavel model, the relative risk of the event ranges from 0.45 to 0.80. The ICER is £16,364 per QALY at the lower value and £52,000 per QALY at the upper value, so the swing is £35,636, the widest bar. Quintavel is fictional and every figure is invented, matching the article's worked example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Relative risk bar for the fictional drug Quintavel" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y_jL = 16364; Y_jU = 52000; R_j = 35636" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-OWSA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "relative-risk-bar-for-the-fictional-drug-quintavel" .

hemo:7000334 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Baseline risk bar in net monetary benefit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For the baseline event risk, ranging from 0.40 to 0.60, incremental net monetary benefit at £30,000 per QALY is minus £400 at the lower value and £6,400 at the upper value, a swing of £6,800. The lower endpoint changes the decision, which a marked threshold line on the diagram shows." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Baseline risk bar in net monetary benefit" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y_jL = -400; Y_jU = 6400; R_j = 6800" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-OWSA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "baseline-risk-bar-in-net-monetary-benefit" .

hemo:7000335 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Net benefit linear in the input"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Incremental net monetary benefit is linear in input j between and beyond the endpoints. In the Quintavel model this holds for the relative risk, baseline risk, acquisition cost and QALY loss per event; otherwise the value is found with a root finder or a fine grid, and the method is reported." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net benefit linear in the input" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-OWSA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-benefit-linear-in-the-input" .

hemo:7000336 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Distinct endpoint results"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "INMB_jU differs from INMB_jL. When both have the same sign, the switching value lies outside the tested range and is reported as such." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Distinct endpoint results" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-OWSA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "distinct-endpoint-results" .

hemo:7000337 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Input not tied to other influential inputs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The analysis moves one input with the others at base case, so it is not used for parameters that are highly correlated with other influential parameters." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Input not tied to other influential inputs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-OWSA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "input-not-tied-to-other-influential-inputs" .

hemo:7000338 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Switching value from two endpoint runs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000211 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel interpolates the input value at which incremental net monetary benefit is zero from the stored endpoint results in named cells." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Switching value from two endpoint runs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-OWSA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "switching-value-from-two-endpoint-runs" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LowValue-LowINMB*(HighValue-LowValue)/(HighINMB-LowINMB)" .

hemo:7000339 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Substitution at the switching value"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Run the model with input j at the switching value and the others at base case. Expected result: TRUE, incremental net monetary benefit within £1 of zero. FALSE shows that net benefit is not linear in the input, so a root finder is needed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Substitution at the switching value" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-OWSA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "substitution-at-the-switching-value" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(INMBAtSwitchingValue)<1" .

hemo:7000340 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Switching relative risk for Quintavel"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At £30,000 per QALY, incremental net monetary benefit is £9,375 at a relative risk of 0.45 and minus £5,500 at 0.80. Interpolation gives a switching relative risk of about 0.6706, inside the tested range. Because net benefit is linear in the relative risk, this equals the analytic switching value of about 0.671 in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Switching relative risk for Quintavel" ;
    hemo:9000014 "theta_jL = 0.45; theta_jU = 0.80; INMB_jL = 9375; INMB_jU = -5500; theta_jS = 0.6706" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-OWSA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "switching-relative-risk-for-quintavel" .

hemo:7000341 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Switching acquisition cost outside the range"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Incremental net monetary benefit is £5,000 at an acquisition cost of £11,000 and £1,000 at £15,000. The switching value is £16,000, outside the tested range, so no tested price changes the decision. The result is exact because net benefit falls by £1 for every £1 of price." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Switching acquisition cost outside the range" ;
    hemo:9000014 "theta_jL = 11000; theta_jU = 15000; INMB_jL = 5000; INMB_jU = 1000; theta_jS = 16000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-OWSA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "switching-acquisition-cost-outside-the-range" .

hemo:7000342 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Marginal change under a fixed budget"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Delta_B is small relative to the budget, so the services affected are those at the margin. A technology with a large budget impact is likely to displace more than marginal activity, so the relevant threshold for it is lower." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Marginal change under a fixed budget" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CET-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "marginal-change-under-a-fixed-budget" .

hemo:7000343 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Health effects in the appraisal unit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Delta_H is measured in QALYs so that k can be compared with appraisal results. Estimates built from mortality effects are extended to life years and to QALYs, including effects on quality of life." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Health effects in the appraisal unit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CET-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "health-effects-in-the-appraisal-unit" .

hemo:7000344 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Specific to the system and period"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "An estimate applies to the health system, expenditure year and outcome data from which it was derived, and is updated as budgets and productivity change." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Specific to the system and period" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CET-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "specific-to-the-system-and-period" .

hemo:7000345 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Supply-side threshold from two named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000212 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel divides the expenditure change by the health change and returns #N/A when the health change is zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Supply-side threshold from two named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CET-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "supply-side-threshold-from-two-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(HealthChange<>0,ExpenditureChange/HealthChange,NA())" .

hemo:7000346 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Direction of the spending and health changes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Test whether expenditure and health move in the same direction. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE means that more spending was associated with less health, so the ratio cannot be read as a cost per QALY." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Direction of the spending and health changes" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CET-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "direction-of-the-spending-and-health-changes" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SIGN(ExpenditureChange)=SIGN(HealthChange)" .

hemo:7000347 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Illustrative marginal cost per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A reduction of £10 million in expenditure is estimated to displace services that would have produced 800 QALYs, so k is £12,500 per QALY. The figures are illustrative. The central published estimate for the English NHS is £12,936 per QALY, at 2008 expenditure with 2008 to 2010 mortality data." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Illustrative marginal cost per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_B = 10000000; Delta_H = 800; k = 12500" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CET-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "illustrative-marginal-cost-per-qaly" .

hemo:7000348 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive threshold and consistent differences"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "k is greater than zero, and Delta_E and Delta_C both take the intervention minus the comparator. The measure keeps its meaning in every quadrant of the cost-effectiveness plane, unlike the ICER." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive threshold and consistent differences" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CET-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-threshold-and-consistent-differences" .

hemo:7000349 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Modifiers weight QALYs rather than change k"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the NICE manual, decision-making modifiers act qualitatively or through QALY weighting, and net health benefit is presented at £25,000 and £35,000 per QALY with and without the weighting." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Modifiers weight QALYs rather than change k" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CET-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "modifiers-weight-qalys-rather-than-change-k" .

hemo:7000350 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Incremental net health benefit in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000213 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel subtracts the incremental cost divided by the threshold from the incremental effect, using named cells." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Incremental net health benefit in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CET-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "incremental-net-health-benefit-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IncrementalEffect-IncrementalCost/Threshold" .

hemo:7000351 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Net health and net monetary benefit agreement"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Multiply INHB by the threshold and compare it with incremental net monetary benefit at the same threshold. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a different threshold in the two cells or an inverted subtraction." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net health and net monetary benefit agreement" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CET-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-health-and-net-monetary-benefit-agreement" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(INHB*Threshold-(Threshold*IncrementalEffect-IncrementalCost))<0.01" .

hemo:7000352 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement with the ICER when effects increase"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a positive incremental effect, test whether a positive INHB coincides with an ICER below the threshold. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Agreement with the ICER when effects increase" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CET-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "agreement-with-the-icer-when-effects-increase" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(IncrementalEffect>0,(INHB>0)=(IncrementalCost/IncrementalEffect<Threshold),\"Not applicable\")" .

hemo:7000353 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment judged at the NHS opportunity-cost estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000354,
        hemo:7000355,
        hemo:7000356 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000357,
        hemo:7000358 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.00005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A treatment costs £6,000 more than current care and adds 0.40 QALYs, an ICER of £15,000 per QALY. At k of £12,936 per QALY, the £6,000 displaces about 0.4638 QALYs elsewhere, so incremental net health benefit is about minus 0.0638 QALYs, a loss of population health even though the ICER lies below NICE's range. The figures are illustrative and match the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Treatment judged at the NHS opportunity-cost estimate" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_E = 0.40; Delta_C = 6000; k = 12936; H_d = 0.4638; INHB = -0.0638" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CET-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "treatment-judged-at-the-nhs-opportunity-cost-estimate" .

hemo:7000354 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_E in the test Treatment judged at the NHS opportunity-cost estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000662 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.4 .

hemo:7000355 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_C in the test Treatment judged at the NHS opportunity-cost estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000663 ;
    rheo:2000001 6000.0 .

hemo:7000356 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "k in the test Treatment judged at the NHS opportunity-cost estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000664 ;
    rheo:2000001 12936.0 .

hemo:7000357 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "H_d in the test Treatment judged at the NHS opportunity-cost estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000660 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.4638 .

hemo:7000358 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "INHB in the test Treatment judged at the NHS opportunity-cost estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000661 ;
    rheo:2000001 -0.0638 .

hemo:7000359 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same treatment at £25,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000360,
        hemo:7000361,
        hemo:7000362 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000363,
        hemo:7000364 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At £25,000 per QALY, the lower value NICE uses to present net health benefit, the £6,000 displaces 0.24 QALYs and incremental net health benefit is 0.16 QALYs. At £35,000 per QALY it is about 0.229 QALYs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same treatment at £25,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_E = 0.40; Delta_C = 6000; k = 25000; H_d = 0.24; INHB = 0.16" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CET-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-treatment-at-25-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7000360 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_E in the test Same treatment at £25,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000662 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.4 .

hemo:7000361 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_C in the test Same treatment at £25,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000663 ;
    rheo:2000001 6000.0 .

hemo:7000362 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "k in the test Same treatment at £25,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000664 ;
    rheo:2000001 25000.0 .

hemo:7000363 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "H_d in the test Same treatment at £25,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000660 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.24 .

hemo:7000364 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "INHB in the test Same treatment at £25,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000661 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.16 .

hemo:7000365 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant hazard across the interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The rate h does not change within the interval. When the hazard changes with age or time since an event, the conversion is applied cycle by cycle with the rate for each cycle, or the probability is taken from a fitted survival curve." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant hazard across the interval" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TP-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-hazard-across-the-interval" .

hemo:7000366 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One exit from the starting state"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The formula describes a single event that removes the person from the starting state. When a state has two or more exits, each exit probability comes from the joint formula for competing hazards on this page, not from this formula applied to each exit separately." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One exit from the starting state" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TP-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-exit-from-the-starting-state" .

hemo:7000367 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Probability from a rate in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000214 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel returns the interval probability from named cells holding the rate and the interval length in matching units." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Probability from a rate in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-TP-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "probability-from-a-rate-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1-EXP(-Rate*CycleLength)" .

hemo:7000368 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Round trip from probability back to rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Convert the probability back with the rate formula on this page. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows mismatched units or a probability computed by a different rule." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Round trip from probability back to rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-TP-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "round-trip-from-probability-back-to-rate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(-LN(1-Probability)/CycleLength-Rate)<1E-9" .

hemo:7000369 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Annual cycle at a rate of 0.10 per year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000370,
        hemo:7000371 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000372 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.00005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A constant rate of 0.10 per year gives a one-year probability of about 0.0952, slightly below the rate because people who have the event early in the year are no longer at risk. The figure matches the comparator probability in the Hazard Ratio article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annual cycle at a rate of 0.10 per year" ;
    hemo:9000014 "h = 0.10; Delta = 1; p = 0.0952" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TP-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annual-cycle-at-a-rate-of-0-10-per-year" .

hemo:7000370 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "h in the test Annual cycle at a rate of 0.10 per year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000666 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.1 .

hemo:7000371 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta in the test Annual cycle at a rate of 0.10 per year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000667 ;
    rheo:2000001 1.0 .

hemo:7000372 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "p in the test Annual cycle at a rate of 0.10 per year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000665 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.0952 .

hemo:7000373 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three-month cycle at a total exit rate of 0.20"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000374,
        hemo:7000375 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000376 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.000005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A constant total exit rate of 0.20 per year over a three-month cycle gives a probability of leaving the state of about 0.04877, the total exit probability in the article's competing-risks example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three-month cycle at a total exit rate of 0.20" ;
    hemo:9000014 "h = 0.20; Delta = 0.25; p = 0.04877" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TP-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-month-cycle-at-a-total-exit-rate-of-0-20" .

hemo:7000374 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "h in the test Three-month cycle at a total exit rate of 0.20"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000666 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.2 .

hemo:7000375 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta in the test Three-month cycle at a total exit rate of 0.20"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000667 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.25 .

hemo:7000376 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "p in the test Three-month cycle at a total exit rate of 0.20"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000665 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.04877 .

hemo:7000377 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant hazard over the observation period"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The implied rate is an average constant hazard. If the hazard rose or fell during the observation period, the rate describes neither the start nor the end of the period." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant hazard over the observation period" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TP-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-hazard-over-the-observation-period" .

hemo:7000378 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Rate from a probability in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000215 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel uses LN, the natural logarithm, on named cells holding the probability and the length of its observation interval." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rate from a probability in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-TP-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rate-from-a-probability-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=-LN(1-Probability)/Interval" .

hemo:7000379 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Implied rate reproduces the observed probability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Convert the implied rate back to a probability over the observation interval. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that LOG was used instead of LN or that the interval was entered in another unit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Implied rate reproduces the observed probability" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-TP-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "implied-rate-reproduces-the-observed-probability" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(1-EXP(-ImpliedRate*Interval)-Probability)<1E-9" .

hemo:7000380 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "One-year probability of 0.20"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000381,
        hemo:7000382 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000383 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.00005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A one-year probability of 0.20 implies a constant rate of about 0.2231 per year, as in the article's rate conversion example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One-year probability of 0.20" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p = 0.20; Delta = 1; h = 0.2231" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TP-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-year-probability-of-0-20" .

hemo:7000381 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "p in the test One-year probability of 0.20"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000669 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.2 .

hemo:7000382 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta in the test One-year probability of 0.20"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000670 ;
    rheo:2000001 1.0 .

hemo:7000383 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "h in the test One-year probability of 0.20"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000668 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.2231 .

hemo:7000384 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Five-year probability of 0.10"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000385,
        hemo:7000386 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000387 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.00005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A study reports that 10% of people had the event over five years. The implied constant rate is about 0.0211 per year, slightly above 0.10 divided by 5." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Five-year probability of 0.10" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p = 0.10; Delta = 5; h = 0.0211" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TP-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "five-year-probability-of-0-10" .

hemo:7000385 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "p in the test Five-year probability of 0.10"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000669 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.1 .

hemo:7000386 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta in the test Five-year probability of 0.10"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000670 ;
    rheo:2000001 5.0 .

hemo:7000387 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "h in the test Five-year probability of 0.10"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000668 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.0211 .

hemo:7000388 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant hazard across both intervals"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The hazard is the same throughout the source interval and the model cycle, so compounding the new probability over Delta_old divided by Delta_new cycles recovers p_old." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant hazard across both intervals" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TP-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-hazard-across-both-intervals" .

hemo:7000389 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-state transition only"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The rescaling is exact only when the starting state has a single exit. With three or more possible transitions from a state, the rows of the transition matrix are converted jointly, for example from the competing hazards or from a matrix root." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-state transition only" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TP-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-state-transition-only" .

hemo:7000390 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Rescaled probability in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000216 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel raises the complement of the source probability to the ratio of the interval lengths, using named cells." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rescaled probability in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-TP-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rescaled-probability-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1-(1-OldProbability)^(NewLength/OldLength)" .

hemo:7000391 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Compounding back to the source interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Compound the new probability over the number of model cycles in the source interval. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that the probability was divided or rescaled by another rule." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Compounding back to the source interval" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-TP-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "compounding-back-to-the-source-interval" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(1-(1-NewProbability)^(OldLength/NewLength)-OldProbability)<1E-9" .

hemo:7000392 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Annual probability rescaled to one month"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000393,
        hemo:7000394,
        hemo:7000395 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000396 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.000005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An annual probability of 0.20 becomes a monthly probability of about 0.01842, as in the article. Dividing 0.20 by 12 would give about 0.01667 instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annual probability rescaled to one month" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_old = 0.20; Delta_old = 12; Delta_new = 1; p_new = 0.01842" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TP-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annual-probability-rescaled-to-one-month" .

hemo:7000393 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "p_old in the test Annual probability rescaled to one month"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000672 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.2 .

hemo:7000394 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_old in the test Annual probability rescaled to one month"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000674 ;
    rheo:2000001 12.0 .

hemo:7000395 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_new in the test Annual probability rescaled to one month"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000673 ;
    rheo:2000001 1.0 .

hemo:7000396 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "p_new in the test Annual probability rescaled to one month"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000671 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.01842 .

hemo:7000397 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Five-year probability rescaled to one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000398,
        hemo:7000399,
        hemo:7000400 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000401 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.00005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A five-year probability of 0.30 becomes an annual probability of about 0.0689, larger than 0.30 divided by 5 because fewer people remain at risk in later years." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Five-year probability rescaled to one year" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_old = 0.30; Delta_old = 5; Delta_new = 1; p_new = 0.0689" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TP-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "five-year-probability-rescaled-to-one-year" .

hemo:7000398 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "p_old in the test Five-year probability rescaled to one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000672 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.3 .

hemo:7000399 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_old in the test Five-year probability rescaled to one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000674 ;
    rheo:2000001 5.0 .

hemo:7000400 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Delta_new in the test Five-year probability rescaled to one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000673 ;
    rheo:2000001 1.0 .

hemo:7000401 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "p_new in the test Five-year probability rescaled to one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000671 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.0689 .

hemo:7000402 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant cause-specific hazards"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both hazards are constant within the interval and their sum is greater than zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant cause-specific hazards" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TP-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-cause-specific-hazards" .

hemo:7000403 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Absorbing destinations within the cycle"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A person who reaches destination 1 or 2 does not move again within the same cycle. If a further transition is possible from a destination, for example from ill to dead within one cycle, the formulas are no longer valid and the full matrix is derived from the transition rate matrix." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absorbing destinations within the cycle" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TP-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absorbing-destinations-within-the-cycle" .

hemo:7000404 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Competing exit probabilities in three cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000217 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With named cells Hazard1, Hazard2 and CycleLength, the three formulas return p_1, p_2 and p_stay respectively." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Competing exit probabilities in three cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-TP-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "competing-exit-probabilities-in-three-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Hazard1/(Hazard1+Hazard2)*(1-EXP(-(Hazard1+Hazard2)*CycleLength)); =Hazard2/(Hazard1+Hazard2)*(1-EXP(-(Hazard1+Hazard2)*CycleLength)); =EXP(-(Hazard1+Hazard2)*CycleLength)" .

hemo:7000405 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Row of competing exits sums to one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Add the two destination probabilities and the probability of remaining. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Row of competing exits sums to one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-TP-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "row-of-competing-exits-sums-to-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ExitProb1+ExitProb2+StayProb-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7000406 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two exits over a three-month cycle"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With hazards of 0.12 and 0.08 per year and a cycle of 0.25 years, the destination probabilities are about 0.02926 and 0.01951 and the probability of remaining is about 0.95123. The unrounded values sum to 1 and match the article's table." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two exits over a three-month cycle" ;
    hemo:9000014 "h_1 = 0.12; h_2 = 0.08; Delta = 0.25; p_1 = 0.02926; p_2 = 0.01951; p_stay = 0.95123" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TP-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-exits-over-a-three-month-cycle" .

hemo:7000407 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Hazards compared at the same time and on the same event"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both hazards refer to the same event definition, time origin and analysis population, and are measured at the same time since the origin." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hazards compared at the same time and on the same event" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hazards-compared-at-the-same-time-and-on-the-same-event" .

hemo:7000408 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Proportional hazards when one ratio summarises follow-up"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Reporting a single HR for the whole follow-up assumes that the ratio is constant over time. The NICE manual states that the assumption should always be assessed, preferably with log-cumulative hazard plots." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Proportional hazards when one ratio summarises follow-up" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "proportional-hazards-when-one-ratio-summarises-follow-up" .

hemo:7000409 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Hazard ratio from two named hazards"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000218 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel divides the treatment hazard by the comparator hazard and returns #N/A when the comparator hazard is not positive." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hazard ratio from two named hazards" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hazard-ratio-from-two-named-hazards" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(ComparatorHazard>0,TreatmentHazard/ComparatorHazard,NA())" .

hemo:7000410 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Hazard ratio reproduces the treatment hazard"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Multiply the hazard ratio by the comparator hazard and compare the product with the treatment hazard. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an inverted ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hazard ratio reproduces the treatment hazard" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hazard-ratio-reproduces-the-treatment-hazard" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(HazardRatio*ComparatorHazard-TreatmentHazard)<1E-12" .

hemo:7000411 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant hazards of 0.07 and 0.10 per year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With illustrative constant hazards of 0.07 per year on treatment and 0.10 per year on the comparator, HR = 0.07 / 0.10 = 0.70, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant hazards of 0.07 and 0.10 per year" ;
    hemo:9000014 "h_T = 0.07; h_C = 0.10; HR = 0.70" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-hazards-of-0-07-and-0-10-per-year" .

hemo:7000412 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Binary treatment covariate and proportional hazards"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Treatment is coded 0 and 1, and the model assumes that the hazards are proportional. A covariate coded in other units gives the hazard ratio per unit of that covariate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Binary treatment covariate and proportional hazards" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "binary-treatment-covariate-and-proportional-hazards" .

hemo:7000413 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Hazard ratio and 95% confidence limits from a coefficient"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000219 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the coefficient in the named cell Coef and its standard error in SE, the three formulas return the hazard ratio and its lower and upper 95% confidence limits, computed on the log scale." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hazard ratio and 95% confidence limits from a coefficient" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hazard-ratio-and-95-confidence-limits-from-a-coefficient" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EXP(Coef); =EXP(Coef-1.96*SE); =EXP(Coef+1.96*SE)" .

hemo:7000414 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reported hazard ratio against its coefficient"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Take the natural logarithm of the reported hazard ratio and compare it with the coefficient. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that the coefficient was reported as the ratio or that the ratio refers to the other reference group." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reported hazard ratio against its coefficient" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reported-hazard-ratio-against-its-coefficient" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LN(HazardRatio)-Coef)<0.001" .

hemo:7000415 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Coefficient of minus 0.3567"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A Cox coefficient of minus 0.3567 for treatment gives a hazard ratio of about 0.7000." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Coefficient of minus 0.3567" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta = -0.3567; HR = 0.7000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "coefficient-of-minus-0-3567" .

hemo:7000416 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Proportional hazards from the origin to t"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The hazard ratio is constant over the whole period from the time origin to t, both within the trial and in any extrapolated period. When the assumption fails, NICE directs analysts to the alternative methods in technical support document 21." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Proportional hazards from the origin to t" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "proportional-hazards-from-the-origin-to-t" .

hemo:7000417 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same population, time origin and event"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The baseline curve describes the target population for the same event and from the same time origin as the trial that estimated the ratio, and competing events are not treated as ordinary independent censoring." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same population, time origin and event" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-population-time-origin-and-event" .

hemo:7000418 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment survival column from a baseline column"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000220 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With comparator survival in column B from row 2 and the hazard ratio in the named cell HazardRatio, the formula in C2, filled down, returns treatment survival at each time." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Treatment survival column from a baseline column" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "treatment-survival-column-from-a-baseline-column" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=B2^HazardRatio" .

hemo:7000419 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Hazard ratio of one leaves the curve unchanged"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Set the hazard ratio to 1 and compare the treatment column with the comparator column over rows 2 to 100. Expected result: TRUE, the curves are identical." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hazard ratio of one leaves the curve unchanged" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hazard-ratio-of-one-leaves-the-curve-unchanged" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(--(C2:C100<>B2:B100))=0" .

hemo:7000420 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-year survival with a hazard ratio of 0.70"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With comparator two-year survival of about 0.81873, from a constant hazard of 0.10 per year, and a hazard ratio of 0.70, treatment two-year survival is about 0.8694, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-year survival with a hazard ratio of 0.70" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_C = 0.81873; HR = 0.70; S_T = 0.8694" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-year-survival-with-a-hazard-ratio-of-0-70" .

hemo:7000421 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Survival at the comparator median"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At the comparator median, where S_C is 0.50, a hazard ratio of 0.70 leaves about 0.6156 of the treated group event-free." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Survival at the comparator median" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_C = 0.50; HR = 0.70; S_T = 0.6156" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "survival-at-the-comparator-median" .

hemo:7000422 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Proportional hazards within the cycle"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The hazard ratio applies throughout the cycle. The comparator hazard need not be constant, because the relationship holds for the cumulative hazard over the cycle." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Proportional hazards within the cycle" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "proportional-hazards-within-the-cycle" .

hemo:7000423 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Single exit or cause-specific use"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The probability refers to one event from the starting state. When a state has competing exits, the ratio is applied to the cause-specific hazard of the event it describes, and the row is then rebuilt with the competing-hazards formula on the Transition Probability page." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Single exit or cause-specific use" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "single-exit-or-cause-specific-use" .

hemo:7000424 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment probability from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000221 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel raises the comparator survival probability for the cycle to the power of the hazard ratio and subtracts the result from 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Treatment probability from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "treatment-probability-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1-(1-ComparatorProb)^HazardRatio" .

hemo:7000425 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement with the rate route"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Convert the comparator probability to a rate, multiply by the hazard ratio, convert back and compare with the model's treatment probability. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that the probability was multiplied directly by the hazard ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Agreement with the rate route" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "agreement-with-the-rate-route" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(TreatmentProb-(1-EXP(HazardRatio*LN(1-ComparatorProb))))<1E-12" .

hemo:7000426 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Annual cycle with a comparator hazard of 0.10"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A comparator probability of about 0.0952 per annual cycle, from a hazard of 0.10 per year, and a hazard ratio of 0.70 give a treatment probability of about 0.0676, as in the article. Multiplying 0.0952 by 0.70 would give about 0.0666." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annual cycle with a comparator hazard of 0.10" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_C = 0.0952; HR = 0.70; p_T = 0.0676" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annual-cycle-with-a-comparator-hazard-of-0-10" .

hemo:7000427 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Comparator probability of 0.20 per cycle"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a comparator probability of 0.20 per cycle and a hazard ratio of 0.70, the treatment probability is about 0.1446, compared with 0.14 from direct multiplication, as in the Transition Probability article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Comparator probability of 0.20 per cycle" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_C = 0.20; HR = 0.70; p_T = 0.1446" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "comparator-probability-of-0-20-per-cycle" .

hemo:7000428 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant time ratio across the survival curve"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The same ratio applies at every percentile of the survival distribution. A quantile-quantile plot of the two groups' survival percentiles that follows a straight line through the origin supports the assumption." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant time ratio across the survival curve" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-AFT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-time-ratio-across-the-survival-curve" .

hemo:7000429 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same distribution and scale in both groups"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Treatment enters as a covariate, so both groups share the error distribution and the scale parameter sigma. If they differ, separate models of the same type are fitted to each arm and no single time ratio exists." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same distribution and scale in both groups" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-AFT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-distribution-and-scale-in-both-groups" .

hemo:7000430 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Time ratio and 95% confidence limits"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000222 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the coefficient in the named cell Coef and its standard error in SE, the three formulas return the time ratio and its lower and upper 95% limits." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Time ratio and 95% confidence limits" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-AFT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "time-ratio-and-95-confidence-limits" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EXP(Coef); =EXP(Coef-1.96*SE); =EXP(Coef+1.96*SE)" .

hemo:7000431 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reported time ratio against its coefficient"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Take the natural logarithm of the reported time ratio and compare it with the coefficient on the log-time scale. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that the published value is an acceleration factor on the reciprocal definition, or a hazard ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reported time ratio against its coefficient" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-AFT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reported-time-ratio-against-its-coefficient" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LN(TimeRatio)-Coef)<0.001" .

hemo:7000432 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Coefficient of 0.4055"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A treatment coefficient of 0.4055 gives a time ratio of about 1.50, so treatment makes survival times 50% longer, as in the article's example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Coefficient of 0.4055" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta_1 = 0.4055; TR = 1.50" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-AFT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "coefficient-of-0-4055" .

hemo:7000433 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Coefficient of minus 0.2231"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A negative coefficient of minus 0.2231 gives a time ratio of about 0.80, so events occur after 80% of the reference time." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Coefficient of minus 0.2231" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta_1 = -0.2231; TR = 0.80" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-AFT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "coefficient-of-minus-0-2231" .

hemo:7000434 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Time ratio holds at the chosen percentile"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The model's constant time ratio implies the same multiplication at every percentile, so S_T(t_T) equals S_C(t_C). Mean survival is multiplied by the same factor; a restricted mean over a fixed horizon is not." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Time ratio holds at the chosen percentile" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-AFT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "time-ratio-holds-at-the-chosen-percentile" .

hemo:7000435 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Treated percentile time from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000223 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel multiplies the reference time at the chosen percentile by the time ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Treated percentile time from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-AFT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "treated-percentile-time-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=TimeRatio*ReferenceTime" .

hemo:7000436 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Treated curve reaches the reference proportion at the scaled time"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With fitted survival functions available for both groups, evaluate treated survival at TimeRatio times ReferenceTime and compare it with reference survival at ReferenceTime. Expected result: the two probabilities are equal to the precision of the fit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Treated curve reaches the reference proportion at the scaled time" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-AFT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "treated-curve-reaches-the-reference-proportion-at-the-scaled-time" .

hemo:7000437 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Median survival with a time ratio of 1.5"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A reference median of 12 months and a time ratio of 1.5 give a treated median of 18 months, as in the article. Equivalently, S(18 | x = 1) equals S_0(12), which is 0.5." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Median survival with a time ratio of 1.5" ;
    hemo:9000014 "TR = 1.5; t_C = 12; t_T = 18" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-AFT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "median-survival-with-a-time-ratio-of-1-5" .

hemo:7000438 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weibull distribution with a common shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both groups follow a Weibull distribution with the same shape parameter. The relationship does not apply to log-logistic, log-normal or generalised gamma models, which do not produce a single hazard ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weibull distribution with a common shape" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-AFT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weibull-distribution-with-a-common-shape" .

hemo:7000439 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Hazard ratio from Weibull accelerated failure time output"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000224 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel combines the named cells Coef and Sigma. The second formula gives the same result from the time ratio and the shape parameter, Shape, equal to 1 divided by Sigma." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hazard ratio from Weibull accelerated failure time output" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-AFT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hazard-ratio-from-weibull-accelerated-failure-time-output" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EXP(-Coef/Sigma); =TimeRatio^(-Shape)" .

hemo:7000440 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement with a Weibull proportional hazards fit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Fit the same data as a Weibull proportional hazards model with treatment as a covariate and compare its hazard ratio with the value implied by the accelerated failure time output. Expected result: TRUE to rounding, because the two are the same model." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Agreement with a Weibull proportional hazards fit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-AFT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "agreement-with-a-weibull-proportional-hazards-fit" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PHHazardRatio-EXP(-Coef/Sigma))<0.001" .

hemo:7000441 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Time ratio of 1.5 with sigma of 0.8"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A coefficient of 0.4055, a time ratio of about 1.5, and a scale parameter of 0.8, a Weibull shape of 1.25, imply a hazard ratio of about 0.6024. A time ratio above 1 corresponds to a hazard ratio below 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Time ratio of 1.5 with sigma of 0.8" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta_1 = 0.4055; sigma = 0.8; HR = 0.6024" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-AFT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "time-ratio-of-1-5-with-sigma-of-0-8" .

hemo:7000442 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Exponential special case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With sigma equal to 1 the Weibull reduces to the exponential, and the hazard ratio is the reciprocal of the time ratio, about 0.667 for a time ratio of 1.5." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exponential special case" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta_1 = 0.4055; sigma = 1; HR = 0.667" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-AFT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exponential-special-case" .

hemo:7000443 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant hazard for the event"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The hazard of event j is constant from the current clock time onwards. A hazard that changes with age or time since an event needs another distribution, such as the Weibull, or an inverse cumulative-hazard method." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant hazard for the event" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DES-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-hazard-for-the-event" .

hemo:7000444 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Next-event advance of the clock"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Candidate times are sampled for every event the patient is at risk of, the clock moves to the earliest, that event's logic is executed, and events made impossible, such as a follow-up visit after death, are cancelled. Ties follow a documented priority rule." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Next-event advance of the clock" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DES-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "next-event-advance-of-the-clock" .

hemo:7000445 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Independent or deliberately shared random numbers"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each U comes from a separate draw, except where common random numbers are used on purpose so that the same simulated patient receives the same draws in each strategy being compared." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Independent or deliberately shared random numbers" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DES-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "independent-or-deliberately-shared-random-numbers" .

hemo:7000446 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Exponential time to event in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000225 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel RAND returns values from 0 up to but not including 1, so 1 minus RAND is used to avoid LN(0). A fixed draw in the named cell UniformDraw is used when results must be reproducible." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exponential time to event in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DES-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exponential-time-to-event-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=-LN(1-RAND())/Rate; =-LN(UniformDraw)/Rate" .

hemo:7000447 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mean of many sampled times"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Sample at least 10,000 times in a column named SampledTimes and compare their mean with 1 divided by the rate. Expected result: TRUE in about 95% of runs, because the relative Monte Carlo standard error of the mean of 10,000 exponential draws is about 1%. Repeated FALSE results point to a sampling error." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mean of many sampled times" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DES-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mean-of-many-sampled-times" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AVERAGE(SampledTimes)*Rate-1)<0.02" .

hemo:7000448 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant hazard of 0.15 per year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With U of 0.30 and a hazard of 0.15 per year, the sampled time to the event is about 8.0265 years." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant hazard of 0.15 per year" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U = 0.30; lambda_j = 0.15; T_j = 8.0265" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DES-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-hazard-of-0-15-per-year" .

hemo:7000449 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Median draw at a hazard of 0.10 per year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A draw of U equal to 0.50 returns the median of the distribution, about 6.9315 years at a hazard of 0.10 per year, which is ln 2 divided by the hazard." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Median draw at a hazard of 0.10 per year" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U = 0.50; lambda_j = 0.10; T_j = 6.9315" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DES-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "median-draw-at-a-hazard-of-0-10-per-year" .

hemo:7000450 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weibull parameterisation stated"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "beta and gamma follow the survival function S(t) = exp(-(t/beta)^gamma). Fitted parameters reported in another parameterisation are converted first." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weibull parameterisation stated" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DES-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weibull-parameterisation-stated" .

hemo:7000451 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Sampling from time zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The formula samples a time from the origin of the fitted curve. Sampling a remaining time for a patient who has already survived to time a, with a rising or falling hazard, requires sampling conditional on survival to a." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sampling from time zero" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DES-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sampling-from-time-zero" .

hemo:7000452 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Weibull time to event in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000226 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel samples from named cells holding the scale and shape parameters." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weibull time to event in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DES-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weibull-time-to-event-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Scale*(-LN(1-RAND()))^(1/Shape)" .

hemo:7000453 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Survival at the sampled time equals the draw"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Evaluate the fitted survival function at the sampled time. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Survival at the sampled time equals the draw" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DES-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "survival-at-the-sampled-time-equals-the-draw" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(EXP(-(SampledTime/Scale)^Shape)-UniformDraw)<1E-9" .

hemo:7000454 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Rising hazard with shape 1.5"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With U of 0.30, a scale of 10 years and a shape of 1.5, the sampled time is about 11.3173 years. The fitted survival function at that time equals 0.30." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rising hazard with shape 1.5" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U = 0.30; beta = 10; gamma = 1.5; T = 11.3173" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DES-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rising-hazard-with-shape-1-5" .

hemo:7000455 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Shape of 1 reduces to the exponential"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the same draw and scale and a shape of 1, the sampled time is about 12.0397 years, identical to the exponential formula with a hazard of 0.10 per year." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Shape of 1 reduces to the exponential" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U = 0.30; beta = 10; gamma = 1; T = 12.0397" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DES-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "shape-of-1-reduces-to-the-exponential" .

hemo:7000456 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Stable system over the observation window"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Arrivals, capacity and service rules do not shift during the observation period, and the system is not in a warm-up phase. The law does not apply mechanically to a transient system." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Stable system over the observation window" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DES-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "stable-system-over-the-observation-window" .

hemo:7000457 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Consistent definitions of the system"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "L, lambda and W refer to the same boundary, for example waiting and service together, and use the same time unit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Consistent definitions of the system" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DES-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "consistent-definitions-of-the-system" .

hemo:7000458 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Little's law comparison in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000227 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel returns the relative gap between the simulated time-average number in the system and the value implied by Little's law, using named cells." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Little's law comparison in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DES-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "little-s-law-comparison-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SimulatedL-ArrivalRate*SimulatedW)/SimulatedL" .

hemo:7000459 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Simulated queue against Little's law"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Compute the relative gap after the warm-up period. Expected result: a gap within the Monte Carlo error of the run, for example below 5%. A larger gap points to an incorrect observation window, missed entities or inconsistent units." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Simulated queue against Little's law" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DES-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "simulated-queue-against-little-s-law" .

hemo:7000460 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Diagnostic service with 18 arrivals per day"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative diagnostic service, 18 patients arrive per day and the simulation estimates an average time in the system of 0.30 days, so about 18 × 0.30 = 5.4 patients should be in the system on average." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Diagnostic service with 18 arrivals per day" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 18; W = 0.30; L = 5.4" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DES-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "diagnostic-service-with-18-arrivals-per-day" .

hemo:7000461 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Absorbing chain"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "At least one state is absorbing and every transient state can reach an absorbing state, directly or through other states. Then Q raised to the power n tends to zero, the whole cohort is eventually absorbed and I minus Q can be inverted." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absorbing chain" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ABS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absorbing-chain" .

hemo:7000462 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Time-homogeneous transition matrix"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Q is the same in every cycle. A model whose probabilities change with age or cycle, such as one using life-table background mortality, has no single fundamental matrix, and its expected time before absorption comes from summing the cohort trace." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Time-homogeneous transition matrix" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ABS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "time-homogeneous-transition-matrix" .

hemo:7000463 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Counting convention"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The starting cycle is counted, so the result equals the sum over all cycles of the proportion outside the absorbing states at the start of each cycle. It applies no half-cycle correction and no discounting." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Counting convention" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ABS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "counting-convention" .

hemo:7000464 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected cycles before absorption in Excel"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000228 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the transient block in the named range TransientQ, Excel 365 returns the column t_abs as a dynamic array. MUNIT builds the identity matrix and SEQUENCE builds the column of ones." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected cycles before absorption in Excel" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ABS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-cycles-before-absorption-in-excel" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MMULT(MINVERSE(MUNIT(ROWS(TransientQ))-TransientQ),SEQUENCE(ROWS(TransientQ),1,1,0))" .

hemo:7000465 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement with a long cohort trace"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Run the cohort trace from everyone in Well until fewer than 1 in 1,000,000 remain alive and sum the Well and Sick proportions over all cycles, starting at cycle 0. Expected result: 10 to four decimal places, matching the Well entry of t_abs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Agreement with a long cohort trace" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ABS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "agreement-with-a-long-cohort-trace" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(SUM(WellColumn)+SUM(SickColumn),4)=10" .

hemo:7000466 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Absorbing row in the transition matrix"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For the row of each state intended to be absorbing, check that the diagonal entry is 1 and the row sums to 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE means that people can leave the state or the row leaks." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absorbing row in the transition matrix" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ABS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absorbing-row-in-the-transition-matrix" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(INDEX(TransitionMatrix,DeadRow,DeadRow)=1,SUM(INDEX(TransitionMatrix,DeadRow,0))=1)" .

hemo:7000467 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three-state Well, Sick and Dead model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Using the article's matrix, 85% of Well stay Well, 10% become Sick and 5% die each cycle, and 80% of Sick stay Sick and 20% die. The transient block is Q = [[0.85,0.10],[0,0.80]], and the expected number of cycles before death is 10 from Well and 5 from Sick." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three-state Well, Sick and Dead model" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q = [[0.85,0.10],[0,0.80]]; I = [[1,0],[0,1]]; c = [1,1]; t_abs = [10,5]" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ABS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-state-well-sick-and-dead-model" .

hemo:7000468 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Absorbing chain with a time-homogeneous matrix"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "As for the expected time before absorption, every transient state can reach an absorbing state and Q and R do not change between cycles." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absorbing chain with a time-homogeneous matrix" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ABS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absorbing-chain-with-a-time-homogeneous-matrix" .

hemo:7000469 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Absorption probabilities in Excel"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000229 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the transient block in TransientQ and the transient to absorbing block in AbsorbR, Excel 365 returns B as a dynamic array." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absorption probabilities in Excel" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ABS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absorption-probabilities-in-excel" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MMULT(MINVERSE(MUNIT(ROWS(TransientQ))-TransientQ),AbsorbR)" .

hemo:7000470 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Absorption probabilities sum to one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Sum each row of B. Expected result: every row equals 1, because absorption is certain in an absorbing chain." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absorption probabilities sum to one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ABS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absorption-probabilities-sum-to-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUM(INDEX(AbsorptionB,RowNumber,0))" .

hemo:7000471 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two death states in the Well and Sick model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The article's Dead state is split into death from other causes and death from the disease. Well people die only of other causes, at 5% a cycle; Sick people die of other causes at 5% and of the disease at 15% a cycle. Starting in Well, half of the cohort eventually dies of each cause; starting in Sick, 25% die of other causes and 75% of the disease. The split of Sick mortality is illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two death states in the Well and Sick model" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q = [[0.85,0.10],[0,0.80]]; I = [[1,0],[0,1]]; R = [[0.05,0],[0.05,0.15]]; B = [[0.5,0.5],[0.25,0.75]]" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ABS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-death-states-in-the-well-and-sick-model" .

hemo:7000472 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Closed cohort with complete follow-up"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every person counted in N is followed to the end of the period or to the event. When people are lost to follow-up or censored, dividing by N understates the risk, and a survival method such as the Kaplan-Meier estimator is used instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Closed cohort with complete follow-up" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-AR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "closed-cohort-with-complete-follow-up" .

hemo:7000473 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Risk stated with its period"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "R applies only to the period over which E was counted. A one-year risk and a five-year risk for the same cohort are different quantities, and the period is reported with every risk." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Risk stated with its period" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-AR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "risk-stated-with-its-period" .

hemo:7000474 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Numerator contained in the denominator"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "E counts only new events among the people in N, so R cannot exceed 1. N excludes people who already have the condition or cannot have it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Numerator contained in the denominator" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-AR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "numerator-contained-in-the-denominator" .

hemo:7000475 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Absolute risk from named counts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000230 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel divides the event count by the number at risk and returns #N/A when the denominator is not positive." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absolute risk from named counts" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-AR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absolute-risk-from-named-counts" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(AtRisk>0,Events/AtRisk,NA())" .

hemo:7000476 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Risk lies between zero and one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Check that the event count does not exceed the number at risk and that the risk lies in the unit interval. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows events counted outside the cohort or a person-time denominator used by mistake." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Risk lies between zero and one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-AR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "risk-lies-between-zero-and-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(Events>=0,Events<=AtRisk,Risk>=0,Risk<=1)" .

hemo:7000477 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "One-year risk of myocardial infarction"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A cohort of 2,000 people is followed for one year with no loss to follow-up, and 120 have a myocardial infarction. The one-year absolute risk is 0.06, as in the article. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One-year risk of myocardial infarction" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E = 120; N = 2000; R = 0.06" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-AR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-year-risk-of-myocardial-infarction" .

hemo:7000478 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Thirteen-year risk of death in a diabetic cohort"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the CDC teaching example, 100 of 189 diabetic men died during 13 years of follow-up, a 13-year risk of about 0.529. The risk describes the whole 13 years and is not an annual figure." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Thirteen-year risk of death in a diabetic cohort" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E = 100; N = 189; R = 0.529" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-AR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "thirteen-year-risk-of-death-in-a-diabetic-cohort" .

hemo:7000479 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Food-specific attack rate in an outbreak"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the CDC outbreak example, 30 of the 99 people who ate potato salad developed gastroenteritis, a risk of about 0.303 over the outbreak period." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Food-specific attack rate in an outbreak" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E = 30; N = 99; R = 0.303" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-AR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "food-specific-attack-rate-in-an-outbreak" .

hemo:7000480 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same outcome, population and period in both arms"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both risks refer to the same event definition, the same randomised population and the same follow-up period. An ARR is reported with that period, because events accrue and the ARR changes as follow-up lengthens." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same outcome, population and period in both arms" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ARR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-outcome-population-and-period-in-both-arms" .

hemo:7000481 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Adverse outcome orientation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The event is one the intervention aims to prevent. For a beneficial outcome, such as response, the subtraction is reversed so that a benefit remains positive." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Adverse outcome orientation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ARR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "adverse-outcome-orientation" .

hemo:7000482 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Absolute risk reduction from event counts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000231 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With comparator events and totals in ComparatorEvents and ComparatorN, and intervention events and totals in InterventionEvents and InterventionN, Excel returns the ARR." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absolute risk reduction from event counts" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ARR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absolute-risk-reduction-from-event-counts" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ComparatorEvents/ComparatorN-InterventionEvents/InterventionN" .

hemo:7000483 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement with the Cochrane risk difference"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Add the ARR to the risk difference computed as intervention risk minus comparator risk. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a reversed subtraction in one of the two cells." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Agreement with the Cochrane risk difference" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ARR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "agreement-with-the-cochrane-risk-difference" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ARR+(InterventionRisk-ComparatorRisk))<1E-12" .

hemo:7000484 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "OSIRIS trial reported in CONSORT 2010"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Death or oxygen dependence occurred in 514 of 1,346 infants with delayed selective surfactant and 429 of 1,344 with early administration, risks of about 0.38187 and 0.31920. The ARR of 0.06267 matches the risk difference of minus 6.3 per cent reported in the CONSORT 2010 explanation for item 17b." ;
    hemo:9000009 "OSIRIS trial reported in CONSORT 2010" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_C = 0.38187; p_I = 0.31920; ARR = 0.06267" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ARR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "osiris-trial-reported-in-consort-2010" .

hemo:7000485 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Relative risk constant across baseline risk"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The relative risk estimated in the trials holds at the baseline risk of the target population. The assumption is stated and, where evidence allows, tested across risk groups." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Relative risk constant across baseline risk" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ARR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "relative-risk-constant-across-baseline-risk" .

hemo:7000486 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Baseline risk and relative risk over the same period"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "p_C and RR refer to the same outcome and time horizon. The Cochrane Handbook recommends computing the ARR for a range of assumed comparator risks." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Baseline risk and relative risk over the same period" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ARR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "baseline-risk-and-relative-risk-over-the-same-period" .

hemo:7000487 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Absolute and relative risk reduction in two cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000232 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the assumed comparator risk in BaselineRisk and the relative risk in RelativeRisk, the two formulas return the ARR and the relative risk reduction." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absolute and relative risk reduction in two cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ARR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absolute-and-relative-risk-reduction-in-two-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=BaselineRisk*(1-RelativeRisk); =1-RelativeRisk" .

hemo:7000488 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "ARR equals the baseline risk times the RRR"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Multiply the baseline risk by the relative risk reduction and compare with the ARR. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that the relative risk and its reduction have been confused." ;
    hemo:9000009 "ARR equals the baseline risk times the RRR" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ARR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "arr-equals-the-baseline-risk-times-the-rrr" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(BaselineRisk*RRR-ARR)<1E-12" .

hemo:7000489 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "High-risk group with a relative risk of 0.75"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000490,
        hemo:7000491 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000492,
        hemo:7000493 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A relative risk of 0.75 applied to a five-year baseline risk of 0.20 gives an ARR of 0.05 and a relative risk reduction of 0.25, as in the article's high-risk group. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "High-risk group with a relative risk of 0.75" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_C = 0.20; RR = 0.75; ARR = 0.05; RRR = 0.25" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ARR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "high-risk-group-with-a-relative-risk-of-0-75" .

hemo:7000490 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "p_C in the test High-risk group with a relative risk of 0.75"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000726 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.2 .

hemo:7000491 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "RR in the test High-risk group with a relative risk of 0.75"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000727 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.75 .

hemo:7000492 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "ARR in the test High-risk group with a relative risk of 0.75"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000724 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.05 .

hemo:7000493 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "RRR in the test High-risk group with a relative risk of 0.75"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000725 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.25 .

hemo:7000494 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cochrane Handbook example with a relative risk of 0.92"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000495,
        hemo:7000496 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000497,
        hemo:7000498 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A risk ratio of 0.92 and an assumed comparator risk of 0.3 give an ARR of 0.024, or 24 fewer events per 1,000, as in section 15.4.4.2 of the Cochrane Handbook." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cochrane Handbook example with a relative risk of 0.92" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_C = 0.3; RR = 0.92; ARR = 0.024; RRR = 0.08" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ARR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cochrane-handbook-example-with-a-relative-risk-of-0-92" .

hemo:7000495 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "p_C in the test Cochrane Handbook example with a relative risk of 0.92"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000726 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.3 .

hemo:7000496 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "RR in the test Cochrane Handbook example with a relative risk of 0.92"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000727 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.92 .

hemo:7000497 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "ARR in the test Cochrane Handbook example with a relative risk of 0.92"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000724 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.024 .

hemo:7000498 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "RRR in the test Cochrane Handbook example with a relative risk of 0.92"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6000725 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.08 .

hemo:7000499 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Benefit direction and an interval that excludes zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A positive ARR gives the number needed to treat for an additional beneficial outcome (NNTB); a negative ARR gives, in absolute value, the number needed to treat for an additional harmful outcome (NNTH). The limits apply directly when both ARR limits are positive. When the ARR interval includes zero, the NNT interval passes through infinity and is reported as running from NNTH through infinity to NNTB." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Benefit direction and an interval that excludes zero" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ARR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "benefit-direction-and-an-interval-that-excludes-zero" .

hemo:7000500 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Period and comparator risk attached to the NNT"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The NNT refers to the follow-up period of the ARR. Limits derived from a pooled relative effect and an assumed comparator risk do not include uncertainty in that comparator risk." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Period and comparator risk attached to the NNT" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ARR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "period-and-comparator-risk-attached-to-the-nnt" .

hemo:7000501 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Reported NNT and limits"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000233 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel rounds the reciprocal of the absolute ARR up to the next whole number and labels it from the sign of the ARR; the limits are returned only when the ARR interval lies wholly above zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reported NNT and limits" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ARR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reported-nnt-and-limits" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(ARR=0,NA(),ROUNDUP(1/ABS(ARR),0)); =IF(ARR>0,\"NNTB\",\"NNTH\"); =IF(ARRLower>0,1/ARRUpper,NA()); =IF(ARRLower>0,1/ARRLower,NA())" .

hemo:7000502 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reciprocal check on the reported NNT"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Confirm that the reported whole number is the smallest integer not below 1 divided by the absolute ARR. Expected result: TRUE for an NNT of 42 at an ARR of 0.024, as in the Cochrane Handbook risk ratio example. FALSE shows rounding to the nearest whole number or down." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reciprocal check on the reported NNT" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ARR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reciprocal-check-on-the-reported-nnt" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ReportedNNT>=1/ABS(ARR),ReportedNNT-1<1/ABS(ARR))" .

hemo:7000503 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Point estimate inside the NNT interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When both ARR limits are positive, confirm that the NNT lies between its limits. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows limits left in their original order." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Point estimate inside the NNT interval" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ARR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "point-estimate-inside-the-nnt-interval" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(NNTLower<=NNT,NNT<=NNTUpper)" .

hemo:7000504 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Altman example with an ARR of 10 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An ARR of 0.10 with a 95% confidence interval of 0.05 to 0.15 gives an NNT of 10 with a 95% confidence interval of about 6.67 to 20, as in Altman (1998)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Altman example with an ARR of 10 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "ARR = 0.10; ARR_L = 0.05; ARR_U = 0.15; NNT = 10; NNT_L = 6.67; NNT_U = 20" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ARR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "altman-example-with-an-arr-of-10-per-cent" .

hemo:7000505 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "OSIRIS trial NNT and interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An ARR of 0.06267 with a 95% confidence interval of 0.027 to 0.099, from the CONSORT 2010 example, gives about 15.96, reported as 16 infants treated early to prevent one death or case of oxygen dependence, with an interval of about 10.10 to 37.04." ;
    hemo:9000009 "OSIRIS trial NNT and interval" ;
    hemo:9000014 "ARR = 0.06267; ARR_L = 0.027; ARR_U = 0.099; NNT = 15.96; NNT_L = 10.10; NNT_U = 37.04" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ARR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "osiris-trial-nnt-and-interval" .

hemo:7000506 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Transitivity across the two sets of trials"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The A versus B and A versus C trials are similar in the distribution of effect modifiers such as severity, line of treatment and outcome timing, so that participants could in principle have been randomised to any of the three treatments." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Transitivity across the two sets of trials" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "transitivity-across-the-two-sets-of-trials" .

hemo:7000507 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Independent sources of direct evidence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "d_AB and d_AC come from different trials. When a three-arm trial contributes to both, the two estimates are correlated and the variance sum understates uncertainty; the covariance is then modelled, for example in a full network meta-analysis." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Independent sources of direct evidence" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "independent-sources-of-direct-evidence" .

hemo:7000508 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Additive scale and one direction convention"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Effects are combined on a scale where they add, such as the mean difference, log odds ratio, log risk ratio or log hazard ratio, and every contrast uses the same direction. The article's indirect-comparison section writes d_XY as X relative to Y; the relation d_AC = d_AB + d_BC holds under either convention if it is applied throughout." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Additive scale and one direction convention" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "additive-scale-and-one-direction-convention" .

hemo:7000509 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Indirect estimate and variance in two cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000234 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the direct log odds ratios in dAC and dAB and their standard errors in seAC and seAB, the two formulas return the indirect estimate and its variance." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Indirect estimate and variance in two cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-NMA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "indirect-estimate-and-variance-in-two-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=dAC-dAB; =seAC^2+seAB^2" .

hemo:7000510 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reproducing TSD 4 Box 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Enter 1.42 and 2.79 with standard errors 0.34 and 0.56. Expected result: an indirect log odds ratio of minus 1.37 and a variance of about 0.429. A value of plus 1.37 shows the subtraction reversed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reproducing TSD 4 Box 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-NMA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reproducing-tsd-4-box-1" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1.42-2.79; =0.34^2+0.56^2" .

hemo:7000511 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "HIV example in NICE DSU TSD 4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Direct log odds ratios of 2.79 (standard error 0.56) for B against A and 1.42 (standard error 0.34) for C against A give an indirect log odds ratio for C against B of minus 1.37 with variance 0.4292, as in Box 1 of TSD 4." ;
    hemo:9000009 "HIV example in NICE DSU TSD 4" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_AC = 1.42; d_AB = 2.79; V_AC = 0.1156; V_AB = 0.3136; d_BC = -1.37; V_BC = 0.4292" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-NMA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hiv-example-in-nice-dsu-tsd-4" .

hemo:7000512 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two odds ratios against placebo"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Odds ratios of 0.70 for B and 0.50 for C against placebo A, with standard errors on the log scale of 0.15 and 0.20, give an indirect log odds ratio of about minus 0.3364 for C against B with variance 0.0625, an odds ratio of about 0.714, the same as 0.50 divided by 0.70. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two odds ratios against placebo" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_AC = -0.6931; d_AB = -0.3567; V_AC = 0.04; V_AB = 0.0225; d_BC = -0.3364; V_BC = 0.0625" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-NMA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-odds-ratios-against-placebo" .

hemo:7000513 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Approximate normality on the log scale"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The indirect log odds ratio is approximately normally distributed, so a 95% interval is the estimate plus or minus 1.96 standard errors on the log scale." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Approximate normality on the log scale" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "approximate-normality-on-the-log-scale" .

hemo:7000514 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Indirect odds ratio and limits in three cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000235 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the indirect log odds ratio in dBC and its variance in VBC, the three formulas return the odds ratio and its 95% limits." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Indirect odds ratio and limits in three cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-NMA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "indirect-odds-ratio-and-limits-in-three-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EXP(dBC); =EXP(dBC-1.96*SQRT(VBC)); =EXP(dBC+1.96*SQRT(VBC))" .

hemo:7000515 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Log-scale symmetry of the interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The odds ratio is the geometric mean of its limits. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows limits built on the odds ratio scale." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log-scale symmetry of the interval" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-NMA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-scale-symmetry-of-the-interval" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ORBC-SQRT(ORBCLower*ORBCUpper))<1E-9" .

hemo:7000516 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Back-transforming the TSD 4 indirect estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An indirect log odds ratio of minus 1.37 with variance 0.4292 gives an odds ratio of about 0.2541 with a 95% confidence interval of about 0.0704 to 0.9177." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Back-transforming the TSD 4 indirect estimate" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_BC = -1.37; V_BC = 0.4292; OR_BC = 0.2541; OR_BC_L = 0.0704; OR_BC_U = 0.9177" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-NMA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "back-transforming-the-tsd-4-indirect-estimate" .

hemo:7000517 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Back-transforming the placebo-anchored example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An indirect log odds ratio of minus 0.3364 with variance 0.0625 gives an odds ratio of about 0.7143 with a 95% confidence interval of about 0.4376 to 1.1660, so the indirect evidence is compatible with no difference between B and C." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Back-transforming the placebo-anchored example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_BC = -0.3364; V_BC = 0.0625; OR_BC = 0.7143; OR_BC_L = 0.4376; OR_BC_U = 1.1660" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-NMA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "back-transforming-the-placebo-anchored-example" .

hemo:7000518 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Three independent sources of evidence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The three direct estimates come from separate sets of trials. Three-arm trials are excluded from the test because they are internally consistent and would dilute any disagreement." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three independent sources of evidence" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-independent-sources-of-evidence" .

hemo:7000519 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Inconsistency, variance, z and two-sided p value"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000236 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the direct and indirect estimates and variances in named cells, the four formulas return omega, its variance, z and the two-sided p value." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Inconsistency, variance, z and two-sided p value" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-NMA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "inconsistency-variance-z-and-two-sided-p-value" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=dBCdir-dBCind; =VBCdir+VBCind; =Omega/SQRT(VarOmega); =2*(1-NORM.S.DIST(ABS(Zstat),TRUE))" .

hemo:7000520 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reproducing the TSD 4 z statistic"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Enter the Box 1 figures. Expected result: about 2.78. A value of about minus 1.36 shows the indirect estimate formed as d_AB minus d_AC, reversing its sign." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reproducing the TSD 4 z statistic" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-NMA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reproducing-the-tsd-4-z-statistic" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(0.47-(1.42-2.79))/SQRT(0.1^2+0.56^2+0.34^2)" .

hemo:7000521 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Inconsistency in the TSD 4 HIV loop"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A direct log odds ratio of 0.47 (standard error 0.10) for C against B, compared with the indirect estimate of minus 1.37 (variance 0.4292), gives an inconsistency of 1.84 with variance 0.4392 and z of about 2.78, evidence of inconsistency with p below 0.01, as in Box 1 of TSD 4." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Inconsistency in the TSD 4 HIV loop" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_BC_dir = 0.47; d_BC_ind = -1.37; V_BC_dir = 0.01; V_BC_ind = 0.4292; omega = 1.84; V_omega = 0.4392; z = 2.78" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-NMA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "inconsistency-in-the-tsd-4-hiv-loop" .

hemo:7000522 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Separate baseline model and additivity on the logit scale"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The baseline probability comes from evidence relevant to the target population and is not counted again as relative-effect evidence. The treatment effect is constant on the log odds scale across baseline risks; models linear in log risk ratios or log hazard rates use the corresponding transformation instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Separate baseline model and additivity on the logit scale" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-NMA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "separate-baseline-model-and-additivity-on-the-logit-scale" .

hemo:7000523 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment probability from a baseline and a log odds ratio"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000237 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the baseline probability in BaselineProb and the network log odds ratio in LogOR, Excel adds the effect on the logit scale and converts back." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Treatment probability from a baseline and a log odds ratio" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-NMA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "treatment-probability-from-a-baseline-and-a-log-odds-ratio" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1/(1+EXP(-(LN(BaselineProb/(1-BaselineProb))+LogOR)))" .

hemo:7000524 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Odds ratio recovered from the two probabilities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Divide the odds of p_k by the odds of p_0. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the odds ratio applied as a risk ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Odds ratio recovered from the two probabilities" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-NMA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "odds-ratio-recovered-from-the-two-probabilities" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((TreatProb/(1-TreatProb))/(BaselineProb/(1-BaselineProb))-OddsRatio)<1E-9" .

hemo:7000525 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Baseline probability of 0.25 and an odds ratio of 0.8"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A probability of 0.25 on standard care and an odds ratio of 0.8 give a treatment probability of about 0.2105, reported as 0.21 in the introduction of TSD 5." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Baseline probability of 0.25 and an odds ratio of 0.8" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_0 = 0.25; OR_k = 0.8; p_k = 0.2105" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-NMA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "baseline-probability-of-0-25-and-an-odds-ratio-of-0-8" .

hemo:7000526 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same population, starting point and discounting"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Q_h and Q_c describe the same starting age and sex mix, from the point in the pathway where the technology is considered, over the remaining lifetime, discounted at the reference-case rate of 3.5% a year. The DSU guide applies this rate even where the committee accepts another rate for the cost-effectiveness analysis." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same population, starting point and discounting" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ASF-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-population-starting-point-and-discounting" .

hemo:7000527 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Carer QALYs excluded"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Carer quality of life included in the model's QALYs is removed before the calculation, both from Q_c and from the incremental QALYs that attract a weight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Carer QALYs excluded" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ASF-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "carer-qalys-excluded" .

hemo:7000528 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Value set for population norms"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "For topics starting after 27 August 2026 (in technology appraisals, an invitation to participate issued after that date) the EQ-5D-5L value set is used for both the model utilities and the general-population norms behind Q_h. Ongoing topics started earlier continue to use EQ-5D-3L values, and the cut-offs are unchanged." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Value set for population norms" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ASF-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "value-set-for-population-norms" .

hemo:7000529 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Shortfall measures in two cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000238 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the general-population QALYs in QALYsGeneral and the condition QALYs in QALYsCondition, the two formulas return absolute and proportional shortfall." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Shortfall measures in two cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ASF-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "shortfall-measures-in-two-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=QALYsGeneral-QALYsCondition; =(QALYsGeneral-QALYsCondition)/QALYsGeneral" .

hemo:7000530 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Shortfalls within their normal ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Check that absolute shortfall is at least 0 and at most the general-population QALYs, and that proportional shortfall is at least 0 and at most 1. Expected result TRUE. FALSE flags undiscounted or mismatched inputs, or negative condition QALYs, which TSD 23 notes are possible but unlikely." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Shortfalls within their normal ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ASF-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "shortfalls-within-their-normal-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(AbsShortfall>=0,AbsShortfall<=QALYsGeneral,PropShortfall>=0,PropShortfall<=1)" .

hemo:7000531 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "DSU hypothetical case with EQ-5D-3L norms"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7000532,
        hemo:7000533 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7000534,
        hemo:7000535 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.0005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A population aged 62, 33% female, has 11.96 discounted general-population QALYs, the sex-weighted average of 11.86 for males and 12.16 for females, and 6.031 under current care. Absolute shortfall is about 5.93 and proportional shortfall about 0.50, as in section 5.1 of TSD 23. Both fall below the lowest cut-offs, so the weight is 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "DSU hypothetical case with EQ-5D-3L norms" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q_h = 11.96; Q_c = 6.031; AS = 5.929; PS = 0.496" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ASF-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "dsu-hypothetical-case-with-eq-5d-3l-norms" .

