hemo:7000546 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Period life table and population utility norms"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Survival comes from national period life tables, for which the DSU guide recommends England 2017 to 2019 at the time of writing, and utility from general-population survey norms under the value set in use." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Period life table and population utility norms" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ASF-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "period-life-table-and-population-utility-norms" .

hemo:7000547 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Deaths spread evenly within each year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "L_t is the mean of the proportions alive at the start and end of year t, a half-cycle correction that assumes deaths occur evenly through the year." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Deaths spread evenly within each year" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ASF-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "deaths-spread-evenly-within-each-year" .

hemo:7000548 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Life-table QALYs in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000239 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With years lived in LifeYears, utility norms in Utilities and the year index from 0 in YearIndex, all in columns of equal length, Excel returns the discounted QALYs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Life-table QALYs in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ASF-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "life-table-qalys-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(LifeYears,Utilities/(1+DiscountRate)^YearIndex)" .

hemo:7000549 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted QALYs below life expectancy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Check that the result is positive and no greater than the sum of years lived. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows utilities above 1 or survivors entered as counts from a life table radix, such as 100,000, rather than as proportions." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted QALYs below life expectancy" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ASF-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-qalys-below-life-expectancy" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(QALYsSex>0,QALYsSex<=SUM(LifeYears))" .

hemo:7000550 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three-year illustration of the life-table sum"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With proportions alive of 1, 0.98, 0.95 and 0.91 at the start of successive years, L_t is 0.99, 0.965 and 0.93 for t of 0, 1 and 2. With utility norms U_t of 0.85, 0.84 and 0.83 and a 3.5% rate, the three years contribute 0.8415, 0.7832 and 0.7206, about 2.3453 QALYs in all. The per-year values are given in this text and the calculator line holds only the scalar inputs and the result, so the example is for reading against HE-IM-ASF-002. The table is illustrative and truncated; a real calculation runs to age 100." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three-year illustration of the life-table sum" ;
    hemo:9000014 "T = 2; r = 0.035; Q_hs = 2.3453" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ASF-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-year-illustration-of-the-life-table-sum" .

hemo:7000551 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Scope of the severity weight and judgement near cut-offs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weight applies in technology appraisals. PMG36 does not apply it to highly specialised technologies, has not initially applied it to technology appraisals of HealthTech and considers it unlikely to be relevant in diagnostics. Shortfall estimates are uncertain, and the DSU guide notes that judgement is needed when an estimate lies close to a cut-off." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Scope of the severity weight and judgement near cut-offs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ASF-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "scope-of-the-severity-weight-and-judgement-near-cut-offs" .

hemo:7000552 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weight on the QALY gain only"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weight multiplies the incremental QALYs of the technology, not the health forgone elsewhere, so a weight of 1.7 is equivalent to judging the unweighted ICER against £42,500 to £59,500 rather than £25,000 to £35,000. PMG36 asks for net health benefit at £25,000 and £35,000 per QALY both with and without the weight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weight on the QALY gain only" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ASF-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weight-on-the-qaly-gain-only" .

hemo:7000553 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Severity weight in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000240 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With absolute and proportional shortfall in AbsShortfall and PropShortfall, Excel returns the weight from table 6.1 of PMG36. Name the result cell SeverityWeight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Severity weight in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ASF-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "severity-weight-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(OR(AbsShortfall>=18,PropShortfall>=0.95),1.7,IF(OR(AbsShortfall>=12,PropShortfall>=0.85),1.2,1))" .

hemo:7000554 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cut-off values take the higher band"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Enter an absolute shortfall of exactly 12 in AbsShortfall and a proportional shortfall of 0.5 in PropShortfall, and check the SeverityWeight cell of HE-IM-ASF-003. Expected result TRUE. FALSE with a weight of 1 shows a strict inequality at the cut-off, and FALSE also shows other inputs in the two cells." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cut-off values take the higher band" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ASF-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cut-off-values-take-the-higher-band" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(AbsShortfall=12,PropShortfall=0.5,SeverityWeight=1.2)" .

