hemo:7001999 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Costs of attracting the risk mix not deducted"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Advertising, benefit design and other screening costs are not subtracted, so the result is an upper bound on the net gain from selection." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Costs of attracting the risk mix not deducted" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CSKM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "costs-of-attracting-the-risk-mix-not-deducted" .

hemo:7002000 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected profit per member and in total from a risk mix in two Excel cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000439 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the payment in Payment, the plan's shares by risk group in MixShare, the expected cost of each group in GroupCost and the number of members in Members, the first formula returns the profit per member and the second the total." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected profit per member and in total from a risk mix in two Excel cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CSKM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-profit-per-member-and-in-total-from-a-risk-mix-in-two-excel-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Payment-SUMPRODUCT(MixShare,GroupCost); =Members*(Payment-SUMPRODUCT(MixShare,GroupCost))" .

hemo:7002001 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Enrolled risk-mix shares sum to one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The plan's shares of members across the risk groups add to 1. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Enrolled risk-mix shares sum to one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CSKM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "enrolled-risk-mix-shares-sum-to-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUM(MixShare)-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002002 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Total risk-mix profit in the article's cream-skimming example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A plan of 1,000 members with an 80% healthy mix expects £500,000. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Total risk-mix profit in the article's cream-skimming example" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CSKM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "total-risk-mix-profit-in-the-article-s-cream-skimming-example" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(1000*(5000-SUMPRODUCT({0.8,0.2},{3500,8500})),0)=500000" .

hemo:7002003 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Risk-mix profit is zero at the payment cell's own mix"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When the payment equals the cell's average expected cost, a plan with the cell's mix expects no profit. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Risk-mix profit is zero at the payment cell's own mix" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CSKM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "risk-mix-profit-is-zero-at-the-payment-cell-s-own-mix" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(5000-SUMPRODUCT({0.7,0.3},{3500,8500}),6)=0" .

hemo:7002004 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Plan enrolling 80% healthy 70-year-olds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's example a plan whose 1,000 members aged 70 are 80% healthy and 20% chronically ill has an expected cost per member of £2,800 plus £1,700, or £4,500. Against the £5,000 payment it expects £500 per member and £500,000 in total." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Plan enrolling 80% healthy 70-year-olds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "R = 5000; m_k = [0.8,0.2]; EC_k = [3500,8500]; N = 1000; pi_bar = 500; Pi = 500000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CSKM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "plan-enrolling-80-healthy-70-year-olds" .

hemo:7002005 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Plan enrolling the payment cell's own risk mix"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the population mix of 70% healthy and 30% chronically ill, the average expected cost equals the £5,000 payment and the plan expects to break even, as the article's payment was set to match the age group's average." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Plan enrolling the payment cell's own risk mix" ;
    hemo:9000014 "R = 5000; m_k = [0.7,0.3]; EC_k = [3500,8500]; N = 1000; pi_bar = 0; Pi = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CSKM-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "plan-enrolling-the-payment-cell-s-own-risk-mix" .

hemo:7002006 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Plan enrolling only healthy 70-year-olds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A plan that enrolled only members without a chronic condition would expect £1,500 per member and £1,500,000 in total for 1,000 members, the largest gain available in this payment cell, computed here for illustration." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Plan enrolling only healthy 70-year-olds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "R = 5000; m_k = [1,0]; EC_k = [3500,8500]; N = 1000; pi_bar = 1500; Pi = 1500000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CSKM-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "plan-enrolling-only-healthy-70-year-olds" .

hemo:7002007 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Groups defined by the actions plans can take"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The groups are those a plan can affect through its own actions in the market concerned, for example through its network or benefit design, as Layton and colleagues recommend. A group no plan action can reach says little about selection incentives." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Groups defined by the actions plans can take" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CSKM-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "groups-defined-by-the-actions-plans-can-take" .

hemo:7002008 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Payments and costs for the same members and period"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both measures compare the payments generated by the payment formula with the costs of the same members over the same period, so the difference and the ratio describe the same group." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Payments and costs for the same members and period" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CSKM-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "payments-and-costs-for-the-same-members-and-period" .

hemo:7002009 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive average cost for the predictive ratio"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The ratio is undefined when the group's average cost is zero; the difference measure remains defined." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive average cost for the predictive ratio" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CSKM-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-average-cost-for-the-predictive-ratio" .

hemo:7002010 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Over- or undercompensation and predictive ratio from member records in two Excel cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000440 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the payments for the group's members in a range named GroupPayment and their costs in a range named GroupCost, the first formula returns over- or undercompensation and the second the predictive ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Over- or undercompensation and predictive ratio from member records in two Excel cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CSKM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "over-or-undercompensation-and-predictive-ratio-from-member-records-in-two-excel-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AVERAGE(GroupPayment)-AVERAGE(GroupCost); =SUM(GroupPayment)/SUM(GroupCost)" .

hemo:7002011 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Predictive ratio consistent with over- or undercompensation for a risk group"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The ratio equals 1 plus the difference divided by the average cost. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Predictive ratio consistent with over- or undercompensation for a risk group" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CSKM-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "predictive-ratio-consistent-with-over-or-undercompensation-for-a-risk-group" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PredictiveRatio-(1+OverComp/AvgCost))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002012 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Predictive ratio for chronically ill 70-year-olds in the article"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A payment of £5,000 against a cost of £8,500 gives 0.59 to two decimals. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Predictive ratio for chronically ill 70-year-olds in the article" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CSKM-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "predictive-ratio-for-chronically-ill-70-year-olds-in-the-article" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(5000/8500,2)=0.59" .

hemo:7002013 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Compensation difference and predictive ratio agree on the direction"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A positive difference goes with a ratio above 1, and a negative difference with a ratio below 1. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Compensation difference and predictive ratio agree on the direction" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CSKM-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "compensation-difference-and-predictive-ratio-agree-on-the-direction" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(OverComp>0)=(PredictiveRatio>1)" .

hemo:7002014 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Overcompensation for 70-year-olds without a chronic condition"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's example the £5,000 payment against an expected cost of £3,500 gives overcompensation of £1,500 and a predictive ratio of 5,000 ÷ 3,500 = 1.43." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Overcompensation for 70-year-olds without a chronic condition" ;
    hemo:9000014 "R_g = 5000; C_g = 3500; OC_g = 1500; PR_g = 1.43" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CSKM-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "overcompensation-for-70-year-olds-without-a-chronic-condition" .

hemo:7002015 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Undercompensation for 70-year-olds with a chronic condition"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Against an expected cost of £8,500 the same payment gives undercompensation of £3,500, shown as minus £3,500, and a predictive ratio of 5,000 ÷ 8,500 = 0.59, the article's figures." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Undercompensation for 70-year-olds with a chronic condition" ;
    hemo:9000014 "R_g = 5000; C_g = 8500; OC_g = -3500; PR_g = 0.59" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CSKM-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "undercompensation-for-70-year-olds-with-a-chronic-condition" .

hemo:7002016 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Compensation measures for all 70-year-olds together"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For the age group as a whole the payment equals the average cost of £5,000, so the difference is zero and the ratio is 1, computed here for illustration, although the two subgroups differ by £5,000 per member." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Compensation measures for all 70-year-olds together" ;
    hemo:9000014 "R_g = 5000; C_g = 5000; OC_g = 0; PR_g = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CSKM-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "compensation-measures-for-all-70-year-olds-together" .

hemo:7002017 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Chance-node branches mutually exclusive and exhaustive"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The branches describe outcomes that cannot occur together and that between them cover every possibility, so the branch probabilities sum to one. Treatment failure and a serious adverse event are not mutually exclusive branches if a patient can have both, and a node that omits a possible outcome misstates the expected cost and outcome." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Chance-node branches mutually exclusive and exhaustive" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CHN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "chance-node-branches-mutually-exclusive-and-exhaustive" .

hemo:7002018 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Branch probabilities conditional on the pathway to the node"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each p_j applies to the people who reach the node, given the events before it. A complication probability placed after a treatment-fails branch is the probability among patients whose treatment failed, not the average across all patients." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Branch probabilities conditional on the pathway to the node" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CHN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "branch-probabilities-conditional-on-the-pathway-to-the-node" .

hemo:7002019 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Chance-node values right to left"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Nodes further from the decision are evaluated first, so that C_j and E_j for a branch leading to another chance node are already expected values. The result is the expected value for the average person reaching the node; no individual receives it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Chance-node values right to left" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CHN-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "chance-node-values-right-to-left" .

hemo:7002020 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected cost and QALYs at a chance node in two cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000441 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the branch probabilities, branch costs and branch QALYs in named ranges of equal length, the two formulas return the expected cost and the expected QALYs at the node, in cells named NodeCost and NodeQALYs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected cost and QALYs at a chance node in two cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CHN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-cost-and-qalys-at-a-chance-node-in-two-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(BranchProbs,BranchCosts); =SUMPRODUCT(BranchProbs,BranchQALYs)" .

hemo:7002021 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Chance-node branch probabilities sum to one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Add the probabilities of the branches leaving the node. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a missing or overlapping branch, or a complement that was not updated when one probability changed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Chance-node branch probabilities sum to one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CHN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "chance-node-branch-probabilities-sum-to-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUM(BranchProbs)-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002022 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Chance-node expected cost lies within its branch costs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A probability-weighted average cannot fall below the smallest branch cost or exceed the largest. With the result in NodeCost, the check returns TRUE. FALSE usually means the probabilities do not sum to one." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Chance-node expected cost lies within its branch costs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CHN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "chance-node-expected-cost-lies-within-its-branch-costs" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(NodeCost>=MIN(BranchCosts),NodeCost<=MAX(BranchCosts))" .

hemo:7002023 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article test strategy reproduced at the disease-status node"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Enter the article's disease-status node of the test strategy: BranchProbs 0.2 and 0.8, BranchCosts 2,350 and 600 and BranchQALYs 7.8 and 9.97. The model's NodeCost cell then returns £950 and its NodeQALYs cell 9.536. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows ranges of different lengths or in different branch orders, or a formula that does not weight by the branch probabilities." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article test strategy reproduced at the disease-status node" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CHN-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-test-strategy-reproduced-at-the-disease-status-node" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(NodeCost,2)=950,ROUND(NodeQALYs,3)=9.536)" .

hemo:7002024 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Test-result node among people with the disease"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative test-and-treat example, 90% of people with the disease test positive (cost £2,300, 8.0 QALYs) and 10% test negative (cost £2,800, 6.0 QALYs). The node's expected cost is £2,350 and its expected QALYs are 7.8." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Test-result node among people with the disease" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_j = [0.90, 0.10]; C_j = [2300, 2800]; E_j = [8.0, 6.0]; k = 2; C_n = 2350; E_n = 7.8" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CHN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "test-result-node-among-people-with-the-disease" .

hemo:7002025 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Test-result node among people without the disease"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Among people without the disease, 15% test positive and are treated unnecessarily (cost £2,300, 9.8 QALYs) and 85% test negative (cost £300, 10.0 QALYs). The node's expected cost is £600 and its expected QALYs are 9.97, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Test-result node among people without the disease" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_j = [0.15, 0.85]; C_j = [2300, 300]; E_j = [9.8, 10.0]; k = 2; C_n = 600; E_n = 9.97" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CHN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "test-result-node-among-people-without-the-disease" .

hemo:7002026 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Disease-status node of the test strategy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a prevalence of 0.20, the disease-status node takes the expected values of the two test-result nodes as its branch values. The test strategy has an expected cost of £950 and expected QALYs of 9.536, the article's figures." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Disease-status node of the test strategy" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_j = [0.20, 0.80]; C_j = [2350, 600]; E_j = [7.8, 9.97]; k = 2; C_n = 950; E_n = 9.536" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CHN-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "disease-status-node-of-the-test-strategy" .

hemo:7002027 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Single chance node of the treat-nobody strategy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Treating nobody leaves untreated disease with £2,500 of later care and 6.0 QALYs, and no cost with 10.0 QALYs for people without the disease. The expected cost is £500 and the expected QALYs are 9.2." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Single chance node of the treat-nobody strategy" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_j = [0.20, 0.80]; C_j = [2500, 0]; E_j = [6.0, 10.0]; k = 2; C_n = 500; E_n = 9.2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CHN-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "single-chance-node-of-the-treat-nobody-strategy" .

hemo:7002028 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal branch costs in the treat-everyone strategy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Treating everyone costs £2,000 on both branches, so the expected cost equals that cost whatever the prevalence, a limiting case. The expected QALYs are 9.44, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal branch costs in the treat-everyone strategy" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_j = [0.20, 0.80]; C_j = [2000, 2000]; E_j = [8.0, 9.8]; k = 2; C_n = 2000; E_n = 9.44" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CHN-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-branch-costs-in-the-treat-everyone-strategy" .

hemo:7002029 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Second-node probability conditional on the first branch"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "p_2 is the probability among people who took the first branch. Test sensitivity and specificity are conditional on true disease status, so they can be used directly at a test-result node placed after a disease-status node." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Second-node probability conditional on the first branch" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CHN-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "second-node-probability-conditional-on-the-first-branch" .

hemo:7002030 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Either node order gives the same pathway probability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The tree can place the test result first and disease status second, using predictive values derived through Bayes theorem from prevalence, sensitivity and specificity. When the conditional probabilities are consistent, both orders give the same pathway probabilities and expected values." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Either node order gives the same pathway probability" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CHN-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "either-node-order-gives-the-same-pathway-probability" .

hemo:7002031 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Pathway probability through two chance nodes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000442 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the first-node probability in Prob1 and the conditional second-node probability in Prob2, the cell, named PathwayProb, returns the pathway probability. For a pathway through more nodes, PRODUCT over a range of the conditional probabilities gives the same result." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Pathway probability through two chance nodes" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CHN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pathway-probability-through-two-chance-nodes" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Prob1*Prob2" .

hemo:7002032 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Pathway probabilities of one strategy sum to one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Add the pathway probabilities of every terminal node in one strategy. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a missing branch or a second-node probability that is not conditional on the first branch." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Pathway probabilities of one strategy sum to one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CHN-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pathway-probabilities-of-one-strategy-sum-to-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUM(PathwayProbs)-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002033 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Pathway table reproduces the rolled-back expected cost"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Multiplying each pathway probability by its cost and summing gives the same expected cost as rolling back the chance nodes. With the rolled-back value in StrategyCost, the check returns TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Pathway table reproduces the rolled-back expected cost" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CHN-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pathway-table-reproduces-the-rolled-back-expected-cost" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(PathwayProbs,PathwayCosts)-StrategyCost)<1E-6" .

hemo:7002034 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article true negative pathway reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Enter the true negative pathway of the article's test strategy: Prob1 0.8, the probability of no disease, and Prob2 0.85, the specificity. The model's PathwayProb cell then rounds to 0.68. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the probabilities added instead of multiplied, or the complement of the specificity entered at the second node." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article true negative pathway reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CHN-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-true-negative-pathway-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(PathwayProb,2)=0.68" .

hemo:7002035 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "True positive pathway in the test strategy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a prevalence of 0.20 and a sensitivity of 0.90, the probability of having the disease and testing positive is 0.18." ;
    hemo:9000009 "True positive pathway in the test strategy" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_1 = 0.20; p_2 = 0.90; pi_t = 0.18" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CHN-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "true-positive-pathway-in-the-test-strategy" .

hemo:7002036 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "False negative pathway in the test strategy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "People with the disease who test negative make up 0.02 of the cohort, the pathway that carries the cost of later care." ;
    hemo:9000009 "False negative pathway in the test strategy" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_1 = 0.20; p_2 = 0.10; pi_t = 0.02" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CHN-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "false-negative-pathway-in-the-test-strategy" .

hemo:7002037 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "False positive pathway in the test strategy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a specificity of 0.85, 15% of the 80% without the disease test positive, a pathway probability of 0.12." ;
    hemo:9000009 "False positive pathway in the test strategy" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_1 = 0.80; p_2 = 0.15; pi_t = 0.12" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CHN-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "false-positive-pathway-in-the-test-strategy" .

hemo:7002038 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "True negative pathway in the test strategy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The remaining pathway has probability 0.68, so the four pathway probabilities of the strategy sum to 1.00." ;
    hemo:9000009 "True negative pathway in the test strategy" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_1 = 0.80; p_2 = 0.85; pi_t = 0.68" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CHN-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "true-negative-pathway-in-the-test-strategy" .

hemo:7002039 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Mutually exclusive, exhaustive and homogeneous cohort states"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every member of the cohort is in exactly one state in every cycle, so each trace row sums to one, and everyone in a state faces the same transition probabilities and rewards. Under these conditions Y is an expected value per person and the cohort size is bookkeeping only." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mutually exclusive, exhaustive and homogeneous cohort states" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CSIM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mutually-exclusive-exhaustive-and-homogeneous-cohort-states" .

hemo:7002040 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Rewards per cycle include the cycle length"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "r is the reward for spending one whole cycle in a state. For QALYs it is the utility weight multiplied by the cycle length, so a six-month cycle in a state with utility 0.8 earns 0.4 QALYs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rewards per cycle include the cycle length" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CSIM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rewards-per-cycle-include-the-cycle-length" .

hemo:7002041 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Counting rule stated with the cycle length"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The trace records the cohort at cycle boundaries while people move at any time within a cycle. Full credit at the start of a cycle overestimates expected values and no credit underestimates them, so the counting rule, the cycle length and any correction are reported and can be varied in sensitivity analysis." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Counting rule stated with the cycle length" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CSIM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "counting-rule-stated-with-the-cycle-length" .

hemo:7002042 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected outcome from a trace with weights and discounting"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000443 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the trace in a range named Trace (one row per cycle from t = 0, one column per state), the rewards in a column named StateRewards and the counting weights and discount factors in columns CycleWeights and DiscountFactors with one row per cycle, the cell returns Y." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected outcome from a trace with weights and discounting" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CSIM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-outcome-from-a-trace-with-weights-and-discounting" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(CycleWeights,DiscountFactors,MMULT(Trace,StateRewards))" .

hemo:7002043 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cohort simulation counting weights sum to the number of cycles"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weights of each of the four rules sum to T, the number of cycles in the horizon. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a missing or doubled weight, or Simpson weights applied with an odd number of cycles." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cohort simulation counting weights sum to the number of cycles" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CSIM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cohort-simulation-counting-weights-sum-to-the-number-of-cycles" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUM(CycleWeights)-Cycles)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002044 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Half-cycle total equals the mean of start and end totals"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the totals under the three rules in HalfCycleTotal, StartTotal and EndTotal, the half-cycle total is the average of the other two. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Half-cycle total equals the mean of start and end totals" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CSIM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "half-cycle-total-equals-the-mean-of-start-and-end-totals" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(HalfCycleTotal-(StartTotal+EndTotal)/2)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002045 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Simpson count for Healthy against the continuous-time area"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Enter the Healthy column of the article's trace, 1, 0.8, 0.64, 0.512 and 0.4096, in a range named HealthyColumn and Simpson's weights in a range of the same size named SimpsonWeights. The Simpson count then agrees with the area under 0.8 to the power t from 0 to 4, the HE-FM-BTH-001 interval area with a hazard of minus ln 0.8, to within 0.0001. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows misplaced odd and even weights or a weight range that is not aligned with the trace." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Simpson count for Healthy against the continuous-time area" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CSIM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "simpson-count-for-healthy-against-the-continuous-time-area" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(SimpsonWeights,HealthyColumn)-(1-0.8^4)/(-LN(0.8)))<0.0001" .

hemo:7002046 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected years in Healthy counted at the end of each cycle"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative three-state model, the Healthy column of the trace over four annual cycles is 1, 0.8, 0.64, 0.512 and 0.4096. With a reward of 1 in Healthy and no discounting, end-of-cycle weights give 2.3616 years." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected years in Healthy counted at the end of each cycle" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_t = [0, 1, 1, 1, 1]; delta_t = [1, 1, 1, 1, 1]; m_t = [1, 0.8, 0.64, 0.512, 0.4096]; r = 1; T = 4; Y = 2.3616" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CSIM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-years-in-healthy-counted-at-the-end-of-each-cycle" .

hemo:7002047 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected years in Healthy counted at the start of each cycle"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Start-of-cycle weights credit the full cohort at t = 0 and nothing at t = 4, giving 2.952 years, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected years in Healthy counted at the start of each cycle" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_t = [1, 1, 1, 1, 0]; delta_t = [1, 1, 1, 1, 1]; m_t = [1, 0.8, 0.64, 0.512, 0.4096]; r = 1; T = 4; Y = 2.952" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CSIM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-years-in-healthy-counted-at-the-start-of-each-cycle" .

hemo:7002048 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected years in Healthy with half-cycle weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Half weights at t = 0 and t = 4 give 2.6568 years, the mean of the start and end counts and the article's figure." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected years in Healthy with half-cycle weights" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_t = [0.5, 1, 1, 1, 0.5]; delta_t = [1, 1, 1, 1, 1]; m_t = [1, 0.8, 0.64, 0.512, 0.4096]; r = 1; T = 4; Y = 2.6568" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CSIM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-years-in-healthy-with-half-cycle-weights" .

hemo:7002049 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected years in Healthy with Simpson's 1/3 weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Simpson's weights of one third, four thirds, two thirds, four thirds and one third, entered to nine decimals, give 2.6459 years. The continuous-time area from HE-FM-BTH-001 is about 2.6458, computed here with unrounded ln 0.8; the article prints 2.6459. The two agree to within 0.0001." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected years in Healthy with Simpson's 1/3 weights" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_t = [0.333333333, 1.333333333, 0.666666667, 1.333333333, 0.333333333]; delta_t = [1, 1, 1, 1, 1]; m_t = [1, 0.8, 0.64, 0.512, 0.4096]; r = 1; T = 4; Y = 2.6459" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CSIM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-years-in-healthy-with-simpson-s-1-3-weights" .

hemo:7002050 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted years in Healthy with half-cycle weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Computed here for illustration: discounting the half-cycle count at an illustrative 3.5% a year, with discount factors of 1 over 1.035 to the power t rounded to six decimals, gives 2.5107 discounted years in Healthy instead of 2.6568." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted years in Healthy with half-cycle weights" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_t = [0.5, 1, 1, 1, 0.5]; delta_t = [1, 0.966184, 0.933511, 0.901943, 0.871442]; m_t = [1, 0.8, 0.64, 0.512, 0.4096]; r = 1; T = 4; Y = 2.5107" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CSIM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-years-in-healthy-with-half-cycle-weights" .

hemo:7002051 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal spread in the two populations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Cohen defined d for two populations whose standard deviations are assumed equal, and the pooled standard deviation estimates that common value. Where a treatment changes the spread of outcomes, Glass's delta, which divides by the comparator group's standard deviation alone, answers a different question." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal spread in the two populations" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-spread-in-the-two-populations" .

hemo:7002052 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same direction of scale in every study"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The method does not correct for instruments on which higher scores mean opposite things. Before standardising, the means from one set of studies are multiplied by minus one so that the sign of d means the same everywhere." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same direction of scale in every study" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-direction-of-scale-in-every-study" .

hemo:7002053 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Uncorrected for small-sample bias"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The sample d tends to overstate the population effect in small samples. Cochrane reviews report Hedges' adjusted g, which multiplies d by a correction factor that approaches one as the sample grows; in the article's trial of 60 participants it changes 0.543 to 0.536. The correction and its standard error are covered on the Hedges' g page." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Uncorrected for small-sample bias" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uncorrected-for-small-sample-bias" .

hemo:7002054 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Pooled standard deviation and Cohen's d in two cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000444 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With named input cells MeanGroup1, MeanGroup2, SDGroup1, SDGroup2, SizeGroup1 and SizeGroup2, the first formula returns the pooled standard deviation in a cell named PooledSD and the second returns d in a cell named CohensD. Names such as N1 or SD1 are not used because Excel reads them as cell references." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Pooled standard deviation and Cohen's d in two cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pooled-standard-deviation-and-cohen-s-d-in-two-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SQRT(((SizeGroup1-1)*SDGroup1^2+(SizeGroup2-1)*SDGroup2^2)/(SizeGroup1+SizeGroup2-2)); =(MeanGroup1-MeanGroup2)/PooledSD" .

hemo:7002055 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Pooled standard deviation within the range of the group values"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The pooled standard deviation cannot be smaller than the smaller group standard deviation or larger than the larger one. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows that variances and standard deviations were mixed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Pooled standard deviation within the range of the group values" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pooled-standard-deviation-within-the-range-of-the-group-values" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(PooledSD>=MIN(SDGroup1,SDGroup2),PooledSD<=MAX(SDGroup1,SDGroup2))" .

hemo:7002056 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal group standard deviations pool to the same value"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For this check, set SDGroup1 and SDGroup2 to the same value; the group sizes in SizeGroup1 and SizeGroup2 can be anything. The model's PooledSD cell must then equal SDGroup1. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a missing square root, variances in place of standard deviations, or a PooledSD cell not linked to SDGroup1 and SDGroup2." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal group standard deviations pool to the same value" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-group-standard-deviations-pool-to-the-same-value" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PooledSD-SDGroup1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002057 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article Cohen's d reproduced to four decimals"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Enter the article's trial, with MeanGroup1 58, MeanGroup2 52, SDGroup1 12, SDGroup2 10, SizeGroup1 30 and SizeGroup2 30. The model's PooledSD cell then rounds to 11.0454 and its CohensD cell to 0.5432. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the groups weighted by size rather than degrees of freedom, or the means divided by an unpooled standard deviation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article Cohen's d reproduced to four decimals" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-cohen-s-d-reproduced-to-four-decimals" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(PooledSD,4)=11.0454,ROUND(CohensD,4)=0.5432)" .

hemo:7002058 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article fatigue trial with 30 patients per arm"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Illustrative trial from the article: intervention mean 58 with standard deviation 12, usual care mean 52 with standard deviation 10, 30 patients in each arm. The pooled standard deviation is the square root of 122, about 11.0454, and d is about 0.5432, shown as 11.05 and 0.543 in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article fatigue trial with 30 patients per arm" ;
    hemo:9000014 "xbar_1 = 58; xbar_2 = 52; s_1 = 12; s_2 = 10; n_1 = 30; n_2 = 30; s_p = 11.0454; d = 0.5432" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-fatigue-trial-with-30-patients-per-arm" .

hemo:7002059 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal group standard deviations return that standard deviation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Computed here for illustration: with both standard deviations equal to 10, the pooled value is 10 whatever the group sizes, and the same six-point difference gives a d of 0.6, a limiting case." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal group standard deviations return that standard deviation" ;
    hemo:9000014 "xbar_1 = 58; xbar_2 = 52; s_1 = 10; s_2 = 10; n_1 = 30; n_2 = 30; s_p = 10; d = 0.6" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-group-standard-deviations-return-that-standard-deviation" .

hemo:7002060 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Unequal group sizes weight the larger group"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Computed here for illustration: with 20 patients in the intervention arm and 40 in usual care, the pooled standard deviation moves towards the larger group's 10, to about 10.6964, and d rises to about 0.5609." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Unequal group sizes weight the larger group" ;
    hemo:9000014 "xbar_1 = 58; xbar_2 = 52; s_1 = 12; s_2 = 10; n_1 = 20; n_2 = 40; s_p = 10.6964; d = 0.5609" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "unequal-group-sizes-weight-the-larger-group" .

hemo:7002061 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Logistic distribution with equal spread in both groups"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The conversion assumes that the underlying continuous outcome follows a logistic distribution with the same standard deviation in both groups. The assumption will not hold exactly, so the Cochrane Handbook treats the result as an approximation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Logistic distribution with equal spread in both groups" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "logistic-distribution-with-equal-spread-in-both-groups" .

hemo:7002062 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Comparator response needed for a probability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The odds ratio alone does not give a probability. A comparator proportion of responders is needed, and the intervention probability then follows from HE-FM-NMA-004." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Comparator response needed for a probability" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "comparator-response-needed-for-a-probability" .

hemo:7002063 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Log odds ratio and odds ratio from a standardised difference"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000445 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the standardised difference in a cell named SMD, the first formula returns the log odds ratio in a cell named LogOR and the second returns the odds ratio. Replacing 1.814 with PI()/SQRT(3) gives the unrounded factor." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log odds ratio and odds ratio from a standardised difference" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-odds-ratio-and-odds-ratio-from-a-standardised-difference" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1.814*SMD; =EXP(LogOR)" .

hemo:7002064 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Log odds ratio cell matches the exact logistic factor"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The model's LogOR cell, computed with 1.814, is compared with SMD multiplied by the exact factor pi over the square root of 3, about 1.8138, with a tolerance of 0.0005 times SMD. The rounded factor 1.814 differs from the exact one by about 0.0002 and passes. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows 1.81, 1.8 or another coarser rounding, which differs by 0.0038 or more, or a LogOR cell not linked to SMD." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log odds ratio cell matches the exact logistic factor" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-odds-ratio-cell-matches-the-exact-logistic-factor" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LogOR-SMD*PI()/SQRT(3))<=0.0005*ABS(SMD)" .

hemo:7002065 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Round trip from the odds ratio back to the standardised difference"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Dividing the natural logarithm of the odds ratio by 1.814 recovers the standardised difference, the direction of conversion in Chinn's paper. With the odds ratio in a cell named OddsRatio, the check returns TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Round trip from the odds ratio back to the standardised difference" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "round-trip-from-the-odds-ratio-back-to-the-standardised-difference" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LN(OddsRatio)/1.814-SMD)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002066 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article log odds ratio reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Enter the article's rounded Hedges' g of 0.54 in SMD. The model's LogOR cell is then within 0.001 of 0.54 times the exact factor PI()/SQRT(3), about 0.9795, and rounds to the article's 0.980. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a factor of 1.81, which gives about 0.9774, or the exponential taken in the LogOR cell." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article log odds ratio reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-log-odds-ratio-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LogOR-0.54*PI()/SQRT(3))<0.001" .

hemo:7002067 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article standardised effect of 0.54"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The article rounds Hedges' g to 0.54. The log odds ratio is about 0.9796, shown as 0.980 in the article, and the odds ratio is about 2.6633; the article exponentiates the rounded 0.980 and reports 2.664." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article standardised effect of 0.54" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d = 0.54; lnOR = 0.9796; OR = 2.6633" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-standardised-effect-of-0-54" .

hemo:7002068 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Lower confidence limit of the article's estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Computed here for illustration: carried through the same conversion, the article's lower 95% limit of 0.021 gives a log odds ratio of about 0.0381 and an odds ratio of about 1.0388, close to no effect." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Lower confidence limit of the article's estimate" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d = 0.021; lnOR = 0.0381; OR = 1.0388" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "lower-confidence-limit-of-the-article-s-estimate" .

hemo:7002069 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Upper confidence limit of the article's estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The upper limit of 1.051 gives a log odds ratio of about 1.9065 and an odds ratio of about 6.7296, computed here for illustration from the article's interval." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Upper confidence limit of the article's estimate" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d = 1.051; lnOR = 1.9065; OR = 6.7296" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "upper-confidence-limit-of-the-article-s-estimate" .

hemo:7002070 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "No difference in means gives an odds ratio of 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A standardised difference of 0 converts to a log odds ratio of 0 and an odds ratio of 1, a limiting case." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No difference in means gives an odds ratio of 1" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d = 0; lnOR = 0; OR = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CD-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-difference-in-means-gives-an-odds-ratio-of-1" .

hemo:7002071 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One costing sample, cost scope and year for all case weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "All group means come from the same costing sample, cost scope and year, so every weight is scaled to the same average case. IHACPA, for example, removes depreciation and other capital costs and direct teaching, training and research costs before it sets cost weights for admitted acute care." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One costing sample, cost scope and year for all case weights" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CWT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-costing-sample-cost-scope-and-year-for-all-case-weights" .

hemo:7002072 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Groups homogeneous enough in cost for a group mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Cases within a group are similar enough in cost for the group mean to stand for them. The weight then gives the expected cost of an average case in the group and says nothing about what one patient will cost; trim points and outlier rules decide how far extreme cases shape it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Groups homogeneous enough in cost for a group mean" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CWT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "groups-homogeneous-enough-in-cost-for-a-group-mean" .

hemo:7002073 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Case weight from group mean costs with SUMPRODUCT"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000446 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the cases and mean costs of every group of the costing sample in equal-sized ranges named SampleCases and SampleMeanCost, and the mean cost of the group of interest in a cell named ThisGroupMeanCost, Excel returns the group's weight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Case weight from group mean costs with SUMPRODUCT" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CWT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "case-weight-from-group-mean-costs-with-sumproduct" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ThisGroupMeanCost/(SUMPRODUCT(SampleCases,SampleMeanCost)/SUM(SampleCases))" .

hemo:7002074 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Case-weighted mean of the case weights equals 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the weights of all groups, computed from the same sample, in a range named GroupWeights, the case-weighted mean of the weights is 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an overall mean taken as the simple average of the group means or from a different sample." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Case-weighted mean of the case weights equals 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CWT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "case-weighted-mean-of-the-case-weights-equals-1" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(SampleCases,GroupWeights)/SUM(SampleCases)-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002075 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weight of illustrative group B in the case weight article"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative costing sample, groups A, B and C have 600, 300 and 100 cases with mean costs of £2,000, £5,000 and £13,000. The overall mean is £4,000,000 over 1,000 cases, or £4,000, so group B's weight is 5,000 / 4,000 = 1.25." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weight of illustrative group B in the case weight article" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_k = [600, 300, 100]; c_bar_k = [2000, 5000, 13000]; K = 3; c_bar_g = 5000; c_bar = 4000; w_g = 1.25" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CWT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weight-of-illustrative-group-b-in-the-case-weight-article" .

hemo:7002076 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weight of illustrative group C in the case weight article"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "From the same sample, group C's mean cost of £13,000 gives a weight of 13,000 / 4,000 = 3.25, and group A's £2,000 gives 0.50. The case-weighted average of the three weights is 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weight of illustrative group C in the case weight article" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_k = [600, 300, 100]; c_bar_k = [2000, 5000, 13000]; K = 3; c_bar_g = 13000; c_bar = 4000; w_g = 3.25" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CWT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weight-of-illustrative-group-c-in-the-case-weight-article" .

hemo:7002077 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Base rate set on the same scale as the case weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The base rate belongs to the same weight scale and year as the weights, so that a case with a weight of 1 at a hospital with no adjustment is paid the base rate. The European Observatory study notes that all countries using relative weights multiply them by a base rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Base rate set on the same scale as the case weights" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CWT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "base-rate-set-on-the-same-scale-as-the-case-weights" .

hemo:7002078 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Add-on and outlier payments outside the case payment formula"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The formula gives the basic payment for a case. Medicare's add-ons for teaching hospitals and hospitals serving many low-income patients, outlier payments for unusually costly cases and England's top-up payments for specialised providers are added separately, so the formula alone does not give total revenue." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Add-on and outlier payments outside the case payment formula" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CWT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "add-on-and-outlier-payments-outside-the-case-payment-formula" .

hemo:7002079 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Case payment from weight, base rate and adjustment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000447 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel multiplies the named cells holding the case weight, the base rate and the hospital adjustment factor, returning the payment in a cell named CasePayment." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Case payment from weight, base rate and adjustment" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CWT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "case-payment-from-weight-base-rate-and-adjustment" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CaseWeight*BaseRate*HospitalAdj" .

hemo:7002080 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Case payment matches the published tariff for the group"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a case at a hospital with HospitalAdj 1, enter the payment published for the case's group in the payer's tariff, taken independently of the model, in a cell named PublishedTariff; for the European Observatory study's example it is EUR 3,900 for a weight of 1.95 at EUR 2,000. The model's CasePayment cell must match it. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a weight or base rate from another year or scale, or a base rate entered per case rather than per unit of weight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Case payment matches the published tariff for the group" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CWT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "case-payment-matches-the-published-tariff-for-the-group" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(CasePayment-PublishedTariff)<0.01" .

hemo:7002081 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Relative weight of 1.95 at a conversion rate of EUR 2,000"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The European Observatory study's hypothetical example multiplies a relative weight of 1.95 by a conversion rate of EUR 2,000, giving a payment of EUR 3,900 with no hospital adjustment." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Relative weight of 1.95 at a conversion rate of EUR 2,000" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_g = 1.95; B = 2000; a_h = 1; P_i = 3900" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CWT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "relative-weight-of-1-95-at-a-conversion-rate-of-eur-2-000" .

hemo:7002082 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Relative weight of 1.95 with a hospital adjustment of 1.05"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The same case at a hospital with an adjustment factor of 1.05 is paid EUR 4,095, computed here for illustration." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Relative weight of 1.95 with a hospital adjustment of 1.05" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_g = 1.95; B = 2000; a_h = 1.05; P_i = 4095" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CWT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "relative-weight-of-1-95-with-a-hospital-adjustment-of-1-05" .

hemo:7002083 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Group B case paid at the case weight article's base rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At the article's illustrative base rate of £4,000, a case in group B with a weight of 1.25 is paid £5,000, the group's mean cost in the costing sample (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Group B case paid at the case weight article's base rate" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_g = 1.25; B = 4000; a_h = 1; P_i = 5000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CWT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "group-b-case-paid-at-the-case-weight-article-s-base-rate" .

hemo:7002084 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weights, reference cost and hospital cost on one costing basis"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weights and c_bar come from one costing sample and year, and C_h is measured on the same cost scope, for example with capital and direct teaching costs treated the same way, so that the costing sample itself scores 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weights, reference cost and hospital cost on one costing basis" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CWT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weights-reference-cost-and-hospital-cost-on-one-costing-basis" .

hemo:7002085 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Comparable coding and complexity within groups across hospitals"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Cases are coded on the same rules in every hospital and complexity within each group does not differ systematically. Up-coding raises CM_h and lowers R_h with no change in efficiency." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Comparable coding and complexity within groups across hospitals" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CWT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "comparable-coding-and-complexity-within-groups-across-hospitals" .

hemo:7002086 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Casemix-adjusted cost ratio with SUMPRODUCT"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000448 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the hospital's cases per group in a range named HospitalCases, the group weights in a range of the same size named GroupWeights, and named cells for the hospital's total cost and the reference cost per unit of weight, Excel returns the ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Casemix-adjusted cost ratio with SUMPRODUCT" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CWT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "casemix-adjusted-cost-ratio-with-sumproduct" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=HospitalCost/(SUMPRODUCT(HospitalCases,GroupWeights)*RefUnitCost)" .

hemo:7002087 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Costing sample scores a casemix-adjusted cost ratio of 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Applied to the costing sample itself, with its total cost and its cases per group, the ratio is 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows weights or a reference cost that do not come from that sample." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Costing sample scores a casemix-adjusted cost ratio of 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CWT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "costing-sample-scores-a-casemix-adjusted-cost-ratio-of-1" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SampleTotalCost/(SUMPRODUCT(SampleCases,GroupWeights)*RefUnitCost)-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002088 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cost ratio of illustrative Hospital X in the case weight article"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Hospital X treats 200, 50 and 10 cases in groups A, B and C, a casemix of 195 weighted cases. Its expected cost at £4,000 per unit of weight is £780,000 against an actual £858,000, a ratio of 1.10, or 10% above the reference." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cost ratio of illustrative Hospital X in the case weight article" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_hg = [200, 50, 10]; w_g = [0.5, 1.25, 3.25]; G = 3; c_bar = 4000; C_h = 858000; CM_h = 195; R_h = 1.1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CWT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cost-ratio-of-illustrative-hospital-x-in-the-case-weight-article" .

hemo:7002089 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cost ratio of illustrative Hospital Y in the case weight article"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Hospital Y treats 50, 100 and 60 cases, a casemix of 345 weighted cases and an expected cost of £1,380,000. Its actual cost of £1,311,000 gives a ratio of 0.95, or 5% below the reference." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cost ratio of illustrative Hospital Y in the case weight article" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_hg = [50, 100, 60]; w_g = [0.5, 1.25, 3.25]; G = 3; c_bar = 4000; C_h = 1311000; CM_h = 345; R_h = 0.95" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CWT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cost-ratio-of-illustrative-hospital-y-in-the-case-weight-article" .

hemo:7002090 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Public patient episode with shadow-priced safety terms left at zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The episode is a public patient episode, so the private patient service and accommodation deductions are zero, and the hospital-acquired complication and avoidable readmission terms are left at zero because they are shadow priced in 2026-27. IHACPA holds any negative result of those deductions at zero NWAU." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Public patient episode with shadow-priced safety terms left at zero" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CWT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "public-patient-episode-with-shadow-priced-safety-terms-left-at-zero" .

hemo:7002091 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Price weight matched to the stay's length and year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "PW_g is the inlier price weight when the stay lies within the AR-DRG's bounds; same-day, short-stay outlier and long-stay outlier stays use the other parameters in the determination's tables. NWAU(26) weights are used only with the 2026-27 NEP." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Price weight matched to the stay's length and year" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CWT-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "price-weight-matched-to-the-stay-s-length-and-year" .

hemo:7002092 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Episode NWAU and price in two cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000449 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The first formula, in a cell named EpisodeNWAU, applies the adjustments held in named cells; the second, in a cell named EpisodePrice, multiplies the result by the NEP held in a cell named NatEffPrice." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Episode NWAU and price in two cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CWT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "episode-nwau-and-price-in-two-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PriceWeight*PaedAdj*(1+ResAdj+IndAdj+RtAdj+DiaAdj)*(1+TreatAdj)+ICUAdjPerHour*ICUHours; =EpisodeNWAU*NatEffPrice" .

hemo:7002093 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Tonsillectomy reproduces IHACPA's published price"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With PriceWeight 0.7417, PaedAdj 1, the other adjustments and ICU hours 0 and NatEffPrice 7418, the price rounds to IHACPA's AUD 5,502. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a weight or NEP from another year, or an additive adjustment entered as 1 instead of 0." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Tonsillectomy reproduces IHACPA's published price" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CWT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "tonsillectomy-reproduces-ihacpa-s-published-price" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(EpisodePrice,0)=5502" .

hemo:7002094 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Tonsillectomy priced at the 2026-27 national efficient price"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "AR-DRG D11Z, tonsillectomy and adenoidectomy, has an inlier price weight of 0.7417 NWAU(26). With no adjustments and a NEP of AUD 7,418 the price is about AUD 5,501.93 (computed here), which IHACPA reports as AUD 5,502." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Tonsillectomy priced at the 2026-27 national efficient price" ;
    hemo:9000014 "PW_g = 0.7417; A_paed = 1; A_res = 0; A_ind = 0; A_rt = 0; A_dia = 0; A_treat = 0; A_icu = 0.0446; h_i = 0; NEP = 7418; NWAU_i = 0.7417; P_i = 5501.93" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CWT-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "tonsillectomy-priced-at-the-2026-27-national-efficient-price" .

hemo:7002095 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Minor-complexity hip replacement priced at the 2026-27 NEP"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "AR-DRG I03B, hip replacement for traumatic condition, minor complexity, has an inlier price weight of 3.8021 NWAU(26). With no adjustments the price is about AUD 28,203.98 (computed here), which IHACPA reports as AUD 28,204." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Minor-complexity hip replacement priced at the 2026-27 NEP" ;
    hemo:9000014 "PW_g = 3.8021; A_paed = 1; A_res = 0; A_ind = 0; A_rt = 0; A_dia = 0; A_treat = 0; A_icu = 0.0446; h_i = 0; NEP = 7418; NWAU_i = 3.8021; P_i = 28203.98" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CWT-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "minor-complexity-hip-replacement-priced-at-the-2026-27-nep" .

hemo:7002096 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Episode with 24 hours in an eligible intensive care unit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An illustrative episode with a price weight of 1.0000 NWAU in an AR-DRG not marked as bundled ICU, and 24 hours in a specified intensive care unit, adds 24 × 0.0446 = 1.0704 NWAU. The episode is worth 2.0704 NWAU, a price of about AUD 15,358.23 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Episode with 24 hours in an eligible intensive care unit" ;
    hemo:9000014 "PW_g = 1; A_paed = 1; A_res = 0; A_ind = 0; A_rt = 0; A_dia = 0; A_treat = 0; A_icu = 0.0446; h_i = 24; NEP = 7418; NWAU_i = 2.0704; P_i = 15358.23" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CWT-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "episode-with-24-hours-in-an-eligible-intensive-care-unit" .

hemo:7002097 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Deaths restricted to the counted cases"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every death in D comes from a case in N_c. A death-to-case ratio, which divides deaths in a period by new cases in the same period, does not meet this condition and cannot be read as the probability that a newly diagnosed case dies." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Deaths restricted to the counted cases" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CFR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "deaths-restricted-to-the-counted-cases" .

hemo:7002098 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Every counted case resolved and detection consistent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The crude ratio is reliable once every counted case has died or recovered and detection of cases and deaths has stayed consistent, as at the end of an outbreak. Part-way through, unresolved cases push it down and preferential ascertainment of severe cases pushes it up." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Every counted case resolved and detection consistent" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CFR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "every-counted-case-resolved-and-detection-consistent" .

hemo:7002099 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Case fatality rate from named death and case counts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000450 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel divides the named cell holding the deaths among the counted cases by the named cell holding the number of cases." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Case fatality rate from named death and case counts" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CFR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "case-fatality-rate-from-named-death-and-case-counts" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Deaths/Cases" .

hemo:7002100 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Case fatality rate reproduces the CDC hepatitis A figure"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Deaths 3 and Cases 555, and the result in a cell named CaseFatality, the case fatality rate as a percentage rounds to 0.5. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the ratio inverted or a result already multiplied by 100." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Case fatality rate reproduces the CDC hepatitis A figure" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CFR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "case-fatality-rate-reproduces-the-cdc-hepatitis-a-figure" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(CaseFatality*100,1)=0.5" .

hemo:7002101 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Deaths in the case fatality numerator do not exceed the cases"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Deaths are counted among the cases in the denominator, so they cannot exceed them. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows deaths taken from outside the case series, as in a death-to-case ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Deaths in the case fatality numerator do not exceed the cases" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CFR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "deaths-in-the-case-fatality-numerator-do-not-exceed-the-cases" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Deaths<=Cases" .

hemo:7002102 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "CDC hepatitis A outbreak with 555 cases and 3 deaths"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The CDC teaching text works through a hepatitis A outbreak with 555 cases, 3 of whom died, a case fatality rate of about 0.0054, reported as 0.5%." ;
    hemo:9000009 "CDC hepatitis A outbreak with 555 cases and 3 deaths" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 3; N_c = 555; CFR = 0.0054" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CFR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cdc-hepatitis-a-outbreak-with-555-cases-and-3-deaths" .

hemo:7002103 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Final case fatality rate in the article's illustrative outbreak"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Once every case has resolved, the article's illustrative outbreak has 60 deaths among 2,000 confirmed cases, a final case fatality rate of 0.030." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Final case fatality rate in the article's illustrative outbreak" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 60; N_c = 2000; CFR = 0.03" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CFR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "final-case-fatality-rate-in-the-article-s-illustrative-outbreak" .

hemo:7002104 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Crude case fatality rate at week 8 of the illustrative outbreak"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At week 8 the same outbreak has 40 deaths among 2,000 confirmed cases, a crude estimate of 0.020. It is too low because 20 of the 960 cases still ill will die." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Crude case fatality rate at week 8 of the illustrative outbreak" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 40; N_c = 2000; CFR = 0.02" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CFR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "crude-case-fatality-rate-at-week-8-of-the-illustrative-outbreak" .

hemo:7002105 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Deaths and recoveries resolve at similar speeds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The estimate is unbiased only if cases that will die and cases that will recover leave the unresolved pool at similar times. If people who die typically do so sooner than others recover, the estimate is too high; if the reverse holds, it is too low." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Deaths and recoveries resolve at similar speeds" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CFR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "deaths-and-recoveries-resolve-at-similar-speeds" .

hemo:7002106 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Recoveries recorded as completely as deaths"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Detection of cases, deaths and recoveries stays consistent over the outbreak and recoveries are recorded as fully as deaths. Missing recoveries shrink the denominator and raise the estimate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Recoveries recorded as completely as deaths" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CFR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "recoveries-recorded-as-completely-as-deaths" .

hemo:7002107 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Resolved-case fatality rate in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000451 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel divides the named cell holding deaths by the sum of the named cells holding deaths and recoveries among detected cases." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Resolved-case fatality rate in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CFR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "resolved-case-fatality-rate-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Deaths/(Deaths+Recoveries)" .

hemo:7002108 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Resolved-case estimate is not below the crude estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Deaths plus recoveries cannot exceed the detected cases, so the resolved-case estimate is at least the crude estimate from the same counts. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows deaths or recoveries counted outside the case series." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Resolved-case estimate is not below the crude estimate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CFR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "resolved-case-estimate-is-not-below-the-crude-estimate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Deaths/(Deaths+Recoveries)>=Deaths/Cases" .

hemo:7002109 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Resolved-case estimate at week 8 of the illustrative outbreak"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At week 8 the article's illustrative outbreak has 40 deaths and 1,000 recoveries, so 40 / 1,040 gives about 0.0385. It is too high, because deaths occur sooner than recoveries in this outbreak and the final value is 0.030." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Resolved-case estimate at week 8 of the illustrative outbreak" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 40; R = 1000; CFR_r = 0.0385" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CFR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "resolved-case-estimate-at-week-8-of-the-illustrative-outbreak" .

hemo:7002110 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Resolved-case estimate once every case has resolved"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When all 2,000 cases have resolved, with 60 deaths and 1,940 recoveries, the resolved-case estimate equals the final crude value of 0.030 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Resolved-case estimate once every case has resolved" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 60; R = 1940; CFR_r = 0.03" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CFR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "resolved-case-estimate-once-every-case-has-resolved" .

hemo:7002111 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant exponential growth of reported cases"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Reported cases grow exponentially with a fixed doubling time over the delay. As growth slows or the epidemic declines, the factor no longer describes the bias." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant exponential growth of reported cases" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CFR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-exponential-growth-of-reported-cases" .

hemo:7002112 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One fixed delay from case report to death report"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every death is reported the same time after its case. Real delays vary from case to case, so the factor indicates the size of the bias rather than giving an exact correction." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One fixed delay from case report to death report" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CFR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-fixed-delay-from-case-report-to-death-report" .

hemo:7002113 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Understatement factor from delay and doubling time"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000452 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel raises 2 to the ratio of the named cells holding the reporting delay and the doubling time, both in the same unit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Understatement factor from delay and doubling time" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CFR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "understatement-factor-from-delay-and-doubling-time" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=2^(ReportDelay/DoublingTime)" .

hemo:7002114 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Understatement factor recovers the delay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The base-2 logarithm of the factor, multiplied by the doubling time, returns the delay. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a factor computed with the delay and doubling time swapped or with EXP in place of a power of 2." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Understatement factor recovers the delay" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CFR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "understatement-factor-recovers-the-delay" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LOG(UnderstatementFactor,2)*DoublingTime-ReportDelay)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002115 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three-week delay with a two-week doubling time"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In Lipsitch and colleagues' example a three-week delay and a two-week doubling time give 2 raised to the power 1.5, about 2.8, so the crude estimate is close to one third of the case fatality rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three-week delay with a two-week doubling time" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d = 3; T_d = 2; B = 2.83" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CFR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-week-delay-with-a-two-week-doubling-time" .

hemo:7002116 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Delay equal to one doubling time"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When deaths are reported one doubling time after their cases, the crude estimate is about half the case fatality rate (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Delay equal to one doubling time" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d = 2; T_d = 2; B = 2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CFR-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "delay-equal-to-one-doubling-time" .

hemo:7002117 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same cases, period and population in both measures"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "AR and CFR use the same case definition and period, and the attack rate's denominator is the population at risk to which M refers." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same cases, period and population in both measures" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CFR-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-cases-period-and-population-in-both-measures" .

hemo:7002118 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "All disease deaths occur among the counted cases"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every death from the disease counted in M occurs among the counted cases. Deaths among infections never ascertained as cases, or deaths after the counting window, break the identity." ;
    hemo:9000009 "All disease deaths occur among the counted cases" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CFR-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "all-disease-deaths-occur-among-the-counted-cases" .

hemo:7002119 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Outbreak mortality from attack rate and case fatality rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000453 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel multiplies the named cells holding the attack rate and the case fatality rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Outbreak mortality from attack rate and case fatality rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CFR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "outbreak-mortality-from-attack-rate-and-case-fatality-rate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AttackRate*CaseFatality" .

hemo:7002120 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mortality product equals deaths over the population at risk"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Take AttackRate and CaseFatality from their own sources, for example a surveillance or serosurvey attack rate and a case series fatality rate, and enter Deaths and Population as an independent count of disease deaths in the population at risk over the same period. The product then matches Deaths over Population to within 5%, a tolerance to set for the data. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a mismatch between the sources in population, case definition or count." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mortality product equals deaths over the population at risk" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CFR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mortality-product-equals-deaths-over-the-population-at-risk" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AttackRate*CaseFatality/(Deaths/Population)-1)<0.05" .

hemo:7002121 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Attack rate of 0.20 with a case fatality rate of 0.03"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's illustrative figures, an attack rate of 0.20 and a case fatality rate of 0.03 give a mortality of 0.006, or 6 deaths per 1,000 people over the outbreak." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Attack rate of 0.20 with a case fatality rate of 0.03" ;
    hemo:9000014 "AR = 0.2; CFR = 0.03; M = 0.006" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CFR-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "attack-rate-of-0-20-with-a-case-fatality-rate-of-0-03" .

hemo:7002122 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Rare disease with a high case fatality rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An attack rate of 0.001 with a case fatality rate of 0.5 gives a mortality of 0.0005, or 1 death per 2,000 people, low despite the high case fatality rate (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rare disease with a high case fatality rate" ;
    hemo:9000014 "AR = 0.001; CFR = 0.5; M = 0.0005" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CFR-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rare-disease-with-a-high-case-fatality-rate" .

hemo:7002123 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Covered days counted as calendar days, not summed supply"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each fill is laid out as a run of calendar dates starting on the dispensing day, so a 30-day supply collected on 1 March covers 1 to 30 March, and a day covered by more than one fill counts once." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Covered days counted as calendar days, not summed supply" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PDC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "covered-days-counted-as-calendar-days-not-summed-supply" .

hemo:7002124 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed end date for the PDC observation period"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The period runs to a fixed end date (the end of the measurement year, disenrolment or death) rather than to the last fill, so a patient who stops refilling is still followed and stopping lowers the PDC. CMS also requires at least two fills on different dates and a treatment period of at least 91 days." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fixed end date for the PDC observation period" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PDC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fixed-end-date-for-the-pdc-observation-period" .

hemo:7002125 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Complete dispensing record with correct days' supply for the PDC"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every fill appears in the data and its recorded days' supply reflects the prescribed dose. Fills paid in cash or made outside the database look like gaps, and imputing one unit a day is less reliable for drugs whose dose varies." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Complete dispensing record with correct days' supply for the PDC" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PDC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "complete-dispensing-record-with-correct-days-supply-for-the-pdc" .

hemo:7002126 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Proportion of days covered from named covered-day and period cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000454 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel divides the named cell holding the unique covered days in the period by the named cell holding the number of days from the index date to the end date. CoveredDays can come from HE-FM-PDC-003 or from the computational function HE-CF-PDC-001." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Proportion of days covered from named covered-day and period cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-PDC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "proportion-of-days-covered-from-named-covered-day-and-period-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CoveredDays/PeriodDays" .

hemo:7002127 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "PDC reproduces the article's shifted five-fill result"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With CoveredDays 150 and PeriodDays 180, and the result in a cell named PDC, the PDC rounded to three decimals is 0.833. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the ratio inverted, or the summed supply of 210 days used as the numerator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "PDC reproduces the article's shifted five-fill result" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PDC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pdc-reproduces-the-article-s-shifted-five-fill-result" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(PDC,3)=0.833" .

hemo:7002128 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Covered days do not exceed the days in the PDC period"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Only days inside the period count, and each counts once, so the covered days cannot exceed the length of the period. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows days' supply summed instead of unique days counted, or supply beyond the end date included." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Covered days do not exceed the days in the PDC period" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PDC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "covered-days-do-not-exceed-the-days-in-the-pdc-period" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CoveredDays<=PeriodDays" .

hemo:7002129 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "PDC of the five-fill history with early refills shifted"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative history (fills on days 1, 22, 45, 121 and 170 with 30, 30, 30, 90 and 30 days' supply, period days 1 to 180), shifting the early refills leaves days 1 to 90 and 121 to 180 covered, 150 days, so the PDC is 150 / 180, about 0.833, above an 80% threshold." ;
    hemo:9000009 "PDC of the five-fill history with early refills shifted" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C = 150; T = 180; PDC = 0.8333" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PDC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pdc-of-the-five-fill-history-with-early-refills-shifted" .

hemo:7002130 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "PDC of the five-fill history with overlaps merged, not shifted"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Merging overlaps instead of shifting them, fills 1 to 3 cover days 1 to 74 and fill 4 covers days 121 to 180, so 134 days are covered and the PDC is about 0.744, below an 80% threshold. Fill 5 (days 170 to 199) lies inside fill 4 and adds nothing." ;
    hemo:9000009 "PDC of the five-fill history with overlaps merged, not shifted" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C = 134; T = 180; PDC = 0.7444" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PDC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pdc-of-the-five-fill-history-with-overlaps-merged-not-shifted" .

hemo:7002131 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "CMS overlap example before and after shifting a same-ingredient refill"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In Example 2 (Tables L-2 and L-3) of Attachment L of the CMS 2026 Star Ratings technical notes, a 120-day period has 59 covered days before the overlap between two products containing lisinopril is shifted and 62 after, so the PDC rises from 49% to 52%." ;
    hemo:9000009 "CMS overlap example before and after shifting a same-ingredient refill" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C = 62; T = 120; PDC = 0.5167" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PDC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cms-overlap-example-before-and-after-shifting-a-same-ingredient-refill" .

hemo:7002132 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Earlier supply finished before a refill is started"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A patient who refills early finishes the supply from the preceding fill before starting the new one, so the early refill extends coverage instead of duplicating it. The rule cannot tell stockpiling for later use from doses already missed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Earlier supply finished before a refill is started" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PDC-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "earlier-supply-finished-before-a-refill-is-started" .

hemo:7002133 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Shift applied to the same drug only, not across a class"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The shift applies to fills of the same drug. Where a measure covers a class, overlapping fills of different drugs are treated as taken together and are not shifted, and a day counts once if at least one drug is available. In Example 3 (Tables L-4 and L-5) of Attachment L of the CMS technical notes, lisinopril overlapping captopril is left unadjusted." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Shift applied to the same drug only, not across a class" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PDC-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "shift-applied-to-the-same-drug-only-not-across-a-class" .

hemo:7002134 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Shifted start day from the dispensing day and the previous fill"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000455 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With fills sorted by dispensing day, Excel takes the later of the named cell holding this fill's dispensing day and the previous fill's shifted start plus its days' supply. In a fill table the formula is filled down a helper column, with the first fill's start equal to its dispensing day." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Shifted start day from the dispensing day and the previous fill" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-PDC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "shifted-start-day-from-the-dispensing-day-and-the-previous-fill" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MAX(FillDay,PrevStart+PrevSupply)" .

hemo:7002135 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Shifted start is never before dispensing or before the previous supply ends"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The shifted start is the later of the dispensing day and the day after the previous supply ends, so it is on or after both and equal to one of them. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an overlap left unshifted, so the same days are counted twice, a start moved earlier than the dispensing day, or a start pushed later than needed, which opens a gap that the fill history does not contain." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Shifted start is never before dispensing or before the previous supply ends" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PDC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "shifted-start-is-never-before-dispensing-or-before-the-previous-supply-ends" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ShiftedStart>=FillDay,ShiftedStart>=PrevStart+PrevSupply,OR(ShiftedStart=FillDay,ShiftedStart=PrevStart+PrevSupply))" .

hemo:7002136 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Shift rule reproduces day 211 for the article's fifth fill"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With FillDay 170, PrevStart 121 and PrevSupply 90, the shifted start is day 211. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 210 shows the previous fill's last day of supply used instead of the day after it, so one day is counted twice." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Shift rule reproduces day 211 for the article's fifth fill" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PDC-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "shift-rule-reproduces-day-211-for-the-article-s-fifth-fill" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ShiftedStart=211" .

hemo:7002137 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Second fill dispensed on day 22 shifted to day 31"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Fill 2 of the article's history is dispensed on day 22 with 9 days of fill 1 left, so it starts on day 31, the day after fill 1 (days 1 to 30) ends." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Second fill dispensed on day 22 shifted to day 31" ;
    hemo:9000014 "f_i = 22; a_prev = 1; S_prev = 30; a_i = 31" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PDC-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "second-fill-dispensed-on-day-22-shifted-to-day-31" .

hemo:7002138 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fourth fill after a gap keeps its dispensing day"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Fill 4 is dispensed on day 121, after shifted fill 3 (days 61 to 90) has ended, so it starts on day 121 and days 91 to 120 stay uncovered." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fourth fill after a gap keeps its dispensing day" ;
    hemo:9000014 "f_i = 121; a_prev = 61; S_prev = 30; a_i = 121" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PDC-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fourth-fill-after-a-gap-keeps-its-dispensing-day" .

hemo:7002139 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fifth fill shifted beyond the end of the 180-day period"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Fill 5 is dispensed on day 170 while the 90-day fill 4 lasts to day 210, so it starts on day 211, after the period has ended, and adds no covered days." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fifth fill shifted beyond the end of the 180-day period" ;
    hemo:9000014 "f_i = 170; a_prev = 121; S_prev = 90; a_i = 211" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PDC-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fifth-fill-shifted-beyond-the-end-of-the-180-day-period" .

hemo:7002140 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Shifted fills of one drug do not overlap"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The fills belong to one drug and have been shifted, so no two of them cover the same day and their days can be added. For a class measure with different drugs the covered days are the union of the arrays, each day counted once, which the sum does not give." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Shifted fills of one drug do not overlap" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PDC-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "shifted-fills-of-one-drug-do-not-overlap" .

hemo:7002141 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Index date as day 1 of the PDC period"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The first fill falls on day 1, the index date, and no fill starts before it, so every covered day counted is inside the period." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Index date as day 1 of the PDC period" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PDC-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "index-date-as-day-1-of-the-pdc-period" .

hemo:7002142 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Covered days from ranges of shifted starts and supplies"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000456 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the shifted start days in a range named ShiftedStarts, the matching days' supply in a range named Supplies and the last day of the period in a cell named EndDay, the formula adds each fill's supply up to the end day and nothing for a fill starting after it. It works as entered in Excel 365 and as an array formula in earlier versions." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Covered days from ranges of shifted starts and supplies" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-PDC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "covered-days-from-ranges-of-shifted-starts-and-supplies" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUM(IF(EndDay-ShiftedStarts+1<Supplies,IF(EndDay-ShiftedStarts+1>0,EndDay-ShiftedStarts+1,0),Supplies))" .

hemo:7002143 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Covered days bounded by the total supply and by the period length"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With day 1 the index date, the end day equals the number of days in the period, and covered days can exceed neither that nor the total days' supply. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows supply past the end day counted, or overlapping days counted twice to the point of exceeding the period." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Covered days bounded by the total supply and by the period length" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PDC-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "covered-days-bounded-by-the-total-supply-and-by-the-period-length" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(CoveredDays<=SUM(Supplies),CoveredDays<=EndDay)" .

hemo:7002144 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Covered days reproduce 150 for the article's fill history"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With ShiftedStarts 1, 31, 61, 121 and 211, Supplies 30, 30, 30, 90 and 30 and EndDay 180, the covered days are 150. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 161 (computed here for illustration) shows the unshifted dispensing days entered, so overlapping days are counted twice; FALSE at 210 shows supply beyond day 180 counted." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Covered days reproduce 150 for the article's fill history" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PDC-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "covered-days-reproduce-150-for-the-article-s-fill-history" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CoveredDays=150" .

hemo:7002145 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Covered days in the 180-day period from the five shifted fills"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With shifted starts on days 1, 31, 61, 121 and 211, fills 1 to 3 add 30 days each, fill 4 adds the 60 days from day 121 to day 180 and fill 5 adds none, 150 covered days in all. The other 60 days of supply fall after day 180." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Covered days in the 180-day period from the five shifted fills" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n = 5; S_i = [30,30,30,90,30]; a_i = [1,31,61,121,211]; E = 180; C = 150" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PDC-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "covered-days-in-the-180-day-period-from-the-five-shifted-fills" .

hemo:7002146 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Covered days over a 240-day period from the same shifted fills"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Extending the period to day 240 lets fills 4 and 5 count in full, so all 210 days of supply are covered and only the 30-day gap from day 91 to day 120 is uncovered, a PDC of 0.875 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Covered days over a 240-day period from the same shifted fills" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n = 5; S_i = [30,30,30,90,30]; a_i = [1,31,61,121,211]; E = 240; C = 210" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PDC-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "covered-days-over-a-240-day-period-from-the-same-shifted-fills" .

hemo:7002147 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Facility supplies the medicine during an inpatient stay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The patient receives the medicine from the facility during the stay, so stay days are neither covered nor uncovered by pharmacy fills, and any supply accumulated during the stay can be used after returning home." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Facility supplies the medicine during an inpatient stay" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PDC-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "facility-supplies-the-medicine-during-an-inpatient-stay" .

hemo:7002148 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Stay supply shifted only to uncovered days after discharge"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Supply that overlaps a stay moves only to days without coverage after discharge. When there are none, as in the second inpatient stay example of Attachment L (Example 2, Tables L-8 and L-9), the supply is not shifted and the covered stay days simply leave the numerator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Stay supply shifted only to uncovered days after discharge" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PDC-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "stay-supply-shifted-only-to-uncovered-days-after-discharge" .

hemo:7002149 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Stay-adjusted PDC from named covered-day, period and stay cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000457 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel divides the named cell holding the covered days outside stays by the period length less the stay days." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Stay-adjusted PDC from named covered-day, period and stay cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-PDC-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "stay-adjusted-pdc-from-named-covered-day-period-and-stay-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CoveredDaysAdj/(PeriodDays-StayDays)" .

hemo:7002150 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Stay-adjusted covered days fit in the days outside stays"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Stay days are fewer than the days in the period, and the covered days outside stays cannot exceed the days outside stays. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows stay days left in the numerator, or stays spanning the whole period, in which case CMS excludes the patient." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Stay-adjusted covered days fit in the days outside stays" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PDC-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "stay-adjusted-covered-days-fit-in-the-days-outside-stays" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(StayDays<PeriodDays,CoveredDaysAdj<=PeriodDays-StayDays)" .

hemo:7002151 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Stay adjustment reproduces the CMS 92% example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With CoveredDaysAdj 12, PeriodDays 15 and StayDays 2, and the result in a cell named StayAdjustedPDC, the percentage rounds to 92. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 80 shows the stay days left in the denominator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Stay adjustment reproduces the CMS 92% example" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PDC-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "stay-adjustment-reproduces-the-cms-92-example" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(StayAdjustedPDC*100,0)=92" .

hemo:7002152 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Ten-day inpatient stay inside the gap of the five-fill history"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the patient in the article's example was an inpatient on days 95 to 104, inside the gap, those 10 days leave the denominator. No supply overlapped the stay, so nothing is shifted, the numerator stays at 150 and the PDC rises from about 0.833 to 150 / 170, about 0.882." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ten-day inpatient stay inside the gap of the five-fill history" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_adj = 150; T = 180; H = 10; PDC_stay = 0.8824" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PDC-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ten-day-inpatient-stay-inside-the-gap-of-the-five-fill-history" .

hemo:7002153 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "CMS example with supply shifted to the days after an inpatient stay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the first inpatient stay example of Attachment L (Example 1, Tables L-6 and L-7), a 15-day period with coverage on days 1 to 8 and 12 to 15 and an inpatient stay on days 5 and 6 has a PDC of 12 out of 15, 80%. Removing the stay days and shifting their 2 days of supply to days 9 and 10 gives 12 covered days out of 13, 92%." ;
    hemo:9000009 "CMS example with supply shifted to the days after an inpatient stay" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_adj = 12; T = 15; H = 2; PDC_stay = 0.9231" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PDC-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cms-example-with-supply-shifted-to-the-days-after-an-inpatient-stay" .

hemo:7002154 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "CMS example where the stay adjustment lowers the PDC"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the second inpatient stay example of Attachment L (Example 2, Tables L-8 and L-9), coverage on days 1 to 7 and 12 to 15 with a stay on days 12 and 13 gives 11 out of 15 before adjustment, 73%. The covered stay days are removed and no uncovered days follow the stay to receive their supply, so the PDC becomes 9 out of 13, 69%." ;
    hemo:9000009 "CMS example where the stay adjustment lowers the PDC" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_adj = 9; T = 15; H = 2; PDC_stay = 0.6923" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PDC-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cms-example-where-the-stay-adjustment-lowers-the-pdc" .

hemo:7002155 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Dispensed supply taken as directed"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Possession stands for use: medicine dispensed is assumed to be taken as prescribed. Patients may give medicine to others, discard it before refilling or stockpile it, none of which the ratio can detect." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Dispensed supply taken as directed" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MPR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "dispensed-supply-taken-as-directed" .

hemo:7002156 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Window long enough after the first dispensing"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Measurement starts with a dispensing, which biases the ratio upwards over short windows. In an asthma cohort whose fills typically lasted 2 to 3 months, the bias was most pronounced over periods shorter than about 9 months." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Window long enough after the first dispensing" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MPR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "window-long-enough-after-the-first-dispensing" .

hemo:7002157 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed-interval MPR from a supply range and window days"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000458 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel sums the named range holding the days' supply of the fills dispensed in the window and divides by the days from the named first dispensing day to the named end day, inclusive." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fixed-interval MPR from a supply range and window days" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MPR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fixed-interval-mpr-from-a-supply-range-and-window-days" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUM(Supplies)/(EndDay-FirstFillDay+1)" .

hemo:7002158 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed-interval MPR reproduces the article's 1.167"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Supplies 30, 30, 30, 90 and 30, FirstFillDay 1 and EndDay 180, and the result in a cell named MPRFixed, the ratio rounded to three decimals is 1.167. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 1.173 (computed here for illustration) shows the window counted as 179 days, without adding 1 for the first day." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fixed-interval MPR reproduces the article's 1.167" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MPR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fixed-interval-mpr-reproduces-the-article-s-1-167" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(MPRFixed,3)=1.167" .

hemo:7002159 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed-interval MPR is at least the PDC on the same fills"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For one drug over the same window, every covered day counted by the proportion of days covered (HE-FM-PDC-001) uses a day of dispensed supply, so the fixed-interval MPR cannot fall below the PDC. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the two measures computed on different windows or fill sets." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fixed-interval MPR is at least the PDC on the same fills" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MPR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fixed-interval-mpr-is-at-least-the-pdc-on-the-same-fills" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MPRFixed>=PDC" .

hemo:7002160 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed-interval MPR of the five-fill history over 180 days"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The article's five fills (days 1, 22, 45, 121 and 170) supply 30 + 30 + 30 + 90 + 30 = 210 days over a 180-day window, so the fixed-interval MPR is 210 / 180, about 1.167, although days 91 to 120 had no medicine." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fixed-interval MPR of the five-fill history over 180 days" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n = 5; S_i = [30,30,30,90,30]; D = 180; MPR_fixed = 1.1667" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MPR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fixed-interval-mpr-of-the-five-fill-history-over-180-days" .

hemo:7002161 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed-interval MPR when the patient stops after the third fill"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the patient in the same example made no fill after day 45, the three fills supply 90 days and the ratio over the 180-day window is 0.5, so the fixed interval records the discontinuation (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fixed-interval MPR when the patient stops after the third fill" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n = 3; S_i = [30,30,30]; D = 180; MPR_fixed = 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MPR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fixed-interval-mpr-when-the-patient-stops-after-the-third-fill" .

hemo:7002162 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment ends when the last supply runs out"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The interval closes at the end of the last fill's supply, so the formula assumes nothing after it matters. A patient who stops after a fill and one who continues beyond the window can have the same ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Treatment ends when the last supply runs out" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MPR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "treatment-ends-when-the-last-supply-runs-out" .

hemo:7002163 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "At least two fills on different days for the refill interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The refill interval needs a first and a last dispensing on different days. With one fill the ratio is that fill's supply over itself, 1 by construction, which says nothing about adherence." ;
    hemo:9000009 "At least two fills on different days for the refill interval" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MPR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "at-least-two-fills-on-different-days-for-the-refill-interval" .

hemo:7002164 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Refill-interval MPR from named first and last fill cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000459 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel sums the named supply range and divides by the named last dispensing day less the first, plus the named last fill's supply." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Refill-interval MPR from named first and last fill cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MPR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "refill-interval-mpr-from-named-first-and-last-fill-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUM(Supplies)/(LastFillDay-FirstFillDay+LastSupply)" .

hemo:7002165 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Refill-interval MPR reproduces the article's 1.055"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Supplies 30, 30, 30, 90 and 30, FirstFillDay 1, LastFillDay 170 and LastSupply 30, and the result in a cell named MPRRefill, the ratio rounded to three decimals is 1.055. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 1.243 (computed here for illustration) shows the last fill's supply left out of the denominator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Refill-interval MPR reproduces the article's 1.055" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MPR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "refill-interval-mpr-reproduces-the-article-s-1-055" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(MPRRefill,3)=1.055" .

hemo:7002166 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Refill-interval MPR has two dispensings on different days"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a patient with a single dispensing, for whom the ratio is 1 by construction and is better reported separately." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Refill-interval MPR has two dispensings on different days" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MPR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "refill-interval-mpr-has-two-dispensings-on-different-days" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LastFillDay>FirstFillDay" .

hemo:7002167 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Refill-interval MPR of the five-fill history"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The first and last dispensings are 169 days apart (day 1 to day 170), and adding the last fill's 30 days gives a denominator of 199, so the ratio is 210 / 199, about 1.055." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Refill-interval MPR of the five-fill history" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n = 5; S_i = [30,30,30,90,30]; f_1 = 1; f_n = 170; S_n = 30; MPR_refill = 1.0553" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MPR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "refill-interval-mpr-of-the-five-fill-history" .

hemo:7002168 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Refill-interval MPR when the patient stops after the third fill"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the patient stops after fill 3 on day 45, the denominator is 44 + 30 = 74 days and the ratio is 90 / 74, about 1.216, against 0.5 for the fixed interval, because the time after the last fill is not counted (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Refill-interval MPR when the patient stops after the third fill" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n = 3; S_i = [30,30,30]; f_1 = 1; f_n = 45; S_n = 30; MPR_refill = 1.2162" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MPR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "refill-interval-mpr-when-the-patient-stops-after-the-third-fill" .

hemo:7002169 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Refilling between first and last dispensing describes adherence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The ratio takes the pattern of refills up to the last dispensing as the measure of adherence and does not account for discontinuation after it. It needs at least two fills on different days." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Refilling between first and last dispensing describes adherence" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MPR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "refilling-between-first-and-last-dispensing-describes-adherence" .

hemo:7002170 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "MPRm from a supply range and named first and last fill cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000460 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel subtracts the named last fill's supply from the summed supply range and divides by the named last dispensing day less the first." ;
    hemo:9000009 "MPRm from a supply range and named first and last fill cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MPR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mprm-from-a-supply-range-and-named-first-and-last-fill-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(SUM(Supplies)-LastSupply)/(LastFillDay-FirstFillDay)" .

hemo:7002171 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "MPRm reproduces 1.065 for the article's fills"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Supplies 30, 30, 30, 90 and 30, LastSupply 30, FirstFillDay 1 and LastFillDay 170, and the result in a cell named MPRModified, the ratio rounded to three decimals is 1.065. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 1.243 (computed here for illustration) shows the last fill's supply left in the numerator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "MPRm reproduces 1.065 for the article's fills" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MPR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mprm-reproduces-1-065-for-the-article-s-fills" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(MPRModified,3)=1.065" .

hemo:7002172 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "MPRm has at least two fills in the supply range"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The MPRm needs at least two fills, and the last dispensing has to fall after the first, or its denominator is zero. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a single dispensing, or fills all dispensed on one day, for which the MPRm is undefined." ;
    hemo:9000009 "MPRm has at least two fills in the supply range" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MPR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mprm-has-at-least-two-fills-in-the-supply-range" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(COUNT(Supplies)>=2,LastFillDay>FirstFillDay)" .

hemo:7002173 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "MPRm of the five-fill history"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Leaving out fill 5's 30 days gives 180 days of supply over the 169 days from day 1 to day 170, a ratio of about 1.065 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "MPRm of the five-fill history" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n = 5; S_i = [30,30,30,90,30]; S_n = 30; f_1 = 1; f_n = 170; MPR_m = 1.0651" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MPR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mprm-of-the-five-fill-history" .

hemo:7002174 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "MPRm when the patient stops after the third fill"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With fills 1 to 3 only, 60 days of supply over the 44 days from day 1 to day 45 give about 1.364 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "MPRm when the patient stops after the third fill" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n = 3; S_i = [30,30,30]; S_n = 30; f_1 = 1; f_n = 45; MPR_m = 1.3636" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MPR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mprm-when-the-patient-stops-after-the-third-fill" .

hemo:7002175 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Cap applied to each patient's ratio before averaging"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The cap is applied to each patient's ratio, and the variant it is applied to is stated, because capping does not reconcile different denominators." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cap applied to each patient's ratio before averaging" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MPR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cap-applied-to-each-patient-s-ratio-before-averaging" .

hemo:7002176 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Capped MPR from a named uncapped ratio cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000461 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel takes the smaller of the named cell holding the uncapped ratio and 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Capped MPR from a named uncapped ratio cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MPR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "capped-mpr-from-a-named-uncapped-ratio-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MIN(MPRUncapped,1)" .

hemo:7002177 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Capped MPR does not exceed 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the cap omitted or applied to an average instead of to the patient's ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Capped MPR does not exceed 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MPR-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "capped-mpr-does-not-exceed-1" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MPRCapped<=1" .

hemo:7002178 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Capped MPR does not exceed the uncapped MPR"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Capping can only lower a ratio. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the capped and uncapped cells taken from different variants or patients." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Capped MPR does not exceed the uncapped MPR" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MPR-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "capped-mpr-does-not-exceed-the-uncapped-mpr" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MPRCapped<=MPRUncapped" .

hemo:7002179 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Capped fixed-interval MPR of the five-fill history"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The fixed-interval MPR of about 1.167 for the article's fills is capped at 1.000, which reads as perfect adherence although 30 of the 180 days had no medicine." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Capped fixed-interval MPR of the five-fill history" ;
    hemo:9000014 "MPR = 1.1667; MPR_capped = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MPR-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "capped-fixed-interval-mpr-of-the-five-fill-history" .

hemo:7002180 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cap leaves an MPR below 1 unchanged"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A patient who stops after the third fill has a fixed-interval MPR of 0.5, which the cap leaves unchanged (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cap leaves an MPR below 1 unchanged" ;
    hemo:9000014 "MPR = 0.5; MPR_capped = 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MPR-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cap-leaves-an-mpr-below-1-unchanged" .

hemo:7002181 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "No tied ranks in the Begg test"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "No two standardised effects and no two variances are equal, so the null variance K(K-1)(2K+5)/18 applies without the tie corrections in Stata's exact formula. Studies of identical precision create ties, and the Cochrane Handbook advises against tests for funnel plot asymmetry when studies have similar standard errors." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No tied ranks in the Begg test" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BEGG-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-tied-ranks-in-the-begg-test" .

hemo:7002182 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Enough studies of differing size for the Begg test"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The normal approximation and the power of the test are poor with few studies. The Cochrane Handbook reports the rule of thumb that tests for funnel plot asymmetry be used only when a meta-analysis includes at least 10 studies, and not when the studies have similar standard errors, with the result read alongside the funnel plot." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Enough studies of differing size for the Begg test" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BEGG-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "enough-studies-of-differing-size-for-the-begg-test" .

hemo:7002183 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Begg normal statistic from named pair counts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000462 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel divides concordant minus discordant pairs, from the named cells, by the number of pairs to give tau in a cell named KendallTau, and by the square root of the null variance for the named number of studies to give the statistic in a cell named BeggZ. =2*(1-NORM.S.DIST(ABS(BeggZ),TRUE)) then gives the two-sided p-value; the continuity-corrected version uses ABS(Concordant-Discordant)-1 as the numerator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Begg normal statistic from named pair counts" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BEGG-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "begg-normal-statistic-from-named-pair-counts" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(Concordant-Discordant)/(Studies*(Studies-1)/2); =(Concordant-Discordant)/SQRT(Studies*(Studies-1)*(2*Studies+5)/18)" .

hemo:7002184 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Begg pair counts do not exceed the number of study pairs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each pair of studies is compared once, so concordant plus discordant pairs cannot exceed K(K-1)/2, and equal it when there are no ties. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows each pair counted in both directions, 90 comparisons instead of 45 for ten studies." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Begg pair counts do not exceed the number of study pairs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BEGG-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "begg-pair-counts-do-not-exceed-the-number-of-study-pairs" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Concordant+Discordant<=Studies*(Studies-1)/2" .

hemo:7002185 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Begg statistic reproduces the article's tau of -0.511"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Concordant 11, Discordant 34 and Studies 10, and tau in a cell named KendallTau, tau rounded to three decimals is -0.511. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at -1.022 shows pairs counted in both directions without halving (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Begg statistic reproduces the article's tau of -0.511" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BEGG-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "begg-statistic-reproduces-the-article-s-tau-of-0-511" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(KendallTau,3)=-0.511" .

hemo:7002186 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Begg statistic for the article's ten illustrative trials"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The article's ten illustrative trials behind a model's hazard ratio give 11 concordant and 34 discordant pairs out of 45, so S is -23, tau is about -0.511, Var(S) is 125 and Z is about -2.06, a two-sided p-value of about 0.040. With the continuity correction the absolute statistic is 22 divided by 11.18, about 1.97 (p about 0.049), and the exact permutation p-value is about 0.047." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Begg statistic for the article's ten illustrative trials" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C = 11; D = 34; K = 10; S = -23; tau = -0.5111; Var_S = 125; Z = -2.0572" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BEGG-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "begg-statistic-for-the-article-s-ten-illustrative-trials" .

hemo:7002187 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Perfect ordering of four studies in the Begg test"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With four studies in perfect order, 6 concordant pairs and none discordant, tau is 1 and the uncorrected Z is about 2.04, above 1.96. The exact two-sided p-value for a perfect ordering with no ties is 2 divided by 4 factorial, about 0.083." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Perfect ordering of four studies in the Begg test" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C = 6; D = 0; K = 4; S = 6; tau = 1; Var_S = 8.6667; Z = 2.0381" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BEGG-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "perfect-ordering-of-four-studies-in-the-begg-test" .

hemo:7002188 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Effect estimates on an approximately normal scale for the Begg test"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each theta_j is on a scale where its sampling distribution is close to normal and v_j is its within-study variance, so ratio measures enter on the log scale. Odds ratios and standardised mean differences are naturally correlated with their standard errors, which can create asymmetry without any small-study effect." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Effect estimates on an approximately normal scale for the Begg test" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BEGG-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "effect-estimates-on-an-approximately-normal-scale-for-the-begg-test" .

hemo:7002189 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Common-effect pooled estimate in the Begg standardisation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The standardisation uses the inverse-variance common-effect estimate, as in Stata's implementation of the test, whatever model the meta-analysis itself reports." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Common-effect pooled estimate in the Begg standardisation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BEGG-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "common-effect-pooled-estimate-in-the-begg-standardisation" .

hemo:7002190 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Standardised Begg effect from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000463 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel subtracts the named cell holding the pooled estimate from the study's effect and divides by the square root of the study's variance less one over the sum of the weights." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standardised Begg effect from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BEGG-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standardised-begg-effect-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(Effect-PooledEffect)/SQRT(StudyVariance-1/SumWeights)" .

hemo:7002191 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted deviations from the Begg pooled estimate sum to zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the effects in a range named Effects and the inverse-variance weights in a range named Weights, the weighted deviations from the pooled estimate in the cell named PooledEffect cancel. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an unweighted mean, or a random-effects mean, entered as the pooled estimate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted deviations from the Begg pooled estimate sum to zero" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BEGG-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-deviations-from-the-begg-pooled-estimate-sum-to-zero" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(Weights,Effects-PooledEffect))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002192 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Begg standardised effect reproduces the article's trial 1 value"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Effect -0.12 and StudyVariance 0.0036 for trial 1, and PooledEffect and SumWeights computed from the ten trials (about -0.1735 and 743.66), the result in a cell named StandardisedEffect rounds to 1.13. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 0.89 shows the variance correction left out (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Begg standardised effect reproduces the article's trial 1 value" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BEGG-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "begg-standardised-effect-reproduces-the-article-s-trial-1-value" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(StandardisedEffect,2)=1.13" .

hemo:7002193 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standardised effect of the most precise of ten trials"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's ten illustrative trials the weights sum to 743.66 and the pooled log hazard ratio is -0.1735. Trial 1, with a log hazard ratio of -0.12 and a standard error of 0.06 (variance 0.0036), has a standardised effect of 0.0535 divided by 0.0475, about 1.13." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standardised effect of the most precise of ten trials" ;
    hemo:9000014 "theta_j = -0.12; theta_IV = -0.1735; v_j = 0.0036; W = 743.66; t_j = 1.1266" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BEGG-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standardised-effect-of-the-most-precise-of-ten-trials" .

hemo:7002194 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standardised effect of the least precise trial with the largest benefit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Trial 9, with a log hazard ratio of -0.55 and a standard error of 0.28 (variance 0.0784), has a standardised effect of about -1.36, the lowest of the ten, so a large benefit in an imprecise trial drives the negative rank correlation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standardised effect of the least precise trial with the largest benefit" ;
    hemo:9000014 "theta_j = -0.55; theta_IV = -0.1735; v_j = 0.0784; W = 743.66; t_j = -1.3563" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BEGG-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standardised-effect-of-the-least-precise-trial-with-the-largest-benefit" .

hemo:7002195 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Price enters the incremental cost linearly"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The incremental cost per patient is u times the unit price plus Delta_C_0, and neither Delta_E nor Delta_C_0 depends on the price. Inputs that act through a non-linear model, such as hazard ratios, need repeated model runs or a numerical search." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Price enters the incremental cost linearly" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BEA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "price-enters-the-incremental-cost-linearly" .

hemo:7002196 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Other inputs held at their base-case values"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every other input stays at its base case while the price varies. PMG36 (section 4.7.23) states that threshold analysis is not suitable for parameters highly correlated with other influential parameters, and should not be used to justify restricting the population to a subgroup on cost-effectiveness grounds." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Other inputs held at their base-case values" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BEA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "other-inputs-held-at-their-base-case-values" .

hemo:7002197 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Break-even price compared with the net price paid by the NHS"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The result is compared with the price the NHS would actually pay, including known price reductions such as patient access schemes, which PMG36 (section 4.4.4) requires in reference-case analyses, not with the list price." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Break-even price compared with the net price paid by the NHS" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BEA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "break-even-price-compared-with-the-net-price-paid-by-the-nhs" .

hemo:7002198 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Break-even unit price from named threshold, effect and cost cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000464 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel subtracts the named cell holding the incremental cost other than acquisition from the threshold multiplied by the incremental QALYs, and divides by the named cell holding the units per patient." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Break-even unit price from named threshold, effect and cost cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BEA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "break-even-unit-price-from-named-threshold-effect-and-cost-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(Threshold*DeltaE-DeltaCOther)/UnitsPerPatient" .

hemo:7002199 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Cost-neutral unit price from named cost and unit cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000464 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel reverses the sign of the named cell holding the incremental cost other than acquisition and divides by the units per patient." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cost-neutral unit price from named cost and unit cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BEA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cost-neutral-unit-price-from-named-cost-and-unit-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=-DeltaCOther/UnitsPerPatient" .

hemo:7002200 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Incremental net monetary benefit is zero at the break-even price"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the result in a cell named BreakEvenPrice, incremental net monetary benefit recomputed at that price from its definition is zero. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the other cost difference entered with the wrong sign, or the units per patient left out." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Incremental net monetary benefit is zero at the break-even price" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BEA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "incremental-net-monetary-benefit-is-zero-at-the-break-even-price" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(Threshold*DeltaE-(UnitsPerPatient*BreakEvenPrice+DeltaCOther))<1E-6" .

hemo:7002201 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gap between break-even and cost-neutral prices equals the value of the gain per unit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the cost-neutral price in a cell named CostNeutralPrice, the break-even price exceeds it by the threshold value of the health gain per unit. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the sign of the other cost difference not reversed in the cost-neutral price." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gap between break-even and cost-neutral prices equals the value of the gain per unit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BEA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gap-between-break-even-and-cost-neutral-prices-equals-the-value-of-the-gain-per-unit" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(BreakEvenPrice-CostNeutralPrice-Threshold*DeltaE/UnitsPerPatient)<1E-6" .

hemo:7002202 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Break-even price reproduces the article's 13,000 pounds per course"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Threshold 25000, DeltaE 0.4, DeltaCOther -3000 and UnitsPerPatient 1, the break-even price is 13,000. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 10,000 shows the cost offsets ignored, and FALSE at 7,000 shows the other cost difference added instead of subtracted (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Break-even price reproduces the article's 13,000 pounds per course" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BEA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "break-even-price-reproduces-the-article-s-13-000-pounds-per-course" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=BreakEvenPrice=13000" .

hemo:7002203 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Break-even and cost-neutral prices of one course at 25,000 pounds per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative medicine, one course per patient gains 0.40 QALYs, and the rest of the pathway adds £2,000 and avoids £5,000, so Delta_C_0 is -£3,000. At £25,000 per QALY the break-even price is £13,000 per course, against a proposed net price of £14,000, and the cost-neutral price is £3,000." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Break-even and cost-neutral prices of one course at 25,000 pounds per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 25000; Delta_E = 0.4; Delta_C_0 = -3000; u = 1; p_star = 13000; p_0 = 3000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BEA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "break-even-and-cost-neutral-prices-of-one-course-at-25-000-pounds-per-qaly" .

hemo:7002204 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Break-even price of the same course at 35,000 pounds per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At £35,000 per QALY the break-even price of the same course rises to £17,000, so the proposed net price of £14,000 is already below it; only the threshold has changed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Break-even price of the same course at 35,000 pounds per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 35000; Delta_E = 0.4; Delta_C_0 = -3000; u = 1; p_star = 17000; p_0 = 3000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BEA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "break-even-price-of-the-same-course-at-35-000-pounds-per-qaly" .

hemo:7002205 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Break-even price per pack when the course is 12 monthly packs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the same course were supplied as 12 monthly packs, the break-even price at £25,000 per QALY would be about £1,083.33 per pack and the cost-neutral price £250 per pack (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Break-even price per pack when the course is 12 monthly packs" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 25000; Delta_E = 0.4; Delta_C_0 = -3000; u = 12; p_star = 1083.33; p_0 = 250" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BEA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "break-even-price-per-pack-when-the-course-is-12-monthly-packs" .

hemo:7002206 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Costs linear and fixed or variable within the relevant range"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Fixed costs stay fixed in total and variable costs stay fixed per unit over the range of activity considered, and the price per unit does not change with volume." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Costs linear and fixed or variable within the relevant range" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BEA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "costs-linear-and-fixed-or-variable-within-the-relevant-range" .

hemo:7002207 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed costs constant only up to capacity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Above the capacity of the current fixed resources, fixed costs step up, and a new break-even volume applies to each block of capacity. Decisions about extra activity within a block rest on marginal cost, not on an average cost that includes a share of fixed costs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fixed costs constant only up to capacity" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BEA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fixed-costs-constant-only-up-to-capacity" .

hemo:7002208 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Break-even volume from named fixed cost, tariff and variable cost cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000465 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel divides the named cell holding the fixed cost for the period by the tariff less the variable cost per unit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Break-even volume from named fixed cost, tariff and variable cost cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BEA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "break-even-volume-from-named-fixed-cost-tariff-and-variable-cost-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=FixedCost/(Tariff-VariableCost)" .

hemo:7002209 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Margin of safety from named expected activity and break-even cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000465 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel subtracts the named break-even volume from the expected activity and divides by the expected activity." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Margin of safety from named expected activity and break-even cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BEA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "margin-of-safety-from-named-expected-activity-and-break-even-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(ExpectedActivity-BreakEvenVolume)/ExpectedActivity" .

hemo:7002210 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Surplus is zero at the break-even volume"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the result in a cell named BreakEvenVolume, the contribution earned at that volume exactly covers the fixed cost. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the fixed cost divided by the tariff instead of by the contribution per unit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Surplus is zero at the break-even volume" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BEA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "surplus-is-zero-at-the-break-even-volume" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(BreakEvenVolume*(Tariff-VariableCost)-FixedCost)<1E-6" .

hemo:7002211 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Tariff exceeds variable cost so that a break-even volume exists"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A break-even volume exists only if each unit contributes something towards fixed costs. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE means every extra unit adds to the loss, and the formula returns a meaningless negative volume." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Tariff exceeds variable cost so that a break-even volume exists" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BEA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "tariff-exceeds-variable-cost-so-that-a-break-even-volume-exists" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Tariff>VariableCost" .

hemo:7002212 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Margin of safety reproduces the day unit example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With FixedCost 270000, Tariff 160, VariableCost 70 and ExpectedActivity 3600, and the result in a cell named MarginOfSafety, the margin rounded to three decimals is 0.167. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 0.2 shows the gap divided by the break-even volume instead of the expected activity (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Margin of safety reproduces the day unit example" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BEA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "margin-of-safety-reproduces-the-day-unit-example" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(MarginOfSafety,3)=0.167" .

hemo:7002213 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Day unit break-even at 3,000 attendances"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative day unit, paid £160 per attendance with variable costs of £70 and fixed costs of £270,000 a year, the contribution is £90 and the break-even volume is 3,000 attendances. With 3,600 attendances expected the margin of safety is about 0.167, or 17%, and the surplus is £54,000." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Day unit break-even at 3,000 attendances" ;
    hemo:9000014 "F = 270000; P = 160; V = 70; Q_e = 3600; Q_star = 3000; MS = 0.1667" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BEA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "day-unit-break-even-at-3-000-attendances" .

hemo:7002214 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Day unit break-even with a second team above 4,000 attendances"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If growth beyond a capacity of 4,000 attendances needs a second team costing £120,000 a year, fixed costs become £390,000 and the break-even volume is about 4,333.3, so the unit only covers its costs again at 4,334 attendances. With 4,500 attendances expected the margin of safety would be about 0.037 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Day unit break-even with a second team above 4,000 attendances" ;
    hemo:9000014 "F = 390000; P = 160; V = 70; Q_e = 4500; Q_star = 4333.33; MS = 0.037" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BEA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "day-unit-break-even-with-a-second-team-above-4-000-attendances" .

hemo:7002215 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Utility additive in log income and health"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Utility is ln Y plus b times h, so the marginal utility of income falls as income rises and the compensating and equivalent variations differ. Weber shows that the two Hicksian measures coincide at every income only when indirect utility is additively separable in income, as with utility linear in income." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Utility additive in log income and health" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVAR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "utility-additive-in-log-income-and-health" .

hemo:7002216 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Health state fixed for the person after the change"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The person cannot buy more or less of the new health state, the quantity case often called the compensating surplus, and the valuation covers one period at the stated income." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Health state fixed for the person after the change" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVAR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "health-state-fixed-for-the-person-after-the-change" .

hemo:7002217 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Compensating variation from named income, coefficient and health change cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000466 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel multiplies the named cell holding income by one less the exponential of minus the health coefficient times the health change." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Compensating variation from named income, coefficient and health change cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CVAR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "compensating-variation-from-named-income-coefficient-and-health-change-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Income*(1-EXP(-HealthCoef*HealthChange))" .

hemo:7002218 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Compensating variation reproduces the article's 4,178.76"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Income 30000, HealthCoef 1 and HealthChange 0.15, and the result in a cell named CompVar, the value rounded to two decimals is 4,178.76. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 4,855.03 shows the equivalent variation formula used instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Compensating variation reproduces the article's 4,178.76" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVAR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "compensating-variation-reproduces-the-article-s-4-178-76" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(CompVar,2)=4178.76" .

hemo:7002219 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Compensating variation does not exceed the linear value of the change"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "One less the exponential of minus x is never above x, so for gains and losses alike the compensating variation is at most income times the coefficient times the change. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the equivalent variation form, the exponential of x less one, used in its place." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Compensating variation does not exceed the linear value of the change" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVAR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "compensating-variation-does-not-exceed-the-linear-value-of-the-change" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CompVar<=Income*HealthCoef*HealthChange" .

hemo:7002220 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Sign of the compensating variation follows the health change"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A gain gives a positive compensating variation and a loss a negative one. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the sign of the exponent reversed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sign of the compensating variation follows the health change" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVAR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sign-of-the-compensating-variation-follows-the-health-change" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SIGN(CompVar)=SIGN(HealthCoef*HealthChange)" .

hemo:7002221 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Compensating variation of a gain from 0.60 to 0.75 in a health index"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With an annual income of £30,000 and b equal to 1, a programme that raises the health index from 0.60 to 0.75 has a compensating variation of £4,178.76, the most the person would pay for the gain." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Compensating variation of a gain from 0.60 to 0.75 in a health index" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y = 30000; b = 1; Delta_h = 0.15; CV = 4178.76" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVAR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "compensating-variation-of-a-gain-from-0-60-to-0-75-in-a-health-index" .

hemo:7002222 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Compensating variation of a loss from 0.60 to 0.45 in a health index"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A loss of the same size has a compensating variation of -£4,855.03 (as in the Equivalent Variation article's loss example): the person would need at least £4,855.03 to accept it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Compensating variation of a loss from 0.60 to 0.45 in a health index" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y = 30000; b = 1; Delta_h = -0.15; CV = -4855.03" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVAR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "compensating-variation-of-a-loss-from-0-60-to-0-45-in-a-health-index" .

hemo:7002223 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Logit errors and utility linear in income for the log-sum formula"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The unobserved parts of utility are independent and identically distributed extreme value, and the marginal utility of income is constant, so the formula cannot separate compensating from equivalent variation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Logit errors and utility linear in income for the log-sum formula" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVAR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "logit-errors-and-utility-linear-in-income-for-the-log-sum-formula" .

hemo:7002224 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Change small relative to income for the log-sum formula"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Train notes that the formula can be used for changes that alter consumer surplus by small amounts per person relative to income, even though in reality the marginal utility of income varies with income. Lancsar and Savage and Ryan disagreed over when health studies should apply it, so the choice of model is a judgement for each study." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Change small relative to income for the log-sum formula" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVAR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "change-small-relative-to-income-for-the-log-sum-formula" .

hemo:7002225 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Log-sum compensating variation from named utility ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000467 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the representative utilities before and after the change in ranges named UtilitiesBefore and UtilitiesAfter and alpha, entered as a positive number, in a cell named MargUtilIncome, Excel takes the difference in the logs of the sums of exponentials and divides by alpha. SUMPRODUCT makes the exponentials evaluate as arrays in any version." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log-sum compensating variation from named utility ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CVAR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-sum-compensating-variation-from-named-utility-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(LN(SUMPRODUCT(EXP(UtilitiesAfter)))-LN(SUMPRODUCT(EXP(UtilitiesBefore))))/MargUtilIncome" .

hemo:7002226 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Log-sum value lies below the improved alternative's utility gain in money"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When only one alternative improves, from ServiceUtilityBefore to ServiceUtilityAfter, the money value per chooser in a cell named LogsumCV is positive and below that alternative's utility gain divided by alpha, because some choosers take other alternatives. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the raw negative cost coefficient used as alpha, or the improved alternative's utility gain divided by alpha used in place of the log-sum." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log-sum value lies below the improved alternative's utility gain in money" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVAR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-sum-value-lies-below-the-improved-alternative-s-utility-gain-in-money" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(MargUtilIncome>0,LogsumCV>0,LogsumCV<(ServiceUtilityAfter-ServiceUtilityBefore)/MargUtilIncome)" .

hemo:7002227 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Log-sum value reproduces the illustrative 26.71"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With UtilitiesBefore 0 and 0.5, UtilitiesAfter 0 and 0.9 and MargUtilIncome 0.01, the value in LogsumCV rounded to two decimals is 26.71. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 40 shows the service's utility gain divided by alpha instead of the log-sum (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log-sum value reproduces the illustrative 26.71" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVAR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-sum-value-reproduces-the-illustrative-26-71" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(LogsumCV,2)=26.71" .

hemo:7002228 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Log-sum value of improving a service against an opt-out"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A choice between opting out (utility 0) and a service (utility 0.5) changes when the service improves to utility 0.9. With a cost coefficient of -0.01 per pound, alpha is 0.01 and the log-sum compensating variation is about £26.71 per person (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log-sum value of improving a service against an opt-out" ;
    hemo:9000014 "J0 = 2; V0_j = [0,0.5]; J1 = 2; V1_j = [0,0.9]; alpha = 0.01; CV = 26.71" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVAR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-sum-value-of-improving-a-service-against-an-opt-out" .

hemo:7002229 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Log-sum value of adding a third alternative to a choice set"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Adding a new alternative with utility 0.3 to the original opt-out and service, with nothing else changed, gives about £41.19 per person (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log-sum value of adding a third alternative to a choice set" ;
    hemo:9000014 "J0 = 2; V0_j = [0,0.5]; J1 = 3; V1_j = [0,0.5,0.3]; alpha = 0.01; CV = 41.19" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVAR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-sum-value-of-adding-a-third-alternative-to-a-choice-set" .

hemo:7002230 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Utility additive in log income and health, valued at the status quo"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Utility is ln Y plus b times h, and the money is measured at the status quo, without the change, with utility held at its level after the change. Under this utility the money value rises with income, so the equivalent variation is at least the compensating variation, as Weber shows for any change whose money value does not fall as income rises." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Utility additive in log income and health, valued at the status quo" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVAR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "utility-additive-in-log-income-and-health-valued-at-the-status-quo" .

hemo:7002231 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Health state not purchasable by the person"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The person cannot buy the new health state, so the measure is the quantity case often called the equivalent surplus, valued for one period at the stated income." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Health state not purchasable by the person" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVAR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "health-state-not-purchasable-by-the-person" .

hemo:7002232 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Equivalent variation from named income, coefficient and health change cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000468 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel multiplies the named cell holding income by the exponential of the health coefficient times the health change, less one." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equivalent variation from named income, coefficient and health change cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVAR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equivalent-variation-from-named-income-coefficient-and-health-change-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Income*(EXP(HealthCoef*HealthChange)-1)" .

hemo:7002233 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equivalent variation reproduces the article's 4,855.03"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Income 30000, HealthCoef 1 and HealthChange 0.15, and the result in a cell named EquivVar, the value rounded to two decimals is 4,855.03. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 4,178.76 shows the compensating variation formula used instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equivalent variation reproduces the article's 4,855.03" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVAR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equivalent-variation-reproduces-the-article-s-4-855-03" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(EquivVar,2)=4855.03" .

hemo:7002234 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equivalent variation is at least the linear value of the change"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The exponential of x less one is never below x, so for gains and losses alike the equivalent variation is at least income times the coefficient times the change. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the compensating variation form used in its place." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equivalent variation is at least the linear value of the change" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVAR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equivalent-variation-is-at-least-the-linear-value-of-the-change" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EquivVar>=Income*HealthCoef*HealthChange" .

hemo:7002235 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equivalent variation is not below the compensating variation of the same change"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the compensating variation of the same change, from the same named cells, in a cell named CompVar, the equivalent variation is at least as large for a gain or a loss. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the two formulas swapped." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equivalent variation is not below the compensating variation of the same change" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVAR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equivalent-variation-is-not-below-the-compensating-variation-of-the-same-change" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EquivVar>=CompVar" .

hemo:7002236 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equivalent variation of a gain from 0.60 to 0.75 in a health index"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With an annual income of £30,000 and b equal to 1, a programme that raises the health index from 0.60 to 0.75 has an equivalent variation of £4,855.03, the least the person would accept to forgo the gain and £676.27 more than its compensating variation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equivalent variation of a gain from 0.60 to 0.75 in a health index" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y = 30000; b = 1; Delta_h = 0.15; EV = 4855.03" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVAR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equivalent-variation-of-a-gain-from-0-60-to-0-75-in-a-health-index" .

hemo:7002237 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equivalent variation of a loss from 0.60 to 0.45 in a health index"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A loss of the same size has an equivalent variation of -£4,178.76: the person would pay up to £4,178.76 to avoid it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equivalent variation of a loss from 0.60 to 0.45 in a health index" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y = 30000; b = 1; Delta_h = -0.15; EV = -4178.76" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVAR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equivalent-variation-of-a-loss-from-0-60-to-0-45-in-a-health-index" .

hemo:7002238 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Copayment counted as part of the option's change"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Any payment the option requires reduces the person's income under that option. In a social appraisal a copayment is a transfer to the health system rather than a resource cost, so the ranking describes one person's preferences, not a full cost-benefit result." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Copayment counted as part of the option's change" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVAR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "copayment-counted-as-part-of-the-option-s-change" .

hemo:7002239 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same status quo for every option ranked"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every option is valued from the same income and health index, so their equivalent variations are comparable and differences between them follow the differences in utility." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same status quo for every option ranked" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVAR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-status-quo-for-every-option-ranked" .

hemo:7002240 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Equivalent variation of an option from named income and health cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000469 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel multiplies the named cell holding the option's income by the exponential of the health coefficient times the option's health change, and subtracts the status quo income." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equivalent variation of an option from named income and health cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVAR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equivalent-variation-of-an-option-from-named-income-and-health-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=OptionIncome*EXP(HealthCoef*OptionHealthChange)-StatusQuoIncome" .

hemo:7002241 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equivalent variation ranks two options as their utilities do"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the equivalent variations of two options in cells named EVOptionA and EVOptionB, and each option's income and health change in named cells, the sign of their difference matches the sign of the difference in utility. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows compensating variations used in place of equivalent variations, or a copayment left out of one option's income." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equivalent variation ranks two options as their utilities do" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVAR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equivalent-variation-ranks-two-options-as-their-utilities-do" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SIGN(EVOptionB-EVOptionA)=SIGN((LN(IncomeB)+HealthCoef*HealthChangeB)-(LN(IncomeA)+HealthCoef*HealthChangeA))" .

hemo:7002242 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equivalent variation of an option reproduces the article's 5,231.31"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With OptionIncome 26100, StatusQuoIncome 30000, HealthCoef 1 and OptionHealthChange 0.3, and the result in a cell named EVOption, the value rounded to two decimals is 5,231.31. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at about 10,495.76 shows the copayment left out (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equivalent variation of an option reproduces the article's 5,231.31" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVAR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equivalent-variation-of-an-option-reproduces-the-article-s-5-231-31" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(EVOption,2)=5231.31" .

hemo:7002243 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment raising the health index by 0.30 with a 3,900 pound copayment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's example treatment B raises the health index from 0.60 to 0.90 and its £3,900 copayment cuts income from £30,000 to £26,100. Its equivalent variation is £5,231.31, above the £4,855.03 of treatment A, which raises the index by 0.15 at no cost, matching the person's preference for B." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Treatment raising the health index by 0.30 with a 3,900 pound copayment" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y_k = 26100; Y_0 = 30000; b = 1; Delta_h_k = 0.3; EV_k = 5231.31" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVAR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "treatment-raising-the-health-index-by-0-30-with-a-3-900-pound-copayment" .

hemo:7002244 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment raising the health index by 0.15 with no copayment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Treatment A leaves income at £30,000 and raises the health index by 0.15, so its equivalent variation is £4,855.03, the same as for the health gain alone." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Treatment raising the health index by 0.15 with no copayment" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y_k = 30000; Y_0 = 30000; b = 1; Delta_h_k = 0.15; EV_k = 4855.03" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVAR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "treatment-raising-the-health-index-by-0-15-with-no-copayment" .

hemo:7002245 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant hazard in each arm over follow-up for the rate ratio"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The hazard in each arm stays constant over the follow-up that the person-time covers, as in an exponential model, which is also a proportional hazards model. When the hazards change over time, one rate per arm averages over periods with different hazards, and a model that lets the hazard vary is needed instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant hazard in each arm over follow-up for the rate ratio" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-hazard-in-each-arm-over-follow-up-for-the-rate-ratio" .

hemo:7002246 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Events and person-time counted on the same basis in both arms"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both arms count the same event from the same time origin, and a person's time at risk stops at the first event or at censoring. The standard error uses the event counts alone, so it treats the counts as Poisson and needs at least one event in each arm." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Events and person-time counted on the same basis in both arms" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "events-and-person-time-counted-on-the-same-basis-in-both-arms" .

hemo:7002247 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Person-time hazard ratio and log standard error from named counts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000470 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the event counts in cells named TreatmentEvents and ComparatorEvents and the person-time in TreatmentPersonTime and ComparatorPersonTime, the first formula returns the hazard ratio, held in a cell named RateHR, and the second the standard error of its natural logarithm." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Person-time hazard ratio and log standard error from named counts" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "person-time-hazard-ratio-and-log-standard-error-from-named-counts" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(TreatmentEvents/TreatmentPersonTime)/(ComparatorEvents/ComparatorPersonTime); =SQRT(1/TreatmentEvents+1/ComparatorEvents)" .

hemo:7002248 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Person-time hazard ratio reproduces 0.70 from the article's rates"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With TreatmentEvents 70, TreatmentPersonTime 1000, ComparatorEvents 100 and ComparatorPersonTime 1000, the hazard ratio in RateHR rounded to four decimals is 0.7. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE at 1.4286 shows the comparator rate divided by the treatment rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Person-time hazard ratio reproduces 0.70 from the article's rates" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "person-time-hazard-ratio-reproduces-0-70-from-the-article-s-rates" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(RateHR,4)=0.7" .

hemo:7002249 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Person-time hazard ratio unchanged when time is counted in months"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Converting both person-time totals from years to months multiplies each rate by the same factor, which cancels in the ratio. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that RateHR was not computed from these four cells; the check cannot detect arms recorded in different units, because both sides read the same cells." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Person-time hazard ratio unchanged when time is counted in months" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "person-time-hazard-ratio-unchanged-when-time-is-counted-in-months" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((TreatmentEvents/(TreatmentPersonTime*12))/(ComparatorEvents/(ComparatorPersonTime*12))-RateHR)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002250 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Seventy and 100 events over 1,000 person-years per arm"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Seventy events over 1,000 person-years on treatment and 100 events over 1,000 person-years on the comparator give rates of 0.07 and 0.10 per person-year, the article's illustrative hazards, so HR = 0.07 / 0.10 = 0.70. The standard error of the log ratio is the square root of 1/70 plus 1/100, about 0.1558 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Seventy and 100 events over 1,000 person-years per arm" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_T = 70; PT_T = 1000; d_C = 100; PT_C = 1000; HR = 0.7; SE_beta = 0.1558" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "seventy-and-100-events-over-1-000-person-years-per-arm" .

hemo:7002251 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Unequal person-time of 800 and 750 person-years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Forty-two events over 800 person-years on treatment and 60 events over 750 person-years on the comparator give rates of 0.0525 and 0.08 per person-year and a hazard ratio of 0.65625, with a standard error of the log ratio of about 0.2012 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Unequal person-time of 800 and 750 person-years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_T = 42; PT_T = 800; d_C = 60; PT_C = 750; HR = 0.65625; SE_beta = 0.2012" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "unequal-person-time-of-800-and-750-person-years" .

hemo:7002252 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Approximate normality of the log hazard ratio"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The log hazard ratio is treated as approximately normal with the stated standard error, so the interval is an approximation that is less reliable with few events." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Approximate normality of the log hazard ratio" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "approximate-normality-of-the-log-hazard-ratio" .

hemo:7002253 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Estimate and standard error from the same model and reference group"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "beta and SE_beta come from the same analysis, with the same reference group and adjustment set as the hazard ratio being reported." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Estimate and standard error from the same model and reference group" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "estimate-and-standard-error-from-the-same-model-and-reference-group" .

hemo:7002254 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Hazard ratio confidence limits for any coverage from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000471 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the log hazard ratio in Coef, its standard error in SE and the standard normal value in ZValue, the two formulas return the lower and upper limits, held in cells named LowerHR and UpperHR. NORM.S.INV(0.975) returns the z value for a 95% interval." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hazard ratio confidence limits for any coverage from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hazard-ratio-confidence-limits-for-any-coverage-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EXP(Coef-ZValue*SE); =EXP(Coef+ZValue*SE)" .

hemo:7002255 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Geometric mean of the limits returns the hazard ratio"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Because the interval is symmetric on the log scale, the square root of the product of the two limits equals the hazard ratio. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows limits computed on the ratio scale or taken from a different estimate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Geometric mean of the limits returns the hazard ratio" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HR-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "geometric-mean-of-the-limits-returns-the-hazard-ratio" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SQRT(LowerHR*UpperHR)-EXP(Coef))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002256 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Hazard ratio interval excludes 1 exactly when the Wald test rejects"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The interval excludes 1 when, and only when, the absolute ratio of the coefficient to its standard error exceeds ZValue. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that the limits and the test used different standard errors." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hazard ratio interval excludes 1 exactly when the Wald test rejects" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HR-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hazard-ratio-interval-excludes-1-exactly-when-the-wald-test-rejects" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(ABS(Coef/SE)>ZValue)=OR(UpperHR<1,LowerHR>1)" .

hemo:7002257 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "95% interval for a hazard ratio of 0.70 with standard error 0.155839"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A log hazard ratio of minus 0.356675, the natural log of 0.70, with the standard error of 0.155839 from the person-time example, gives a 95% interval of about 0.5158 to 0.9501 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "95% interval for a hazard ratio of 0.70 with standard error 0.155839" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta = -0.356675; SE_beta = 0.155839; z = 1.96; HR_L = 0.5158; HR_U = 0.9501" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "95-interval-for-a-hazard-ratio-of-0-70-with-standard-error-0-155839" .

hemo:7002258 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Interval for a pooled hazard ratio of 0.88 from a logrank variance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In their section 11 example, which rebuilds the bladder cancer trial from its Kaplan-Meier curve and numbers at risk, Tierney and colleagues pool the time intervals to a hazard ratio of 0.88 with a logrank variance of 119.80. The log hazard ratio is about minus 0.1278 and its standard error 1 divided by the square root of 119.80, about 0.0914, giving about 0.7357 to 1.0527, the 0.74 to 1.05 they report." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Interval for a pooled hazard ratio of 0.88 from a logrank variance" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta = -0.1278; SE_beta = 0.0914; z = 1.96; HR_L = 0.7357; HR_U = 1.0527" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "interval-for-a-pooled-hazard-ratio-of-0-88-from-a-logrank-variance" .

hemo:7002259 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Reported interval symmetric on the log scale"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The published interval was computed on the log scale from a large-sample standard error, as Cox and logrank analyses usually report it, and its limits are given to enough significant figures; rounding of the limits passes straight into the standard error." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reported interval symmetric on the log scale" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reported-interval-symmetric-on-the-log-scale" .

hemo:7002260 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Coverage of the reported interval known"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The coverage of the interval is stated, so that z can be matched to it. Most trial reports give 95% intervals." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Coverage of the reported interval known" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HR-013" ;
    hemo:9000023 "coverage-of-the-reported-interval-known" .

hemo:7002261 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Log hazard ratio standard error from named interval limits"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000472 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the published limits in cells named LowerHR and UpperHR and the standard normal value in ZValue, the formula returns the standard error, held in a cell named SELogHR." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log hazard ratio standard error from named interval limits" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HR-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-hazard-ratio-standard-error-from-named-interval-limits" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(LN(UpperHR)-LN(LowerHR))/(2*ZValue)" .

hemo:7002262 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reported hazard ratio sits at the log midpoint of its interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The mean of the logs of the two limits is close to the log of the reported hazard ratio, which is in a cell named ReportedHR. For the bladder cancer example the gap is about 0.0012. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an interval not built on the log scale, a mistyped limit or an interval belonging to another estimate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reported hazard ratio sits at the log midpoint of its interval" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HR-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reported-hazard-ratio-sits-at-the-log-midpoint-of-its-interval" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((LN(UpperHR)+LN(LowerHR))/2-LN(ReportedHR))<0.01" .

hemo:7002263 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Recovered standard error rebuilds the upper limit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Adding 2 times ZValue times the recovered standard error to the log of the lower limit returns the upper limit. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the standard error computed with a different z value." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Recovered standard error rebuilds the upper limit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HR-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "recovered-standard-error-rebuilds-the-upper-limit" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(EXP(LN(LowerHR)+2*ZValue*SELogHR)-UpperHR)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002264 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Bladder cancer trial interval of 0.71 to 1.02"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Tierney and colleagues' bladder cancer example reports a hazard ratio of 0.85 with a 95% interval of 0.71 to 1.02, giving a standard error of about 0.0924 for the log hazard ratio and a variance of about 0.0085, as in the paper." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Bladder cancer trial interval of 0.71 to 1.02" ;
    hemo:9000014 "HR_U = 1.02; HR_L = 0.71; z = 1.96; SE_beta = 0.0924" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "bladder-cancer-trial-interval-of-0-71-to-1-02" .

hemo:7002265 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Round trip from the 0.5158 to 0.9501 interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Applied to the interval from HE-EX-HR-009, the formula returns about 0.1558, the standard error that produced it (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Round trip from the 0.5158 to 0.9501 interval" ;
    hemo:9000014 "HR_U = 0.9501; HR_L = 0.5158; z = 1.96; SE_beta = 0.1558" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HR-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "round-trip-from-the-0-5158-to-0-9501-interval" .

hemo:7002266 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Single event type for the cumulative hazard and survival link"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "S_t is the survival function for one event type, so H_t equals minus log S_t exactly. With competing events, minus log of an all-cause survival gives the all-cause cumulative hazard, and the cause-specific cumulative hazard does not convert to a cause-specific probability through 1 minus exp(minus H)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Single event type for the cumulative hazard and survival link" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CUMH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "single-event-type-for-the-cumulative-hazard-and-survival-link" .

hemo:7002267 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Survival estimated with non-informative censoring"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "When S_t comes from censored trial data, censored patients are assumed to have the same risk of the event as those still followed, the condition TSD 14 states for the standard survival methods." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Survival estimated with non-informative censoring" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CUMH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "survival-estimated-with-non-informative-censoring" .

hemo:7002268 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Cumulative hazard and event probability from a named survival cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000473 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the survival probability in a cell named SurvProb, the first formula returns the cumulative hazard, held in a cell named CumHaz, and the second the probability of having had the event. LN is the natural logarithm." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cumulative hazard and event probability from a named survival cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CUMH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cumulative-hazard-and-event-probability-from-a-named-survival-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=-LN(SurvProb); =1-SurvProb" .

hemo:7002269 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cumulative hazard returns the survival probability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Exponentiate minus the cumulative hazard and compare with the survival probability. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a base-10 logarithm or a cumulative hazard taken from a different curve." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cumulative hazard returns the survival probability" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CUMH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cumulative-hazard-returns-the-survival-probability" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(EXP(-CumHaz)-SurvProb)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002270 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cumulative hazard passes 1 exactly when survival falls below 0.3679"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The cumulative hazard exceeds 1 if and only if survival is below exp(minus 1). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows that CumHaz holds an event probability or was computed with LOG instead of LN." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cumulative hazard passes 1 exactly when survival falls below 0.3679" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CUMH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cumulative-hazard-passes-1-exactly-when-survival-falls-below-0-3679" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(CumHaz>1)=(SurvProb<EXP(-1))" .

hemo:7002271 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cumulative hazard of 0.8 from four-year survival of 0.4493"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative Weibull example, survival to year 4 is 0.4493, so the cumulative hazard is about 0.8001 (exactly 0.8 before survival was rounded) while the probability of having died by year 4 is 0.5507." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cumulative hazard of 0.8 from four-year survival of 0.4493" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_t = 0.4493; H_t = 0.8001; F_t = 0.5507" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CUMH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cumulative-hazard-of-0-8-from-four-year-survival-of-0-4493" .

hemo:7002272 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cumulative hazard above 1 at five-year survival of 0.3269"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At year 5 survival is 0.3269 and the cumulative hazard about 1.118: a cumulative hazard, not a probability of 112%. The probability of having died is 0.6731." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cumulative hazard above 1 at five-year survival of 0.3269" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_t = 0.3269; H_t = 1.1181; F_t = 0.6731" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CUMH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cumulative-hazard-above-1-at-five-year-survival-of-0-3269" .

hemo:7002273 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cumulative hazard of 0.5 against an event probability of 0.39"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A survival probability of 0.6065 gives a cumulative hazard of about 0.5, while the probability of having had the event is about 0.39, the gap the article warns misleads quietly." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cumulative hazard of 0.5 against an event probability of 0.39" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_t = 0.6065; H_t = 0.5001; F_t = 0.3935" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CUMH-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cumulative-hazard-of-0-5-against-an-event-probability-of-0-39" .

hemo:7002274 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Single exit from the state for the cumulative hazard conversion"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The event is the only way out of the starting state. When a state has competing exits, a cause-specific cumulative hazard cannot be converted on its own, because people removed by another exit cannot have the event; the joint calculation is HE-FM-TP-004." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Single exit from the state for the cumulative hazard conversion" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CUMH-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "single-exit-from-the-state-for-the-cumulative-hazard-conversion" .

hemo:7002275 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Clock measured from the origin of the fitted curve"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "H_t and H_prev are read at times since the curve's own origin, such as randomisation, which in a cohort model is time since model start. When risk depends on time spent in a state, the clock restarts on entry and the model needs tunnel states, as in the DARTH tutorial." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Clock measured from the origin of the fitted curve" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CUMH-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "clock-measured-from-the-origin-of-the-fitted-curve" .

hemo:7002276 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Fitted curve describes the modelled population"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The cumulative hazard comes from a curve fitted to, or validated for, the population and event the model represents, over the whole horizon, including any extrapolated part." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fitted curve describes the modelled population" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CUMH-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fitted-curve-describes-the-modelled-population" .

hemo:7002277 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Cycle probabilities from a column of cumulative hazards"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000474 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the cumulative hazard at the start of the model in B2 (0 at time zero) and at successive cycle ends in B3 downwards, the formula in C3, filled down, returns each cycle's probability. For one cycle from named cells CumHazStart and CumHazEnd, the second formula returns the probability, held in a cell named CycleProb." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cycle probabilities from a column of cumulative hazards" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CUMH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cycle-probabilities-from-a-column-of-cumulative-hazards" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1-EXP(-(B3-B2)); =1-EXP(-(CumHazEnd-CumHazStart))" .

hemo:7002278 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cohort trace from cumulative hazard cycle probabilities reproduces the curve"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the cycle probabilities in a range named CycleProbs and the cumulative hazard at the last cycle end in FinalCumHaz, the sum of log(1 minus p) over the cycles equals minus the final cumulative hazard, so the trace matches the fitted survival. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows increments of H used as probabilities or a cycle missed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cohort trace from cumulative hazard cycle probabilities reproduces the curve" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CUMH-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cohort-trace-from-cumulative-hazard-cycle-probabilities-reproduces-the-curve" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(LN(1-CycleProbs))+FinalCumHaz)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002279 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cycle probability below the cumulative hazard increment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a positive increment, 1 minus exp(minus x) is always below x. Expected result: TRUE when CumHazEnd exceeds CumHazStart. FALSE shows that the increment itself was entered as the probability." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cycle probability below the cumulative hazard increment" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CUMH-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cycle-probability-below-the-cumulative-hazard-increment" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CycleProb<CumHazEnd-CumHazStart" .

hemo:7002280 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Year 3 probability of 0.2108 from a Weibull cumulative hazard"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With H(t) = 0.10 t^1.5, the cumulative hazard is 0.5196 at year 3 and 0.2828 at year 2. The rise of 0.2368 gives a probability of death in year 3 of about 0.2108 among those alive at its start, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Year 3 probability of 0.2108 from a Weibull cumulative hazard" ;
    hemo:9000014 "H_t = 0.519615; H_prev = 0.282843; p_t = 0.2108" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CUMH-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "year-3-probability-of-0-2108-from-a-weibull-cumulative-hazard" .

hemo:7002281 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Year 6 probability of 0.2965 as the hazard rises"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At year 6 the cumulative hazard is 1.4697 against 1.1180 at year 5, a rise of 0.3517 and a cycle probability of about 0.2965, larger than in year 3 for the same cycle length because the hazard is rising." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Year 6 probability of 0.2965 as the hazard rises" ;
    hemo:9000014 "H_t = 1.469694; H_prev = 1.118034; p_t = 0.2965" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CUMH-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "year-6-probability-of-0-2965-as-the-hazard-rises" .

hemo:7002282 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "First annual cycle starting from a cumulative hazard of zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the first cycle the starting cumulative hazard is 0, so the probability is 1 minus exp(minus 0.1), about 0.0952." ;
    hemo:9000009 "First annual cycle starting from a cumulative hazard of zero" ;
    hemo:9000014 "H_t = 0.1; H_prev = 0; p_t = 0.0952" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CUMH-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "first-annual-cycle-starting-from-a-cumulative-hazard-of-zero" .

hemo:7002283 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weibull parameterisation stated before transfer to a model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The formula uses lambda t^gamma, as in TSD 21. Software and tutorials also write (lambda t)^gamma, as in the DARTH tutorial, so the scale parameter differs between sources for the same curve and must be converted before use." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weibull parameterisation stated before transfer to a model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CUMH-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weibull-parameterisation-stated-before-transfer-to-a-model" .

hemo:7002284 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Straight line on the log scale judged within follow-up only"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A straight log-cumulative hazard plot supports the Weibull or exponential shape within the observed data. TSD 14 notes that such checks address internal validity, not whether the extrapolated part of the curve is plausible." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Straight line on the log scale judged within follow-up only" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CUMH-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "straight-line-on-the-log-scale-judged-within-follow-up-only" .

hemo:7002285 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Weibull cumulative hazard and its log from named parameters"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000475 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the parameters in cells named WeibullScale and WeibullShape and the time in TimeYears, the formulas return the cumulative hazard and its natural log." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weibull cumulative hazard and its log from named parameters" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CUMH-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weibull-cumulative-hazard-and-its-log-from-named-parameters" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=WeibullScale*TimeYears^WeibullShape; =LN(WeibullScale)+WeibullShape*LN(TimeYears)" .

hemo:7002286 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gradient between two times recovers the Weibull shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the cumulative hazards CumHaz1 and CumHaz2 computed at times Time1 and Time2 from the same curve, the slope of log H against log t equals WeibullShape. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the (lambda t)^gamma form mixed with the lambda t^gamma form or a column computed from different parameters." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gradient between two times recovers the Weibull shape" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CUMH-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gradient-between-two-times-recovers-the-weibull-shape" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((LN(CumHaz2)-LN(CumHaz1))/(LN(Time2)-LN(Time1))-WeibullShape)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002287 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weibull parameters reproduce the survival reported by the fitting software"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the survival at TimeYears reported by the software that fitted the curve held in a cell named FittedSurv, exp of minus the cumulative hazard matches it. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a scale parameter copied from a different parameterisation, such as the (lambda t)^gamma form or a log-scale coefficient." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weibull parameters reproduce the survival reported by the fitting software" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CUMH-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weibull-parameters-reproduce-the-survival-reported-by-the-fitting-software" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(EXP(-WeibullScale*TimeYears^WeibullShape)-FittedSurv)<1E-6" .

hemo:7002288 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weibull cumulative hazard of 0.8 at year 4 with gamma of 1.5"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With lambda of 0.10 and gamma of 1.5, H(4) = 0.10 x 8 = 0.8 and its natural log is about minus 0.2231, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weibull cumulative hazard of 0.8 at year 4 with gamma of 1.5" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 0.1; gamma = 1.5; t = 4; H_t = 0.8; logH = -0.2231" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CUMH-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weibull-cumulative-hazard-of-0-8-at-year-4-with-gamma-of-1-5" .

hemo:7002289 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weibull log cumulative hazard at year 1 equals log lambda"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At t of 1, H equals lambda, 0.1, and its log is about minus 2.3026, the intercept of the line. The gradient between years 1 and 4 is (minus 0.2231 plus 2.3026) divided by 1.3863, which is 1.5, the shape parameter." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weibull log cumulative hazard at year 1 equals log lambda" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 0.1; gamma = 1.5; t = 1; H_t = 0.1; logH = -2.3026" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CUMH-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weibull-log-cumulative-hazard-at-year-1-equals-log-lambda" .

hemo:7002290 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Exponential case with gamma of 1 on the log-cumulative hazard scale"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With gamma of 1 the curve is exponential: H(4) = 0.4, log H about minus 0.9163, and the line has gradient 1 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exponential case with gamma of 1 on the log-cumulative hazard scale" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 0.1; gamma = 1; t = 4; H_t = 0.4; logH = -0.9163" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CUMH-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exponential-case-with-gamma-of-1-on-the-log-cumulative-hazard-scale" .

hemo:7002291 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Straight-line demand and cost between the two quantities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Demand and marginal cost are linear between q_star and q_d, so the area between them is a triangle; with curved demand the triangle is an approximation. Marginal cost is constant in the insurance case, as Feldstein and Gruber assume." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Straight-line demand and cost between the two quantities" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWL-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "straight-line-demand-and-cost-between-the-two-quantities" .

hemo:7002292 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Demand curve measures the marginal value of each unit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The demand price is read as what the marginal unit is worth to its users. Where patients misjudge the value of care, or where use has external effects, the demand curve does not measure social value and the triangle misstates the loss." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Demand curve measures the marginal value of each unit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWL-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "demand-curve-measures-the-marginal-value-of-each-unit" .

hemo:7002293 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Only one market distorted for the deadweight triangle"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Related markets are undistorted. Hines shows that when a tax pushes demand into a market that is already distorted, the loss becomes a trapezoid rather than a triangle." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Only one market distorted for the deadweight triangle" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWL-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "only-one-market-distorted-for-the-deadweight-triangle" .

hemo:7002294 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Deadweight loss triangle from named wedge and quantities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000476 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the wedge in a cell named Wedge and the quantities in DistortedQty and EfficientQty, the formula returns the deadweight loss, held in a cell named DeadweightLoss." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Deadweight loss triangle from named wedge and quantities" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DWL-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "deadweight-loss-triangle-from-named-wedge-and-quantities" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=0.5*Wedge*ABS(DistortedQty-EfficientQty)" .

hemo:7002295 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Deadweight loss equals cost minus value of the extra units"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For insurance-induced use on linear demand, with the unit cost in UnitCost and the patient's price in PatientPrice, the extra units cost UnitCost each and are valued at the average of the two prices, and the difference is the triangle (200,000 minus 120,000 pounds in the first example). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a wedge that is not UnitCost minus PatientPrice." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Deadweight loss equals cost minus value of the extra units" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWL-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "deadweight-loss-equals-cost-minus-value-of-the-extra-units" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((UnitCost-(UnitCost+PatientPrice)/2)*(DistortedQty-EfficientQty)-DeadweightLoss)<1E-6" .

hemo:7002296 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Deadweight losses on one linear curve scale with the square of the wedge"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "On one linear demand curve the ratio of two losses equals the squared ratio of their wedges, with the losses in DWLLow and DWLHigh and the wedges in WedgeLow and WedgeHigh. Expected result: TRUE (0.5625 for wedges of 30 and 40). FALSE shows quantities taken from different demand curves or curved demand." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Deadweight losses on one linear curve scale with the square of the wedge" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWL-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "deadweight-losses-on-one-linear-curve-scale-with-the-square-of-the-wedge" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(DWLLow/DWLHigh-(WedgeLow/WedgeHigh)^2)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002297 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Physiotherapy at a 20 per cent coinsurance rate on linear demand"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Sessions cost 50 pounds and demand is q = 10000 minus 100p. Full-price use is 5,000 sessions; at the insured price of 10 pounds use is 9,000. The wedge of 40 pounds over 4,000 extra sessions gives a deadweight loss of 80,000 pounds a year, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Physiotherapy at a 20 per cent coinsurance rate on linear demand" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w = 40; q_d = 9000; q_star = 5000; DWL = 80000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "physiotherapy-at-a-20-per-cent-coinsurance-rate-on-linear-demand" .

hemo:7002298 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same demand curve at a 40 per cent coinsurance rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At a patient price of 20 pounds use falls to 8,000 sessions, the wedge is 30 pounds and the loss 45,000 pounds, 0.5625 of the previous loss, as the square-of-the-wedge rule predicts." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same demand curve at a 40 per cent coinsurance rate" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w = 30; q_d = 8000; q_star = 5000; DWL = 45000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-demand-curve-at-a-40-per-cent-coinsurance-rate" .

hemo:7002299 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Less responsive demand at a 20 per cent coinsurance rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With demand q = 6000 minus 20p, use at 10 pounds rises only to 5,800, and the same wedge of 40 pounds gives a loss of 16,000 pounds instead of 80,000, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Less responsive demand at a 20 per cent coinsurance rate" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w = 40; q_d = 5800; q_star = 5000; DWL = 16000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "less-responsive-demand-at-a-20-per-cent-coinsurance-rate" .

hemo:7002300 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Small tax on a good supplied at constant marginal cost"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The producer price stays fixed, so the whole tax passes to buyers, and the tax is small enough for the second-order approximation to hold. On linear demand the expression is exact; on curved demand it is an approximation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Small tax on a good supplied at constant marginal cost" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWL-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "small-tax-on-a-good-supplied-at-constant-marginal-cost" .

hemo:7002301 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Compensated elasticity and no other distorted market"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The elasticity is the compensated one; Hines reports that ordinary triangles usually approximate compensated measures closely, with exceptions. Other markets are undistorted, so no cross-market terms arise." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Compensated elasticity and no other distorted market" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWL-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "compensated-elasticity-and-no-other-distorted-market" .

hemo:7002302 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Harberger deadweight loss from named elasticity, tax rate and spending"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000477 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the absolute elasticity in Elasticity, the tax as a proportion in TaxRate and the pre-tax price and quantity in PreTaxPrice and PreTaxQty, the formula returns the approximate loss, held in a cell named HarbergerDWL." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Harberger deadweight loss from named elasticity, tax rate and spending" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DWL-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "harberger-deadweight-loss-from-named-elasticity-tax-rate-and-spending" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=0.5*Elasticity*TaxRate^2*PreTaxPrice*PreTaxQty" .

hemo:7002303 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Harberger inputs entered with the right signs and units"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The elasticity must be entered as an absolute value and the tax as a proportion of the price. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a signed elasticity, which would make the loss negative, or a tax entered in pounds or per cent." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Harberger inputs entered with the right signs and units" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWL-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "harberger-inputs-entered-with-the-right-signs-and-units" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(Elasticity>=0,TaxRate>=0,TaxRate<1)" .

hemo:7002304 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Harberger loss close to the triangle from observed quantities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the quantity after the tax in PostTaxQty, the triangle measured from the observed fall in quantity is within 5 per cent of the approximation. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an elasticity that does not match the observed response, or a tax too large for the approximation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Harberger loss close to the triangle from observed quantities" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWL-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "harberger-loss-close-to-the-triangle-from-observed-quantities" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(HarbergerDWL-0.5*TaxRate*PreTaxPrice*(PreTaxQty-PostTaxQty))<=0.05*HarbergerDWL" .

hemo:7002305 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Twenty per cent tax at the article's full price"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At the article's full price of 50 pounds and 5,000 sessions, demand q = 10000 minus 100p has a point elasticity of 1.0. A 20 per cent tax raises the price to 60 pounds and cuts use by 1,000, a loss of 5,000 pounds, which the approximation reproduces exactly because demand is linear (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Twenty per cent tax at the article's full price" ;
    hemo:9000014 "eps = 1; tau = 0.2; p = 50; q = 5000; DWL = 5000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "twenty-per-cent-tax-at-the-article-s-full-price" .

hemo:7002306 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Doubling the tax rate quadruples the Harberger loss"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At a 40 per cent rate on the same curve the loss is 20,000 pounds, four times the loss at 20 per cent (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Doubling the tax rate quadruples the Harberger loss" ;
    hemo:9000014 "eps = 1; tau = 0.4; p = 50; q = 5000; DWL = 20000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "doubling-the-tax-rate-quadruples-the-harberger-loss" .

hemo:7002307 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Elasticity of 0.2 on the less responsive curve"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "On the article's less responsive curve, q = 6000 minus 20p, the elasticity at 50 pounds is 0.2, and the same 20 per cent tax costs 1,000 pounds (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Elasticity of 0.2 on the less responsive curve" ;
    hemo:9000014 "eps = 0.2; tau = 0.2; p = 50; q = 5000; DWL = 1000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "elasticity-of-0-2-on-the-less-responsive-curve" .

hemo:7002308 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Care supplied at constant cost with uninsured price normalised to 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Feldstein and Gruber assume constant cost, so there is no change in producer surplus, and measure care so that its price without insurance is 1. With prices in pounds, E is spending at full cost and P the patient's share." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Care supplied at constant cost with uninsured price normalised to 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWL-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "care-supplied-at-constant-cost-with-uninsured-price-normalised-to-1" .

hemo:7002309 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Out-of-pocket spending below any cap"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The patient faces P_1 on the margin, so out-of-pocket spending stays below the plan's maximum; above the cap the marginal price is zero and the formula does not apply." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Out-of-pocket spending below any cap" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWL-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "out-of-pocket-spending-below-any-cap" .

hemo:7002310 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Risk-bearing change evaluated separately"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The formula values reduced distortion only. Feldstein and Gruber evaluate the change in the risk people bear as a separate effect of ambiguous sign and add the two." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Risk-bearing change evaluated separately" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWL-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "risk-bearing-change-evaluated-separately" .

hemo:7002311 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Reduction in deadweight loss from named spending and coinsurance cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000478 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With spending at full cost in SpendInitial and SpendNew and the coinsurance rates in CoinsInitial and CoinsNew, the first formula returns the reduction, held in DWLReduction. Under a constant elasticity in Elasticity, the second gives SpendNew from SpendInitial." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reduction in deadweight loss from named spending and coinsurance cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DWL-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reduction-in-deadweight-loss-from-named-spending-and-coinsurance-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(SpendInitial-SpendNew)*(1-CoinsNew)+0.5*(CoinsNew-CoinsInitial)*(SpendInitial-SpendNew); =SpendInitial*(CoinsInitial/CoinsNew)^Elasticity" .

hemo:7002312 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reduction equals cost saved minus the value of forgone care"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The rectangle and triangle together equal the fall in spending at full cost minus the value patients placed on the forgone care, valued at the average of the two patient prices (50,000 minus 15,000 pounds in the first example). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the rectangle built on 1 minus P_0 instead of 1 minus P_1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reduction equals cost saved minus the value of forgone care" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWL-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reduction-equals-cost-saved-minus-the-value-of-forgone-care" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(DWLReduction-(SpendInitial-SpendNew)*(1-(CoinsInitial+CoinsNew)/2))<1E-6" .

hemo:7002313 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Coinsurance rates and spending in valid ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The new rate exceeds the old, neither exceeds 1, and spending does not rise. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows rates entered as percentages, the two rates swapped or spending in the wrong cells." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Coinsurance rates and spending in valid ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWL-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "coinsurance-rates-and-spending-in-valid-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(CoinsInitial>=0,CoinsNew>CoinsInitial,CoinsNew<=1,SpendNew<=SpendInitial)" .

hemo:7002314 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Raising coinsurance from 20 to 40 per cent in the physiotherapy example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In money terms, 9,000 and 8,000 sessions at 50 pounds are 450,000 and 400,000 pounds of care at full cost. The rectangle is 50,000 times 0.6, 30,000 pounds, the triangle 0.5 x 0.2 x 50,000, 5,000 pounds, and the reduction 35,000 pounds, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Raising coinsurance from 20 to 40 per cent in the physiotherapy example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_0 = 450000; E_1 = 400000; P_0 = 0.2; P_1 = 0.4; dDWL = 35000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "raising-coinsurance-from-20-to-40-per-cent-in-the-physiotherapy-example" .

hemo:7002315 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant elasticity of 0.33 with coinsurance rising from 20 to 50 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 1,000 units of care at 20 per cent coinsurance and a constant elasticity of 0.33, raising the rate to 50 per cent cuts use to about 739.06 units and the deadweight loss by about 169.61 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant elasticity of 0.33 with coinsurance rising from 20 to 50 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_0 = 1000; E_1 = 739.0602; P_0 = 0.2; P_1 = 0.5; dDWL = 169.61" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-elasticity-of-0-33-with-coinsurance-rising-from-20-to-50-per-cent" .

hemo:7002316 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "No change in use gives no reduction in deadweight loss"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If use does not respond to the higher coinsurance rate, E_1 equals E_0 and there is no gain from reduced distortion, as Feldstein and Gruber found at zero elasticity." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No change in use gives no reduction in deadweight loss" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_0 = 1000; E_1 = 1000; P_0 = 0.2; P_1 = 0.5; dDWL = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-change-in-use-gives-no-reduction-in-deadweight-loss" .

hemo:7002317 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Excess burden applied only to tax-financed net spending"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "G is the net effect on public budgets financed by taxes. OMB states that investments funded by user charges that work like market prices carry no excess burden, and DFØ bases the cost on the net financing need." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Excess burden applied only to tax-financed net spending" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWL-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "excess-burden-applied-only-to-tax-financed-net-spending" .

hemo:7002318 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One marginal excess burden for all tax-financed costs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The same lambda applies to every tax-financed cost in the comparison, as a national figure set in guidance. OMB allows a different figure where specific information supports one." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One marginal excess burden for all tax-financed costs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWL-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-marginal-excess-burden-for-all-tax-financed-costs" .

hemo:7002319 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Social cost of public funding from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000479 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the marginal excess burden in ExcessBurden and the net public cost in NetPublicCost, the formula returns the adjusted cost, held in AdjustedCost." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Social cost of public funding from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DWL-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "social-cost-of-public-funding-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(1+ExcessBurden)*NetPublicCost" .

hemo:7002320 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Adjusted public cost consistent with a plausible excess burden"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The adjustment equals ExcessBurden times NetPublicCost and the rate is not negative and is below 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a rate entered as a percentage (25 instead of 0.25) or the factor applied to gross spending." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Adjusted public cost consistent with a plausible excess burden" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWL-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "adjusted-public-cost-consistent-with-a-plausible-excess-burden" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ExcessBurden>=0,ExcessBurden<1,ABS(AdjustedCost-NetPublicCost-ExcessBurden*NetPublicCost)<1E-6)" .

hemo:7002321 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Ranking by cost per QALY unchanged when all costs share one tax-financed budget"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With incremental costs CostA and CostB and QALY gains QalyA and QalyB, all on the same budget, scaling every cost by the same factor leaves the ranking unchanged. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE would show the factor applied to one option only." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ranking by cost per QALY unchanged when all costs share one tax-financed budget" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWL-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ranking-by-cost-per-qaly-unchanged-when-all-costs-share-one-tax-financed-budget" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(CostA/QalyA<CostB/QalyB)=((1+ExcessBurden)*CostA/QalyA<(1+ExcessBurden)*CostB/QalyB)" .

hemo:7002322 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "OMB supplementary analysis with a 25 per cent excess burden"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Public expenditure of 1 million US dollars is multiplied by 1.25 in the OMB supplementary analysis, giving a social cost of 1.25 million." ;
    hemo:9000009 "OMB supplementary analysis with a 25 per cent excess burden" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 0.25; G = 1000000; C_adj = 1250000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "omb-supplementary-analysis-with-a-25-per-cent-excess-burden" .

hemo:7002323 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Norwegian tax financing cost on a measure of 10 million kroner"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A measure with net public financing of 10 million kroner carries a tax financing cost of 2 million, a total of 12 million kroner." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Norwegian tax financing cost on a measure of 10 million kroner" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 0.2; G = 10000000; C_adj = 12000000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "norwegian-tax-financing-cost-on-a-measure-of-10-million-kroner" .

hemo:7002324 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Green Book default of no excess burden"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Under the UK Green Book default the costs of raising public funds are not included, which is lambda of 0: a net public cost of 500,000 pounds stays 500,000." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Green Book default of no excess burden" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda = 0; G = 500000; C_adj = 500000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWL-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "green-book-default-of-no-excess-burden" .

hemo:7002325 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal set size and equal appearances in a balanced design"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every set has k objects and every object appears r times, so no object gains from the way sets were drawn. Orthogonal main effects designs give sets of unequal size and are now seen as inappropriate for the object case." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal set size and equal appearances in a balanced design" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BWS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-set-size-and-equal-appearances-in-a-balanced-design" .

hemo:7002326 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Whole-number parameters before constructing the design"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The identities give r and lambda for chosen v, b and k; when either is not a whole number no balanced incomplete block design has those parameters, and another number of sets or set size is chosen. Designs are then constructed or taken from published tables." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Whole-number parameters before constructing the design" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BWS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "whole-number-parameters-before-constructing-the-design" .

hemo:7002327 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Best-worst design appearances and pair count from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000480 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the numbers of sets, objects per set and objects in Sets, SetSize and Objects, the formulas return the appearances, held in Appearances, and the pair count, held in PairCount." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Best-worst design appearances and pair count from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BWS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "best-worst-design-appearances-and-pair-count-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Sets*SetSize/Objects; =Appearances*(SetSize-1)/(Objects-1)" .

hemo:7002328 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Best-worst design parameters are whole numbers"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both derived parameters must be whole numbers. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a combination of sets, set size and objects for which no balanced design exists." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Best-worst design parameters are whole numbers" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BWS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "best-worst-design-parameters-are-whole-numbers" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(Appearances=INT(Appearances),PairCount=INT(PairCount))" .

hemo:7002329 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Incidence matrix shows every pair together equally often"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the design as a 0 and 1 incidence matrix named Incidence (objects in rows, sets in columns), the off-diagonal cells of Incidence times its transpose all equal PairCount and the diagonal cells equal Appearances. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an unbalanced design or a typing error in the sets." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Incidence matrix shows every pair together equally often" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BWS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "incidence-matrix-shows-every-pair-together-equally-often" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT((MMULT(Incidence,TRANSPOSE(Incidence))-PairCount*(1-MUNIT(Objects))-Appearances*MUNIT(Objects))^2)=0" .

hemo:7002330 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Seven objects in seven sets of four"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The seven-set design used by Hollin and colleagues shows seven objects in sets of four: each object appears four times and each pair twice, as in the article (7 x 4 = 28 appearances)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Seven objects in seven sets of four" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b = 7; k = 4; v = 7; r = 4; lambda = 2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BWS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "seven-objects-in-seven-sets-of-four" .

hemo:7002331 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Four objects in four sets of three"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Four objects in four sets of three give r = 3 and lambda = 2, the first example in the Penn State course notes." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Four objects in four sets of three" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b = 4; k = 3; v = 4; r = 3; lambda = 2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BWS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "four-objects-in-four-sets-of-three" .

hemo:7002332 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Eight objects in eight sets of four with no balanced design"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Eight objects in eight sets of four give r = 4 but lambda of about 1.7143, not a whole number, so no balanced incomplete block design has these parameters (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Eight objects in eight sets of four with no balanced design" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b = 8; k = 4; v = 8; r = 4; lambda = 1.7143" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BWS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "eight-objects-in-eight-sets-of-four-with-no-balanced-design" .

hemo:7002333 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Every respondent completes the same design"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each respondent answers every set and sees item i r_i times, so N times r_i is the number of opportunities. With several design versions or missing tasks, the opportunities are counted directly." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Every respondent completes the same design" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BWS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "every-respondent-completes-the-same-design" .

hemo:7002334 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Scores read as an ordering summary"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Best-minus-worst scores summarise ordering. Ratio-scale properties come from a choice model such as the maxdiff model, not from the counts." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Scores read as an ordering summary" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BWS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "scores-read-as-an-ordering-summary" .

hemo:7002335 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Standardised best-minus-worst score from named counts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000481 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the counts in BestCount and WorstCount, the number of respondents in Respondents and the item's appearances per respondent in Appearances, the formula returns the score." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standardised best-minus-worst score from named counts" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BWS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standardised-best-minus-worst-score-from-named-counts" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(BestCount-WorstCount)/(Respondents*Appearances)" .

hemo:7002336 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "One best and one worst choice per set and respondent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With all items' counts in ranges named BestCounts and WorstCounts and the number of sets per respondent in Sets, each count total equals respondents times sets (7 for one respondent in the article). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows missing or double-counted choices." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One best and one worst choice per set and respondent" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BWS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-best-and-one-worst-choice-per-set-and-respondent" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(SUM(BestCounts)=Respondents*Sets,SUM(WorstCounts)=Respondents*Sets)" .

hemo:7002337 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standardised scores within minus 1 and 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With all items' scores in a range named Scores, every score lies between minus 1 and 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows sample-wide counts divided by one respondent's opportunities instead of N times r_i." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standardised scores within minus 1 and 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BWS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standardised-scores-within-minus-1-and-1" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(MAX(Scores)<=1,MIN(Scores)>=-1)" .

hemo:7002338 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Object A always chosen best in the seven-set design"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's example one respondent sees each object four times; object A is chosen best four times and never worst, a score of 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Object A always chosen best in the seven-set design" ;
    hemo:9000014 "B_i = 4; W_i = 0; N = 1; r_i = 4; S_i = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BWS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "object-a-always-chosen-best-in-the-seven-set-design" .

hemo:7002339 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Object D chosen best once"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Object D is chosen best once, in the only set where it is the strongest object, and never worst, a score of 0.25, above C's score of 0 although C ranks higher in the respondent's true order." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Object D chosen best once" ;
    hemo:9000014 "B_i = 1; W_i = 0; N = 1; r_i = 4; S_i = 0.25" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BWS-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "object-d-chosen-best-once" .

hemo:7002340 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Object F chosen worst twice"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Object F is chosen worst twice and never best, a score of minus 0.5." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Object F chosen worst twice" ;
    hemo:9000014 "B_i = 0; W_i = 2; N = 1; r_i = 4; S_i = -0.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BWS-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "object-f-chosen-worst-twice" .

hemo:7002341 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Sample of 100 respondents"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If 100 respondents each see an item four times and choose it best 180 times and worst 60 times, its score is 120 / 400 = 0.3 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sample of 100 respondents" ;
    hemo:9000014 "B_i = 180; W_i = 60; N = 100; r_i = 4; S_i = 0.3" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BWS-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sample-of-100-respondents" .

hemo:7002342 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Random utility with independent extreme value errors for the pair"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The utility difference of a pair is V_b minus V_w plus random error terms, and the errors give the logit form over ordered pairs. The utilities are on one scale for the set, with the error scale held constant." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Random utility with independent extreme value errors for the pair" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BWS-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "random-utility-with-independent-extreme-value-errors-for-the-pair" .

hemo:7002343 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Best and worst chosen jointly from the same set"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The respondent chooses the pair in one step from all ordered pairs of distinct items; the sequential model (HE-FM-BWS-004) instead chooses the worst item after removing the best." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Best and worst chosen jointly from the same set" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BWS-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "best-and-worst-chosen-jointly-from-the-same-set" .

hemo:7002344 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Maxdiff pair probability from a range of set utilities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000482 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the set's utilities in a column range named SetUtils and the chosen items' utilities in UtilBest and UtilWorst, the formula returns the probability, held in MaxDiffProb." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Maxdiff pair probability from a range of set utilities" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BWS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "maxdiff-pair-probability-from-a-range-of-set-utilities" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EXP(UtilBest-UtilWorst)/(SUMPRODUCT(EXP(SetUtils))*SUMPRODUCT(EXP(-SetUtils))-COUNT(SetUtils))" .

hemo:7002345 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Maxdiff denominator equals the explicit sum over ordered pairs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the denominator held in MaxDiffDenom, summing exp(V_j minus V_k) over the full matrix and subtracting the J diagonal ones gives the same value. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows pairs of an item with itself left in the denominator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Maxdiff denominator equals the explicit sum over ordered pairs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BWS-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "maxdiff-denominator-equals-the-explicit-sum-over-ordered-pairs" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(EXP(SetUtils-TRANSPOSE(SetUtils)))-COUNT(SetUtils)-MaxDiffDenom)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002346 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal utilities give one over J(J minus 1) under maxdiff"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When every utility in SetUtils is equal, each ordered pair has probability 1 / (J (J minus 1)). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a wrong count of pairs in the denominator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal utilities give one over J(J minus 1) under maxdiff" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BWS-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-utilities-give-one-over-j-j-minus-1-under-maxdiff" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(MAX(SetUtils)=MIN(SetUtils),ABS(MaxDiffProb-1/(COUNT(SetUtils)*(COUNT(SetUtils)-1)))<1E-12,TRUE)" .

hemo:7002347 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's set 1 with A best and G worst"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With utilities of 1.0, 0.5, 0 and minus 0.5 for A, C, E and G, S_pos is about 5.9735 and S_neg about 3.6231, so the denominator is about 17.643 and the probability of A best and G worst about 0.254, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's set 1 with A best and G worst" ;
    hemo:9000014 "V_b = 1; V_w = -0.5; S_pos = 5.973534; S_neg = 3.623131; J = 4; P_max = 0.254" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BWS-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-set-1-with-a-best-and-g-worst" .

hemo:7002348 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal utilities in a set of four"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When all four utilities are equal every ordered pair is equally likely, 1 / 12 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal utilities in a set of four" ;
    hemo:9000014 "V_b = 0; V_w = 0; S_pos = 4; S_neg = 4; J = 4; P_max = 0.0833" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BWS-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-utilities-in-a-set-of-four" .

hemo:7002349 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Worst chosen from the items left after the best"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The respondent first picks the best item and then the worst from the rest, as in rank-ordered or exploded logit analysis; the joint probability is the product of the two choices." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Worst chosen from the items left after the best" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BWS-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "worst-chosen-from-the-items-left-after-the-best" .

hemo:7002350 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same utility scale for best and worst choices"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The worst choice uses minus the same utilities and the same error scale as the best choice. Worst choices may follow a different mental process, in which case the scale can differ." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same utility scale for best and worst choices" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BWS-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-utility-scale-for-best-and-worst-choices" .

hemo:7002351 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Sequential best-then-worst probability from a range of set utilities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000483 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the set's utilities in SetUtils and the chosen items' utilities in UtilBest and UtilWorst, the formula returns the probability, held in SeqProb." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sequential best-then-worst probability from a range of set utilities" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BWS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sequential-best-then-worst-probability-from-a-range-of-set-utilities" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EXP(UtilBest)/SUMPRODUCT(EXP(SetUtils))*EXP(-UtilWorst)/(SUMPRODUCT(EXP(-SetUtils))-EXP(-UtilBest))" .

hemo:7002352 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Sequential pair probability not above the best-choice probability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The joint probability is the best-choice probability times a conditional probability, so it cannot exceed the first factor. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the best item left in the worst-choice denominator with a sign error, or utilities entered with the wrong sign." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sequential pair probability not above the best-choice probability" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BWS-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sequential-pair-probability-not-above-the-best-choice-probability" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(SeqProb>0,SeqProb<=EXP(UtilBest)/SUMPRODUCT(EXP(SetUtils)))" .

hemo:7002353 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal utilities give one over J(J minus 1) under the sequential model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With equal utilities the sequential probability is 1 / J times 1 / (J minus 1). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the best item not removed before the worst choice." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal utilities give one over J(J minus 1) under the sequential model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BWS-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-utilities-give-one-over-j-j-minus-1-under-the-sequential-model" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(MAX(SetUtils)=MIN(SetUtils),ABS(SeqProb-1/(COUNT(SetUtils)*(COUNT(SetUtils)-1)))<1E-12,TRUE)" .

hemo:7002354 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's set 1 under the sequential model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the same utilities, A is best with probability 2.718 / 5.974, about 0.455, and G is then worst among C, E and G with probability 1.649 / 3.256, about 0.506, a joint probability of about 0.2305, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's set 1 under the sequential model" ;
    hemo:9000014 "V_b = 1; V_w = -0.5; S_pos = 5.973534; S_neg = 3.623131; P_seq = 0.2305" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BWS-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-set-1-under-the-sequential-model" .

hemo:7002355 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal utilities in a set of four under the sequential model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With four equal utilities the best item has probability 1/4 and the worst then 1/3, a joint probability of 1/12, the same as the maxdiff model in this case (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal utilities in a set of four under the sequential model" ;
    hemo:9000014 "V_b = 0; V_w = 0; S_pos = 4; S_neg = 4; P_seq = 0.0833" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BWS-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-utilities-in-a-set-of-four-under-the-sequential-model" .

hemo:7002356 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal likelihood with known standard error and a normal prior"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The interim estimate is approximately normal around the true effect with standard error s, and the prior is normal, so the posterior is normal with the stated mean and variance." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal likelihood with known standard error and a normal prior" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BAD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-likelihood-with-known-standard-error-and-a-normal-prior" .

hemo:7002357 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Prior fixed before the interim data"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The prior is specified in the protocol and not chosen after seeing the data. A posterior summary is conditional on that prior, which may not be the prior an appraisal would choose." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prior fixed before the interim data" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BAD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prior-fixed-before-the-interim-data" .

hemo:7002358 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal posterior and posterior probability from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000484 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With PriorMean, PriorVar, InterimEst, InterimSE and MinEffect named, the formulas return the posterior variance (PostVar), the posterior mean (PostMean) and the posterior probability that the effect exceeds MinEffect (PostProb)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal posterior and posterior probability from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BAD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-posterior-and-posterior-probability-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1/(1/PriorVar+1/InterimSE^2); =PostVar*(PriorMean/PriorVar+InterimEst/InterimSE^2); =NORM.S.DIST((PostMean-MinEffect)/SQRT(PostVar),TRUE)" .

hemo:7002359 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior precision equals prior plus data precision"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Multiplying the posterior variance by the sum of the two precisions returns 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows standard deviations used where variances belong." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Posterior precision equals prior plus data precision" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BAD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "posterior-precision-equals-prior-plus-data-precision" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PostVar*(1/PriorVar+1/InterimSE^2)-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002360 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior mean lies between the prior mean and the interim estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A precision-weighted average cannot fall outside its two inputs. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows weights that do not sum to 1 or a sign error." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Posterior mean lies between the prior mean and the interim estimate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BAD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "posterior-mean-lies-between-the-prior-mean-and-the-interim-estimate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(PostMean>=MIN(PriorMean,InterimEst),PostMean<=MAX(PriorMean,InterimEst))" .

hemo:7002361 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's interim look on incremental net monetary benefit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a prior mean of 0 pounds and standard deviation of 2,000 pounds, and an interim estimate of 1,200 pounds with standard error 800, the estimate is 6.25 times as precise as the prior. The posterior mean is about 1,034.48 pounds with standard deviation 742.8, z_1 is about 1.3927 and the posterior probability of positive net benefit about 0.918, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's interim look on incremental net monetary benefit" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m_0 = 0; v_0 = 4000000; y = 1200; s = 800; a = 0; v_1 = 551724.1; m_1 = 1034.48; z_1 = 1.3927" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BAD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-interim-look-on-incremental-net-monetary-benefit" .

hemo:7002362 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Informative prior centred on 500 pounds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a prior mean of 500 pounds and standard deviation 1,000, the same interim data give a posterior mean of about 926.83 pounds, z_1 of about 1.4837 and a posterior probability of about 0.931 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Informative prior centred on 500 pounds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m_0 = 500; v_0 = 1000000; y = 1200; s = 800; a = 0; v_1 = 390243.9; m_1 = 926.83; z_1 = 1.4837" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BAD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "informative-prior-centred-on-500-pounds" .

hemo:7002363 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Minimum effect of 500 pounds in the success criterion"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Requiring net benefit above 500 pounds instead of above zero, the article's prior and data give z_1 of about 0.7196 and a posterior probability of about 0.764 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Minimum effect of 500 pounds in the success criterion" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m_0 = 0; v_0 = 4000000; y = 1200; s = 800; a = 500; v_1 = 551724.1; m_1 = 1034.48; z_1 = 0.7196" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BAD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "minimum-effect-of-500-pounds-in-the-success-criterion" .

hemo:7002364 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Second-stage estimate normal and independent of the first given the effect"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Given the true effect, the second-stage estimate is normal with standard error s_2 and independent of the first, so its predictive distribution has the interim posterior mean and the sum of the posterior and sampling variances." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Second-stage estimate normal and independent of the first given the effect" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BAD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "second-stage-estimate-normal-and-independent-of-the-first-given-the-effect" .

hemo:7002365 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Final analysis pools the prior and both stages"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The final posterior combines the prior with both estimates by precision weighting, and success means a final posterior probability of a positive effect above Phi(z_c). A different final rule changes y2_crit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Final analysis pools the prior and both stages" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BAD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "final-analysis-pools-the-prior-and-both-stages" .

hemo:7002366 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Predictive probability of final success from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000485 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With PriorMean, PriorVar, InterimEst, InterimSE, Stage2SE and ZFinal named, and PostMean and PostVar from HE-FM-BAD-001, the formulas return the final variance (FinalVar), the boundary (Stage2Crit) and the predictive probability (PredProb). ZFinal is NORM.S.INV(0.975) for a 0.975 rule." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Predictive probability of final success from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BAD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "predictive-probability-of-final-success-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1/(1/PriorVar+1/InterimSE^2+1/Stage2SE^2); =Stage2SE^2*(ZFinal/SQRT(FinalVar)-PriorMean/PriorVar-InterimEst/InterimSE^2); =1-NORM.S.DIST((Stage2Crit-PostMean)/SQRT(PostVar+Stage2SE^2),TRUE)" .

hemo:7002367 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Second-stage boundary gives exactly the final success threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Plugging Stage2Crit in as the second-stage estimate makes the final posterior mean divided by the final standard deviation equal ZFinal. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a boundary computed without the prior or with the interim posterior variance in place of the final one." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Second-stage boundary gives exactly the final success threshold" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BAD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "second-stage-boundary-gives-exactly-the-final-success-threshold" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(FinalVar*(PriorMean/PriorVar+InterimEst/InterimSE^2+Stage2Crit/Stage2SE^2)/SQRT(FinalVar)-ZFinal)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002368 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Predictive probability one half when the boundary equals the posterior mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When the interim posterior mean sits exactly on the boundary the predictive distribution is centred on it. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a predictive distribution centred on the interim estimate instead of the posterior mean." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Predictive probability one half when the boundary equals the posterior mean" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BAD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "predictive-probability-one-half-when-the-boundary-equals-the-posterior-mean" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(ABS(Stage2Crit-PostMean)<1E-9,ABS(PredProb-0.5)<1E-9,TRUE)" .

hemo:7002369 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's interim look, predictive probability about 0.474"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's prior and interim data and a second stage of 100 patients per arm with standard error 800, the final standard deviation would be about 544.3, success needs a second-stage estimate above about 1,104.5 pounds, and z_pp is about 0.0641, so the predictive probability of success is about 0.474, above the futility bound of 0.10 (the article, rounding the boundary to 1,104.3, reports 0.4745)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's interim look: predictive probability about 0.474" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m_0 = 0; v_0 = 4000000; y_1 = 1200; s_1 = 800; s_2 = 800; z_c = 1.96; v_1 = 551724.1; m_1 = 1034.48; v_f = 296296.3; y2_crit = 1104.48; z_pp = 0.0641" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BAD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-interim-look-predictive-probability-about-0-474" .

hemo:7002370 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Interim estimate of zero triggers the futility rule"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the interim estimate had been 0 pounds, the posterior mean would be 0, success would need a second-stage estimate above about 2,304.5 pounds and the predictive probability would be about 0.017, below 0.10, so the protocol would stop for futility (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Interim estimate of zero triggers the futility rule" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m_0 = 0; v_0 = 4000000; y_1 = 0; s_1 = 800; s_2 = 800; z_c = 1.96; v_1 = 551724.1; m_1 = 0; v_f = 296296.3; y2_crit = 2304.48; z_pp = 2.111" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BAD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "interim-estimate-of-zero-triggers-the-futility-rule" .

hemo:7002371 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Interim estimate of 1,600 pounds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An interim estimate of 1,600 pounds gives a posterior mean of about 1,379.31, a boundary of about 704.5 pounds and a predictive probability of about 0.732 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Interim estimate of 1,600 pounds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m_0 = 0; v_0 = 4000000; y_1 = 1600; s_1 = 800; s_2 = 800; z_c = 1.96; v_1 = 551724.1; m_1 = 1379.31; v_f = 296296.3; y2_crit = 704.48; z_pp = -0.6182" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BAD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "interim-estimate-of-1-600-pounds" .

hemo:7002372 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Two arms with outcomes observed quickly"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The rule allocates between an experimental and a control arm, and the posterior probability is updated from outcomes already observed, so the outcome must be available soon after treatment for the allocation to adapt." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two arms with outcomes observed quickly" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BAD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-arms-with-outcomes-observed-quickly" .

hemo:7002373 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Stable patient population and standard of care over recruitment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Robertson and colleagues describe time trends, from changes in standard of care or drift in the patients recruited, as a major barrier to response-adaptive randomisation, because they can distort standard analyses." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Stable patient population and standard of care over recruitment" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BAD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "stable-patient-population-and-standard-of-care-over-recruitment" .

hemo:7002374 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Thall and Wathen allocation probability from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000486 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the posterior probability in PostProbBetter and the tuning constant in Tuning, the formula returns the allocation probability, held in AllocProb." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Thall and Wathen allocation probability from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BAD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "thall-and-wathen-allocation-probability-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PostProbBetter^Tuning/(PostProbBetter^Tuning+(1-PostProbBetter)^Tuning)" .

hemo:7002375 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Allocation probabilities to the two arms sum to 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The probability for the control arm, the same rule applied to 1 minus P, and AllocProb sum to 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows P^c used on its own without the denominator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Allocation probabilities to the two arms sum to 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BAD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "allocation-probabilities-to-the-two-arms-sum-to-1" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AllocProb+(1-PostProbBetter)^Tuning/((1-PostProbBetter)^Tuning+PostProbBetter^Tuning)-1)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002376 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Allocation between one half and P for a tuning constant below 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For 0 < c < 1 and P above 0.5 the allocation probability lies strictly between 0.5 and P. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the tuning constant applied to only one term." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Allocation between one half and P for a tuning constant below 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BAD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "allocation-between-one-half-and-p-for-a-tuning-constant-below-1" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(AND(Tuning>0,Tuning<1,PostProbBetter>0.5),AND(AllocProb>0.5,AllocProb<PostProbBetter),TRUE)" .

hemo:7002377 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's allocation with P of 0.918 and c of one half"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a posterior probability of 0.918 and c of 0.5, the square roots are about 0.958 and 0.286, so the next patient joins the experimental arm with probability about 0.770, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's allocation with P of 0.918 and c of one half" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P = 0.918; c = 0.5; pi_E = 0.7699" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BAD-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-allocation-with-p-of-0-918-and-c-of-one-half" .

hemo:7002378 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson sampling with c of 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With c of 1 the allocation probability equals the posterior probability, 0.918 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Thompson sampling with c of 1" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P = 0.918; c = 1; pi_E = 0.918" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BAD-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "thompson-sampling-with-c-of-1" .

hemo:7002379 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Tuning constant rising with enrolment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With c = i / (2n) after 50 of 200 planned patients, c is 0.125 and the allocation probability about 0.575, closer to equal allocation early in the trial (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Tuning constant rising with enrolment" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P = 0.918; c = 0.125; pi_E = 0.5749" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BAD-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "tuning-constant-rising-with-enrolment" .

hemo:7002380 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Binary response observed before each interim look"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each patient's response is binary and known before the next look, patients are exchangeable with one response rate, and the prior is beta." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Binary response observed before each interim look" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BAD-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "binary-response-observed-before-each-interim-look" .

hemo:7002381 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Design parameters fixed in advance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "N_max, p_0, theta_T, theta_L and theta_U are chosen before the trial, Lee and Liu by searching for the values that meet type I and type II error constraints." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Design parameters fixed in advance" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BAD-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "design-parameters-fixed-in-advance" .

hemo:7002382 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Lee and Liu predictive probability from weight and posterior columns"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000487 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the predictive weights for i = 0 to m in a range named PredWeights, the matching final posterior probabilities in PostProbs and the threshold in ThetaT, the formula returns the predictive probability, held in PredProbLL. HE-CF-BAD-002 shows how to fill the two columns." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Lee and Liu predictive probability from weight and posterior columns" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BAD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "lee-and-liu-predictive-probability-from-weight-and-posterior-columns" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(PredWeights*(PostProbs>ThetaT))" .

hemo:7002383 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Beta-binomial predictive weights sum to 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weights over i = 0 to m form a probability distribution. Expected result: TRUE when the weights are computed rather than typed from rounded values. FALSE shows a missing value of i or wrong beta-binomial parameters." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Beta-binomial predictive weights sum to 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BAD-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "beta-binomial-predictive-weights-sum-to-1" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUM(PredWeights)-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002384 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Final posterior probabilities rise with the number of future responses"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each extra response raises B_i, so the column never falls. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows responses and non-responses swapped in the beta parameters." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Final posterior probabilities rise with the number of future responses" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BAD-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "final-posterior-probabilities-rise-with-the-number-of-future-responses" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(--(OFFSET(PostProbs,1,0,ROWS(PostProbs)-1)<OFFSET(PostProbs,0,0,ROWS(PostProbs)-1)))=0" .

hemo:7002385 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Lee and Liu example with 16 responses in 23 patients"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With N_max of 40, 16 responses in 23 patients, a beta(0.6, 0.4) prior, p_0 of 0.6 and theta_T of 0.90, Y is beta-binomial(17, 16.6, 7.4). B_i is below 0.90 for 11 or fewer further responses and above it for 12 or more, so PP is the predictive weight of 12 to 17 responses, 0.5656, as Lee and Liu report." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Lee and Liu example with 16 responses in 23 patients" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m = 17; w_i = [0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0001, 0.0006, 0.0021, 0.0058, 0.0135, 0.0276, 0.0497, 0.0794, 0.1129, 0.1426, 0.1587, 0.1532, 0.1246, 0.0811, 0.0381, 0.0099]; B_i = [0.0059, 0.0138, 0.0296, 0.0581, 0.1049, 0.1743, 0.2679, 0.3821, 0.5085, 0.6349, 0.7489, 0.8415, 0.9089, 0.9528, 0.9781, 0.9910, 0.9968, 0.9990]; theta_T = 0.9; PP = 0.5656" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BAD-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "lee-and-liu-example-with-16-responses-in-23-patients" .

hemo:7002386 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Four patients to come with a uniform prior"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With N_max of 10, 4 responses in 6 patients, a uniform beta(1, 1) prior, p_0 of 0.5 and theta_T of 0.90, only 4 responses among the last 4 patients lifts B_i above 0.90 (0.9673; 3 responses give 0.8867), so PP is the weight of that result, about 0.2121 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Four patients to come with a uniform prior" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m = 4; w_i = [0.0455, 0.1515, 0.2727, 0.3182, 0.2121]; B_i = [0.2744, 0.5000, 0.7256, 0.8867, 0.9673]; theta_T = 0.9; PP = 0.2121" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BAD-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "four-patients-to-come-with-a-uniform-prior" .

hemo:7002387 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Only the price of good j changes between the two arc cross-price observations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Income, preferences, the price of good i and other prices are the same in both observations, so the change in Q_i is attributed to the price of j." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Only the price of good j changes between the two arc cross-price observations" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XPE-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "only-the-price-of-good-j-changes-between-the-two-arc-cross-price-observations" .

hemo:7002388 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Cross-price elasticity price measured where the prescribing or buying decision is made"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "P_j is the price faced by whoever chooses, such as the patient's co-payment; for medicines the response passes through prescribers and pharmacists, so the elasticity summarises the whole chain." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cross-price elasticity price measured where the prescribing or buying decision is made" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XPE-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cross-price-elasticity-price-measured-where-the-prescribing-or-buying-decision-is-made" .

hemo:7002389 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Arc cross-price elasticity from named quantities and prices"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000488 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the quantities of good i in QtyAfter and QtyBefore and the prices of good j in PriceAfter and PriceBefore, the formula returns the arc elasticity, held in ArcCrossElasticity." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Arc cross-price elasticity from named quantities and prices" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-XPE-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "arc-cross-price-elasticity-from-named-quantities-and-prices" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=((QtyAfter-QtyBefore)/(QtyAfter+QtyBefore))/((PriceAfter-PriceBefore)/(PriceAfter+PriceBefore))" .

hemo:7002390 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Arc cross-price elasticity equals the ratio of midpoint percentage changes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Recomputing with each change divided by AVERAGE of its two values gives the same result, because the factors of 2 cancel. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a change divided by the first value instead of the average." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Arc cross-price elasticity equals the ratio of midpoint percentage changes" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XPE-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "arc-cross-price-elasticity-equals-the-ratio-of-midpoint-percentage-changes" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(((QtyAfter-QtyBefore)/AVERAGE(QtyAfter,QtyBefore))/((PriceAfter-PriceBefore)/AVERAGE(PriceAfter,PriceBefore))-ArcCrossElasticity)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002391 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Arc cross-price elasticity symmetric in the start point"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Swapping the before and after values leaves the result unchanged. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Arc cross-price elasticity symmetric in the start point" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XPE-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "arc-cross-price-elasticity-symmetric-in-the-start-point" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(((QtyBefore-QtyAfter)/(QtyBefore+QtyAfter))/((PriceBefore-PriceAfter)/(PriceBefore+PriceAfter))-ArcCrossElasticity)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002392 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Generic dispensing when the branded co-payment rises from 8 to 12 pounds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Generic packs rise from 6,000 to 7,000 a month when the branded co-payment rises from 8 to 12 pounds: 1,000 / 6,500, or 0.1538, divided by 4 / 10, or 0.40, gives about 0.38, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generic dispensing when the branded co-payment rises from 8 to 12 pounds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q_i1 = 7000; Q_i0 = 6000; P_j1 = 12; P_j0 = 8; eps_arc = 0.3846" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generic-dispensing-when-the-branded-co-payment-rises-from-8-to-12-pounds" .

hemo:7002393 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Arc cross-price elasticity of generic dispensing read in the opposite direction"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Treating the later month as the start (7,000 to 6,000 packs as the co-payment falls from 12 to 8 pounds) gives the same 0.3846, the reason for using midpoints." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Arc cross-price elasticity of generic dispensing read in the opposite direction" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q_i1 = 6000; Q_i0 = 7000; P_j1 = 8; P_j0 = 12; eps_arc = 0.3846" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "arc-cross-price-elasticity-of-generic-dispensing-read-in-the-opposite-direction" .

hemo:7002394 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Arc own-price elasticity of the branded medicine"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With i equal to j, branded packs falling from 4,000 to 2,800 as the branded co-payment rises from 8 to 12 pounds give minus 0.3529 / 0.40, about minus 0.88, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Arc own-price elasticity of the branded medicine" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q_i1 = 2800; Q_i0 = 4000; P_j1 = 12; P_j0 = 8; eps_arc = -0.8824" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "arc-own-price-elasticity-of-the-branded-medicine" .

hemo:7002395 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Linear cross-price demand relation over the observed price range"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The slope b_ij is constant between the observed points; with curved demand the formula holds only at the point where the slope is measured." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Linear cross-price demand relation over the observed price range" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XPE-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "linear-cross-price-demand-relation-over-the-observed-price-range" .

hemo:7002396 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Other prices and income held fixed for the point cross-price elasticity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The slope is a partial effect, so it applies only while the other prices and income stay where they were." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Other prices and income held fixed for the point cross-price elasticity" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XPE-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "other-prices-and-income-held-fixed-for-the-point-cross-price-elasticity" .

hemo:7002397 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Point cross-price elasticity from a named slope, price and quantity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000489 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the slope in CrossSlope and the price and quantity in PriceJ and QtyI, the formula returns the point elasticity, held in PointCrossElasticity. The slope from two observations is =(QtyAfter-QtyBefore)/(PriceAfter-PriceBefore)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Point cross-price elasticity from a named slope, price and quantity" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-XPE-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "point-cross-price-elasticity-from-a-named-slope-price-and-quantity" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CrossSlope*PriceJ/QtyI" .

hemo:7002398 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Point cross-price elasticity at the midpoint equals the arc value"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With PriceJ and QtyI set to the averages of the two observations, the point elasticity equals ArcCrossElasticity from HE-IM-XPE-001. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Point cross-price elasticity at the midpoint equals the arc value" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XPE-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "point-cross-price-elasticity-at-the-midpoint-equals-the-arc-value" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(CrossSlope*AVERAGE(PriceAfter,PriceBefore)/AVERAGE(QtyAfter,QtyBefore)-ArcCrossElasticity)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002399 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Sign of the point cross-price elasticity follows the slope"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Prices and quantities are positive, so the elasticity has the sign of the slope. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sign of the point cross-price elasticity follows the slope" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XPE-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sign-of-the-point-cross-price-elasticity-follows-the-slope" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(PriceJ>0,QtyI>0,SIGN(PointCrossElasticity)=SIGN(CrossSlope))" .

hemo:7002400 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Generic demand at the starting co-payment of 8 pounds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The straight line through the article's two observations has a slope of 1,000 packs per 4 pounds, 250 packs per pound. At 8 pounds and 6,000 packs the point elasticity is 250 x 8 / 6,000, about 0.33 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generic demand at the starting co-payment of 8 pounds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_ij = 250; P_j = 8; Q_i = 6000; eps_ij = 0.3333" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generic-demand-at-the-starting-co-payment-of-8-pounds" .

hemo:7002401 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Generic demand at the midpoint co-payment of 10 pounds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At the midpoint, 10 pounds and 6,500 packs, the point elasticity is 250 x 10 / 6,500, about 0.3846, equal to the arc elasticity (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generic demand at the midpoint co-payment of 10 pounds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_ij = 250; P_j = 10; Q_i = 6500; eps_ij = 0.3846" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generic-demand-at-the-midpoint-co-payment-of-10-pounds" .

hemo:7002402 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Generic demand at the new co-payment of 12 pounds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At 12 pounds and 7,000 packs the point elasticity is about 0.43 (computed here for illustration), so a single figure depends on where it is measured." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generic demand at the new co-payment of 12 pounds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_ij = 250; P_j = 12; Q_i = 7000; eps_ij = 0.4286" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generic-demand-at-the-new-co-payment-of-12-pounds" .

hemo:7002403 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant elasticities over the price range"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Log quantity is linear in log prices, as in Meng and colleagues' alcohol demand equations, so each elasticity is the same at every price in the range." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant elasticities over the price range" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XPE-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-elasticities-over-the-price-range" .

hemo:7002404 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Other prices, income and preferences unchanged in the cross-price elasticity projection"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Only P_i and P_j change; further goods with changing prices add further factors, which the matrix version (HE-CF-XPE-001) handles." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Other prices, income and preferences unchanged in the cross-price elasticity projection" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XPE-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "other-prices-income-and-preferences-unchanged-in-the-cross-price-elasticity-projection" .

hemo:7002405 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Quantity after own and cross price changes from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000490 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With QtyBefore, OwnPriceAfter, OwnPriceBefore, OtherPriceAfter, OtherPriceBefore, OwnElasticity and CrossElasticity named, the formula returns the new quantity, held in QtyProjected." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Quantity after own and cross price changes from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-XPE-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "quantity-after-own-and-cross-price-changes-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=QtyBefore*(OwnPriceAfter/OwnPriceBefore)^OwnElasticity*(OtherPriceAfter/OtherPriceBefore)^CrossElasticity" .

hemo:7002406 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cross-price elasticity projection unchanged when neither price changes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With both price ratios equal to 1 the projection equals QtyBefore whatever the elasticities. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cross-price elasticity projection unchanged when neither price changes" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XPE-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cross-price-elasticity-projection-unchanged-when-neither-price-changes" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(AND(OwnPriceAfter=OwnPriceBefore,OtherPriceAfter=OtherPriceBefore),ABS(QtyProjected-QtyBefore)<1E-9,TRUE)" .

hemo:7002407 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Log change in quantity equals the elasticity-weighted log price changes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "LN(QtyProjected/QtyBefore) equals OwnElasticity times the log own-price ratio plus CrossElasticity times the log cross-price ratio. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log change in quantity equals the elasticity-weighted log price changes" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XPE-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-change-in-quantity-equals-the-elasticity-weighted-log-price-changes" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LN(QtyProjected/QtyBefore)-OwnElasticity*LN(OwnPriceAfter/OwnPriceBefore)-CrossElasticity*LN(OtherPriceAfter/OtherPriceBefore))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002408 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Generic packs after the branded co-payment rise under a constant elasticity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the generic co-payment unchanged at 2 pounds and a cross elasticity of 0.3846, a branded co-payment rise from 8 to 12 pounds projects 6,000 x 1.5 to the power 0.3846, about 7,013 generic packs, close to the 7,000 observed (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generic packs after the branded co-payment rise under a constant elasticity" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q_i0 = 6000; P_i1 = 2; P_i0 = 2; P_j1 = 12; P_j0 = 8; eps_ii = -0.3; eps_ij = 0.3846; Q_i1 = 7012.55" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generic-packs-after-the-branded-co-payment-rise-under-a-constant-elasticity" .

hemo:7002409 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Branded packs after their own co-payment rise under a constant elasticity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With an own-price elasticity of minus 0.8824 and the generic price unchanged, branded packs fall from 4,000 to about 2,797, close to the 2,800 observed (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Branded packs after their own co-payment rise under a constant elasticity" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q_i0 = 4000; P_i1 = 12; P_i0 = 8; P_j1 = 2; P_j0 = 2; eps_ii = -0.8824; eps_ij = 0.1; Q_i1 = 2796.9" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "branded-packs-after-their-own-co-payment-rise-under-a-constant-elasticity" .

hemo:7002410 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Own and cross-price elasticity response to a 10 per cent tax on two substitutes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If a tax raises both prices by 10 per cent, with an own elasticity of minus 0.8 and a cross elasticity of 0.3, 1,000 units become 1,000 x 1.1 to the power minus 0.5, about 953.5; the small-change sum, 1 minus 0.08 plus 0.03, gives 950 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Own and cross-price elasticity response to a 10 per cent tax on two substitutes" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q_i0 = 1000; P_i1 = 1.1; P_i0 = 1; P_j1 = 1.1; P_j0 = 1; eps_ii = -0.8; eps_ij = 0.3; Q_i1 = 953.46" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "own-and-cross-price-elasticity-response-to-a-10-per-cent-tax-on-two-substitutes" .

hemo:7002411 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Smooth demand at a utility-maximising choice for the Slutsky cross-price decomposition"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The Slutsky equation holds for continuous, locally non-satiated preferences with single-valued, differentiable demands, evaluated where income equals the expenditure needed for the utility level." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Smooth demand at a utility-maximising choice for the Slutsky cross-price decomposition" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XPE-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "smooth-demand-at-a-utility-maximising-choice-for-the-slutsky-cross-price-decomposition" .

hemo:7002412 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Elasticities and budget share measured at the same point"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "eps_ij, w_j and eta_i refer to the same prices, income and population; the elasticity form follows from multiplying the Slutsky equation by P_j / Q_i." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Elasticities and budget share measured at the same point" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XPE-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "elasticities-and-budget-share-measured-at-the-same-point" .

hemo:7002413 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Compensated cross elasticity from named gross elasticity, share and income elasticity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000491 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With GrossCrossElasticity, BudgetShareJ and IncomeElasticityI named, the formula returns the compensated elasticity, held in CompensatedCrossElasticity." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Compensated cross elasticity from named gross elasticity, share and income elasticity" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-XPE-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "compensated-cross-elasticity-from-named-gross-elasticity-share-and-income-elasticity" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=GrossCrossElasticity+BudgetShareJ*IncomeElasticityI" .

hemo:7002414 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Budget share entered as a proportion in the Slutsky cross-price equation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The budget share is at least zero and at most 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a share typed as a percentage." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Budget share entered as a proportion in the Slutsky cross-price equation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XPE-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "budget-share-entered-as-a-proportion-in-the-slutsky-cross-price-equation" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(BudgetShareJ>=0,BudgetShareJ<=1)" .

hemo:7002415 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gross and compensated cross elasticities equal when the income elasticity is zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With IncomeElasticityI set to 0 the two elasticities are equal. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gross and compensated cross elasticities equal when the income elasticity is zero" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XPE-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gross-and-compensated-cross-elasticities-equal-when-the-income-elasticity-is-zero" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(IncomeElasticityI=0,ABS(CompensatedCrossElasticity-GrossCrossElasticity)<1E-12,TRUE)" .

hemo:7002416 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Generic demand when the branded co-payment is a tiny budget share"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the branded co-payment takes 0.2 per cent of the budget and the income elasticity of generic use is 0.5, the compensated elasticity is 0.3846 plus 0.001, about 0.3856, so gross and compensated values nearly coincide (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generic demand when the branded co-payment is a tiny budget share" ;
    hemo:9000014 "eps_ij = 0.3846; w_j = 0.002; eta_i = 0.5; eps_c_ij = 0.3856" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generic-demand-when-the-branded-co-payment-is-a-tiny-budget-share" .

hemo:7002417 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gross cross-price complements that are net substitutes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a gross elasticity of minus 0.1, a budget share of 0.3 for good j and an income elasticity of 1 for good i, the compensated elasticity is plus 0.2: the sign changes once the income effect is removed (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gross cross-price complements that are net substitutes" ;
    hemo:9000014 "eps_ij = -0.1; w_j = 0.3; eta_i = 1; eps_c_ij = 0.2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gross-cross-price-complements-that-are-net-substitutes" .

hemo:7002418 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Cross-price elasticity symmetry applies to compensated effects only"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The Hicksian price derivatives are symmetric; gross (Marshallian) cross effects are not, because income effects differ between goods." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cross-price elasticity symmetry applies to compensated effects only" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XPE-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cross-price-elasticity-symmetry-applies-to-compensated-effects-only" .

hemo:7002419 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same population and prices for both compensated cross-price elasticities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both elasticities and both budget shares refer to one consumer's or one population's demand system at the same prices." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same population and prices for both compensated cross-price elasticities" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XPE-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-population-and-prices-for-both-compensated-cross-price-elasticities" .

hemo:7002420 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Reverse compensated elasticity from named shares"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000492 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With CompensatedCrossElasticity, BudgetShareI and BudgetShareJ named, the formula returns the reverse compensated elasticity, held in ReverseCompensated." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reverse compensated elasticity from named shares" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-XPE-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reverse-compensated-elasticity-from-named-shares" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=BudgetShareI*CompensatedCrossElasticity/BudgetShareJ" .

hemo:7002421 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Share-weighted compensated elasticities equal in both directions"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "BudgetShareI times CompensatedCrossElasticity equals BudgetShareJ times ReverseCompensated. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Share-weighted compensated elasticities equal in both directions" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XPE-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "share-weighted-compensated-elasticities-equal-in-both-directions" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(BudgetShareI*CompensatedCrossElasticity-BudgetShareJ*ReverseCompensated)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002422 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reverse compensated elasticity has the same sign"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Net substitutes are reciprocal, so the two compensated elasticities share a sign. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reverse compensated elasticity has the same sign" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XPE-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reverse-compensated-elasticity-has-the-same-sign" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SIGN(ReverseCompensated)=SIGN(CompensatedCrossElasticity)" .

hemo:7002423 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Compensated cross-price elasticity of a small-share product and its large-share counterpart"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If good i takes 1 per cent of the budget and good j 10 per cent, a compensated elasticity of 0.5 for i with respect to the price of j implies only 0.05 for j with respect to the price of i (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Compensated cross-price elasticity of a small-share product and its large-share counterpart" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_i = 0.01; eps_c_ij = 0.5; w_j = 0.1; eps_c_ji = 0.05" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "compensated-cross-price-elasticity-of-a-small-share-product-and-its-large-share-counterpart" .

hemo:7002424 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal budget shares give equal compensated elasticities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With both goods at 5 per cent of the budget the two compensated elasticities are equal (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal budget shares give equal compensated elasticities" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_i = 0.05; eps_c_ij = 0.5; w_j = 0.05; eps_c_ji = 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XPE-013" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-budget-shares-give-equal-compensated-elasticities" .

hemo:7002425 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Parallel trends in the absence of the policy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Without the policy the treated group's mean would have changed by the same amount as the comparison group's. The assumption concerns changes, not levels, and is sensitive to scale: trends parallel in rates need not be parallel in log rates." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Parallel trends in the absence of the policy" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "parallel-trends-in-the-absence-of-the-policy" .

hemo:7002426 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "No anticipation and no spillovers in a difference-in-differences design"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The policy has no effect before it starts, and one unit's outcome does not depend on another unit's treatment, so the comparison group is not affected by the policy." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No anticipation and no spillovers in a difference-in-differences design" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-anticipation-and-no-spillovers-in-a-difference-in-differences-design" .

hemo:7002427 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same outcome definition and scale in all four difference-in-differences cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "All four means use the same measure, population base and period length; a change of coding or denominator in one cell shifts the estimate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same outcome definition and scale in all four difference-in-differences cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-outcome-definition-and-scale-in-all-four-difference-in-differences-cells" .

hemo:7002428 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-by-two difference-in-differences from named group means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000493 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the four means in cells named TreatedAfter, TreatedBefore, ComparisonAfter and ComparisonBefore, the formula returns the estimate, held in a cell named DiDEstimate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-by-two difference-in-differences from named group means" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-by-two-difference-in-differences-from-named-group-means" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(TreatedAfter-TreatedBefore)-(ComparisonAfter-ComparisonBefore)" .

hemo:7002429 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Difference-in-differences estimate equals the gap from the treated counterfactual mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The counterfactual mean for the treated group is TreatedBefore plus the comparison group's change (52.0 minus 2.0, or 50.0, in the first example), and the estimate is TreatedAfter minus that counterfactual. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Difference-in-differences estimate equals the gap from the treated counterfactual mean" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "difference-in-differences-estimate-equals-the-gap-from-the-treated-counterfactual-mean" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(DiDEstimate-(TreatedAfter-(TreatedBefore+ComparisonAfter-ComparisonBefore)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002430 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Difference-in-differences estimate unchanged by a fixed group difference"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Adding the same constant to both of a group's means, a fixed difference between groups, leaves the estimate unchanged; with 10 added to the treated group the check returns TRUE. FALSE shows a level comparison in one period instead of a difference of changes." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Difference-in-differences estimate unchanged by a fixed group difference" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "difference-in-differences-estimate-unchanged-by-a-fixed-group-difference" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(((TreatedAfter+10)-(TreatedBefore+10))-(ComparisonAfter-ComparisonBefore)-DiDEstimate)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002431 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Difference-in-differences for a care-coordination payment and emergency admissions"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustration region A falls from 52.0 to 47.0 admissions per 1,000 and region B from 48.0 to 46.0, so the estimate is minus 5.0 minus minus 2.0, or minus 3.0 per 1,000 per year." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Difference-in-differences for a care-coordination payment and emergency admissions" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y_T1 = 47; Y_T0 = 52; Y_C1 = 46; Y_C0 = 48; tau = -3" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "difference-in-differences-for-a-care-coordination-payment-and-emergency-admissions" .

hemo:7002432 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Card and Krueger difference-in-differences for the New Jersey minimum wage rise"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Card and Krueger's Table 3 reports mean full-time-equivalent employment per store of 20.44 before and 21.03 after in New Jersey and 23.33 and 21.17 in eastern Pennsylvania. The rounded means give 0.59 minus minus 2.16, or 2.75; Card and Krueger report 2.76 from unrounded data." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Card and Krueger difference-in-differences for the New Jersey minimum wage rise" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y_T1 = 21.03; Y_T0 = 20.44; Y_C1 = 21.17; Y_C0 = 23.33; tau = 2.75" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "card-and-krueger-difference-in-differences-for-the-new-jersey-minimum-wage-rise" .

hemo:7002433 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Placebo estimate across two pre-policy years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Applying the same formula to 2021 and 2023, both before the policy, gives (52.0 minus 58.0) minus (48.0 minus 50.0), or minus 4.0, where a value near zero would be expected under parallel trends." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Placebo estimate across two pre-policy years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y_T1 = 52; Y_T0 = 58; Y_C1 = 48; Y_C0 = 50; tau = -4" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "placebo-estimate-across-two-pre-policy-years" .

hemo:7002434 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Balanced panel or repeated cross-sections for the difference-in-differences regression"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a balanced panel the regression with a constant, D, P and D x P gives the same coefficient as one with unit and period fixed effects; the form with a constant also applies to repeated cross-sections." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Balanced panel or repeated cross-sections for the difference-in-differences regression" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DID-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "balanced-panel-or-repeated-cross-sections-for-the-difference-in-differences-regression" .

hemo:7002435 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard errors clustered at the level of policy assignment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Outcomes are correlated within areas or hospitals over time, so standard errors are clustered at the level at which the policy was assigned, which needs enough treated and comparison clusters." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standard errors clustered at the level of policy assignment" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DID-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standard-errors-clustered-at-the-level-of-policy-assignment" .

hemo:7002436 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Difference-in-differences regression coefficients from named group means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000494 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the four means named as in HE-IM-DID-001, the first three formulas give the constant, the group gap and the common change, held in Alpha, GapD and ChangeP, and the fourth the interaction coefficient, held in Interaction. With unit-level data in columns, LINEST on columns D, P and D x P returns the same coefficients." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Difference-in-differences regression coefficients from named group means" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "difference-in-differences-regression-coefficients-from-named-group-means" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ComparisonBefore; =TreatedBefore-ComparisonBefore; =ComparisonAfter-ComparisonBefore; =TreatedAfter-TreatedBefore-ComparisonAfter+ComparisonBefore" .

hemo:7002437 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Difference-in-differences regression coefficients reproduce the four group means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The fitted value for the treated group after the policy equals the observed mean. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the interaction coefficient taken from a specification without the separate D and P terms." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Difference-in-differences regression coefficients reproduce the four group means" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "difference-in-differences-regression-coefficients-reproduce-the-four-group-means" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(Alpha+GapD+ChangeP+Interaction-TreatedAfter)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002438 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Interaction coefficient equals the two-by-two estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The interaction equals DiDEstimate from HE-IM-DID-001. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Interaction coefficient equals the two-by-two estimate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DID-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "interaction-coefficient-equals-the-two-by-two-estimate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(Interaction-DiDEstimate)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002439 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fitted treated mean after the policy in the admissions example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha of 48.0, a fixed gap of 4.0, a common change of minus 2.0 and an interaction of minus 3.0, the fitted mean for region A after the policy is 47.0, the observed value." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fitted treated mean after the policy in the admissions example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 48; gamma_D = 4; lambda_P = -2; tau = -3; D = 1; P = 1; Y = 47" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fitted-treated-mean-after-the-policy-in-the-admissions-example" .

hemo:7002440 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fitted comparison mean after the policy in the admissions example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For region B after the policy only the constant and the common change apply: 48.0 minus 2.0 gives 46.0." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fitted comparison mean after the policy in the admissions example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 48; gamma_D = 4; lambda_P = -2; tau = -3; D = 0; P = 1; Y = 46" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fitted-comparison-mean-after-the-policy-in-the-admissions-example" .

hemo:7002441 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fitted New Jersey mean from the Card and Krueger difference-in-differences regression"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "From Card and Krueger's rounded means, alpha is 23.33, the gap minus 2.89, the common change minus 2.16 and the interaction 2.75, so the fitted New Jersey mean after the rise is 21.03." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fitted New Jersey mean from the Card and Krueger difference-in-differences regression" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 23.33; gamma_D = -2.89; lambda_P = -2.16; tau = 2.75; D = 1; P = 1; Y = 21.03" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fitted-new-jersey-mean-from-the-card-and-krueger-difference-in-differences-regression" .

hemo:7002442 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Differential trend continues in a straight line"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The difference in trends seen before the policy would have continued at the same rate per year. Rambachan and Roth bound how far the post-policy violation can deviate from such a linear extrapolation, which is preferable to a single corrected number." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Differential trend continues in a straight line" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DID-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "differential-trend-continues-in-a-straight-line" .

hemo:7002443 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Pre-policy periods free of anticipation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The placebo interval ends before the policy is announced, so delta_pre reflects trends and not early responses." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Pre-policy periods free of anticipation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DID-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pre-policy-periods-free-of-anticipation" .

hemo:7002444 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Trend-adjusted estimate from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000495 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the unadjusted estimate in DiDEstimate, the placebo estimate in PlaceboDiD and the two interval lengths in PreYears and PostYears, the formula returns the adjusted estimate, held in AdjustedDiD." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Trend-adjusted estimate from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "trend-adjusted-estimate-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=DiDEstimate-PlaceboDiD*PostYears/PreYears" .

hemo:7002445 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Adjusted estimate equals the estimate when the placebo is zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Setting PlaceboDiD to 0 must return DiDEstimate. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Adjusted estimate equals the estimate when the placebo is zero" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DID-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "adjusted-estimate-equals-the-estimate-when-the-placebo-is-zero" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(PlaceboDiD=0,ABS(AdjustedDiD-DiDEstimate)<1E-9,TRUE)" .

hemo:7002446 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Pre-trend interval lengths entered as positive years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both intervals are above zero and below 50 years. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows calendar years such as 2023 entered instead of interval lengths." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Pre-trend interval lengths entered as positive years" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DID-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pre-trend-interval-lengths-entered-as-positive-years" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(PreYears>0,PostYears>0,PreYears<50,PostYears<50)" .

hemo:7002447 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Admissions example with a two-year differential decline before the policy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The placebo estimate of minus 4.0 over 2021 to 2023, carried over the two years to 2025, explains a gap of 4.0, so the estimate of minus 3.0 becomes plus 1.0 admissions per 1,000, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Admissions example with a two-year differential decline before the policy" ;
    hemo:9000014 "tau = -3; delta_pre = -4; s_pre = 2; s_post = 2; tau_adj = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "admissions-example-with-a-two-year-differential-decline-before-the-policy" .

hemo:7002448 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same pre-trend carried over a one-year post-policy interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the after period were one year after the before period, half of the pre-policy difference would be carried forward: minus 3.0 plus 2.0 gives minus 1.0 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same pre-trend carried over a one-year post-policy interval" ;
    hemo:9000014 "tau = -3; delta_pre = -4; s_pre = 2; s_post = 1; tau_adj = -1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-pre-trend-carried-over-a-one-year-post-policy-interval" .

hemo:7002449 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "No differential pre-trend leaves the estimate unchanged"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a placebo estimate of zero the adjusted estimate equals the unadjusted one." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No differential pre-trend leaves the estimate unchanged" ;
    hemo:9000014 "tau = -3; delta_pre = 0; s_pre = 2; s_post = 2; tau_adj = -3" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-differential-pre-trend-leaves-the-estimate-unchanged" .

hemo:7002450 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Parallel trends between each cohort and the never-treated group"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Without treatment, each cohort's mean would have changed like the never-treated mean from g minus 1 to t. Callaway and Sant'Anna also allow not-yet-treated units as the comparison, and conditional versions with covariates." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Parallel trends between each cohort and the never-treated group" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DID-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "parallel-trends-between-each-cohort-and-the-never-treated-group" .

hemo:7002451 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Staggered adoption that stays on and is not anticipated"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Units remain treated after adoption, and outcomes in g minus 1 are not affected by the coming policy." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Staggered adoption that stays on and is not anticipated" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DID-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "staggered-adoption-that-stays-on-and-is-not-anticipated" .

hemo:7002452 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Group-time effect from named cohort and never-treated means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000496 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the cohort's means in CohortNow and CohortBase and the never-treated means in NeverNow and NeverBase, the formula returns ATT(g,t), held in GroupTimeATT." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Group-time effect from named cohort and never-treated means" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DID-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "group-time-effect-from-named-cohort-and-never-treated-means" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(CohortNow-CohortBase)-(NeverNow-NeverBase)" .

hemo:7002453 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Group-time effect is zero for a cohort that moves with the never-treated group"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the cohort's change equals the never-treated change, the effect is zero. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Group-time effect is zero for a cohort that moves with the never-treated group" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DID-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "group-time-effect-is-zero-for-a-cohort-that-moves-with-the-never-treated-group" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(CohortNow-CohortBase=NeverNow-NeverBase,GroupTimeATT=0,TRUE)" .

hemo:7002454 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cohort adopting in 2023, effect in 2025"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In an illustrative panel, units adopting in 2023 average 59 admissions per 1,000 in 2022 and 51 in 2025, while never-treated units fall from 49 to 46, so the effect two years after adoption is minus 8 minus minus 3, or minus 5 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cohort adopting in 2023, effect in 2025" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y_g_t = 51; Y_g_base = 59; Y_n_t = 46; Y_n_base = 49; ATT_gt = -5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cohort-adopting-in-2023-effect-in-2025" .

hemo:7002455 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cohort adopting in 2024, effect in the adoption year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Units adopting in 2024 move from 53 in 2023 to 50 in 2024 while never-treated units fall from 48 to 47, an effect of minus 2 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cohort adopting in 2024, effect in the adoption year" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Y_g_t = 50; Y_g_base = 53; Y_n_t = 47; Y_n_base = 48; ATT_gt = -2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cohort-adopting-in-2024-effect-in-the-adoption-year" .

hemo:7002456 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Difference-in-differences effect applied to the population covered"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "tau is the average effect on the treated, so N is the treated population; applying it to later adopters assumes they would gain as much." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Difference-in-differences effect applied to the population covered" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DID-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "difference-in-differences-effect-applied-to-the-population-covered" .

hemo:7002457 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Difference-in-differences effect persists over the year costed"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The rate change holds for the full year; Kristensen and colleagues found the Advancing Quality mortality reduction no longer significant by 42 months, so effect duration is a modelling choice." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Difference-in-differences effect persists over the year costed" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DID-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "difference-in-differences-effect-persists-over-the-year-costed" .

hemo:7002458 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Net policy cost from named estimate, population and costs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000497 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With ProgrammeCost, DiDEstimate (per 1,000), CoveredPopulation and CostPerEvent named, the formula returns the net cost, held in NetPolicyCost." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net policy cost from named estimate, population and costs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DID-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-policy-cost-from-named-estimate-population-and-costs" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ProgrammeCost+DiDEstimate*CoveredPopulation/1000*CostPerEvent" .

hemo:7002459 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Net policy cost equals programme cost when the difference-in-differences estimate is zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With DiDEstimate set to 0 the net cost equals ProgrammeCost. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net policy cost equals programme cost when the difference-in-differences estimate is zero" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DID-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-policy-cost-equals-programme-cost-when-the-difference-in-differences-estimate-is-zero" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(DiDEstimate=0,ABS(NetPolicyCost-ProgrammeCost)<1E-6,TRUE)" .

hemo:7002460 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Events per year consistent with a difference-in-differences rate per 1,000"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The change in events per year, DiDEstimate times CoveredPopulation / 1000, is no larger in size than the covered population. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an implausible absolute rate above 1,000 per 1,000, such as an event count or a money value entered in place of the rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Events per year consistent with a difference-in-differences rate per 1,000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DID-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "events-per-year-consistent-with-a-difference-in-differences-rate-per-1-000" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(DiDEstimate*CoveredPopulation/1000)<=CoveredPopulation" .

hemo:7002461 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Net cost of the care-coordination payment from the unadjusted difference-in-differences estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 200,000 residents aged 75 and over, a cost of 3,000 pounds per admission and a payment costing 1.2 million pounds a year, 600 fewer admissions save 1.8 million pounds, a net saving of 0.6 million, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net cost of the care-coordination payment from the unadjusted difference-in-differences estimate" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_prog = 1200000; tau = -3; N = 200000; c_event = 3000; C_net = -600000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-cost-of-the-care-coordination-payment-from-the-unadjusted-difference-in-differences-estimate" .

hemo:7002462 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Care-coordination payment with the trend-adjusted estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the trend-adjusted estimate of plus 1.0 per 1,000, 200 more admissions cost 0.6 million pounds, and the net cost is about 1.8 million, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Care-coordination payment with the trend-adjusted estimate" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_prog = 1200000; tau = 1; N = 200000; c_event = 3000; C_net = 1800000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DID-013" ;
    hemo:9000023 "care-coordination-payment-with-the-trend-adjusted-estimate" .

hemo:7002463 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Threshold reflects the harm of a missed case against an unnecessary intervention"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Vickers and Elkin derive p_t from a decision tree in which the expected value of treating equals that of not treating, so the odds p_t / (1 minus p_t) equal the harm of an unnecessary intervention divided by the harm of a missed case. The threshold range is set before the curve is read." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Threshold reflects the harm of a missed case against an unnecessary intervention" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "threshold-reflects-the-harm-of-a-missed-case-against-an-unnecessary-intervention" .

hemo:7002464 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same expected benefit for every case and harm for every non-case in net benefit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Kerr and colleagues note that the formula assumes every case gains the same expected benefit and every non-case bears the same expected cost, whatever the predicted risk. Subgroups with different thresholds need separate curves." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same expected benefit for every case and harm for every non-case in net benefit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-expected-benefit-for-every-case-and-harm-for-every-non-case-in-net-benefit" .

hemo:7002465 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Decision curve net benefit from validation data separate from model development"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Net benefit estimated in the data used to build the model is optimistic; simulations by Vickers and colleagues found repeated 10-fold cross-validation the best correction, and transfer to a new setting needs external validation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Decision curve net benefit from validation data separate from model development" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "decision-curve-net-benefit-from-validation-data-separate-from-model-development" .

hemo:7002466 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Decision curve net benefit from named counts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000498 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the counts in cells named TruePos, FalsePos and SampleSize and the threshold in Threshold, the formula returns the net benefit, held in a cell named NetBenefit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Decision curve net benefit from named counts" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DCA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "decision-curve-net-benefit-from-named-counts" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=TruePos/SampleSize-FalsePos/SampleSize*Threshold/(1-Threshold)" .

hemo:7002467 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Net benefit not above the prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the number of patients with the event in EventCount, net benefit cannot exceed EventCount / SampleSize, reached only when every case and no non-case is classed positive. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a threshold entered as a percentage, which makes the false positive weight negative, or an event count from a different sample." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net benefit not above the prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-benefit-not-above-the-prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=NetBenefit<=EventCount/SampleSize+1E-12" .

hemo:7002468 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Threshold entered as a probability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The threshold must be a probability strictly above zero and below 1, and the positives cannot exceed the sample. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a threshold typed as 15 instead of 0.15." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Threshold entered as a probability" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "threshold-entered-as-a-probability" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(Threshold>0,Threshold<1,TruePos+FalsePos<=SampleSize)" .

hemo:7002469 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Seminal vesicle invasion model at a 10 per cent threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In Vickers and Elkin's validation sample of 902 men, the prediction model classed 65 men with seminal vesicle invasion and 225 without it as positive at a 10 per cent threshold, giving a net benefit of 0.0443." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Seminal vesicle invasion model at a 10 per cent threshold" ;
    hemo:9000014 "TP = 65; FP = 225; n = 902; p_t = 0.1; NB = 0.0443" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "seminal-vesicle-invasion-model-at-a-10-per-cent-threshold" .

hemo:7002470 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Admission-risk model A at a 15 per cent threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Model A classes the medium and high risk groups as positive: 22 admissions and 28 patients not admitted among 100. The false positive weight is 0.15 / 0.85, about 0.1765, and the net benefit 0.1706, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Admission-risk model A at a 15 per cent threshold" ;
    hemo:9000014 "TP = 22; FP = 28; n = 100; p_t = 0.15; NB = 0.1706" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "admission-risk-model-a-at-a-15-per-cent-threshold" .

hemo:7002471 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Admission-risk model B at a 40 per cent threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Model B overestimates the medium group's risk at 45 per cent, so at 40 per cent it still classes 22 admissions and 28 non-admissions as positive. With a weight of about 0.6667 its net benefit is 0.0333, against 0.0833 for model A, which classes only the high group (13 and 7) as positive." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Admission-risk model B at a 40 per cent threshold" ;
    hemo:9000014 "TP = 22; FP = 28; n = 100; p_t = 0.4; NB = 0.0333" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "admission-risk-model-b-at-a-40-per-cent-threshold" .

hemo:7002472 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Intervene-in-all prevalence taken from the same validation sample"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "pi is the event rate in the sample used for the model's curve, so the defaults and the model are compared on the same patients." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Intervene-in-all prevalence taken from the same validation sample" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "intervene-in-all-prevalence-taken-from-the-same-validation-sample" .

hemo:7002473 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Intervening in everyone uses the threshold only as an exchange rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Kerr and colleagues note that the treat-all and treat-none policies use no individual risks, but the threshold is still used to value false positives against true positives." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Intervening in everyone uses the threshold only as an exchange rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "intervening-in-everyone-uses-the-threshold-only-as-an-exchange-rate" .

hemo:7002474 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Net benefit of intervening in everyone from named prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000499 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the prevalence in a cell named Prevalence and the threshold in Threshold, the formula returns the net benefit of intervening in everyone, held in NetBenefitAll." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net benefit of intervening in everyone from named prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DCA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-benefit-of-intervening-in-everyone-from-named-prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Prevalence-(1-Prevalence)*Threshold/(1-Threshold)" .

hemo:7002475 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Intervene-in-all line crosses zero at the prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Threshold set equal to Prevalence, NetBenefitAll is zero. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the weight applied to the prevalence instead of its complement." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Intervene-in-all line crosses zero at the prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "intervene-in-all-line-crosses-zero-at-the-prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(ABS(Threshold-Prevalence)<1E-12,ABS(NetBenefitAll)<1E-9,TRUE)" .

hemo:7002476 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Intervene-in-all net benefit not above the prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "NetBenefitAll never exceeds Prevalence and approaches it as the threshold approaches zero. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a threshold entered as a percentage." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Intervene-in-all net benefit not above the prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "intervene-in-all-net-benefit-not-above-the-prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=NetBenefitAll<=Prevalence+1E-12" .

hemo:7002477 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Intervening in all 100 patients at 15 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 26 admissions among 100 patients the net benefit of intervening in everyone at 15 per cent is about 0.1294, the same as model B, which classes everyone positive." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Intervening in all 100 patients at 15 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi = 0.26; p_t = 0.15; NB_all = 0.1294" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "intervening-in-all-100-patients-at-15-per-cent" .

hemo:7002478 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Intervening in all 100 patients at 40 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At 40 per cent the false positive weight is about 0.6667 and the net benefit of intervening in everyone is about minus 0.2333, as in the article's table." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Intervening in all 100 patients at 40 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi = 0.26; p_t = 0.4; NB_all = -0.2333" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "intervening-in-all-100-patients-at-40-per-cent" .

hemo:7002479 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Net benefit of removing the seminal vesicles in every man at 10 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Vickers and Elkin report that with 87 of 902 men having seminal vesicle invasion, intervening in all at 10 per cent gives minus 0.0039, below the model's 0.0443." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net benefit of removing the seminal vesicles in every man at 10 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi = 0.096452; p_t = 0.1; NB_all = -0.0039" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-benefit-of-removing-the-seminal-vesicles-in-every-man-at-10-per-cent" .

hemo:7002480 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Both net benefits computed at the same threshold in the same sample"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "NB_model and NB_all come from the same patients at the same p_t; mixing thresholds or samples breaks the conversion." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Both net benefits computed at the same threshold in the same sample" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "both-net-benefits-computed-at-the-same-threshold-in-the-same-sample" .

hemo:7002481 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Intervening in everyone is the reference practice"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The conversion answers how many unnecessary interventions the model would save against intervening in everyone; against intervening in no one the net benefit itself is the comparison." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Intervening in everyone is the reference practice" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "intervening-in-everyone-is-the-reference-practice" .

hemo:7002482 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Interventions avoided from named net benefits"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000500 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the two net benefits in NetBenefitModel and NetBenefitAll and the threshold in Threshold, the formula returns net interventions avoided per 100, held in AvoidedPer100." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Interventions avoided from named net benefits" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DCA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "interventions-avoided-from-named-net-benefits" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(NetBenefitModel-NetBenefitAll)*(1-Threshold)/Threshold*100" .

hemo:7002483 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Interventions avoided equal fewer false positives less weighted extra false negatives"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the reduction in false positives in FewerFalsePos, the extra missed cases in ExtraFalseNeg and the sample size in SampleSize, the avoided count per 100 equals (FewerFalsePos minus ExtraFalseNeg times (1 minus Threshold) / Threshold) / SampleSize times 100 (46 minus 4 x 5.667 for model A at 15 per cent). Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Interventions avoided equal fewer false positives less weighted extra false negatives" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "interventions-avoided-equal-fewer-false-positives-less-weighted-extra-false-negatives" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AvoidedPer100-(FewerFalsePos-ExtraFalseNeg*(1-Threshold)/Threshold)/SampleSize*100)<1E-6" .

hemo:7002484 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Model A against intervening in everyone at 15 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Model A's net benefit of 0.1706 against 0.1294 for everyone, times 0.85 / 0.15 and 100, gives about 23.3 interventions avoided per 100: 46 fewer unnecessary interventions less 4 missed admissions weighted by about 5.67 each." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Model A against intervening in everyone at 15 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "NB_model = 0.170588; NB_all = 0.129412; p_t = 0.15; avoided = 23.33" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "model-a-against-intervening-in-everyone-at-15-per-cent" .

hemo:7002485 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Model A against intervening in everyone at 40 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At 40 per cent model A avoids 67 unnecessary interventions and misses 13 extra admissions, each weighted 1.5, a net 47.5 per 100 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Model A against intervening in everyone at 40 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "NB_model = 0.083333; NB_all = -0.233333; p_t = 0.4; avoided = 47.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "model-a-against-intervening-in-everyone-at-40-per-cent" .

hemo:7002486 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Interventions avoided by the seminal vesicle model against removal in every man"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 0.0443 for the model and minus 0.0039 for intervening in all at 10 per cent, the model avoids about 43.5 unnecessary operations per 100 men net of missed cases: 590 fewer false positives less 22 extra false negatives times 9, over 902 men (computed here for illustration from Vickers and Elkin's counts, against 43 in their Table 2)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Interventions avoided by the seminal vesicle model against removal in every man" ;
    hemo:9000014 "NB_model = 0.044346; NB_all = -0.003942; p_t = 0.1; avoided = 43.46" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "interventions-avoided-by-the-seminal-vesicle-model-against-removal-in-every-man" .

hemo:7002487 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Threshold benefit and harm the same for every case and non-case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "G and L do not vary with predicted risk; Kerr and colleagues state this as an assumption embedded in decision curve net benefit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Threshold benefit and harm the same for every case and non-case" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "threshold-benefit-and-harm-the-same-for-every-case-and-non-case" .

hemo:7002488 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Threshold benefit and harm in a common unit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Only the ratio L / G matters, so both must be measured in the same unit; a ratio elicited directly (such as nine to one) can be used without either value." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Threshold benefit and harm in a common unit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCA-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "threshold-benefit-and-harm-in-a-common-unit" .

hemo:7002489 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Threshold probability from named benefit and harm"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000501 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the benefit to a case in BenefitCase and the harm to a non-case in HarmNonCase, the formula returns the threshold, held in ThresholdImplied." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Threshold probability from named benefit and harm" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DCA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "threshold-probability-from-named-benefit-and-harm" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=HarmNonCase/(BenefitCase+HarmNonCase)" .

hemo:7002490 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Threshold odds equal the harm to benefit ratio"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The odds of the implied threshold equal HarmNonCase / BenefitCase. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows benefit and harm swapped." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Threshold odds equal the harm to benefit ratio" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "threshold-odds-equal-the-harm-to-benefit-ratio" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ThresholdImplied/(1-ThresholdImplied)-HarmNonCase/BenefitCase)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002491 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Threshold benefit and harm entered as positive values"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both inputs must be above zero; a harm entered as a negative number gives a threshold outside the probability scale. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Threshold benefit and harm entered as positive values" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "threshold-benefit-and-harm-entered-as-positive-values" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(BenefitCase>0,HarmNonCase>0)" .

hemo:7002492 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Decision curve threshold for an admission-prevention programme valued by an economic model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If a decision model values reaching an admission-prone patient at 1,500 pounds and treating a patient unnecessarily at a loss of 500 pounds, the implied threshold is 500 / 2,000, or 25 per cent, as in the article's illustration." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Decision curve threshold for an admission-prevention programme valued by an economic model" ;
    hemo:9000014 "G = 1500; L = 500; p_t = 0.25" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "decision-curve-threshold-for-an-admission-prevention-programme-valued-by-an-economic-model" .

hemo:7002493 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Biopsy threshold when a missed high-grade cancer is nine times worse than an unnecessary biopsy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If missing a high-grade cancer is judged nine times worse than an unnecessary biopsy, so that at most 10 men would be biopsied to find one cancer, the threshold is 1 / 10, or 10 per cent." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Biopsy threshold when a missed high-grade cancer is nine times worse than an unnecessary biopsy" ;
    hemo:9000014 "G = 9; L = 1; p_t = 0.1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "biopsy-threshold-when-a-missed-high-grade-cancer-is-nine-times-worse-than-an-unnecessary-biopsy" .

hemo:7002494 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Classifications made at the threshold implied by G and L"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The equality V = G x NB holds when patients are classed at p_t = L / (G + L); at another threshold V still values the classifications but no longer matches the curve." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Classifications made at the threshold implied by G and L" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCA-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "classifications-made-at-the-threshold-implied-by-g-and-l" .

hemo:7002495 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Decision curve monetary values cover the whole pathway after classification"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "G and L include downstream costs and health effects valued at a stated cost-effectiveness threshold, and the cost of running the model is excluded unless added. A cost-effectiveness analysis relaxes these simplifications." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Decision curve monetary values cover the whole pathway after classification" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCA-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "decision-curve-monetary-values-cover-the-whole-pathway-after-classification" .

hemo:7002496 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Decision curve monetary gain per patient from named counts and values"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000502 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With BenefitCase, HarmNonCase, TruePos, FalsePos and SampleSize named, the formula returns the gain per patient, held in GainPerPatient." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Decision curve monetary gain per patient from named counts and values" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DCA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "decision-curve-monetary-gain-per-patient-from-named-counts-and-values" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=BenefitCase*TruePos/SampleSize-HarmNonCase*FalsePos/SampleSize" .

hemo:7002497 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Monetary gain equals the benefit per case times net benefit at the implied threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the net benefit at ThresholdImplied in NetBenefit, GainPerPatient equals BenefitCase times NetBenefit. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a threshold that does not match L / (G + L)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Monetary gain equals the benefit per case times net benefit at the implied threshold" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "monetary-gain-equals-the-benefit-per-case-times-net-benefit-at-the-implied-threshold" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(GainPerPatient-BenefitCase*NetBenefit)<1E-6" .

hemo:7002498 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Model A at the implied 25 per cent threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 1,500 pounds per admission-prone patient reached and 500 pounds lost per unnecessary intervention, model A's 22 true and 28 false positives per 100 are worth 190 pounds per patient, matching 1,500 times its net benefit of 0.1267." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Model A at the implied 25 per cent threshold" ;
    hemo:9000014 "G = 1500; L = 500; TP = 22; FP = 28; n = 100; V = 190" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "model-a-at-the-implied-25-per-cent-threshold" .

hemo:7002499 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Intervening in everyone at the implied 25 per cent threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Intervening in all 100 patients gives 26 true and 74 false positives and is worth 20 pounds per patient, matching 1,500 times 0.0133." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Intervening in everyone at the implied 25 per cent threshold" ;
    hemo:9000014 "G = 1500; L = 500; TP = 26; FP = 74; n = 100; V = 20" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCA-013" ;
    hemo:9000023 "intervening-in-everyone-at-the-implied-25-per-cent-threshold" .

hemo:7002500 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Prevalence-based YLD without age weighting or discounting"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Since GBD 2010, YLDs are prevalence times disability weight with no age weighting or discounting; the GBD 1990 incidence-based form with a 3 per cent discount rate and age weights gives different numbers." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prevalence-based YLD without age weighting or discounting" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prevalence-based-yld-without-age-weighting-or-discounting" .

hemo:7002501 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One named weight set for every sequela"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "All weights come from one set (for example GBD 2013), because revised health-state descriptions moved some weights sharply between rounds." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One named weight set for every sequela" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-named-weight-set-for-every-sequela" .

hemo:7002502 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Years lived with disability from named cases and weight"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000503 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With prevalent cases in PrevalentCases and the weight in DisabilityWeight, the formula returns the YLDs, held in YLDCondition. For several sequelae in columns, =SUMPRODUCT(CasesRange,WeightRange) adds them before any comorbidity adjustment." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Years lived with disability from named cases and weight" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DWT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "years-lived-with-disability-from-named-cases-and-weight" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PrevalentCases*DisabilityWeight" .

hemo:7002503 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Disability weight on the 0 to 1 scale and YLD not above person-years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weight is at least 0 and at most 1, so YLDCondition cannot exceed PrevalentCases. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a utility value (1 for full health) entered in place of a disability weight, or a weight in per cent." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Disability weight on the 0 to 1 scale and YLD not above person-years" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "disability-weight-on-the-0-to-1-scale-and-yld-not-above-person-years" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(DisabilityWeight>=0,DisabilityWeight<=1,YLDCondition<=PrevalentCases)" .

hemo:7002504 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Condition A affecting 1,000 people with a weight of 0.10"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7006645,
        hemo:7006646 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7006647 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative population, 1,000 people with condition A at a weight of 0.10 give 100 YLDs, before any adjustment for comorbidity." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Condition A affecting 1,000 people with a weight of 0.10" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P = 1000; DW = 0.1; YLD = 100" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "condition-a-affecting-1-000-people-with-a-weight-of-0-10" .

hemo:7002505 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Condition B affecting 500 people with a weight of 0.30"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7006648,
        hemo:7006649 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7006650 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Five hundred people with condition B at 0.30 give 150 YLDs; with condition A the unadjusted total is 250." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Condition B affecting 500 people with a weight of 0.30" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P = 500; DW = 0.3; YLD = 150" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "condition-b-affecting-500-people-with-a-weight-of-0-30" .

hemo:7002506 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Complete hearing loss under the GBD 2010 and GBD 2013 weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7006651,
        hemo:7006652 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7006653 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For 1,000 people with complete hearing loss, the GBD 2010 weight of 0.033 gives 33 YLDs and the revised GBD 2013 weight of 0.215 gives 215 (computed here for illustration), so the weight set alone changes the burden more than sixfold." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Complete hearing loss under the GBD 2010 and GBD 2013 weights" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P = 1000; DW = 0.215; YLD = 215" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "complete-hearing-loss-under-the-gbd-2010-and-gbd-2013-weights" .

hemo:7002507 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Multiplicative combination of disability weights for comorbid health loss"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each condition removes the same proportion of the health left by the other. Vos and colleagues report that tests on real data suggested the multiplicative model was the most appropriate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Multiplicative combination of disability weights for comorbid health loss" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "multiplicative-combination-of-disability-weights-for-comorbid-health-loss" .

hemo:7002508 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weights from the same set and on the same scale"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both stand-alone weights come from one weight set and are at least 0 and at most 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weights from the same set and on the same scale" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weights-from-the-same-set-and-on-the-same-scale" .

hemo:7002509 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Combined disability weight from two named weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000504 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the stand-alone weights in WeightOne and WeightTwo, the formula returns the combined weight, held in CombinedWeight. For several weights in a range, =1-PRODUCT(1-WeightRange) entered as an array formula gives the same rule." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Combined disability weight from two named weights" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DWT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "combined-disability-weight-from-two-named-weights" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1-(1-WeightOne)*(1-WeightTwo)" .

hemo:7002510 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Combined weight not below the larger weight and not above the sum"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The combined weight is at least the larger stand-alone weight and at most their sum, and never above 1. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Combined weight not below the larger weight and not above the sum" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "combined-weight-not-below-the-larger-weight-and-not-above-the-sum" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(CombinedWeight>=MAX(WeightOne,WeightTwo),CombinedWeight<=WeightOne+WeightTwo,CombinedWeight<=1)" .

hemo:7002511 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Combined disability weight for conditions A and B"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A person with condition A (0.10) and condition B (0.30) has a combined weight of 1 minus 0.90 x 0.70, or 0.37, below the 0.40 that addition would give." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Combined disability weight for conditions A and B" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DW_1 = 0.1; DW_2 = 0.3; DW_12 = 0.37" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "combined-disability-weight-for-conditions-a-and-b" .

hemo:7002512 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Combined disability weight for two mild conditions"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Two conditions of weight 0.05 each combine to 0.0975, close to their sum of 0.10 because mild weights barely overlap (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Combined disability weight for two mild conditions" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DW_1 = 0.05; DW_2 = 0.05; DW_12 = 0.0975" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "combined-disability-weight-for-two-mild-conditions" .

hemo:7002513 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Combined disability weight for a severe and a moderate condition"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Weights of 0.71 and 0.30 combine to 0.797, where addition would give 1.01, more than death (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Combined disability weight for a severe and a moderate condition" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DW_1 = 0.71; DW_2 = 0.3; DW_12 = 0.797" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "combined-disability-weight-for-a-severe-and-a-moderate-condition" .

hemo:7002514 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Apportioning in proportion to stand-alone weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "GBD 2010 apportioned the combined weight to each contributing sequela in proportion to its weight on its own; other sharing rules give other cause-specific totals with the same overall total." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Apportioning in proportion to stand-alone weights" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "apportioning-in-proportion-to-stand-alone-weights" .

hemo:7002515 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Attributed share of a combined weight from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000505 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With CombinedWeight, the condition's own weight in OwnWeight and the two stand-alone weights in WeightOne and WeightTwo, the formula returns the attributed share, held in AttributedWeight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Attributed share of a combined weight from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DWT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "attributed-share-of-a-combined-weight-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CombinedWeight*OwnWeight/(WeightOne+WeightTwo)" .

hemo:7002516 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Attributed shares add to the combined weight"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "AttributedWeight plus the share attributed to the other condition equals CombinedWeight (0.0925 plus 0.2775 is 0.37). Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Attributed shares add to the combined weight" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "attributed-shares-add-to-the-combined-weight" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AttributedWeight+CombinedWeight*(WeightOne+WeightTwo-OwnWeight)/(WeightOne+WeightTwo)-CombinedWeight)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002517 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Condition A's share of the combined weight of 0.37"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Condition A's share is 0.37 x 0.10 / 0.40, or 0.0925, so its 50 comorbid cases add 4.625 YLDs to the 95 from people with A only, 99.625 in all, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Condition A's share of the combined weight of 0.37" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DW_12 = 0.37; DW_j = 0.1; DW_1 = 0.1; DW_2 = 0.3; DW_j_star = 0.0925" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "condition-a-s-share-of-the-combined-weight-of-0-37" .

hemo:7002518 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Condition B's share of the combined weight of 0.37"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Condition B's share is 0.37 x 0.30 / 0.40, or 0.2775; with 135 YLDs from people with B only, its YLDs are 148.875 and, with 80 years of life lost, its DALYs 228.875, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Condition B's share of the combined weight of 0.37" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DW_12 = 0.37; DW_j = 0.3; DW_1 = 0.1; DW_2 = 0.3; DW_j_star = 0.2775" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "condition-b-s-share-of-the-combined-weight-of-0-37" .

hemo:7002519 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Conditions occur independently within the age-sex group for comorbidity-adjusted YLDs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The chance of having both is the product of the two prevalences, as GBD 2010 assumed within each age, sex, country and year; dependent comorbidity needs data on joint prevalence." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Conditions occur independently within the age-sex group for comorbidity-adjusted YLDs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "conditions-occur-independently-within-the-age-sex-group-for-comorbidity-adjusted-ylds" .

hemo:7002520 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Multiplicative weights for co-occurring conditions"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "People with both conditions carry the combined weight of HE-FM-DWT-002." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Multiplicative weights for co-occurring conditions" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "multiplicative-weights-for-co-occurring-conditions" .

hemo:7002521 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Comorbidity-adjusted YLD rate and total from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000506 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With prevalences PrevOne and PrevTwo, weights WeightOne and WeightTwo and the population in Population, the formula returns total adjusted YLDs, held in AdjustedYLD." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Comorbidity-adjusted YLD rate and total from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DWT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "comorbidity-adjusted-yld-rate-and-total-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Population*(1-(1-PrevOne*WeightOne)*(1-PrevTwo*WeightTwo))" .

hemo:7002522 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Adjusted YLDs equal the count over people with one or both conditions"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With independence, comorbid cases are Population x PrevOne x PrevTwo; YLDs from people with one condition only plus comorbid cases at the combined weight equal AdjustedYLD (95 plus 135 plus 18.5 in the example). Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Adjusted YLDs equal the count over people with one or both conditions" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "adjusted-ylds-equal-the-count-over-people-with-one-or-both-conditions" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(Population*(PrevOne*(1-PrevTwo)*WeightOne+PrevTwo*(1-PrevOne)*WeightTwo+PrevOne*PrevTwo*(1-(1-WeightOne)*(1-WeightTwo)))-AdjustedYLD)<1E-6" .

hemo:7002523 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Adjusted YLDs not above the unadjusted sum"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Adjustment can only reduce the total. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Adjusted YLDs not above the unadjusted sum" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "adjusted-ylds-not-above-the-unadjusted-sum" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AdjustedYLD<=Population*(PrevOne*WeightOne+PrevTwo*WeightTwo)+1E-9" .

hemo:7002524 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Comorbidity-adjusted YLDs for conditions A and B in a population of 10,000"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Condition A has prevalence 0.10 and weight 0.10 (rate 0.01) and condition B prevalence 0.05 and weight 0.30 (rate 0.015). The adjusted rate is 1 minus 0.99 x 0.985, or 0.02485, which is 248.5 YLDs in 10,000 people, matching the article's count of 95 plus 135 plus 18.5." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Comorbidity-adjusted YLDs for conditions A and B in a population of 10,000" ;
    hemo:9000014 "y_1 = 0.01; y_2 = 0.015; y_12 = 0.02485" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "comorbidity-adjusted-ylds-for-conditions-a-and-b-in-a-population-of-10-000" .

hemo:7002525 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Comorbidity-adjusted YLDs for two rare mild conditions"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With rates of 0.002 and 0.001 the adjusted rate is 0.002998, almost exactly the sum, because comorbid cases are rare (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Comorbidity-adjusted YLDs for two rare mild conditions" ;
    hemo:9000014 "y_1 = 0.002; y_2 = 0.001; y_12 = 0.002998" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "comorbidity-adjusted-ylds-for-two-rare-mild-conditions" .

hemo:7002526 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Intervention changes non-fatal health only when counting DALYs averted"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Mortality is unchanged, so years of life lost are untouched and only the YLD term changes; WHO-CHOICE population models allow an intervention to change the disability weight as one of its rates." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Intervention changes non-fatal health only when counting DALYs averted" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWT-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "intervention-changes-non-fatal-health-only-when-counting-dalys-averted" .

hemo:7002527 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weights from one set with the multiplicative rule for comorbid people"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Before and after weights for comorbid people are combined weights (HE-FM-DWT-002) from the same weight set as the stand-alone weights." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weights from one set with the multiplicative rule for comorbid people" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWT-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weights-from-one-set-with-the-multiplicative-rule-for-comorbid-people" .

hemo:7002528 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "DALYs averted from named group sizes and weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000507 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With GroupOneN, GroupOnePre, GroupOnePost, GroupTwoN, GroupTwoPre and GroupTwoPost named, the formula returns DALYs averted, held in DALYsAverted; cost per DALY averted is =ProgrammeCost/DALYsAverted." ;
    hemo:9000009 "DALYs averted from named group sizes and weights" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DWT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "dalys-averted-from-named-group-sizes-and-weights" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=GroupOneN*(GroupOnePre-GroupOnePost)+GroupTwoN*(GroupTwoPre-GroupTwoPost)" .

hemo:7002529 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Comorbid gain equals the combined weight less the remaining weight"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the stand-alone weight of the condition that remains in OtherWeight and of the relieved condition in TargetWeight, for the second group GroupTwoPre minus GroupTwoPost equals 1 minus (1 minus OtherWeight) x (1 minus TargetWeight) minus OtherWeight (0.37 minus 0.10, or 0.27). Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Comorbid gain equals the combined weight less the remaining weight" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "comorbid-gain-equals-the-combined-weight-less-the-remaining-weight" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((GroupTwoPre-GroupTwoPost)-((1-(1-OtherWeight)*(1-TargetWeight))-OtherWeight))<1E-12" .

hemo:7002530 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Comorbid gain not above the stand-alone weight"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the stand-alone weight of the relieved condition in TargetWeight, relieving it in someone who keeps the condition in OtherWeight cannot gain more than TargetWeight. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Comorbid gain not above the stand-alone weight" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "comorbid-gain-not-above-the-stand-alone-weight" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=GroupTwoPre-GroupTwoPost<=TargetWeight+1E-12" .

hemo:7002531 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "DALYs averted by relieving condition B in 100 people with B only and 10 who also have A"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Health loss falls from 0.30 to zero in the first group and from 0.37 to 0.10 in the second: 30 plus 2.7 gives 32.7 DALYs averted. At a cost of 16,350 international dollars the programme costs 500 per DALY averted, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "DALYs averted by relieving condition B in 100 people with B only and 10 who also have A" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_1 = 100; w_1_pre = 0.3; w_1_post = 0; n_2 = 10; w_2_pre = 0.37; w_2_post = 0.1; DALY_av = 32.7" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "dalys-averted-by-relieving-condition-b-in-100-people-with-b-only-and-10-who-also-have-a" .

hemo:7002532 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "DALYs averted with the comorbidity overlap ignored"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Crediting all 110 people with the stand-alone weight of 0.30 gives 33.0 DALYs averted, overstating the gain; the error grows with the share of treated people who have both conditions." ;
    hemo:9000009 "DALYs averted with the comorbidity overlap ignored" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_1 = 110; w_1_pre = 0.3; w_1_post = 0; n_2 = 0; w_2_pre = 0.37; w_2_post = 0.1; DALY_av = 33" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "dalys-averted-with-the-comorbidity-overlap-ignored" .

hemo:7002533 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Person trade-off judgements of equal claim on resources"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The respondent compares life extensions for two groups and states the size at which they have an equal claim; the weight follows from the ratio alone." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Person trade-off judgements of equal claim on resources" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWT-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "person-trade-off-judgements-of-equal-claim-on-resources" .

hemo:7002534 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "First person trade-off weight from named numbers"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000508 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the reference group in RefPeople and the equivalent group in EquivPeople, the formula returns the weight, held in PTOOneWeight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "First person trade-off weight from named numbers" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DWT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "first-person-trade-off-weight-from-named-numbers" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1-RefPeople/EquivPeople" .

hemo:7002535 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "First person trade-off equivalent group at least as large as the reference"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "EquivPeople must be at least RefPeople for a weight of 0 or more. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the two numbers swapped." ;
    hemo:9000009 "First person trade-off equivalent group at least as large as the reference" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWT-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "first-person-trade-off-equivalent-group-at-least-as-large-as-the-reference" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(EquivPeople>=RefPeople,PTOOneWeight>=0,PTOOneWeight<1)" .

hemo:7002536 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "GBD 1990 example of 8,000 people with a severe disability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If 1,000 healthy people have an equal claim to 8,000 people with a severe disability, the weight is 1 minus 1,000 / 8,000, or 0.875." ;
    hemo:9000009 "GBD 1990 example of 8,000 people with a severe disability" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_ref = 1000; N_eq = 8000; DW = 0.875" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-013" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gbd-1990-example-of-8-000-people-with-a-severe-disability" .

hemo:7002537 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "First person trade-off disability weight from an equivalence of 1,250 people"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If 1,250 people with a condition are judged equal to 1,000 healthy people, the weight is 0.2 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "First person trade-off disability weight from an equivalence of 1,250 people" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_ref = 1000; N_eq = 1250; DW = 0.2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-014" ;
    hemo:9000023 "first-person-trade-off-disability-weight-from-an-equivalence-of-1-250-people" .

hemo:7002538 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Cure removes the whole disability weight in the second person trade-off"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A cure returns a person to full health for the period valued, so the health gained per cure equals the weight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cure removes the whole disability weight in the second person trade-off" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DWT-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cure-removes-the-whole-disability-weight-in-the-second-person-trade-off" .

hemo:7002539 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Second person trade-off weight from named numbers"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000509 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With LivesProlonged and CuresEquivalent named, the formula returns the weight, held in PTOTwoWeight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Second person trade-off weight from named numbers" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DWT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "second-person-trade-off-weight-from-named-numbers" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LivesProlonged/CuresEquivalent" .

hemo:7002540 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Second person trade-off cures at least as many as lives prolonged"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "CuresEquivalent must be at least LivesProlonged for a weight not above 1. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Second person trade-off cures at least as many as lives prolonged" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DWT-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "second-person-trade-off-cures-at-least-as-many-as-lives-prolonged" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(CuresEquivalent>=LivesProlonged,PTOTwoWeight>0,PTOTwoWeight<=1)" .

hemo:7002541 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "GBD 1990 person trade-off example of 5,000 cures of blindness"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If 5,000 cures of blindness are judged equal to prolonging the lives of 1,000 people, the weight is 1,000 / 5,000, or 0.2." ;
    hemo:9000009 "GBD 1990 person trade-off example of 5,000 cures of blindness" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_life = 1000; N_cure = 5000; DW = 0.2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-015" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gbd-1990-person-trade-off-example-of-5-000-cures-of-blindness" .

hemo:7002542 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Second person trade-off disability weight for a condition judged half as bad as death"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If 2,000 cures are judged equal to 1,000 lives prolonged, the weight is 0.5 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Second person trade-off disability weight for a condition judged half as bad as death" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_life = 1000; N_cure = 2000; DW = 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DWT-016" ;
    hemo:9000023 "second-person-trade-off-disability-weight-for-a-condition-judged-half-as-bad-as-death" .

hemo:7002543 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Quantitative clustering variables on comparable scales"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both variables are quantitative and on similar ranges, as with the two counts in the article's example; otherwise the variable with the larger variance dominates the distance." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Quantitative clustering variables on comparable scales" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CLU-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "quantitative-clustering-variables-on-comparable-scales" .

hemo:7002544 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Clustering variables chosen on subject-matter grounds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The variables define what similar means: segmenting on care use and segmenting on diagnoses group the same patients differently, so the choice is stated before any algorithm is run." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Clustering variables chosen on subject-matter grounds" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CLU-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "clustering-variables-chosen-on-subject-matter-grounds" .

hemo:7002545 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Squared distance between two patient profiles from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000510 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the two units' values in EdI, EdJ, OpI and OpJ, the formula returns the squared distance, held in SqDistance. For p variables held in two equal-length ranges ProfileI and ProfileJ, =SUMXMY2(ProfileI,ProfileJ) gives the same sum." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Squared distance between two patient profiles from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CLU-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "squared-distance-between-two-patient-profiles-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(EdI-EdJ)^2+(OpI-OpJ)^2" .

hemo:7002546 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Squared distance matches SUMXMY2 on the two profile ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "SqDistance equals the built-in sum of squared differences over the ranges ProfileI (EdI and OpI) and ProfileJ (EdJ and OpJ). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a missing square or a variable left out." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Squared distance matches SUMXMY2 on the two profile ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CLU-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "squared-distance-matches-sumxmy2-on-the-two-profile-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SqDistance-SUMXMY2(ProfileI,ProfileJ))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002547 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Squared distance zero only for identical profiles"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "SqDistance is 0 exactly when the two units have the same value on both variables. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows differences added without squaring, which can cancel." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Squared distance zero only for identical profiles" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CLU-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "squared-distance-zero-only-for-identical-profiles" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(SqDistance=0)=AND(EdI=EdJ,OpI=OpJ)" .

hemo:7002548 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient P2 against patient P3 in the six-patient example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "P2 has 1 emergency attendance and 2 outpatient appointments and P3 has 2 and 0, so the squared distance is 1 plus 4, which is 5, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient P2 against patient P3 in the six-patient example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "x_i1 = 1; x_j1 = 2; x_i2 = 2; x_j2 = 0; d_ij = 5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-p2-against-patient-p3-in-the-six-patient-example" .

hemo:7002549 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient P2 against patient P4 in the six-patient example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "P4 has 5 attendances and 4 appointments, so the squared distance from P2 is 16 plus 4, which is 20; P2 is nearer P3 and joins its cluster." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient P2 against patient P4 in the six-patient example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "x_i1 = 1; x_j1 = 5; x_i2 = 2; x_j2 = 4; d_ij = 20" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-p2-against-patient-p4-in-the-six-patient-example" .

hemo:7002550 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient P2 against the converged mean of cluster A"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "After the first update the mean of cluster A is (1, 1), so P2 at (1, 2) is at squared distance 1 from it, against 25 from the cluster B mean (5, 5), and stays in A." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient P2 against the converged mean of cluster A" ;
    hemo:9000014 "x_i1 = 1; x_j1 = 1; x_i2 = 2; x_j2 = 1; d_ij = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-p2-against-the-converged-mean-of-cluster-a" .

hemo:7002551 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weights chosen for the purpose of the segmentation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Equal influence is not always right: standardising can obscure groups that only some variables separate, so the weights are a stated analyst choice." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weights chosen for the purpose of the segmentation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CLU-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weights-chosen-for-the-purpose-of-the-segmentation" .

hemo:7002552 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Standardising weights computed on the clustered sample"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Inverse-variance weights use the variance of each variable in the units being clustered; weights from another sample give a different balance." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standardising weights computed on the clustered sample" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CLU-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standardising-weights-computed-on-the-clustered-sample" .

hemo:7002553 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted squared distance from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000511 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With weights in WeightOne and WeightTwo and values in VarOneI, VarOneJ, VarTwoI and VarTwoJ, the formula returns the weighted distance, held in WeightedDistance. A standardising weight is =1/VAR.S(range) over the variable's values; for p variables, =SUMPRODUCT(Weights,(ProfileI-ProfileJ)^2) gives the same result." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted squared distance from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CLU-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-squared-distance-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=WeightOne*(VarOneI-VarOneJ)^2+WeightTwo*(VarTwoI-VarTwoJ)^2" .

hemo:7002554 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted distance matches the SUMPRODUCT form"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "WeightedDistance equals SUMPRODUCT of the weights range Weights and the squared differences of ProfileI and ProfileJ. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a weight applied to the wrong variable." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted distance matches the SUMPRODUCT form" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CLU-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-distance-matches-the-sumproduct-form" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(WeightedDistance-SUMPRODUCT(Weights,(ProfileI-ProfileJ)^2))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002555 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weights not negative and weighted distance not negative"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both weights are zero or above, so the weighted distance is too. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a negative weight or a sign error." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weights not negative and weighted distance not negative" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CLU-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weights-not-negative-and-weighted-distance-not-negative" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(WeightOne>=0,WeightTwo>=0,WeightedDistance>=0)" .

hemo:7002556 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patients P1 and P5 on emergency attendances and cost without weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With weights of 1, the squared difference of 36 in attendances is lost against the squared cost difference of 51,840,000 pounds squared, giving 51,840,036 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patients P1 and P5 on emergency attendances and cost without weights" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_1 = 1; x_i1 = 0; x_j1 = 6; w_2 = 1; x_i2 = 400; x_j2 = 7600; D_ij = 51840036" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patients-p1-and-p5-on-emergency-attendances-and-cost-without-weights" .

hemo:7002557 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patients P1 and P5 with standardising weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the six patients the sample variance is 5.6 for attendances and 10,359,000 for cost; weights of 1 / 5.6 and 1 / 10,359,000 give 6.4286 plus 5.0043, about 11.4329, so both variables now count (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patients P1 and P5 with standardising weights" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_1 = 0.178571; x_i1 = 0; x_j1 = 6; w_2 = 0.0000000965344; x_i2 = 400; x_j2 = 7600; D_ij = 11.4329" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patients-p1-and-p5-with-standardising-weights" .

hemo:7002558 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Within-cluster sum of squares from the best of several k-means starts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "K-means can stop at a local minimum that depends on the starting centroids, so W_K is taken from several starts or, for tiny data, an exhaustive search." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Within-cluster sum of squares from the best of several k-means starts" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CLU-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "within-cluster-sum-of-squares-from-the-best-of-several-k-means-starts" .

hemo:7002559 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same units, variables and scaling for every number of clusters"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "W_K and W_1 are computed on the same data and weights; changing variables or scaling between solutions makes the shares incomparable." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same units, variables and scaling for every number of clusters" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CLU-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-units-variables-and-scaling-for-every-number-of-clusters" .

hemo:7002560 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Share of scatter removed from named sums of squares"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000512 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With W_K in WithinSS and W_1 in TotalSS, the formula returns the share removed, held in ScatterRemoved. For two variables in ranges EdValues and OpValues, W_1 is =DEVSQ(EdValues)+DEVSQ(OpValues)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Share of scatter removed from named sums of squares" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CLU-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "share-of-scatter-removed-from-named-sums-of-squares" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1-WithinSS/TotalSS" .

hemo:7002561 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Share removed uses the total scatter about the overall mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "ScatterRemoved equals 1 minus WithinSS divided by DEVSQ of each clustering variable added together, which is W_1, the one-cluster sum of squares. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows W_1 summed by hand with an error or about the wrong mean." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Share removed uses the total scatter about the overall mean" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CLU-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "share-removed-uses-the-total-scatter-about-the-overall-mean" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ScatterRemoved-(1-WithinSS/(DEVSQ(EdValues)+DEVSQ(OpValues))))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002562 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Within-cluster sum of squares does not rise when a cluster is added"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the best solutions for two and three clusters in WithinSSTwo and WithinSSThree, the three-cluster value is no larger and ScatterRemoved is zero or above. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a local minimum or a different scaling between the runs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Within-cluster sum of squares does not rise when a cluster is added" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CLU-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "within-cluster-sum-of-squares-does-not-rise-when-a-cluster-is-added" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(WithinSSThree<=WithinSSTwo,ScatterRemoved>=0)" .

hemo:7002563 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two clusters of the six patients"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With one cluster the mean is (3, 3) and W(1) is 56; the two clusters with means (1, 1) and (5, 5) give W(2) of 8, removing 48 of the 56 units of scatter, a share of about 0.8571 (86 per cent), as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two clusters of the six patients" ;
    hemo:9000014 "W_K = 8; W_1 = 56; R_K = 0.8571" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-clusters-of-the-six-patients" .

hemo:7002564 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Best three-cluster split of the six patients"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The best three-cluster splits give W(3) of 5, a share of about 0.9107; the further gain of 3 units, about 5 per cent of the total, is small, so the kink is at two clusters, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Best three-cluster split of the six patients" ;
    hemo:9000014 "W_K = 5; W_1 = 56; R_K = 0.9107" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "best-three-cluster-split-of-the-six-patients" .

hemo:7002565 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three clusters stuck at a local minimum"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Starting k-means for three clusters from P1, P2 and P4 converges to clusters {P1, P3}, {P2} and {P4, P5, P6} with W(3) of 6.5 and a share of about 0.8839, worse than the best split's 5 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three clusters stuck at a local minimum" ;
    hemo:9000014 "W_K = 6.5; W_1 = 56; R_K = 0.8839" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-clusters-stuck-at-a-local-minimum" .

hemo:7002566 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Class shares and class distributions taken from the fitted mixture model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "pi_k and f_k come from a mixture model fitted by maximum likelihood or Bayesian methods, with the shares adding to 1; the posterior inherits their estimation uncertainty." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Class shares and class distributions taken from the fitted mixture model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CLU-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "class-shares-and-class-distributions-taken-from-the-fitted-mixture-model" .

hemo:7002567 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Each unit belongs to exactly one latent class"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The classes are mutually exclusive and exhaustive, so the posterior probabilities for a unit add to 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Each unit belongs to exactly one latent class" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CLU-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "each-unit-belongs-to-exactly-one-latent-class" .

hemo:7002568 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior class probability from named shares and likelihoods"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000513 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With ShareOne, DensOne, ShareTwo and DensTwo named, the formula returns the posterior probability of class 1, held in PostOne. For K classes in ranges Shares and Dens, =INDEX(Shares,1)*INDEX(Dens,1)/SUMPRODUCT(Shares,Dens) gives class 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Posterior class probability from named shares and likelihoods" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CLU-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "posterior-class-probability-from-named-shares-and-likelihoods" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ShareOne*DensOne/(ShareOne*DensOne+ShareTwo*DensTwo)" .

hemo:7002569 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior odds equal prior odds times the likelihood ratio"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "PostOne / (1 minus PostOne) equals ShareOne / ShareTwo times DensOne / DensTwo. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a share or likelihood attached to the wrong class." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Posterior odds equal prior odds times the likelihood ratio" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CLU-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "posterior-odds-equal-prior-odds-times-the-likelihood-ratio" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PostOne/(1-PostOne)-(ShareOne/ShareTwo)*(DensOne/DensTwo))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002570 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Class shares add to one and the posterior is a probability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "ShareOne plus ShareTwo is 1, and PostOne is at least 0 and at most 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows shares entered as percentages or not adding up." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Class shares add to one and the posterior is a probability" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CLU-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "class-shares-add-to-one-and-the-posterior-is-a-probability" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS(ShareOne+ShareTwo-1)<1E-9,PostOne>=0,PostOne<=1)" .

hemo:7002571 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient with 3 emergency attendances and a high-use class of 20 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If attendances follow a Poisson distribution with mean 5 in a high-use class holding 20 per cent of patients and mean 1 in a low-use class, 3 attendances have likelihoods of about 0.1404 and 0.0613; the posterior probability of the high-use class is about 0.364 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient with 3 emergency attendances and a high-use class of 20 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi_1 = 0.2; f_1 = 0.140374; pi_2 = 0.8; f_2 = 0.061313; post_1 = 0.364" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-with-3-emergency-attendances-and-a-high-use-class-of-20-per-cent" .

hemo:7002572 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient with 6 emergency attendances in the same two-class model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 6 attendances the likelihoods are about 0.1462 and 0.0005, so the posterior probability of the high-use class is about 0.9862 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient with 6 emergency attendances in the same two-class model" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi_1 = 0.2; f_1 = 0.146223; pi_2 = 0.8; f_2 = 0.000511; post_1 = 0.9862" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-with-6-emergency-attendances-in-the-same-two-class-model" .

hemo:7002573 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient with 1 emergency attendance in the same two-class model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 1 attendance the likelihoods are about 0.0337 and 0.3679, giving a high-use probability of about 0.0224 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient with 1 emergency attendance in the same two-class model" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi_1 = 0.2; f_1 = 0.03369; pi_2 = 0.8; f_2 = 0.367879; post_1 = 0.0224" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-with-1-emergency-attendance-in-the-same-two-class-model" .

hemo:7002574 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Silhouette distances measured as in the clustering"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "a_i and b_i use ordinary Euclidean distances on the same scaled variables as the clustering; the unit's cluster has at least one other member." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Silhouette distances measured as in the clustering" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CLU-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "silhouette-distances-measured-as-in-the-clustering" .

hemo:7002575 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Nearest other cluster chosen by mean distance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "With more than two clusters, b_i is the smallest of the mean distances to each other cluster." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Nearest other cluster chosen by mean distance" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CLU-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "nearest-other-cluster-chosen-by-mean-distance" .

hemo:7002576 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Silhouette from named mean distances"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000514 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the mean distances in MeanOwn and MeanOther, the formula returns the silhouette, held in Silhouette; =AVERAGE over the column of silhouettes gives the mean for the solution." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Silhouette from named mean distances" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CLU-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "silhouette-from-named-mean-distances" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(MeanOther-MeanOwn)/MAX(MeanOwn,MeanOther)" .

hemo:7002577 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Silhouette matches its two-branch form"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The silhouette equals 1 minus a_i / b_i (MeanOwn / MeanOther) when b_i exceeds a_i, and b_i / a_i minus 1 otherwise. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows MIN used in place of MAX." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Silhouette matches its two-branch form" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CLU-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "silhouette-matches-its-two-branch-form" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(Silhouette-IF(MeanOther>MeanOwn,1-MeanOwn/MeanOther,MeanOther/MeanOwn-1))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002578 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Silhouette sign follows which cluster is nearer"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The silhouette is positive when the unit is nearer its own cluster on average and negative when it is nearer another. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Silhouette sign follows which cluster is nearer" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CLU-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "silhouette-sign-follows-which-cluster-is-nearer" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SIGN(Silhouette)=SIGN(MeanOther-MeanOwn)" .

hemo:7002579 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Silhouette of patient P2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "P2's distances are 1.414 and 2.236 to P1 and P3, mean 1.825, and 4.472, 6.403 and 4.243 to cluster B, mean 5.039, so s is 3.214 / 5.039, about 0.6378 (0.638 in the article)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Silhouette of patient P2" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_i = 1.8251; b_i = 5.0393; s_i = 0.6378" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "silhouette-of-patient-p2" .

hemo:7002580 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Silhouette of patient P1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "P1's mean distance to P2 and P3 is 1.825 and to cluster B 6.433, giving about 0.7163, the highest of the six (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Silhouette of patient P1" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_i = 1.8251; b_i = 6.4327; s_i = 0.7163" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-013" ;
    hemo:9000023 "silhouette-of-patient-p1" .

hemo:7002581 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Unit closer to another cluster than its own"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A unit with a mean distance of 3 to its own cluster and 2 to the nearest other cluster has a silhouette of minus 1 / 3, about minus 0.3333, a sign that it is misallocated (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Unit closer to another cluster than its own" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_i = 3; b_i = 2; s_i = -0.3333" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CLU-014" ;
    hemo:9000023 "unit-closer-to-another-cluster-than-its-own" .

hemo:7002582 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Ratings treated as an interval scale in a ratings-based conjoint study"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Differences between ratings mean the same anywhere on the scale, which justifies least-squares estimation; with only ordinal judgements a nonmetric method is used instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ratings treated as an interval scale in a ratings-based conjoint study" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CJA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ratings-treated-as-an-interval-scale-in-a-ratings-based-conjoint-study" .

hemo:7002583 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Balanced orthogonal design for the mean-difference part-worth"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Levels and pairs of levels appear equally often, as in the eight-profile full factorial or an orthogonal fraction, so the attribute codes are uncorrelated and each mean difference equals the regression coefficient." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Balanced orthogonal design for the mean-difference part-worth" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CJA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "balanced-orthogonal-design-for-the-mean-difference-part-worth" .

hemo:7002584 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Additive part-worths without interactions"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The trade-off between two attributes does not depend on the levels of the others (preferential independence); a main-effects design assumes this and cannot estimate interactions." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Additive part-worths without interactions" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CJA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "additive-part-worths-without-interactions" .

hemo:7002585 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Part-worth from mean ratings with AVERAGEIF"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000515 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the ratings in Ratings and the attribute's 0 and 1 codes in WaitCode, the formula returns the part-worth, held in PartWorthWait; the same formula on LocalCode and NurseCode gives PartWorthLocal and PartWorthNurse, and the intercept, held in Intercept, is the predicted rating of the reference profile, =INDEX(LINEST(Ratings,AttributeCodes),1,4), the last value LINEST returns; it is not that profile's observed rating, which equals it here only by chance. =LINEST(Ratings,AttributeCodes) fits all attributes at once and returns the coefficients in reverse column order, intercept last." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Part-worth from mean ratings with AVERAGEIF" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CJA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "part-worth-from-mean-ratings-with-averageif" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AVERAGEIF(WaitCode,1,Ratings)-AVERAGEIF(WaitCode,0,Ratings)" .

hemo:7002586 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mean-difference location part-worth equals the least-squares coefficient"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the codes for waiting time, location and lead in the three columns of AttributeCodes, PartWorthLocal equals the location coefficient, the second value returned by LINEST. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an unbalanced design, where the shortcut fails (2.00 against 1.25 with profile 8 dropped)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mean-difference location part-worth equals the least-squares coefficient" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CJA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mean-difference-location-part-worth-equals-the-least-squares-coefficient" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PartWorthLocal-INDEX(LINEST(Ratings,AttributeCodes),1,2))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002587 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Part-worths and intercept reproduce the mean rating"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In a balanced two-level design each dummy equals 1 in half the profiles, so the mean rating equals the intercept plus half the sum of the part-worths (4.75 in the example). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an intercept that is not the fitted one, or an unbalanced design." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Part-worths and intercept reproduce the mean rating" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CJA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "part-worths-and-intercept-reproduce-the-mean-rating" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AVERAGE(Ratings)-(Intercept+0.5*(PartWorthWait+PartWorthLocal+PartWorthNurse)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002588 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Waiting time part-worth in the outpatient clinic example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The four 12-week profiles average (3 + 4 + 2 + 4) / 4, or 3.25, and the four 4-week profiles (6 + 8 + 5 + 6) / 4, or 6.25, so the 12-week part-worth is minus 3.00, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Waiting time part-worth in the outpatient clinic example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Rbar_1 = 3.25; Rbar_0 = 6.25; b_k = -3" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "waiting-time-part-worth-in-the-outpatient-clinic-example" .

hemo:7002589 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Local clinic part-worth in the outpatient clinic example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Local profiles average 5.50 and hospital profiles 4.00, so the local part-worth is plus 1.50, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Local clinic part-worth in the outpatient clinic example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Rbar_1 = 5.5; Rbar_0 = 4; b_k = 1.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "local-clinic-part-worth-in-the-outpatient-clinic-example" .

hemo:7002590 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Nurse-led clinic part-worth in the outpatient clinic example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Nurse-led profiles average 4.25 and consultant-led profiles 5.25, so the nurse-led part-worth is minus 1.00, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Nurse-led clinic part-worth in the outpatient clinic example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Rbar_1 = 4.25; Rbar_0 = 5.25; b_k = -1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "nurse-led-clinic-part-worth-in-the-outpatient-clinic-example" .

hemo:7002591 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Additive model holds across the profiles predicted"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Predictions add independent part-worths, so they are valid only if preferences for one attribute do not depend on the levels of another." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Additive model holds across the profiles predicted" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CJA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "additive-model-holds-across-the-profiles-predicted" .

hemo:7002592 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Predicted profiles use only levels included in the study"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each code is 0 or 1 for a level that was rated; values between or beyond the studied levels need an assumption about the shape of the part-worth function." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Predicted profiles use only levels included in the study" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CJA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "predicted-profiles-use-only-levels-included-in-the-study" .

hemo:7002593 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Predicted clinic rating from named part-worths and codes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000516 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Intercept, PartWorthWait, PartWorthLocal, PartWorthNurse and the profile's codes WaitCode, LocalCode and NurseCode named, the formula returns the prediction, held in PredictedRating." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Predicted clinic rating from named part-worths and codes" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CJA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "predicted-clinic-rating-from-named-part-worths-and-codes" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Intercept+PartWorthWait*WaitCode+PartWorthLocal*LocalCode+PartWorthNurse*NurseCode" .

hemo:7002594 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Predicted rating matches the SUMPRODUCT form"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "PredictedRating equals Intercept plus SUMPRODUCT of the part-worth range PartWorths and the code range ProfileCodes, in the same attribute order. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a part-worth paired with the wrong code." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Predicted rating matches the SUMPRODUCT form" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CJA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "predicted-rating-matches-the-sumproduct-form" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PredictedRating-(Intercept+SUMPRODUCT(PartWorths,ProfileCodes)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002595 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Predicted rating within the range the part-worths allow"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 0 and 1 codes the prediction lies between the intercept plus all negative part-worths and the intercept plus all positive ones, 2.0 to 7.5 in the example. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a code outside 0 and 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Predicted rating within the range the part-worths allow" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CJA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "predicted-rating-within-the-range-the-part-worths-allow" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(PredictedRating>=Intercept+MIN(0,PartWorthWait)+MIN(0,PartWorthLocal)+MIN(0,PartWorthNurse),PredictedRating<=Intercept+MAX(0,PartWorthWait)+MAX(0,PartWorthLocal)+MAX(0,PartWorthNurse))" .

hemo:7002596 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Local nurse-led clinic with a 4-week wait"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "6.00 plus 1.50 minus 1.00 gives a predicted rating of 6.5, above the reference hospital consultant clinic at 6.0, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Local nurse-led clinic with a 4-week wait" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_0 = 6; b_W = -3; x_W = 0; b_L = 1.5; x_L = 1; b_N = -1; x_N = 1; R_hat = 6.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "local-nurse-led-clinic-with-a-4-week-wait" .

hemo:7002597 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Local nurse-led clinic with a 12-week wait"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Adding the 12-week part-worth of minus 3.00 lowers the prediction to 3.5, below the reference clinic, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Local nurse-led clinic with a 12-week wait" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_0 = 6; b_W = -3; x_W = 1; b_L = 1.5; x_L = 1; b_N = -1; x_N = 1; R_hat = 3.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "local-nurse-led-clinic-with-a-12-week-wait" .

hemo:7002598 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Local consultant-led clinic with a 4-week wait"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The prediction is 7.5 against an observed rating of 8 for profile 3, a residual of 0.5, one of the four misses that give the residual sum of squares of 1.0 in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Local consultant-led clinic with a 4-week wait" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_0 = 6; b_W = -3; x_W = 0; b_L = 1.5; x_L = 1; b_N = -1; x_N = 0; R_hat = 7.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "local-consultant-led-clinic-with-a-4-week-wait" .

hemo:7002599 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Ranges computed over the levels included in the conjoint study"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each range covers only the levels shown, so a wider range of waits would raise waiting time's share without any change in preferences." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ranges computed over the levels included in the conjoint study" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CJA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ranges-computed-over-the-levels-included-in-the-conjoint-study" .

hemo:7002600 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "All attribute ranges on the same part-worth scale"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The ranges come from one model for one respondent or one pooled sample, so they share a scale." ;
    hemo:9000009 "All attribute ranges on the same part-worth scale" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CJA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "all-attribute-ranges-on-the-same-part-worth-scale" .

hemo:7002601 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Relative importance from named attribute ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000517 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the ranges in RangeOne, RangeTwo and RangeThree, the formula returns the first attribute's importance, held in ImportanceOne; ImportanceTwo and ImportanceThree follow by swapping the numerator. A dummy-coded attribute's range is =MAX(0,LevelWorths)-MIN(0,LevelWorths) over its non-reference part-worths." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Relative importance from named attribute ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CJA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "relative-importance-from-named-attribute-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=RangeOne/(RangeOne+RangeTwo+RangeThree)" .

hemo:7002602 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Relative importances of all attributes add to one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "ImportanceOne, ImportanceTwo and ImportanceThree add to 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a range left out of a denominator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Relative importances of all attributes add to one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CJA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "relative-importances-of-all-attributes-add-to-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ImportanceOne+ImportanceTwo+ImportanceThree-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002603 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Attribute ranges entered as non-negative differences"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each range is zero or above, so no importance exceeds 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a signed part-worth, such as minus 3.00, entered as a range." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Attribute ranges entered as non-negative differences" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CJA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "attribute-ranges-entered-as-non-negative-differences" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(RangeOne>=0,RangeTwo>=0,RangeThree>=0,ImportanceOne<=1)" .

hemo:7002604 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Waiting time importance in the outpatient clinic example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Ranges of 3.00 for waiting time, 1.50 for location and 1.00 for clinic lead give waiting time a share of 3.00 / 5.50, about 0.5455 (54.5 per cent in the article)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Waiting time importance in the outpatient clinic example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r_1 = 3; r_2 = 1.5; r_3 = 1; RI_1 = 0.5455" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "waiting-time-importance-in-the-outpatient-clinic-example" .

hemo:7002605 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Clinic lead importance in the outpatient clinic example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Putting clinic lead first, 1.00 / 5.50 gives about 0.1818, the 18.2 per cent in the article; location takes 27.3 per cent." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Clinic lead importance in the outpatient clinic example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r_1 = 1; r_2 = 3; r_3 = 1.5; RI_1 = 0.1818" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "clinic-lead-importance-in-the-outpatient-clinic-example" .

hemo:7002606 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Waiting time importance with a 26-week maximum wait"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If value fell linearly by 0.375 a week, a range of waits from 4 to 26 weeks would give a waiting time range of 8.25 and a share of about 0.7674, against 0.5455 with a 12-week maximum (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Waiting time importance with a 26-week maximum wait" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r_1 = 8.25; r_2 = 1.5; r_3 = 1; RI_1 = 0.7674" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "waiting-time-importance-with-a-26-week-maximum-wait" .

hemo:7002607 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Conjoint attribute b continuous and linear over the range used"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The part-worth of b is the same for every unit; a two-level attribute gives a per-unit value only by assuming linearity between its levels, such as minus 3.00 over 8 weeks." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Conjoint attribute b continuous and linear over the range used" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CJA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "conjoint-attribute-b-continuous-and-linear-over-the-range-used" .

hemo:7002608 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Both conjoint part-worths from the same model and scale"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "b_a and b_b come from one fitted model, so the scale cancels in the ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Both conjoint part-worths from the same model and scale" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CJA-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "both-conjoint-part-worths-from-the-same-model-and-scale" .

hemo:7002609 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Offsetting change from named part-worths"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000518 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With PartWorthA and PartWorthB named, the formula returns the offsetting change in b, held in OffsetChange. A per-unit part-worth from two levels is =PartWorthTwoLevel/(HighLevel-LowLevel)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Offsetting change from named part-worths" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CJA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "offsetting-change-from-named-part-worths" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=-PartWorthA/PartWorthB" .

hemo:7002610 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Offsetting change leaves the profile's value unchanged"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "PartWorthA plus PartWorthB times OffsetChange is 0. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the minus sign dropped or the ratio inverted." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Offsetting change leaves the profile's value unchanged" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CJA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "offsetting-change-leaves-the-profile-s-value-unchanged" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PartWorthA+PartWorthB*OffsetChange)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002611 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Offsetting change positive when the two part-worths have opposite signs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A desirable change in a paired with an undesirable attribute b, such as waiting, gives a positive offsetting change. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Offsetting change positive when the two part-worths have opposite signs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CJA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "offsetting-change-positive-when-the-two-part-worths-have-opposite-signs" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SIGN(OffsetChange)=-SIGN(PartWorthA)*SIGN(PartWorthB)" .

hemo:7002612 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Extra weeks of waiting accepted for a local clinic"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A per-week part-worth of minus 3.00 / 8, or minus 0.375, and a local part-worth of 1.50 give an offsetting wait of 4.0 weeks, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Extra weeks of waiting accepted for a local clinic" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_a = 1.5; b_b = -0.375; dx_b = 4" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "extra-weeks-of-waiting-accepted-for-a-local-clinic" .

hemo:7002613 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Extra weeks of waiting accepted to keep a consultant lead"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Keeping a consultant lead is worth 1.00, so the offsetting wait is 1.00 / 0.375, about 2.6667 weeks (2.7 in the article)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Extra weeks of waiting accepted to keep a consultant lead" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_a = 1; b_b = -0.375; dx_b = 2.6667" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "extra-weeks-of-waiting-accepted-to-keep-a-consultant-lead" .

hemo:7002614 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Orthodontic first appointment at a local clinic"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In Ryan and Farrar's choice study a local first appointment was worth 0.77 and each month of waiting minus 0.59, so respondents would accept about 1.3051 extra months of waiting, reported as 1.3 months." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Orthodontic first appointment at a local clinic" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_a = 0.77; b_b = -0.59; dx_b = 1.3051" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CJA-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "orthodontic-first-appointment-at-a-local-clinic" .

hemo:7002615 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant transition rates over the illness-death interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The three intensities do not change within the interval (a time-homogeneous Markov process); with age-dependent rates the formula applies piece by piece over intervals short enough for the rates to be treated as constant." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant transition rates over the illness-death interval" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CONT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-transition-rates-over-the-illness-death-interval" .

hemo:7002616 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Progressive illness-death structure without recovery"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Nobody returns from Sick to Well, and the Sick exit rate differs from the Well exit rate; when they are equal the Sick probability is q_WS times t times exp(minus q_SD t). Models with recovery or more states need the matrix exponential (HE-CF-CONT-001)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Progressive illness-death structure without recovery" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CONT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "progressive-illness-death-structure-without-recovery" .

hemo:7002617 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Illness-death interval probabilities from named rates"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000519 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With RateWS, RateWD, RateSD and CycleLength named, the three formulas return the probabilities of staying Well, being Sick and being dead, held in ProbWW, ProbWS and ProbWD." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Illness-death interval probabilities from named rates" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CONT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "illness-death-interval-probabilities-from-named-rates" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EXP(-(RateWS+RateWD)*CycleLength); =RateWS/(RateSD-RateWS-RateWD)*(EXP(-(RateWS+RateWD)*CycleLength)-EXP(-RateSD*CycleLength)); =1-ProbWW-ProbWS" .

hemo:7002618 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two intervals equal one interval of twice the length"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Sick at the end of two intervals is Well then Sick, or Sick then still Sick, so the formula at twice CycleLength equals ProbWW times ProbWS plus ProbWS times EXP(minus RateSD times CycleLength). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a probability built row by row instead of from the matrix exponential." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two intervals equal one interval of twice the length" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CONT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-intervals-equal-one-interval-of-twice-the-length" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(RateWS/(RateSD-RateWS-RateWD)*(EXP(-(RateWS+RateWD)*2*CycleLength)-EXP(-RateSD*2*CycleLength))-(ProbWW*ProbWS+ProbWS*EXP(-RateSD*CycleLength)))<1E-12" .

hemo:7002619 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Death probability includes deaths after falling Sick"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "ProbWD exceeds the direct deaths from Well, RateWD / (RateWS plus RateWD) times (1 minus ProbWW), whenever RateSD and CycleLength are above 0. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the competing-risk split used, which leaves out the two-step path." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Death probability includes deaths after falling Sick" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CONT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "death-probability-includes-deaths-after-falling-sick" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ProbWD>RateWD/(RateWS+RateWD)*(1-ProbWW)" .

hemo:7002620 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "One-year probabilities in the article's illness-death example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With rates of 0.30, 0.05 and 0.40 a year, staying Well is exp(minus 0.35), about 0.7047; being Sick is 6 times (0.704688 minus 0.670320), about 0.2062; and death by either route takes the remaining 0.0891, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One-year probabilities in the article's illness-death example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q_WS = 0.3; q_WD = 0.05; q_SD = 0.4; t = 1; p_WW = 0.7047; p_WS = 0.2062; p_WD = 0.0891" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CONT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-year-probabilities-in-the-article-s-illness-death-example" .

hemo:7002621 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "One-month probabilities in the article's illness-death example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Over a month the same rates give about 0.9713, 0.0242 and 0.0045 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One-month probabilities in the article's illness-death example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q_WS = 0.3; q_WD = 0.05; q_SD = 0.4; t = 0.083333; p_WW = 0.9713; p_WS = 0.0242; p_WD = 0.0045" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CONT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-month-probabilities-in-the-article-s-illness-death-example" .

hemo:7002622 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Decompensated cirrhosis, liver cancer and death"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Chhatwal and colleagues estimated rates of 0.0967 from decompensated cirrhosis to hepatocellular carcinoma, 0.2402 from cirrhosis to death and 0.5573 from carcinoma to death; the annual probabilities are about 0.7140, 0.0620 and 0.2241 (the source reports 0.0619 for the middle value)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Decompensated cirrhosis, liver cancer and death" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q_WS = 0.0967; q_WD = 0.2402; q_SD = 0.5573; t = 1; p_WW = 0.714; p_WS = 0.062; p_WD = 0.2241" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CONT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "decompensated-cirrhosis-liver-cancer-and-death" .

hemo:7002623 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant rates over a lifetime horizon without discounting"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Rates do not change with age or time in state and time is counted to death without discounting; discounted times are HE-FM-CONT-004." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant rates over a lifetime horizon without discounting" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CONT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-rates-over-a-lifetime-horizon-without-discounting" .

hemo:7002624 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Sick entered only from Well and at most once"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Without recovery, the expected number of entries to Sick is the share q_WS / (q_WS plus q_WD); with recovery, expected times come from integrating the matrix exponential." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sick entered only from Well and at most once" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CONT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sick-entered-only-from-well-and-at-most-once" .

hemo:7002625 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected years Well and Sick from named rates"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000520 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With RateWS, RateWD and RateSD named, the three formulas return expected years Well, Sick and alive, held in TimeWell, TimeSick and LifeExp." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected years Well and Sick from named rates" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CONT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-years-well-and-sick-from-named-rates" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1/(RateWS+RateWD); =RateWS/(RateWS+RateWD)/RateSD; =TimeWell+TimeSick" .

hemo:7002626 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected entries to Sick balance expected exits from Sick"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "People enter Sick at rate RateWS for every year spent Well and leave at rate RateSD for every year spent Sick, so TimeSick times RateSD equals RateWS times TimeWell. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the share falling Sick or the Sick sojourn left out." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected entries to Sick balance expected exits from Sick" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CONT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-entries-to-sick-balance-expected-exits-from-sick" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(TimeSick*RateSD-RateWS*TimeWell)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002627 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected time Sick below the mean Sick sojourn when some die while Well"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Only the share who fall Sick spend time there, so with RateWD above 0 TimeSick is below 1 / RateSD. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the mean sojourn 1 / RateSD used for everyone." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected time Sick below the mean Sick sojourn when some die while Well" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CONT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-time-sick-below-the-mean-sick-sojourn-when-some-die-while-well" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(RateWD>0,TimeSick<1/RateSD,ABS(TimeSick-1/RateSD)<1E-12)" .

hemo:7002628 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Life expectancy in the article's illness-death example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With rates of 0.30, 0.05 and 0.40, expected time Well is 1 / 0.35, about 2.8571 years, and Sick 0.857 times 2.5, about 2.1429 years, a life expectancy of 5.000 years, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Life expectancy in the article's illness-death example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q_WS = 0.3; q_WD = 0.05; q_SD = 0.4; L_W = 2.8571; L_S = 2.1429; LE = 5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CONT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "life-expectancy-in-the-article-s-illness-death-example" .

hemo:7002629 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Slower death after falling Sick"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Halving the Sick death rate to 0.20 doubles expected time Sick to about 4.2857 years and raises life expectancy to about 7.1429 years (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Slower death after falling Sick" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q_WS = 0.3; q_WD = 0.05; q_SD = 0.2; L_W = 2.8571; L_S = 4.2857; LE = 7.1429" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CONT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "slower-death-after-falling-sick" .

hemo:7002630 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Life expectancy in the liver disease intensity matrix"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Chhatwal and colleagues' rates of 0.0967, 0.2402 and 0.5573, expected time in decompensated cirrhosis is about 2.9682 years and with carcinoma about 0.515 years, a life expectancy of about 3.4833 years (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Life expectancy in the liver disease intensity matrix" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q_WS = 0.0967; q_WD = 0.2402; q_SD = 0.5573; L_W = 2.9682; L_S = 0.515; LE = 3.4833" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CONT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "life-expectancy-in-the-liver-disease-intensity-matrix" .

hemo:7002631 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Annual discount rate applied as compound annual discounting"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "d is the rate in the discrete formula 1 / (1 plus d) to the power t, as used in reference-case analyses; t is in years." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annual discount rate applied as compound annual discounting" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CONT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annual-discount-rate-applied-as-compound-annual-discounting" .

hemo:7002632 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same discount rate for costs and health unless stated"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "One rho is used for both costs and QALYs when the annual rates are equal; separate rates need separate rho values." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same discount rate for costs and health unless stated" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CONT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-discount-rate-for-costs-and-health-unless-stated" .

hemo:7002633 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous discount rate and factor from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000521 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With AnnualRate and Years named, the first formula returns the continuous rate, held in ContRate, and the second the discount factor, held in DiscFactor." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuous discount rate and factor from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CONT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuous-discount-rate-and-factor-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LN(1+AnnualRate); =EXP(-ContRate*Years)" .

hemo:7002634 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous and annual discount factors agree"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "DiscFactor equals (1 plus AnnualRate) to the power minus Years. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the annual rate used in the exponent." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuous and annual discount factors agree" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CONT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuous-and-annual-discount-factors-agree" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(DiscFactor-(1+AnnualRate)^-Years)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002635 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous rate below the annual rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a positive annual rate the continuous rate is smaller, about 0.0344 against 0.035. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuous rate below the annual rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CONT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuous-rate-below-the-annual-rate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(AnnualRate>0,ContRate<AnnualRate,ABS(ContRate)<1E-12)" .

hemo:7002636 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous equivalent of a 3.5 per cent annual rate at 10 years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "rho is log 1.035, about 0.0344, and the factor at 10 years is about 0.7089, the same as 1.035 to the power minus 10 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuous equivalent of a 3.5 per cent annual rate at 10 years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d = 0.035; t = 10; rho = 0.0344; DF_t = 0.7089" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CONT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuous-equivalent-of-a-3-5-per-cent-annual-rate-at-10-years" .

hemo:7002637 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous equivalent of a 1.5 per cent annual rate at 10 years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "rho is about 0.0149 and the factor at 10 years about 0.8617 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuous equivalent of a 1.5 per cent annual rate at 10 years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d = 0.015; t = 10; rho = 0.0149; DF_t = 0.8617" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CONT-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuous-equivalent-of-a-1-5-per-cent-annual-rate-at-10-years" .

hemo:7002638 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant rates and utilities over a lifetime horizon"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Rates and utilities do not change with age or time in state and the horizon is lifetime; otherwise the integral is evaluated numerically." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant rates and utilities over a lifetime horizon" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CONT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-rates-and-utilities-over-a-lifetime-horizon" .

hemo:7002639 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Progressive illness-death model starting Well for discounted QALYs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Everyone starts Well and Sick people do not recover, as in HE-FM-CONT-001." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Progressive illness-death model starting Well for discounted QALYs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CONT-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "progressive-illness-death-model-starting-well-for-discounted-qalys" .

hemo:7002640 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted QALYs from named rates, utilities and continuous rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000522 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With UtilWell, UtilSick, RateWS, RateWD, RateSD and ContRate named, the first two formulas return discounted years Well and Sick, held in DiscTimeWell and DiscTimeSick, and the third the discounted QALYs, held in DiscQALY." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted QALYs from named rates, utilities and continuous rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CONT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-qalys-from-named-rates-utilities-and-continuous-rate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1/(RateWS+RateWD+ContRate); =RateWS/(RateWS+RateWD+ContRate)/(RateSD+ContRate); =UtilWell*DiscTimeWell+UtilSick*DiscTimeSick" .

hemo:7002641 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted entries to Sick balance discounted exits"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "DiscTimeSick times (RateSD plus ContRate) equals RateWS times DiscTimeWell. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows rho added to one denominator but not the other." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted entries to Sick balance discounted exits" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CONT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-entries-to-sick-balance-discounted-exits" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(DiscTimeSick*(RateSD+ContRate)-RateWS*DiscTimeWell)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002642 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted QALYs no larger than undiscounted QALYs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a non-negative ContRate and utilities, DiscQALY does not exceed the same expression with ContRate set to 0. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows rho subtracted instead of added." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted QALYs no larger than undiscounted QALYs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CONT-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-qalys-no-larger-than-undiscounted-qalys" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=DiscQALY<=UtilWell/(RateWS+RateWD)+UtilSick*RateWS/(RateWS+RateWD)/RateSD" .

hemo:7002643 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted QALYs at 3.5 per cent in the article's example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With rates of 0.30, 0.05 and 0.40, utilities of 0.85 Well and 0.60 Sick and rho of 0.0344, discounted time is about 2.601 years Well and 1.797 years Sick, giving about 3.2892 QALYs (utilities and result computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted QALYs at 3.5 per cent in the article's example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "u_W = 0.85; u_S = 0.6; q_WS = 0.3; q_WD = 0.05; q_SD = 0.4; rho = 0.034401; QALY_d = 3.2892" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CONT-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-qalys-at-3-5-per-cent-in-the-article-s-example" .

hemo:7002644 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Undiscounted QALYs in the illness-death example with rho of zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With rho of 0 the formula returns 0.85 times 2.857 plus 0.60 times 2.143, about 3.7143 QALYs, the undiscounted times of HE-FM-CONT-002 weighted by utility (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Undiscounted QALYs in the illness-death example with rho of zero" ;
    hemo:9000014 "u_W = 0.85; u_S = 0.6; q_WS = 0.3; q_WD = 0.05; q_SD = 0.4; rho = 0; QALY_d = 3.7143" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CONT-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "undiscounted-qalys-in-the-illness-death-example-with-rho-of-zero" .

hemo:7002645 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "No unmeasured confounders of censoring and the outcome"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Data are available on every baseline and time-dependent factor that predicts both switching and survival; this cannot be tested from the observed data, and with all such factors unmeasured IPCW reduces to simple censoring." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No unmeasured confounders of censoring and the outcome" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCEN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-unmeasured-confounders-of-censoring-and-the-outcome" .

hemo:7002646 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Positivity, every patient has some chance of remaining unswitched"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "p_t is above 0 at every covariate level (positivity); if some covariate level makes switching certain, the method cannot work." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positivity: every patient has some chance of remaining unswitched" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCEN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positivity-every-patient-has-some-chance-of-remaining-unswitched" .

hemo:7002647 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Unstabilised IPCW weight from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000523 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the previous weight in PrevWeight and the probability of remaining unswitched in ProbUnswitched, the formula returns the weight, held in IPCWWeight. With a fitted logistic model of switching, ProbUnswitched is 1 minus the predicted probability of switching in the interval." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Unstabilised IPCW weight from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DCEN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "unstabilised-ipcw-weight-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PrevWeight/ProbUnswitched" .

hemo:7002648 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted non-switchers stand in for the whole eligible group"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With PrevWeight equal to 1 and ProbUnswitched equal to NonSwitchers / AtRisk for a covariate group, NonSwitchers times IPCWWeight equals AtRisk (30 times 2 equals 60 in the article). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the probability of switching used in place of the probability of remaining unswitched." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted non-switchers stand in for the whole eligible group" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCEN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-non-switchers-stand-in-for-the-whole-eligible-group" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(NonSwitchers*IPCWWeight-AtRisk)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002649 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "IPCW weight never below the previous weight"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "ProbUnswitched is a probability, so the weight can only stay the same or rise. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a probability entered as a percentage." ;
    hemo:9000009 "IPCW weight never below the previous weight" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCEN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ipcw-weight-never-below-the-previous-weight" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ProbUnswitched>0,ProbUnswitched<=1,IPCWWeight>=PrevWeight)" .

hemo:7002650 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Progressed non-switcher in the article's control arm"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Half of the 60 progressed patients stayed unswitched, so each progressed non-switcher gets weight 1 / 0.5, which is 2, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Progressed non-switcher in the article's control arm" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_prev = 1; p_t = 0.5; w_t = 2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "progressed-non-switcher-in-the-article-s-control-arm" .

hemo:7002651 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Progression-free patient who cannot switch"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Progression-free patients cannot switch, so their probability of remaining uncensored is 1 and the weight stays 1, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Progression-free patient who cannot switch" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_prev = 1; p_t = 1; w_t = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "progression-free-patient-who-cannot-switch" .

hemo:7002652 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three non-switchers left among 60 eligible patients"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Had 57 of the 60 progressed patients switched, each of the 3 non-switchers would weigh 60 / 3, which is 20, as in the article's extreme-weights step." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three non-switchers left among 60 eligible patients" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_prev = 1; p_t = 0.05; w_t = 20" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-non-switchers-left-among-60-eligible-patients" .

hemo:7002653 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Numerator model uses baseline covariates only"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The numerator conditions on baseline covariates, which then also enter the outcome model; time-dependent covariates appear only in the denominator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Numerator model uses baseline covariates only" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCEN-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "numerator-model-uses-baseline-covariates-only" .

hemo:7002654 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same switching data for numerator and denominator models"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both probabilities are estimated on the same patients and intervals, so their ratio is 1 when time-dependent covariates add nothing." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same switching data for numerator and denominator models" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCEN-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-switching-data-for-numerator-and-denominator-models" .

hemo:7002655 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Stabilised IPCW weight from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000524 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With PrevStabWeight, ProbUnswitchedBaseline and ProbUnswitchedFull named, the formula returns the stabilised weight, held in StabWeight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Stabilised IPCW weight from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DCEN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "stabilised-ipcw-weight-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PrevStabWeight*ProbUnswitchedBaseline/ProbUnswitchedFull" .

hemo:7002656 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Stabilised weights of the unswitched add up to their number"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the numerator equal to the overall share unswitched, the stabilised weights StabWeightProg and StabWeightPF of the ProgNonSwitch progressed non-switchers and PFCount progression-free patients add up to the number unswitched, 30 times 1.6 plus 90 times 0.8, or 120. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows unstabilised weights used (30 times 2 plus 90 times 1 is 150) or a numerator not equal to the overall share unswitched." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Stabilised weights of the unswitched add up to their number" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCEN-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "stabilised-weights-of-the-unswitched-add-up-to-their-number" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ProgNonSwitch*StabWeightProg+PFCount*StabWeightPF-(ProgNonSwitch+PFCount))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002657 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Stabilised weight is the unstabilised weight times the numerator"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the first interval StabWeight equals IPCWWeight from HE-FM-DCEN-001 times ProbUnswitchedBaseline. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows numerator and denominator swapped." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Stabilised weight is the unstabilised weight times the numerator" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCEN-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "stabilised-weight-is-the-unstabilised-weight-times-the-numerator" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(StabWeight-IPCWWeight*ProbUnswitchedBaseline)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002658 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Progressed non-switcher with stabilised weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With no baseline covariates, the numerator is the overall share unswitched, 120 of 150 or 0.8, so a progressed non-switcher gets 0.8 / 0.5, which is 1.6, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Progressed non-switcher with stabilised weights" ;
    hemo:9000014 "sw_prev = 1; p_num = 0.8; p_den = 0.5; sw_t = 1.6" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "progressed-non-switcher-with-stabilised-weights" .

hemo:7002659 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Progression-free patient with stabilised weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A progression-free patient, who cannot switch, gets 0.8 / 1, which is 0.8, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Progression-free patient with stabilised weights" ;
    hemo:9000014 "sw_prev = 1; p_num = 0.8; p_den = 1; sw_t = 0.8" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "progression-free-patient-with-stabilised-weights" .

hemo:7002660 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Dependent censoring explained by the measured prognostic groups"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Within each group, censored and uncensored patients have the same hazard, so the weighted risk set represents everyone event free; in the article switching depends only on progression." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Dependent censoring explained by the measured prognostic groups" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCEN-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "dependent-censoring-explained-by-the-measured-prognostic-groups" .

hemo:7002661 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Switchers censored before deaths in the IPCW-weighted interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Switchers are censored at the start of the interval, before any deaths in it, and the weights apply to the patients still at risk." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Switchers censored before deaths in the IPCW-weighted interval" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCEN-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "switchers-censored-before-deaths-in-the-ipcw-weighted-interval" .

hemo:7002662 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "IPCW-weighted survival step from named counts and weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000525 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With SurvPrev, WeightOne, DeathsOne, AtRiskOne, WeightTwo, DeathsTwo and AtRiskTwo named, the formula returns survival at the end of the interval, held in WeightedSurv. For many patients, =SurvPrev*(1-SUMPRODUCT(Weights,Deaths)/SUMPRODUCT(Weights,AtRisk)) uses one row per patient." ;
    hemo:9000009 "IPCW-weighted survival step from named counts and weights" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DCEN-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ipcw-weighted-survival-step-from-named-counts-and-weights" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SurvPrev*(1-(WeightOne*DeathsOne+WeightTwo*DeathsTwo)/(WeightOne*AtRiskOne+WeightTwo*AtRiskTwo))" .

hemo:7002663 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted survival unchanged when every weight is doubled"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Only relative weights matter, which is why stabilised and unstabilised weights give the same 0.585. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows weights applied to the deaths but not to the risk set." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted survival unchanged when every weight is doubled" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCEN-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-survival-unchanged-when-every-weight-is-doubled" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SurvPrev*(1-(2*WeightOne*DeathsOne+2*WeightTwo*DeathsTwo)/(2*WeightOne*AtRiskOne+2*WeightTwo*AtRiskTwo))-WeightedSurv)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002664 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted survival between the two groups' own survival"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weighted conditional survival is an average of the groups' conditional survivals, 0.6 and 0.9 in the example, so WeightedSurv lies between SurvPrev times each. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a negative weight or survival not carried forward from SurvPrev." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted survival between the two groups' own survival" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCEN-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-survival-between-the-two-groups-own-survival" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(WeightedSurv>=SurvPrev*MIN(1-DeathsOne/AtRiskOne,1-DeathsTwo/AtRiskTwo),WeightedSurv<=SurvPrev*MAX(1-DeathsOne/AtRiskOne,1-DeathsTwo/AtRiskTwo))" .

hemo:7002665 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Year-2 survival with switchers censored and reweighted"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With weights of 2 for the 30 progressed non-switchers (12 deaths) and 1 for the 90 progression-free patients (9 deaths), the weighted deaths are 33 in a weighted risk set of 150, so survival is 0.75 times 0.78, or 0.585, the no-switching value, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Year-2 survival with switchers censored and reweighted" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_1 = 0.75; w_1 = 2; d_1 = 12; n_1 = 30; w_2 = 1; d_2 = 9; n_2 = 90; S_2 = 0.585" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "year-2-survival-with-switchers-censored-and-reweighted" .

hemo:7002666 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Year-2 survival with switchers simply censored"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With both weights 1 the risk set is 120 with 21 deaths, giving 0.75 times 0.825, or 0.61875, 3.4 percentage points too high, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Year-2 survival with switchers simply censored" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_1 = 0.75; w_1 = 1; d_1 = 12; n_1 = 30; w_2 = 1; d_2 = 9; n_2 = 90; S_2 = 0.61875" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "year-2-survival-with-switchers-simply-censored" .

hemo:7002667 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Year-2 survival with stabilised weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Weights of 1.6 and 0.8 give 26.4 weighted deaths in a weighted risk set of 120, the same conditional survival of 0.78 and 0.585 at two years, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Year-2 survival with stabilised weights" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_1 = 0.75; w_1 = 1.6; d_1 = 12; n_1 = 30; w_2 = 0.8; d_2 = 9; n_2 = 90; S_2 = 0.585" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "year-2-survival-with-stabilised-weights" .

hemo:7002668 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Year-2 survival with three heavily weighted non-switchers"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 3 progressed non-switchers weighted 20 and one death among them, survival is 0.75 times (1 minus 29 / 150), about 0.605; with two deaths it falls to 0.505, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Year-2 survival with three heavily weighted non-switchers" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_1 = 0.75; w_1 = 20; d_1 = 1; n_1 = 3; w_2 = 1; d_2 = 9; n_2 = 90; S_2 = 0.605" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "year-2-survival-with-three-heavily-weighted-non-switchers" .

hemo:7002669 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Censoring independent of the cost and survival process"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Kaplan-Meier estimation of the censoring distribution assumes censoring does not depend on prognosis or spending." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Censoring independent of the cost and survival process" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCEN-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "censoring-independent-of-the-cost-and-survival-process" .

hemo:7002670 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Restricted period with enough complete cases for the weighted cost estimator"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Costs are estimated up to a limit within follow-up, and S_c_i stays well above 0; with heavy censoring a few complete cases carry large weights." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Restricted period with enough complete cases for the weighted cost estimator" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCEN-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "restricted-period-with-enough-complete-cases-for-the-weighted-cost-estimator" .

hemo:7002671 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted mean cost from named patient ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000526 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 1 or 0 complete-case flags in Complete, costs in Costs and censoring survival in CensSurv (one row per patient, any positive value in censored rows), the formula returns the weighted mean, held in IPWMeanCost." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted mean cost from named patient ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DCEN-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-mean-cost-from-named-patient-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(Complete,Costs/CensSurv)/COUNT(Costs)" .

hemo:7002672 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weights of complete cases add up to the number of patients"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When the longest time is a complete case and times are distinct, the inverse censoring probabilities of the complete cases add to N (1 plus 1.333 plus 2.667, or 5, in the example). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows censoring survival estimated with deaths as the event." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weights of complete cases add up to the number of patients" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCEN-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weights-of-complete-cases-add-up-to-the-number-of-patients" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(Complete,1/CensSurv)-COUNT(Costs))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002673 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted mean not below the complete-case costs spread over all patients"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each weight is at least 1, so IPWMeanCost is at least the sum of complete-case costs divided by N. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows censoring probabilities entered as percentages." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted mean not below the complete-case costs spread over all patients" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCEN-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-mean-not-below-the-complete-case-costs-spread-over-all-patients" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IPWMeanCost>=SUMPRODUCT(Complete,Costs)/COUNT(Costs)" .

hemo:7002674 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Five patients with two censored over three years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Patients die at 0.5 and 1.5 years with costs of 6,000 and 18,000 pounds, are censored at 1 and 2 years with 5,000 and 9,000, and one is followed to the 3-year limit with 12,000. The censoring survival is 1, 0.75 and 0.375 at the three complete-case times, so the weighted mean is (6,000 + 24,000 + 32,000) / 5, or 12,400 pounds, against a full-sample mean of 10,000 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Five patients with two censored over three years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N = 5; Delta_i = [1,0,1,0,1]; A_i = [6000,5000,18000,9000,12000]; S_c_i = [1,1,0.75,0.75,0.375]; mu = 12400" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "five-patients-with-two-censored-over-three-years" .

hemo:7002675 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same five patients with no censoring in the weighted cost estimator"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With every patient a complete case, all weights are 1 and the estimator equals the plain mean of 10,000 pounds (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same five patients with no censoring in the weighted cost estimator" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N = 5; Delta_i = [1,1,1,1,1]; A_i = [6000,5000,18000,9000,12000]; S_c_i = [1,1,1,1,1]; mu = 10000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-five-patients-with-no-censoring-in-the-weighted-cost-estimator" .

hemo:7002676 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant hazard within year 1 and a constant hazard after year 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Survival is exponential within the first year and from year 1 onwards with the year-2 hazard, an illustrative extrapolation; mean survival is the area under the extrapolated curve." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant hazard within year 1 and a constant hazard after year 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCEN-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-hazard-within-year-1-and-a-constant-hazard-after-year-1" .

hemo:7002677 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Year-2 conditional survival free of censoring bias"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "q_2 estimates what would have happened without switching only if it comes from an analysis that removes the dependence, such as IPCW." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Year-2 conditional survival free of censoring bias" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DCEN-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "year-2-conditional-survival-free-of-censoring-bias" .

hemo:7002678 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-piece mean survival from named survival probabilities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000527 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With SurvYearOne and CondSurvTwo named, the formula returns mean survival, held in MeanSurv." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-piece mean survival from named survival probabilities" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DCEN-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-piece-mean-survival-from-named-survival-probabilities" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(1-SurvYearOne)/(-LN(SurvYearOne))+SurvYearOne/(-LN(CondSurvTwo))" .

hemo:7002679 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mean survival between the end-of-year count and the trapezoid count"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With annual survival falling by CondSurvTwo each year after the first, the end-of-year counts add to SurvYearOne / (1 minus CondSurvTwo); the trapezoid (half-cycle) rule adds 0.5 and, because each exponential piece is convex, overstates the area, so the continuous mean lies between the two (3.41 and 3.91 for the target). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a probability used as a hazard or LOG10 used for LN." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mean survival between the end-of-year count and the trapezoid count" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCEN-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mean-survival-between-the-end-of-year-count-and-the-trapezoid-count" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(MeanSurv>SurvYearOne/(1-CondSurvTwo),MeanSurv<0.5+SurvYearOne/(1-CondSurvTwo))" .

hemo:7002680 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Survival inputs above zero and below one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both probabilities are above 0 and below 1, so both hazards are positive and MeanSurv is finite and positive. Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Survival inputs above zero and below one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DCEN-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "survival-inputs-above-zero-and-below-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(SurvYearOne>0,SurvYearOne<1,CondSurvTwo>0,CondSurvTwo<1,MeanSurv>0)" .

hemo:7002681 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mean survival without switching or with IPCW"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With S_1 of 0.75 and q_2 of 0.78 the hazards are 0.2877 and 0.2485, so mean survival is 0.869 plus 0.75 / 0.2485, about 3.8876 years (3.89 in the article)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mean survival without switching or with IPCW" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_1 = 0.75; q_2 = 0.78; T_bar = 3.8876" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mean-survival-without-switching-or-with-ipcw" .

hemo:7002682 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mean survival with switchers censored"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With q_2 of 0.825 the year-2 hazard is 0.1924 and mean survival about 4.7677 years (4.77 in the article), 0.88 life-years more than the target, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mean survival with switchers censored" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_1 = 0.75; q_2 = 0.825; T_bar = 4.7677" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DCEN-013" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mean-survival-with-switchers-censored" .

hemo:7002683 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Targets on comparable scales or weighted to be so"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Absolute differences are added across targets, so targets in different units or of different precision need weights that make their distances comparable." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Targets on comparable scales or weighted to be so" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BOPT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "targets-on-comparable-scales-or-weighted-to-be-so" .

hemo:7002684 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Each loss evaluation is a full model run"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The loss is a black-box function of the parameters; the search sees only the values returned by the runs made." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Each loss evaluation is a full model run" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BOPT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "each-loss-evaluation-is-a-full-model-run" .

hemo:7002685 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-target calibration loss from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000528 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Weight1, Pred1, Target1, Weight2, Pred2 and Target2 named, the formula returns the loss, held in CalibLoss." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-target calibration loss from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BOPT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-target-calibration-loss-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Weight1*ABS(Pred1-Target1)+Weight2*ABS(Pred2-Target2)" .

hemo:7002686 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Calibration loss no smaller than either weighted gap"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "CalibLoss is at least Weight1 times ABS(Pred1 minus Target1) and at least Weight2 times ABS(Pred2 minus Target2). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows signed differences that cancel, such as plus 3.52 and minus 3.52 giving a loss of 0." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Calibration loss no smaller than either weighted gap" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BOPT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "calibration-loss-no-smaller-than-either-weighted-gap" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(CalibLoss>=Weight1*ABS(Pred1-Target1)-1E-12,CalibLoss>=Weight2*ABS(Pred2-Target2)-1E-12)" .

hemo:7002687 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Absolute-difference loss no larger than total weight times the largest gap"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "CalibLoss is at most (Weight1 plus Weight2) times the larger absolute gap. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows squared gaps used in a loss described as absolute (3.52 squared is about 12.4)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absolute-difference loss no larger than total weight times the largest gap" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BOPT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absolute-difference-loss-no-larger-than-total-weight-times-the-largest-gap" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CalibLoss<=(Weight1+Weight2)*MAX(ABS(Pred1-Target1),ABS(Pred2-Target2))+1E-12" .

hemo:7002688 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Ten-year incidence of 9.56 per cent against a 30 per cent target"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With annual probability 0.01, ten-year incidence is 1 minus 0.99 to the power 10, about 9.5618 per cent, a loss of about 20.4382 points against the 30 per cent target (20.44 in the article)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ten-year incidence of 9.56 per cent against a 30 per cent target" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_1 = 1; g_1 = 9.5618; T_1 = 30; w_2 = 0; g_2 = 0; T_2 = 0; L = 20.4382" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ten-year-incidence-of-9-56-per-cent-against-a-30-per-cent-target" .

hemo:7002689 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Ten-year incidence at an annual probability of 0.04"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At 0.04 the model predicts about 33.5167 per cent, a loss of about 3.5167 points (3.52 in the article)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ten-year incidence at an annual probability of 0.04" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_1 = 1; g_1 = 33.5167; T_1 = 30; w_2 = 0; g_2 = 0; T_2 = 0; L = 3.5167" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ten-year-incidence-at-an-annual-probability-of-0-04" .

hemo:7002690 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Incidence and prevalence targets with a weight of 0.5 on prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Adding a prevalence target of 10 per cent, predicted at 12 per cent with weight 0.5, gives 3.52 plus 1, a loss of 4.52 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Incidence and prevalence targets with a weight of 0.5 on prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_1 = 1; g_1 = 33.52; T_1 = 30; w_2 = 0.5; g_2 = 12; T_2 = 10; L = 4.52" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "incidence-and-prevalence-targets-with-a-weight-of-0-5-on-prevalence" .

hemo:7002691 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Smoothness of the loss set by the kernel"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The squared exponential kernel assumes a smooth loss surface; a loss with a sharp minimum, such as an absolute difference, is approximated less well near the minimum." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Smoothness of the loss set by the kernel" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BOPT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "smoothness-of-the-loss-set-by-the-kernel" .

hemo:7002692 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Kernel parameters fixed or estimated from the runs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The article fixes the prior mean, variance and length-scale for clarity; in practice they are usually estimated from the runs made so far by maximum likelihood or a maximum a posteriori estimate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Kernel parameters fixed or estimated from the runs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BOPT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "kernel-parameters-fixed-or-estimated-from-the-runs" .

hemo:7002693 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Squared exponential kernel from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000529 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With ThetaA, ThetaB, LengthScale and SFVar named, the formulas return the prior correlation and covariance, held in KernelCorr and KernelCov." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Squared exponential kernel from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BOPT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "squared-exponential-kernel-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EXP(-(ThetaA-ThetaB)^2/(2*LengthScale^2)); =SFVar*KernelCorr" .

hemo:7002694 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Log of the kernel correlation equals minus the squared distance over twice the squared length-scale"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "LN(KernelCorr) times 2 times LengthScale squared plus (ThetaA minus ThetaB) squared is zero. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the distance not squared or 2 times LengthScale used in place of 2 times its square." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log of the kernel correlation equals minus the squared distance over twice the squared length-scale" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BOPT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-of-the-kernel-correlation-equals-minus-the-squared-distance-over-twice-the-squared-length-scale" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LN(KernelCorr)*2*LengthScale^2+(ThetaA-ThetaB)^2)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002695 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Kernel covariance no larger than the prior variance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "KernelCov equals SFVar at zero distance and is below it otherwise. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the minus sign dropped from the exponent (about 22.8 times SFVar for 0.01 and 0.06)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Kernel covariance no larger than the prior variance" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BOPT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "kernel-covariance-no-larger-than-the-prior-variance" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(ThetaA=ThetaB,ABS(KernelCov-SFVar)<1E-12,AND(KernelCov<SFVar,KernelCov>0))" .

hemo:7002696 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Correlation between the two initial runs at 0.01 and 0.06"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a length-scale of 0.02, 2 times 0.02 squared is 0.0008, and the squared distance 0.0025 gives exp(minus 3.125), about 0.0439, a covariance of about 4.3937 with prior variance 100, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Correlation between the two initial runs at 0.01 and 0.06" ;
    hemo:9000014 "theta_a = 0.01; theta_b = 0.06; ell = 0.02; sf2 = 100; c_ab = 0.0439; k_ab = 4.3937" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "correlation-between-the-two-initial-runs-at-0-01-and-0-06" .

hemo:7002697 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Correlation of the candidate 0.04 with the run at 0.01"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The squared distance 0.0009 gives exp(minus 1.125), about 0.3247, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Correlation of the candidate 0.04 with the run at 0.01" ;
    hemo:9000014 "theta_a = 0.04; theta_b = 0.01; ell = 0.02; sf2 = 100; c_ab = 0.3247; k_ab = 32.4652" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "correlation-of-the-candidate-0-04-with-the-run-at-0-01" .

hemo:7002698 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Correlation of the candidate 0.04 with the run at 0.06"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The squared distance 0.0004 gives exp(minus 0.5), about 0.6065, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Correlation of the candidate 0.04 with the run at 0.06" ;
    hemo:9000014 "theta_a = 0.04; theta_b = 0.06; ell = 0.02; sf2 = 100; c_ab = 0.6065; k_ab = 60.6531" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "correlation-of-the-candidate-0-04-with-the-run-at-0-06" .

hemo:7002699 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Noise-free model runs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The losses are observed without simulation noise, as for a deterministic cohort model; a microsimulation with a finite number of simulated people adds a noise variance to the diagonal of the run covariance matrix." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Noise-free model runs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BOPT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "noise-free-model-runs" .

hemo:7002700 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed prior mean, variance and length-scale for the posterior"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The prior mean, variance and length-scale are held fixed when the posterior is computed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fixed prior mean, variance and length-scale for the posterior" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BOPT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fixed-prior-mean-variance-and-length-scale-for-the-posterior" .

hemo:7002701 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-run Gaussian process posterior from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000530 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Corr1, Corr2, Corr12, PriorMean, Loss1, Loss2 and SFVar named, the formulas return the two weights, the posterior mean and the posterior variance, held in GPWeight1, GPWeight2, PostMean and PostVar." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-run Gaussian process posterior from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BOPT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-run-gaussian-process-posterior-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(Corr1-Corr12*Corr2)/(1-Corr12^2); =(Corr2-Corr12*Corr1)/(1-Corr12^2); =PriorMean+GPWeight1*(Loss1-PriorMean)+GPWeight2*(Loss2-PriorMean); =SFVar*(1-(Corr1*GPWeight1+Corr2*GPWeight2))" .

hemo:7002702 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior weights solve the correlation system of the two runs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "GPWeight1 plus Corr12 times GPWeight2 equals Corr1, and Corr12 times GPWeight1 plus GPWeight2 equals Corr2. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the division by 1 minus Corr12 squared left out (0.29800 instead of 0.29858 for the first weight) or the weights swapped." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Posterior weights solve the correlation system of the two runs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BOPT-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "posterior-weights-solve-the-correlation-system-of-the-two-runs" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS(GPWeight1+Corr12*GPWeight2-Corr1)<1E-9,ABS(Corr12*GPWeight1+GPWeight2-Corr2)<1E-9)" .

hemo:7002703 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior variance not negative and not above the prior variance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "PostVar is from 0 up to SFVar. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the explained part added instead of subtracted (about 145.7 at 0.04)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Posterior variance not negative and not above the prior variance" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BOPT-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "posterior-variance-not-negative-and-not-above-the-prior-variance" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(PostVar>=-1E-9,PostVar<=SFVar+1E-9)" .

hemo:7002704 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior at the candidate 0.04 after runs at 0.01 and 0.06"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With correlations of 0.3247 and 0.6065 to the runs and 0.0439 between them, the weights are about 0.2986 and 0.5934; the posterior mean is about 17.8394 and the variance about 54.3143, a standard deviation of about 7.37, as in the article (17.84 and 54.31)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Posterior at the candidate 0.04 after runs at 0.01 and 0.06" ;
    hemo:9000014 "c_1 = 0.324652; c_2 = 0.606531; c_12 = 0.043937; mu_0 = 20; y_1 = 20.4382; y_2 = 16.1385; sf2 = 100; a_1 = 0.2986; a_2 = 0.5934; mu_n = 17.8394; var_n = 54.3143" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "posterior-at-the-candidate-0-04-after-runs-at-0-01-and-0-06" .

hemo:7002705 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior at the candidate 0.035, midway between the runs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Midway the two correlations are equal at about 0.4578 and each weight is about 0.4386; the posterior mean is about 18.4987 and the variance about 59.8421, a standard deviation of about 7.74, as in the article's table." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Posterior at the candidate 0.035, midway between the runs" ;
    hemo:9000014 "c_1 = 0.4578334; c_2 = 0.4578334; c_12 = 0.043937; mu_0 = 20; y_1 = 20.4382; y_2 = 16.1385; sf2 = 100; a_1 = 0.4386; a_2 = 0.4386; mu_n = 18.4987; var_n = 59.8421" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "posterior-at-the-candidate-0-035-midway-between-the-runs" .

hemo:7002706 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior at an evaluated value, the run at 0.06"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At a run the correlation with it is 1, so the weights are 0 and 1; the posterior mean equals the observed loss of 16.1385 and the variance is 0 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Posterior at an evaluated value, the run at 0.06" ;
    hemo:9000014 "c_1 = 0.043937; c_2 = 1; c_12 = 0.043937; mu_0 = 20; y_1 = 20.4382; y_2 = 16.1385; sf2 = 100; a_1 = 0; a_2 = 1; mu_n = 16.1385; var_n = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "posterior-at-an-evaluated-value-the-run-at-0-06" .

hemo:7002707 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal posterior for the loss at the candidate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The loss at the candidate is normally distributed with mean mu_n and standard deviation s_n, as a Gaussian process gives; at an evaluated value without noise s_n is 0 and the expected improvement is 0." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal posterior for the loss at the candidate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BOPT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-posterior-for-the-loss-at-the-candidate" .

hemo:7002708 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Phi_z evaluated at the z of the same candidate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Phi_z must be the normal distribution function at the z computed from L_best, mu_n and s_n; a value for a rounded or different z changes the result." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Phi_z evaluated at the z of the same candidate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-BOPT-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "phi-z-evaluated-at-the-z-of-the-same-candidate" .

hemo:7002709 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected improvement from named posterior summaries"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000531 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With BestLoss, PostMean and PostSD named, the first formula returns the standardised gap, held in StdGap, and the second the expected improvement, held in ExpImp." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected improvement from named posterior summaries" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-BOPT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-improvement-from-named-posterior-summaries" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(BestLoss-PostMean)/PostSD; =(BestLoss-PostMean)*NORM.S.DIST(StdGap,TRUE)+PostSD*NORM.S.DIST(StdGap,FALSE)" .

hemo:7002710 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected improvement at least the expected gain and never negative"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "ExpImp is at least the larger of BestLoss minus PostMean and 0. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the density term left out (about minus 0.695 at 0.04)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected improvement at least the expected gain and never negative" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BOPT-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-improvement-at-least-the-expected-gain-and-never-negative" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ExpImp>=MAX(BestLoss-PostMean,0)-1E-12" .

hemo:7002711 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected improvement no more than the expected gain plus the peak density times the standard deviation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "ExpImp is at most the larger of BestLoss minus PostMean and 0, plus PostSD times 0.39894, the standard normal density at 0. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the maximisation form applied to a loss, gap PostMean minus BestLoss (about 3.87 against a bound of 2.94 at 0.04)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected improvement no more than the expected gain plus the peak density times the standard deviation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-BOPT-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-improvement-no-more-than-the-expected-gain-plus-the-peak-density-times-the-standard-deviation" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ExpImp<=MAX(BestLoss-PostMean,0)+PostSD*0.39894229+1E-12" .

hemo:7002712 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected improvement at the candidate 0.04 in the article example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The gap 16.1385 minus 17.8394 over 7.3698 gives z of about minus 0.2308, where Phi is about 0.40874; the expected improvement is about minus 0.695 plus 2.863, or 2.1676, as in the article, which rounds z to minus 0.23 and gives 2.17." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected improvement at the candidate 0.04 in the article example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "L_best = 16.1385; mu_n = 17.8394; s_n = 7.3698; Phi_z = 0.40874; z = -0.2308; EI = 2.1676" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-improvement-at-the-candidate-0-04-in-the-article-example" .

hemo:7002713 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected improvement at the candidate 0.05 in the article example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With posterior mean 16.651 and standard deviation 4.6028, z is about minus 0.1113 and Phi about 0.45567, so the expected improvement is about 1.5914 (1.59 in the article's table)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected improvement at the candidate 0.05 in the article example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "L_best = 16.1385; mu_n = 16.651; s_n = 4.6028; Phi_z = 0.45567; z = -0.1113; EI = 1.5914" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-improvement-at-the-candidate-0-05-in-the-article-example" .

hemo:7002714 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected improvement at 0.035 in the second iteration"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "After the run at 0.04 the best loss is 3.5167; at 0.035 the posterior mean is 3.7091 and the standard deviation 1.3888, so z is about minus 0.1385, Phi about 0.44491 and the expected improvement about 0.4632, as in the article (0.46)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected improvement at 0.035 in the second iteration" ;
    hemo:9000014 "L_best = 3.5167; mu_n = 3.7091; s_n = 1.3888; Phi_z = 0.44491; z = -0.1385; EI = 0.4632" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-BOPT-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-improvement-at-0-035-in-the-second-iteration" .

hemo:7002715 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Age-specific use rates held at base-year levels"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Rates do not change between the base year and year t, so the forecast moves only with the size and age mix of the population; scenarios relax this by trending the rates or adjusting them for changes in prevalence or incidence." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Age-specific use rates held at base-year levels" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DFC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "age-specific-use-rates-held-at-base-year-levels" .

hemo:7002716 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Base-year activity measures use under base-year supply"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The rates come from recorded utilisation, which reflects the beds, clinics and gatekeeping of the base year; the forecast is of use under similar supply, not of need." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Base-year activity measures use under base-year supply" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DFC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "base-year-activity-measures-use-under-base-year-supply" .

hemo:7002717 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Age groups cover the whole population once"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The groups do not overlap and together make up the population whose use is forecast." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Age groups cover the whole population once" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DFC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "age-groups-cover-the-whole-population-once" .

hemo:7002718 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Demographic projection from named population and admission ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000532 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With base-year populations and admissions by age group in BasePop and BaseUse and projected populations in ProjPop, the first formula returns the base-year rates, held in UseRates, and the second the forecast, held in Forecast." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Demographic projection from named population and admission ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DFC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "demographic-projection-from-named-population-and-admission-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=BaseUse/BasePop; =SUMPRODUCT(ProjPop,UseRates)" .

hemo:7002719 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Projection equals base-year use scaled by each group's population growth"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Forecast equals the sum over age groups of BaseUse times ProjPop / BasePop. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a single crude rate applied to the whole projected population (23,130 instead of 24,950)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Projection equals base-year use scaled by each group's population growth" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DFC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "projection-equals-base-year-use-scaled-by-each-group-s-population-growth" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(Forecast-SUMPRODUCT(BaseUse,ProjPop/BasePop))<1E-6" .

hemo:7002720 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Projection lies within the range set by the lowest and highest group rates"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Forecast divided by the total projected population is an average of the group rates, so it lies from the lowest to the highest of UseRates. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the rates added across groups before multiplying (257,000 times 0.70, or 179,900)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Projection lies within the range set by the lowest and highest group rates" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DFC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "projection-lies-within-the-range-set-by-the-lowest-and-highest-group-rates" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(Forecast>=SUM(ProjPop)*MIN(UseRates),Forecast<=SUM(ProjPop)*MAX(UseRates))" .

hemo:7002721 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Base-year admissions in the ageing district"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "200,000 people aged 0 to 64 at 0.05, 40,000 aged 65 to 79 at 0.20 and 10,000 aged 80 and over at 0.45 give 10,000, 8,000 and 4,500, a total of 22,500 emergency admissions, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Base-year admissions in the ageing district" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P_1 = 200000; P_2 = 40000; P_3 = 10000; r_1 = 0.05; r_2 = 0.2; r_3 = 0.45; U_t = 22500" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DFC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "base-year-admissions-in-the-ageing-district" .

hemo:7002722 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Year 5 admissions at constant rates in the ageing district"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The projected populations of 198,000, 46,000 and 13,000 give 9,900, 9,200 and 5,850, or 24,950 admissions, 10.9 per cent more while the population grows 2.8 per cent, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Year 5 admissions at constant rates in the ageing district" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P_1 = 198000; P_2 = 46000; P_3 = 13000; r_1 = 0.05; r_2 = 0.2; r_3 = 0.45; U_t = 24950" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DFC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "year-5-admissions-at-constant-rates-in-the-ageing-district" .

hemo:7002723 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Year 5 admissions with lower rates in the older groups"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Lowering the 65 to 79 rate by 5 per cent to 0.19 and the 80 and over rate by 10 per cent to 0.405 gives 23,905 admissions, growth of about 6.2 per cent, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Year 5 admissions with lower rates in the older groups" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P_1 = 198000; P_2 = 46000; P_3 = 13000; r_1 = 0.05; r_2 = 0.19; r_3 = 0.405; U_t = 23905" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DFC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "year-5-admissions-with-lower-rates-in-the-older-groups" .

hemo:7002724 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "No clear trend or seasonal pattern in the smoothed series"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Simple smoothing gives a flat forecast, so it fits series that move around a slowly changing level; trend and seasonal patterns need Holt or seasonal methods." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No clear trend or seasonal pattern in the smoothed series" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DFC-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-clear-trend-or-seasonal-pattern-in-the-smoothed-series" .

hemo:7002725 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Smoothing parameter and starting level estimated from training data"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "alpha and the initial level are chosen by minimising the sum of squared one-step errors over the data used for fitting, then held fixed for the forecast." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Smoothing parameter and starting level estimated from training data" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DFC-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "smoothing-parameter-and-starting-level-estimated-from-training-data" .

hemo:7002726 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Simple exponential smoothing update from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000533 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Alpha, LatestObs and PrevForecast named, the formula returns the next forecast, held in NextForecast." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Simple exponential smoothing update from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DFC-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "simple-exponential-smoothing-update-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Alpha*LatestObs+(1-Alpha)*PrevForecast" .

hemo:7002727 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Smoothing update equals the error-correction form"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "NextForecast equals PrevForecast plus Alpha times (LatestObs minus PrevForecast). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the weights swapped, 0.7 on the observation (2,070 instead of 2,030)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Smoothing update equals the error-correction form" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DFC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "smoothing-update-equals-the-error-correction-form" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(NextForecast-(PrevForecast+Alpha*(LatestObs-PrevForecast)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002728 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Smoothed forecast lies between the latest observation and the previous forecast"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "NextForecast is no lower than the smaller and no higher than the larger of LatestObs and PrevForecast. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows Alpha entered as a percentage, 30 (5,000)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Smoothed forecast lies between the latest observation and the previous forecast" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DFC-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "smoothed-forecast-lies-between-the-latest-observation-and-the-previous-forecast" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(NextForecast>=MIN(LatestObs,PrevForecast),NextForecast<=MAX(LatestObs,PrevForecast))" .

hemo:7002729 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Monthly emergency admissions with a smoothing parameter of 0.3"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If 2,100 admissions were observed against a forecast of 2,000, the next forecast is 0.3 times 2,100 plus 0.7 times 2,000, or 2,030 (figures illustrative)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Monthly emergency admissions with a smoothing parameter of 0.3" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.3; y_t = 2100; yhat_t = 2000; yhat_next = 2030" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DFC-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "monthly-emergency-admissions-with-a-smoothing-parameter-of-0-3" .

hemo:7002730 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Monthly emergency admissions with a smoothing parameter of 0.8"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha of 0.8 the same month moves the forecast to 2,080, following the latest observation more closely (figures illustrative)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Monthly emergency admissions with a smoothing parameter of 0.8" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.8; y_t = 2100; yhat_t = 2000; yhat_next = 2080" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DFC-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "monthly-emergency-admissions-with-a-smoothing-parameter-of-0-8" .

hemo:7002731 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "A month below forecast with a smoothing parameter of 0.3"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If only 1,900 admissions were observed against a forecast of 2,000, the next forecast falls to 1,970 (figures illustrative)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "A month below forecast with a smoothing parameter of 0.3" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.3; y_t = 1900; yhat_t = 2000; yhat_next = 1970" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DFC-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "a-month-below-forecast-with-a-smoothing-parameter-of-0-3" .

hemo:7002732 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Test periods not used to fit the forecasting method"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Accuracy is measured on data held back from fitting; errors on the training data overstate how well the method forecasts." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Test periods not used to fit the forecasting method" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DFC-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "test-periods-not-used-to-fit-the-forecasting-method" .

hemo:7002733 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Observed values above zero for the percentage error"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every observed value in the test periods is positive and the data have a meaningful zero; otherwise the MAPE is undefined or misleading and the MAE or a scaled error is used." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Observed values above zero for the percentage error" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DFC-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "observed-values-above-zero-for-the-percentage-error" .

hemo:7002734 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "MAE and MAPE from named observed and forecast ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000534 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the test-period observations in TestObs and the forecasts in Forecasts, the formulas return the mean absolute error and the mean absolute percentage error, held in MeanAbsErr and MeanAbsPctErr (dynamic-array Excel; older versions need array entry)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "MAE and MAPE from named observed and forecast ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DFC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mae-and-mape-from-named-observed-and-forecast-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AVERAGE(ABS(TestObs-Forecasts)); =100*AVERAGE(ABS((TestObs-Forecasts)/TestObs))" .

hemo:7002735 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mean absolute error averages the unsigned errors"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "MeanAbsErr equals SUMPRODUCT(ABS(TestObs minus Forecasts)) over COUNT(TestObs). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows signed errors averaged, which lets errors cancel (46.67 instead of 80)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mean absolute error averages the unsigned errors" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DFC-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mean-absolute-error-averages-the-unsigned-errors" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(MeanAbsErr-SUMPRODUCT(ABS(TestObs-Forecasts))/COUNT(TestObs))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002736 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Percentage errors divide by observed values that are all above zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every observed value is non-zero and MeanAbsPctErr equals 100 times the average of the absolute errors divided by the observed values. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows errors divided by the forecasts (3.94 instead of 3.74 per cent) or a zero count in the test periods." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Percentage errors divide by observed values that are all above zero" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DFC-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "percentage-errors-divide-by-observed-values-that-are-all-above-zero" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(MIN(ABS(TestObs))>0,ABS(MeanAbsPctErr-100*SUMPRODUCT(ABS(TestObs-Forecasts)/ABS(TestObs))/COUNT(TestObs))<1E-9,FALSE)" .

hemo:7002737 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three months of admissions against a flat forecast of 2,030"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Observed admissions of 2,050, 1,980 and 2,200 give errors of 20, minus 50 and 170, an MAE of 80 admissions and a MAPE of about 3.7427 per cent (figures illustrative)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three months of admissions against a flat forecast of 2,030" ;
    hemo:9000014 "y_1 = 2050; y_2 = 1980; y_3 = 2200; f_1 = 2030; f_2 = 2030; f_3 = 2030; e_1 = 20; e_2 = -50; e_3 = 170; MAE = 80; MAPE = 3.7427" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DFC-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-months-of-admissions-against-a-flat-forecast-of-2-030" .

hemo:7002738 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three months of a rare procedure against a flat forecast of 2.5"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Counts of 2, 1 and 4 give errors of minus 0.5, minus 1.5 and 1.5, an MAE of about 1.1667 procedures but a MAPE of about 70.8333 per cent, driven by the month with a count of 1 (figures illustrative)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three months of a rare procedure against a flat forecast of 2.5" ;
    hemo:9000014 "y_1 = 2; y_2 = 1; y_3 = 4; f_1 = 2.5; f_2 = 2.5; f_3 = 2.5; e_1 = -0.5; e_2 = -1.5; e_3 = 1.5; MAE = 1.1667; MAPE = 70.8333" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DFC-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-months-of-a-rare-procedure-against-a-flat-forecast-of-2-5" .

hemo:7002739 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Reference standard taken as correct in the accuracy table"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each person's true status is the reference standard result, so the measures describe agreement with that standard; when the standard is imperfect the estimates can differ from true accuracy." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reference standard taken as correct in the accuracy table" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reference-standard-taken-as-correct-in-the-accuracy-table" .

hemo:7002740 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One threshold and one population behind the four cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "All four counts come from the same people tested at the same positivity threshold; moving the threshold raises one of sensitivity and specificity and lowers the other." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One threshold and one population behind the four cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-threshold-and-one-population-behind-the-four-cells" .

hemo:7002741 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Predictive values tied to the study sample's prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "PPV and NPV read from the table carry the sample prevalence, (TP + FN) over all four counts; they apply elsewhere only if the prevalence is the same, otherwise HE-FM-DXA-003 recomputes them." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Predictive values tied to the study sample's prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "predictive-values-tied-to-the-study-sample-s-prevalence" .

hemo:7002742 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Sensitivity, specificity and predictive values from named counts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000535 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the four counts named TruePos, FalseNeg, TrueNeg and FalsePos, the formulas return sensitivity, specificity and the two predictive values, held in Sens, Spec, PosPredValue and NegPredValue." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sensitivity, specificity and predictive values from named counts" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DXA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sensitivity-specificity-and-predictive-values-from-named-counts" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=TruePos/(TruePos+FalseNeg); =TrueNeg/(TrueNeg+FalsePos); =TruePos/(TruePos+FalsePos); =TrueNeg/(TrueNeg+FalseNeg)" .

hemo:7002743 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive predictive value from the table agrees with Bayes' theorem"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "PosPredValue equals Sens times the number with the condition divided by (Sens times that number plus (1 minus Spec) times the number without it). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a measure taken from the wrong row or column: with Sens entered as 48 of 276 (the PPV) the check returns FALSE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive predictive value from the table agrees with Bayes' theorem" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DXA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-predictive-value-from-the-table-agrees-with-bayes-theorem" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PosPredValue-Sens*(TruePos+FalseNeg)/(Sens*(TruePos+FalseNeg)+(1-Spec)*(TrueNeg+FalsePos)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002744 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Negative predictive value from the table agrees with Bayes' theorem"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "NegPredValue equals Spec times the number without the condition divided by (Spec times that number plus (1 minus Sens) times the number with it). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows specificity computed along the row as TrueNeg / (TrueNeg plus FalseNeg), 0.9972 for test A." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Negative predictive value from the table agrees with Bayes' theorem" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DXA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "negative-predictive-value-from-the-table-agrees-with-bayes-theorem" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(NegPredValue-Spec*(TrueNeg+FalsePos)/(Spec*(TrueNeg+FalsePos)+(1-Sens)*(TruePos+FalseNeg)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002745 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Triage test A in 1,000 people at 5 per cent prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Of 50 people with the condition, 48 test positive; of 950 without it, 722 test negative. Sensitivity is 0.96 and specificity 0.76; only 48 of the 276 positive results are cases, a PPV of about 0.1739, and 722 of the 724 negative results are correct, an NPV of about 0.9972, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Triage test A in 1,000 people at 5 per cent prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "TP = 48; FN = 2; TN = 722; FP = 228; Se = 0.96; Sp = 0.76; PPV = 0.1739; NPV = 0.9972" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "triage-test-a-in-1-000-people-at-5-per-cent-prevalence" .

hemo:7002746 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Triage test B in 1,000 people at 5 per cent prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Test B finds 40 of the 50 cases and clears 912 of the 950 non-cases: sensitivity 0.80, specificity 0.96, PPV 40 of 78 or about 0.5128, NPV 912 of 922 or about 0.9892, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Triage test B in 1,000 people at 5 per cent prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "TP = 40; FN = 10; TN = 912; FP = 38; Se = 0.8; Sp = 0.96; PPV = 0.5128; NPV = 0.9892" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "triage-test-b-in-1-000-people-at-5-per-cent-prevalence" .

hemo:7002747 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Sensitivity and specificity from the same study and threshold for likelihood ratios"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both proportions come from one two-by-two table at one threshold, so the ratios describe one way of using the test." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sensitivity and specificity from the same study and threshold for likelihood ratios" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sensitivity-and-specificity-from-the-same-study-and-threshold-for-likelihood-ratios" .

hemo:7002748 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "No empty cells for finite likelihood ratios"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "LR_pos has no finite value when Sp is 1, LR_neg is undefined when Sp is 0, and DOR is 0 or has no finite value when any cell of the table is 0; the formulas need Se and Sp strictly above 0 and below 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No empty cells for finite likelihood ratios" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-empty-cells-for-finite-likelihood-ratios" .

hemo:7002749 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Likelihood ratios and diagnostic odds ratio from named sensitivity and specificity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000536 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Sens and Spec named, the formulas return the positive and negative likelihood ratios and the diagnostic odds ratio, held in LRPos, LRNeg and DiagOR." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Likelihood ratios and diagnostic odds ratio from named sensitivity and specificity" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DXA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "likelihood-ratios-and-diagnostic-odds-ratio-from-named-sensitivity-and-specificity" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Sens/(1-Spec); =(1-Sens)/Spec; =LRPos/LRNeg" .

hemo:7002750 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Diagnostic odds ratio agrees with its cross-product form"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "DiagOR equals Sens times Spec divided by ((1 minus Sens) times (1 minus Spec)), the form estimated by TP times TN over FP times FN. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the two ratios multiplied instead of divided (4 times 0.0526, about 0.21, for test A)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Diagnostic odds ratio agrees with its cross-product form" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DXA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "diagnostic-odds-ratio-agrees-with-its-cross-product-form" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(DiagOR/(Sens*Spec/((1-Sens)*(1-Spec)))-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002751 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Informative test has a positive ratio above one and a negative ratio below one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When Sens plus Spec exceeds 1, LRPos is above 1 and LRNeg below 1; otherwise neither holds. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the negative ratio inverted as Spec / (1 minus Sens), which gives 19 for test A." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Informative test has a positive ratio above one and a negative ratio below one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DXA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "informative-test-has-a-positive-ratio-above-one-and-a-negative-ratio-below-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(Sens+Spec>1,AND(LRPos>1,LRNeg<1),AND(LRPos<=1,LRNeg>=1))" .

hemo:7002752 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Likelihood ratios of triage test A"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With sensitivity 0.96 and specificity 0.76, LR_pos is 0.96 over 0.24, or 4.0, LR_neg is 0.04 over 0.76, about 0.0526, and the DOR is 76, as in the article. At 5 per cent prevalence the pre-test odds of about 0.0526 times 4 give post-test odds of about 0.2105, a post-test probability of 0.1739, the PPV of HE-FM-DXA-001." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Likelihood ratios of triage test A" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Se = 0.96; Sp = 0.76; LR_pos = 4; LR_neg = 0.0526; DOR = 76" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "likelihood-ratios-of-triage-test-a" .

hemo:7002753 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Likelihood ratios of triage test B"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With sensitivity 0.80 and specificity 0.96, LR_pos is 20, LR_neg about 0.2083 and the DOR 96, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Likelihood ratios of triage test B" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Se = 0.8; Sp = 0.96; LR_pos = 20; LR_neg = 0.2083; DOR = 96" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "likelihood-ratios-of-triage-test-b" .

hemo:7002754 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Sensitivity and specificity transfer to the target population"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The formulas move only prevalence; if the case mix or position in the pathway differs, sensitivity and specificity may change too and need their own estimates." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sensitivity and specificity transfer to the target population" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sensitivity-and-specificity-transfer-to-the-target-population" .

hemo:7002755 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Prevalence of the people actually tested"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "p is the pre-test probability in the population tested, not the share of cases in an enriched or case-control validation sample." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prevalence of the people actually tested" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prevalence-of-the-people-actually-tested" .

hemo:7002756 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Predictive values at a stated prevalence from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000537 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Sens, Spec and Prev named, the formulas return the positive and negative predictive values, held in PPVPrev and NPVPrev." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Predictive values at a stated prevalence from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DXA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "predictive-values-at-a-stated-prevalence-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Sens*Prev/(Sens*Prev+(1-Spec)*(1-Prev)); =Spec*(1-Prev)/(Spec*(1-Prev)+(1-Sens)*Prev)" .

hemo:7002757 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Post-test odds of a positive result equal pre-test odds times the positive likelihood ratio"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "PPVPrev / (1 minus PPVPrev) equals Prev / (1 minus Prev) times Sens / (1 minus Spec). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows prevalence left out, for example PPVPrev set equal to Sens." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Post-test odds of a positive result equal pre-test odds times the positive likelihood ratio" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DXA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "post-test-odds-of-a-positive-result-equal-pre-test-odds-times-the-positive-likelihood-ratio" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PPVPrev/(1-PPVPrev)-Prev/(1-Prev)*Sens/(1-Spec))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002758 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Post-test odds of a negative result equal pre-test odds times the negative likelihood ratio"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "(1 minus NPVPrev) / NPVPrev equals Prev / (1 minus Prev) times (1 minus Sens) / Spec. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows NPVPrev set equal to Spec or to the study's NPV at another prevalence." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Post-test odds of a negative result equal pre-test odds times the negative likelihood ratio" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DXA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "post-test-odds-of-a-negative-result-equal-pre-test-odds-times-the-negative-likelihood-ratio" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((1-NPVPrev)/NPVPrev-Prev/(1-Prev)*(1-Sens)/Spec)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002759 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Triage test A at 5 per cent prevalence by Bayes' theorem"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "0.96 times 0.05 is 0.048 against 0.24 times 0.95, or 0.228, so PPV is about 0.1739 and NPV about 0.9972, matching the counts in HE-FM-DXA-001." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Triage test A at 5 per cent prevalence by Bayes' theorem" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Se = 0.96; Sp = 0.76; p = 0.05; PPV = 0.1739; NPV = 0.9972" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "triage-test-a-at-5-per-cent-prevalence-by-bayes-theorem" .

hemo:7002760 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Triage tests A and B at 2 per cent prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At 2 per cent prevalence test A's PPV falls to about 0.0755 (NPV 0.9989), while test B's is about 0.2899 (NPV 0.9958) (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Triage tests A and B at 2 per cent prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Se = 0.96; Sp = 0.76; p = 0.02; PPV = 0.0755; NPV = 0.9989" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "triage-tests-a-and-b-at-2-per-cent-prevalence" .

hemo:7002761 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Claims algorithm validated at 90 per cent sensitivity and 95 per cent specificity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Applied where the true prevalence is 2 per cent, the algorithm's PPV is 0.018 over 0.067, about 0.2687, as on the Criterion Validity page; in that page's validation sample, with 20 per cent cases, it is about 0.8182." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Claims algorithm validated at 90 per cent sensitivity and 95 per cent specificity" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Se = 0.9; Sp = 0.95; p = 0.02; PPV = 0.2687; NPV = 0.9979" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "claims-algorithm-validated-at-90-per-cent-sensitivity-and-95-per-cent-specificity" .

hemo:7002762 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Both kinds of error weighted equally in the proportion correct"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A false negative and a false positive each count as one wrong result, whatever their consequences." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Both kinds of error weighted equally in the proportion correct" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "both-kinds-of-error-weighted-equally-in-the-proportion-correct" .

hemo:7002763 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Prevalence of the population in which correctness is counted"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The result applies only at the prevalence p; the same test has a different proportion correct elsewhere." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prevalence of the population in which correctness is counted" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prevalence-of-the-population-in-which-correctness-is-counted" .

hemo:7002764 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Proportion correct from named prevalence, sensitivity and specificity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000538 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Prev, Sens and Spec named, the formula returns the proportion of correct results, held in PropCorrect." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Proportion correct from named prevalence, sensitivity and specificity" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DXA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "proportion-correct-from-named-prevalence-sensitivity-and-specificity" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Prev*Sens+(1-Prev)*Spec" .

hemo:7002765 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Proportion correct lies within the range set by sensitivity and specificity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "As a weighted average, PropCorrect is no smaller than the lower and no larger than the higher of Sens and Spec. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows Youden's index, Sens plus Spec minus 1 (0.72 for test A), reported as accuracy." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Proportion correct lies within the range set by sensitivity and specificity" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DXA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "proportion-correct-lies-within-the-range-set-by-sensitivity-and-specificity" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(PropCorrect>=MIN(Sens,Spec)-1E-12,PropCorrect<=MAX(Sens,Spec)+1E-12)" .

hemo:7002766 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gap between proportion correct and specificity equals prevalence times the gap from sensitivity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "PropCorrect minus Spec equals Prev times (Sens minus Spec). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the weights swapped, prevalence applied to specificity (0.95 instead of 0.770 for test A)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gap between proportion correct and specificity equals prevalence times the gap from sensitivity" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DXA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gap-between-proportion-correct-and-specificity-equals-prevalence-times-the-gap-from-sensitivity" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PropCorrect-Spec-Prev*(Sens-Spec))<1E-12" .

hemo:7002767 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Proportion correct of the two triage tests at 5 per cent prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Test A scores 0.048 plus 0.722, or 0.770, and test B 0.040 plus 0.912, or 0.952, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Proportion correct of the two triage tests at 5 per cent prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p = 0.05; Se = 0.96; Sp = 0.76; Acc = 0.77" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "proportion-correct-of-the-two-triage-tests-at-5-per-cent-prevalence" .

hemo:7002768 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Rule that calls everyone negative at 5 per cent prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With sensitivity 0 and specificity 1 the proportion correct is 0.95, barely below test B's 0.952, as the article notes." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rule that calls everyone negative at 5 per cent prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p = 0.05; Se = 0; Sp = 1; Acc = 0.95" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rule-that-calls-everyone-negative-at-5-per-cent-prevalence" .

hemo:7002769 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Missed cases and true negatives fare as without testing"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A false negative leads to the same care and outcomes as no testing and a true negative to no consequences, so only true and false positives change value; any harm from a missed case beyond that, or anxiety from a false positive, would need its own term." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Missed cases and true negatives fare as without testing" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "missed-cases-and-true-negatives-fare-as-without-testing" .

hemo:7002770 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Gain and loss valued per person at a stated value of health"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "G is the QALY gain of a treated case times the value of a QALY minus treatment and confirmation costs; in the article 1 QALY at 25,000 pounds, the lower end of NICE's range, less 3,000 and 400, gives 21,600. No discounting or time horizon is modelled." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gain and loss valued per person at a stated value of health" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gain-and-loss-valued-per-person-at-a-stated-value-of-health" .

hemo:7002771 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Every positive triage result confirmed by a perfect test"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "All positives go on to a confirmatory test assumed perfect, so false positives are cleared at cost L and true positives are treated." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Every positive triage result confirmed by a perfect test" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DXA-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "every-positive-triage-result-confirmed-by-a-perfect-test" .

hemo:7002772 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Net monetary benefit of a triage test from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000539 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Prev, Sens, Spec, GainTP, LossFP and TestCost named, the formula returns the net monetary benefit per person tested, held in NMBTest." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net monetary benefit of a triage test from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DXA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-monetary-benefit-of-a-triage-test-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Prev*Sens*GainTP-(1-Prev)*(1-Spec)*LossFP-TestCost" .

hemo:7002773 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Triage test net benefit no higher than that of a perfect test"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "NMBTest is at most Prev times GainTP minus TestCost, the value of finding every case with no false positives. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the false positive cost added instead of subtracted (1,088 against a bound of 1,040 for test A at 5 per cent)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Triage test net benefit no higher than that of a perfect test" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DXA-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "triage-test-net-benefit-no-higher-than-that-of-a-perfect-test" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=NMBTest<=Prev*GainTP-TestCost+1E-9" .

hemo:7002774 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Triage test net benefit no lower than the worst case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "NMBTest is at least minus TestCost minus (1 minus Prev) times LossFP, the result if no case were found and every non-case tested positive. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows GainTP and LossFP swapped (about minus 4,946 against a bound of minus 420)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Triage test net benefit no lower than the worst case" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DXA-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "triage-test-net-benefit-no-lower-than-the-worst-case" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=NMBTest>=-TestCost-(1-Prev)*LossFP-1E-9" .

hemo:7002775 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Triage test net benefit equals the gain times decision-curve net benefit less the test cost"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the decision-curve threshold set to LossFP / (GainTP plus LossFP), (NMBTest plus TestCost) / GainTP equals the true positive share Prev times Sens minus the false positive share (1 minus Prev) times (1 minus Spec) times the threshold odds, threshold / (1 minus threshold). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows LossFP left out of NMBTest (0.048 against 0.0438 for test A at 5 per cent)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Triage test net benefit equals the gain times decision-curve net benefit less the test cost" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DXA-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "triage-test-net-benefit-equals-the-gain-times-decision-curve-net-benefit-less-the-test-cost" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((NMBTest+TestCost)/GainTP-(Prev*Sens-(1-Prev)*(1-Spec)*(LossFP/(GainTP+LossFP))/(1-LossFP/(GainTP+LossFP))))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002776 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Triage test A at 5 per cent prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "0.05 times 0.96 times 21,600 is 1,036.8, 0.95 times 0.24 times 400 is 91.2, and minus the 40 pound test the net monetary benefit is 905.6 pounds per person, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Triage test A at 5 per cent prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p = 0.05; Se = 0.96; Sp = 0.76; G = 21600; L = 400; c = 40; NMB = 905.6" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "triage-test-a-at-5-per-cent-prevalence" .

hemo:7002777 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Triage test B at 5 per cent prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "864 minus 15.2 minus 40 gives 808.8 pounds per person, 96.80 pounds less than test A, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Triage test B at 5 per cent prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p = 0.05; Se = 0.8; Sp = 0.96; G = 21600; L = 400; c = 40; NMB = 808.8" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "triage-test-b-at-5-per-cent-prevalence" .

hemo:7002778 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Triage test A at 2 per cent prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "414.72 minus 94.08 minus 40 gives 280.64 pounds, below test B's 289.92 at the same prevalence, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Triage test A at 2 per cent prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p = 0.02; Se = 0.96; Sp = 0.76; G = 21600; L = 400; c = 40; NMB = 280.64" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DXA-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "triage-test-a-at-2-per-cent-prevalence" .

hemo:7002779 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One time origin for the entry time and the later time"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both survival probabilities are measured from the same origin, such as diagnosis, and t is at or after l." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One time origin for the entry time and the later time" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-LTR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-time-origin-for-the-entry-time-and-the-later-time" .

hemo:7002780 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Entrants share the survival function of the cohort from the origin"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Event time and entry time are independent given that the event time exceeds entry, so late entrants are representative of everyone still event free at their entry time; this can and should be tested." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Entrants share the survival function of the cohort from the origin" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-LTR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "entrants-share-the-survival-function-of-the-cohort-from-the-origin" .

hemo:7002781 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Conditional survival from named survival probabilities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000540 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With SurvT and SurvL named, the formula returns survival beyond t given survival to entry, held in CondSurv." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Conditional survival from named survival probabilities" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-LTR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "conditional-survival-from-named-survival-probabilities" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SurvT/SurvL" .

hemo:7002782 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Conditional survival at least the unconditional survival and at most one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Because SurvL is at most 1 and at least SurvT, CondSurv lies from SurvT up to 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the two probabilities multiplied (0.125 for the registry example) or swapped (about 3.56)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Conditional survival at least the unconditional survival and at most one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-LTR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "conditional-survival-at-least-the-unconditional-survival-and-at-most-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(CondSurv>=SurvT-1E-12,CondSurv<=1+1E-12)" .

hemo:7002783 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Conditional survival times survival to entry recovers survival from the origin"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "CondSurv times SurvL equals SurvT. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the difference SurvL minus SurvT used in place of the ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Conditional survival times survival to entry recovers survival from the origin" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-LTR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "conditional-survival-times-survival-to-entry-recovers-survival-from-the-origin" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(CondSurv*SurvL-SurvT)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002784 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Surviving to 33 months after entry at 12 months in the registry example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "From the corrected Kaplan-Meier curve, survival is 0.1875 at 33 months and 0.6667 at 12 months, so a patient entering at 12 months has a probability of about 0.2812 of surviving to 33 months (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Surviving to 33 months after entry at 12 months in the registry example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_t = 0.1875; S_l = 0.6667; S_cond = 0.2812" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-LTR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "surviving-to-33-months-after-entry-at-12-months-in-the-registry-example" .

hemo:7002785 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Conditional survival under a constant hazard"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a constant hazard of 0.1 a year, survival is 0.1353 at 20 years and 0.2231 at 15, so a person entering at 15 years survives 5 more with probability about 0.6065, the same as a new person over 5 years (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Conditional survival under a constant hazard" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_t = 0.1353; S_l = 0.2231; S_cond = 0.6065" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-LTR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "conditional-survival-under-a-constant-hazard" .

hemo:7002786 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Entry and event times independent in the risk-set correction"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The corrected risk sets estimate survival from the origin only if entry time and event time are independent given that the event comes after entry; the correction fixes the denominators, not the selection." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Entry and event times independent in the risk-set correction" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-LTR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "entry-and-event-times-independent-in-the-risk-set-correction" .

hemo:7002787 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Follow-up intervals open at entry and closed at exit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Someone entering exactly at t_j is not at risk at t_j, and someone exiting at t_j is; censoring at t_j is treated as after the event." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Follow-up intervals open at entry and closed at exit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-LTR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "follow-up-intervals-open-at-entry-and-closed-at-exit" .

hemo:7002788 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Entry-restricted risk set and survival step from named ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000541 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With entry and exit times in EntryTimes and ExitTimes and EventTime, Deaths and SurvPrev named, the first formula returns the number at risk, held in AtRisk, and the second the survival after the step, held in SurvNew." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Entry-restricted risk set and survival step from named ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-LTR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "entry-restricted-risk-set-and-survival-step-from-named-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=COUNTIF(EntryTimes,\"<\"&EventTime)-COUNTIF(ExitTimes,\"<\"&EventTime); =SurvPrev*(1-Deaths/AtRisk)" .

hemo:7002789 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Risk set equals the records open at the event time"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "AtRisk equals the number of records with entry before EventTime and exit at or after it. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows entry times ignored (6 instead of 3 at month 6)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Risk set equals the records open at the event time" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-LTR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "risk-set-equals-the-records-open-at-the-event-time" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AtRisk=COUNTIFS(EntryTimes,\"<\"&EventTime,ExitTimes,\">=\"&EventTime)" .

hemo:7002790 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Left-truncated survival step carried forward from the previous level"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "SurvNew is no higher than SurvPrev, not below zero, and equals SurvPrev times (AtRisk minus Deaths) over AtRisk. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows survival not carried forward, 0.75 at month 18 against a previous 0.6667." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Left-truncated survival step carried forward from the previous level" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-LTR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "left-truncated-survival-step-carried-forward-from-the-previous-level" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(SurvNew<=SurvPrev,SurvNew>=0,ABS(SurvNew*AtRisk-SurvPrev*(AtRisk-Deaths))<1E-9)" .

hemo:7002791 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Risk set at month 6 in the six-patient registry example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At month 6 only A, B and C have entered and none has left, so 3 are at risk; one death gives survival of 2 out of 3, about 0.6667, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Risk set at month 6 in the six-patient registry example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_in = 3; N_out = 0; d_j = 1; S_prev = 1; n_j = 3; S_j = 0.6667" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-LTR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "risk-set-at-month-6-in-the-six-patient-registry-example" .

hemo:7002792 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Risk set at month 18 in the six-patient registry example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "By month 18 five patients have entered (F enters at 20) and A has left, so 4 are at risk; survival falls from 0.6667 to 0.5, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Risk set at month 18 in the six-patient registry example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_in = 5; N_out = 1; d_j = 1; S_prev = 0.6667; n_j = 4; S_j = 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-LTR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "risk-set-at-month-18-in-the-six-patient-registry-example" .

hemo:7002793 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Risk set at month 33 in the six-patient registry example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "All six have entered and A, B, D and C have left, so E and F are at risk; survival falls from 0.375 to 0.1875, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Risk set at month 33 in the six-patient registry example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_in = 6; N_out = 4; d_j = 1; S_prev = 0.375; n_j = 2; S_j = 0.1875" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-LTR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "risk-set-at-month-33-in-the-six-patient-registry-example" .

hemo:7002794 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Month 6 when entry times are ignored"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Counting everyone from diagnosis puts all six at risk at month 6, so survival is 5 out of 6, about 0.8333 instead of 0.6667, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Month 6 when entry times are ignored" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_in = 6; N_out = 0; d_j = 1; S_prev = 1; n_j = 6; S_j = 0.8333" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-LTR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "month-6-when-entry-times-are-ignored" .

hemo:7002795 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant hazard from the time origin"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The hazard is the same at every time since the origin, so time before entry carries no information once the entry term is included; with a changing hazard the Weibull form of HE-FM-LTR-004 or another distribution is needed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant hazard from the time origin" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-LTR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-hazard-from-the-time-origin" .

hemo:7002796 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Independent entry for the exponential fit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Entry times are independent of event times given that events follow entry, as for the risk-set correction." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Independent entry for the exponential fit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-LTR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "independent-entry-for-the-exponential-fit" .

hemo:7002797 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Exponential rate and mean from named entry, exit and status ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000542 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With EntryTimes, ExitTimes and Status named, the first formula returns the rate, held in ExpRate, and the second the mean, held in ExpMeanTime." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exponential rate and mean from named entry, exit and status ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-LTR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exponential-rate-and-mean-from-named-entry-exit-and-status-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUM(Status)/(SUM(ExitTimes)-SUM(EntryTimes)); =1/ExpRate" .

hemo:7002798 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Exponential rate maximises the left-truncated log-likelihood"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The log-likelihood SUM(Status) times LN(rate) minus rate times the person-time from entry is higher at ExpRate than at 1 per cent above or below it. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows person-time counted from the origin (a rate of 0.0272 is not the maximum)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exponential rate maximises the left-truncated log-likelihood" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-LTR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exponential-rate-maximises-the-left-truncated-log-likelihood" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(SUM(Status)*LN(ExpRate)-ExpRate*(SUM(ExitTimes)-SUM(EntryTimes))>SUM(Status)*LN(1.01*ExpRate)-1.01*ExpRate*(SUM(ExitTimes)-SUM(EntryTimes)),SUM(Status)*LN(ExpRate)-ExpRate*(SUM(ExitTimes)-SUM(EntryTimes))>SUM(Status)*LN(0.99*ExpRate)-0.99*ExpRate*(SUM(ExitTimes)-SUM(EntryTimes)))" .

hemo:7002799 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fitted exponential survival at the mean time is exp(-1)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "EXP(minus ExpRate times ExpMeanTime) equals EXP(minus 1), about 0.368. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the median, LN(2) / ExpRate, reported as the mean (survival 0.5 there)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fitted exponential survival at the mean time is exp(-1)" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-LTR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fitted-exponential-survival-at-the-mean-time-is-exp-1" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(EXP(-ExpRate*ExpMeanTime)-EXP(-1))<1E-12" .

hemo:7002800 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Exponential rate for the six registry patients"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Four deaths over 103 person-months from entry give a rate of about 0.0388 per month, about 0.47 per person-year as in the article, and a mean of 25.75 months (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exponential rate for the six registry patients" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 4; PT = 103; lambda = 0.0388; T_mean = 25.75" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-LTR-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exponential-rate-for-the-six-registry-patients" .

hemo:7002801 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Exponential rate when person-time is counted from diagnosis"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Counting from diagnosis gives 147 person-months, a rate of about 0.0272 per month (0.33 per person-year, as in the article) and a mean of 36.75 months, 11 months longer (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exponential rate when person-time is counted from diagnosis" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 4; PT = 147; lambda = 0.0272; T_mean = 36.75" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-LTR-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exponential-rate-when-person-time-is-counted-from-diagnosis" .

hemo:7002802 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weibull form for the survival curve from the origin"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Survival from the origin follows S(t) = exp(minus (t / b)^k) with the shape and scale shared by everyone in the group; other distributions change the density and survival terms but keep the entry term minus log S(L_i)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weibull form for the survival curve from the origin" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-LTR-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weibull-form-for-the-survival-curve-from-the-origin" .

hemo:7002803 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Independent entry and one record per person"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Entry is independent of the event time given that the event follows entry; a person with a gap in observation contributes one such term per observed interval." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Independent entry and one record per person" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-LTR-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "independent-entry-and-one-record-per-person" .

hemo:7002804 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Weibull contribution of a left-truncated record from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000543 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With EventFlag, Shape, Scale, ExitTime and EntryTime named, the formula returns the log-likelihood contribution, held in LogLikI; summing it over records and maximising with Solver over Shape and Scale fits the curve." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weibull contribution of a left-truncated record from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-LTR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weibull-contribution-of-a-left-truncated-record-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EventFlag*(LN(Shape/Scale)+(Shape-1)*LN(ExitTime/Scale))-(ExitTime/Scale)^Shape+(EntryTime/Scale)^Shape" .

hemo:7002805 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Entry term raises the contribution of a late entrant"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For EntryTime above 0, LogLikI exceeds the same expression without the entry term, and equals it when EntryTime is 0. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the entry term left out or subtracted." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Entry term raises the contribution of a late entrant" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-LTR-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "entry-term-raises-the-contribution-of-a-late-entrant" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(EntryTime>0,LogLikI>EventFlag*(LN(Shape/Scale)+(Shape-1)*LN(ExitTime/Scale))-(ExitTime/Scale)^Shape,ABS(LogLikI-(EventFlag*(LN(Shape/Scale)+(Shape-1)*LN(ExitTime/Scale))-(ExitTime/Scale)^Shape))<1E-12)" .

hemo:7002806 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Contribution equals the log of the density or survival conditional on entry"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "EXP(LogLikI) equals the Weibull density (for an event) or survival (for censoring) at ExitTime divided by survival at EntryTime. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the sign of the entry term reversed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Contribution equals the log of the density or survival conditional on entry" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-LTR-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "contribution-equals-the-log-of-the-density-or-survival-conditional-on-entry" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(EXP(LogLikI)-IF(EventFlag=1,Shape/Scale*(ExitTime/Scale)^(Shape-1),1)*EXP(-(ExitTime/Scale)^Shape)/EXP(-(EntryTime/Scale)^Shape))<1E-12" .

hemo:7002807 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient F entering at 20 months and dying at 33 months"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With shape 1.2 and scale 30 months, the contribution is about minus 3.7062 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient F entering at 20 months and dying at 33 months" ;
    hemo:9000014 "delta_i = 1; k = 1.2; b = 30; X_i = 33; L_i = 20; l_i = -3.7062" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-LTR-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-f-entering-at-20-months-and-dying-at-33-months" .

hemo:7002808 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient F with the entry term left out"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Setting the entry time to 0 drops (20 / 30)^1.2, about 0.6147, and gives about minus 4.3210, the contribution of a patient observed from diagnosis (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient F with the entry term left out" ;
    hemo:9000014 "delta_i = 1; k = 1.2; b = 30; X_i = 33; L_i = 0; l_i = -4.321" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-LTR-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-f-with-the-entry-term-left-out" .

hemo:7002809 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient E entering at 12 months and censored at 36 months"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A censored record contributes log survival to 36 months minus log survival to 12 months, about minus 0.9115 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient E entering at 12 months and censored at 36 months" ;
    hemo:9000014 "delta_i = 0; k = 1.2; b = 30; X_i = 36; L_i = 12; l_i = -0.9115" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-LTR-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-e-entering-at-12-months-and-censored-at-36-months" .

hemo:7002810 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Linear cost of care in the mixed payment model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Total cost is c times q, the simple case Ellis and McGuire focus on; with rising marginal cost the reimbursed part becomes r times total cost and the margin no longer falls at a constant rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Linear cost of care in the mixed payment model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CTH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "linear-cost-of-care-in-the-mixed-payment-model" .

hemo:7002811 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Payment based only on verifiable cost and case counts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both parts of the payment depend on things the payer can verify, the case and its recorded cost; the patient benefit that the provider weighs (HE-FM-CTH-002) does not enter the payment." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Payment based only on verifiable cost and case counts" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CTH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "payment-based-only-on-verifiable-cost-and-case-counts" .

hemo:7002812 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Revenue and margin per case from named payment parameters"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000544 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With ProspAmt, ReimbShare, UnitCost and CareUnits named, the formulas return revenue per case and the provider margin, held in CaseRevenue and CaseMargin." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Revenue and margin per case from named payment parameters" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CTH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "revenue-and-margin-per-case-from-named-payment-parameters" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ProspAmt+ReimbShare*UnitCost*CareUnits; =ProspAmt-(1-ReimbShare)*UnitCost*CareUnits" .

hemo:7002813 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mixed payment margin equals revenue minus the cost of care"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "CaseMargin equals CaseRevenue minus UnitCost times CareUnits. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the reimbursed share applied where the provider's share belongs: for the pure case price over four days, ProspAmt minus ReimbShare times cost gives 3,200 instead of 1,600." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mixed payment margin equals revenue minus the cost of care" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CTH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mixed-payment-margin-equals-revenue-minus-the-cost-of-care" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(CaseMargin-(CaseRevenue-UnitCost*CareUnits))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002814 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mixed payment revenue lies from the prospective amount to that amount plus full cost"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "CaseRevenue is at least ProspAmt and at most ProspAmt plus UnitCost times CareUnits, since no more than the whole cost is reimbursed. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the share entered as a percentage (50 instead of 0.5), which gives revenue of 161,600 pounds for the eight-day blend." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mixed payment revenue lies from the prospective amount to that amount plus full cost" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CTH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mixed-payment-revenue-lies-from-the-prospective-amount-to-that-amount-plus-full-cost" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(CaseRevenue>=ProspAmt-1E-9,CaseRevenue<=ProspAmt+UnitCost*CareUnits+1E-9)" .

hemo:7002815 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Blend of 1,600 pounds plus half of cost for an eight-day stay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a fixed part of 1,600 pounds, half of cost reimbursed and bed-days at 400 pounds, an eight-day stay brings 1,600 plus 1,600, or 3,200 pounds, exactly its cost, so the margin is zero, as in the article's table." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Blend of 1,600 pounds plus half of cost for an eight-day stay" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P = 1600; r = 0.5; c = 400; q = 8; R = 3200; M = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "blend-of-1-600-pounds-plus-half-of-cost-for-an-eight-day-stay" .

hemo:7002816 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Pure case price of 3,200 pounds for a four-day stay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With no cost reimbursed the hospital receives 3,200 pounds whatever the stay; at four days the cost is 1,600 pounds and the margin 1,600 pounds, as in the article's table." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Pure case price of 3,200 pounds for a four-day stay" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P = 3200; r = 0; c = 400; q = 4; R = 3200; M = 1600" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pure-case-price-of-3-200-pounds-for-a-four-day-stay" .

hemo:7002817 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Full cost reimbursement of a twelve-day stay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With no fixed part and all cost reimbursed, revenue equals the 4,800 pound cost of a twelve-day stay and the margin is zero, as in the article's table." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Full cost reimbursement of a twelve-day stay" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P = 0; r = 1; c = 400; q = 12; R = 4800; M = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "full-cost-reimbursement-of-a-twelve-day-stay" .

hemo:7002818 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Costly case of ten days under the blend"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Two days beyond the eight-day stay cost 800 pounds; the blend reimburses half, so revenue rises to 3,600 pounds and the margin falls to minus 400 pounds. Under the pure case price two extra days would cut the margin by the full 800 pounds, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Costly case of ten days under the blend" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P = 1600; r = 0.5; c = 400; q = 10; R = 3600; M = -400" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "costly-case-of-ten-days-under-the-blend" .

hemo:7002819 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant index of agency across the stay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "alpha does not change with q or with the hospital's net revenue; Ellis and McGuire note that it is nearly constant when the amounts for each patient are small relative to the hospital's totals. The objective alpha B(q) + R(q) minus c q used in the article is that simplification." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant index of agency across the stay" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CTH-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-index-of-agency-across-the-stay" .

hemo:7002820 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Straight-line marginal benefit with a positive index of agency"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Marginal benefit falls by b_1 for each extra unit and alpha is positive; with a curved benefit function the first-order condition alpha b(q) = (1 minus r) c still holds but must be solved numerically." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Straight-line marginal benefit with a positive index of agency" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CTH-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "straight-line-marginal-benefit-with-a-positive-index-of-agency" .

hemo:7002821 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Bed-days chosen from named benefit, cost and agency parameters"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000545 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With BenIntercept, BenSlope, ReimbShare, UnitCost and AgencyIndex named, the formula returns the stay the provider chooses, held in ChosenDays." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Bed-days chosen from named benefit, cost and agency parameters" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CTH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "bed-days-chosen-from-named-benefit-cost-and-agency-parameters" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MAX(0,(BenIntercept-(1-ReimbShare)*UnitCost/AgencyIndex)/BenSlope)" .

hemo:7002822 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Provider's first-order condition holds at the chosen stay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When ChosenDays is positive, AgencyIndex times the marginal benefit at ChosenDays equals (1 minus ReimbShare) times UnitCost; when it is zero, the weighted benefit of the first unit is no more than that cost. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the index of agency applied to cost instead of benefit, which gives ten days instead of four under pure case payment." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Provider's first-order condition holds at the chosen stay" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CTH-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "provider-s-first-order-condition-holds-at-the-chosen-stay" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(ChosenDays>0,ABS(AgencyIndex*(BenIntercept-BenSlope*ChosenDays)-(1-ReimbShare)*UnitCost)<1E-9,AgencyIndex*BenIntercept<=(1-ReimbShare)*UnitCost)" .

hemo:7002823 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Chosen stay no longer than the stay that maximises patient benefit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a positive index of agency and no more than full reimbursement, ChosenDays is at most BenIntercept / BenSlope, where marginal benefit reaches zero. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the provider's cost added to marginal benefit instead of subtracted, which gives twenty days against a ceiling of twelve." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Chosen stay no longer than the stay that maximises patient benefit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CTH-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "chosen-stay-no-longer-than-the-stay-that-maximises-patient-benefit" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ChosenDays<=BenIntercept/BenSlope+1E-9" .

hemo:7002824 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Pure case payment with an index of agency of 0.5"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With no cost reimbursed the provider bears 400 pounds a day but values benefit at half, so it stops where marginal benefit is 800 pounds: (1,200 minus 800) / 100 gives four days, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Pure case payment with an index of agency of 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_0 = 1200; b_1 = 100; r = 0; c = 400; alpha = 0.5; q = 4" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pure-case-payment-with-an-index-of-agency-of-0-5" .

hemo:7002825 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Half of cost reimbursed with an index of agency of 0.5"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The provider now bears 200 pounds a day, so it stops where half the marginal benefit is 200 pounds: eight days, the efficient stay, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Half of cost reimbursed with an index of agency of 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_0 = 1200; b_1 = 100; r = 0.5; c = 400; alpha = 0.5; q = 8" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "half-of-cost-reimbursed-with-an-index-of-agency-of-0-5" .

hemo:7002826 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Full cost reimbursement with an index of agency of 0.5"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With all cost reimbursed the provider bears nothing, so care continues until marginal benefit reaches zero at twelve days, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Full cost reimbursement with an index of agency of 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_0 = 1200; b_1 = 100; r = 1; c = 400; alpha = 0.5; q = 12" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "full-cost-reimbursement-with-an-index-of-agency-of-0-5" .

hemo:7002827 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Perfect agent under pure case payment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha equal to 1 and no cost reimbursed the provider sets marginal benefit equal to the full 400 pound cost and chooses the efficient eight days, the case in which Ellis and McGuire find prospective payment efficient." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Perfect agent under pure case payment" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_0 = 1200; b_1 = 100; r = 0; c = 400; alpha = 1; q = 8" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "perfect-agent-under-pure-case-payment" .

hemo:7002828 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Quarter of cost reimbursed with an index of agency of 0.5"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The provider bears 300 pounds a day and stops where half the marginal benefit equals it, at six days (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Quarter of cost reimbursed with an index of agency of 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_0 = 1200; b_1 = 100; r = 0.25; c = 400; alpha = 0.5; q = 6" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "quarter-of-cost-reimbursed-with-an-index-of-agency-of-0-5" .

hemo:7002829 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Index of agency from 0 to 1 for the efficient share"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "alpha is positive and at most 1, so r_star runs from 0 (perfect agent) towards 1; an alpha above 1, a provider who overweights patient benefit, would call for a negative share, which a cost reimbursement rule cannot provide." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Index of agency from 0 to 1 for the efficient share" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CTH-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "index-of-agency-from-0-to-1-for-the-efficient-share" .

hemo:7002830 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Zero margin on an efficient stay as the normalisation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Setting P so that payment equals cost at q_eff is the article's choice; any other fixed part leaves the chosen stay unchanged and only moves money between payer and provider." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Zero margin on an efficient stay as the normalisation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CTH-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "zero-margin-on-an-efficient-stay-as-the-normalisation" .

hemo:7002831 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Efficient stay, reimbursed share and fixed part from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000546 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With BenIntercept, BenSlope, UnitCost and AgencyIndex named, the formulas return the efficient stay, the efficient reimbursed share and the budget-matched fixed part, held in EffDays, EffShare and BlendFixed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Efficient stay, reimbursed share and fixed part from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CTH-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "efficient-stay-reimbursed-share-and-fixed-part-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(BenIntercept-UnitCost)/BenSlope; =1-AgencyIndex; =(1-EffShare)*UnitCost*EffDays" .

hemo:7002832 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Provider chooses the efficient stay at the efficient reimbursed share"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Putting EffShare into the provider's choice, (BenIntercept minus (1 minus EffShare) times UnitCost / AgencyIndex) / BenSlope, returns EffDays. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the share set equal to alpha instead of 1 minus alpha: with alpha of 0.8 the provider would choose eleven days instead of eight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Provider chooses the efficient stay at the efficient reimbursed share" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CTH-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "provider-chooses-the-efficient-stay-at-the-efficient-reimbursed-share" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((BenIntercept-(1-EffShare)*UnitCost/AgencyIndex)/BenSlope-EffDays)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002833 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Blended payment for an efficient stay equals its cost"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "BlendFixed plus EffShare times UnitCost times EffDays equals UnitCost times EffDays. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the fixed part set at the reimbursed share of cost instead of the provider's share: with alpha of 0.8 the payment would be 1,280 pounds against a cost of 3,200." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Blended payment for an efficient stay equals its cost" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CTH-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "blended-payment-for-an-efficient-stay-equals-its-cost" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(BlendFixed+EffShare*UnitCost*EffDays-UnitCost*EffDays)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002834 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Efficient blend for an index of agency of 0.5"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The efficient stay is (1,200 minus 400) / 100, or eight days; half of cost is reimbursed, and the fixed part is 3,200 minus 0.5 times 400 times 8, or 1,600 pounds, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Efficient blend for an index of agency of 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_0 = 1200; b_1 = 100; c = 400; alpha = 0.5; q_eff = 8; r_star = 0.5; P = 1600" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "efficient-blend-for-an-index-of-agency-of-0-5" .

hemo:7002835 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Perfect agent needs pure case payment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha equal to 1 no cost is reimbursed and the whole 3,200 pound cost of an eight-day stay is paid as a case price, as Ellis and McGuire state for a perfect agent." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Perfect agent needs pure case payment" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_0 = 1200; b_1 = 100; c = 400; alpha = 1; q_eff = 8; r_star = 0; P = 3200" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "perfect-agent-needs-pure-case-payment" .

hemo:7002836 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Efficient blend for an index of agency of 0.8"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "One fifth of cost is reimbursed and the fixed part is 0.8 times 400 times 8, or 2,560 pounds (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Efficient blend for an index of agency of 0.8" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_0 = 1200; b_1 = 100; c = 400; alpha = 0.8; q_eff = 8; r_star = 0.2; P = 2560" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CTH-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "efficient-blend-for-an-index-of-agency-of-0-8" .

hemo:7002837 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same year for relative values, indices and conversion factor"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "All inputs come from the same calendar year's final rule, because the factor is set under budget neutrality for that year's relative values (HE-FM-CVF-003)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same year for relative values, indices and conversion factor" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVF-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-year-for-relative-values-indices-and-conversion-factor" .

hemo:7002838 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Participating supplier and services outside anaesthesia"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The amount is for a participating supplier; a non-participating supplier receives 95 per cent. Anaesthesia services use separate conversion factors (20.5998 and 20.4976 for 2026) and are not priced this way." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Participating supplier and services outside anaesthesia" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVF-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "participating-supplier-and-services-outside-anaesthesia" .

hemo:7002839 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Published indices used as given"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The indices already include the statutory one-quarter work adjustment and any floors, so the analyst applies the published values without further adjustment." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Published indices used as given" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVF-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "published-indices-used-as-given" .

hemo:7002840 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Fee schedule amount and geographic adjustment factor from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000547 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With WorkRVU, PERVU, MPRVU, WorkGPCI, PEGPCI, MPGPCI and ConvFactor named, the first formula returns the fee schedule amount in the component form, held in FeeAmount, and the second the regulation's geographic adjustment factor as the sum of each component's share of the total relative value times its index, held in GeoAdjFactor." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fee schedule amount and geographic adjustment factor from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CVF-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fee-schedule-amount-and-geographic-adjustment-factor-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(WorkRVU*WorkGPCI+PERVU*PEGPCI+MPRVU*MPGPCI)*ConvFactor; =WorkRVU/(WorkRVU+PERVU+MPRVU)*WorkGPCI+PERVU/(WorkRVU+PERVU+MPRVU)*PEGPCI+MPRVU/(WorkRVU+PERVU+MPRVU)*MPGPCI" .

hemo:7002841 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Geographic adjustment factor lies within the range of the three indices"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Because the shares of the three components add to one, GeoAdjFactor is no lower than the smallest and no higher than the largest of WorkGPCI, PEGPCI and MPGPCI. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the three indices added without their shares, 2.97 for Service A's locality." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Geographic adjustment factor lies within the range of the three indices" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVF-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "geographic-adjustment-factor-lies-within-the-range-of-the-three-indices" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(GeoAdjFactor>=MIN(WorkGPCI,PEGPCI,MPGPCI)-1E-12,GeoAdjFactor<=MAX(WorkGPCI,PEGPCI,MPGPCI)+1E-12)" .

hemo:7002842 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fee schedule amount equals total units times the GAF times the conversion factor"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "FeeAmount, computed component by component, equals (WorkRVU plus PERVU plus MPRVU) times GeoAdjFactor times ConvFactor, the product form of 42 CFR 414.20(a). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the fee priced with the simple average of the indices, 76.05 dollars instead of 82.83." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fee schedule amount equals total units times the GAF times the conversion factor" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVF-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fee-schedule-amount-equals-total-units-times-the-gaf-times-the-conversion-factor" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(FeeAmount-(WorkRVU+PERVU+MPRVU)*GeoAdjFactor*ConvFactor)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002843 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Service A at national average indices with the 2026 default factor"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 1.00 work, 1.20 practice expense and 0.10 malpractice units, 2.30 in total, and every index at 1.00, the fee is 2.30 times 33.4009, or 76.82 dollars, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Service A at national average indices with the 2026 default factor" ;
    hemo:9000014 "W = 1; PE = 1.2; MP = 0.1; GPCI_W = 1; GPCI_PE = 1; GPCI_MP = 1; CF = 33.4009; Fee = 76.82" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVF-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "service-a-at-national-average-indices-with-the-2026-default-factor" .

hemo:7002844 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Service A in a locality with indices of 1.02, 1.15 and 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The adjusted total is 1.02 plus 1.38 plus 0.08, or 2.48 units, and the fee 2.48 times 33.4009, or 82.83 dollars, about 7.8 per cent above the national amount; the weighted GAF is 2.48 / 2.30, or 1.0783, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Service A in a locality with indices of 1.02, 1.15 and 0.80" ;
    hemo:9000014 "W = 1; PE = 1.2; MP = 0.1; GPCI_W = 1.02; GPCI_PE = 1.15; GPCI_MP = 0.8; CF = 33.4009; Fee = 82.83" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVF-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "service-a-in-a-locality-with-indices-of-1-02-1-15-and-0-80" .

hemo:7002845 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Service A in the same locality at the qualifying participant factor"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At the 2026 factor for qualifying participants in advanced alternative payment models, 33.5675, the same 2.48 units pay 83.25 dollars (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Service A in the same locality at the qualifying participant factor" ;
    hemo:9000014 "W = 1; PE = 1.2; MP = 0.1; GPCI_W = 1.02; GPCI_PE = 1.15; GPCI_MP = 0.8; CF = 33.5675; Fee = 83.25" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVF-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "service-a-in-the-same-locality-at-the-qualifying-participant-factor" .

hemo:7002846 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Multiplicative chain in the order CMS applies it"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "CMS multiplies the 2025 factor by the budget neutrality adjustment, then the update, then the 2.50 per cent increase; because the steps multiply, their order does not change the result, but adding the percentages does." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Multiplicative chain in the order CMS applies it" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVF-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "multiplicative-chain-in-the-order-cms-applies-it" .

hemo:7002847 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Budget neutrality multiplier estimated by CMS"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "BN is CMS's estimate from prior-year utilisation of what keeps spending within 20 million dollars of what it would have been without the revaluations; HE-FM-CVF-003 shows the logic in simplified form." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Budget neutrality multiplier estimated by CMS" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVF-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "budget-neutrality-multiplier-estimated-by-cms" .

hemo:7002848 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Qualifying and non-qualifying conversion factors from named update components"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000548 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With PrevCF, BNAdj, UpdateQP, UpdateOther and OneYearInc named, the formulas return the two factors rounded to four decimals as CMS publishes them, held in CFQualAPM and CFNonQualAPM." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Qualifying and non-qualifying conversion factors from named update components" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CVF-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "qualifying-and-non-qualifying-conversion-factors-from-named-update-components" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(PrevCF*BNAdj*(1+UpdateQP)*(1+OneYearInc),4); =ROUND(PrevCF*BNAdj*(1+UpdateOther)*(1+OneYearInc),4)" .

hemo:7002849 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two 2026 conversion factors differ only by their statutory updates"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "CFQualAPM / CFNonQualAPM equals (1 plus UpdateQP) / (1 plus UpdateOther), within the rounding to four decimals. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the one-year increase left out of one factor: 32.7488 against 33.4009 gives a ratio of 0.9805 instead of 1.0050." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two 2026 conversion factors differ only by their statutory updates" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVF-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-2026-conversion-factors-differ-only-by-their-statutory-updates" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(CFQualAPM/CFNonQualAPM-(1+UpdateQP)/(1+UpdateOther))<1E-5" .

hemo:7002850 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Rebuilt factors match the published 2026 conversion factors"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the 2026 inputs (PrevCF 32.3465, BNAdj 1.0049, UpdateQP 0.0075, UpdateOther 0.0025, OneYearInc 0.025) the factors equal 33.5675 and 33.4009. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the percentages added instead of multiplied, which gives 33.5563 and 33.3945." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rebuilt factors match the published 2026 conversion factors" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVF-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rebuilt-factors-match-the-published-2026-conversion-factors" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS(CFQualAPM-33.5675)<0.00005,ABS(CFNonQualAPM-33.4009)<0.00005)" .

hemo:7002851 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "2026 conversion factor for practitioners who are not qualifying participants"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "32.3465 times 1.0049 times 1.0025 times 1.0250 gives 33.4009, the factor CMS generally treats as the default, as in the article and the final rule." ;
    hemo:9000009 "2026 conversion factor for practitioners who are not qualifying participants" ;
    hemo:9000014 "CF_prev = 32.3465; BN = 1.0049; u = 0.0025; k = 0.025; CF_new = 33.4009" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVF-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "2026-conversion-factor-for-practitioners-who-are-not-qualifying-participants" .

hemo:7002852 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "2026 conversion factor for qualifying participants"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Replacing the 0.25 per cent update with 0.75 per cent gives 33.5675, as in the article and the final rule." ;
    hemo:9000009 "2026 conversion factor for qualifying participants" ;
    hemo:9000014 "CF_prev = 32.3465; BN = 1.0049; u = 0.0075; k = 0.025; CF_new = 33.5675" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVF-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "2026-conversion-factor-for-qualifying-participants" .

hemo:7002853 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "2027 proposed factor for qualifying participants rebuilt from the fact sheet"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Starting from 33.5675, the proposed budget neutrality adjustment of 0.53 per cent, the 0.75 per cent update and removal of the 2.50 per cent increase give about 33.1693, matching the proposed 33.17; the same chain from 33.4009 with the 0.25 per cent update gives 32.84 (computed here for illustration; the final 2027 rule may differ)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "2027 proposed factor for qualifying participants rebuilt from the fact sheet" ;
    hemo:9000014 "CF_prev = 33.5675; BN = 1.0053; u = 0.0075; k = -0.024390; CF_new = 33.1693" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVF-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "2027-proposed-factor-for-qualifying-participants-rebuilt-from-the-fact-sheet" .

hemo:7002854 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Projected volumes held fixed in the budget neutrality calculation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The same volumes price both schedules, so any change in billing behaviour after the revaluation is outside the calculation; CMS uses prior-year utilisation for the same purpose." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Projected volumes held fixed in the budget neutrality calculation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVF-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "projected-volumes-held-fixed-in-the-budget-neutrality-calculation" .

hemo:7002855 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Adjustment made only above the 20 million dollar limit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The statute allows relative value changes to move Part B spending by up to 20 million dollars a year; beyond that CMS restores neutrality through the conversion factor, which the formula does in full." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Adjustment made only above the 20 million dollar limit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVF-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "adjustment-made-only-above-the-20-million-dollar-limit" .

hemo:7002856 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Budget neutrality multiplier and adjusted factor from named ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000549 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With projected volumes, old units and new units in ranges named Volumes, OldRVUs and NewRVUs, in the same service order, and the starting factor named OldCF, the formulas return the multiplier and the adjusted factor, held in BNMult and AdjCF." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Budget neutrality multiplier and adjusted factor from named ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CVF-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "budget-neutrality-multiplier-and-adjusted-factor-from-named-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(Volumes,OldRVUs)/SUMPRODUCT(Volumes,NewRVUs); =OldCF*BNMult" .

hemo:7002857 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Projected spending unchanged at the adjusted conversion factor"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "SUMPRODUCT(Volumes, NewRVUs) times AdjCF equals SUMPRODUCT(Volumes, OldRVUs) times OldCF. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the multiplier inverted (2,780 / 2,800), which gives a factor of 32.7643 and spending of 91,085 dollars instead of 92,400." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Projected spending unchanged at the adjusted conversion factor" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVF-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "projected-spending-unchanged-at-the-adjusted-conversion-factor" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(Volumes,NewRVUs)*AdjCF-SUMPRODUCT(Volumes,OldRVUs)*OldCF)<1E-9*SUMPRODUCT(Volumes,OldRVUs)*OldCF" .

hemo:7002858 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Conversion factor moves against the change in total units"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the revaluation lowers total weighted units, AdjCF is above OldCF; otherwise it is not above it. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the inverted multiplier again, which lowers the factor to 32.7643 after a cut." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Conversion factor moves against the change in total units" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVF-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "conversion-factor-moves-against-the-change-in-total-units" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(SUMPRODUCT(Volumes,NewRVUs)<SUMPRODUCT(Volumes,OldRVUs),AdjCF>OldCF,AdjCF<=OldCF)" .

hemo:7002859 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-service schedule with a 2.5 per cent cut to service B's work units"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Service A has 2.00 units and 600 claims; service B's 4.00 units fall to 3.95 over 400 claims. Total units fall from 2,800 to 2,780, the multiplier is 1.007194 and the factor rises from 33.00 to 33.2374, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-service schedule with a 2.5 per cent cut to service B's work units" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q_A = 600; q_B = 400; R_A_old = 2; R_A_new = 2; R_B_old = 4; R_B_new = 3.95; CF_old = 33; BN = 1.007194; CF_adj = 33.2374" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVF-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-service-schedule-with-a-2-5-per-cent-cut-to-service-b-s-work-units" .

hemo:7002860 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-service fee schedule with service B's units raised to 4.05"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An increase pulls the factor down: total units rise to 2,820, the multiplier is 0.992908 and the factor falls to 32.7660 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-service fee schedule with service B's units raised to 4.05" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q_A = 600; q_B = 400; R_A_old = 2; R_A_new = 2; R_B_old = 4; R_B_new = 4.05; CF_old = 33; BN = 0.992908; CF_adj = 32.766" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVF-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-service-fee-schedule-with-service-b-s-units-raised-to-4-05" .

hemo:7002861 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Resource use proportional to Medicare relative values"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Within a category, the health system's resources per encounter are assumed proportional to the Medicare relative values of its codes, as HERC assumes for VA outpatient care." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Resource use proportional to Medicare relative values" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVF-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "resource-use-proportional-to-medicare-relative-values" .

hemo:7002862 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One cost per unit for each category of care"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The factor is computed separately for each category (HERC uses 12), so relativities are kept within a category but not imposed across categories." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One cost per unit for each category of care" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CVF-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-cost-per-unit-for-each-category-of-care" .

hemo:7002863 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Category cost per unit and encounter costs from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000550 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the category's spending named CatSpend and the units of each encounter in a range named EncRVUs, the first formula returns the cost per unit, held in CostPerRVU, and the second spills the encounter costs, held in EncCost." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Category cost per unit and encounter costs from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CVF-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "category-cost-per-unit-and-encounter-costs-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CatSpend/SUM(EncRVUs); =CostPerRVU*EncRVUs" .

hemo:7002864 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Encounter costs add up to the category's spending"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "SUM(EncCost) equals CatSpend. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows spending divided by the number of encounters instead of their units: for encounters of 1, 2.30 and 4 units and spending of 730 dollars, the costs add to 1,776.33 dollars." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Encounter costs add up to the category's spending" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVF-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "encounter-costs-add-up-to-the-category-s-spending" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUM(EncCost)-CatSpend)<1E-9*CatSpend" .

hemo:7002865 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Encounter costs keep the Medicare relativities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The ratio of the second encounter's cost to the first equals the ratio of their units. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a flat amount per visit added to each cost, such as 10 dollars, which breaks the proportionality." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Encounter costs keep the Medicare relativities" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CVF-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "encounter-costs-keep-the-medicare-relativities" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(INDEX(EncCost,2)/INDEX(EncCost,1)-INDEX(EncRVUs,2)/INDEX(EncRVUs,1))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002866 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Category with 9 million dollars of spending and 200,000 units"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The cost per unit is 45 dollars, so an encounter of 2.30 units is costed at 103.50 dollars (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Category with 9 million dollars of spending and 200,000 units" ;
    hemo:9000014 "X_c = 9000000; R_tot = 200000; R_i = 2.3; CF_c = 45; C_i = 103.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVF-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "category-with-9-million-dollars-of-spending-and-200-000-units" .

hemo:7002867 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Second HERC care category with a higher cost per unit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A category with 2.4 million dollars of spending and 40,000 units has a cost per unit of 60 dollars, so the same 2.30-unit encounter would be costed at 138 dollars there (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Second HERC care category with a higher cost per unit" ;
    hemo:9000014 "X_c = 2400000; R_tot = 40000; R_i = 2.3; CF_c = 60; C_i = 138" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CVF-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "second-herc-care-category-with-a-higher-cost-per-unit" .

hemo:7002868 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Sensitivity and specificity transfer from the validation sample"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The correction needs the algorithm's sensitivity and specificity in the population being corrected to be the values estimated in the validation study, known and constant; the article flags this transfer as something to check." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sensitivity and specificity transfer from the validation sample" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRV-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sensitivity-and-specificity-transfer-from-the-validation-sample" .

hemo:7002869 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Informative algorithm with Se + Sp above 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Youden's index must be positive; when Se + Sp equals 1 the flagged share carries no information about prevalence and the formula is undefined." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Informative algorithm with Se + Sp above 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRV-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "informative-algorithm-with-se-sp-above-1" .

hemo:7002870 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Corrected prevalence from the flagged share and named accuracy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000551 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With FlagShare, AlgSens and AlgSpec named, the formula returns the truncated Rogan-Gladen prevalence, held in TruePrev." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Corrected prevalence from the flagged share and named accuracy" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CRV-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "corrected-prevalence-from-the-flagged-share-and-named-accuracy" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MIN(1,MAX(0,(FlagShare+AlgSpec-1)/(AlgSens+AlgSpec-1)))" .

hemo:7002871 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Corrected prevalence reproduces the flagged share"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When TruePrev is strictly inside the range 0 to 1, AlgSens times TruePrev plus (1 minus AlgSpec) times (1 minus TruePrev) returns FlagShare; when it is truncated, FlagShare lies at or below the false positive rate or at or above the sensitivity. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the flagged share divided by sensitivity alone (0.0744), which would flag 11.3 per cent instead of 6.7." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Corrected prevalence reproduces the flagged share" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRV-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "corrected-prevalence-reproduces-the-flagged-share" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(AND(TruePrev>0,TruePrev<1),ABS(AlgSens*TruePrev+(1-AlgSpec)*(1-TruePrev)-FlagShare)<1E-9,OR(FlagShare<=1-AlgSpec,FlagShare>=AlgSens))" .

hemo:7002872 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Corrected prevalence no higher than the flagged share divided by sensitivity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every true case found is flagged, so FlagShare is at least AlgSens times TruePrev and TruePrev is at most FlagShare / AlgSens. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the false positive rate 0.05 entered in place of specificity, which drives the estimate to its ceiling of 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Corrected prevalence no higher than the flagged share divided by sensitivity" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRV-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "corrected-prevalence-no-higher-than-the-flagged-share-divided-by-sensitivity" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=TruePrev<=FlagShare/AlgSens+1E-12" .

hemo:7002873 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Heart failure algorithm flagging 6.7 per cent of a claims database"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With sensitivity 0.90 and specificity 0.95, (0.067 minus 0.05) / 0.85 gives a true prevalence of 0.02, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Heart failure algorithm flagging 6.7 per cent of a claims database" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 0.067; Se = 0.9; Sp = 0.95; p = 0.02" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRV-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "heart-failure-algorithm-flagging-6-7-per-cent-of-a-claims-database" .

hemo:7002874 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Heart failure algorithm corrected in its validation sample"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the validation sample the algorithm flags 220 of 1,000 patients; (0.22 minus 0.05) / 0.85 gives 0.20, the 200 of 1,000 with heart failure in the records." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Heart failure algorithm corrected in its validation sample" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 0.22; Se = 0.9; Sp = 0.95; p = 0.2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRV-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "heart-failure-algorithm-corrected-in-its-validation-sample" .

hemo:7002875 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Flagged share below the false positive rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the algorithm flagged only 4 per cent, the uncorrected estimate would be (0.04 minus 0.05) / 0.85, about minus 0.0118, which is truncated to 0: the algorithm's accuracy cannot be right for that population (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Flagged share below the false positive rate" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 0.04; Se = 0.9; Sp = 0.95; p = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRV-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "flagged-share-below-the-false-positive-rate" .

hemo:7002876 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Cost depends only on true disease status"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A flagged patient costs C_1 if a true case and C_0 otherwise, whatever the flag; if false positives are sicker than the average non-case, C_0 should be their own mean cost." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cost depends only on true disease status" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRV-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cost-depends-only-on-true-disease-status" .

hemo:7002877 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Predictive value of the population costed"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "PPV is the share of true cases among the flagged patients actually costed, which depends on the prevalence there; HE-FM-DXA-003 computes it from sensitivity, specificity and prevalence." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Predictive value of the population costed" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRV-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "predictive-value-of-the-population-costed" .

hemo:7002878 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Flagged-cohort mean cost and its bias from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000552 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With PPVFlag, CostCase and CostNonCase named, the formulas return the mean cost of the flagged cohort and its bias against the cost of true cases, held in FlagMeanCost and FlagCostBias." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Flagged-cohort mean cost and its bias from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CRV-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "flagged-cohort-mean-cost-and-its-bias-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PPVFlag*CostCase+(1-PPVFlag)*CostNonCase; =FlagMeanCost-CostCase" .

hemo:7002879 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Flagged-cohort bias equals the false positive share times the cost gap"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "FlagCostBias equals minus (1 minus PPVFlag) times (CostCase minus CostNonCase). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the weights swapped, with PPV applied to the non-case cost: a mean of 1,909 pounds and a bias of minus 4,091 instead of minus 909." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Flagged-cohort bias equals the false positive share times the cost gap" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRV-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "flagged-cohort-bias-equals-the-false-positive-share-times-the-cost-gap" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(FlagCostBias+(1-PPVFlag)*(CostCase-CostNonCase))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002880 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Flagged-cohort mean cost lies from the non-case cost to the case cost"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "As a weighted average, FlagMeanCost is no lower than the smaller and no higher than the larger of CostCase and CostNonCase. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the PPV entered as a percentage (81.8), which gives 410,000 pounds." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Flagged-cohort mean cost lies from the non-case cost to the case cost" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRV-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "flagged-cohort-mean-cost-lies-from-the-non-case-cost-to-the-case-cost" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(FlagMeanCost>=MIN(CostCase,CostNonCase)-1E-9,FlagMeanCost<=MAX(CostCase,CostNonCase)+1E-9)" .

hemo:7002881 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Flagged cohort in the validation sample"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 180 of 220 flagged patients true cases (PPV 0.8181818), cases at 6,000 pounds and non-cases at 1,000, the mean is about 5,091 pounds, 909 pounds or 15.2 per cent below the true 6,000, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Flagged cohort in the validation sample" ;
    hemo:9000014 "PPV = 0.8181818; C_1 = 6000; C_0 = 1000; C_flag = 5090.91; Bias = -909.09" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRV-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "flagged-cohort-in-the-validation-sample" .

hemo:7002882 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Flagged cohort in the full database at 2 per cent prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At the database's PPV of 0.2686567 the mean falls to about 2,343 pounds, less than half the true 6,000, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Flagged cohort in the full database at 2 per cent prevalence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "PPV = 0.2686567; C_1 = 6000; C_0 = 1000; C_flag = 2343.28; Bias = -3656.72" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRV-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "flagged-cohort-in-the-full-database-at-2-per-cent-prevalence" .

hemo:7002883 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Flagged-cohort mean cost of an algorithm with no false positives"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a PPV of 1 the flagged mean equals the cost of cases and the bias is zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Flagged-cohort mean cost of an algorithm with no false positives" ;
    hemo:9000014 "PPV = 1; C_1 = 6000; C_0 = 1000; C_flag = 6000; Bias = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRV-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "flagged-cohort-mean-cost-of-an-algorithm-with-no-false-positives" .

hemo:7002884 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weights supplied by the survey and used as given"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weights are the survey's own, such as the Health Survey for England's selection, non-response and calibration weights; multiplying every weight by the same constant, for example to gross up to the population, leaves P_w unchanged." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weights supplied by the survey and used as given" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XSD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weights-supplied-by-the-survey-and-used-as-given" .

hemo:7002885 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One measurement occasion and valid answers only"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each respondent is counted once, at the survey date, and the n counts exclude missing answers; if missingness depends on the condition, the weights do not correct for it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One measurement occasion and valid answers only" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XSD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-measurement-occasion-and-valid-answers-only" .

hemo:7002886 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted prevalence from named weighting-class ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000553 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the class weights, case counts and respondent counts in ranges named ClassWeights, ClassCases and ClassSizes, in the same order, the formula returns the weighted prevalence, held in WtdPrev. For respondent-level data with a 0 or 1 condition flag, SUMPRODUCT of weights and flags over SUM of weights gives the same result." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted prevalence from named weighting-class ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-XSD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-prevalence-from-named-weighting-class-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(ClassWeights,ClassCases)/SUMPRODUCT(ClassWeights,ClassSizes)" .

hemo:7002887 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted prevalence times the weighted total returns the weighted cases"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "WtdPrev times SUMPRODUCT(ClassWeights, ClassSizes) equals SUMPRODUCT(ClassWeights, ClassCases). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the unweighted share, 0.075, reported as the weighted prevalence: 300 weighted cases implied against 294." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted prevalence times the weighted total returns the weighted cases" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XSD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-prevalence-times-the-weighted-total-returns-the-weighted-cases" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(WtdPrev*SUMPRODUCT(ClassWeights,ClassSizes)-SUMPRODUCT(ClassWeights,ClassCases))<1E-9*SUMPRODUCT(ClassWeights,ClassSizes)" .

hemo:7002888 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted prevalence lies within the range of the class prevalences"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "As a weighted average of the class prevalences ClassCases / ClassSizes (0.09, 0.075 and 0.06), WtdPrev lies from the lowest to the highest: at least one class prevalence is at or below it and at least one at or above it (SUMPRODUCT keeps the check valid without dynamic arrays). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows weighted cases divided by unweighted respondents after the weights are grossed up by 1,000, which gives 73.5." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted prevalence lies within the range of the class prevalences" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XSD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-prevalence-lies-within-the-range-of-the-class-prevalences" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(SUMPRODUCT(--(ClassCases/ClassSizes<=WtdPrev+1E-12))>=1,SUMPRODUCT(--(ClassCases/ClassSizes>=WtdPrev-1E-12))>=1)" .

hemo:7002889 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three weighting classes with an over-sampled region"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Classes of 1,000, 2,000 and 1,000 respondents with weights 0.6, 1.2 and 1.0 and 90, 150 and 60 cases give 294 / 4,000, a weighted prevalence of 0.0735 against an unweighted 300 / 4,000 or 0.075 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three weighting classes with an over-sampled region" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_1 = 0.6; w_2 = 1.2; w_3 = 1; d_1 = 90; d_2 = 150; d_3 = 60; n_1 = 1000; n_2 = 2000; n_3 = 1000; P_w = 0.0735" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XSD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-weighting-classes-with-an-over-sampled-region" .

hemo:7002890 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three-class survey prevalence with equal weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With every weight equal to 1 the estimate is the unweighted share, 0.075 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three-class survey prevalence with equal weights" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_1 = 1; w_2 = 1; w_3 = 1; d_1 = 90; d_2 = 150; d_3 = 60; n_1 = 1000; n_2 = 2000; n_3 = 1000; P_w = 0.075" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XSD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-class-survey-prevalence-with-equal-weights" .

hemo:7002891 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three-class survey prevalence with weights grossed up to the population"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Multiplying the weights by 1,000 to represent 4 million people leaves the prevalence at 0.0735 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three-class survey prevalence with weights grossed up to the population" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_1 = 600; w_2 = 1200; w_3 = 1000; d_1 = 90; d_2 = 150; d_3 = 60; n_1 = 1000; n_2 = 2000; n_3 = 1000; P_w = 0.0735" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XSD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-class-survey-prevalence-with-weights-grossed-up-to-the-population" .

hemo:7002892 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Steady-state population for the prevalence relation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Incidence, mean duration and the size of the population are stable over time and there is no net migration of cases; Reichenheim and Coutinho list stationarity among the conditions for relating cross-sectional measures to incidence." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Steady-state population for the prevalence relation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XSD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "steady-state-population-for-the-prevalence-relation" .

hemo:7002893 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Consistent time units for incidence and duration"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "I and D use the same time unit, such as per person-year and years; a rate per year with a duration in months overstates I D twelvefold." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Consistent time units for incidence and duration" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XSD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "consistent-time-units-for-incidence-and-duration" .

hemo:7002894 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Steady-state prevalence and its approximation from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000554 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With IncRate and MeanDur named, the formulas return the exact steady-state prevalence and the approximation, held in PrevExact and PrevApprox." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Steady-state prevalence and its approximation from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-XSD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "steady-state-prevalence-and-its-approximation-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IncRate*MeanDur/(1+IncRate*MeanDur); =IncRate*MeanDur" .

hemo:7002895 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Prevalence odds equal incidence times mean duration"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "PrevExact / (1 minus PrevExact) equals IncRate times MeanDur. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the approximation reported as the exact value: 0.012 has odds of 0.012146, not 0.012." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prevalence odds equal incidence times mean duration" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XSD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prevalence-odds-equal-incidence-times-mean-duration" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PrevExact/(1-PrevExact)-IncRate*MeanDur)<1E-12" .

hemo:7002896 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Exact steady-state prevalence no higher than the approximation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Because 1 + IncRate times MeanDur is at least 1, PrevExact is at most PrevApprox and below 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the solved form written with 1 minus I D in the denominator, which gives 0.012146 against 0.012." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exact steady-state prevalence no higher than the approximation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XSD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exact-steady-state-prevalence-no-higher-than-the-approximation" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(PrevExact<=PrevApprox+1E-15,PrevExact<1)" .

hemo:7002897 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Condition with an incidence of 2 per 1,000 and a mean duration of six years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Half of new cases last 10 years and half 2, so the mean duration is six years; I times D is 0.012, the article's total prevalence of 1.2 per cent, and the exact steady-state value is 0.012 / 1.012, about 0.011858 (exact value computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Condition with an incidence of 2 per 1,000 and a mean duration of six years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "I = 0.002; D = 6; P = 0.011858; P_approx = 0.012" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XSD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "condition-with-an-incidence-of-2-per-1-000-and-a-mean-duration-of-six-years" .

hemo:7002898 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mild form with an incidence of 1 per 1,000 and ten years' duration"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The approximation gives the article's 0.010; the exact steady-state value is 0.01 / 1.01, about 0.009901 (exact value computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mild form with an incidence of 1 per 1,000 and ten years' duration" ;
    hemo:9000014 "I = 0.001; D = 10; P = 0.009901; P_approx = 0.01" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XSD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mild-form-with-an-incidence-of-1-per-1-000-and-ten-years-duration" .

hemo:7002899 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Common condition where the approximation fails"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With an incidence of 0.05 per person-year and five years' duration, I times D is 0.25 but the steady-state prevalence is 0.20, so the approximation overstates it by a quarter (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Common condition where the approximation fails" ;
    hemo:9000014 "I = 0.05; D = 5; P = 0.2; P_approx = 0.25" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XSD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "common-condition-where-the-approximation-fails" .

hemo:7002900 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Utility constant over the disease course within each form"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each form has one utility whatever the time since diagnosis, as in the article; if utility declines with time since diagnosis, long-duration cases are sampled late in their course and the gap can reverse." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Utility constant over the disease course within each form" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XSD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "utility-constant-over-the-disease-course-within-each-form" .

hemo:7002901 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Steady state for each form of the condition"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Incidence and mean duration of each form are stable, so the prevalent pool holds the forms in proportion to I_k times D_k (HE-FM-XSD-002)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Steady state for each form of the condition" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-XSD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "steady-state-for-each-form-of-the-condition" .

hemo:7002902 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Prevalence-weighted and incidence-weighted mean utility from named ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000555 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the incidence, mean duration and utility of each form in ranges named IncRates, Durations and Utils, in the same order, the formulas return the prevalent-case and incident-case means, held in UtilPrev and UtilInc." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prevalence-weighted and incidence-weighted mean utility from named ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-XSD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prevalence-weighted-and-incidence-weighted-mean-utility-from-named-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(IncRates,Durations,Utils)/SUMPRODUCT(IncRates,Durations); =SUMPRODUCT(IncRates,Utils)/SUM(IncRates)" .

hemo:7002903 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reweighting prevalent cases by inverse duration recovers the incident mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Taking each form's share of the prevalent pool, IncRates times Durations over their SUMPRODUCT, dividing it by Durations and averaging Utils with the result returns UtilInc. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the survey mean of prevalent cases, 0.75, used as the mean at diagnosis." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reweighting prevalent cases by inverse duration recovers the incident mean" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XSD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reweighting-prevalent-cases-by-inverse-duration-recovers-the-incident-mean" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(IncRates*Durations/SUMPRODUCT(IncRates,Durations)/Durations,Utils)/SUMPRODUCT(IncRates*Durations/SUMPRODUCT(IncRates,Durations)/Durations)-UtilInc)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002904 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gap between prevalent and incident means equals the duration covariance over the mean duration"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "(UtilPrev minus UtilInc) times the incidence-weighted mean duration equals the incidence-weighted mean of Durations times Utils minus the mean duration times UtilInc, the covariance of duration and utility among new cases. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an unweighted mean of the forms' utilities, 0.65, reported as the survey mean." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gap between prevalent and incident means equals the duration covariance over the mean duration" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-XSD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gap-between-prevalent-and-incident-means-equals-the-duration-covariance-over-the-mean-duration" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((UtilPrev-UtilInc)*SUMPRODUCT(IncRates,Durations)/SUM(IncRates)-(SUMPRODUCT(IncRates,Durations,Utils)/SUM(IncRates)-SUMPRODUCT(IncRates,Durations)/SUM(IncRates)*UtilInc))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002905 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mild and severe forms of a chronic condition"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With incidence 0.001 per person-year for each form, durations of 10 and 2 years and utilities of 0.80 and 0.50, the prevalent mean is 0.009 / 0.012, or 0.75, and the incident mean 0.0013 / 0.002, or 0.65, so the survey overstates the utility at diagnosis by 0.10, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mild and severe forms of a chronic condition" ;
    hemo:9000014 "I_1 = 0.001; I_2 = 0.001; D_1 = 10; D_2 = 2; u_1 = 0.8; u_2 = 0.5; u_prev = 0.75; u_inc = 0.65" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XSD-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mild-and-severe-forms-of-a-chronic-condition" .

hemo:7002906 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal durations of two forms remove the prevalent-case utility gap"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If both forms lasted five years, the prevalent and incident means would both be 0.65 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equal durations of two forms remove the prevalent-case utility gap" ;
    hemo:9000014 "I_1 = 0.001; I_2 = 0.001; D_1 = 5; D_2 = 5; u_1 = 0.8; u_2 = 0.5; u_prev = 0.65; u_inc = 0.65" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XSD-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equal-durations-of-two-forms-remove-the-prevalent-case-utility-gap" .

hemo:7002907 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Severe form three times as common at onset"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With incidences of 0.0005 and 0.0015 and the article's durations and utilities, the incident mean is 0.575 and the prevalent mean 0.6875, a gap of 0.1125 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Severe form three times as common at onset" ;
    hemo:9000014 "I_1 = 0.0005; I_2 = 0.0015; D_1 = 10; D_2 = 2; u_1 = 0.8; u_2 = 0.5; u_prev = 0.6875; u_inc = 0.575" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-XSD-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "severe-form-three-times-as-common-at-onset" .

hemo:7002908 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive costs with fitted means from a gamma GLM"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both the observed cost and the fitted mean are positive; the log term is undefined for a cost of zero, so zero costs belong to the first part of a two-part model and the gamma GLM to the positive costs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive costs with fitted means from a gamma GLM" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DEVR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-costs-with-fitted-means-from-a-gamma-glm" .

hemo:7002909 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Unweighted and unscaled gamma deviance residuals"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every patient has a prior weight of 1 and the residual is not divided by the estimated dispersion, as in Stata's glm, whose overall deviance is the weighted sum of the unit deviances; residuals are therefore compared within one fit, not across models." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Unweighted and unscaled gamma deviance residuals" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DEVR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "unweighted-and-unscaled-gamma-deviance-residuals" .

hemo:7002910 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Gamma unit deviance and deviance residual from named cost cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000556 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With CostObs and CostFit named, the formulas return the gamma unit deviance and the deviance residual, held in GamUnitDev and GamDevRes. SIGN returns 0 when the cost equals its fitted mean." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gamma unit deviance and deviance residual from named cost cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DEVR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gamma-unit-deviance-and-deviance-residual-from-named-cost-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=2*((CostObs-CostFit)/CostFit-LN(CostObs/CostFit)); =SIGN(CostObs-CostFit)*SQRT(GamUnitDev)" .

hemo:7002911 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gamma deviance residual squares to the unit deviance and keeps the sign of the raw residual"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "GamUnitDev is not negative, GamDevRes squared returns GamUnitDev, and GamDevRes has the sign of CostObs minus CostFit. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the sign left off the square root, which reports the 1,000 pound patient as +0.929." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gamma deviance residual squares to the unit deviance and keeps the sign of the raw residual" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DEVR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gamma-deviance-residual-squares-to-the-unit-deviance-and-keeps-the-sign-of-the-raw-residual" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(GamUnitDev>=0,ABS(GamDevRes^2-GamUnitDev)<1E-9*MAX(1,GamUnitDev),SIGN(GamDevRes)=SIGN(CostObs-CostFit))" .

hemo:7002912 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gamma deviance residual smaller in size than the Pearson residual above the mean and larger below it"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Because 2(x minus 1 minus ln x) is below (x minus 1) squared for x = CostObs / CostFit above 1 and above it for x below 1, GamDevRes is no larger in size than the Pearson residual (CostObs minus CostFit) / CostFit for costs above the mean and no smaller below it. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the log term dropped from the unit deviance, which gives the 6,000 pound patient a residual of +1.414 against a Pearson residual of +1.000." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gamma deviance residual smaller in size than the Pearson residual above the mean and larger below it" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DEVR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gamma-deviance-residual-smaller-in-size-than-the-pearson-residual-above-the-mean-and-larger-below-it" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(CostObs>=CostFit,ABS(GamDevRes)<=ABS(CostObs-CostFit)/CostFit+1E-12,ABS(GamDevRes)>=ABS(CostObs-CostFit)/CostFit-1E-12)" .

hemo:7002913 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient costing 6,000 pounds against a fitted mean of 3,000"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An intercept-only gamma GLM with a log link fits the sample mean, 3,000 pounds, to all three patients; for the 6,000 pound patient the unit deviance is 2 x (1 minus 0.6931) = 0.6137 and the residual +0.783, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient costing 6,000 pounds against a fitted mean of 3,000" ;
    hemo:9000014 "y = 6000; mu = 3000; d = 0.6137; r_D = 0.783" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DEVR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-costing-6-000-pounds-against-a-fitted-mean-of-3-000" .

hemo:7002914 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient costing 1,000 pounds against a fitted mean of 3,000"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The cheapest patient has unit deviance 0.8639 and residual minus 0.929, the largest in size of the three although the Pearson residual, minus 0.667, is smaller in size than the expensive patient's +1.000, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient costing 1,000 pounds against a fitted mean of 3,000" ;
    hemo:9000014 "y = 1000; mu = 3000; d = 0.8639; r_D = -0.929" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DEVR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-costing-1-000-pounds-against-a-fitted-mean-of-3-000" .

hemo:7002915 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient costing 2,000 pounds against a fitted mean of 3,000"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The middle patient has unit deviance 0.1443 and residual minus 0.380; the three unit deviances add to the model deviance of 1.622, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient costing 2,000 pounds against a fitted mean of 3,000" ;
    hemo:9000014 "y = 2000; mu = 3000; d = 0.1443; r_D = -0.380" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DEVR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-costing-2-000-pounds-against-a-fitted-mean-of-3-000" .

hemo:7002916 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One record per patient with the cumulative hazard from the fitted model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "H is the fitted cumulative hazard at the patient's own observed time, from a Cox model with its baseline hazard or from a parametric survival model, and each patient has a single record; with several records per patient the martingale residuals are first summed within the patient." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One record per patient with the cumulative hazard from the fitted model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DEVR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-record-per-patient-with-the-cumulative-hazard-from-the-fitted-model" .

hemo:7002917 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive cumulative hazard for the survival deviance residual"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "H is above zero, which holds for any patient followed for some time under a model with a positive hazard; the sign is written M / |M| in the Math line, so the calculator cannot show the case M = 0." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive cumulative hazard for the survival deviance residual" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DEVR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-cumulative-hazard-for-the-survival-deviance-residual" .

hemo:7002918 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Martingale and survival deviance residuals from named event and hazard cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000557 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With EventInd (1 or 0) and CumHaz named, the formulas return the martingale residual and the survival deviance residual, held in MartRes and SurvDevRes." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Martingale and survival deviance residuals from named event and hazard cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DEVR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "martingale-and-survival-deviance-residuals-from-named-event-and-hazard-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EventInd-CumHaz; =SIGN(MartRes)*SQRT(-2*(MartRes+EventInd*LN(EventInd-MartRes)))" .

hemo:7002919 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Survival deviance residual sign follows the cumulative hazard"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A censored patient has SurvDevRes equal to minus the square root of twice CumHaz, and a patient with an event has a positive SurvDevRes exactly when CumHaz is below 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the martingale residual computed as CumHaz minus EventInd, which gives the month 1 death a residual of minus 0.685." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Survival deviance residual sign follows the cumulative hazard" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DEVR-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "survival-deviance-residual-sign-follows-the-cumulative-hazard" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(EventInd=0,ABS(SurvDevRes+SQRT(2*CumHaz))<1E-9,(SurvDevRes>0)=(CumHaz<1))" .

hemo:7002920 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Squared survival deviance residual equals the Poisson unit deviance of the event indicator"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "SurvDevRes squared equals the Poisson unit deviance with the event indicator as the count and CumHaz as its mean: 2(ln(1 / CumHaz) minus (1 minus CumHaz)) after an event and 2 CumHaz after censoring. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the factor minus 2 written as minus 1, which halves the square to 1.047 for the month 1 death." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Squared survival deviance residual equals the Poisson unit deviance of the event indicator" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DEVR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "squared-survival-deviance-residual-equals-the-poisson-unit-deviance-of-the-event-indicator" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SurvDevRes^2-IF(EventInd=1,2*(LN(1/CumHaz)-(1-CumHaz)),2*CumHaz))<1E-9*MAX(1,SurvDevRes^2)" .

hemo:7002921 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient who died at month 1 under an exponential hazard of 0.15 a month"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The fitted cumulative hazard is 0.15, so M = 0.85 and the residual is +1.447, the largest of the four patients, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient who died at month 1 under an exponential hazard of 0.15 a month" ;
    hemo:9000014 "delta = 1; H = 0.15; M = 0.85; r_D = 1.447" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DEVR-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-who-died-at-month-1-under-an-exponential-hazard-of-0-15-a-month" .

hemo:7002922 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient censored at month 5 under an exponential hazard of 0.15 a month"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The censored patient has H = 0.75, M = minus 0.75 and residual minus 1.225, minus the square root of 1.5, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient censored at month 5 under an exponential hazard of 0.15 a month" ;
    hemo:9000014 "delta = 0; H = 0.75; M = -0.75; r_D = -1.225" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DEVR-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-censored-at-month-5-under-an-exponential-hazard-of-0-15-a-month" .

hemo:7002923 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient who died at month 11 under an exponential hazard of 0.15 a month"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The late death has H = 1.65 and M = minus 0.65, further from zero than the month 3 death's +0.55 on the martingale scale, but its deviance residual, minus 0.546, is smaller in size than that patient's +0.705, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patient who died at month 11 under an exponential hazard of 0.15 a month" ;
    hemo:9000014 "delta = 1; H = 1.65; M = -0.65; r_D = -0.546" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DEVR-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patient-who-died-at-month-11-under-an-exponential-hazard-of-0-15-a-month" .

hemo:7002924 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Half a standard deviation summarises earlier published MIDs in chronic disease"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The 0.5 multiple comes from a review that re-expressed 62 published MIDs as effect sizes and framed its conclusion for chronic diseases; population-based estimation and brief follow-up gave smaller values and acute conditions larger ones, so the multiple is a summary, not a property of any one instrument." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Half a standard deviation summarises earlier published MIDs in chronic disease" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DMID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "half-a-standard-deviation-summarises-earlier-published-mids-in-chronic-disease" .

hemo:7002925 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Baseline standard deviation from the population of interest"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "SD_0 is the spread at baseline in the sample whose change is being judged; a more heterogeneous sample has a larger SD_0 and so a larger yardstick, although patients' perception of change is the same." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Baseline standard deviation from the population of interest" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DMID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "baseline-standard-deviation-from-the-population-of-interest" .

hemo:7002926 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Multiple of the baseline standard deviation from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000558 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With BaseSD and SDMult named, the formula returns the distribution-based yardstick, held in MIDSD." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Multiple of the baseline standard deviation from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DMID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "multiple-of-the-baseline-standard-deviation-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SDMult*BaseSD" .

hemo:7002927 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard deviation multiple entered as a fraction of one standard deviation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "SDMult is positive and no more than 1 and MIDSD is no larger than BaseSD, as for the 0.2 and 0.5 multiples. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the half standard deviation rule entered as 50, which gives a yardstick of 10 index points on a scale that ends at 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standard deviation multiple entered as a fraction of one standard deviation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DMID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standard-deviation-multiple-entered-as-a-fraction-of-one-standard-deviation" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(SDMult>0,SDMult<=1,MIDSD<=BaseSD)" .

hemo:7002928 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Half a standard deviation of an EQ-5D-5L index with SD 0.20"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a baseline standard deviation of 0.20, half a standard deviation is 0.10 index points, as in the article's illustrative example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Half a standard deviation of an EQ-5D-5L index with SD 0.20" ;
    hemo:9000014 "k_SD = 0.5; SD_0 = 0.2; MID_SD = 0.1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DMID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "half-a-standard-deviation-of-an-eq-5d-5l-index-with-sd-0-20" .

hemo:7002929 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cohen's small benchmark for an EQ-5D-5L index with SD 0.20"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An effect size of 0.2 against the same standard deviation is 0.04 index points, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cohen's small benchmark for an EQ-5D-5L index with SD 0.20" ;
    hemo:9000014 "k_SD = 0.2; SD_0 = 0.2; MID_SD = 0.04" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DMID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cohen-s-small-benchmark-for-an-eq-5d-5l-index-with-sd-0-20" .

hemo:7002930 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Half a standard deviation in a more heterogeneous sample"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the baseline standard deviation were 0.30, the half standard deviation yardstick would rise to 0.15 with no change in what patients perceive (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Half a standard deviation in a more heterogeneous sample" ;
    hemo:9000014 "k_SD = 0.5; SD_0 = 0.3; MID_SD = 0.15" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DMID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "half-a-standard-deviation-in-a-more-heterogeneous-sample" .

hemo:7002931 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Reliability for the SEM estimated in a stable population"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "R is a reliability coefficient from the same population, preferably test-retest reliability in patients whose health has not changed; with Cronbach's alpha the SEM reflects only the variability of the instrument at one measurement." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reliability for the SEM estimated in a stable population" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DMID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reliability-for-the-sem-estimated-in-a-stable-population" .

hemo:7002932 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard error of measurement from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000559 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With ScoreSD and Reliab named, the formula returns the standard error of measurement, held in SEMVal." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standard error of measurement from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DMID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standard-error-of-measurement-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ScoreSD*SQRT(1-Reliab)" .

hemo:7002933 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Error variance plus true score variance equals the observed score variance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Under classical test theory SEMVal squared plus Reliab times ScoreSD squared returns ScoreSD squared. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the square root left out, SD x (1 minus R) = 0.04, for which the two parts add to 0.0336 instead of 0.04." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Error variance plus true score variance equals the observed score variance" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DMID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "error-variance-plus-true-score-variance-equals-the-observed-score-variance" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SEMVal^2+Reliab*ScoreSD^2-ScoreSD^2)<1E-9*ScoreSD^2" .

hemo:7002934 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reliability entered as a coefficient and the SEM no larger than the standard deviation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Reliab is no lower than 0 and no higher than 1, and SEMVal does not exceed ScoreSD. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the reliability entered as 80, which the test rejects before the square root of a negative number is used." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reliability entered as a coefficient and the SEM no larger than the standard deviation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DMID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reliability-entered-as-a-coefficient-and-the-sem-no-larger-than-the-standard-deviation" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(OR(Reliab<0,Reliab>1),FALSE,SEMVal<=ScoreSD)" .

hemo:7002935 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "SEM of an EQ-5D-5L index with SD 0.20 and reliability 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a standard deviation of 0.20 and test-retest reliability of 0.80, the SEM is 0.20 x 0.447 = 0.0894, shown as 0.089 in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "SEM of an EQ-5D-5L index with SD 0.20 and reliability 0.80" ;
    hemo:9000014 "SD = 0.2; R = 0.8; SEM = 0.0894" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DMID-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sem-of-an-eq-5d-5l-index-with-sd-0-20-and-reliability-0-80" .

hemo:7002936 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "SEM equal to half a standard deviation at reliability 0.75"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At a reliability of 0.75 the SEM of a score with standard deviation 0.20 is 0.10, the same as half a standard deviation, as de Vet and colleagues note and the article repeats." ;
    hemo:9000009 "SEM equal to half a standard deviation at reliability 0.75" ;
    hemo:9000014 "SD = 0.2; R = 0.75; SEM = 0.1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DMID-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sem-equal-to-half-a-standard-deviation-at-reliability-0-75" .

hemo:7002937 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Independent equal measurement errors for the MDC and reliable change index"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The two scores carry independent errors with the same SEM, so the variance of their difference is 2 SEM squared; the 1.96 multiplier assumes normally distributed errors." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Independent equal measurement errors for the MDC and reliable change index" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DMID-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "independent-equal-measurement-errors-for-the-mdc-and-reliable-change-index" .

hemo:7002938 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Minimally detectable change and reliable change index from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000560 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With SEMVal (HE-FM-DMID-002), ScoreT1 and ScoreT2 named, the formulas return the standard error of the difference, the MDC and the reliable change index, held in SDiffVal, MDCVal and RelChange." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Minimally detectable change and reliable change index from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DMID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "minimally-detectable-change-and-reliable-change-index-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SQRT(2)*SEMVal; =1.96*SDiffVal; =(ScoreT2-ScoreT1)/SDiffVal" .

hemo:7002939 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reliable change index beyond 1.96 exactly when the change exceeds the MDC"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The absolute value of RelChange exceeds 1.96 exactly when the absolute change ScoreT2 minus ScoreT1 exceeds MDCVal. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the index divided by the SEM instead of the standard error of the difference: a change of 0.20 then gives 2.24, reliable, although 0.20 is below the MDC of 0.248 (unrounded SEM, computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reliable change index beyond 1.96 exactly when the change exceeds the MDC" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DMID-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reliable-change-index-beyond-1-96-exactly-when-the-change-exceeds-the-mdc" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(ABS(RelChange)>1.96)=(ABS(ScoreT2-ScoreT1)>MDCVal)" .

hemo:7002940 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "MDC equals 1.96 times the square root of 2 SEMs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "MDCVal divided by SEMVal returns 1.96 x sqrt(2), about 2.772. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the square root of 2 left out, MDC = 1.96 SEM, which gives a ratio of 1.96 and an MDC of 0.175 instead of 0.248 (unrounded SEM, computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "MDC equals 1.96 times the square root of 2 SEMs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DMID-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mdc-equals-1-96-times-the-square-root-of-2-sems" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(MDCVal/SEMVal-1.96*SQRT(2))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002941 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Detectable and reliable change for an EQ-5D-5L index with the article's rounded SEM"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's rounded SEM of 0.089, the standard error of the difference is 0.126, the MDC 1.96 x 0.126 = 0.247 and a patient whose index rises from 0.60 to 0.75 has RC = 0.15 / 0.126 = 1.19, below 1.96, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Detectable and reliable change for an EQ-5D-5L index with the article's rounded SEM" ;
    hemo:9000014 "SEM = 0.089; x_1 = 0.6; x_2 = 0.75; S_diff = 0.126; MDC = 0.247; RC = 1.19" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DMID-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "detectable-and-reliable-change-for-an-eq-5d-5l-index-with-the-article-s-rounded-sem" .

hemo:7002942 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Detectable and reliable change from the unrounded SEM"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Carrying the SEM unrounded (0.08944) gives a standard error of the difference of 0.1265, an MDC of 0.2479 and the same RC of 1.19; the article's 0.247 comes from multiplying the rounded 0.126 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Detectable and reliable change from the unrounded SEM" ;
    hemo:9000014 "SEM = 0.08944; x_1 = 0.6; x_2 = 0.75; S_diff = 0.1265; MDC = 0.2479; RC = 1.19" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DMID-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "detectable-and-reliable-change-from-the-unrounded-sem" .

hemo:7002943 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reliable improvement of 0.30 index points"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A patient whose index rises from 0.50 to 0.80 has RC = 0.30 / 0.1265 = 2.37, beyond 1.96, and a change larger than the MDC (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reliable improvement of 0.30 index points" ;
    hemo:9000014 "SEM = 0.08944; x_1 = 0.5; x_2 = 0.8; S_diff = 0.1265; MDC = 0.2479; RC = 2.37" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DMID-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reliable-improvement-of-0-30-index-points" .

hemo:7002944 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Decrement measured from the baseline it is applied to"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "U_0 and U_1 come from the same dataset, instrument and value set; moving a decrement measured from full health onto a disease state assumes the same absolute effect at any level of health." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Decrement measured from the baseline it is applied to" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DISU-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "decrement-measured-from-the-baseline-it-is-applied-to" .

hemo:7002945 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant decrement over the harm's duration without discounting"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The decrement applies unchanged for dur years and the loss is undiscounted; with discounting or a changing decrement, HE-FM-QALY-001 applies period by period." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant decrement over the harm's duration without discounting" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DISU-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-decrement-over-the-harm-s-duration-without-discounting" .

hemo:7002946 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Disutility and QALY loss from named utility cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000561 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With BaseUtil, HarmUtil and HarmYears named, the formulas return the decrement and the QALY loss, held in Disut and QALYLoss." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Disutility and QALY loss from named utility cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DISU-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "disutility-and-qaly-loss-from-named-utility-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=BaseUtil-HarmUtil; =Disut*HarmYears" .

hemo:7002947 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "QALY loss equals the QALYs without the harm minus the QALYs with it"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "QALYLoss equals BaseUtil times HarmYears minus HarmUtil times HarmYears, and is not negative when the harm lowers utility. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the decrement computed as HarmUtil minus BaseUtil, the negative sign convention some studies use, which gives a loss of minus 0.50 for condition A." ;
    hemo:9000009 "QALY loss equals the QALYs without the harm minus the QALYs with it" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DISU-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "qaly-loss-equals-the-qalys-without-the-harm-minus-the-qalys-with-it" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS(QALYLoss-(BaseUtil*HarmYears-HarmUtil*HarmYears))<1E-9*MAX(1,BaseUtil*HarmYears),QALYLoss>=0)" .

hemo:7002948 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Decrement for condition A from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7002949,
        hemo:7002950,
        hemo:7002951 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7002952,
        hemo:7002953 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.05 ;
    hemo:9000008 "People of about 65 with neither condition have mean utility 0.80 and those with condition A 0.70, so d_A = 0.10, as in the article; over five years the loss is 0.50 QALYs (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Decrement for condition A from a baseline utility of 0.80" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U_0 = 0.8; U_1 = 0.7; dur = 5; d = 0.1; Q_loss = 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DISU-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "decrement-for-condition-a-from-a-baseline-utility-of-0-80" .

hemo:7002949 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "U_0 in the test Decrement for condition A from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002290 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.8 .

hemo:7002950 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "U_1 in the test Decrement for condition A from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002291 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.7 .

hemo:7002951 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "dur in the test Decrement for condition A from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002293 ;
    rheo:2000001 5.0 .

hemo:7002952 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "d in the test Decrement for condition A from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002289 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.1 .

hemo:7002953 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Q_loss in the test Decrement for condition A from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002292 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.5 .

hemo:7002954 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Decrement for condition B from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7002955,
        hemo:7002956,
        hemo:7002957 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7002958,
        hemo:7002959 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 0.60 for condition B alone, d_B = 0.20, as in the article, and the loss over five years is 1.00 QALY (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Decrement for condition B from a baseline utility of 0.80" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U_0 = 0.8; U_1 = 0.6; dur = 5; d = 0.2; Q_loss = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DISU-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "decrement-for-condition-b-from-a-baseline-utility-of-0-80" .

hemo:7002955 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "U_0 in the test Decrement for condition B from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002290 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.8 .

hemo:7002956 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "U_1 in the test Decrement for condition B from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002291 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.6 .

hemo:7002957 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "dur in the test Decrement for condition B from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002293 ;
    rheo:2000001 5.0 .

hemo:7002958 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "d in the test Decrement for condition B from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002289 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.2 .

hemo:7002959 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Q_loss in the test Decrement for condition B from a baseline utility of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002292 ;
    rheo:2000001 1.0 .

hemo:7002960 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Shared baseline for both single-condition decrements"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "U_0 is the utility of people with neither condition from the same dataset and age group, so the TSD 12 baselines for each condition coincide; TSD 12 states that assuming perfect health as the baseline for people without a condition is inappropriate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Shared baseline for both single-condition decrements" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DISU-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "shared-baseline-for-both-single-condition-decrements" .

hemo:7002961 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "No utilities measured in people with both conditions"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The rules estimate a combined state that has not been measured; when utilities from people with both conditions exist they are used directly." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No utilities measured in people with both conditions" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DISU-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-utilities-measured-in-people-with-both-conditions" .

hemo:7002962 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Combined utility under three rules from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000562 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With NeitherUtil, UtilA and UtilB named, the formulas return the additive, multiplicative and minimum estimates, held in UAdd, UMult and UMin." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Combined utility under three rules from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DISU-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "combined-utility-under-three-rules-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=NeitherUtil-(NeitherUtil-UtilA)-(NeitherUtil-UtilB); =NeitherUtil*(UtilA/NeitherUtil)*(UtilB/NeitherUtil); =MIN(NeitherUtil,UtilA,UtilB)" .

hemo:7002963 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Multiplicative minus additive combined utility equals the product of decrements over the baseline"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "UMult minus UAdd equals (NeitherUtil minus UtilA) times (NeitherUtil minus UtilB) divided by NeitherUtil, 0.025 in the article. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the multiplicative rule applied to the raw utilities without the baseline (0.42), which gives minus 0.08." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Multiplicative minus additive combined utility equals the product of decrements over the baseline" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DISU-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "multiplicative-minus-additive-combined-utility-equals-the-product-of-decrements-over-the-baseline" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((UMult-UAdd)-(NeitherUtil-UtilA)*(NeitherUtil-UtilB)/NeitherUtil)<1E-9" .

hemo:7002964 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Additive, multiplicative and minimum combined utilities in rising order"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When neither single-condition utility is above the baseline or below zero, UAdd is no higher than UMult and UMult no higher than UMin. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the multiplicative rule applied without the baseline (0.42), which falls below the additive 0.50." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Additive, multiplicative and minimum combined utilities in rising order" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DISU-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "additive-multiplicative-and-minimum-combined-utilities-in-rising-order" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(AND(UtilA<=NeitherUtil,UtilB<=NeitherUtil,UtilA>=0,UtilB>=0),AND(UAdd<=UMult+1E-12,UMult<=UMin+1E-12),TRUE)" .

hemo:7002965 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Conditions A and B from a baseline of 0.80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 0.80 for neither condition, 0.70 for A and 0.60 for B, the additive rule gives 0.50, the multiplicative 0.80 x 0.875 x 0.75 = 0.525 and the minimum 0.60, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Conditions A and B from a baseline of 0.80" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U_0 = 0.8; U_A = 0.7; U_B = 0.6; U_add = 0.5; U_mult = 0.525; U_min = 0.6" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DISU-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "conditions-a-and-b-from-a-baseline-of-0-80" .

hemo:7002966 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same conditions combined as if from full health"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Combining the raw utilities on a baseline of 1 gives a multiplicative value of 0.70 x 0.60 = 0.42, as in the article's step 5, and an additive value of 0.30 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same conditions combined as if from full health" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U_0 = 1; U_A = 0.7; U_B = 0.6; U_add = 0.3; U_mult = 0.42; U_min = 0.6" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DISU-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-conditions-combined-as-if-from-full-health" .

hemo:7002967 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Avoided condition would have started at once and lasted the full period"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each avoided case of B would otherwise have started at the outset and lasted dur years, nobody dies and gains are undiscounted, as in the article's example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Avoided condition would have started at once and lasted the full period" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DISU-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "avoided-condition-would-have-started-at-once-and-lasted-the-full-period" .

hemo:7002968 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "QALY gain and cost per QALY from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000563 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With OneCondUtil, BothUtil, AvoidYears and CaseCost named, the formulas return the QALY gain per case avoided and the cost per QALY, held in QALYGain and CostPerQALY." ;
    hemo:9000009 "QALY gain and cost per QALY from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DISU-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "qaly-gain-and-cost-per-qaly-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(OneCondUtil-BothUtil)*AvoidYears; =CaseCost/QALYGain" .

hemo:7002969 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cost per QALY times QALY gain returns the cost per case avoided"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "QALYGain is positive and CostPerQALY times QALYGain returns CaseCost. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the ratio inverted, QALYs per pound (0.00005 under the additive rule), or a combined utility above the utility with A alone, as when the minimum rule is replaced by the maximum (0.80), which makes the gain negative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cost per QALY times QALY gain returns the cost per case avoided" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DISU-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cost-per-qaly-times-qaly-gain-returns-the-cost-per-case-avoided" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(QALYGain>0,ABS(CostPerQALY*QALYGain-CaseCost)<1E-9*MAX(1,CaseCost))" .

hemo:7002970 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gain per case of B avoided under the additive rule"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With U_A = 0.70 and the additive combined utility 0.50 over five years, the gain is 1.00 QALY and the cost per QALY at 20,000 pounds per case is 20,000 pounds, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gain per case of B avoided under the additive rule" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U_A = 0.7; U_AB = 0.5; dur = 5; C_case = 20000; G = 1; CPQ = 20000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DISU-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gain-per-case-of-b-avoided-under-the-additive-rule" .

hemo:7002971 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gain per case of B avoided under the multiplicative rule"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The multiplicative combined utility of 0.525 gives a gain of 0.875 QALYs and a cost per QALY of about 22,857 pounds, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gain per case of B avoided under the multiplicative rule" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U_A = 0.7; U_AB = 0.525; dur = 5; C_case = 20000; G = 0.875; CPQ = 22857.14" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DISU-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gain-per-case-of-b-avoided-under-the-multiplicative-rule" .

hemo:7002972 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gain per case of B avoided under the minimum rule"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The minimum rule's 0.60 gives a gain of 0.50 QALYs and a cost per QALY of 40,000 pounds, above an illustrative threshold of 25,000 pounds that the other two rules meet, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gain per case of B avoided under the minimum rule" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U_A = 0.7; U_AB = 0.6; dur = 5; C_case = 20000; G = 0.5; CPQ = 40000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DISU-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gain-per-case-of-b-avoided-under-the-minimum-rule" .

hemo:7002973 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Age within the range of the Health Survey for England sample"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The regression was fitted to EQ-5D responses from participants aged 16 to 98 in the 2003 and 2006 surveys, so it is used for ages in that range and reflects the population of those years." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Age within the range of the Health Survey for England sample" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DISU-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "age-within-the-range-of-the-health-survey-for-england-sample" .

hemo:7002974 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same instrument and value set as the condition utilities"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The baseline is the EQ-5D valued with UK general public time trade-off weights, so the multiplier and other utilities in the model need the same instrument and value set." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same instrument and value set as the condition utilities" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DISU-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-instrument-and-value-set-as-the-condition-utilities" .

hemo:7002975 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "General population baseline and proportional loss from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000564 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With IsMale, AgeYrs and PropMult named, the formulas return the Ara and Brazier baseline and the absolute loss from the proportional decrement, held in GPUtil and PropLoss." ;
    hemo:9000009 "General population baseline and proportional loss from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DISU-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "general-population-baseline-and-proportional-loss-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=0.9508566+0.0212126*IsMale-0.0002587*AgeYrs-0.0000332*AgeYrs^2; =(1-PropMult)*GPUtil" .

hemo:7002976 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Age in years within the survey range and sex coded 0 or 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "AgeYrs is from 16 to 98, IsMale is 0 or 1, and GPUtil is no higher than the intercept plus the male shift. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows age entered in months (720), outside the survey range, which would give a baseline of minus 16.4." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Age in years within the survey range and sex coded 0 or 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DISU-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "age-in-years-within-the-survey-range-and-sex-coded-0-or-1" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(AgeYrs>=16,AgeYrs<=98,OR(IsMale=0,IsMale=1),GPUtil<=0.9508566+0.0212126*IsMale)" .

hemo:7002977 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Proportional multiplier entered as a ratio and the loss smaller than the baseline"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "PropMult is above 0 and no higher than 1, and PropLoss is not negative and smaller than GPUtil. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the 12.5 per cent decrement entered as 12.5 in place of the multiplier 0.875, which gives a loss of minus 9.38 for a woman aged 60." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Proportional multiplier entered as a ratio and the loss smaller than the baseline" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DISU-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "proportional-multiplier-entered-as-a-ratio-and-the-loss-smaller-than-the-baseline" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(PropMult>0,PropMult<=1,PropLoss>=0,PropLoss<GPUtil)" .

hemo:7002978 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Baseline and proportional loss for a woman aged 60"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The baseline is 0.9508566 minus 0.0002587 times 60 minus 0.0000332 times 3,600, which is 0.8158, and removing 12.5 per cent costs about 0.102, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Baseline and proportional loss for a woman aged 60" ;
    hemo:9000014 "male = 0; age = 60; m = 0.875; U_gp = 0.8158; Loss = 0.102" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DISU-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "baseline-and-proportional-loss-for-a-woman-aged-60" .

hemo:7002979 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Baseline and proportional loss for a woman aged 80"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At 80 the baseline is 0.7177 and the same proportional decrement costs about 0.090, less than at 60, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Baseline and proportional loss for a woman aged 80" ;
    hemo:9000014 "male = 0; age = 80; m = 0.875; U_gp = 0.7177; Loss = 0.090" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DISU-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "baseline-and-proportional-loss-for-a-woman-aged-80" .

hemo:7002980 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Baseline and proportional loss for a man aged 60"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a man aged 60 the baseline is 0.0212 higher, 0.8370, and the proportional loss about 0.105 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Baseline and proportional loss for a man aged 60" ;
    hemo:9000014 "male = 1; age = 60; m = 0.875; U_gp = 0.8370; Loss = 0.105" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DISU-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "baseline-and-proportional-loss-for-a-man-aged-60" .

hemo:7002981 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Monotonic sigmoid curve fitted over the doses that matter"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The response rises monotonically with dose towards a plateau, and the curve's parameters come from trials covering the doses being compared; outside that range the result rests on the functional form, not on data." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Monotonic sigmoid curve fitted over the doses that matter" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DOSE-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "monotonic-sigmoid-curve-fitted-over-the-doses-that-matter" .

hemo:7002982 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Population-average response on the sigmoid Emax curve"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "E_D is the average response in the population the curve was fitted to; subgroups by weight or tolerability can sit on different parts of the curve." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Population-average response on the sigmoid Emax curve" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DOSE-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "population-average-response-on-the-sigmoid-emax-curve" .

hemo:7002983 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Sigmoid Emax response from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000565 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With DoseMg, PlaceboResp, MaxEffect, ED50Dose and HillCoef named, the formula returns the expected response, held in RespDose." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sigmoid Emax response from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DOSE-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sigmoid-emax-response-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PlaceboResp+MaxEffect*DoseMg^HillCoef/(ED50Dose^HillCoef+DoseMg^HillCoef)" .

hemo:7002984 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Share of the maximum effect depends only on the dose as a multiple of ED50"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "(RespDose minus PlaceboResp) / MaxEffect equals k to the power HillCoef over 1 plus k to that power, with k = DoseMg / ED50Dose. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the Hill power left off ED50 in the denominator, which gives 0.598 at 150 mg instead of 0.477." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Share of the maximum effect depends only on the dose as a multiple of ED50" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DOSE-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "share-of-the-maximum-effect-depends-only-on-the-dose-as-a-multiple-of-ed50" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((RespDose-PlaceboResp)/MaxEffect-(DoseMg/ED50Dose)^HillCoef/(1+(DoseMg/ED50Dose)^HillCoef))<1E-9" .

hemo:7002985 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Response probability is a valid proportion"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When the response is the proportion of patients responding, RespDose is no lower than 0 and no higher than 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the placebo response entered as a percentage (20), which gives 20.28." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Response probability is a valid proportion" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DOSE-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "response-probability-is-a-valid-proportion" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(RespDose>=0,RespDose<=1)" .

hemo:7002986 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Response at 150 mg with ED50 100 mg and Hill coefficient 2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With E_0 = 0.20, E_max = 0.40, ED_50 = 100 mg and h = 2, the response at 150 mg is 0.20 + 0.40 x 22,500 / 32,500, or 0.476923, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Response at 150 mg with ED50 100 mg and Hill coefficient 2" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_0 = 0.2; E_max = 0.4; D = 150; ED_50 = 100; h = 2; E_D = 0.476923" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOSE-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "response-at-150-mg-with-ed50-100-mg-and-hill-coefficient-2" .

hemo:7002987 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Response at 200 mg with ED50 100 mg and Hill coefficient 2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At 200 mg the fraction is 40,000 / 50,000 = 0.80, so the response is 0.52, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Response at 200 mg with ED50 100 mg and Hill coefficient 2" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_0 = 0.2; E_max = 0.4; D = 200; ED_50 = 100; h = 2; E_D = 0.52" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOSE-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "response-at-200-mg-with-ed50-100-mg-and-hill-coefficient-2" .

hemo:7002988 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Response at 200 mg with a hyperbolic Emax curve"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With h = 1 the same 200 mg dose gives 0.20 + 0.40 x 200 / 300, or 0.4667 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Response at 200 mg with a hyperbolic Emax curve" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_0 = 0.2; E_max = 0.4; D = 200; ED_50 = 100; h = 1; E_D = 0.4667" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOSE-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "response-at-200-mg-with-a-hyperbolic-emax-curve" .

hemo:7002989 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same sigmoid Emax curve as the response formula"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The share follows from HE-FM-DOSE-001 by subtracting E_0 and dividing by E_max, so it carries the same assumptions about the curve." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same sigmoid Emax curve as the response formula" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DOSE-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-sigmoid-emax-curve-as-the-response-formula" .

hemo:7002990 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Share of the maximum effect from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000566 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With DoseMg, ED50Dose and HillCoef named as in HE-FM-DOSE-001, the formulas return the dose multiple and the share of the maximum effect, held in DoseMultiple and MaxShare." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Share of the maximum effect from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DOSE-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "share-of-the-maximum-effect-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=DoseMg/ED50Dose; =DoseMultiple^HillCoef/(1+DoseMultiple^HillCoef)" .

hemo:7002991 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Share of the maximum effect below one half below ED50 and at least one half from ED50"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "MaxShare is below 0.5 when DoseMultiple is below 1 and at least 0.5 otherwise. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the Hill power left off the numerator, k / (1 + k^h), which gives 0.40 at twice ED50 with h = 2." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Share of the maximum effect below one half below ED50 and at least one half from ED50" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DOSE-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "share-of-the-maximum-effect-below-one-half-below-ed50-and-at-least-one-half-from-ed50" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(DoseMultiple<1,MaxShare<0.5,MaxShare>=0.5)" .

hemo:7002992 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Doubling the dose from ED50 with a hyperbolic curve"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With h = 1, a dose of twice ED_50 reaches 2 / 3 of the maximum effect, 0.667, against 0.5 at ED_50, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Doubling the dose from ED50 with a hyperbolic curve" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 200; ED_50 = 100; h = 1; k = 2; S = 0.667" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOSE-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "doubling-the-dose-from-ed50-with-a-hyperbolic-curve" .

hemo:7002993 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Doubling the dose from ED50 with a Hill coefficient of 2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With h = 2 the same doubling reaches 4 / 5 of the maximum, 0.80, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Doubling the dose from ED50 with a Hill coefficient of 2" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 200; ED_50 = 100; h = 2; k = 2; S = 0.8" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOSE-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "doubling-the-dose-from-ed50-with-a-hill-coefficient-of-2" .

hemo:7002994 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Half the maximum effect at ED50"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At D = ED_50 the share is one half whatever the Hill coefficient, as the definition of ED_50 requires." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Half the maximum effect at ED50" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 100; ED_50 = 100; h = 2; k = 1; S = 0.5" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOSE-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "half-the-maximum-effect-at-ed50" .

hemo:7002995 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One vial size and no sharing of opened vials"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "All vials hold v mg at p_v pounds and any drug left in an opened vial is discarded; with several vial sizes the cheapest combination covering the dose replaces n_v times p_v." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One vial size and no sharing of opened vials" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DOSE-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-vial-size-and-no-sharing-of-opened-vials" .

hemo:7002996 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Whole-vial, shared and wasted drug cost from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000567 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With AdminDose, VialMg and VialPrice named, ROUNDUP returns the vials opened into VialsOpened, and the formulas return the whole-vial cost, the shared cost and the wasted cost, held in VialCost, SharedCost and WasteCost." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Whole-vial, shared and wasted drug cost from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DOSE-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "whole-vial-shared-and-wasted-drug-cost-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUNDUP(AdminDose/VialMg,0); =VialsOpened*VialPrice; =AdminDose*VialPrice/VialMg; =VialCost-SharedCost" .

hemo:7002997 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Vials opened are the fewest that cover the dose"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "VialsOpened is a whole number, VialsOpened times VialMg covers AdminDose and one vial fewer would not. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the vial count rounded to the nearest whole number, which opens one 100 mg vial for a 120 mg dose." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Vials opened are the fewest that cover the dose" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DOSE-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "vials-opened-are-the-fewest-that-cover-the-dose" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(VialsOpened=INT(VialsOpened),VialsOpened*VialMg>=AdminDose,(VialsOpened-1)*VialMg<AdminDose)" .

hemo:7002998 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Wasted drug costs less than one vial"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "WasteCost is not negative and is below VialPrice, since at most part of one vial is discarded. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows three vials opened for 150 mg, which wastes 450 pounds, more than one vial." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Wasted drug costs less than one vial" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DOSE-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "wasted-drug-costs-less-than-one-vial" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(WasteCost>=-1E-9*VialPrice,WasteCost<VialPrice)" .

hemo:7002999 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "150 mg dose from 100 mg vials at 300 pounds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A 150 mg dose needs two 100 mg vials, 600 pounds, against 450 pounds with sharing, so 150 pounds of drug is discarded each time; over 12 administrations the course costs 7,200 pounds, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "150 mg dose from 100 mg vials at 300 pounds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_v = 2; p_v = 300; D = 150; v = 100; C_vial = 600; C_share = 450; C_waste = 150" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOSE-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "150-mg-dose-from-100-mg-vials-at-300-pounds" .

hemo:7003000 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "200 mg dose from 100 mg vials at 300 pounds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A 200 mg dose uses the same two vials with nothing wasted, so both costs are 600 pounds, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "200 mg dose from 100 mg vials at 300 pounds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_v = 2; p_v = 300; D = 200; v = 100; C_vial = 600; C_share = 600; C_waste = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOSE-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "200-mg-dose-from-100-mg-vials-at-300-pounds" .

hemo:7003001 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Drug cost in proportion to the dose delivered under RDI scaling"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The scaling assumes the drug cost falls in proportion to the dose; under whole-vial pricing a reduced dose saves money only when fewer vials are opened." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Drug cost in proportion to the dose delivered under RDI scaling" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DOSE-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "drug-cost-in-proportion-to-the-dose-delivered-under-rdi-scaling" .

hemo:7003002 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "RDI from the trial that supplies the efficacy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Trial efficacy already reflects the doses received in the trial, so an RDI from the same trial lowers cost without changing effect; an RDI from another source breaks that link." ;
    hemo:9000009 "RDI from the trial that supplies the efficacy" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DOSE-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rdi-from-the-trial-that-supplies-the-efficacy" .

hemo:7003003 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Drug cost after relative dose intensity from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000568 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With PlannedCost and RelDoseInt named, the formula returns the modelled drug cost, held in DrugCostRDI." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Drug cost after relative dose intensity from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DOSE-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "drug-cost-after-relative-dose-intensity-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PlannedCost*RelDoseInt" .

hemo:7003004 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Relative dose intensity entered as a proportion and cost no higher than planned"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "RelDoseInt is above 0 and no higher than 1, and DrugCostRDI does not exceed PlannedCost. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an RDI of 90 per cent entered as 90, which gives a course cost of 486,000 pounds." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Relative dose intensity entered as a proportion and cost no higher than planned" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DOSE-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "relative-dose-intensity-entered-as-a-proportion-and-cost-no-higher-than-planned" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(RelDoseInt>0,RelDoseInt<=1,DrugCostRDI<=PlannedCost)" .

hemo:7003005 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Course at 150 mg with vial sharing and an RDI of 0.90"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A planned course costing 5,400 pounds with vial sharing costs 4,860 pounds at an RDI of 0.90 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Course at 150 mg with vial sharing and an RDI of 0.90" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_planned = 5400; RDI = 0.9; C_drug = 4860" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOSE-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "course-at-150-mg-with-vial-sharing-and-an-rdi-of-0-90" .

hemo:7003006 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Planned cost at the lower end of the RDI range in NICE appraisals"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At an RDI of 0.85, the lower end of the 85 to 100 per cent range Dasgupta and colleagues report, a planned cost of 600 pounds per administration becomes 510 pounds (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Planned cost at the lower end of the RDI range in NICE appraisals" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_planned = 600; RDI = 0.85; C_drug = 510" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DOSE-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "planned-cost-at-the-lower-end-of-the-rdi-range-in-nice-appraisals" .

hemo:7003007 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Amounts fall at whole-year points with year 0 as the start of treatment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each cost and QALY is treated as falling at a single point in its year and is discounted by the discrete annual factor, with the discount base year fixed at the start of treatment, the rule Attema and colleagues recommend to stop the base year being moved to improve a ratio." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Amounts fall at whole-year points with year 0 as the start of treatment" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DDIS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "amounts-fall-at-whole-year-points-with-year-0-as-the-start-of-treatment" .

hemo:7003008 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Increments over the same comparator for each programme"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "C_0, C_a and Q_b are differences from no intervention, and programmes compared on their ratios are independent of each other, as in the article's example of a prevention programme and a treatment." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Increments over the same comparator for each programme" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DDIS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "increments-over-the-same-comparator-for-each-programme" .

hemo:7003009 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted cost, discounted QALYs and ratio of a two-instalment programme from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000569 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With CostY0, CostYa, YearA, QALYb, YearB, RateC and RateH named, the formulas return the discounted cost, the discounted QALY gain and the ratio, held in DiscCost, DiscQALY and ICERval." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted cost, discounted QALYs and ratio of a two-instalment programme from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DDIS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-cost-discounted-qalys-and-ratio-of-a-two-instalment-programme-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CostY0+CostYa/(1+RateC)^YearA; =QALYb/(1+RateH)^YearB; =DiscCost/DiscQALY" .

hemo:7003010 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discount rates entered as decimals with the health rate no higher than the cost rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "RateC is at least 0 and below 1, and RateH is at least 0 and no higher than RateC, as in all three of the article's pairs. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the rates entered as percentages (3.5 and 1.5), which shrink the discounted gain to almost nothing, or the two rates entered the wrong way round." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discount rates entered as decimals with the health rate no higher than the cost rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DDIS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discount-rates-entered-as-decimals-with-the-health-rate-no-higher-than-the-cost-rate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(RateC>=0,RateC<1,RateH>=0,RateH<=RateC)" .

hemo:7003011 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounting shrinks the QALY gain and the second instalment"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "DiscQALY is no larger than QALYb, and DiscCost lies between CostY0 and CostY0 plus CostYa. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the discount factor multiplied in place of divided, which turns the 1.2 QALYs of the prevention programme into 2.39 at 3.5 per cent." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounting shrinks the QALY gain and the second instalment" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DDIS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounting-shrinks-the-qaly-gain-and-the-second-instalment" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(DiscQALY<=QALYb,DiscCost>=CostY0,DiscCost<=CostY0+CostYa)" .

hemo:7003012 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Prevention programme with both streams discounted at 3.5 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Costs of 12,000 pounds in year 0 and in year 10 and a gain of 1.2 QALYs in year 20, discounted at the NICE reference-case 3.5 per cent for both streams, give a discounted cost of 20,507.03 pounds, a discounted gain of 0.60308 QALYs and a ratio of 34,004 pounds per QALY, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prevention programme with both streams discounted at 3.5 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_0 = 12000; C_a = 12000; a = 10; Q_b = 1.2; b = 20; r_C = 0.035; r_H = 0.035; C_d = 20507.03; Q_d = 0.60308; ICER = 34004" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DDIS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prevention-programme-with-both-streams-discounted-at-3-5-per-cent" .

hemo:7003013 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Prevention programme with both streams discounted at 1.5 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At 1.5 per cent for both streams the same programme has a discounted cost of 22,340.01 pounds, a gain of 0.89096 QALYs and a ratio of 25,074 pounds per QALY, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prevention programme with both streams discounted at 1.5 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_0 = 12000; C_a = 12000; a = 10; Q_b = 1.2; b = 20; r_C = 0.015; r_H = 0.015; C_d = 22340.01; Q_d = 0.89096; ICER = 25074" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DDIS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prevention-programme-with-both-streams-discounted-at-1-5-per-cent" .

hemo:7003014 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Prevention programme with costs at 3 per cent and health at 1.5 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Under the Dutch reference-case pair only the year-10 cost changes from the previous example: the discounted cost is 20,929.13 pounds and the ratio 23,490 pounds per QALY, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prevention programme with costs at 3 per cent and health at 1.5 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_0 = 12000; C_a = 12000; a = 10; Q_b = 1.2; b = 20; r_C = 0.03; r_H = 0.015; C_d = 20929.13; Q_d = 0.89096; ICER = 23490" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DDIS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prevention-programme-with-costs-at-3-per-cent-and-health-at-1-5-per-cent" .

hemo:7003015 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment with its whole cost in year 0 and its QALY gain in year 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The article's treatment costs 20,000 pounds in year 0, entered here with no second instalment, and gains 0.8 QALYs in year 1, so only the QALYs are discounted: 25,875 pounds per QALY at 3.5 per cent, and 25,375 under either pair with a health rate of 1.5 per cent. The prevention programme has the lower ratio under both pairs with a 1.5 per cent health rate and the higher ratio at 3.5 per cent." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Treatment with its whole cost in year 0 and its QALY gain in year 1" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_0 = 20000; C_a = 0; a = 1; Q_b = 0.8; b = 1; r_C = 0.035; r_H = 0.035; C_d = 20000; Q_d = 0.77295; ICER = 25875" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DDIS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "treatment-with-its-whole-cost-in-year-0-and-its-qaly-gain-in-year-1" .

hemo:7003016 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Health measured in QALYs whose money value grows at a constant rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Costs are valued as forgone consumption and discounted at r_C, health effects are counted in QALYs, and the money value of a QALY grows at the same rate g_v in every year; in the Gravelle and Smith welfare model g_v depends on growth in the direct utility value of health, income growth, the elasticity of the marginal utility of income and insurance against the income losses of ill health." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Health measured in QALYs whose money value grows at a constant rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DDIS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "health-measured-in-qalys-whose-money-value-grows-at-a-constant-rate" .

hemo:7003017 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Gravelle and Smith framing with no binding health budget"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The derivation values health in consumption terms; Claxton and colleagues show that with a fixed health budget and decisions based on incremental ratios the gap between the rates comes instead from growth in the threshold (HE-FM-DDIS-003)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gravelle and Smith framing with no binding health budget" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DDIS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gravelle-and-smith-framing-with-no-binding-health-budget" .

hemo:7003018 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Exact and subtraction health discount rates from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000570 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With RateC and GrowthV named, the formulas return the exact health rate and the subtraction approximation, held in HealthRate and HealthRateSub." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exact and subtraction health discount rates from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DDIS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exact-and-subtraction-health-discount-rates-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(1+RateC)/(1+GrowthV)-1; =RateC-GrowthV" .

hemo:7003019 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounting at the health rate equals inflating at the growth rate and discounting at the cost rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a QALY in year 20, (1 plus GrowthV) to the power 20 divided by (1 plus RateC) to the power 20 equals (1 plus HealthRate) to the power minus 20. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the subtraction rate used as if exact: 1.5 per cent gives a weight of 0.74247 where the equivalence needs 0.74572." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounting at the health rate equals inflating at the growth rate and discounting at the cost rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DDIS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounting-at-the-health-rate-equals-inflating-at-the-growth-rate-and-discounting-at-the-cost-rate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((1+GrowthV)^20/(1+RateC)^20-(1+HealthRate)^-20)<1E-12" .

hemo:7003020 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cost rate and growth rate entered as decimals"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "RateC and GrowthV are each above minus 1 and below 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows growth entered as 1.5 for 1.5 per cent, which gives a health rate of about minus 0.59." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cost rate and growth rate entered as decimals" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DDIS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cost-rate-and-growth-rate-entered-as-decimals" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(RateC>-1,RateC<1,GrowthV>-1,GrowthV<1)" .

hemo:7003021 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cost rate of 3 per cent and growth of 1.5 per cent in the value of health"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The exact health rate is 1.03 divided by 1.015, minus one, or 0.0148, about 1.48 per cent, slightly below the 1.5 per cent given by subtraction, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cost rate of 3 per cent and growth of 1.5 per cent in the value of health" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r_C = 0.03; g_v = 0.015; r_H = 0.0148; r_H_sub = 0.015" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DDIS-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cost-rate-of-3-per-cent-and-growth-of-1-5-per-cent-in-the-value-of-health" .

hemo:7003022 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Growth at the low end of the Dutch estimate of 0.6 to 2.9 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With growth of 0.6 per cent the exact health rate would be about 2.39 per cent and the subtraction rate 2.4 per cent (computed here for illustration); the Dutch guideline uses a growth rate of 1.5 per cent, slightly below the average of its range." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Growth at the low end of the Dutch estimate of 0.6 to 2.9 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r_C = 0.03; g_v = 0.006; r_H = 0.0239; r_H_sub = 0.024" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DDIS-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "growth-at-the-low-end-of-the-dutch-estimate-of-0-6-to-2-9-per-cent" .

hemo:7003023 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed budget with the threshold set by displaced care"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Extra spending displaces other care at the margin, so health forgone in year t is the cost divided by the threshold k_t, and k_t grows at a constant rate g_k, k_(t+1) = k_t (1 + g_k), as Attema and colleagues set out." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fixed budget with the threshold set by displaced care" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DDIS-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fixed-budget-with-the-threshold-set-by-displaced-care" .

hemo:7003024 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Health forgone discounted at the same rate as health gained"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Displaced and gained health are discounted at one health rate r_H, so the comparison of a programme's gains with the health its costs displace is made in present QALYs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Health forgone discounted at the same rate as health gained" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DDIS-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "health-forgone-discounted-at-the-same-rate-as-health-gained" .

hemo:7003025 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Effective cost rate and discounted health forgone from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000571 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With RateH, GrowthK, CostT, ThreshK0 and YearT named, the formulas return the effective cost rate and the present health forgone, held in EffCostRate and HealthForgone." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Effective cost rate and discounted health forgone from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DDIS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "effective-cost-rate-and-discounted-health-forgone-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(1+RateH)*(1+GrowthK)-1; =CostT/(ThreshK0*(1+GrowthK)^YearT*(1+RateH)^YearT)" .

hemo:7003026 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Health forgone equals the cost discounted at the effective rate and divided by today's threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "HealthForgone equals CostT divided by ThreshK0 times (1 plus EffCostRate) to the power YearT. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the effective rate taken as the sum of the two rates, 0.03, which gives 0.4465 QALYs against 0.4455." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Health forgone equals the cost discounted at the effective rate and divided by today's threshold" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DDIS-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "health-forgone-equals-the-cost-discounted-at-the-effective-rate-and-divided-by-today-s-threshold" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(HealthForgone-CostT/(ThreshK0*(1+EffCostRate)^YearT))<1E-12" .

hemo:7003027 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Effective cost rate at least the health rate when the threshold does not fall"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "EffCostRate is no lower than RateH exactly when GrowthK is 0 or more, allowing for rounding of 1E-12. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the threshold growth subtracted in place of added, which gives about zero for the example rates." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Effective cost rate at least the health rate when the threshold does not fall" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DDIS-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "effective-cost-rate-at-least-the-health-rate-when-the-threshold-does-not-fall" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(EffCostRate-RateH>=-1E-12)=(GrowthK>=0)" .

hemo:7003028 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Threshold growing at 1.5 per cent with a health rate of 1.5 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An effective cost rate of about 3.02 per cent follows, and 12,000 pounds spent in year 10 against a threshold of 20,000 pounds per QALY today displaces about 0.4455 present QALYs (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Threshold growing at 1.5 per cent with a health rate of 1.5 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r_H = 0.015; g_k = 0.015; C_t = 12000; k_0 = 20000; t = 10; r_C_star = 0.030225; H_PV = 0.4455" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DDIS-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "threshold-growing-at-1-5-per-cent-with-a-health-rate-of-1-5-per-cent" .

hemo:7003029 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant threshold with a health rate of 1.5 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With no threshold growth the effective cost rate equals the health rate and the same cost displaces about 0.5170 present QALYs, the case in which Claxton and colleagues find equal rates correct (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant threshold with a health rate of 1.5 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r_H = 0.015; g_k = 0; C_t = 12000; k_0 = 20000; t = 10; r_C_star = 0.015; H_PV = 0.517" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DDIS-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-threshold-with-a-health-rate-of-1-5-per-cent" .

hemo:7003030 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Whole programme shifted with unchanged amounts and rates"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every cost and QALY moves by the same s years with no change in its size, and both rates stay constant; Keeler and Cretin state their delay result for the case in which the ability to produce the health effect does not diminish too quickly over time." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Whole programme shifted with unchanged amounts and rates" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DDIS-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "whole-programme-shifted-with-unchanged-amounts-and-rates" .

hemo:7003031 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Delay factor and delayed ratio from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000572 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With RateH, RateC and DelayYears named and ICERval, CostY0, CostYa, YearA, QALYb and YearB from HE-FM-DDIS-001, the formulas return the delay factor and the delayed ratio, held in DelayFactor and ICERDelayed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Delay factor and delayed ratio from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DDIS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "delay-factor-and-delayed-ratio-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=((1+RateH)/(1+RateC))^DelayYears; =ICERval*DelayFactor" .

hemo:7003032 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Delayed ratio equals the ratio recomputed with every year moved by the delay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "ICERDelayed equals the two-instalment ratio of HE-FM-DDIS-001 recomputed with YearA and YearB increased by DelayYears and the year-0 cost discounted for DelayYears. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the factor inverted, (1.03 / 1.015) to the power 10, which raises the ratio to about 27,202 pounds per QALY." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Delayed ratio equals the ratio recomputed with every year moved by the delay" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DDIS-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "delayed-ratio-equals-the-ratio-recomputed-with-every-year-moved-by-the-delay" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ICERDelayed-(CostY0/(1+RateC)^DelayYears+CostYa/(1+RateC)^(YearA+DelayYears))/(QALYb/(1+RateH)^(YearB+DelayYears)))<1E-6*ICERDelayed" .

hemo:7003033 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Delay factor below one exactly when the health rate is below the cost rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a positive DelayYears, DelayFactor is below 1 when RateH is below RateC and equals 1 under equal rates. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the exponent entered as minus DelayYears, which gives a factor of about 1.158 for the example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Delay factor below one exactly when the health rate is below the cost rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DDIS-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "delay-factor-below-one-exactly-when-the-health-rate-is-below-the-cost-rate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(DelayYears>0,(DelayFactor<1)=(RateH<RateC),TRUE)" .

hemo:7003034 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Prevention programme delayed by 10 years at 3 and 1.5 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The factor is (1.015 / 1.03) to the power 10, about 0.86355, so the ratio of 23,490 pounds per QALY falls to 20,285, about 14 per cent lower for an unchanged programme, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prevention programme delayed by 10 years at 3 and 1.5 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r_H = 0.015; r_C = 0.03; s = 10; ICER_0 = 23490; F_s = 0.86355; ICER_s = 20285" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DDIS-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prevention-programme-delayed-by-10-years-at-3-and-1-5-per-cent" .

hemo:7003035 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Prevention programme delayed by 10 years at 3.5 per cent for both streams"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Under equal rates the factor is one and the ratio stays at 34,004 pounds per QALY (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prevention programme delayed by 10 years at 3.5 per cent for both streams" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r_H = 0.035; r_C = 0.035; s = 10; ICER_0 = 34004; F_s = 1; ICER_s = 34004" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DDIS-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prevention-programme-delayed-by-10-years-at-3-5-per-cent-for-both-streams" .

hemo:7003036 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discount base year placed five years before the start of the programme"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Moving the base year earlier by five years has the same arithmetic as a five-year delay: at 3 and 1.5 per cent the factor is about 0.92927 and the ratio falls from 23,490 to about 21,829 pounds per QALY (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discount base year placed five years before the start of the programme" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r_H = 0.015; r_C = 0.03; s = 5; ICER_0 = 23490; F_s = 0.92927; ICER_s = 21829" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DDIS-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discount-base-year-placed-five-years-before-the-start-of-the-programme" .

hemo:7003037 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive parameters and components that add to one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every alpha_j is above zero and the components p_1, p_2 and p_3 are non-negative and add to one, so the row is a valid row of a transition matrix in every draw." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive parameters and components that add to one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DIRI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-parameters-and-components-that-add-to-one" .

hemo:7003038 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One precision parameter for the whole row"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Once the means are fixed, every variance and covariance follows from alpha_0, so the row cannot carry a well-estimated death probability alongside a poorly estimated progression probability from a different source." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One precision parameter for the whole row" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DIRI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-precision-parameter-for-the-whole-row" .

hemo:7003039 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Dirichlet moments for a three-destination row from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000573 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Alpha1, Alpha2 and Alpha3 named, the formulas return the parameter sum, the mean and variance of the second component, the variance of the first, their covariance and their correlation, held in AlphaSum, MeanP2, VarP2, VarP1, CovP12 and CorrP12." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Dirichlet moments for a three-destination row from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DIRI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "dirichlet-moments-for-a-three-destination-row-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Alpha1+Alpha2+Alpha3; =Alpha2/AlphaSum; =Alpha2*(AlphaSum-Alpha2)/(AlphaSum^2*(AlphaSum+1)); =Alpha1*(AlphaSum-Alpha1)/(AlphaSum^2*(AlphaSum+1)); =-Alpha1*Alpha2/(AlphaSum^2*(AlphaSum+1)); =CovP12/SQRT(VarP1*VarP2)" .

hemo:7003040 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Variance of a Dirichlet component cancels its covariances with the rest of the row"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Because the row always adds to one, VarP2 plus CovP12 plus the covariance of the second and third components, minus Alpha2 times Alpha3 over AlphaSum squared times (AlphaSum plus 1), is zero. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the variance written with AlphaSum cubed in place of AlphaSum squared times (AlphaSum plus 1), 0.0016 in place of 0.001584." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Variance of a Dirichlet component cancels its covariances with the rest of the row" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DIRI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "variance-of-a-dirichlet-component-cancels-its-covariances-with-the-rest-of-the-row" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(VarP2+CovP12-Alpha2*Alpha3/(AlphaSum^2*(AlphaSum+1)))<1E-15" .

hemo:7003041 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Correlation of two Dirichlet components negative and above minus one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "CorrP12 is below 0 and above minus 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the minus sign left off the covariance, which turns the correlation of the example to plus 0.76." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Correlation of two Dirichlet components negative and above minus one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DIRI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "correlation-of-two-dirichlet-components-negative-and-above-minus-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(CorrP12<0,CorrP12>-1)" .

hemo:7003042 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Row fitted to 70 stable, 20 progressed and 10 dead out of 100"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the zero prior the row is Dirichlet(70, 20, 10): the progression probability has mean 0.20 and variance 0.001584 (standard deviation about 0.0398), the covariance between staying stable and progressing is minus 0.001386, and their correlation is about minus 0.76, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Row fitted to 70 stable, 20 progressed and 10 dead out of 100" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha_1 = 70; alpha_2 = 20; alpha_3 = 10; alpha_0 = 100; E_2 = 0.2; V_2 = 0.001584; V_1 = 0.002079; C_12 = -0.001386; R_12 = -0.7638" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DIRI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "row-fitted-to-70-stable-20-progressed-and-10-dead-out-of-100" .

hemo:7003043 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same proportions observed in 10 patients"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Dirichlet(7, 2, 1) has the same means but about nine times the variance, 0.014545 for progression, while the correlation is unchanged at about minus 0.76 because it depends only on the means (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same proportions observed in 10 patients" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha_1 = 7; alpha_2 = 2; alpha_3 = 1; alpha_0 = 10; E_2 = 0.2; V_2 = 0.014545; V_1 = 0.019091; C_12 = -0.012727; R_12 = -0.7638" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DIRI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-proportions-observed-in-10-patients" .

hemo:7003044 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Row after a uniform prior is added to the counts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Adding one to each count gives Dirichlet(71, 21, 11), with a progression mean of 0.204 as in the article and a slightly smaller variance of 0.001561 (variance and correlation computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Row after a uniform prior is added to the counts" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha_1 = 71; alpha_2 = 21; alpha_3 = 11; alpha_0 = 103; E_2 = 0.2039; V_2 = 0.001561; V_1 = 0.002059; C_12 = -0.001351; R_12 = -0.7538" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DIRI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "row-after-a-uniform-prior-is-added-to-the-counts" .

hemo:7003045 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Counts from the population, starting state and interval of the model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The counts come from patients in the same starting state, followed over an interval equal to the model cycle without irregular or censored follow-up, each counted in exactly one destination." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Counts from the population, starting state and interval of the model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DIRI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "counts-from-the-population-starting-state-and-interval-of-the-model" .

hemo:7003046 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Zero prior valid only when every destination was observed"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Setting every a_j to zero gives an improper prior whose posterior is proper only if each destination has at least one observation; a clinically impossible transition, such as a return from death, is left out of the row as a structural zero rather than given prior weight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Zero prior valid only when every destination was observed" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DIRI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "zero-prior-valid-only-when-every-destination-was-observed" .

hemo:7003047 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior Dirichlet parameter, beta marginal and mean from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000574 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With PriorJ, CountJ, PriorSum and CountSum named, the formulas return the posterior parameter, the second parameter of the beta marginal and the posterior mean, held in AlphaJ, BetaJ and MeanJ. With the posterior parameters of the whole row in a range named AlphaRow, the row checks below apply." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Posterior Dirichlet parameter, beta marginal and mean from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DIRI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "posterior-dirichlet-parameter-beta-marginal-and-mean-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PriorJ+CountJ; =PriorSum+CountSum-AlphaJ; =AlphaJ/(PriorSum+CountSum)" .

hemo:7003048 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Both parameters of the beta marginal above zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "AlphaJ and BetaJ are both above 0, as GAMMA.INV and BETA.INV require. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a destination with a zero count and the zero prior, for which the spreadsheet functions return the #NUM! error." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Both parameters of the beta marginal above zero" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DIRI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "both-parameters-of-the-beta-marginal-above-zero" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(AlphaJ>0,BetaJ>0)" .

hemo:7003049 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior means across the row add to one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The posterior parameters in AlphaRow, divided by PriorSum plus CountSum, add to 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the prior added to the counts but left out of the denominator, which gives 103 / 100 = 1.03 for the uniform-prior example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Posterior means across the row add to one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DIRI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "posterior-means-across-the-row-add-to-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUM(AlphaRow)/(PriorSum+CountSum)-1)<1E-12" .

hemo:7003050 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Progression count of 20 out of 100 with the zero prior"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The posterior parameter is 20, the beta marginal is Beta(20, 80) and the mean is the observed proportion of 0.20, as in the article; the central 95 per cent of that beta runs from about 0.128 to 0.283." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Progression count of 20 out of 100 with the zero prior" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_j = 0; n_j = 20; A_0 = 0; N = 100; alpha_j = 20; b_j = 80; E_j = 0.2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DIRI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "progression-count-of-20-out-of-100-with-the-zero-prior" .

hemo:7003051 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Progression count of 20 out of 100 with a uniform prior over three destinations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "One is added to each of the three counts, so the parameter is 21 and the mean 21 / 103 = 0.204, as in the article's Dirichlet(71, 21, 11); with 100 patients the prior changes little." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Progression count of 20 out of 100 with a uniform prior over three destinations" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_j = 1; n_j = 20; A_0 = 3; N = 100; alpha_j = 21; b_j = 82; E_j = 0.2039" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DIRI-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "progression-count-of-20-out-of-100-with-a-uniform-prior-over-three-destinations" .

hemo:7003052 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Return from the progressed state never observed in 60 patients"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 0 returning, 45 remaining progressed and 15 dying, the zero prior gives no valid distribution, while the uniform prior gives Dirichlet(1, 46, 16), a mean return probability of 1 / 63 = 0.016 and a beta marginal Beta(1, 62) whose central 95 per cent runs from about 0.0004 to 0.058, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Return from the progressed state never observed in 60 patients" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_j = 1; n_j = 0; A_0 = 3; N = 60; alpha_j = 1; b_j = 62; E_j = 0.0159" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DIRI-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "return-from-the-progressed-state-never-observed-in-60-patients" .

hemo:7003053 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Anchor correlated with the change score"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The anchor is valid for the score: Terwee and colleagues ask for a correlation of at least 0.30 between the change score and the anchor, and the credibility instrument of Devji and colleagues treats at least 0.5 as moderate to high; the article's example has 0.52." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Anchor correlated with the change score" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MCID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "anchor-correlated-with-the-change-score" .

hemo:7003054 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Both anchor groups from the same cohort and interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The two groups were measured with the same instrument over the same interval, and the category that counts as minimal on the anchor is chosen before the analysis." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Both anchor groups from the same cohort and interval" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MCID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "both-anchor-groups-from-the-same-cohort-and-interval" .

hemo:7003055 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Between-group minimal important difference from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000575 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With MeanChgMin and MeanChgSame named, the formula returns the between-group estimate, held in MIDBetween." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Between-group minimal important difference from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MCID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "between-group-minimal-important-difference-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MeanChgMin-MeanChgSame" .

hemo:7003056 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Minimally improved group changed more than the unchanged group"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For improvement MeanChgMin is above MeanChgSame and MIDBetween is their difference, so it is positive. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the two groups entered the wrong way round, which gives minus 6.0 points." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Minimally improved group changed more than the unchanged group" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MCID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "minimally-improved-group-changed-more-than-the-unchanged-group" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(MeanChgMin>MeanChgSame,ABS(MIDBetween-(MeanChgMin-MeanChgSame))<1E-12)" .

hemo:7003057 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Validation cohort with mean changes of 8.0 and 2.0 points"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Patients rating themselves a little better improved by 8.0 points on average and those rating themselves about the same by 2.0, so the between-group estimate is 8.0 minus 2.0, or 6.0 points, as in the article; the mean change method alone would give 8.0." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Validation cohort with mean changes of 8.0 and 2.0 points" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_M = 8; d_S = 2; MID_between = 6" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "validation-cohort-with-mean-changes-of-8-0-and-2-0-points" .

hemo:7003058 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Deterioration in the same cohort"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Patients rating themselves a little worse changed by minus 5.0 points, so the between-group estimate for deterioration is minus 7.0 points, larger in size than the 6.0 for improvement (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Deterioration in the same cohort" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_M = -5; d_S = 2; MID_between = -7" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "deterioration-in-the-same-cohort" .

hemo:7003059 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Anchor as reference standard with a fixed split of the cohort"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The anchor divides the cohort into improved and not improved before any cut-off is tried, and a patient reaches a cut-off when the change is at least the cut-off; in the article's example the 90 patients rating themselves better are improved and the 110 others are the reference group." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Anchor as reference standard with a fixed split of the cohort" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MCID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "anchor-as-reference-standard-with-a-fixed-split-of-the-cohort" .

hemo:7003060 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Share of improved patients near one half"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Terwee and colleagues note that the ROC estimate is biased when the share of improved patients is not 50 per cent; in the article's example it is 45 per cent, so a predictive modelling estimate would be a useful check." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Share of improved patients near one half" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MCID-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "share-of-improved-patients-near-one-half" .

hemo:7003061 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Sensitivity, specificity, misclassification sum and Youden index of one cut-off from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000576 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With ImpReach, ImpTotal, NotImpReach and NotImpTotal named, the formulas return the sensitivity, the specificity, the misclassification sum and the Youden index, held in SensC, SpecC, MisclassSum and YoudenJ." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sensitivity, specificity, misclassification sum and Youden index of one cut-off from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MCID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sensitivity-specificity-misclassification-sum-and-youden-index-of-one-cut-off-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ImpReach/ImpTotal; =(NotImpTotal-NotImpReach)/NotImpTotal; =(1-SensC)+(1-SpecC); =SensC+SpecC-1" .

hemo:7003062 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Sensitivity and specificity consistent with the counts in each anchor group"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "ImpReach is no more than ImpTotal and NotImpReach no more than NotImpTotal, SensC times ImpTotal returns ImpReach, and (1 minus SpecC) times NotImpTotal returns NotImpReach. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows specificity entered as the share of the reference group reaching the cut-off, 16 / 110 = 0.145 in place of 0.855." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sensitivity and specificity consistent with the counts in each anchor group" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MCID-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sensitivity-and-specificity-consistent-with-the-counts-in-each-anchor-group" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ImpReach<=ImpTotal,NotImpReach<=NotImpTotal,ABS(SensC*ImpTotal-ImpReach)<1E-9,ABS((1-SpecC)*NotImpTotal-NotImpReach)<1E-9)" .

hemo:7003063 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cut-off of 6 points in the article's cohort"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Of 90 improved patients 72 reach 6 points (sensitivity 0.800) and of 110 others 16 do (specificity 94 / 110 = 0.855); the misclassification sum of 0.345 is the smallest of the four cut-offs, so the ROC threshold is 6 points, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cut-off of 6 points in the article's cohort" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_c = 72; N_I = 90; b_c = 16; N_N = 110; Se_c = 0.8; Sp_c = 0.855; M_c = 0.345; J_c = 0.655" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cut-off-of-6-points-in-the-article-s-cohort" .

hemo:7003064 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cut-off of 4 points in the article's cohort"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Eighty improved and 30 other patients reach 4 points, giving sensitivity 0.889, specificity 0.727 and a misclassification sum of 0.384, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cut-off of 4 points in the article's cohort" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_c = 80; N_I = 90; b_c = 30; N_N = 110; Se_c = 0.889; Sp_c = 0.727; M_c = 0.384; J_c = 0.616" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cut-off-of-4-points-in-the-article-s-cohort" .

hemo:7003065 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cut-off of 10 points in the article's cohort"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Forty-five improved and 3 other patients reach 10 points, giving sensitivity 0.500, specificity 0.973 and a misclassification sum of 0.527, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cut-off of 10 points in the article's cohort" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_c = 45; N_I = 90; b_c = 3; N_N = 110; Se_c = 0.5; Sp_c = 0.973; M_c = 0.527; J_c = 0.473" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cut-off-of-10-points-in-the-article-s-cohort" .

hemo:7003066 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Approximately normal change among patients not importantly changed"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The 1.645 multiplier assumes the change scores of the not importantly changed group are close to normal, so that about 5 per cent of them exceed the cut-off; in the article's example that group is the 70 patients rating themselves about the same." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Approximately normal change among patients not importantly changed" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MCID-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "approximately-normal-change-among-patients-not-importantly-changed" .

hemo:7003067 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Ninety-five per cent limit cut-off from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000577 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With MeanChgSame and SDChgSame named, the formula returns the cut-off, held in LimitC95." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ninety-five per cent limit cut-off from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MCID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ninety-five-per-cent-limit-cut-off-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MeanChgSame+1.645*SDChgSame" .

hemo:7003068 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cut-off above the unchanged group's mean change"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "SDChgSame is above 0 and LimitC95 is above MeanChgSame. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the standard deviation subtracted, which gives minus 6.2 points, a limit for deterioration rather than improvement." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cut-off above the unchanged group's mean change" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MCID-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cut-off-above-the-unchanged-group-s-mean-change" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(SDChgSame>0,LimitC95>MeanChgSame)" .

hemo:7003069 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Ninety-five per cent of a normal unchanged group falls below the cut-off"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "NORM.DIST at LimitC95 with the unchanged group's mean and standard deviation returns 0.95. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the two-sided multiplier 1.96 used, which gives a cut-off of 11.8 points and 0.975." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ninety-five per cent of a normal unchanged group falls below the cut-off" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MCID-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ninety-five-per-cent-of-a-normal-unchanged-group-falls-below-the-cut-off" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(NORM.DIST(LimitC95,MeanChgSame,SDChgSame,TRUE)-0.95)<0.0005" .

hemo:7003070 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Unchanged group with mean change 2.0 and standard deviation 5.0"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The cut-off is 2.0 + 1.645 x 5.0 = 10.225, shown as 10.2 points in the article, against 6 for the ROC cut-off and 8.0 for the mean change method." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Unchanged group with mean change 2.0 and standard deviation 5.0" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_S = 2; s_S = 5; c_95 = 10.2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "unchanged-group-with-mean-change-2-0-and-standard-deviation-5-0" .

hemo:7003071 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same mean with a standard deviation of 4.0"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Less spread among unchanged patients lowers the cut-off to 2.0 + 1.645 x 4.0 = 8.58 points (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same mean with a standard deviation of 4.0" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_S = 2; s_S = 4; c_95 = 8.58" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-mean-with-a-standard-deviation-of-4-0" .

hemo:7003072 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal changes with a common standard deviation in both arms"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Changes in each arm are normally distributed and differ only in their means, the simple model Snapinn and Jiang use to compare responder and mean-based analyses; with other shapes the shares have to come from the observed distribution of change." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal changes with a common standard deviation in both arms" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MCID-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-changes-with-a-common-standard-deviation-in-both-arms" .

hemo:7003073 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Responder shares and their difference from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000578 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With CutOff, MeanCtrl, MeanTrt and SDChange named, the formulas return the two standardised distances, the two responder shares and their difference, held in ZCtrl, ZTrt, PropCtrl, PropTrt and RespDiff." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Responder shares and their difference from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MCID-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "responder-shares-and-their-difference-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(CutOff-MeanCtrl)/SDChange; =(CutOff-MeanTrt)/SDChange; =1-NORM.S.DIST(ZCtrl,TRUE); =1-NORM.S.DIST(ZTrt,TRUE); =PropTrt-PropCtrl" .

hemo:7003074 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Responder difference has the same sign as the difference in means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "RespDiff is positive exactly when MeanTrt is above MeanCtrl. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the distances computed as mean minus cut-off, which gives 0.631 with control against 0.500 with treatment and a negative difference." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Responder difference has the same sign as the difference in means" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MCID-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "responder-difference-has-the-same-sign-as-the-difference-in-means" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(RespDiff>0)=(MeanTrt>MeanCtrl)" .

hemo:7003075 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Half of an arm reaches a threshold equal to its mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When CutOff equals MeanTrt, PropTrt is 0.5. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows NORM.S.DIST used without its cumulative argument set to TRUE, which returns the density 0.399 and a share of 0.601." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Half of an arm reaches a threshold equal to its mean" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MCID-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "half-of-an-arm-reaches-a-threshold-equal-to-its-mean" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(CutOff=MeanTrt,ABS(PropTrt-0.5)<1E-12,TRUE)" .

hemo:7003076 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mean changes of 2 and 6 points with standard deviation 12 and a 6-point threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The control mean is a third of a standard deviation below the threshold, so 1 minus Phi(0.333), about 0.369, of control patients reach it; the treated mean equals the threshold, so half do, and the responder difference is about 0.131, as in the article, although the 4-point difference in means is below the between-group MID of 6.0." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mean changes of 2 and 6 points with standard deviation 12 and a 6-point threshold" ;
    hemo:9000014 "c = 6; mu_C = 2; mu_T = 6; sigma = 12; Phi_C = 0.63056; Phi_T = 0.5; z_C = 0.3333; z_T = 0; P_C = 0.3694; P_T = 0.5; RD = 0.1306" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mean-changes-of-2-and-6-points-with-standard-deviation-12-and-a-6-point-threshold" .

hemo:7003077 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same trial with the 10.2-point limit as threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At a threshold of 10.2 points the shares fall to about 0.247 with control and 0.363 with treatment, a difference of about 0.116 (computed here for illustration), so the threshold chosen changes the responder shares a model would use." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same trial with the 10.2-point limit as threshold" ;
    hemo:9000014 "c = 10.2; mu_C = 2; mu_T = 6; sigma = 12; Phi_C = 0.7528; Phi_T = 0.63683; z_C = 0.6833; z_T = 0.35; P_C = 0.2472; P_T = 0.3632; RD = 0.116" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-trial-with-the-10-2-point-limit-as-threshold" .

hemo:7003078 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Two equal arms, a continuous outcome and a two-sided test"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The outcome is approximately normal with the same standard deviation in both arms, the arms are of equal size and the analysis compares means with a two-sided test; other designs need other formulas." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two equal arms, a continuous outcome and a two-sided test" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MCID-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-equal-arms-a-continuous-outcome-and-a-two-sided-test" .

hemo:7003079 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Target difference important to a stakeholder group"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "DELTA2 asks for a target difference that is important to at least one key stakeholder group and realistic; it need not be the minimum important value if a larger difference is realistic." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Target difference important to a stakeholder group" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MCID-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "target-difference-important-to-a-stakeholder-group" .

hemo:7003080 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Patients per arm from the significance level, power, standard deviation and target difference"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000579 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With AlphaLevel, PowerLevel, SDOutcome and TargetDiff named, the formulas return the two normal quantiles, the unrounded number per arm and the number rounded up, held in ZAlpha, ZBeta, NPerArmRaw and NPerArm." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Patients per arm from the significance level, power, standard deviation and target difference" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MCID-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "patients-per-arm-from-the-significance-level-power-standard-deviation-and-target-difference" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=NORM.S.INV(1-AlphaLevel/2); =NORM.S.INV(PowerLevel); =2*(ZAlpha+ZBeta)^2*SDOutcome^2/TargetDiff^2; =ROUNDUP(NPerArmRaw,0)" .

hemo:7003081 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Number per arm times the squared standardised difference over two returns the squared quantile sum"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "NPerArmRaw times TargetDiff squared over (2 times SDOutcome squared) equals (ZAlpha plus ZBeta) squared, 10.51 for 5 per cent and 90 per cent power. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the factor 2 left out, which halves the trial to 42.0 per arm." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Number per arm times the squared standardised difference over two returns the squared quantile sum" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MCID-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "number-per-arm-times-the-squared-standardised-difference-over-two-returns-the-squared-quantile-sum" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(NPerArmRaw*TargetDiff^2/(2*SDOutcome^2)-(ZAlpha+ZBeta)^2)<1E-9" .

hemo:7003082 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Significance level and power entered as proportions and the number rounded up"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "AlphaLevel is above 0 and below 0.5, PowerLevel is above 0.5 and below 1, and NPerArm is at least NPerArmRaw. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows power entered as 90 for 90 per cent, for which NORM.S.INV returns #NUM!, so the check shows that error rather than FALSE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Significance level and power entered as proportions and the number rounded up" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MCID-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "significance-level-and-power-entered-as-proportions-and-the-number-rounded-up" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(AlphaLevel>0,AlphaLevel<0.5,PowerLevel>0.5,PowerLevel<1,NPerArm>=NPerArmRaw)" .

hemo:7003083 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Between-group MID of 6.0 points with standard deviation 12, 5 per cent significance and 90 per cent power"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Twice (1.96 + 1.2816) squared times 144 over 36 gives 84.1, so 85 patients per arm are needed, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Between-group MID of 6.0 points with standard deviation 12, 5 per cent significance and 90 per cent power" ;
    hemo:9000014 "z_a = 1.96; z_b = 1.2816; sigma = 12; delta = 6; n = 84.1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "between-group-mid-of-6-0-points-with-standard-deviation-12-5-per-cent-significance-and-90-per-cent-power" .

hemo:7003084 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Target difference of 4 points in the same trial"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A 4-point target gives 189.1, or 190 patients per arm, as in the article, so the chosen difference drives trial size and cost." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Target difference of 4 points in the same trial" ;
    hemo:9000014 "z_a = 1.96; z_b = 1.2816; sigma = 12; delta = 4; n = 189.1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "target-difference-of-4-points-in-the-same-trial" .

hemo:7003085 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standardised difference of 0.78 with 80 per cent power"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the outcome measured in standard deviations, a difference of 0.78 at 5 per cent significance and 80 per cent power needs 25.8, or 26 per arm, the figure Whitley and Ball give." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standardised difference of 0.78 with 80 per cent power" ;
    hemo:9000014 "z_a = 1.96; z_b = 0.8416; sigma = 1; delta = 0.78; n = 25.8" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MCID-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standardised-difference-of-0-78-with-80-per-cent-power" .

hemo:7003086 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Progressive structure with an absorbing death state"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The annual matrix has zeros below the diagonal (no return from progressed to progression-free) and death has 1 on its diagonal, so the matrix is upper triangular and the closed form applies; other structures need the general root of HE-CF-TMAT-001." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Progressive structure with an absorbing death state" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TMAT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "progressive-structure-with-an-absorbing-death-state" .

hemo:7003087 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same six-month matrix in both halves of the year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The root assumes that one shorter-cycle matrix applies throughout the original interval, so transition risks do not change within the year being split." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same six-month matrix in both halves of the year" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TMAT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-six-month-matrix-in-both-halves-of-the-year" .

hemo:7003088 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Annual matrix with a valid root"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "p_11 and p_22 are above zero and the result has no negative entry; Chhatwal and colleagues list among the necessary conditions for a valid rate matrix that no transition reachable through other states has a zero entry." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annual matrix with a valid root" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TMAT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annual-matrix-with-a-valid-root" .

hemo:7003089 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Six-month root of a progressive three-state annual matrix from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000580 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the annual entries in P11, P12 and P22 named, the formulas return the five non-trivial entries of the six-month matrix, held in R11, R22, R12, R13 and R23." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Six-month root of a progressive three-state annual matrix from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-TMAT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "six-month-root-of-a-progressive-three-state-annual-matrix-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SQRT(P11); =SQRT(P22); =P12/(R11+R22); =1-R11-R12; =1-R22" .

hemo:7003090 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two six-month cycles reproduce the annual progression-free row"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "R11 squared returns P11, R11 times R12 plus R12 times R22 returns P12, and R11 times R13 plus R12 times R23 plus R13 returns the annual death probability 1 minus P11 minus P12. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the cell-by-cell six-month entries 0.843110, 0.105573 and 0.051317, which return 0.710834, 0.170786 and 0.118380 in place of 0.70, 0.20 and 0.10." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two six-month cycles reproduce the annual progression-free row" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-TMAT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-six-month-cycles-reproduce-the-annual-progression-free-row" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS(R11^2-P11)<1E-9,ABS(R11*R12+R12*R22-P12)<1E-9,ABS(R11*R13+R12*R23+R13-(1-P11-P12))<1E-9)" .

hemo:7003091 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Every six-month entry a valid probability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The smallest of R11, R12, R13, R22 and R23 is at least 0 and the largest at most 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows an annual matrix without a valid root, such as the fourth example, whose six-month death probability from progression-free is minus 0.195706." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Every six-month entry a valid probability" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-TMAT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "every-six-month-entry-a-valid-probability" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(MIN(R11,R12,R13,R22,R23)>=0,MAX(R11,R12,R13,R22,R23)<=1)" .

hemo:7003092 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Annual matrix with 70 per cent staying progression-free, 20 per cent progressing and 60 per cent staying progressed"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The square roots of 0.70 and 0.60 are 0.836660 and 0.774597, so the six-month progression probability is 0.20 / 1.611257 = 0.124127, death from progression-free is 0.039213 and death from progressed 0.225403; squaring the root returns 0.100000 for annual death from progression-free, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annual matrix with 70 per cent staying progression-free, 20 per cent progressing and 60 per cent staying progressed" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_11 = 0.7; p_22 = 0.6; p_12 = 0.2; r_11 = 0.83666; r_22 = 0.774597; r_12 = 0.124127; r_13 = 0.039213; r_23 = 0.225403" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TMAT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annual-matrix-with-70-per-cent-staying-progression-free-20-per-cent-progressing-and-60-per-cent-staying-progressed" .

hemo:7003093 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Slower disease with 90 per cent staying progression-free and 6 per cent progressing"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With p_11 = 0.90, p_12 = 0.06 and p_22 = 0.80 the six-month progression probability is 0.032554 and death from progression-free 0.018763, and squaring the root returns the annual death probability of 0.04 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Slower disease with 90 per cent staying progression-free and 6 per cent progressing" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_11 = 0.9; p_22 = 0.8; p_12 = 0.06; r_11 = 0.948683; r_22 = 0.894427; r_12 = 0.032554; r_13 = 0.018763; r_23 = 0.105573" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TMAT-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "slower-disease-with-90-per-cent-staying-progression-free-and-6-per-cent-progressing" .

hemo:7003094 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "No progression, where the root equals the cell-by-cell conversion"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With p_12 = 0 the progression-free row has a single exit to an absorbing state, so the six-month death probability is 1 minus the square root of 0.90, 0.051317, the same as HE-FM-TP-003 gives cell by cell (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No progression, where the root equals the cell-by-cell conversion" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_11 = 0.9; p_22 = 0.6; p_12 = 0; r_11 = 0.948683; r_22 = 0.774597; r_12 = 0; r_13 = 0.051317; r_23 = 0.225403" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TMAT-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-progression-where-the-root-equals-the-cell-by-cell-conversion" .

hemo:7003095 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Annual matrix with no direct death from progression-free has no valid root"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If half stay progression-free and half progress, with no direct death, while 90 per cent of the progressed die each year, the closed form gives a six-month death probability from progression-free of minus 0.195706, not a valid probability, because death is reachable through the progressed state but has a zero annual entry (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annual matrix with no direct death from progression-free has no valid root" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_11 = 0.5; p_22 = 0.1; p_12 = 0.5; r_11 = 0.707107; r_22 = 0.316228; r_12 = 0.488599; r_13 = -0.195706; r_23 = 0.683772" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TMAT-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annual-matrix-with-no-direct-death-from-progression-free-has-no-valid-root" .

hemo:7003096 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant weight over the whole duration of a case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each case carries the same disability weight for its average duration L, which ends at remission or death; a condition with stages needs one term per sequela." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant weight over the whole duration of a case" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-YLD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-weight-over-the-whole-duration-of-a-case" .

hemo:7003097 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Future health loss assigned to the year and age of onset"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The count credits the reference year with health loss that will be lived over the next L years, so it reflects new cases rather than the health loss lived in that year." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Future health loss assigned to the year and age of onset" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-YLD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "future-health-loss-assigned-to-the-year-and-age-of-onset" .

hemo:7003098 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Incidence-based years lived with disability from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000581 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With IncCases, DisWeight and DurationYrs named, the formula returns the incidence-based YLDs, held in YLDInc. PrevYears holds the person-years lived with the condition in the same year, for the steady-state check." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Incidence-based years lived with disability from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-YLD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "incidence-based-years-lived-with-disability-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IncCases*DisWeight*DurationYrs" .

hemo:7003099 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Disability weight on its 0 to 1 scale and YLDs no more than the years lived with the condition"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "DisWeight is at least 0 and at most 1, so YLDInc cannot exceed IncCases times DurationYrs. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the weight entered as 20 for 0.20, which gives 20,000 YLDs for 1,000 years lived with the condition." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Disability weight on its 0 to 1 scale and YLDs no more than the years lived with the condition" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-YLD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "disability-weight-on-its-0-to-1-scale-and-ylds-no-more-than-the-years-lived-with-the-condition" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(DisWeight>=0,DisWeight<=1,YLDInc<=IncCases*DurationYrs)" .

hemo:7003100 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Incidence and prevalence counts agree in a steady state"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When incidence has been stable for at least DurationYrs years, so that PrevYears equals IncCases times DurationYrs, YLDInc equals PrevYears times DisWeight. Expected result: TRUE in a steady state. FALSE shows the duration entered in months, 120 in place of 10, which gives 2,400 YLDs against 200." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Incidence and prevalence counts agree in a steady state" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-YLD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "incidence-and-prevalence-counts-agree-in-a-steady-state" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(YLDInc-PrevYears*DisWeight)<1E-9" .

hemo:7003101 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Condition with 100 new cases a year, a weight of 0.20 and a duration of 10 years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003102,
        hemo:7003103,
        hemo:7003104 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003105 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "This year's 100 new cases give 100 x 0.20 x 10 = 200 YLDs, as in the article's steady state, where the prevalence-based count of 1,000 person-years at 0.20 also gives 200." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Condition with 100 new cases a year, a weight of 0.20 and a duration of 10 years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "I = 100; DW = 0.2; L = 10; YLD_inc = 200" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-YLD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "condition-with-100-new-cases-a-year-a-weight-of-0-20-and-a-duration-of-10-years" .

hemo:7003102 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "I in the test Condition with 100 new cases a year, a weight of 0.20 and a duration of 10 years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002414 ;
    rheo:2000001 100.0 .

hemo:7003103 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "DW in the test Condition with 100 new cases a year, a weight of 0.20 and a duration of 10 years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002415 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.2 .

hemo:7003104 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "L in the test Condition with 100 new cases a year, a weight of 0.20 and a duration of 10 years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002416 ;
    rheo:2000001 10.0 .

hemo:7003105 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "YLD_inc in the test Condition with 100 new cases a year, a weight of 0.20 and a duration of 10 years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002413 ;
    rheo:2000001 200.0 .

hemo:7003106 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same condition after a programme halves new cases to 50 a year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003107,
        hemo:7003108,
        hemo:7003109 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003110 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The incidence-based count falls at once to 50 x 0.20 x 10 = 100 YLDs, crediting the reference year with all the future health loss of the smaller cohort, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same condition after a programme halves new cases to 50 a year" ;
    hemo:9000014 "I = 50; DW = 0.2; L = 10; YLD_inc = 100" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-YLD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-condition-after-a-programme-halves-new-cases-to-50-a-year" .

hemo:7003107 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "I in the test Same condition after a programme halves new cases to 50 a year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002414 ;
    rheo:2000001 50.0 .

hemo:7003108 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "DW in the test Same condition after a programme halves new cases to 50 a year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002415 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.2 .

hemo:7003109 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "L in the test Same condition after a programme halves new cases to 50 a year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002416 ;
    rheo:2000001 10.0 .

hemo:7003110 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "YLD_inc in the test Same condition after a programme halves new cases to 50 a year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002413 ;
    rheo:2000001 100.0 .

hemo:7003111 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous discounting from the year of onset without age weighting"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Health loss is discounted continuously at a constant rate from onset, with the same weight throughout the case; the original DALY also multiplied each year by an age weight, which this form leaves out, as the article does." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuous discounting from the year of onset without age weighting" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-YLD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuous-discounting-from-the-year-of-onset-without-age-weighting" .

hemo:7003112 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted years lived with disability per case and per cohort from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000582 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With DisWeight, DiscRate, DurationYrs and IncCases named, the formulas return the discounted YLDs per case and for the cohort, held in YLDCase and YLDDisc." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted years lived with disability per case and per cohort from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-YLD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-years-lived-with-disability-per-case-and-per-cohort-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=DisWeight*(1-EXP(-DiscRate*DurationYrs))/DiscRate; =IncCases*YLDCase" .

hemo:7003113 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted YLDs per case between the fully discounted and undiscounted bounds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "DiscRate is above 0 and below 1, and YLDCase lies between DisWeight times DurationYrs times EXP(minus DiscRate times DurationYrs) and DisWeight times DurationYrs. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the rate entered as 3 for 3 per cent, or the sign of the exponent dropped, which gives minus 2.33 YLDs per case for the first example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted YLDs per case between the fully discounted and undiscounted bounds" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-YLD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-ylds-per-case-between-the-fully-discounted-and-undiscounted-bounds" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(DiscRate>0,DiscRate<1,YLDCase<=DisWeight*DurationYrs,YLDCase>=DisWeight*DurationYrs*EXP(-DiscRate*DurationYrs))" .

hemo:7003114 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Condition with 100 new cases, a weight of 0.20 and 10 years at 3 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Ten years at 3 per cent are worth 8.639 present years, so each case gives 1.7279 discounted YLDs and the 100 new cases 172.8, against 200 undiscounted; the gap of 27.2 comes from the convention alone, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Condition with 100 new cases, a weight of 0.20 and 10 years at 3 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DW = 0.2; r = 0.03; L = 10; I = 100; YLD_case = 1.7279; YLD_d = 172.8" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-YLD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "condition-with-100-new-cases-a-weight-of-0-20-and-10-years-at-3-per-cent" .

hemo:7003115 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "YLDs averted each year by 50 prevented cases"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A programme that prevents 50 cases a year averts 100 undiscounted YLDs over the 10 years each case would have lasted, or 86.4 with continuous discounting at 3 per cent, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "YLDs averted each year by 50 prevented cases" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DW = 0.2; r = 0.03; L = 10; I = 50; YLD_case = 1.7279; YLD_d = 86.4" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-YLD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ylds-averted-each-year-by-50-prevented-cases" .

hemo:7003116 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Larson's case with a weight of 0.6 for 10 years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "One case at weight 0.6 for 10 years at 3 per cent gives 5.1836 discounted YLDs, the value Larson reproduces from Fox-Rushby and Hanson." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Larson's case with a weight of 0.6 for 10 years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DW = 0.6; r = 0.03; L = 10; I = 1; YLD_case = 5.1836; YLD_d = 5.1836" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-YLD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "larson-s-case-with-a-weight-of-0-6-for-10-years" .

hemo:7003117 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Forty years at full weight"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Forty years at 3 per cent are worth about 23.3 present years before any disability weight is applied, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Forty years at full weight" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DW = 1; r = 0.03; L = 40; I = 1; YLD_case = 23.29; YLD_d = 23.29" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-YLD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "forty-years-at-full-weight" .

hemo:7003118 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed duration with one full person-year per cohort per year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every case lasts exactly L years, causes no deaths and then resolves completely, and each annual cohort contributes one full person-year in each of its L years, as in the article's illustrative condition." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fixed duration with one full person-year per cohort per year" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-YLD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fixed-duration-with-one-full-person-year-per-cohort-per-year" .

hemo:7003119 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One step change in incidence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Incidence was I_old for at least L years before the change and I_new in every year since, so the people living with the condition this year come from these two cohort sizes only." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One step change in incidence" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-YLD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-step-change-in-incidence" .

hemo:7003120 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Prevalence-based years lived with disability after a change in incidence from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000583 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With YearsSince, IncNew, IncOld, DurationYrs and DisWeight named, the formula returns the prevalence-based YLDs for the reference year, held in YLDPrev." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Prevalence-based years lived with disability after a change in incidence from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-YLD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "prevalence-based-years-lived-with-disability-after-a-change-in-incidence-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(YearsSince*IncNew+(DurationYrs-YearsSince)*IncOld)*DisWeight" .

hemo:7003121 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Years since the change within the duration and the count between the two steady states"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "YearsSince is from 0 to DurationYrs, and YLDPrev lies between the steady-state counts for the smaller and the larger incidence. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows YearsSince entered beyond the duration, 12 for a 10-year condition, which gives 80 YLDs, below the 100 of the new steady state." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Years since the change within the duration and the count between the two steady states" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-YLD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "years-since-the-change-within-the-duration-and-the-count-between-the-two-steady-states" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(YearsSince>=0,YearsSince<=DurationYrs,YLDPrev>=MIN(IncNew,IncOld)*DurationYrs*DisWeight,YLDPrev<=MAX(IncNew,IncOld)*DurationYrs*DisWeight)" .

hemo:7003122 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Five years after new cases halved from 100 to 50 a year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Five cohorts of 50 and five of 100 give 750 person-years and (5 x 50 + 5 x 100) x 0.20 = 150 YLDs, a fall of only a quarter while the incidence-based count has halved to 100, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Five years after new cases halved from 100 to 50 a year" ;
    hemo:9000014 "k = 5; I_new = 50; I_old = 100; L = 10; DW = 0.2; YLD_prev = 150" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-YLD-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "five-years-after-new-cases-halved-from-100-to-50-a-year" .

hemo:7003123 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Year before the change"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With k = 0 every cohort is of the old size, 1,000 person-years, and the count is 200, equal to the incidence-based count of the steady state." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Year before the change" ;
    hemo:9000014 "k = 0; I_new = 50; I_old = 100; L = 10; DW = 0.2; YLD_prev = 200" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-YLD-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "year-before-the-change" .

hemo:7003124 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Ten years after the change"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When the last of the larger cohorts has recovered, all 10 cohorts are of 50 and the count is 100, matching the incidence-based count, five years after the article's reference year." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ten years after the change" ;
    hemo:9000014 "k = 10; I_new = 50; I_old = 100; L = 10; DW = 0.2; YLD_prev = 100" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-YLD-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ten-years-after-the-change" .

hemo:7003125 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Each tunnel state lasts exactly one cycle"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A tunnel state has transitions only to the next state in the chain and to exits such as death, never to itself, so its diagonal entry is zero and a person spends at most one cycle in it. Each row of the expanded matrix still sums to 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Each tunnel state lasts exactly one cycle" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TUN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "each-tunnel-state-lasts-exactly-one-cycle" .

hemo:7003126 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Duration effect over a whole number of cycles"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Risks, costs or utilities change over the first K cycles since entry and are constant from cycle K+1 onwards, which is the long-term state. An effect that changes over a period that is not a whole number of cycles has to be approximated by one that is." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Duration effect over a whole number of cycles" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TUN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "duration-effect-over-a-whole-number-of-cycles" .

hemo:7003127 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Every route into the clinical state enters the first tunnel state"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "All entrants, whatever state they come from, start the clock in T_1. Whether a repeat event sends people back to T_1 is a modelling decision; if it does, p_(i,T_1) is above zero for the tunnel states and L, and s_k excludes that route." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Every route into the clinical state enters the first tunnel state" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TUN-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "every-route-into-the-clinical-state-enters-the-first-tunnel-state" .

hemo:7003128 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Tunnel columns of a cohort trace"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000584 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In a trace with one column per state and one row per cycle, the first formula fills the T1 column from the previous row and a row of entry probabilities, the second fills each later tunnel column from the previous tunnel column in the row above, and the third fills the long-term column. Named cells refer to the row above; copied down, the formulas shift each tunnel cohort one column to the right per row." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Tunnel columns of a cohort trace" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-TUN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "tunnel-columns-of-a-cohort-trace" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(PrevRow,EntryProbRow); =PrevTunnel*TunnelSurv; =PrevLastTunnel*LastTunnelSurv+PrevLongTerm*LongTermSurv" .

hemo:7003129 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Tunnel states have a zero diagonal"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the K diagonal entries of the tunnel rows of the expanded matrix in a range named TunnelDiag, the sum of their squares is zero. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a tunnel state in which part of the cohort can stay for a second cycle." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Tunnel states have a zero diagonal" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-TUN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "tunnel-states-have-a-zero-diagonal" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMSQ(TunnelDiag)=0" .

hemo:7003130 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Single-entry cohort reaches the long-term state with the product of tunnel survivals"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a cohort that all enters T1 together, the number in L at the end of cycle K equals the entrants times the product of s_1 to s_K, 706.56 for 1,000 entrants in the article's example. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a misrouted or lingering tunnel row." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Single-entry cohort reaches the long-term state with the product of tunnel survivals" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-TUN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "single-entry-cohort-reaches-the-long-term-state-with-the-product-of-tunnel-survivals" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LongTermAtK-Entrants*PRODUCT(TunnelSurvRange))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003131 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Single-entry cohort handed from the last tunnel state to the long-term state"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's example 1,000 people enter T1 just after a myocardial infarction, with annual death probabilities of 0.20, 0.08 and 0.04 in the three tunnel years and 0.03 afterwards. At the end of year 2 all 736 survivors are in T3, so in year 3 the long-term state receives 736 × 0.96 = 706.56; in year 4 it keeps 706.56 × 0.97 = 685.36. The cohort here has no origin state, so the entry vector p_(i,T_1) is all zero over T1, T2, T3, L and Dead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Single-entry cohort handed from the last tunnel state to the long-term state" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_S_tunnels = 5; m_(i,t) = [0, 0, 736, 0, 264]; p_(i,T_1) = [0, 0, 0, 0, 0]; m_(T_k,t) = 0; s_k = 0.80; m_(T_K,t) = 736; s_K = 0.96; m_(L,t) = 0; s_L = 0.97; m_(T_1,t+1) = 0; m_(T_(k+1),t+1) = 0; m_(L,t+1) = 706.56" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TUN-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "single-entry-cohort-handed-from-the-last-tunnel-state-to-the-long-term-state" .

hemo:7003132 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Staggered entry from an event-free state, year 3 to year 4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's staggered-entry example 1,000 people start event-free, and each year 5 per cent have an infarction and 1 per cent die. At the end of year 3 there are 830.584 event-free, 44.18 in T1, 37.6 in T2 and 36.8 in T3 (computed here from the same model). One more cycle gives 830.584 × 0.05 = 41.53 new entrants, 44.18 × 0.80 = 35.34 in T2, 37.6 × 0.92 = 34.59 in T3 and 36.8 × 0.96 = 35.33 in L, the year 4 figures in the article. States are ordered event-free, T1, T2, T3, L and Dead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Staggered entry from an event-free state, year 3 to year 4" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_S_tunnels = 6; m_(i,t) = [830.584, 44.18, 37.6, 36.8, 0, 50.836]; p_(i,T_1) = [0.05, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]; m_(T_k,t) = 44.18; s_k = 0.80; m_(T_K,t) = 36.8; s_K = 0.96; m_(L,t) = 0; s_L = 0.97; m_(T_1,t+1) = 41.5292; m_(T_(k+1),t+1) = 35.344; m_(L,t+1) = 35.328" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TUN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "staggered-entry-from-an-event-free-state-year-3-to-year-4" .

hemo:7003133 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One state expanded into a tunnel"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The count applies to one tunnelled state. The tutorial discusses a single tunnel and notes that the same principles apply to more; each further tunnelled state adds its own n_tunnels minus one states." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One state expanded into a tunnel" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TUN-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-state-expanded-into-a-tunnel" .

hemo:7003134 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Tunnel length set by the cycle length"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "n_tunnels is the number of cycles over which the duration effect changes plus one for the long-term state, so it depends on the cycle length: an effect that changes over three years needs four states with annual cycles and 37 with monthly ones." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Tunnel length set by the cycle length" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TUN-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "tunnel-length-set-by-the-cycle-length" .

hemo:7003135 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Expanded state count in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000585 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Excel returns the size of the expanded model from named cells holding the number of states before expansion and the number of states the tunnelled state is split into." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expanded state count in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-TUN-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expanded-state-count-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=StatesBefore+TunnelSplit-1" .

hemo:7003136 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expanded tunnel matrix has the predicted size"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The expanded matrix, in a range named ExpandedMatrix, is square with as many rows as the formula predicts. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a missing long-term state or a tunnel state left out of the matrix." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expanded tunnel matrix has the predicted size" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-TUN-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expanded-tunnel-matrix-has-the-predicted-size" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROWS(ExpandedMatrix)=StatesBefore+TunnelSplit-1,COLUMNS(ExpandedMatrix)=ROWS(ExpandedMatrix))" .

hemo:7003137 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Post-infarction state split into three annual tunnel states and a long-term state"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The article's memoryless model has event-free, post-infarction and Dead. Splitting post-infarction into T1, T2, T3 and L gives six states, as in its staggered-entry example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Post-infarction state split into three annual tunnel states and a long-term state" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_S = 3; n_tunnels = 4; n_S_tunnels = 6" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TUN-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "post-infarction-state-split-into-three-annual-tunnel-states-and-a-long-term-state" .

hemo:7003138 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Sick state of the Sick-Sicker tutorial split over a 75-cycle horizon"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the tutorial the duration effect in the Sick state lasts the whole 75-cycle horizon, so Sick becomes 75 tunnel states and the four-state model grows to 78 states." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sick state of the Sick-Sicker tutorial split over a 75-cycle horizon" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_S = 4; n_tunnels = 75; n_S_tunnels = 78" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TUN-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sick-state-of-the-sick-sicker-tutorial-split-over-a-75-cycle-horizon" .

hemo:7003139 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three-year duration effect in a monthly model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With monthly cycles the same three-year effect needs 36 tunnel states and a long-term state, so the three-state model grows to 39 states rather than six (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three-year duration effect in a monthly model" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_S = 3; n_tunnels = 37; n_S_tunnels = 39" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TUN-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-year-duration-effect-in-a-monthly-model" .

hemo:7003140 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weights from the occupancy at the start of the cycle"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weights are the numbers in each state at the end of cycle t, which are the people at risk during cycle t+1. At least one of them is above zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weights from the occupancy at the start of the cycle" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TUN-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weights-from-the-occupancy-at-the-start-of-the-cycle" .

hemo:7003141 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Average specific to one cycle and one entry history"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The result describes one cycle of one strategy. It changes from cycle to cycle and with the incidence of the entering event, so it summarises a tunnel model rather than replacing it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Average specific to one cycle and one entry history" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-TUN-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "average-specific-to-one-cycle-and-one-entry-history" .

hemo:7003142 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Average death probability of tunnel states in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000586 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the occupancies of T1 to L in a row named TunnelOccRow and their death probabilities in a row of the same length named ExitProbRow, Excel returns the weighted average." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Average death probability of tunnel states in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-TUN-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "average-death-probability-of-tunnel-states-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(TunnelOccRow,ExitProbRow)/SUM(TunnelOccRow)" .

hemo:7003143 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Average tunnel death probability within the range of its inputs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A weighted mean lies between the smallest and largest of the death probabilities it averages. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a missing or mismatched denominator, such as expected deaths left undivided or divided by only some of the tunnel states." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Average tunnel death probability within the range of its inputs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-TUN-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "average-tunnel-death-probability-within-the-range-of-its-inputs" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(AvgExitProb>=MIN(ExitProbRow),AvgExitProb<=MAX(ExitProbRow))" .

hemo:7003144 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Post-infarction average after four years at 5 per cent incidence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's staggered-entry example, 41.53 × 0.20 + 35.34 × 0.08 + 34.59 × 0.04 + 35.33 × 0.03 gives 13.58 expected deaths among 146.79 post-infarction people, an average of 0.0925." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Post-infarction average after four years at 5 per cent incidence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m_T1 = 41.5292; m_T2 = 35.344; m_T3 = 34.592; m_L = 35.328; q_1 = 0.20; q_2 = 0.08; q_3 = 0.04; q_L = 0.03; q_bar = 0.0925" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TUN-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "post-infarction-average-after-four-years-at-5-per-cent-incidence" .

hemo:7003145 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Post-infarction average after four years at 10 per cent incidence"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At an incidence of 10 per cent the post-infarction group holds more recent entrants, 70.50 in T1, 63.37 in T2, 65.50 in T3 and 70.66 in L, and the average is 0.0885, as in the article (occupancies computed here from the same model)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Post-infarction average after four years at 10 per cent incidence" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m_T1 = 70.4969; m_T2 = 63.368; m_T3 = 65.504; m_L = 70.656; q_1 = 0.20; q_2 = 0.08; q_3 = 0.04; q_L = 0.03; q_bar = 0.0885" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TUN-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "post-infarction-average-after-four-years-at-10-per-cent-incidence" .

hemo:7003146 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Everyone in the first tunnel state after one year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "After the first year of the staggered-entry example all 50 post-infarction people are in T1, so the average equals the first-year probability of 0.20, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Everyone in the first tunnel state after one year" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m_T1 = 50; m_T2 = 0; m_T3 = 0; m_L = 0; q_1 = 0.20; q_2 = 0.08; q_3 = 0.04; q_L = 0.03; q_bar = 0.20" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-TUN-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "everyone-in-the-first-tunnel-state-after-one-year" .

hemo:7003147 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "PFS and OS from the same arm and time origin"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both curves describe the same treatment arm and population, are measured from model entry and are read at the same time t. PFS counts death without progression as an event, so the true PFS curve cannot lie above OS." ;
    hemo:9000009 "PFS and OS from the same arm and time origin" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PSM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pfs-and-os-from-the-same-arm-and-time-origin" .

hemo:7003148 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Forward-only movement through the partitioned states"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "People move only forward, from progression-free to progressed to dead, which TSD 19 regards as generally reasonable in advanced cancer. Each curve is modelled independently, so the formula imposes no link between progression and later mortality: a treatment effect on progression changes the dead share only if the OS curve itself changes." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Forward-only movement through the partitioned states" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PSM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "forward-only-movement-through-the-partitioned-states" .

hemo:7003149 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Partitioned survival state shares from two curve columns"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000587 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With time in column A, PFS in column B and OS in column C from row 2, the three formulas entered in columns D, E and F and filled down return the progression-free, progressed and dead shares." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Partitioned survival state shares from two curve columns" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-PSM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "partitioned-survival-state-shares-from-two-curve-columns" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=B2; =C2-B2; =1-C2" .

hemo:7003150 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "PFS curve never above OS across the partitioned survival grid"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Count the grid times in rows 2 to 602 at which PFS exceeds OS. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows crossed curves, and the negative progressed shares they produce have to be resolved in the curve fitting, not in the state shares." ;
    hemo:9000009 "PFS curve never above OS across the partitioned survival grid" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PSM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pfs-curve-never-above-os-across-the-partitioned-survival-grid" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(--(B2:B602>C2:C602))=0" .

hemo:7003151 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Partitioned survival progressed and dead shares within zero and one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Check that every progressed share in column E and dead share in column F lies between 0 and 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows crossed curves, a survival value above 1 or a curve entered as a percentage." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Partitioned survival progressed and dead shares within zero and one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PSM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "partitioned-survival-progressed-and-dead-shares-within-zero-and-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(MIN(E2:E602)>=0,MAX(E2:E602)<=1,MIN(F2:F602)>=0,MAX(F2:F602)<=1)" .

hemo:7003152 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard care occupancy at one year in the partitioned survival example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With exponential PFS and OS hazards of 1.0 and 0.5 a year, the article's standard-care arm has 36.8% progression-free, 23.9% progressed and 39.3% dead at one year." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standard care occupancy at one year in the partitioned survival example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_PFS = 0.36788; S_OS = 0.60653; P_PF = 0.36788; P_PD = 0.23865; P_D = 0.39347" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PSM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standard-care-occupancy-at-one-year-in-the-partitioned-survival-example" .

hemo:7003153 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "New treatment occupancy at one year in the partitioned survival example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With hazards of 2/3 and 0.4 a year, hazard ratios of about 0.67 and 0.8 applied to standard care as in HE-FM-HR-003, the new treatment has 51.3% progression-free, 15.7% progressed and 33.0% dead at one year, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "New treatment occupancy at one year in the partitioned survival example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_PFS = 0.51342; S_OS = 0.67032; P_PF = 0.51342; P_PD = 0.15690; P_D = 0.32968" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PSM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "new-treatment-occupancy-at-one-year-in-the-partitioned-survival-example" .

hemo:7003154 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Nested TTD, PFS and OS curves at every time"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "At every time S_TTD is no higher than S_PFS and S_PFS no higher than S_OS. This holds when initial treatment stops at or before progression or death. People cannot move back to a lower-indexed state, so no one restarts initial treatment once it has stopped." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Nested TTD, PFS and OS curves at every time" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PSM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "nested-ttd-pfs-and-os-curves-at-every-time" .

hemo:7003155 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same arm and time origin for the three partitioning curves"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "TTD, PFS and OS describe the same treatment arm and are measured from model entry, so the differences between them are shares of one cohort at the same time." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same arm and time origin for the three partitioning curves" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PSM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-arm-and-time-origin-for-the-three-partitioning-curves" .

hemo:7003156 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Four partitioned survival state shares from three curve columns"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000588 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With TTD in column B, PFS in column C and OS in column D from row 2, the four formulas filled down return the on-treatment, off-treatment, progressed and dead shares." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Four partitioned survival state shares from three curve columns" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-PSM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "four-partitioned-survival-state-shares-from-three-curve-columns" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=B2; =C2-B2; =D2-C2; =1-D2" .

hemo:7003157 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three partitioning curves nested at every grid time"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Count the rows from 2 to 602 where TTD exceeds PFS or PFS exceeds OS. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows treatment continuing beyond progression or crossed PFS and OS curves." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Three partitioning curves nested at every grid time" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PSM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "three-partitioning-curves-nested-at-every-grid-time" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(--(B2:B602>C2:C602))+SUMPRODUCT(--(C2:C602>D2:D602))=0" .

hemo:7003158 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Four-state shares at one year with an illustrative TTD of 0.30"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Taking the article's standard-care PFS and OS at one year and an illustrative 30% still on initial treatment, 6.8% are progression-free off treatment, while the progressed and dead shares are unchanged from the three-state example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Four-state shares at one year with an illustrative TTD of 0.30" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_TTD = 0.30; S_PFS = 0.36788; S_OS = 0.60653; P_ON = 0.30; P_OFF = 0.06788; P_PD = 0.23865; P_D = 0.39347" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PSM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "four-state-shares-at-one-year-with-an-illustrative-ttd-of-0-30" .

hemo:7003159 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One utility for all time in each partitioned survival state"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each alive state has one utility for all time spent in it, whatever the time since entry or the time to death. Over long horizons PMG36 (section 4.3.7) asks for utilities to be adjusted so that they do not exceed general population values at a given age; utilities then vary with time and the areas are weighted cycle by cycle instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One utility for all time in each partitioned survival state" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PSM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-utility-for-all-time-in-each-partitioned-survival-state" .

hemo:7003160 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "PFS and OS areas from the same curves and horizon"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A_PF and A_OS come from the pair of curves used for state occupancy and cover the same horizon, so A_PF is no larger than A_OS." ;
    hemo:9000009 "PFS and OS areas from the same curves and horizon" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PSM-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "pfs-and-os-areas-from-the-same-curves-and-horizon" .

hemo:7003161 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Partitioned survival QALYs from two areas"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000589 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the areas in named cells AreaPFS and AreaOS and the utilities in UtilPF and UtilPD, the formula returns QALYs per person." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Partitioned survival QALYs from two areas" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-PSM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "partitioned-survival-qalys-from-two-areas" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=UtilPF*AreaPFS+UtilPD*(AreaOS-AreaPFS)" .

hemo:7003162 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Partitioned survival QALYs bounded by the utilities times life expectancy"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "QALYs in a cell named QALY must lie between the lower and the higher utility multiplied by the area under OS. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows double counting, such as progression-free time valued again inside the OS area, or crossed curves." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Partitioned survival QALYs bounded by the utilities times life expectancy" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PSM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "partitioned-survival-qalys-bounded-by-the-utilities-times-life-expectancy" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(QALY>=MIN(UtilPF,UtilPD)*AreaOS-1E-12,QALY<=MAX(UtilPF,UtilPD)*AreaOS+1E-12)" .

hemo:7003163 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard care QALYs in the partitioned survival example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Mean PFS of 1.0 year and mean OS of 2.0 years leave 1.0 year progressed. At utilities of 0.75 and 0.60 the arm accrues 1.35 QALYs, undiscounted, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standard care QALYs in the partitioned survival example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "u_PF = 0.75; u_PD = 0.60; A_PF = 1.0; A_OS = 2.0; QALY = 1.35" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PSM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standard-care-qalys-in-the-partitioned-survival-example" .

hemo:7003164 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "New treatment QALYs in the partitioned survival example"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Mean PFS of 1.5 years and mean OS of 2.5 years also leave 1.0 year progressed, giving 1.725 QALYs. The gain of 0.375 QALYs comes entirely from progression-free time valued at 0.75." ;
    hemo:9000009 "New treatment QALYs in the partitioned survival example" ;
    hemo:9000014 "u_PF = 0.75; u_PD = 0.60; A_PF = 1.5; A_OS = 2.5; QALY = 1.725" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PSM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "new-treatment-qalys-in-the-partitioned-survival-example" .

hemo:7003165 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant PFS and OS hazards for a lifetime"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both hazards stay constant from model entry for life, as in the exponential model of TSD 14 (section 2.1), which asks whether the hazard is likely to remain constant over an entire lifetime. The PFS hazard is at least the OS hazard, so the PFS curve never rises above OS." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant PFS and OS hazards for a lifetime" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PSM-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-pfs-and-os-hazards-for-a-lifetime" .

hemo:7003166 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous discounting of partitioned survival areas"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Discounting uses exp(minus rho t), which matches annual discounting at rate d when rho = log(1 + d) (HE-FM-CONT-003). The NICE reference case uses 3.5% a year for costs and health effects (PMG36, section 4.5.1)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuous discounting of partitioned survival areas" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PSM-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuous-discounting-of-partitioned-survival-areas" .

hemo:7003167 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Exponential partitioned survival QALYs in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000590 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the hazards in HazPFS and HazOS, the utilities in UtilPF and UtilPD and the annual discount rate in DiscRate, the formula converts the annual rate to rho inside the cell; a DiscRate of 0 gives undiscounted QALYs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exponential partitioned survival QALYs in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-PSM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exponential-partitioned-survival-qalys-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=UtilPF/(HazPFS+LN(1+DiscRate))+UtilPD*(1/(HazOS+LN(1+DiscRate))-1/(HazPFS+LN(1+DiscRate)))" .

hemo:7003168 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Exponential closed form against a monthly partitioned survival grid"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Build the same curves on a monthly grid to 50 years with HE-CF-PSM-001 and compare its QALYs, held in QALYgrid, with the closed form. Expected result: TRUE; in the standard-care example the gap is about 0.0003 undiscounted and 0.0002 at 3.5%. FALSE shows a hazard per month mixed with years or an annual rate used where rho belongs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exponential closed form against a monthly partitioned survival grid" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PSM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exponential-closed-form-against-a-monthly-partitioned-survival-grid" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(QALYgrid-(UtilPF/(HazPFS+LN(1+DiscRate))+UtilPD*(1/(HazOS+LN(1+DiscRate))-1/(HazPFS+LN(1+DiscRate)))))<0.001" .

hemo:7003169 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Undiscounted lifetime QALYs for standard care with exponential curves"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Hazards of 1.0 and 0.5 a year give 0.75 divided by 1.0 plus 0.60 times (2.0 minus 1.0), or 1.35 QALYs, as in HE-EX-PSM-004." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Undiscounted lifetime QALYs for standard care with exponential curves" ;
    hemo:9000014 "u_PF = 0.75; u_PD = 0.60; lambda_PFS = 1.0; lambda_OS = 0.5; rho = 0; QALY_exp = 1.35" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PSM-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "undiscounted-lifetime-qalys-for-standard-care-with-exponential-curves" .

hemo:7003170 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Undiscounted lifetime QALYs for the new treatment with exponential curves"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Hazards of 2/3 and 0.4 a year, with 2/3 entered as 0.666667, give about 1.725 QALYs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Undiscounted lifetime QALYs for the new treatment with exponential curves" ;
    hemo:9000014 "u_PF = 0.75; u_PD = 0.60; lambda_PFS = 0.666667; lambda_OS = 0.4; rho = 0; QALY_exp = 1.725" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PSM-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "undiscounted-lifetime-qalys-for-the-new-treatment-with-exponential-curves" .

hemo:7003171 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard care QALYs discounted at 3.5% a year with exponential curves"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Discounting continuously at rho = log(1.035), about 0.034401, reduces standard-care QALYs from 1.35 to about 1.2678; the new treatment falls from 1.725 to about 1.5952. The discounted figures are computed for this record and do not appear in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standard care QALYs discounted at 3.5% a year with exponential curves" ;
    hemo:9000014 "u_PF = 0.75; u_PD = 0.60; lambda_PFS = 1.0; lambda_OS = 0.5; rho = 0.034401; QALY_exp = 1.2678" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PSM-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standard-care-qalys-discounted-at-3-5-a-year-with-exponential-curves" .

hemo:7003172 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Lifetime horizon so every final window lies inside the model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The horizon covers the whole cohort's survival and results are undiscounted, so each person's final window falls inside the model. With a shorter horizon, people alive at its end have not yet entered their final window and W no longer equals the area under OS from 0 to a." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Lifetime horizon so every final window lies inside the model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PSM-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "lifetime-horizon-so-every-final-window-lies-inside-the-model" .

hemo:7003173 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Utility depends on time to death alone"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Utility varies only with time to death, not with progression. The exponential form is a convenience; for other OS curves W is the area under that curve from 0 to a, found numerically or, within follow-up, from a Kaplan-Meier curve (HE-FM-ADMC-003)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Utility depends on time to death alone" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-PSM-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "utility-depends-on-time-to-death-alone" .

hemo:7003174 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Time-to-death QALYs from an exponential OS hazard"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000591 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the OS hazard in HazOS, the window in years in Window and the utilities in UtilFar and UtilNear, the first formula returns W into a cell named W and the second returns the QALYs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Time-to-death QALYs from an exponential OS hazard" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-PSM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "time-to-death-qalys-from-an-exponential-os-hazard" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(1-EXP(-HazOS*Window))/HazOS; =UtilFar*(1/HazOS-W)+UtilNear*W" .

hemo:7003175 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Partitioned survival final-window time within its feasible range"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "W must be below the window length and below mean survival 1/lambda_OS, and above the window length times survival at the end of the window. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows W set to the full window for everyone, which ignores people who die within a of model entry, or a value that is not an area under OS." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Partitioned survival final-window time within its feasible range" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-PSM-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "partitioned-survival-final-window-time-within-its-feasible-range" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(W<Window,W>Window*EXP(-HazOS*Window),W<1/HazOS)" .

hemo:7003176 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard care QALYs by time to death"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With an OS hazard of 0.5 a year and a six-month window, W is about 0.4424 years and the remaining 1.5576 years are valued at 0.72, giving about 1.3427 QALYs (1.343 in the article)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standard care QALYs by time to death" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda_OS = 0.5; a = 0.5; u_far = 0.72; u_near = 0.50; W = 0.44240; QALY_TTD = 1.34267" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PSM-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standard-care-qalys-by-time-to-death" .

hemo:7003177 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "New treatment QALYs by time to death"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With an OS hazard of 0.4 a year, W is about 0.4532 years and QALYs are about 1.7003. The gain over standard care is about 0.358, against 0.375 with progression-based utilities, because almost all the extra time is valued at the utility for time further from death." ;
    hemo:9000009 "New treatment QALYs by time to death" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda_OS = 0.4; a = 0.5; u_far = 0.72; u_near = 0.50; W = 0.45317; QALY_TTD = 1.70030" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-PSM-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "new-treatment-qalys-by-time-to-death" .

hemo:7003178 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant transition matrix and constant discount rate for the discounted matrix"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Q is the same in every cycle and the discount rate does not change over the horizon. Sonnenberg and Beck wrote that discounting cannot be used with the fundamental matrix solution because of its time variance; a constant geometric discount multiplies every cycle by the same factor and so folds into Q, but a discount schedule that changes over time, or a matrix that changes with age, does not, and the discounted total then comes from a cohort trace (HE-FM-CSIM-001)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant transition matrix and constant discount rate for the discounted matrix" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MKCH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-transition-matrix-and-constant-discount-rate-for-the-discounted-matrix" .

hemo:7003179 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Start-of-cycle counting with an undiscounted first cycle in the discounted fundamental matrix"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Membership at the start of cycle k, for k from 0 upwards, is counted in full and discounted by (1 + r) to the power minus k Delta, so the starting cycle has a factor of 1. No half-cycle correction is applied. Sonnenberg and Beck's correction for a matrix solution subtracts half a cycle from the membership of each starting state, which at a factor of 1 subtracts 0.5 from t_disc." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Start-of-cycle counting with an undiscounted first cycle in the discounted fundamental matrix" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MKCH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "start-of-cycle-counting-with-an-undiscounted-first-cycle-in-the-discounted-fundamental-matrix" .

hemo:7003180 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Absorbing chain for the discounted fundamental matrix"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every transient state can reach an absorbing state, so Q to the power k tends to zero, as Grinstead and Snell show for any absorbing chain, and the discounted powers of Q tend to zero faster still; I minus Q divided by the discount factor can then be inverted." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Absorbing chain for the discounted fundamental matrix" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MKCH-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "absorbing-chain-for-the-discounted-fundamental-matrix" .

hemo:7003181 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted fundamental matrix and its row sums in Excel"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000592 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the transient block in the named range TransientQ, the annual discount rate in DiscRate and the cycle length in years in CycleYears, Excel 365 returns N_disc as a dynamic array with the first formula and the column t_disc with the second. MUNIT builds the identity matrix and SEQUENCE the column of ones." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted fundamental matrix and its row sums in Excel" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MKCH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-fundamental-matrix-and-its-row-sums-in-excel" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MINVERSE(MUNIT(ROWS(TransientQ))-TransientQ/(1+DiscRate)^CycleYears); =MMULT(MINVERSE(MUNIT(ROWS(TransientQ))-TransientQ/(1+DiscRate)^CycleYears),SEQUENCE(ROWS(TransientQ),1,1,0))" .

hemo:7003182 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted fundamental matrix agrees with a discounted cohort run"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Run the cohort from Well for 3,000 annual cycles, sum the proportion alive at the start of each cycle k multiplied by 1.035 to the power minus k, starting at k equal to 0, and compare it with the Well entry of t_disc. Expected result: TRUE, both 10.7260 to four decimal places." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted fundamental matrix agrees with a discounted cohort run" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MKCH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-fundamental-matrix-agrees-with-a-discounted-cohort-run" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(SUMPRODUCT(AliveCol,1/1.035^CycleCol),4)=ROUND(INDEX(TDisc,1),4)" .

hemo:7003183 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted occupancy below the undiscounted value and the perpetuity bound"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each entry of t_disc is no larger than the undiscounted t of HE-FM-ABS-001 and below the discounted value of one cycle a period forever, (1 + r) to the power Delta divided by that factor minus 1, which is 29.5714 at 3.5% with annual cycles. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE flags a discount applied the wrong way round, such as Q multiplied by 1.035 rather than divided by it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted occupancy below the undiscounted value and the perpetuity bound" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MKCH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-occupancy-below-the-undiscounted-value-and-the-perpetuity-bound" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(MAX(TDisc-TUndisc)<=0,MAX(TDisc)<(1+DiscRate)^CycleYears/((1+DiscRate)^CycleYears-1))" .

hemo:7003184 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Well and Ill chain with recovery discounted at 3.5 per cent a year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's chain, 85% of Well stay Well, 10% fall ill and 5% die each year, and of Ill 20% recover, 70% stay Ill and 10% die. At 3.5% a year with annual cycles, N_disc has rows 8.2603, 2.4658 and 4.9315, 4.5616, so discounted life expectancy is 10.7260 years from Well, matching a discounted cohort run, or 10.2260 after subtracting half a cycle, as in the article. From Ill it is 9.4932 years (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Well and Ill chain with recovery discounted at 3.5 per cent a year" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q = [[0.85,0.10],[0.20,0.70]]; I = [[1,0],[0,1]]; r = 0.035; Delta = 1; c = [1,1]; N_disc = [[8.2603,2.4658],[4.9315,4.5616]]; t_disc = [10.7260,9.4932]" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MKCH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "well-and-ill-chain-with-recovery-discounted-at-3-5-per-cent-a-year" .

hemo:7003185 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Zero discount rate returns the undiscounted Well and Ill fundamental matrix"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With r equal to zero the discount factor is 1 and N_disc is the fundamental matrix of the article, rows 12, 4 and 8, 6, with 16 expected years before death from Well and 14 from Ill, the result of HE-FM-ABS-001." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Zero discount rate returns the undiscounted Well and Ill fundamental matrix" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q = [[0.85,0.10],[0.20,0.70]]; I = [[1,0],[0,1]]; r = 0; Delta = 1; c = [1,1]; N_disc = [[12,4],[8,6]]; t_disc = [16,14]" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MKCH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "zero-discount-rate-returns-the-undiscounted-well-and-ill-fundamental-matrix" .

hemo:7003186 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Re-enterable Markov chain state entered only from the starting state"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "State j can be entered only from state i, as in a chain whose only transient states are Well and Ill. Where j can also be entered from a third transient state, the entries from that state are added to e_ij." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Re-enterable Markov chain state entered only from the starting state" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MKCH-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "re-enterable-markov-chain-state-entered-only-from-the-starting-state" .

hemo:7003187 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Exits from the starting state go to the re-enterable state or to absorption"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "h_ij takes the share of exits from i that go to j, so every exit from i leads to j or to an absorbing state. With another transient state reachable from i, the probability of ever entering j is n_ij divided by n_jj from the fundamental matrix instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exits from the starting state go to the re-enterable state or to absorption" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MKCH-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exits-from-the-starting-state-go-to-the-re-enterable-state-or-to-absorption" .

hemo:7003188 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Time-homogeneous chain started outside the re-enterable state"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The probabilities are the same in every cycle and the person starts in i, not in j. A person starting in j has one extra episode already under way: from Ill in the article's chain, 1 plus 8 times 0.10 gives 1.8 episodes and 6 years Ill, the Ill to Ill entry of N (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Time-homogeneous chain started outside the re-enterable state" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MKCH-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "time-homogeneous-chain-started-outside-the-re-enterable-state" .

hemo:7003189 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Episode decomposition of a re-enterable Markov chain state in Excel"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000593 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With n_ii, p_ij, p_jj and p_ii in cells named N_ii, P_ij, P_jj and P_ii, the four formulas return e_ij, L_j, T_ij and h_ij in turn; the third refers to the first two results held in cells named E_ij and L_j." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Episode decomposition of a re-enterable Markov chain state in Excel" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MKCH-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "episode-decomposition-of-a-re-enterable-markov-chain-state-in-excel" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=N_ii*P_ij; =1/(1-P_jj); =E_ij*L_j; =P_ij/(1-P_ii)" .

hemo:7003190 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Episode total equals the Well to Ill entry of the fundamental matrix"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "T_ij equals entry i, j of N from HE-FM-ABS-001, 4 for Well to Ill in the example. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE flags an n_ii taken as 1 divided by 1 minus p_ii, which ignores the time spent in i after recovering." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Episode total equals the Well to Ill entry of the fundamental matrix" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MKCH-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "episode-total-equals-the-well-to-ill-entry-of-the-fundamental-matrix" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(T_ij-INDEX(FundN,1,2))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003191 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Probability of ever entering agrees with the fundamental matrix ratio"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each person who enters j then spends n_jj expected cycles there, so h_ij also equals n_ij divided by n_jj: 4/6 = 0.6667 in the example (computed here for illustration). Expected result: TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Probability of ever entering agrees with the fundamental matrix ratio" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MKCH-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "probability-of-ever-entering-agrees-with-the-fundamental-matrix-ratio" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(H_ij-INDEX(FundN,1,2)/INDEX(FundN,2,2))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003192 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Ill episodes from a Well start in a chain with recovery"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "From Well, a person spends 12 expected years in Well and 10% fall ill each year, giving 12 × 0.10 = 1.2 expected episodes of illness, each lasting 1 divided by 0.30, or 3.33 years on average, so 4 expected years Ill, the Well to Ill entry of N. The probability of ever falling ill is 0.10/0.15 = 0.6667, two in three, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ill episodes from a Well start in a chain with recovery" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_ii = 12; p_ij = 0.10; p_jj = 0.70; p_ii = 0.85; e_ij = 1.2; L_j = 3.3333; T_ij = 4; h_ij = 0.6667" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MKCH-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ill-episodes-from-a-well-start-in-a-chain-with-recovery" .

hemo:7003193 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Ill episodes from a Well start when no one recovers"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the 0.20 recovery probability is added to staying Ill, giving an Ill row of 0, 0.90, 0.10, no one returns to Well, so n_ii falls to 6.6667 and a Well start has 0.6667 expected episodes, each lasting 10 years, or 6.6667 years Ill, as in the article. Recovery adds episodes (1.2 against 0.67) but shortens each one, so total time Ill falls from 6.67 to 4 years (episode counts computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ill episodes from a Well start when no one recovers" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_ii = 6.6667; p_ij = 0.10; p_jj = 0.90; p_ii = 0.85; e_ij = 0.6667; L_j = 10; T_ij = 6.6667; h_ij = 0.6667" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MKCH-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ill-episodes-from-a-well-start-when-no-one-recovers" .

hemo:7003194 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Population-level cure with zero excess hazard in the mixture cure model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Cure means that the excess (cause-specific) hazard of the cured group is zero, so cured patients die at general population rates; the model does not identify which patients are cured. Because a survival function must reach zero, the model is fitted to relative or cause-specific survival, not to all-cause survival alone." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Population-level cure with zero excess hazard in the mixture cure model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "population-level-cure-with-zero-excess-hazard-in-the-mixture-cure-model" .

hemo:7003195 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected survival from matched life tables in the mixture cure model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "S_star comes from life tables for the right calendar year, stratified by age and sex. If cured patients keep an excess risk, a standardised mortality ratio can be applied to the general population mortality rates behind S_star." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected survival from matched life tables in the mixture cure model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-survival-from-matched-life-tables-in-the-mixture-cure-model" .

hemo:7003196 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Mature data and a justified uncured distribution for a mixture cure fit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "TSD 21 lists three assumptions: the data are sufficient to estimate a cure fraction reliably, a cure fraction exists and cure is reasonable at a given time point, and the distribution chosen for the uncured is appropriate. Different uncured distributions fitted to the same data can give very different values of pi." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mature data and a justified uncured distribution for a mixture cure fit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mature-data-and-a-justified-uncured-distribution-for-a-mixture-cure-fit" .

hemo:7003197 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Mixture cure all-cause survival from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000594 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With BgSurv, CureFrac and UncuredSurv named for one time point, the formula returns all-cause survival, held in AllCauseSurv. Filled down a column of times, it gives the whole curve." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mixture cure all-cause survival from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CRM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mixture-cure-all-cause-survival-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=BgSurv*(CureFrac+(1-CureFrac)*UncuredSurv)" .

hemo:7003198 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Back-solving uncured survival from the mixture cure curve"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Relative survival minus the cure fraction, divided by 1 minus the cure fraction, returns the survival of the uncured. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows background survival left out or applied to one group only, or pi and 1 minus pi swapped." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Back-solving uncured survival from the mixture cure curve" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "back-solving-uncured-survival-from-the-mixture-cure-curve" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((AllCauseSurv/BgSurv-CureFrac)/(1-CureFrac)-UncuredSurv)<1E-9" .

hemo:7003199 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mixture cure relative survival not below the cure fraction"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "All-cause survival divided by background survival lies from the cure fraction up to 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a cure fraction above 1 or a survival entered as a percentage." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mixture cure relative survival not below the cure fraction" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mixture-cure-relative-survival-not-below-the-cure-fraction" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(AllCauseSurv/BgSurv>=CureFrac,AllCauseSurv/BgSurv<=1)" .

hemo:7003200 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mixture cure survival at 5 years with a cure fraction of 0.25"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's illustrative constant hazards, background survival at 5 years is exp(minus 0.04 times 5), about 0.8187, and survival of the uncured from an excess hazard of 0.46 a year is exp(minus 2.3), about 0.1003. A cure fraction of 0.25 gives all-cause survival of about 0.2662 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mixture cure survival at 5 years with a cure fraction of 0.25" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_star = 0.818731; pi = 0.25; S_u = 0.100259; S = 0.266247" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mixture-cure-survival-at-5-years-with-a-cure-fraction-of-0-25" .

hemo:7003201 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mixture cure survival at 5 years with a cure fraction of 0.10"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The same inputs with the comparator's cure fraction of 0.10 give about 0.1557, so the extra 15 percentage points of cure already add about 0.11 to survival at 5 years (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mixture cure survival at 5 years with a cure fraction of 0.10" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_star = 0.818731; pi = 0.10; S_u = 0.100259; S = 0.155750" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mixture-cure-survival-at-5-years-with-a-cure-fraction-of-0-10" .

hemo:7003202 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mixture cure survival at 20 years once the uncured have almost all died"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "By 20 years survival of the uncured is about 0.0001, so relative survival is close to the cure fraction of 0.25, but all-cause survival is only about 0.1124 because cured patients also die of other causes; background survival is about 0.4493 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mixture cure survival at 20 years once the uncured have almost all died" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_star = 0.449329; pi = 0.25; S_u = 0.000101; S = 0.112366" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mixture-cure-survival-at-20-years-once-the-uncured-have-almost-all-died" .

hemo:7003203 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "No separate cured and uncured groups in the non-mixture cure model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The cohort is not split into cured and uncured groups, so there is no survival model specific to uncured patients. The distribution behind F_z must be flexible enough to follow the cohort's survival as it approaches the cure fraction." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No separate cured and uncured groups in the non-mixture cure model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-separate-cured-and-uncured-groups-in-the-non-mixture-cure-model" .

hemo:7003204 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Cure time fixed by the final boundary knot in a flexible non-mixture model"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "When F_z is defined with restricted cubic splines, the analyst fixes the time at which the excess hazard is taken to reach zero through the final boundary knot; from then on the all-cause hazard is other-cause mortality alone." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cure time fixed by the final boundary knot in a flexible non-mixture model" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cure-time-fixed-by-the-final-boundary-knot-in-a-flexible-non-mixture-model" .

hemo:7003205 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Non-mixture cure all-cause survival from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000595 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With BgSurv, CureFrac and CdfValue named for one time point, the formula returns all-cause survival, held in NmcSurv." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Non-mixture cure all-cause survival from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CRM-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "non-mixture-cure-all-cause-survival-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=BgSurv*CureFrac^CdfValue" .

hemo:7003206 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Recovering the distribution value from non-mixture cure survival"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The log of relative survival divided by the log of the cure fraction returns F_z(t). Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the cure fraction or the background term applied in another way." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Recovering the distribution value from non-mixture cure survival" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "recovering-the-distribution-value-from-non-mixture-cure-survival" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LN(NmcSurv/BgSurv)/LN(CureFrac)-CdfValue)<1E-9" .

hemo:7003207 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Non-mixture relative survival from the cure fraction up to 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "All-cause survival divided by background survival is at least the cure fraction and at most 1. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a distribution value outside its range, for example a cumulative hazard of 1.5 entered for F_z(t), or a survival entered as a percentage." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Non-mixture relative survival from the cure fraction up to 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "non-mixture-relative-survival-from-the-cure-fraction-up-to-1" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(NmcSurv/BgSurv>=CureFrac,NmcSurv/BgSurv<=1)" .

hemo:7003208 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Non-mixture cure survival halfway along the distribution function"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a cure fraction of 0.25, F_z(t) of 0.5 and background survival of 0.8187, relative survival is 0.25 to the power 0.5, which is 0.5, and all-cause survival is about 0.4094 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Non-mixture cure survival halfway along the distribution function" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_star = 0.818731; pi = 0.25; F = 0.5; S = 0.4093655" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "non-mixture-cure-survival-halfway-along-the-distribution-function" .

hemo:7003209 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Non-mixture cure survival once the distribution function has reached 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When F_z(t) has reached 1, relative survival equals the cure fraction and all-cause survival is S_star times pi, about 0.1123 with background survival of 0.4493, the level the mixture model approaches once the uncured have died (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Non-mixture cure survival once the distribution function has reached 1" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_star = 0.449329; pi = 0.25; F = 1; S = 0.112332" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "non-mixture-cure-survival-once-the-distribution-function-has-reached-1" .

hemo:7003210 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Cured and uncured patients share the same background mortality"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both groups face the same general population mortality, and uncured patients carry the excess hazard in addition, so E_U is below E_B." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cured and uncured patients share the same background mortality" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRM-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cured-and-uncured-patients-share-the-same-background-mortality" .

hemo:7003211 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Lifetime areas under the cure model survival curves"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "E_B and E_U are areas over a horizon long enough for the cohort to have died. Areas cut at an earlier horizon give a restricted mean, as in HE-FM-ADMC-003, and understate T_bar while cured patients are still alive." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Lifetime areas under the cure model survival curves" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRM-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "lifetime-areas-under-the-cure-model-survival-curves" .

hemo:7003212 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Cure-fraction mean survival from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000596 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With CureFrac, MeanBg and MeanUncured named, the formula returns mean overall survival, held in MeanSurv. For the constant-hazard check, BgHazard and ExcessHazard hold mu and lambda." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cure-fraction mean survival from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CRM-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cure-fraction-mean-survival-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CureFrac*MeanBg+(1-CureFrac)*MeanUncured" .

hemo:7003213 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cure-fraction mean survival lies between the group means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "MeanSurv is no lower than the smaller and no higher than the larger of MeanBg and MeanUncured. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a cure fraction entered as a percentage, such as 25 instead of 0.25." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cure-fraction mean survival lies between the group means" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRM-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cure-fraction-mean-survival-lies-between-the-group-means" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(MeanSurv>=MIN(MeanBg,MeanUncured),MeanSurv<=MAX(MeanBg,MeanUncured))" .

hemo:7003214 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cure-fraction mean survival recomputed from constant hazards"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With constant hazards, MeanSurv equals the cure fraction over mu plus the uncured share over mu plus lambda. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows E_U taken as one over the excess hazard alone." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cure-fraction mean survival recomputed from constant hazards" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRM-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cure-fraction-mean-survival-recomputed-from-constant-hazards" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(MeanSurv-(CureFrac/BgHazard+(1-CureFrac)/(BgHazard+ExcessHazard)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003215 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mean survival with a cure fraction of 0.10"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With E_B of 25 years (background hazard 0.04 a year) and E_U of 2 years (total hazard 0.50 a year for the uncured), a cure fraction of 0.10 gives 2.5 plus 1.8, or 4.3 years, as in the article's table." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mean survival with a cure fraction of 0.10" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi = 0.10; E_B = 25; E_U = 2; T_bar = 4.3" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mean-survival-with-a-cure-fraction-of-0-10" .

hemo:7003216 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mean survival with a cure fraction of 0.25"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A cure fraction of 0.25 gives 6.25 plus 1.5, or 7.75 years. Against the comparator with 0.10 the gain is 3.45 years, which is 0.15 times 23, all from the extra cure, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mean survival with a cure fraction of 0.25" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi = 0.25; E_B = 25; E_U = 2; T_bar = 7.75" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mean-survival-with-a-cure-fraction-of-0-25" .

hemo:7003217 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Mean survival with a cure fraction of 0.40"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A cure fraction of 0.40 gives 10 plus 1.2, or 11.2 years, the last row of the article's table." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mean survival with a cure fraction of 0.40" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi = 0.40; E_B = 25; E_U = 2; T_bar = 11.2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mean-survival-with-a-cure-fraction-of-0-40" .

hemo:7003218 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant background and excess hazards for the closed-form cure QALYs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both hazards are constant, so both survival curves are exponential. A real model uses age-specific life-table hazards and a fitted uncured curve, and the areas are then computed numerically, as in HE-CF-CRM-001." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant background and excess hazards for the closed-form cure QALYs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRM-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-background-and-excess-hazards-for-the-closed-form-cure-qalys" .

hemo:7003219 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant utilities by cure status over the lifetime"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Cured and uncured patients each keep one utility for their remaining lifetime. Utilities that change with age or time since treatment need the numerical form." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant utilities by cure status over the lifetime" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRM-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-utilities-by-cure-status-over-the-lifetime" .

hemo:7003220 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous discounting equivalent to the annual cure model discount rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "r is log(1 plus d): 0.034401 for the NICE reference case of 3.5 per cent a year (PMG36 section 4.5.1) and 0.014889 for the 1.5 per cent a committee may consider under section 4.5.3. The same rate applies to costs and QALYs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuous discounting equivalent to the annual cure model discount rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-CRM-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuous-discounting-equivalent-to-the-annual-cure-model-discount-rate" .

hemo:7003221 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted cure QALYs from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000597 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With CureFrac, UtilCured, UtilUncured, BgHazard, ExcessHazard and the annual rate DiscRate named, the formula returns discounted QALYs, held in DiscQALY; LN converts the annual rate to the continuous rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted cure QALYs from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-CRM-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-cure-qalys-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=CureFrac*UtilCured/(BgHazard+LN(1+DiscRate))+(1-CureFrac)*UtilUncured/(BgHazard+ExcessHazard+LN(1+DiscRate))" .

hemo:7003222 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted cure QALYs at a cure fraction of 0.25 reproduce the article"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's inputs, CureFrac = 0.25 and DiscRate = 0.035, DiscQALY is about 3.530. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows 0.035 used as the continuous rate, which gives about 3.508." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted cure QALYs at a cure fraction of 0.25 reproduce the article" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRM-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-cure-qalys-at-a-cure-fraction-of-0-25-reproduce-the-article" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(DiscQALY-3.530185)<0.00001" .

hemo:7003223 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted cure QALYs below undiscounted cure QALYs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a positive discount rate DiscQALY is below the same formula with the rate set to 0. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a discount rate entered with the wrong sign." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted cure QALYs below undiscounted cure QALYs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-CRM-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-cure-qalys-below-undiscounted-cure-qalys" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=DiscQALY<CureFrac*UtilCured/BgHazard+(1-CureFrac)*UtilUncured/(BgHazard+ExcessHazard)" .

hemo:7003224 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted cure QALYs with a cure fraction of 0.10 at 3.5 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Comparator with pi = 0.10, utilities 0.80 cured and 0.60 uncured, background hazard 0.04 and excess hazard 0.46: the discounted means are about 13.44 years for cured and 1.871 for uncured patients, giving about 2.086 QALYs, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted cure QALYs with a cure fraction of 0.10 at 3.5 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi = 0.10; u_C = 0.8; u_U = 0.6; mu = 0.04; lambda = 0.46; r = 0.0344014; QALY_d = 2.085725" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-cure-qalys-with-a-cure-fraction-of-0-10-at-3-5-per-cent" .

hemo:7003225 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted cure QALYs with a cure fraction of 0.25 at 3.5 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The new treatment with pi = 0.25 gives about 3.530 QALYs, a discounted gain of about 1.444 over the comparator, about half the undiscounted gain of 2.82, because the benefit of cure arrives decades later." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted cure QALYs with a cure fraction of 0.25 at 3.5 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi = 0.25; u_C = 0.8; u_U = 0.6; mu = 0.04; lambda = 0.46; r = 0.0344014; QALY_d = 3.530185" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-cure-qalys-with-a-cure-fraction-of-0-25-at-3-5-per-cent" .

hemo:7003226 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Undiscounted cure QALYs with a cure fraction of 0.25"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With r = 0 the formula returns 0.25 times 25 times 0.80 plus 0.75 times 2 times 0.60, or 5.9 QALYs, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Undiscounted cure QALYs with a cure fraction of 0.25" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi = 0.25; u_C = 0.8; u_U = 0.6; mu = 0.04; lambda = 0.46; r = 0; QALY_d = 5.9" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "undiscounted-cure-qalys-with-a-cure-fraction-of-0-25" .

hemo:7003227 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted cure QALYs with a cure fraction of 0.25 at 1.5 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At 1.5 per cent a year the new treatment gives about 4.518 QALYs and the comparator about 2.506, a gain of about 2.01 QALYs, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted cure QALYs with a cure fraction of 0.25 at 1.5 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "pi = 0.25; u_C = 0.8; u_U = 0.6; mu = 0.04; lambda = 0.46; r = 0.0148886; QALY_d = 4.517719" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-CRM-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-cure-qalys-with-a-cure-fraction-of-0-25-at-1-5-per-cent" .

hemo:7003228 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Means and covariance taken from one joint distribution"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "E_N, E_U and Cov_NU describe the same population or the same set of paired simulation draws. Taking the two means from different sources and setting the covariance to zero assumes independence rather than establishing it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Means and covariance taken from one joint distribution" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EV-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "means-and-covariance-taken-from-one-joint-distribution" .

hemo:7003229 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Finite variances for the product identity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both quantities have finite variances, so the covariance exists. No distributional form and no independence is needed; with independence the identity reduces to the product of the means." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Finite variances for the product identity" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EV-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "finite-variances-for-the-product-identity" .

hemo:7003230 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected product from summary cells and from paired draws"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000598 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With MeanAdm, MeanUnitCost and CovAdmCost named, the first formula returns the expected product. With paired draws or patient records in the ranges AdmDraws and CostDraws, the second returns the mean of the products directly, which equals the first when the means and the population covariance COVARIANCE.P are taken from the same draws." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected product from summary cells and from paired draws" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EV-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-product-from-summary-cells-and-from-paired-draws" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MeanAdm*MeanUnitCost+CovAdmCost; =SUMPRODUCT(AdmDraws,CostDraws)/COUNT(AdmDraws)" .

hemo:7003231 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Product identity reproduced on paired draws"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "On paired draws, the mean of the products equals the product of the averages plus COVARIANCE.P of the two ranges. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the sample covariance COVARIANCE.S used in place of the population covariance, which divides by n minus 1, or ranges of different lengths." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Product identity reproduced on paired draws" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EV-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "product-identity-reproduced-on-paired-draws" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(AdmDraws,CostDraws)/COUNT(AdmDraws)/(AVERAGE(AdmDraws)*AVERAGE(CostDraws)+COVARIANCE.P(AdmDraws,CostDraws))-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7003232 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Admissions and cost per admission with a covariance of 300"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a mean of 1.5 admissions, a mean of £3,000 per admission and a covariance of 300, the expected cost is 1.5 x 3,000 + 300 = 4,800 pounds per patient, against £4,500 from multiplying the means, as in the article. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Admissions and cost per admission with a covariance of 300" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_N = 1.5; E_U = 3000; Cov_NU = 300; E_NU = 4800" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EV-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "admissions-and-cost-per-admission-with-a-covariance-of-300" .

hemo:7003233 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same admission means with independent counts and unit costs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When admissions and cost per admission are independent the covariance is zero and the expected cost is the product of the means, £4,500 per patient, so the covariance of 300 accounts for the whole gap of £300 in the first example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same admission means with independent counts and unit costs" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_N = 1.5; E_U = 3000; Cov_NU = 0; E_NU = 4500" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EV-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-admission-means-with-independent-counts-and-unit-costs" .

hemo:7003234 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same admission means with a negative covariance of 300"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If patients with more admissions had cheaper admissions, a covariance of minus 300 would lower the expected cost to £4,200 per patient, below the product of the means; correlation can narrow or widen the gap, as the article notes. The figure is computed here for illustration." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same admission means with a negative covariance of 300" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_N = 1.5; E_U = 3000; Cov_NU = -300; E_NU = 4200" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EV-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-admission-means-with-a-negative-covariance-of-300" .

hemo:7003235 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Smooth output and a concentrated parameter distribution"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The output is twice differentiable near the mean and the parameter distribution is concentrated enough for third and higher-order terms to be small. With a wide distribution or strong curvature the approximation can miss by a large margin, as for the log-normal cost in HE-EX-EV-006." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Smooth output and a concentrated parameter distribution" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EV-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "smooth-output-and-a-concentrated-parameter-distribution" .

hemo:7003236 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Single uncertain parameter in the second-order expansion"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The form is written for one parameter. With several parameters each pair adds a cross term with its covariance; leaving the cross terms out assumes the parameters are uncorrelated." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Single uncertain parameter in the second-order expansion" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EV-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "single-uncertain-parameter-in-the-second-order-expansion" .

hemo:7003237 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Second-order expected output from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000599 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With OutputAtMean, SecondDeriv and ParamVar named, the first formula returns the approximation, held in ApproxOutput. For the fracture example the second formula computes it directly from MeanHazard, Horizon and HazardVar." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Second-order expected output from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EV-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "second-order-expected-output-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=OutputAtMean+0.5*SecondDeriv*ParamVar; =(1-EXP(-MeanHazard*Horizon))-0.5*Horizon^2*EXP(-MeanHazard*Horizon)*HazardVar" .

hemo:7003238 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Analytic second derivative of the fracture probability matches a central difference"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A central difference with a step of 0.001 around the mean hazard reproduces the analytic second derivative of the fracture probability held in SecondDeriv. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows a sign error or a missing square on the horizon, which gives about minus 3.03 in place of minus 15.16." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Analytic second derivative of the fracture probability matches a central difference" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EV-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "analytic-second-derivative-of-the-fracture-probability-matches-a-central-difference" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(((1-EXP(-(MeanHazard+0.001)*Horizon))-2*(1-EXP(-MeanHazard*Horizon))+(1-EXP(-(MeanHazard-0.001)*Horizon)))/0.001^2-SecondDeriv)<0.001" .

hemo:7003239 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Second-order correction has the sign of the curvature"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The approximation lies below the output at the mean when the second derivative is negative and above it when the second derivative is positive. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the correction subtracted rather than added, or a second derivative taken of a different output." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Second-order correction has the sign of the curvature" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EV-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "second-order-correction-has-the-sign-of-the-curvature" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SIGN(ApproxOutput-OutputAtMean)=SIGN(SecondDeriv)" .

hemo:7003240 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Five-year fracture probability at an uncertain hazard"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At a mean hazard of 0.10 a year and a horizon of 5 years the deterministic probability is about 0.3935 and its second derivative about minus 15.16. With a hazard variance of 0.005 the correction is about minus 0.038 and the approximate expectation about 0.356, close to the exact 0.36 from HE-FM-EV-003, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Five-year fracture probability at an uncertain hazard" ;
    hemo:9000014 "g_mu = 0.39347; d2g = -15.163; Var_theta = 0.005; E_g = 0.35556" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EV-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "five-year-fracture-probability-at-an-uncertain-hazard" .

hemo:7003241 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Five-year fracture-free survival at the same uncertain hazard"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Fracture-free survival exp(minus 5h) is convex, so the same terms with the opposite sign raise its approximate expectation from about 0.6065 to about 0.6444, above the exact 0.64: the sign of the correction follows the curvature. The approximation is computed here for illustration." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Five-year fracture-free survival at the same uncertain hazard" ;
    hemo:9000014 "g_mu = 0.60653; d2g = 15.163; Var_theta = 0.005; E_g = 0.64444" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EV-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "five-year-fracture-free-survival-at-the-same-uncertain-hazard" .

hemo:7003242 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Exponential of a log cost with a standard deviation of 1.0"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a log-normal cost with a median of £2,000 and a standard deviation of log cost of 1.0, the output is the exponential of log cost, whose second derivative equals the output itself, £2,000 at the mean log cost. The approximation gives £3,000 against the exact mean of about £3,297 from HE-FM-EV-004, so with a large variance the expansion understates the gap. The figures are computed here for illustration." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exponential of a log cost with a standard deviation of 1.0" ;
    hemo:9000014 "g_mu = 2000; d2g = 2000; Var_theta = 1; E_g = 3000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EV-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exponential-of-a-log-cost-with-a-standard-deviation-of-1-0" .

hemo:7003243 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Hazard constant over the horizon in every draw"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each value of h applies unchanged from time 0 to t; the uncertainty is in the level of the hazard, not in its shape over time." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hazard constant over the horizon in every draw" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EV-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hazard-constant-over-the-horizon-in-every-draw" .

hemo:7003244 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Gamma distribution of the hazard in shape and scale form"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The hazard follows a gamma distribution with shape k and scale s. Excel GAMMA.DIST and Python random.gammavariate take the scale; R rgamma takes the rate as its third positional argument, so a rate needs converting to 1 over the rate before use here." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gamma distribution of the hazard in shape and scale form" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EV-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gamma-distribution-of-the-hazard-in-shape-and-scale-form" .

hemo:7003245 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Uncertain hazard shared by the whole cohort"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The average is over uncertainty in a hazard shared by every patient, the parameter or second-order uncertainty of the article, so the result is the expected cohort probability, not a probability known to apply to each patient. Read as variation in hazard between patients, the same formula gives the marginal survival of a gamma-frailty population." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Uncertain hazard shared by the whole cohort" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EV-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uncertain-hazard-shared-by-the-whole-cohort" .

hemo:7003246 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Expected event probability under a gamma hazard from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000600 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With HazShape, HazScale and Horizon named, the formula returns the expected event probability, held in ExpProb. Excel GAMMA.DIST and GAMMA.INV take the same shape and scale arguments." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Expected event probability under a gamma hazard from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EV-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "expected-event-probability-under-a-gamma-hazard-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1-(1+HazScale*Horizon)^(-HazShape)" .

hemo:7003247 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gamma parameters reproduce the hazard mean and variance and the expected probability lies below the deterministic one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The shape times the scale equals the reported mean hazard MeanHazard, the shape times the scale squared equals the reported variance HazardVar, and the expected probability is positive and below the probability at the mean hazard. Expected result: TRUE for any positive horizon. FALSE shows the rate entered in place of the scale: a rate of 20 gives a mean hazard of 40." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gamma parameters reproduce the hazard mean and variance and the expected probability lies below the deterministic one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EV-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gamma-parameters-reproduce-the-hazard-mean-and-variance-and-the-expected-probability-lies-below-the-deterministic-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS(HazShape*HazScale-MeanHazard)<1E-9,ABS(HazShape*HazScale^2-HazardVar)<1E-9,ExpProb>0,ExpProb<1-EXP(-MeanHazard*Horizon))" .

hemo:7003248 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Gamma hazard with shape 2 and scale 0.05 over five years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a mean hazard of 0.10 a year and a variance of 0.005, the expected fracture-free survival over 5 years is 1.25 raised to the power minus 2, or 0.64, and the expected fracture probability 0.36, against 0.3935 at the mean hazard. At £12,000 per fracture the expected cost is £4,320 rather than about £4,722 per person, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Gamma hazard with shape 2 and scale 0.05 over five years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "k = 2; s = 0.05; t = 5; S_bar = 0.64; p_bar = 0.36" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EV-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "gamma-hazard-with-shape-2-and-scale-0-05-over-five-years" .

hemo:7003249 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same gamma hazard over a horizon of 23 years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Over 23 years the expected probability is about 0.7837 against about 0.8997 at the mean hazard, a gap of about 0.116 and the largest for this hazard; the article places the peak at a horizon of about 20 to 25 years." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same gamma hazard over a horizon of 23 years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "k = 2; s = 0.05; t = 23; S_bar = 0.21633; p_bar = 0.78367" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EV-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-gamma-hazard-over-a-horizon-of-23-years" .

hemo:7003250 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "More precise hazard with the same mean of 0.10"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With shape 200 and scale 0.0005, the same mean of 0.10 but a standard deviation of about 0.0071, the expected probability over 5 years is about 0.3931, within 0.0004 of the deterministic 0.3935: the gap shrinks with a more precise hazard, as the article states. The figures are computed here for illustration." ;
    hemo:9000009 "More precise hazard with the same mean of 0.10" ;
    hemo:9000014 "k = 200; s = 0.0005; t = 5; S_bar = 0.60691; p_bar = 0.39309" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EV-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "more-precise-hazard-with-the-same-mean-of-0-10" .

hemo:7003251 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Log cost normally distributed with no zero costs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The natural log of cost follows a normal distribution, which requires every cost to be positive; zero costs need a separate part of the model." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log cost normally distributed with no zero costs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EV-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-cost-normally-distributed-with-no-zero-costs" .

hemo:7003252 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Log-normal parameters treated as known"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "mu and sigma are treated as known values. When they are estimated from a sample they carry sampling error, which this formula does not reflect." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log-normal parameters treated as known" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EV-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-normal-parameters-treated-as-known" .

hemo:7003253 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Log-normal expected cost and median from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000601 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With MeanLogCost and SDLogCost named, the formulas return the expected cost, held in ExpCost, and the median, held in MedianCost. A median of £2,000 gives MeanLogCost as =LN(2000)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log-normal expected cost and median from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EV-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-normal-expected-cost-and-median-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EXP(MeanLogCost+SDLogCost^2/2); =EXP(MeanLogCost)" .

hemo:7003254 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Share of log-normal patients below the expected cost"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "LOGNORM.DIST at the expected cost equals NORM.S.DIST at half the standard deviation of log cost, about 0.6915 for a standard deviation of 1.0, the share of patients who cost less than the mean in the article. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows the squared standard deviation not halved, which puts the computed mean at about the 84th percentile." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Share of log-normal patients below the expected cost" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EV-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "share-of-log-normal-patients-below-the-expected-cost" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LOGNORM.DIST(ExpCost,MeanLogCost,SDLogCost,TRUE)-NORM.S.DIST(SDLogCost/2,TRUE))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003255 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Log-normal cost with a median of £2,000 and a standard deviation of log cost of 1.0"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With mu equal to ln 2000, about 7.601, and sigma of 1.0, the expected cost is £2,000 times exp(0.5), about £3,297, about 65 per cent above the median, as in the article. For 5,000 patients the expected budget is about £16.49 million against £10.0 million from the median. The figures are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Log-normal cost with a median of £2,000 and a standard deviation of log cost of 1.0" ;
    hemo:9000014 "mu = 7.600902; sigma = 1; E_C = 3297.44; M_C = 2000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EV-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "log-normal-cost-with-a-median-of-2-000-and-a-standard-deviation-of-log-cost-of-1-0" .

hemo:7003256 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same median with a standard deviation of log cost of 1.2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the same median and a standard deviation of log cost of 1.2, the expected cost rises to about £4,109, as in the article, so the mean depends on how the upper tail is modelled." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same median with a standard deviation of log cost of 1.2" ;
    hemo:9000014 "mu = 7.6009025; sigma = 1.2; E_C = 4108.87; M_C = 2000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EV-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-median-with-a-standard-deviation-of-log-cost-of-1-2" .

hemo:7003257 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One normative standard for every population and both sexes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The years lost for a death depend only on the age at death, not on where the death happened or on local life expectancy. GBD from 2010 onwards and WHO use one standard for both sexes; the GBD 1990 standard had separate tables for males and females." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One normative standard for every population and both sexes" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-YLL-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-normative-standard-for-every-population-and-both-sexes" .

hemo:7003258 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard value applied to every death in the age group"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each death in an age group counts the tabulated value for that group, so the result depends on the age grouping of the death data. WHO tabulates the standards for neonatal and postneonatal deaths, ages 1 to 4, five-year groups to 80 to 84, and 85 and over." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Standard value applied to every death in the age group" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-YLL-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "standard-value-applied-to-every-death-in-the-age-group" .

hemo:7003259 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Years of life lost counted without discounting or age weighting"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each standard year counts in full, as in GBD from 2010 onwards and in WHO estimates since its 2012 consultations. The discounted form of the original DALY is HE-FM-YLL-003." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Years of life lost counted without discounting or age weighting" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-YLL-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "years-of-life-lost-counted-without-discounting-or-age-weighting" .

hemo:7003260 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Years of life lost for one age group from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000602 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the deaths in a cell named Deaths and the standard value for the age group in StdLE, the formula returns the YLLs for the group, held in YLLGroup." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Years of life lost for one age group from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-YLL-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "years-of-life-lost-for-one-age-group-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Deaths*StdLE" .

hemo:7003261 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive standard years per death and the age group product reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Deaths are zero or more, StdLE is above zero and YLLGroup equals Deaths times StdLE. Expected result: TRUE. FALSE shows, for example, a death at age 88 counted as life expectancy at birth minus age, 86.01 minus 88, or minus 1.99 years, where the GBD 2010 standard gives 5.05 years at ages 85 and over." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive standard years per death and the age group product reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-YLL-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-standard-years-per-death-and-the-age-group-product-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(Deaths>=0,StdLE>0,ABS(YLLGroup-Deaths*StdLE)<1E-9)" .

