hemo:7003457 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Even flow within each year of a continuously discounted stream"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The amount accrues at a constant pace through time, as a QALY gain does while a person lives in a health state. A cost paid at one moment, such as a treatment given at the start, is discounted with the single-value factor instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Even flow within each year of a continuously discounted stream" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DISC-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "even-flow-within-each-year-of-a-continuously-discounted-stream" .

hemo:7003458 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous rate taken from the annual rate in force"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "rho is derived from the annual rate r set by the governing guidance, so the continuous and discrete factors agree at each whole year. Larson notes that a continuous rate of 0.03 corresponds to an annual rate of exp(0.03) minus 1, about 0.0305." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuous rate taken from the annual rate in force" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DISC-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuous-rate-taken-from-the-annual-rate-in-force" .

hemo:7003459 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuously discounted even flow from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000620 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The first formula returns the continuous rate. In the second, EXP(minus rho times T) equals (1 + r) to the power minus T, so the total needs only the annual rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuously discounted even flow from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DISC-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuously-discounted-even-flow-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LN(1+DiscRate); =YearlyAmount*(1-(1+DiscRate)^-Years)/LN(1+DiscRate)" .

hemo:7003460 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous total between end-of-year and start-of-year totals"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a positive rate the continuously discounted total lies above the end-of-year total and below the start-of-year total for the same amount and number of years. The expected result is TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuous total between end-of-year and start-of-year totals" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DISC-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuous-total-between-end-of-year-and-start-of-year-totals" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ContTotal>PV(DiscRate,Years,-YearlyAmount),ContTotal<PV(DiscRate,Years,-YearlyAmount,0,1))" .

hemo:7003461 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Larson's continuous-time adjustment factor reproduces the continuous total"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Multiplying the start-of-year total by Larson's adjustment factor, (1 minus exp(minus rho)) divided by rho, gives the continuous total exactly. The expected result is TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Larson's continuous-time adjustment factor reproduces the continuous total" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DISC-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "larson-s-continuous-time-adjustment-factor-reproduces-the-continuous-total" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ContTotal-(1-1/(1+DiscRate))/LN(1+DiscRate)*PV(DiscRate,Years,-YearlyAmount,0,1))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003462 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Larson's ten years discounted continuously at a continuous rate of 0.03"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003463,
        hemo:7003464,
        hemo:7003465 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003466,
        hemo:7003467 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Ten years of 1 discounted continuously at 0.03 are worth 8.6394 present years, Larson's continuous-time value. The annual rate that gives the same factors is about 0.0305." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Larson's ten years discounted continuously at a continuous rate of 0.03" ;
    hemo:9000014 "r = 0.0304545; q = 1; T = 10; rho = 0.03; Q_c = 8.6394" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DISC-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "larson-s-ten-years-discounted-continuously-at-a-continuous-rate-of-0-03" .

