    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002634 ;
    rheo:2000001 15614.700000000000728 .

hemo:7003490 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Annualised sums falling at the end of each year of use"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each annual sum is treated as falling at the end of its year. If the sums are treated as falling at the start of each year, the factor becomes 1 plus r, times A, and the annual charge is lower by the factor 1 plus r, so the convention has to match the timing of the model's other costs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annualised sums falling at the end of each year of use" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ANLS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annualised-sums-falling-at-the-end-of-each-year-of-use" .

hemo:7003491 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Annualisation rate equal to the evaluation's real discount rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The rate r is the one used to discount the evaluation's other costs, so that capital and recurrent costs are valued on one basis, for example 3.5% a year in the NICE reference case (PMG36, section 4.5.1). It is a real rate, applied to prices held constant in one price year." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annualisation rate equal to the evaluation's real discount rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ANLS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annualisation-rate-equal-to-the-evaluation-s-real-discount-rate" .

hemo:7003492 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Resale value counted whether or not the asset is sold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "S reflects the opportunity cost of the asset at the end of its useful life and does not depend on an actual sale, in line with the Green Book (2026) treatment of residual values." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Resale value counted whether or not the asset is sold" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ANLS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "resale-value-counted-whether-or-not-the-asset-is-sold" .

hemo:7003493 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Replacement price for capital bought in earlier years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "For an asset already in use, K is its current replacement price and n a full useful life. Capital bought in earlier years can still be resold, so it still has an opportunity cost and is not treated as costless." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Replacement price for capital bought in earlier years" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ANLS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "replacement-price-for-capital-bought-in-earlier-years" .

hemo:7003494 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same service in every year of the useful life"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The asset gives the same service in each year of its life. Equipment that becomes obsolete before it wears out has a shorter effective life, and a life set too long lowers the annual charge, so n, r and S belong in sensitivity analysis when capital is a large share of cost." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same service in every year of the useful life" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ANLS-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-service-in-every-year-of-the-useful-life" .

hemo:7003495 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Annualised capital charge net of resale value from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000622 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the price in a cell named CapitalPrice, the resale value in ResaleValue, the rate in DiscountRate and the life in UsefulLife, the formula returns E. The built-in form =PMT(DiscountRate,UsefulLife,-CapitalPrice,ResaleValue) gives the same result." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annualised capital charge net of resale value from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ANLS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annualised-capital-charge-net-of-resale-value-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(CapitalPrice-ResaleValue*(1+DiscountRate)^-UsefulLife)/((1-(1+DiscountRate)^-UsefulLife)/DiscountRate)" .

hemo:7003496 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Rearranged annualisation form with a holding charge on resale value"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The charge in a cell named AnnualCharge equals K minus S divided by the annuity factor, plus r times S. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows that the resale value was subtracted without discounting, which understates the charge by r times S." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rearranged annualisation form with a holding charge on resale value" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ANLS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rearranged-annualisation-form-with-a-holding-charge-on-resale-value" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AnnualCharge-((CapitalPrice-ResaleValue)/((1-(1+DiscountRate)^-UsefulLife)/DiscountRate)+DiscountRate*ResaleValue))<0.01" .

hemo:7003497 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Annualised charges and discounted resale value recover the purchase price"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Discount the n annual charges and the resale value back to the start of year 1. Expected result TRUE, because the total equals K. FALSE shows charges computed for the start of each year or at a different rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annualised charges and discounted resale value recover the purchase price" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ANLS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annualised-charges-and-discounted-resale-value-recover-the-purchase-price" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PV(DiscountRate,UsefulLife,-AnnualCharge,-ResaleValue)-CapitalPrice)<0.01" .

hemo:7003498 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Retinal camera with a GBP 5,000 resale value annualised over five years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An illustrative retinal camera costs GBP 50,000, lasts 5 years and has a resale value of GBP 5,000, with costs discounted at 3.5%. The annuity factor is about 4.5151 and the present value of the resale value about GBP 4,210, so the annualised charge is about GBP 10,142 a year, against GBP 9,000 under straight-line depreciation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Retinal camera with a GBP 5,000 resale value annualised over five years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K = 50000; S = 5000; r = 0.035; n = 5; A = 4.51505; E = 10141.66" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ANLS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "retinal-camera-with-a-gbp-5-000-resale-value-annualised-over-five-years" .

hemo:7003499 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "No value left at the end of the useful life"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The input is worth nothing when it is replaced. When it can be sold or reused, HE-FM-ANLS-001 with the discounted resale value applies instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No value left at the end of the useful life" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ANLS-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-value-left-at-the-end-of-the-useful-life" .

hemo:7003500 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Life set by the replacement or repeat interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "For training and other start-up inputs, n is the interval at which the input is repeated. The GHCC glossary gives the example that training repeated every five years is spread over five years." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Life set by the replacement or repeat interval" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ANLS-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "life-set-by-the-replacement-or-repeat-interval" .

hemo:7003501 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Annualised charge with no resale value using Excel PMT"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000623 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "PMT returns the equal end-of-year payment that repays a loan of K at rate r over n years. The price is entered as a negative present value so that the charge is positive, and the type argument is left at 0 for end-of-year sums." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annualised charge with no resale value using Excel PMT" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ANLS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annualised-charge-with-no-resale-value-using-excel-pmt" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PMT(DiscountRate,UsefulLife,-CapitalPrice)" .

hemo:7003502 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Annualised charge without resale value repays the price and exceeds straight-line"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The charge in a cell named AnnualCharge has a present value over n years equal to the price and is larger than the price divided by the useful life. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a start-of-year charge, a rate entered as a percentage or a rate of zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annualised charge without resale value repays the price and exceeds straight-line" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ANLS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annualised-charge-without-resale-value-repays-the-price-and-exceeds-straight-line" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS(PV(DiscountRate,UsefulLife,-AnnualCharge)-CapitalPrice)<0.01,AnnualCharge>CapitalPrice/UsefulLife)" .

hemo:7003503 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Retinal camera with no resale value annualised over five years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The GBP 50,000 camera with no resale value, a 5-year life and a 3.5% rate has an annualised charge of about GBP 11,074 a year, against GBP 10,000 under straight-line depreciation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Retinal camera with no resale value annualised over five years" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K = 50000; r = 0.035; n = 5; A = 4.51505; E = 11074.07" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ANLS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "retinal-camera-with-no-resale-value-annualised-over-five-years" .

hemo:7003504 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Screener training annualised over its four-year repeat interval"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Training that costs GBP 12,000 and is repeated every 4 years has an annuity factor of about 3.6731 at 3.5% and an annualised charge of about GBP 3,267 a year, against GBP 3,000 on a straight-line basis." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Screener training annualised over its four-year repeat interval" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K = 12000; r = 0.035; n = 4; A = 3.67308; E = 3267.01" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ANLS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "screener-training-annualised-over-its-four-year-repeat-interval" .

hemo:7003505 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Straight-line and annualised charges with no resale value"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both charges use the same price and useful life and no resale value. With a resale value the straight-line charge is K minus S divided by n, and the gap also includes the holding charge of r times S." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Straight-line and annualised charges with no resale value" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ANLS-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "straight-line-and-annualised-charges-with-no-resale-value" .

hemo:7003506 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Annualised to straight-line ratio from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000624 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the life in UsefulLife and the rate in DiscountRate, the formula returns R_SL. Multiplying it by the straight-line charge gives the equivalent annual cost with no resale value." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annualised to straight-line ratio from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ANLS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annualised-to-straight-line-ratio-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=UsefulLife/((1-(1+DiscountRate)^-UsefulLife)/DiscountRate)" .

hemo:7003507 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Annualised to straight-line ratios reproduce the article's table at 3.5%"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The ratios for lives of 5, 10, 20 and 60 years at 3.5% round to 1.107, 1.202, 1.407 and 2.405. Expected result TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annualised to straight-line ratios reproduce the article's table at 3.5%" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ANLS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annualised-to-straight-line-ratios-reproduce-the-article-s-table-at-3-5" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(5/((1-1.035^-5)/0.035),3)=1.107,ROUND(10/((1-1.035^-10)/0.035),3)=1.202,ROUND(20/((1-1.035^-20)/0.035),3)=1.407,ROUND(60/((1-1.035^-60)/0.035),3)=2.405)" .

hemo:7003508 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Annualised to straight-line ratio tends to one at a near-zero rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At a rate of 0.000001 the ratio for a 60-year life is within 0.001 of 1. Expected result TRUE. A result far from 1 shows an error in the annuity factor." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Annualised to straight-line ratio tends to one at a near-zero rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ANLS-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "annualised-to-straight-line-ratio-tends-to-one-at-a-near-zero-rate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(60/((1-(1+0.000001)^-60)/0.000001)-1)<0.001" .

hemo:7003509 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Five-year device ratio of annualised to straight-line charge at 3.5%"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a five-year device at 3.5% the annuity factor is about 4.515, so the economic charge is about 11% above straight-line depreciation, as in the article's table." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Five-year device ratio of annualised to straight-line charge at 3.5%" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n = 5; r = 0.035; A = 4.51505; R_SL = 1.1074" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ANLS-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "five-year-device-ratio-of-annualised-to-straight-line-charge-at-3-5" .

hemo:7003510 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Sixty-year building ratio of annualised to straight-line charge at 3.5%"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a building with a 60-year life at 3.5% the annuity factor is about 24.945, so the economic charge is about 2.4 times the straight-line charge. Services that occupy purpose-built space show the largest effect." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sixty-year building ratio of annualised to straight-line charge at 3.5%" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n = 60; r = 0.035; A = 24.94473; R_SL = 2.4053" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ANLS-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sixty-year-building-ratio-of-annualised-to-straight-line-charge-at-3-5" .

hemo:7003511 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Sixty-year building ratio of annualised to straight-line charge at 1.5%"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At 1.5%, the rate NICE allows for alternative analyses in specific circumstances (PMG36, section 4.5.2), the annuity factor for 60 years is about 39.380 and the economic charge about 1.52 times the straight-line charge, so the gap for long-lived assets depends heavily on the rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sixty-year building ratio of annualised to straight-line charge at 1.5%" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n = 60; r = 0.015; A = 39.38027; R_SL = 1.5236" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ANLS-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sixty-year-building-ratio-of-annualised-to-straight-line-charge-at-1-5" .

hemo:7003512 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Known within-study variances on an approximately normal effect scale"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each y_i is approximately normally distributed with a variance v_i that is treated as known. The Cochrane Handbook advises that a ratio measure always enters the regression as its logarithm, so that the exponential of beta_1 is the relative change in the effect per unit of the covariate (HE-FM-MREG-004)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Known within-study variances on an approximately normal effect scale" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MREG-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "known-within-study-variances-on-an-approximately-normal-effect-scale" .

hemo:7003513 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Linear covariate relation with normal residual heterogeneity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The true effects lie around a line that is linear in x_i on the chosen scale, with normally distributed deviations of variance tau2. The model is usually fitted in two steps, first estimating tau2 and then estimating beta_0 and beta_1 by weighted least squares with the weights of HE-FM-MREG-002. Treating the estimate of tau2 as known makes the standard errors too small, and the Knapp and Hartung adjustment, which bases tests on a t distribution with k minus p degrees of freedom for k studies and p coefficients, gives error rates closer to nominal." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Linear covariate relation with normal residual heterogeneity" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MREG-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "linear-covariate-relation-with-normal-residual-heterogeneity" .

hemo:7003514 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Enough studies and pre-specified covariates for a meta-regression"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The Cochrane Handbook says meta-regression should generally not be considered with fewer than ten studies, cites typical advice of at least ten studies for each characteristic modelled, and asks for a small number of characteristics pre-specified in the protocol with a scientific rationale for each. Participants are randomised within trials but not between them, so beta_1 describes an observational association across studies." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Enough studies and pre-specified covariates for a meta-regression" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MREG-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "enough-studies-and-pre-specified-covariates-for-a-meta-regression" .

hemo:7003515 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted least squares slope and intercept of a meta-regression from three ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000625 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the study estimates in a range named StudyEst, the covariate values in a range named Covariate and the weights of HE-FM-MREG-002 in a range named W, the first formula returns beta_1 and the second beta_0, with the first result held in a cell named Slope. SUMPRODUCT evaluates the array arithmetic without an array entry." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted least squares slope and intercept of a meta-regression from three ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MREG-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-least-squares-slope-and-intercept-of-a-meta-regression-from-three-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(W,Covariate-SUMPRODUCT(W,Covariate)/SUM(W),StudyEst)/SUMPRODUCT(W,(Covariate-SUMPRODUCT(W,Covariate)/SUM(W))^2); =SUMPRODUCT(W,StudyEst)/SUM(W)-Slope*SUMPRODUCT(W,Covariate)/SUM(W)" .

hemo:7003516 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Meta-regression estimates lying exactly on a line return its slope"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Three estimates placed exactly on the line with intercept 0.11 and slope 0.30, at covariate values of -3, -2 and -1, return a slope of 0.30 whatever weights are used, here 10, 25 and 14. Expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the weights and covariate ranges misaligned or the weighted mean of the covariate omitted." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Meta-regression estimates lying exactly on a line return its slope" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MREG-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "meta-regression-estimates-lying-exactly-on-a-line-return-its-slope" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(SUMPRODUCT({10,25,14},{-3,-2,-1}-SUMPRODUCT({10,25,14},{-3,-2,-1})/49,{-0.79,-0.49,-0.19})/SUMPRODUCT({10,25,14},({-3,-2,-1}-SUMPRODUCT({10,25,14},{-3,-2,-1})/49)^2),9)=0.3" .

hemo:7003517 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted meta-regression residuals sum to zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With an intercept in the model, the weighted residuals of a weighted least squares fit sum to zero. Expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows an intercept computed with unweighted means or weights that differ from those used for the slope." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted meta-regression residuals sum to zero" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MREG-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-meta-regression-residuals-sum-to-zero" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(W,StudyEst-Intercept-Slope*Covariate))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003518 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Meta-regression line plus residual terms for one illustrative trial"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The article's illustrative fit on the baseline log-odds of the event has a slope of 0.30 and an effect of -0.40 at the trials' mean log-odds of -1.70, which corresponds to an intercept beta_0 of 0.11 at a log-odds of zero. A trial at the mean whose true log odds ratio lies 0.10 below the line and whose sampling error is +0.05 reports a log odds ratio of -0.45. The deviation and error values are illustrative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Meta-regression line plus residual terms for one illustrative trial" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta_0 = 0.11; beta_1 = 0.30; x_i = -1.70; u_i = -0.10; e_i = 0.05; y_i = -0.45" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "meta-regression-line-plus-residual-terms-for-one-illustrative-trial" .

hemo:7003519 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Meta-regression line at a decision population's baseline log-odds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a population with a baseline risk of 5%, a log-odds of about -2.944, the line with both error terms set to zero gives an expected log odds ratio of about -0.7732, an odds ratio of about 0.462. The value matches the centred form in HE-FM-MREG-005, as it must." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Meta-regression line at a decision population's baseline log-odds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta_0 = 0.11; beta_1 = 0.30; x_i = -2.944; u_i = 0; e_i = 0; y_i = -0.7732" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "meta-regression-line-at-a-decision-population-s-baseline-log-odds" .

hemo:7003520 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Residual variance taken from the fitted meta-regression"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The tau2 in the weight is the residual estimate from the model that contains the covariates, estimated by a method such as restricted maximum likelihood or DerSimonian and Laird, and then treated as known while the coefficients are estimated." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Residual variance taken from the fitted meta-regression" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MREG-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "residual-variance-taken-from-the-fitted-meta-regression" .

hemo:7003521 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Meta-regression weights from a variance range and the residual tau2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000626 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the within-study variances in a range named StudyVar and the residual between-study variance in a cell named ResidTau2, the formula returns the weights as an array, or one weight per row when written against a single variance cell." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Meta-regression weights from a variance range and the residual tau2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MREG-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "meta-regression-weights-from-a-variance-range-and-the-residual-tau2" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1/(StudyVar+ResidTau2)" .

hemo:7003522 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Meta-regression weight positive and no larger than the fixed-effect weight"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With one weight in a cell named Weight and its within-study variance in a cell named Variance, the weight lies above zero and at or below 1/v_i. Expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows a negative tau2 or a standard error entered as a variance." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Meta-regression weight positive and no larger than the fixed-effect weight" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MREG-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "meta-regression-weight-positive-and-no-larger-than-the-fixed-effect-weight" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(Weight>0,Weight<=1/Variance)" .

hemo:7003523 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Smaller illustrative trial meta-regression weight reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A within-study variance of 0.04 and a residual tau2 of 0.03 return a weight of 14.2857. Expected result is TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Smaller illustrative trial meta-regression weight reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MREG-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "smaller-illustrative-trial-meta-regression-weight-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(1/(0.04+0.03),4)=14.2857" .

hemo:7003524 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Meta-regression weight of a smaller illustrative trial"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A trial with a within-study variance of 0.04 and a residual tau2 of 0.03, as in the article's illustrative fit, has a weight of about 14.29." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Meta-regression weight of a smaller illustrative trial" ;
    hemo:9000014 "v_i = 0.04; tau2 = 0.03; w_i = 14.2857" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "meta-regression-weight-of-a-smaller-illustrative-trial" .

hemo:7003525 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Meta-regression weight of a larger illustrative trial"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A trial with a within-study variance of 0.01 and the same residual tau2 has a weight of 25. It carries 1.75 times the weight of the smaller trial, against four times under fixed-effect weights of 100 and 25." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Meta-regression weight of a larger illustrative trial" ;
    hemo:9000014 "v_i = 0.01; tau2 = 0.03; w_i = 25" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "meta-regression-weight-of-a-larger-illustrative-trial" .

hemo:7003526 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fixed-effect meta-regression weight with zero residual variance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With tau2 set to zero the weight reduces to the inverse of the within-study variance, 100 for a variance of 0.01." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fixed-effect meta-regression weight with zero residual variance" ;
    hemo:9000014 "v_i = 0.01; tau2 = 0; w_i = 100" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fixed-effect-meta-regression-weight-with-zero-residual-variance" .

hemo:7003527 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same studies and same estimator for both between-study variances"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both variances come from the same set of studies on the same effect scale and from the same estimator of tau2, so that the fall reflects the covariates and not a change of method or of sample." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same studies and same estimator for both between-study variances" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MREG-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-studies-and-same-estimator-for-both-between-study-variances" .

hemo:7003528 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Share of heterogeneity explained from two tau2 cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000627 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the between-study variance without covariates in a cell named Tau2NoCov and the residual variance in a cell named Tau2Resid, the formula returns the proportion explained." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Share of heterogeneity explained from two tau2 cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MREG-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "share-of-heterogeneity-explained-from-two-tau2-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(Tau2NoCov-Tau2Resid)/Tau2NoCov" .

hemo:7003529 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Share of heterogeneity explained never above one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the result in a cell named ShareExplained, the residual variance is not negative and the share is at most 1. Expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the two variances swapped in the denominator or a negative residual estimate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Share of heterogeneity explained never above one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MREG-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "share-of-heterogeneity-explained-never-above-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(Tau2Resid>=0,ShareExplained<=1)" .

hemo:7003530 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "BCG vaccine share of heterogeneity reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The two estimates from the BCG vaccine example return 65% when rounded to two decimals. Expected result is TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "BCG vaccine share of heterogeneity reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MREG-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "bcg-vaccine-share-of-heterogeneity-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND((0.3132-0.1108)/0.3132,2)=0.65" .

hemo:7003531 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Illustrative baseline-risk meta-regression explaining two thirds of heterogeneity"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative example the between-study variance falls from 0.09 to a residual 0.03 when the baseline log-odds is added, so the covariate accounts for about 67% of the heterogeneity." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Illustrative baseline-risk meta-regression explaining two thirds of heterogeneity" ;
    hemo:9000014 "tau2_RE = 0.09; tau2_MR = 0.03; R2_het = 0.6667" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "illustrative-baseline-risk-meta-regression-explaining-two-thirds-of-heterogeneity" .

hemo:7003532 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "BCG vaccine meta-regression with two moderators"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In Viechtbauer's BCG vaccine example the restricted maximum likelihood estimate of tau2 falls from 0.3132 to 0.1108 when absolute latitude and year are added, so about 65% of the heterogeneity is accounted for." ;
    hemo:9000009 "BCG vaccine meta-regression with two moderators" ;
    hemo:9000014 "tau2_RE = 0.3132; tau2_MR = 0.1108; R2_het = 0.6462" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "bcg-vaccine-meta-regression-with-two-moderators" .

hemo:7003533 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Ratio measure regressed on the log scale"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The relation is linear on the log scale, so on the ratio scale each unit of the covariate multiplies the ratio measure by the same factor. The Cochrane Handbook states that a ratio measure should always enter the regression as its logarithm." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ratio measure regressed on the log scale" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MREG-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ratio-measure-regressed-on-the-log-scale" .

hemo:7003534 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Relative change in a ratio measure from a meta-regression slope cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000628 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the log-scale slope in a cell named Slope and the change in the covariate in a cell named CovChange, the formula returns the multiplicative change in the ratio measure." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Relative change in a ratio measure from a meta-regression slope cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MREG-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "relative-change-in-a-ratio-measure-from-a-meta-regression-slope-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EXP(Slope*CovChange)" .

hemo:7003535 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Relative change matches the ratio of two predicted ratio measures"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For covariate values in cells named CovA and CovB and the intercept in a cell named Intercept, the factor equals the predicted ratio measure at CovB divided by that at CovA. Expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows a slope taken from a regression on the ratio scale or not exponentiated." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Relative change matches the ratio of two predicted ratio measures" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MREG-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "relative-change-matches-the-ratio-of-two-predicted-ratio-measures" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(EXP(Slope*(CovB-CovA))-EXP(Intercept+Slope*CovB)/EXP(Intercept+Slope*CovA))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003536 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Per-unit odds ratio change reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A slope of 0.30 returns a per-unit factor of 1.3499. Expected result is TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Per-unit odds ratio change reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MREG-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "per-unit-odds-ratio-change-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(EXP(0.3),4)=1.3499" .

hemo:7003537 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Odds ratio change per unit of baseline log-odds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's illustrative slope of 0.30, each unit increase in the baseline log-odds multiplies the odds ratio by about 1.35, so the protective effect weakens as baseline risk rises." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Odds ratio change per unit of baseline log-odds" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta_1 = 0.30; Delta_x = 1; RC = 1.3499" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "odds-ratio-change-per-unit-of-baseline-log-odds" .

hemo:7003538 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Odds ratio change from the trials' mean risk to a 5% baseline risk"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Moving from the trials' mean log-odds of -1.70 to the log-odds of a 5% risk, about -2.944, is a change of about -1.244. The factor is about 0.689, the ratio of the adjusted odds ratio of about 0.462 to the odds ratio of 0.670 at the mean." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Odds ratio change from the trials' mean risk to a 5% baseline risk" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta_1 = 0.30; Delta_x = -1.244; RC = 0.6885" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "odds-ratio-change-from-the-trials-mean-risk-to-a-5-baseline-risk" .

hemo:7003539 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Covariate centred on the scale of the linear predictor"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The covariate is centred at its mean on the scale used in the model. For meta-regression on baseline risk with a logit link, TSD 3 centres on the mean baseline log-odds, so z must also be a log-odds and x_bar a mean of log-odds." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Covariate centred on the scale of the linear predictor" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MREG-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "covariate-centred-on-the-scale-of-the-linear-predictor" .

hemo:7003540 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Decision population inside the covariate range of the trials"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The line is used within the range of covariate values the trials cover, 4% to 35% control-group risk in the article's illustrative example, where a 5% target lies inside the range." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Decision population inside the covariate range of the trials" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MREG-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "decision-population-inside-the-covariate-range-of-the-trials" .

hemo:7003541 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One interaction term common to all treatments in a network meta-regression"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "In a network meta-analysis TSD 3 favours a single interaction term common to all treatments relative to the reference, since separate terms could lead a strict cost-effectiveness analysis to recommend different treatments for different subgroups. One b then adjusts every comparison with the reference." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One interaction term common to all treatments in a network meta-regression" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-MREG-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-interaction-term-common-to-all-treatments-in-a-network-meta-regression" .

hemo:7003542 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Adjusted relative effect from a centred meta-regression in one cell"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000629 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the effect at the mean in a cell named EffectAtMean, the interaction in Interaction, the mean covariate in CovMean and the population's covariate value in CovValue, the first formula returns theta_z. The second takes a baseline risk in a cell named Risk and converts it to log-odds inside the formula." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Adjusted relative effect from a centred meta-regression in one cell" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-MREG-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "adjusted-relative-effect-from-a-centred-meta-regression-in-one-cell" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EffectAtMean+Interaction*(CovValue-CovMean); =EffectAtMean+Interaction*(LN(Risk/(1-Risk))-CovMean)" .

hemo:7003543 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Adjusted effect returns to d at the trials' mean baseline risk"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The baseline risk whose log-odds is the mean of -1.70, about 0.1544653, returns an effect of -0.40. Expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the risk entered without the logit conversion or a centring value on another scale." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Adjusted effect returns to d at the trials' mean baseline risk" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MREG-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "adjusted-effect-returns-to-d-at-the-trials-mean-baseline-risk" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(-0.40+0.30*(LN(0.1544653/(1-0.1544653))+1.70),4)=-0.4" .

hemo:7003544 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's 5% baseline risk adjustment reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A 5% baseline risk with the article's illustrative fit returns an adjusted log odds ratio of -0.773. Expected result is TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's 5% baseline risk adjustment reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-MREG-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-5-baseline-risk-adjustment-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(-0.40+0.30*(LN(0.05/0.95)+1.70),3)=-0.773" .

hemo:7003545 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Adjusted log odds ratio for a 5% baseline risk population"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With d of -0.40 at the trials' mean log-odds of -1.70, an interaction of 0.30 and a decision population with a 5% baseline risk, a log-odds of about -2.944, the adjusted log odds ratio is about -0.773, an odds ratio of about 0.462, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Adjusted log odds ratio for a 5% baseline risk population" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d = -0.40; b = 0.30; z = -2.9444; x_bar = -1.70; theta_z = -0.7733" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "adjusted-log-odds-ratio-for-a-5-baseline-risk-population" .

hemo:7003546 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Centred meta-regression effect at the mean covariate value"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At z equal to the mean of -1.70, a baseline risk of about 15.4%, the adjustment term is zero and the effect is d." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Centred meta-regression effect at the mean covariate value" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d = -0.40; b = 0.30; z = -1.70; x_bar = -1.70; theta_z = -0.40" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "centred-meta-regression-effect-at-the-mean-covariate-value" .

hemo:7003547 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Centred meta-regression effect at a 35% baseline risk"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At the top of the illustrative range, a 35% baseline risk or a log-odds of about -0.619, the adjusted log odds ratio is about -0.0757, an odds ratio of about 0.927, so little benefit remains (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Centred meta-regression effect at a 35% baseline risk" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d = -0.40; b = 0.30; z = -0.6190; x_bar = -1.70; theta_z = -0.0757" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-MREG-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "centred-meta-regression-effect-at-a-35-baseline-risk" .

hemo:7003548 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Simple hyperbolic weight measured from the moment of choice"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weight depends only on the delay counted from the person's present, so it is re-anchored as time passes and an outcome two months away today is one month away next month. Frederick and colleagues report that Strotz recognised that any discount function other than the exponential gives time-inconsistent preferences, and the re-anchoring is where that inconsistency arises." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Simple hyperbolic weight measured from the moment of choice" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HYPD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "simple-hyperbolic-weight-measured-from-the-moment-of-choice" .

hemo:7003549 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Hyperbolic parameter and delay in one time unit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The product alpha t has no unit, so alpha per month is used with t in months. Moving to years multiplies alpha by 12, because the product for a given calendar delay must stay the same." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hyperbolic parameter and delay in one time unit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HYPD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hyperbolic-parameter-and-delay-in-one-time-unit" .

hemo:7003550 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Simple hyperbola as a descriptive model of individual choice"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The form describes how individuals weigh delayed outcomes. For the NICE reference case, section 4.5.1 of PMG36 discounts costs and health effects at a constant 3.5% a year, and Attema and colleagues note that almost all guidelines prescribe constant rates, so the hyperbola informs behavioural parameters such as uptake or adherence, not the reference-case rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Simple hyperbola as a descriptive model of individual choice" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HYPD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "simple-hyperbola-as-a-descriptive-model-of-individual-choice" .

hemo:7003551 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Simple hyperbolic discount factor from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000630 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the parameter in HypAlpha and the delay in Delay, the cell returns the weight. The second formula fills a column of weights for the delays 0, 1, 2 and onwards in Excel 365 or Excel 2021." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Simple hyperbolic discount factor from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HYPD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "simple-hyperbolic-discount-factor-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1/(1+HypAlpha*Delay); =1/(1+HypAlpha*(SEQUENCE(Periods)-1))" .

hemo:7003552 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's simple hyperbolic weights reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha = 0.4 the weights one and two periods ahead are 0.7143 and 0.5556 to four decimal places, as in the article. The expected result is TRUE. Writing the second weight as 1/(1+0.4)^2, the compounding error, gives 0.5102 and makes it FALSE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's simple hyperbolic weights reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HYPD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-simple-hyperbolic-weights-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS(1/(1+0.4*1)-0.7143)<0.0001,ABS(1/(1+0.4*2)-0.5556)<0.0001)" .

hemo:7003553 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Simple hyperbolic weight not below the constant-rate factor with the same first-period rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a positive alpha and a whole number of periods, 1/(1 + alpha t) is never below 1/(1 + alpha)^t, with equality at t = 0 and t = 1, because (1 + alpha)^t is at least 1 + alpha t. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows a delay that is a fraction of one period, where the inequality reverses, or an alpha of zero or below." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Simple hyperbolic weight not below the constant-rate factor with the same first-period rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HYPD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "simple-hyperbolic-weight-not-below-the-constant-rate-factor-with-the-same-first-period-rate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(HypAlpha>0,1/(1+HypAlpha*Delay)>=(1+HypAlpha)^-Delay-1E-12)" .

hemo:7003554 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Simple hyperbolic weight one month ahead with alpha of 0.4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003555,
        hemo:7003556 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003557 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.00005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The article's illustrative smoker, with alpha = 0.4 a month, places a weight of about 0.714 on an outcome one month away, 1 divided by 1.4." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Simple hyperbolic weight one month ahead with alpha of 0.4" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.4; t = 1; D_H = 0.7143" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "simple-hyperbolic-weight-one-month-ahead-with-alpha-of-0-4" .

hemo:7003555 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "alpha in the test Simple hyperbolic weight one month ahead with alpha of 0.4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002677 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.4 .

hemo:7003556 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "t in the test Simple hyperbolic weight one month ahead with alpha of 0.4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002678 ;
    rheo:2000001 1.0 .

hemo:7003557 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "D_H in the test Simple hyperbolic weight one month ahead with alpha of 0.4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002676 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.7143 .

hemo:7003558 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Simple hyperbolic weight two months ahead with alpha of 0.4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003559,
        hemo:7003560 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003561 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.00005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Two months ahead the same smoker's weight is about 0.556, 1 divided by 1.8, as in the article's worked example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Simple hyperbolic weight two months ahead with alpha of 0.4" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.4; t = 2; D_H = 0.5556" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "simple-hyperbolic-weight-two-months-ahead-with-alpha-of-0-4" .

hemo:7003559 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "alpha in the test Simple hyperbolic weight two months ahead with alpha of 0.4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002677 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.4 .

hemo:7003560 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "t in the test Simple hyperbolic weight two months ahead with alpha of 0.4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002678 ;
    rheo:2000001 2.0 .

hemo:7003561 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "D_H in the test Simple hyperbolic weight two months ahead with alpha of 0.4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002676 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.5556 .

hemo:7003562 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Simple hyperbolic weight ten years ahead against the constant-rate factor"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003563,
        hemo:7003564 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003565 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.00005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha = 0.035 a year an outcome ten years ahead keeps a weight of about 0.741, against about 0.709 under constant discounting at 3.5% a year (computed here for illustration), although both forms give 0.966 one year ahead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Simple hyperbolic weight ten years ahead against the constant-rate factor" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.035; t = 10; D_H = 0.7407" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "simple-hyperbolic-weight-ten-years-ahead-against-the-constant-rate-factor" .

hemo:7003563 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "alpha in the test Simple hyperbolic weight ten years ahead against the constant-rate factor"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002677 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.035 .

hemo:7003564 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "t in the test Simple hyperbolic weight ten years ahead against the constant-rate factor"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002678 ;
    rheo:2000001 10.0 .

hemo:7003565 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "D_H in the test Simple hyperbolic weight ten years ahead against the constant-rate factor"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002676 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.7407 .

hemo:7003566 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Simple hyperbolic weight at zero delay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003567,
        hemo:7003568 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003569 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An outcome now keeps its full value whatever alpha is, a limiting case that checks an implementation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Simple hyperbolic weight at zero delay" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.4; t = 0; D_H = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "simple-hyperbolic-weight-at-zero-delay" .

hemo:7003567 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "alpha in the test Simple hyperbolic weight at zero delay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002677 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.4 .

hemo:7003568 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "t in the test Simple hyperbolic weight at zero delay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002678 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.0 .

hemo:7003569 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "D_H in the test Simple hyperbolic weight at zero delay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002676 ;
    rheo:2000001 1.0 .

hemo:7003570 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Per-period rate defined from adjacent hyperbolic weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The rate is the discrete per-period rate D(t)/D(t + 1) minus 1, the definition behind the per-period rates that Frederick and colleagues give for the quasi-hyperbolic form. For the simple hyperbola the instantaneous rate, the slope of minus log D at t, takes the same value alpha/(1 + alpha t), so the expression serves for both. That does not hold in general, since the constant-rate factor has a per-period rate of r but an instantaneous rate of log(1 + r)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Per-period rate defined from adjacent hyperbolic weights" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HYPD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "per-period-rate-defined-from-adjacent-hyperbolic-weights" .

hemo:7003571 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Rate re-measured from each new present"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The rate path is seen from the moment of choice. When the person reaches delay t, the next period again carries the first-period rate alpha, which is why a plan made in advance can be reversed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rate re-measured from each new present" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HYPD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rate-re-measured-from-each-new-present" .

hemo:7003572 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Implied per-period rate of the simple hyperbola from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000631 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The first formula gives the rate directly. The second builds it from the weights at Delay and Delay plus 1 and returns the same value, which checks a table of weights." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Implied per-period rate of the simple hyperbola from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HYPD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "implied-per-period-rate-of-the-simple-hyperbola-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=HypAlpha/(1+HypAlpha*Delay); =(1/(1+HypAlpha*Delay))/(1/(1+HypAlpha*(Delay+1)))-1" .

hemo:7003573 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Implied hyperbolic rate equals the ratio of adjacent weights minus one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The closed form and the ratio of the weights at Delay and Delay plus 1 agree for any delay. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the weights taken two periods apart or alpha entered differently in the two parts." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Implied hyperbolic rate equals the ratio of adjacent weights minus one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HYPD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "implied-hyperbolic-rate-equals-the-ratio-of-adjacent-weights-minus-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(HypAlpha/(1+HypAlpha*Delay)-((1+HypAlpha*(Delay+1))/(1+HypAlpha*Delay)-1))<1E-12" .

hemo:7003574 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Implied hyperbolic rate falls with delay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a positive alpha the rate one period later is lower than the rate at Delay. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows alpha entered as zero or below, where the rate does not decline." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Implied hyperbolic rate falls with delay" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HYPD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "implied-hyperbolic-rate-falls-with-delay" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(HypAlpha>0,HypAlpha/(1+HypAlpha*(Delay+1))<HypAlpha/(1+HypAlpha*Delay))" .

hemo:7003575 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "First-period hyperbolic rate with alpha of 0.4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Between now and one month ahead the article's smoker discounts at 0.4 a month, the value of alpha itself." ;
    hemo:9000009 "First-period hyperbolic rate with alpha of 0.4" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.4; t = 0; rho_t = 0.4" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "first-period-hyperbolic-rate-with-alpha-of-0-4" .

hemo:7003576 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Hyperbolic rate between months one and two with alpha of 0.4"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Between one and two months ahead the rate has fallen to about 0.286, 0.4 divided by 1.4, matching the ratio of the article's weights 0.714 and 0.556 minus 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hyperbolic rate between months one and two with alpha of 0.4" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.4; t = 1; rho_t = 0.2857" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hyperbolic-rate-between-months-one-and-two-with-alpha-of-0-4" .

hemo:7003577 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Hyperbolic rate a year ahead with alpha of 0.4 a month"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Between months 12 and 13 the rate is about 0.069 a month, 0.4 divided by 5.8, less than a fifth of the first-month rate (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Hyperbolic rate a year ahead with alpha of 0.4 a month" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.4; t = 12; rho_t = 0.069" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "hyperbolic-rate-a-year-ahead-with-alpha-of-0-4-a-month" .

hemo:7003578 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive parameters of the generalised hyperbola"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both alpha and beta are above zero, so the weight is 1 at t = 0 and falls with delay. The formula divides by alpha, so a constant-rate analysis is written with exp(minus beta t) directly, not with alpha set to zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive parameters of the generalised hyperbola" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HYPD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-parameters-of-the-generalised-hyperbola" .

hemo:7003579 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Generalised hyperbola parameters in the time unit of the delay"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Alpha and beta are per period in the unit of t. Restating a monthly delay in years multiplies both by 12, which leaves the ratio beta over alpha unchanged." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generalised hyperbola parameters in the time unit of the delay" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HYPD-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generalised-hyperbola-parameters-in-the-time-unit-of-the-delay" .

hemo:7003580 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Generalised hyperbolic discount factor from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000632 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the parameters in GenAlpha and GenBeta and the delay in Delay, the cell returns the weight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generalised hyperbolic discount factor from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HYPD-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generalised-hyperbolic-discount-factor-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(1+GenAlpha*Delay)^(-GenBeta/GenAlpha)" .

hemo:7003581 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Generalised hyperbola reduces to the simple hyperbola when beta equals alpha"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Entering beta equal to alpha gives the same weight as 1/(1 + alpha t). The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows an exponent typed as minus beta times alpha or minus beta alone." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generalised hyperbola reduces to the simple hyperbola when beta equals alpha" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HYPD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generalised-hyperbola-reduces-to-the-simple-hyperbola-when-beta-equals-alpha" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((1+GenAlpha*Delay)^(-GenAlpha/GenAlpha)-1/(1+GenAlpha*Delay))<1E-12" .

hemo:7003582 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Generalised hyperbola approaches the continuous constant-rate weight as alpha shrinks"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha = 0.000001, beta = 0.1 and ten periods the weight is within 0.00001 of EXP(minus 1). The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the exponent written without the division by alpha." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generalised hyperbola approaches the continuous constant-rate weight as alpha shrinks" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HYPD-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generalised-hyperbola-approaches-the-continuous-constant-rate-weight-as-alpha-shrinks" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((1+0.000001*10)^(-0.1/0.000001)-EXP(-0.1*10))<0.00001" .

hemo:7003583 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Generalised hyperbola with beta half of alpha at two periods"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha = 0.4 and beta = 0.2 the weight two periods ahead is 1.8 to the power minus 0.5, about 0.745 (illustrative parameters, computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generalised hyperbola with beta half of alpha at two periods" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.4; beta = 0.2; t = 2; D_G = 0.7454" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generalised-hyperbola-with-beta-half-of-alpha-at-two-periods" .

hemo:7003584 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Generalised hyperbola close to constant discounting with a very small alpha"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha = 0.0001 and beta = 0.1 the weight ten periods ahead is about 0.3681, close to exp(minus 1), about 0.3679, the constant-rate weight at a continuous rate of 0.1 (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Generalised hyperbola close to constant discounting with a very small alpha" ;
    hemo:9000014 "alpha = 0.0001; beta = 0.1; t = 10; D_G = 0.3681" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "generalised-hyperbola-close-to-constant-discounting-with-a-very-small-alpha" .

hemo:7003585 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Immediate outcome carries a quasi-hyperbolic weight of one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "D(0) = 1 for the present period and the formula applies to whole delays of 1 or more, so the weight falls by the factor beta delta over the first period and by delta over each later period." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Immediate outcome carries a quasi-hyperbolic weight of one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HYPD-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "immediate-outcome-carries-a-quasi-hyperbolic-weight-of-one" .

hemo:7003586 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Period length chosen with the one-period conflict in mind"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Gruber and Köszegi describe the quasi-hyperbolic model as a theoretical device that confines self-control conflict to exactly one period, so beta and delta are tied to the chosen period length and the period is set with that limit in view." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Period length chosen with the one-period conflict in mind" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HYPD-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "period-length-chosen-with-the-one-period-conflict-in-mind" .

hemo:7003587 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Quasi-hyperbolic weight and per-period rates from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000633 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The first formula returns the weight with the immediate period handled by IF. The second and third return the short-run and long-run per-period rates." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Quasi-hyperbolic weight and per-period rates from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HYPD-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "quasi-hyperbolic-weight-and-per-period-rates-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(Delay=0,1,QHBeta*QHDelta^Delay); =(1-QHBeta*QHDelta)/(QHBeta*QHDelta); =(1-QHDelta)/QHDelta" .

hemo:7003588 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Quasi-hyperbolic short-run rate above the long-run rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With beta below 1 the rate between now and the next period exceeds the rate between later periods, as Frederick and colleagues state. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows beta set to 1, where the rates are equal, or beta entered above 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Quasi-hyperbolic short-run rate above the long-run rate" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HYPD-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "quasi-hyperbolic-short-run-rate-above-the-long-run-rate" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(1-QHBeta*QHDelta)/(QHBeta*QHDelta)>(1-QHDelta)/QHDelta" .

hemo:7003589 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's quasi-hyperbolic weights reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With beta = 0.7 and delta = 0.99 the weights one and two periods ahead are 0.693 and 0.686 to three decimal places. The expected result is TRUE. Writing the second weight as (0.7*0.99)^2, the compounded-beta error, gives 0.480 and makes it FALSE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's quasi-hyperbolic weights reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HYPD-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-quasi-hyperbolic-weights-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS(0.7*0.99-0.693)<0.0005,ABS(0.7*0.99^2-0.686)<0.0005)" .

hemo:7003590 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's quasi-hyperbolic smoker one month ahead"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With beta = 0.7 and delta = 0.99 a month the weight one month ahead is 0.693. The rate is about 0.443 between now and next month and about 0.0101 between any two later months, as in the article's example (illustrative values)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's quasi-hyperbolic smoker one month ahead" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta = 0.7; delta = 0.99; t = 1; D_Q = 0.693; r_0 = 0.443; r_L = 0.0101" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-quasi-hyperbolic-smoker-one-month-ahead" .

hemo:7003591 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Quasi-hyperbolic weight at Wang and Sloan's estimates for adherence in diabetes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Wang and Sloan estimated beta = 0.38 and delta = 0.88 per period of their model for older people with diabetes. One period ahead the weight is about 0.334, so the short-run rate is about 1.99 against about 0.136 between later periods (computed here for illustration)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Quasi-hyperbolic weight at Wang and Sloan's estimates for adherence in diabetes" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta = 0.38; delta = 0.88; t = 1; D_Q = 0.3344; r_0 = 1.9904; r_L = 0.1364" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "quasi-hyperbolic-weight-at-wang-and-sloan-s-estimates-for-adherence-in-diabetes" .

hemo:7003592 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Quasi-hyperbolic weight without present bias"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With beta = 1 the two rates are equal, about 0.0101 a month for delta = 0.99, and the weight two months ahead is 0.9801, a limiting case that returns exponential discounting." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Quasi-hyperbolic weight without present bias" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta = 1; delta = 0.99; t = 2; D_Q = 0.9801; r_0 = 0.0101; r_L = 0.0101" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "quasi-hyperbolic-weight-without-present-bias" .

hemo:7003593 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "All reversal-check weights from one function seen from today"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The three weights come from the same discount function evaluated at the present, so M_1 is today's view of next period's choice. Next period the person re-evaluates with w_0 and w_1 again, which is where a naive plan unravels." ;
    hemo:9000009 "All reversal-check weights from one function seen from today" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HYPD-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "all-reversal-check-weights-from-one-function-seen-from-today" .

hemo:7003594 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Reversal-check amounts in common units and fixed over time"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The amounts a and b are in the same units and do not change between the two judgements, so any change in the ranking comes from the weights alone. Attema and colleagues give the example of preferring one programme now and the other a year later with nothing changed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Reversal-check amounts in common units and fixed over time" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-HYPD-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "reversal-check-amounts-in-common-units-and-fixed-over-time" .

hemo:7003595 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Preference reversal check from named weights and amounts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000634 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the amounts in SoonerAmount and LaterAmount and the weights in Weight0, Weight1 and Weight2, the first two formulas return M_0 and M_1 and the third returns TRUE when the plan reverses, with the two margins in cells named WaitNow and WaitNext." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Preference reversal check from named weights and amounts" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-HYPD-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "preference-reversal-check-from-named-weights-and-amounts" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LaterAmount*Weight1-SoonerAmount*Weight0; =LaterAmount*Weight2-SoonerAmount*Weight1; =AND(WaitNow<0,WaitNext>0)" .

hemo:7003596 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant-rate weights give proportional margins and no reversal"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With constant-rate weights 1, delta and delta squared in Weight0, Weight1 and Weight2, M_1 equals Weight1 times M_0 for any amounts, so the two margins share a sign. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows hyperbolic or quasi-hyperbolic weights, or weights that do not come from one constant rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant-rate weights give proportional margins and no reversal" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HYPD-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-rate-weights-give-proportional-margins-and-no-reversal" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((LaterAmount*Weight2-SoonerAmount*Weight1)-Weight1*(LaterAmount*Weight1-SoonerAmount*Weight0))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003597 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's quasi-hyperbolic reversal reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a = 10, b = 13, beta = 0.7 and delta = 0.99, M_0 is negative and M_1 positive. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows beta applied to the immediate outcome as well." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's quasi-hyperbolic reversal reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-HYPD-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-quasi-hyperbolic-reversal-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(13*0.7*0.99-10<0,13*0.7*0.99^2-10*0.7*0.99>0)" .

hemo:7003598 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's quasi-hyperbolic smoker plans to quit next month"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With weights 1, 0.693 and 0.68607 from beta = 0.7 and delta = 0.99, quitting loses by 0.991 today but wins by about 1.989 when judged for next month, the article's preference reversal (illustrative values)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's quasi-hyperbolic smoker plans to quit next month" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 10; b = 13; w_0 = 1; w_1 = 0.693; w_2 = 0.68607; M_0 = -0.991; M_1 = 1.9889" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-013" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-quasi-hyperbolic-smoker-plans-to-quit-next-month" .

hemo:7003599 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's simple hyperbolic smoker plans to quit next month"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With weights 1, 0.714286 and 0.555556 from alpha = 0.4, quitting loses by about 0.714 today and wins by about 0.079 for next month, as in the article's table (9.29 against 10, and 7.22 against 7.14)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's simple hyperbolic smoker plans to quit next month" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 10; b = 13; w_0 = 1; w_1 = 0.714286; w_2 = 0.555556; M_0 = -0.7143; M_1 = 0.0794" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-014" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-simple-hyperbolic-smoker-plans-to-quit-next-month" .

hemo:7003600 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's impatient exponential smoker never plans to quit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With weights 1, 0.75 and 0.5625 from delta = 0.75, waiting loses both today and for next month, so the steep constant discounter is impatient but consistent." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's impatient exponential smoker never plans to quit" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 10; b = 13; w_0 = 1; w_1 = 0.75; w_2 = 0.5625; M_0 = -0.25; M_1 = -0.1875" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-HYPD-015" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-impatient-exponential-smoker-never-plans-to-quit" .

hemo:7003601 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Decision maker free to act on or set aside a study result"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "After each result the option with the higher posterior expected net benefit is chosen, which may be the current choice. Because keeping the current choice is always open, V_S is at least V_0 and EVSI cannot be negative, although a particular result can still lead to a choice that later proves worse." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Decision maker free to act on or set aside a study result" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVSI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "decision-maker-free-to-act-on-or-set-aside-a-study-result" .

hemo:7003602 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Risk-neutral choice on expected net benefit for EVSI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Options are ranked by expected net benefit at a stated cost-effectiveness threshold, the risk-neutral rule that Kunst and colleagues state for EVSI. Net benefit can be net monetary or net health benefit, with the three net benefit inputs on the same basis." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Risk-neutral choice on expected net benefit for EVSI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVSI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "risk-neutral-choice-on-expected-net-benefit-for-evsi" .

hemo:7003603 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-result study with the same accuracy in both states"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The study is summarised by one positive or negative result whose chance of pointing the right way is q in either state, an illustrative simplification of a study that usually returns a continuous estimate. Different accuracies in the two states change P_pos and the posterior probabilities but not the structure of the calculation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-result study with the same accuracy in both states" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVSI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-result-study-with-the-same-accuracy-in-both-states" .

hemo:7003604 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Costless reversal, full implementation and no delay in per-patient EVSI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Per-patient EVSI here assumes that adoption can be reversed at no cost, that the chosen option is fully implemented and that neither the study nor adoption is delayed, the assumptions Strong and colleagues state for per-person EVSI within one jurisdiction. Departures from them need explicit treatment." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Costless reversal, full implementation and no delay in per-patient EVSI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVSI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "costless-reversal-full-implementation-and-no-delay-in-per-patient-evsi" .

hemo:7003605 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "EVSI of a two-result study from named cells with LET"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000635 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the prior probability of state F in a cell named PriorProb, the accuracy in Accuracy and the three net benefits in NBStandard, NBNewWorks and NBNewFails, the formula returns EVSI per patient in Excel 2021 or Microsoft 365. The helper names pp, fp, fn, bp and bn hold P_pos, pF_pos, pF_neg, B_pos and B_neg." ;
    hemo:9000009 "EVSI of a two-result study from named cells with LET" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVSI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "evsi-of-a-two-result-study-from-named-cells-with-let" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LET(pp,PriorProb*Accuracy+(1-PriorProb)*(1-Accuracy),fp,PriorProb*Accuracy/pp,fn,PriorProb*(1-Accuracy)/(1-pp),bp,fp*NBNewWorks+(1-fp)*NBNewFails,bn,fn*NBNewWorks+(1-fn)*NBNewFails,pp*MAX(NBStandard,bp)+(1-pp)*MAX(NBStandard,bn)-MAX(NBStandard,PriorProb*NBNewWorks+(1-PriorProb)*NBNewFails))" .

hemo:7003606 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-result study preserves the prior expected net benefit of the new option"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Averaging B_pos and B_neg, held in cells named BPos and BNeg, over the result probabilities, with P_pos in PPos, returns the prior expected net benefit of B, GBP 1,050 in the example. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows posterior probabilities computed without dividing by the probability of the result, or result probabilities that do not match the accuracy." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-result study preserves the prior expected net benefit of the new option" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVSI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-result-study-preserves-the-prior-expected-net-benefit-of-the-new-option" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PPos*BPos+(1-PPos)*BNeg-(PriorProb*NBNewWorks+(1-PriorProb)*NBNewFails))<1E-6" .

hemo:7003607 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's EVSI of GBP 73 and GBP 171 reproduced for studies S1 and S2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The joint probabilities of state F and a positive result, 0.315 for S1 and 0.405 for S2, and of state F and a negative result, 0.135 and 0.045, give EVSI of GBP 73 and GBP 171 per patient when rounded to the penny. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows that the decision was not allowed to switch to A after a negative result." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's EVSI of GBP 73 and GBP 171 reproduced for studies S1 and S2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVSI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-evsi-of-gbp-73-and-gbp-171-reproduced-for-studies-s1-and-s2" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(0.48*MAX(1000,(0.315/0.48)*1600+(1-0.315/0.48)*600)+0.52*MAX(1000,(0.135/0.52)*1600+(1-0.135/0.52)*600)-1050,2)=73,ROUND(0.46*MAX(1000,(0.405/0.46)*1600+(1-0.405/0.46)*600)+0.54*MAX(1000,(0.045/0.54)*1600+(1-0.045/0.54)*600)-1050,2)=171)" .

hemo:7003608 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Smaller study S1 whose result points the right way seven times in ten"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative example, A is worth GBP 1,000 per patient, B GBP 1,600 if it works and GBP 600 if not, and state F has a prior probability of 0.45, so B is chosen now at GBP 1,050. Study S1 gives a positive result with probability 0.48, after which B is kept at GBP 1,256.25, and a negative result with probability 0.52, after which B falls to about GBP 859.62 and A is chosen. EVSI is GBP 73 per patient, a third of the EVPI of GBP 220." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Smaller study S1 whose result points the right way seven times in ten" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p = 0.45; q = 0.7; NB_A = 1000; NB_BF = 1600; NB_BU = 600; P_pos = 0.48; pF_pos = 0.65625; pF_neg = 0.259615; B_pos = 1256.25; B_neg = 859.62; V_S = 1123; V_0 = 1050; EVSI = 73" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVSI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "smaller-study-s1-whose-result-points-the-right-way-seven-times-in-ten" .

hemo:7003609 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Larger study S2 whose result points the right way nine times in ten"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With q of 0.9 in the same illustrative example, a positive result (probability 0.46) raises the probability of state F to about 0.880 and a negative result (probability 0.54) lowers it to about 0.083, so the decision switches to A after a negative result. The expected net benefit with the study is GBP 1,221 and EVSI is GBP 171 per patient, about 78% of EVPI." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Larger study S2 whose result points the right way nine times in ten" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p = 0.45; q = 0.9; NB_A = 1000; NB_BF = 1600; NB_BU = 600; P_pos = 0.46; pF_pos = 0.880435; pF_neg = 0.083333; B_pos = 1480.43; B_neg = 683.33; V_S = 1221; V_0 = 1050; EVSI = 171" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVSI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "larger-study-s2-whose-result-points-the-right-way-nine-times-in-ten" .

hemo:7003610 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Perfectly accurate two-result study recovering EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With q of 1 the result reveals the state, so B is chosen in state F and A in state U, and EVSI equals the EVPI of GBP 220 per patient that HE-FM-VOI-001 gives for the same two states, an upper limiting case that checks the implementation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Perfectly accurate two-result study recovering EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p = 0.45; q = 1; NB_A = 1000; NB_BF = 1600; NB_BU = 600; P_pos = 0.45; pF_pos = 1; pF_neg = 0; B_pos = 1600; B_neg = 600; V_S = 1270; V_0 = 1050; EVSI = 220" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVSI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "perfectly-accurate-two-result-study-recovering-evpi" .

hemo:7003611 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Uninformative two-result study with a coin-toss result"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With q of 0.5 the result is unrelated to the state, both posterior probabilities equal the prior 0.45, B is chosen after either result and EVSI is zero, the lower limiting case." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Uninformative two-result study with a coin-toss result" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p = 0.45; q = 0.5; NB_A = 1000; NB_BF = 1600; NB_BU = 600; P_pos = 0.5; pF_pos = 0.45; pF_neg = 0.45; B_pos = 1050; B_neg = 1050; V_S = 1050; V_0 = 1050; EVSI = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVSI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uninformative-two-result-study-with-a-coin-toss-result" .

hemo:7003612 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal prior and normal study estimate of incremental net benefit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Incremental net benefit has a normal prior with variance v0, and the study estimate is normal around the true value with known variance sigma2 divided by n, the conjugate pair for which Jalal and Alarid-Escudero derive the variance fraction (equations 7 to 12). With skewed priors or study estimates the expression is an approximation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal prior and normal study estimate of incremental net benefit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVSI-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-prior-and-normal-study-estimate-of-incremental-net-benefit" .

hemo:7003613 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Study that informs incremental net benefit directly"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The study estimates incremental net benefit itself, so enough data would resolve all of its prior uncertainty. When a study informs only some parameters, the reducible variance is the part explained by those parameters, and EVSI is bounded by their EVPPI (HE-FM-VOI-003) rather than by EVPI." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Study that informs incremental net benefit directly" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVSI-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "study-that-informs-incremental-net-benefit-directly" .

hemo:7003614 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Sampling variance of a two-arm trial with equal arms"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a two-arm trial with n patients in each arm, the estimate of incremental net benefit is a difference of two independent means, so sigma2 is the sum of the per-patient variances of net benefit in the two arms and n is the number per arm." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Sampling variance of a two-arm trial with equal arms" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVSI-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "sampling-variance-of-a-two-arm-trial-with-equal-arms" .

hemo:7003615 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Preposterior variance of incremental net benefit from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000636 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the prior variance in a cell named PriorVarINB, the per-patient sampling variance in SamplingVar and the study size in StudySize, the formula returns s2. Its square root is the preposterior standard deviation used by HE-FM-EVSI-003." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Preposterior variance of incremental net benefit from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVSI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "preposterior-variance-of-incremental-net-benefit-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PriorVarINB*StudySize/(StudySize+SamplingVar/PriorVarINB)" .

hemo:7003616 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Preposterior variance equals prior variance less posterior variance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the result in a cell named PrepostVar, the posterior variance after n patients, one over the sum of the prior precision and n over sigma2, subtracted from the prior variance gives the same value. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the posterior variance entered in place of the preposterior variance, or n0 computed as v0 over sigma2." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Preposterior variance equals prior variance less posterior variance" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVSI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "preposterior-variance-equals-prior-variance-less-posterior-variance" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PrepostVar-(PriorVarINB-1/(1/PriorVarINB+StudySize/SamplingVar)))<1E-6" .

hemo:7003617 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Preposterior variance for 100 patients per arm against a prior effective size of 200"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Illustrative inputs with a prior standard deviation of incremental net benefit of GBP 1,000 per patient, a prior variance of 1,000,000, and per-patient standard deviations of net benefit of GBP 10,000 in each arm give a sampling variance of 200,000,000 and a prior effective sample size of 200 per arm. A trial of 100 per arm resolves a third of the prior variance, a preposterior variance of about 333,333." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Preposterior variance for 100 patients per arm against a prior effective size of 200" ;
    hemo:9000014 "v0 = 1000000; sigma2 = 200000000; n = 100; n0 = 200; nu = 0.333333; s2 = 333333.33" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVSI-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "preposterior-variance-for-100-patients-per-arm-against-a-prior-effective-size-of-200" .

hemo:7003618 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Preposterior variance with no new patients"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With n equal to zero the posterior mean equals the prior mean whatever happens, so the preposterior variance is zero and the study has no value, the lower limiting case." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Preposterior variance with no new patients" ;
    hemo:9000014 "v0 = 1000000; sigma2 = 200000000; n = 0; n0 = 200; nu = 0; s2 = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVSI-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "preposterior-variance-with-no-new-patients" .

hemo:7003619 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Two options compared on incremental net benefit in the closed form"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The closed form holds for a choice between two options, where the decision depends only on the sign of incremental net benefit. With three or more options the expected maximum has no one-dimensional closed form and simulation is needed, although Lee and colleagues derive a two-dimensional closed form for three options and note that the sample information algorithms can be adapted to it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two options compared on incremental net benefit in the closed form" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVSI-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-options-compared-on-incremental-net-benefit-in-the-closed-form" .

hemo:7003620 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal preposterior distribution of the posterior mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The posterior mean of incremental net benefit is normal across possible results, which is exact for a normal prior and a normal study estimate and approximate otherwise. The second ISPOR report states that EVSI can be computed analytically under normality with a known reduction in variance, and that sampling-based methods are needed otherwise." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal preposterior distribution of the posterior mean" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVSI-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-preposterior-distribution-of-the-posterior-mean" .

hemo:7003621 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Closed-form EVSI from the prior mean and preposterior variance in Excel"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000637 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the prior mean of incremental net benefit in a cell named PriorMeanINB and the preposterior variance in PrepostVar, the formula returns EVSI per patient. NORM.S.DIST with FALSE gives the density and with TRUE the cumulative probability." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Closed-form EVSI from the prior mean and preposterior variance in Excel" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVSI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "closed-form-evsi-from-the-prior-mean-and-preposterior-variance-in-excel" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SQRT(PrepostVar)*NORM.S.DIST(ABS(PriorMeanINB)/SQRT(PrepostVar),FALSE)-ABS(PriorMeanINB)*(1-NORM.S.DIST(ABS(PriorMeanINB)/SQRT(PrepostVar),TRUE))" .

hemo:7003622 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Closed-form EVSI plus the current value equals the unit normal loss integral"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "EVSI in a cell named EVSIPerPerson plus the larger of m0 and zero equals the expected maximum of the posterior mean and zero, m0 times 1 minus Phi(minus m0 over s) plus s times phi(minus m0 over s), the unit normal loss integral in the form given by Lee and colleagues. Expected result TRUE for either sign of m0. FALSE shows the absolute value omitted when m0 is negative or Phi(z) used where 1 minus Phi(z) belongs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Closed-form EVSI plus the current value equals the unit normal loss integral" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVSI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "closed-form-evsi-plus-the-current-value-equals-the-unit-normal-loss-integral" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(EVSIPerPerson+MAX(PriorMeanINB,0)-(PriorMeanINB*(1-NORM.S.DIST(-PriorMeanINB/SQRT(PrepostVar),TRUE))+SQRT(PrepostVar)*NORM.S.DIST(-PriorMeanINB/SQRT(PrepostVar),FALSE)))<1E-6" .

hemo:7003623 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Closed-form EVSI rises with trial size toward EVPI for the illustrative prior"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For the prior with mean GBP 500 and variance 1,000,000 and n0 of 200, the preposterior variances for 100 and 400 per arm and the prior variance give EVSI of GBP 61.68, GBP 134.97 and GBP 197.80 per patient when rounded to the penny, rising with n toward EVPI. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the posterior variance entered in place of the preposterior variance, which swaps the values for 100 and 400 per arm." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Closed-form EVSI rises with trial size toward EVPI for the illustrative prior" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVSI-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "closed-form-evsi-rises-with-trial-size-toward-evpi-for-the-illustrative-prior" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(SQRT(1E6/3)*(NORM.S.DIST(500/SQRT(1E6/3),FALSE)-500/SQRT(1E6/3)*(1-NORM.S.DIST(500/SQRT(1E6/3),TRUE))),2)=61.68,ROUND(SQRT(2E6/3)*(NORM.S.DIST(500/SQRT(2E6/3),FALSE)-500/SQRT(2E6/3)*(1-NORM.S.DIST(500/SQRT(2E6/3),TRUE))),2)=134.97,ROUND(SQRT(1E6)*(NORM.S.DIST(500/SQRT(1E6),FALSE)-500/SQRT(1E6)*(1-NORM.S.DIST(500/SQRT(1E6),TRUE))),2)=197.8)" .

hemo:7003624 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Closed-form EVSI for 100 patients per arm with a prior mean of GBP 500"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003625,
        hemo:7003626 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003627,
        hemo:7003628,
        hemo:7003629,
        hemo:7003630,
        hemo:7003631 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.005 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For the illustrative prior with mean GBP 500 and standard deviation GBP 1,000 per patient, the preposterior variance of about 333,333 for 100 per arm gives a preposterior standard deviation of about GBP 577 and z of about 0.866. EVSI is about GBP 61.68 per patient, about 31% of the per-person EVPI of about GBP 197.80." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Closed-form EVSI for 100 patients per arm with a prior mean of GBP 500" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m0 = 500; s2 = 333333.33; Q_z = 0.19323812; s = 577.350266; z = 0.866025; phi_z = 0.274189; EVSI = 61.68" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVSI-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "closed-form-evsi-for-100-patients-per-arm-with-a-prior-mean-of-gbp-500" .

