hemo:7003648 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant beneficiary population able to act on the result from year 0"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "N patients a year face the decision and every cohort from year 0 benefits from the result. Because benefits arrive only when the study reports, the first ISPOR report notes that the beneficiary population is usually adjusted for the time a study takes, which here means starting the sum at the year the result is available." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Constant beneficiary population able to act on the result from year 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVSI-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "constant-beneficiary-population-able-to-act-on-the-result-from-year-0" .

hemo:7003649 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Justified decision lifetime explored in scenarios"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Y stands in for future changes such as patent expiry, new comparators and other research. The first ISPOR report recommends justifying the effective time horizon and exploring alternatives in scenario analyses, because value of information results can be highly sensitive to it." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Justified decision lifetime explored in scenarios" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVSI-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "justified-decision-lifetime-explored-in-scenarios" .

hemo:7003650 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Population EVSI with the beneficiary factor from Excel PV"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000638 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With per-person EVSI in a cell named EVSIPerPerson, the annual population in AnnualPop, the rate in DiscountRate and the lifetime in DecisionYears, PV with type 1 returns D, the present value of one patient a year with the first in year 0." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Population EVSI with the beneficiary factor from Excel PV" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVSI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "population-evsi-with-the-beneficiary-factor-from-excel-pv" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=EVSIPerPerson*AnnualPop*PV(DiscountRate,DecisionYears,-1,0,1)" .

hemo:7003651 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted population EVSI no larger than the undiscounted total"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Population EVSI in a cell named PopEVSI does not exceed per-person EVSI times the annual population times the number of years. Expected result TRUE for a rate of zero or above. FALSE shows a negative rate or a factor that counts more than Y cohorts." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted population EVSI no larger than the undiscounted total" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVSI-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-population-evsi-no-larger-than-the-undiscounted-total" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PopEVSI<=EVSIPerPerson*AnnualPop*DecisionYears" .

hemo:7003652 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Population EVSI of study S1 reproduced at 3.5% over five years"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Per-person EVSI of GBP 73 for 2,000 patients a year over five years at 3.5% rounds to GBP 682,270. Expected result TRUE. A result of about GBP 659,197 shows the first cohort discounted as well." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Population EVSI of study S1 reproduced at 3.5% over five years" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVSI-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "population-evsi-of-study-s1-reproduced-at-3-5-over-five-years" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(73*2000*(1+0.035)*(1-(1+0.035)^-5)/0.035,0)=682270" .

