hemo:7003674 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Equity weights act on incremental QALYs only"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weight multiplies the QALYs gained over the comparator, not total QALYs and not costs. PMG36 applies the severity weights to QALYs (section 6.2.16 and table 6.1), and Wailoo and colleagues describe them as applied to the incremental QALYs estimated in the cost-effectiveness assessment. Total QALYs that patients would have under current care attract no weight (HE-ER-ASF-005)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equity weights act on incremental QALYs only" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equity-weights-act-on-incremental-qalys-only" .

hemo:7003675 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Equity weight reflects value outside the QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A decision-making modifier in PMG36 (section 6.2.11) is a factor that the estimated QALY cannot include. A weight is therefore set only for value that the QALY measure leaves out, and the same concern is not weighted twice under two names." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equity weight reflects value outside the QALY" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equity-weight-reflects-value-outside-the-qaly" .

hemo:7003676 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weights multiplied in after the unweighted analysis"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The formula applies fixed weights to QALY gains already estimated without weights, the approach of the NICE modifier. Wailoo, Tsuchiya and McCabe warn that such a simple calculation after estimating cost per unweighted QALY will in many situations not reflect the preferences on which the weights are based." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weights multiplied in after the unweighted analysis" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weights-multiplied-in-after-the-unweighted-analysis" .

hemo:7003677 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Source of the group weights"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each w_g is set before the calculation, for example from absolute and proportional shortfall through the band rule of HE-FM-ASF-003, or as the relative weight implied by an inequality aversion parameter (HE-FM-ATK-004). In NICE technology appraisal, social characteristics such as income do not earn a QALY weight (PMG36, section 4.12.7)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Source of the group weights" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "source-of-the-group-weights" .

hemo:7003678 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Equity-weighted QALY total with SUMPRODUCT over group rows"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000639 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With one row per group, the weights in a range named EquityWeight and the group QALY gains in GroupQALYGain, the formula returns the equity-weighted QALY gain for any number of groups, of which the two-group calculator form is the special case. The two ranges have the same length and order." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equity-weighted QALY total with SUMPRODUCT over group rows" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EQWA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equity-weighted-qaly-total-with-sumproduct-over-group-rows" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(EquityWeight,GroupQALYGain)" .

hemo:7003679 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equity-weighted QALY total reproduces the article's two subgroups"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Weights of 1.7 and 1 on group gains of 180 and 560 QALYs give 866 weighted QALYs. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows weights applied to per-patient gains without the group sizes, or to the wrong rows." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equity-weighted QALY total reproduces the article's two subgroups" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQWA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equity-weighted-qaly-total-reproduces-the-article-s-two-subgroups" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT({1.7;1},{180;560})=866" .

hemo:7003680 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equity-weighted QALY total lies within the smallest and largest weight times the gain"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the result of HE-IM-EQWA-001 in a cell named WeightedQALYGain and every group gaining QALYs, the weighted total is at least the smallest weight times the unweighted total and at most the largest weight times it. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a weight applied to total QALYs or a gain entered with the wrong sign." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equity-weighted QALY total lies within the smallest and largest weight times the gain" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQWA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equity-weighted-qaly-total-lies-within-the-smallest-and-largest-weight-times-the-gain" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(WeightedQALYGain>=MIN(EquityWeight)*SUM(GroupQALYGain),WeightedQALYGain<=MAX(EquityWeight)*SUM(GroupQALYGain))" .

hemo:7003681 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two subgroups of one medicine weighted at 1.7 and 1"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003682,
        hemo:7003683,
        hemo:7003684,
        hemo:7003685 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003686,
        hemo:7003687,
        hemo:7003688 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative example, 300 patients in subgroup A each gain 0.6 QALYs and attract the weight of 1.7, and 700 patients in subgroup B each gain 0.8 QALYs at a weight of 1. The group gains are 300 × 0.6 = 180 and 700 × 0.8 = 560 QALYs, the weighted values 306 and 560, and the equity-weighted gain 866 QALYs against 740 unweighted." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two subgroups of one medicine weighted at 1.7 and 1" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_1 = 1.7; Delta_E_1 = 180; w_2 = 1; Delta_E_2 = 560; V_1 = 306; V_2 = 560; Delta_E_w = 866" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQWA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-subgroups-of-one-medicine-weighted-at-1-7-and-1" .

hemo:7003682 a owl:NamedIndividual,
