hemo:7003697 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive QALY gain and cost for the equity-weighted ICER"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The formula applies when the programme gains QALYs at extra cost. With a QALY loss or a saving, the ratio changes meaning, and net health benefit (HE-FM-EQWA-003) is the safer comparison." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive QALY gain and cost for the equity-weighted ICER" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-qaly-gain-and-cost-for-the-equity-weighted-icer" .

hemo:7003698 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One weight for the whole group in the equity-weighted ICER"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Everyone in the group carries the same weight, so dividing the ICER by w and multiplying the threshold by w give the same decision. With several weights in one population the weighted gain comes from HE-FM-EQWA-001 and the equivalence holds only for each group taken alone." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One weight for the whole group in the equity-weighted ICER" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-weight-for-the-whole-group-in-the-equity-weighted-icer" .

hemo:7003699 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Equity weighting leaves cost and displaced care unchanged"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weighted ICER is used for the decision only and does not change the cost of a QALY. The real cost of the programme and the care displaced to pay for it are the same as in the unweighted analysis, and PMG36 asks for net health benefit with and without the weighting to show the effect on opportunity costs (section 6.3.2)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equity weighting leaves cost and displaced care unchanged" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equity-weighting-leaves-cost-and-displaced-care-unchanged" .

hemo:7003700 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Equity-weighted ICER and equivalent threshold from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000640 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the incremental cost in IncrementalCost, the incremental QALYs in IncrementalQALYs, the weight in QALYWeight and the value of a QALY in QALYValue, the first formula returns the weighted ICER and the second the equivalent threshold for the unweighted ICER." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Equity-weighted ICER and equivalent threshold from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EQWA-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "equity-weighted-icer-and-equivalent-threshold-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IncrementalCost/(QALYWeight*IncrementalQALYs); =QALYWeight*QALYValue" .

hemo:7003701 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted ICER and equivalent threshold give the same decision"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a positive QALY gain and weight, the weighted ICER lies at or below lambda exactly when the unweighted ICER lies at or below w times lambda. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a weight entered below zero, which reverses the inequality." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted ICER and equivalent threshold give the same decision" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQWA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-icer-and-equivalent-threshold-give-the-same-decision" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(IncrementalCost/(QALYWeight*IncrementalQALYs)<=QALYValue)=(IncrementalCost/IncrementalQALYs<=QALYWeight*QALYValue)" .

hemo:7003702 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's weighted ICER and threshold range for a 1.7 weight"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A weight of 1.7 on 0.6 QALYs at GBP 30,000 gives about GBP 29,412 per QALY, and the GBP 25,000 to GBP 35,000 range becomes GBP 42,500 to GBP 59,500. Expected result TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's weighted ICER and threshold range for a 1.7 weight" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQWA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-weighted-icer-and-threshold-range-for-a-1-7-weight" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(30000/(1.7*0.6),0)=29412,ABS(1.7*25000-42500)<0.01,ABS(1.7*35000-59500)<0.01)" .

hemo:7003703 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Severe subgroup with a 1.7 weight judged at GBP 35,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative subgroup A the medicine costs GBP 30,000 more per patient and gains 0.6 QALYs, an unweighted ICER of GBP 50,000 per QALY. With the weight of 1.7 the weighted gain is 1.7 × 0.6 = 1.02 QALYs and the weighted ICER is about GBP 29,412 per QALY, below GBP 35,000. The same decision follows from comparing GBP 50,000 with the equivalent threshold of GBP 59,500." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Severe subgroup with a 1.7 weight judged at GBP 35,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = 30000; w = 1.7; Delta_E = 0.6; lambda = 35000; ICER_w = 29411.76; lambda_w = 59500" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQWA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "severe-subgroup-with-a-1-7-weight-judged-at-gbp-35-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7003704 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Severe subgroup with a 1.7 weight judged at GBP 25,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At the lower end of the NICE range the weighted ICER of about GBP 29,412 is above GBP 25,000, and the equivalent threshold for the unweighted ICER is GBP 42,500 per QALY (1.7 × 25,000), still below GBP 50,000." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Severe subgroup with a 1.7 weight judged at GBP 25,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = 30000; w = 1.7; Delta_E = 0.6; lambda = 25000; ICER_w = 29411.76; lambda_w = 42500" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQWA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "severe-subgroup-with-a-1-7-weight-judged-at-gbp-25-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7003705 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Subgroup with a weight of 1 where the weighted ICER is unchanged"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Subgroup B gains 0.8 QALYs per patient at an extra GBP 24,000 and carries a weight of 1, so the weighted and unweighted ICERs are both GBP 30,000 per QALY and the equivalent threshold is lambda itself." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Subgroup with a weight of 1 where the weighted ICER is unchanged" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = 24000; w = 1; Delta_E = 0.8; lambda = 35000; ICER_w = 30000; lambda_w = 35000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQWA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "subgroup-with-a-weight-of-1-where-the-weighted-icer-is-unchanged" .

hemo:7003706 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Displaced health is not equity weighted"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The health lost elsewhere is counted in unweighted QALYs, as in the NICE presentation of net health benefit with and without the weighting (PMG36, section 6.3.2), which is why the weighted value can be positive while total population health falls. Cookson and colleagues note that the distribution of the opportunity cost also matters, which this formula does not capture." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Displaced health is not equity weighted" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "displaced-health-is-not-equity-weighted" .

hemo:7003707 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Net health benefit reported at two values of a QALY, weighted and unweighted"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "PMG36 section 6.3.2 asks for net health benefit at GBP 25,000 and GBP 35,000 per QALY, both with and without the QALY weighting, so four values are normally reported for each weighted programme or subgroup." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net health benefit reported at two values of a QALY, weighted and unweighted" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-health-benefit-reported-at-two-values-of-a-qaly-weighted-and-unweighted" .

hemo:7003708 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Per-patient net health benefit scaled by group size"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Delta_E and Delta_C are per patient, so NHB_w and NHB_u are per patient. Population values multiply each by the number of patients in the group, and several groups are added in HE-CF-EQWA-001." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Per-patient net health benefit scaled by group size" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "per-patient-net-health-benefit-scaled-by-group-size" .

hemo:7003709 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted and unweighted net health benefit from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000641 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the cells named as for the weighted ICER, the first formula returns the weighted and the second the unweighted net health benefit per patient. Both are run with QALYValue set to 25000 and to 35000." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted and unweighted net health benefit from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EQWA-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-and-unweighted-net-health-benefit-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=QALYWeight*IncrementalQALYs-IncrementalCost/QALYValue; =IncrementalQALYs-IncrementalCost/QALYValue" .

hemo:7003710 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted and unweighted net health benefit differ by the weighted extra gain"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the two results of HE-IM-EQWA-003 in cells named WeightedNHB and UnweightedNHB, the weighted value minus the unweighted value equals w minus 1, times the QALY gain, whatever lambda is. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the displaced health divided by the weight as well." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted and unweighted net health benefit differ by the weighted extra gain" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQWA-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-and-unweighted-net-health-benefit-differ-by-the-weighted-extra-gain" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((WeightedNHB-UnweightedNHB)-(QALYWeight-1)*IncrementalQALYs)<0.000001" .

hemo:7003711 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's per-patient net health benefits for the severe subgroup"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Subgroup A gives about 0.163 weighted and minus 0.257 unweighted at GBP 35,000, and minus 0.18 weighted at GBP 25,000. Expected result TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's per-patient net health benefits for the severe subgroup" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQWA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-per-patient-net-health-benefits-for-the-severe-subgroup" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(1.7*0.6-30000/35000,3)=0.163,ROUND(0.6-30000/35000,3)=-0.257,ROUND(1.7*0.6-30000/25000,2)=-0.18)" .

hemo:7003712 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Severe subgroup net health benefit at GBP 35,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative subgroup A, GBP 30,000 displaces about 0.8571 QALYs at GBP 35,000 per QALY. The weighted net health benefit is about 0.1629 QALYs per patient and the unweighted value about minus 0.2571, so the weight turns a health loss into a weighted gain." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Severe subgroup net health benefit at GBP 35,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = 30000; lambda = 35000; w = 1.7; Delta_E = 0.6; H_d = 0.8571; NHB_w = 0.1629; NHB_u = -0.2571" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQWA-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "severe-subgroup-net-health-benefit-at-gbp-35-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7003713 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Severe subgroup net health benefit at GBP 25,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At GBP 25,000 per QALY the same GBP 30,000 displaces 1.2 QALYs, and net health benefit is minus 0.18 QALYs per patient weighted and minus 0.6 unweighted, both negative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Severe subgroup net health benefit at GBP 25,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = 30000; lambda = 25000; w = 1.7; Delta_E = 0.6; H_d = 1.2; NHB_w = -0.18; NHB_u = -0.6" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQWA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "severe-subgroup-net-health-benefit-at-gbp-25-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7003714 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Subgroup with a weight of 1 where both net health benefits agree"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Subgroup B gains 0.8 QALYs per patient at an extra GBP 24,000 and carries a weight of 1. At GBP 35,000 per QALY about 0.6857 QALYs are displaced and both net health benefits are about 0.1143 QALYs per patient." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Subgroup with a weight of 1 where both net health benefits agree" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = 24000; lambda = 35000; w = 1; Delta_E = 0.8; H_d = 0.6857; NHB_w = 0.1143; NHB_u = 0.1143" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQWA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "subgroup-with-a-weight-of-1-where-both-net-health-benefits-agree" .

hemo:7003715 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Positive cost and QALY gain for a break-even weight"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Delta_C and Delta_E are both above zero. A programme that saves money and gains health needs no weight, and one that loses health cannot be rescued by a weight above 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Positive cost and QALY gain for a break-even weight" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "positive-cost-and-qaly-gain-for-a-break-even-weight" .

hemo:7003716 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Break-even weight depends on the value of a QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Because lambda sits in the denominator, the break-even weight is higher at GBP 25,000 than at GBP 35,000 per QALY, so it is reported at each value used in the decision." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Break-even weight depends on the value of a QALY" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "break-even-weight-depends-on-the-value-of-a-qaly" .

hemo:7003717 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Break-even weight read against the weights available"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The value is compared with the weights the decision rule allows, for example the NICE severity weights of 1.2 and 1.7 (PMG36, table 6.1), or with the range of weights explored in a sensitivity analysis, as Cookson and colleagues recommend." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Break-even weight read against the weights available" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQWA-013" ;
    hemo:9000023 "break-even-weight-read-against-the-weights-available" .

hemo:7003718 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Break-even equity weight from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000642 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the cells named as for the weighted ICER, the formula returns the weight at which the weighted net health benefit is zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Break-even equity weight from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EQWA-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "break-even-equity-weight-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IncrementalCost/(QALYValue*IncrementalQALYs)" .

hemo:7003719 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted net health benefit is zero at the break-even weight"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Entering the break-even weight from a cell named SwitchWeight as the QALY weight gives a weighted net health benefit of zero. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows lambda and the QALY gain swapped or the ICER used in place of the incremental cost." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Weighted net health benefit is zero at the break-even weight" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQWA-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "weighted-net-health-benefit-is-zero-at-the-break-even-weight" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SwitchWeight*IncrementalQALYs-IncrementalCost/QALYValue)<0.000001" .

hemo:7003720 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's break-even weights at the two NICE values of a QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Subgroup A breaks even at about 1.43 at GBP 35,000 and at 2 at GBP 25,000. Expected result TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's break-even weights at the two NICE values of a QALY" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQWA-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-break-even-weights-at-the-two-nice-values-of-a-qaly" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(30000/(0.6*35000),2)=1.43,30000/(0.6*25000)=2)" .

hemo:7003721 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Severe subgroup break-even weight at GBP 35,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For the article's illustrative subgroup A, GBP 30,000 for 0.6 QALYs breaks even at a weight of about 1.43 at GBP 35,000 per QALY, below the 1.7 that the subgroup's severity earns." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Severe subgroup break-even weight at GBP 35,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = 30000; lambda = 35000; Delta_E = 0.6; w_star = 1.4286" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQWA-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "severe-subgroup-break-even-weight-at-gbp-35-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7003722 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Severe subgroup break-even weight at GBP 25,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At GBP 25,000 per QALY the same subgroup needs a weight of 2.0, above every NICE severity weight." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Severe subgroup break-even weight at GBP 25,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = 30000; lambda = 25000; Delta_E = 0.6; w_star = 2.0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQWA-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "severe-subgroup-break-even-weight-at-gbp-25-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7003723 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Break-even weight below one for a subgroup already cost-effective"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Subgroup B, at GBP 24,000 for 0.8 QALYs, has a break-even weight of about 0.857 at GBP 35,000 per QALY. A value below 1 shows that no priority weight is needed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Break-even weight below one for a subgroup already cost-effective" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_C = 24000; lambda = 35000; Delta_E = 0.8; w_star = 0.857" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQWA-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "break-even-weight-below-one-for-a-subgroup-already-cost-effective" .

hemo:7003724 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "YLL and YLD for one cause counted for the same population and year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both parts refer to the same cause, sex, age group, location and year, as in WHO's formula DALY(c,s,a,t) = YLL(c,s,a,t) + YLD(c,s,a,t). Adding YLLs for one year to YLDs for another, or for a different age group, gives a figure that belongs to no population." ;
    hemo:9000009 "YLL and YLD for one cause counted for the same population and year" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DALY-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "yll-and-yld-for-one-cause-counted-for-the-same-population-and-year" .

hemo:7003725 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One set of value choices for both parts of a DALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The two parts use the same conventions. From GBD 2010 onwards, and in WHO estimates after its decision in late 2012, both are undiscounted and not age-weighted, YLDs are counted by prevalence with an adjustment for comorbidity, and YLLs use a normative standard life table. The original GBD 1990 DALY counted YLDs by incidence and applied a 3% discount rate and age weights to both parts." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One set of value choices for both parts of a DALY" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DALY-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-set-of-value-choices-for-both-parts-of-a-daly" .

hemo:7003726 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "DALYs for a cause from named YLL and YLD cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000643 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the cause's years of life lost in YLLCause and its years lived with disability in YLDCause, the first formula returns the DALYs, held in DALYCause, and the second the share of the total that comes from deaths, held in ShareYLL." ;
    hemo:9000009 "DALYs for a cause from named YLL and YLD cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DALY-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "dalys-for-a-cause-from-named-yll-and-yld-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=YLLCause+YLDCause; =YLLCause/DALYCause" .

hemo:7003727 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "DALY total equals its parts and is not below either part"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With DALYCause, YLLCause and YLDCause filled, the total equals the sum and is at least as large as each part. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows a part entered with the wrong sign or a total typed in by hand that no longer matches its parts." ;
    hemo:9000009 "DALY total equals its parts and is not below either part" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DALY-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "daly-total-equals-its-parts-and-is-not-below-either-part" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS(DALYCause-(YLLCause+YLDCause))<1E-9,DALYCause>=YLLCause,DALYCause>=YLDCause)" .

hemo:7003728 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fatal and non-fatal shares of a DALY total add to one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The share of the total from YLLs, held in ShareYLL, and the share from YLDs add to 1, as 68.7% and 31.3% do for GBD 2021. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows ShareYLL divided by the wrong total, such as YLLs divided by YLDs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fatal and non-fatal shares of a DALY total add to one" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DALY-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fatal-and-non-fatal-shares-of-a-daly-total-add-to-one" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ShareYLL+YLDCause/DALYCause-1)<1E-9" .

hemo:7003729 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Global DALYs in 2021 summed from GBD 2021 years of life lost and years lived with disability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003730,
        hemo:7003731 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003732 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "GBD 2021 reported 1.98 billion YLLs and 907 million YLDs worldwide in 2021, entered here in millions. Their sum is 2,887 million against the reported total of 2.88 billion, a gap that comes from rounding in the published figures, and YLLs supply about 69% of the total (68.7% as reported)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Global DALYs in 2021 summed from GBD 2021 years of life lost and years lived with disability" ;
    hemo:9000014 "YLL = 1980; YLD = 907; DALY = 2887" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DALY-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "global-dalys-in-2021-summed-from-gbd-2021-years-of-life-lost-and-years-lived-with-disability" .

hemo:7003730 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "YLL in the test Global DALYs in 2021 summed from GBD 2021 years of life lost and years lived with disability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002756 ;
    rheo:2000001 1980.0 .

hemo:7003731 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "YLD in the test Global DALYs in 2021 summed from GBD 2021 years of life lost and years lived with disability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002757 ;
    rheo:2000001 907.0 .

hemo:7003732 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "DALY in the test Global DALYs in 2021 summed from GBD 2021 years of life lost and years lived with disability"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002755 ;
    rheo:2000001 2887.0 .

hemo:7003733 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Untreated cohort in the article's DALY example summed from its two parts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003734,
        hemo:7003735 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003736 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative cohort without treatment, 20 deaths at age 40 give 900 YLLs and 180 survivors living 10 years at a weight of 0.3 give 540 YLDs, a total of 1,440 DALYs, of which deaths supply 62.5%." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Untreated cohort in the article's DALY example summed from its two parts" ;
    hemo:9000014 "YLL = 900; YLD = 540; DALY = 1440" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DALY-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "untreated-cohort-in-the-article-s-daly-example-summed-from-its-two-parts" .

hemo:7003734 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "YLL in the test Untreated cohort in the article's DALY example summed from its two parts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002756 ;
    rheo:2000001 900.0 .

hemo:7003735 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "YLD in the test Untreated cohort in the article's DALY example summed from its two parts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002757 ;
    rheo:2000001 540.0 .

hemo:7003736 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "DALY in the test Untreated cohort in the article's DALY example summed from its two parts"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002755 ;
    rheo:2000001 1440.0 .

hemo:7003737 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Purely fatal cause in a DALY sum as a limiting case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003738,
        hemo:7003739 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003740 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a cause with no period of illness counted, YLD is zero and the DALY equals the YLL, here the 900 years from the 20 deaths in the article's example. This limiting case checks that a blank YLD cell is read as zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Purely fatal cause in a DALY sum as a limiting case" ;
    hemo:9000014 "YLL = 900; YLD = 0; DALY = 900" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DALY-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "purely-fatal-cause-in-a-daly-sum-as-a-limiting-case" .

hemo:7003738 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "YLL in the test Purely fatal cause in a DALY sum as a limiting case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002756 ;
    rheo:2000001 900.0 .

hemo:7003739 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "YLD in the test Purely fatal cause in a DALY sum as a limiting case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002757 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.0 .

hemo:7003740 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "DALY in the test Purely fatal cause in a DALY sum as a limiting case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002755 ;
    rheo:2000001 900.0 .

hemo:7003741 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Deaths at one age and illness of one length and weight in a cohort DALY scenario"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "All deaths occur at the start and at one age, and every survivor lives exactly T years with the condition at one weight, as in the article's illustrative cohort. No discounting or age weighting is applied, as in burden estimates from GBD 2010 onwards, and HE-FM-DALY-004 gives the discounted form. Deaths at several ages need one YLL term for each age (HE-CF-YLL-001), and cases of different lengths one YLD term for each." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Deaths at one age and illness of one length and weight in a cohort DALY scenario" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DALY-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "deaths-at-one-age-and-illness-of-one-length-and-weight-in-a-cohort-daly-scenario" .

hemo:7003742 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Survivors outlive the period of illness in a cohort DALY scenario"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "No survivor dies during the T years with the condition, and T is no longer than L. If death follows a period of illness, the years of life lost begin at the death, as in the Fox-Rushby and Hanson case that Larson recalculates." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Survivors outlive the period of illness in a cohort DALY scenario" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DALY-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "survivors-outlive-the-period-of-illness-in-a-cohort-daly-scenario" .

hemo:7003743 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Undiscounted cohort DALYs from named scenario cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000644 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Deaths, StdLE, Survivors, DisWeight and DurationYrs named for one scenario, the first formula returns the scenario's DALYs, held in CohortDALY. The second sets Survivors from the cohort size in CohortSize, so that deaths prevented move into the survivors automatically." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Undiscounted cohort DALYs from named scenario cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DALY-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "undiscounted-cohort-dalys-from-named-scenario-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Deaths*StdLE+Survivors*DisWeight*DurationYrs; =CohortSize-Deaths" .

hemo:7003744 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cohort DALYs within the cohort's standard years of life"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Deaths and survivors make up the cohort, and with a weight no higher than 1 and a duration no longer than L the DALYs cannot exceed the cohort size times L, 9,000 in the article's example. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows deaths and survivors that do not add up to the cohort, as when the survivors are left at the untreated number." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cohort DALYs within the cohort's standard years of life" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DALY-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cohort-dalys-within-the-cohort-s-standard-years-of-life" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(Deaths+Survivors=CohortSize,CohortDALY<=CohortSize*StdLE)" .

hemo:7003745 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's cohort of 200 adults without the treatment programme"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Without treatment 20 of 200 adults aged 40 die, each losing 45 standard years, and the 180 survivors live 10 years at a weight of 0.3, giving 900 YLLs and 540 YLDs, or 1,440 DALYs. All inputs are illustrative, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's cohort of 200 adults without the treatment programme" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 20; L = 45; S = 180; DW = 0.3; T = 10; DALY = 1440" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DALY-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-cohort-of-200-adults-without-the-treatment-programme" .

hemo:7003746 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's cohort of 200 adults with the treatment programme"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With treatment 8 die and the 192 survivors live the same 10 years at a weight of 0.1, giving 360 YLLs and 192 YLDs, or 552 DALYs. The 12 people whose deaths are prevented add 12 YLDs, since they live with the condition too." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's cohort of 200 adults with the treatment programme" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 8; L = 45; S = 192; DW = 0.1; T = 10; DALY = 552" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DALY-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-cohort-of-200-adults-with-the-treatment-programme" .

hemo:7003747 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same cohort, horizon and conventions in both DALY scenarios"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both scenarios follow the same people over the same time horizon with the same life table, disability weights and discount rate, and costs are counted on a stated convention. Fox-Rushby and Hanson found many published analyses could not be compared or transferred because these assumptions differed or were unclear." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same cohort, horizon and conventions in both DALY scenarios" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DALY-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-cohort-horizon-and-conventions-in-both-daly-scenarios" .

hemo:7003748 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Programme averts DALYs at a positive extra cost"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The ratio is read as a cost per DALY averted only when DALY_av is above zero and the extra cost is positive. A programme that averts DALYs and saves money dominates its comparator, and one that adds DALYs at extra cost is dominated, so neither is summarised by the ratio. Ties in cost or in DALYs are classified by the dominance rule HE-FM-DOM-001, with DALYs averted as the effect." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Programme averts DALYs at a positive extra cost" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DALY-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "programme-averts-dalys-at-a-positive-extra-cost" .

hemo:7003749 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Cost per DALY averted from named scenario cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000645 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the costs in CostProg and CostComp and the DALYs in DALYsProg and DALYsComp, the first formula returns the DALYs averted, held in DALYsAverted, and the second the cost per DALY averted, held in CostPerDALY." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cost per DALY averted from named scenario cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DALY-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cost-per-daly-averted-from-named-scenario-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=DALYsComp-DALYsProg; =(CostProg-CostComp)/DALYsAverted" .

hemo:7003750 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cost per DALY averted times DALYs averted returns the extra cost"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the ratio in CostPerDALY, the DALYs averted are positive and the ratio times the DALYs averted equals the extra cost. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the denominator written as the programme's DALYs less the comparator's, which gives minus USD 500 in the article's example." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Cost per DALY averted times DALYs averted returns the extra cost" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DALY-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "cost-per-daly-averted-times-dalys-averted-returns-the-extra-cost" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(DALYsComp>DALYsProg,ABS(CostPerDALY*(DALYsComp-DALYsProg)-(CostProg-CostComp))<1E-6)" .

hemo:7003751 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's programme undiscounted at USD 444,000 extra cost"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003752,
        hemo:7003753,
        hemo:7003754,
        hemo:7003755 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003756,
        hemo:7003757 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The programme lowers the cohort's DALYs to 552 against 1,440, averting 888, and costs USD 444,000 more, so it costs USD 500 per DALY averted. The comparator's cost is entered as 0 so that C_1 holds the extra cost. All figures are illustrative, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's programme undiscounted at USD 444,000 extra cost" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DALY_0 = 1440; DALY_1 = 552; C_1 = 444000; C_0 = 0; DALY_av = 888; ICER = 500" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DALY-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-programme-undiscounted-at-usd-444-000-extra-cost" .

