hemo:7003765 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Deaths and onset of illness both at time zero in a discounted cohort DALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each death and the start of each survivor's illness fall at time 0, so both streams are discounted from the same point. When death follows T years of illness the years lost begin at T, and their present value is multiplied by e to the minus rT. Larson's recalculation of the Fox-Rushby and Hanson case gives 5.1836 discounted YLDs for 10 years at a weight of 0.6 and 15.9823 discounted YLLs for the 34.73 years lost after them, 21.166 DALYs in all." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Deaths and onset of illness both at time zero in a discounted cohort DALY" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DALY-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "deaths-and-onset-of-illness-both-at-time-zero-in-a-discounted-cohort-daly" .

hemo:7003766 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous discounting at one rate with no age weighting"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "One constant rate applies throughout, in continuous time as in Larson's equation 1, and the age weights of the original DALY are left out. Discounted DALYs serve economic evaluation or historical comparison, since GBD from 2010 onwards and WHO after its 2012 decision use a 0% rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuous discounting at one rate with no age weighting" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DALY-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuous-discounting-at-one-rate-with-no-age-weighting" .

hemo:7003767 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Continuously discounted cohort DALYs from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000646 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Deaths, StdLE, Survivors, DisWeight, DurationYrs and DiscRate named, the cell returns the discounted DALYs of one scenario, held in DALYDisc." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Continuously discounted cohort DALYs from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DALY-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "continuously-discounted-cohort-dalys-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Deaths*(1-EXP(-DiscRate*StdLE))/DiscRate+Survivors*DisWeight*(1-EXP(-DiscRate*DurationYrs))/DiscRate" .

hemo:7003768 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted cohort DALYs above zero and below the undiscounted total"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a rate above 0 and below 1, DALYDisc is above zero and below the undiscounted total of the same cohort. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the rate entered as 3 for 3%, or a dropped minus sign in the exponent, which gives a negative total." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted cohort DALYs above zero and below the undiscounted total" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DALY-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-cohort-dalys-above-zero-and-below-the-undiscounted-total" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(DiscRate>0,DiscRate<1,DALYDisc>0,DALYDisc<Deaths*StdLE+Survivors*DisWeight*DurationYrs)" .

hemo:7003769 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's continuous discount factors for 45 and 10 years reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The factors at 3% for 45 and 10 years round to 24.692 and 8.639, as in the article. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows discrete start-of-year factors, which give 25.254 and 8.786." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's continuous discount factors for 45 and 10 years reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DALY-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-continuous-discount-factors-for-45-and-10-years-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS((1-EXP(-0.03*45))/0.03-24.692)<0.0005,ABS((1-EXP(-0.03*10))/0.03-8.639)<0.0005)" .

hemo:7003770 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's untreated cohort discounted continuously at 3 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Discounting the 45 standard years per death to 24.692 and the 10 years of illness to 8.639 gives 960.37 DALYs in place of 1,440. The article shows 960.35 because it multiplies the rounded factors." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's untreated cohort discounted continuously at 3 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 20; L = 45; S = 180; DW = 0.3; T = 10; r = 0.03; f_L = 24.6920; f_T = 8.6394; DALY_d = 960.37" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DALY-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-untreated-cohort-discounted-continuously-at-3-per-cent" .

hemo:7003771 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's treated cohort discounted continuously at 3 per cent"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 8 deaths and 192 survivors at a weight of 0.1 the discounted total is 363.41 DALYs, as in the article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's treated cohort discounted continuously at 3 per cent" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 8; L = 45; S = 192; DW = 0.1; T = 10; r = 0.03; f_L = 24.6920; f_T = 8.6394; DALY_d = 363.41" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DALY-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-treated-cohort-discounted-continuously-at-3-per-cent" .

hemo:7003772 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted cohort DALYs at a rate close to zero as a limiting case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At a rate of 0.0000001 the factors are close to 45 and 10 years and the total returns the undiscounted 1,440 DALYs of HE-FM-DALY-002 to two decimals, which checks the implementation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted cohort DALYs at a rate close to zero as a limiting case" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = 20; L = 45; S = 180; DW = 0.3; T = 10; r = 0.0000001; f_L = 44.9999; f_T = 10.0000; DALY_d = 1440.00" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DALY-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-cohort-dalys-at-a-rate-close-to-zero-as-a-limiting-case" .

hemo:7003773 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "DALY count and population for the same place, group and year"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The DALYs and the population refer to the same location, sex, age group and year. An all-age rate depends on the age structure, so comparisons between places or over time use age-specific or age-standardised rates." ;
    hemo:9000009 "DALY count and population for the same place, group and year" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-DALY-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "daly-count-and-population-for-the-same-place-group-and-year" .

hemo:7003774 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "DALY rate per 100,000 from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000647 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With DALYCount and Population named, the cell returns DALYs per 100,000 population, held in DALYRate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "DALY rate per 100,000 from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-DALY-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "daly-rate-per-100-000-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=DALYCount/Population*100000" .

hemo:7003775 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "DALY rate times population over 100,000 returns the DALY count"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Multiplying the rate in DALYRate by the population and dividing by 100,000 returns the count. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows a rate scaled per 1,000 or per person." ;
    hemo:9000009 "DALY rate times population over 100,000 returns the DALY count" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-DALY-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "daly-rate-times-population-over-100-000-returns-the-daly-count" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(DALYRate*Population/100000-DALYCount)<1E-6" .

hemo:7003776 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Illustrative district DALY rate per 100,000"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "If the article's illustrative 1,440 DALYs arose in a district of 250,000 people, an illustrative population, the rate would be 576 DALYs per 100,000 population." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Illustrative district DALY rate per 100,000" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DALY = 1440; Pop = 250000; DALY_rate = 576" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DALY-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "illustrative-district-daly-rate-per-100-000" .

hemo:7003777 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "DALY rate in a population of exactly 100,000 as a limiting case"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When the population is 100,000 the rate equals the DALY count, a check that the scaling is applied once." ;
    hemo:9000009 "DALY rate in a population of exactly 100,000 as a limiting case" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DALY = 1440; Pop = 100000; DALY_rate = 1440" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-DALY-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "daly-rate-in-a-population-of-exactly-100-000-as-a-limiting-case" .

hemo:7003778 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Additive main effects with no interactions beyond the N3 term"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each dimension contributes its own decrement whatever the levels on the other dimensions, and the only terms that depend on the whole profile are the constant and N3. Dolan and colleagues reported that none of the models with interactions between dimensions improved the fit significantly and that many introduced inconsistencies into the estimated values, and that without N3 the model underestimated the values of less severe states and overestimated those of more severe ones." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Additive main effects with no interactions beyond the N3 term" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQ3L-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "additive-main-effects-with-no-interactions-beyond-the-n3-term" .

hemo:7003779 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Level 3 decrement at least as large as the level 2 decrement on each dimension"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "On every dimension the decrement at level 3 is no smaller than the one at level 2, and both are zero or positive, so a state that is worse on one dimension and the same on the others never scores higher. A coefficient set that breaks this ordering is not logically consistent." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Level 3 decrement at least as large as the level 2 decrement on each dimension" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQ3L-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "level-3-decrement-at-least-as-large-as-the-level-2-decrement-on-each-dimension" .

hemo:7003780 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Not every national EQ-5D-3L value set takes the constant and N3 form"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The form applies to value sets estimated with a constant, level 2 and level 3 dummies and N3, as the UK tariff was, and to sets reported without the constant or without N3, which are scored by entering zero for the missing coefficient. Sets with any other term cannot be scored this way. The US time trade-off set of Shaw, Johnson and Coons 2005 is a D1 model with terms for the number of dimensions with problems beyond the first and for the numbers at level 2 and at level 3 beyond the first, some of them squared, and no constant or N3 term, so it cannot be scored with this formula and is not formalised here." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Not every national EQ-5D-3L value set takes the constant and N3 form" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQ3L-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "not-every-national-eq-5d-3l-value-set-takes-the-constant-and-n3-form" .

hemo:7003781 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Coefficients entered as positive decrements"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The constant, the level decrements and the N3 term are entered as positive amounts that are subtracted from 1. Tables that print them as negative coefficients added to 1, as the EuroQol reference volume does, describe the same model, and their signs are dropped before entry." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Coefficients entered as positive decrements" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQ3L-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "coefficients-entered-as-positive-decrements" .

hemo:7003782 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "EQ-5D-3L main-effects utility from named level and decrement ranges"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000648 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the five reported levels in a range named Levels, the decrements at those levels in a range named Decrements and the constant and N3 coefficients in cells named Alpha and Gamma, the formula returns U. SUM(Levels)>5 is TRUE for any problem and MAX(Levels)=3 for any level 3, and Excel treats TRUE as 1 when it multiplies." ;
    hemo:9000009 "EQ-5D-3L main-effects utility from named level and decrement ranges" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EQ3L-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "eq-5d-3l-main-effects-utility-from-named-level-and-decrement-ranges" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1-Alpha*(SUM(Levels)>5)-SUM(Decrements)-Gamma*(MAX(Levels)=3)" .

hemo:7003783 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's four illustrative EQ-5D-3L states reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The illustrative coefficients give 0.73 for 21121, 0.59 for 22221, 0.20 for 21131 and minus 0.03 for 31131. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a dropped constant or an N3 term charged more than once." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's four illustrative EQ-5D-3L states reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQ3L-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-four-illustrative-eq-5d-3l-states-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(1-(0.08+0.07+0.12),2)=0.73,ROUND(1-(0.08+0.07+0.10+0.04+0.12),2)=0.59,ROUND(1-(0.08+0.07+0.38+0.27),2)=0.2,ROUND(1-(0.08+0.30+0.38+0.27),2)=-0.03)" .

hemo:7003784 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "EQ-5D-3L utility of one only for full health"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a positive constant, the utility in a cell named Utility3L is at most 1 and equals 1 exactly when every level in Levels is 1. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a constant charged for 11111 or omitted for a state with problems." ;
    hemo:9000009 "EQ-5D-3L utility of one only for full health" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQ3L-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "eq-5d-3l-utility-of-one-only-for-full-health" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(Utility3L<=1,(ROUND(Utility3L,6)=1)=(SUM(Levels)=5))" .

hemo:7003785 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Illustrative EQ-5D-3L state 21121 with two level 2 problems"@en ;
