    rdfs:label "N_3 in the test EQ-5D-3L full health 11111 scores one under any coefficient set"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002791 ;
    rheo:2000001 0.0 .

hemo:7003839 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "U in the test EQ-5D-3L full health 11111 scores one under any coefficient set"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002782 ;
    rheo:2000001 1.0 .

hemo:7003840 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "UK tariff coefficients as published by the MVH study"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The coefficients are those of the UK time trade-off tariff, 0.081 for the constant, 0.069 and 0.314 for mobility, 0.104 and 0.214 for self-care, 0.036 and 0.094 for usual activities, 0.123 and 0.386 for pain or discomfort, 0.071 and 0.236 for anxiety or depression and 0.269 for N3. They are taken from Table 1 of the Dolan, Gudex, Kind and Williams discussion paper and agree with the UK row of Table 2.2 of the EuroQol reference volume." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK tariff coefficients as published by the MVH study" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQ3L-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-tariff-coefficients-as-published-by-the-mvh-study" .

hemo:7003841 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Whole-number levels in the order of the EQ-5D-3L profile"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The levels are entered as whole numbers 1, 2 or 3 in the profile order mobility, self-care, usual activities, pain or discomfort and anxiety or depression. The min and max indicators are exact only for those values, so a mean level or a missing response has to be resolved before scoring." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Whole-number levels in the order of the EQ-5D-3L profile" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQ3L-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "whole-number-levels-in-the-order-of-the-eq-5d-3l-profile" .

hemo:7003842 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Utilities reported to three decimals on a scale anchored at full health and dead"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Full health is 1 and dead is 0, and the published tariff lists every state to three decimals, from 1.000 for 11111 down to minus 0.594 for 33333. The value of minus 0.402 that the discussion paper gives for the unconscious state is a mean of observed valuations and does not come from this model." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Utilities reported to three decimals on a scale anchored at full health and dead" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQ3L-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "utilities-reported-to-three-decimals-on-a-scale-anchored-at-full-health-and-dead" .

hemo:7003843 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "UK MVH EQ-5D-3L tariff from five named level cells with CHOOSE"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000649 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the five levels in cells named Lev_MO, Lev_SC, Lev_UA, Lev_PD and Lev_AD, CHOOSE picks each dimension's decrement for the level reported and the two comparisons set the constant and N3. Rounding the result to 3 decimals with ROUND matches the published tariff." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK MVH EQ-5D-3L tariff from five named level cells with CHOOSE" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EQ3L-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-mvh-eq-5d-3l-tariff-from-five-named-level-cells-with-choose" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=1-0.081*(MAX(Lev_MO,Lev_SC,Lev_UA,Lev_PD,Lev_AD)>1)-CHOOSE(Lev_MO,0,0.069,0.314)-CHOOSE(Lev_SC,0,0.104,0.214)-CHOOSE(Lev_UA,0,0.036,0.094)-CHOOSE(Lev_PD,0,0.123,0.386)-CHOOSE(Lev_AD,0,0.071,0.236)-0.269*(MAX(Lev_MO,Lev_SC,Lev_UA,Lev_PD,Lev_AD)=3)" .

hemo:7003844 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK EQ-5D-3L tariff worst state below zero at minus 0.594"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "State 33333 scores minus 0.594 and lies below dead. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a missing coefficient, N3 charged more than once or coefficients entered with their printed negative signs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK EQ-5D-3L tariff worst state below zero at minus 0.594" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQ3L-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-eq-5d-3l-tariff-worst-state-below-zero-at-minus-0-594" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(1-(0.081+0.314+0.214+0.094+0.386+0.236+0.269),3)=-0.594,1-(0.081+0.314+0.214+0.094+0.386+0.236+0.269)<0)" .

hemo:7003845 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK EQ-5D-3L tariff appendix values reproduced for five states"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The coefficients give 0.850 for 21111, 0.414 for 11113, 0.255 for 11223, 0.516 for 22222 and 0.196 for 32211, the values printed in the tariff appendix. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a transcription error in a coefficient or levels read in the wrong dimension order." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK EQ-5D-3L tariff appendix values reproduced for five states" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQ3L-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-eq-5d-3l-tariff-appendix-values-reproduced-for-five-states" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(1-0.081-0.069,3)=0.85,ROUND(1-0.081-0.236-0.269,3)=0.414,ROUND(1-0.081-0.036-0.123-0.236-0.269,3)=0.255,ROUND(1-0.081-0.069-0.104-0.036-0.123-0.071,3)=0.516,ROUND(1-0.081-0.314-0.104-0.036-0.269,3)=0.196)" .

hemo:7003846 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK tariff value of EQ-5D-3L full health 11111"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With every level at 1 neither indicator is set and no decrement applies, so the UK tariff gives 1, the limiting case at the top of the scale." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK tariff value of EQ-5D-3L full health 11111" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 1; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 1; l_PD = 1; l_AD = 1; D = 0; N_3 = 0; U = 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQ3L-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-tariff-value-of-eq-5d-3l-full-health-11111" .

hemo:7003847 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK tariff value of the mild EQ-5D-3L state 21111"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Some problems walking about and nothing else costs the constant 0.081 and the mobility level 2 decrement 0.069, giving 0.850, the value printed in the tariff appendix." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK tariff value of the mild EQ-5D-3L state 21111" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 2; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 1; l_PD = 1; l_AD = 1; D = 1; N_3 = 0; U = 0.850" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQ3L-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-tariff-value-of-the-mild-eq-5d-3l-state-21111" .

hemo:7003848 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK tariff value of EQ-5D-3L state 11113 with one dimension at level 3"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Extreme anxiety or depression alone costs the constant 0.081, the level 3 decrement 0.236 and the N3 decrement 0.269, giving 0.414. A single level 3 response is enough to bring in N3." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK tariff value of EQ-5D-3L state 11113 with one dimension at level 3" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 1; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 1; l_PD = 1; l_AD = 3; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U = 0.414" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQ3L-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-tariff-value-of-eq-5d-3l-state-11113-with-one-dimension-at-level-3" .

hemo:7003849 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK tariff value of EQ-5D-3L state 11223 as worked in the MVH paper"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The discussion paper's own example subtracts the constant 0.081, the usual activities and pain level 2 decrements 0.036 and 0.123, the anxiety or depression level 3 decrement 0.236 and N3 0.269 from 1, giving 0.255." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK tariff value of EQ-5D-3L state 11223 as worked in the MVH paper" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 1; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 2; l_PD = 2; l_AD = 3; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U = 0.255" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQ3L-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-tariff-value-of-eq-5d-3l-state-11223-as-worked-in-the-mvh-paper" .

hemo:7003850 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK tariff value of the worst EQ-5D-3L state 33333"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Every dimension at level 3 costs the constant, the five level 3 decrements and N3 once, 1.594 in all, giving minus 0.594, the minimum of the UK tariff." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK tariff value of the worst EQ-5D-3L state 33333" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 3; l_SC = 3; l_UA = 3; l_PD = 3; l_AD = 3; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U = -0.594" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQ3L-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-tariff-value-of-the-worst-eq-5d-3l-state-33333" .

hemo:7003851 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Both EQ-5D-3L states scored with one value set and held constant"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "U_a, U_b and gamma come from the same value set, and each utility is constant for the T years without discounting. Discounted gains follow HE-FN-DISC-001, and states scored with different sets, such as a 3L and a 5L set, are not compared with this formula." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Both EQ-5D-3L states scored with one value set and held constant" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQ3L-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "both-eq-5d-3l-states-scored-with-one-value-set-and-held-constant" .

hemo:7003852 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "N3 share defined only for a positive EQ-5D-3L utility gap"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The share needs U_a above U_b. When both states are departures from 11111 the constant cancels, so the gap is the N3 term, when it differs, plus the difference in level decrements." ;
    hemo:9000009 "N3 share defined only for a positive EQ-5D-3L utility gap" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EQ3L-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "n3-share-defined-only-for-a-positive-eq-5d-3l-utility-gap" .

hemo:7003853 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "QALY difference between two EQ-5D-3L states from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000650 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the utilities of the kept and avoided states in cells named UtilityKept and UtilityAvoided and the years in YearsInState, the formula returns dQ." ;
    hemo:9000009 "QALY difference between two EQ-5D-3L states from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EQ3L-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "qaly-difference-between-two-eq-5d-3l-states-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(UtilityKept-UtilityAvoided)*YearsInState" .

hemo:7003854 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "N3 share of an EQ-5D-3L utility gap from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000650 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the N3 decrement in a cell named Gamma and the two N3 indicators in N3Kept and N3Avoided, the formula returns s_N3." ;
    hemo:9000009 "N3 share of an EQ-5D-3L utility gap from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EQ3L-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "n3-share-of-an-eq-5d-3l-utility-gap-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=Gamma*(N3Avoided-N3Kept)/(UtilityKept-UtilityAvoided)" .

hemo:7003855 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK tariff EQ-5D-3L QALY gains for the N3 and level 2 comparisons"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Two years in 21121 instead of 21131 gain 1.064 QALYs and instead of 22221 gain 0.28 QALYs. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows utilities taken from a different value set." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK tariff EQ-5D-3L QALY gains for the N3 and level 2 comparisons" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQ3L-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-tariff-eq-5d-3l-qaly-gains-for-the-n3-and-level-2-comparisons" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND((0.727-0.195)*2,3)=1.064,ROUND((0.727-0.587)*2,2)=0.28)" .

hemo:7003856 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "N3 share of the UK tariff gap between EQ-5D-3L states 21121 and 21131"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The N3 decrement divided by the utility gap of 0.532 rounds to 0.5056. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows N3 left out of one of the two states." ;
    hemo:9000009 "N3 share of the UK tariff gap between EQ-5D-3L states 21121 and 21131" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EQ3L-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "n3-share-of-the-uk-tariff-gap-between-eq-5d-3l-states-21121-and-21131" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(0.269*(1-0)/(0.727-0.195),4)=0.5056" .

hemo:7003857 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK tariff QALY gain from keeping EQ-5D-3L state 21121 instead of 21131"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Under the UK tariff 21121 scores 0.727 and 21131 scores 0.195. Keeping patients out of the level 3 pain state for 2 years gains 1.064 QALYs, and the N3 decrement 0.269 accounts for about 51% of the utility gap of 0.532." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK tariff QALY gain from keeping EQ-5D-3L state 21121 instead of 21131" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U_a = 0.727; U_b = 0.195; T = 2; gamma = 0.269; N3_a = 0; N3_b = 1; dQ = 1.064; s_N3 = 0.5056" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQ3L-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-tariff-qaly-gain-from-keeping-eq-5d-3l-state-21121-instead-of-21131" .

hemo:7003858 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK tariff QALY gain from keeping EQ-5D-3L state 21121 instead of 22221"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "State 22221 scores 0.587 under the UK tariff. Avoiding two extra level 2 problems for 2 years gains 0.28 QALYs, with no N3 share, so the single step to level 3 in the previous example is worth about 3.8 times as much." ;
    hemo:9000009 "UK tariff QALY gain from keeping EQ-5D-3L state 21121 instead of 22221" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U_a = 0.727; U_b = 0.587; T = 2; gamma = 0.269; N3_a = 0; N3_b = 0; dQ = 0.28; s_N3 = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQ3L-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "uk-tariff-qaly-gain-from-keeping-eq-5d-3l-state-21121-instead-of-22221" .

hemo:7003859 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's illustrative EQ-5D-3L QALY gain and cost per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's illustrative utilities of 0.73 and 0.20 and gamma of 0.27, two years gain 1.06 QALYs and N3 explains about 51% of the gap. An illustrative extra cost of GBP 10,600 then gives GBP 10,000 per QALY, as in the incremental ratio of HE-FM-CUA-001." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's illustrative EQ-5D-3L QALY gain and cost per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "U_a = 0.73; U_b = 0.20; T = 2; gamma = 0.27; N3_a = 0; N3_b = 1; dQ = 1.06; s_N3 = 0.5094" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EQ3L-013" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-illustrative-eq-5d-3l-qaly-gain-and-cost-per-qaly" .

hemo:7003860 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Option chosen on current evidence held fixed across all EVPI draws"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The option d* is the one with the highest mean net benefit over the same draws, and it is held fixed in every draw. NBcur_s is the net benefit of d* in draw s, not that of whichever option happens to be best in that draw, so the loss is never negative." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Option chosen on current evidence held fixed across all EVPI draws" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "option-chosen-on-current-evidence-held-fixed-across-all-evpi-draws" .

hemo:7003861 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "EVPI draws taken from the probabilistic analysis without extra sampling"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The draws are equally likely samples from the joint distribution of the uncertain inputs, and each draw holds the net benefit of every option at the same threshold. The ISPOR methods report describes this as a single-loop Monte Carlo scheme that needs no sampling beyond the probabilistic analysis. A deterministic run at mean input values cannot replace the draws in a non-linear model." ;
    hemo:9000009 "EVPI draws taken from the probabilistic analysis without extra sampling" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "evpi-draws-taken-from-the-probabilistic-analysis-without-extra-sampling" .

hemo:7003862 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Risk-neutral choice by highest expected net benefit in EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The decision on current evidence is the option with the highest expected net benefit, the choice of a risk-neutral decision maker. A risk-averse decision rule can choose a different option, and the mean loss of that option is then larger than EVPI as defined here." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Risk-neutral choice by highest expected net benefit in EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "risk-neutral-choice-by-highest-expected-net-benefit-in-evpi" .

hemo:7003863 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "EVPI as mean opportunity loss from a draw by option table in Excel"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000651 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With one row per draw and one column per option in a range named NB, a helper column RowMax holding the maximum of each row and a helper row ColMeans holding the mean of each column, INDEX and MATCH pick the column of the option with the highest mean and SUMPRODUCT averages the loss over the draws. The formula needs no array entry." ;
    hemo:9000009 "EVPI as mean opportunity loss from a draw by option table in Excel" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVPI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "evpi-as-mean-opportunity-loss-from-a-draw-by-option-table-in-excel" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(RowMax-INDEX(NB,0,MATCH(MAX(ColMeans),ColMeans,0)))/ROWS(NB)" .

hemo:7003864 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "EVPI opportunity-loss form equals the mean of maxima less the maximum of means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The mean loss from the table equals the mean of the row maxima less the largest column mean, the form in HE-IM-VOI-001. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows that the fixed column is not the option with the highest mean, or that the two forms use different draws." ;
    hemo:9000009 "EVPI opportunity-loss form equals the mean of maxima less the maximum of means" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "evpi-opportunity-loss-form-equals-the-mean-of-maxima-less-the-maximum-of-means" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(RowMax-INDEX(NB,0,MATCH(MAX(ColMeans),ColMeans,0)))/ROWS(NB)-(AVERAGE(RowMax)-MAX(ColMeans)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003865 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "No negative opportunity loss in any EVPI draw"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "No draw has a row maximum below the net benefit of the option chosen on current evidence. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows that RowMax does not cover every option column or was filled down over the wrong rows." ;
    hemo:9000009 "No negative opportunity loss in any EVPI draw" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "no-negative-opportunity-loss-in-any-evpi-draw" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(--(RowMax<INDEX(NB,0,MATCH(MAX(ColMeans),ColMeans,0))))=0" .

hemo:7003866 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's EVPI of 0.06 QALYs reproduced from opportunity losses"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The five draws at GBP 25,000 per QALY give a mean loss of 0.06 QALYs when rounded to two decimals. Expected result TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's EVPI of 0.06 QALYs reproduced from opportunity losses" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-evpi-of-0-06-qalys-reproduced-from-opportunity-losses" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(SUMPRODUCT({0.1;0;0.3;0;0.25}-{0.1;-0.2;0.3;-0.1;0.25})/5,2)=0.06" .

hemo:7003867 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's five draws at GBP 25,000 per QALY as opportunity losses"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003868,
        hemo:7003869,
        hemo:7003870 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003871,
        hemo:7003872 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative example a new drug is compared with standard care, whose net benefit is set to zero, and the drug's incremental net health benefit in the five draws is 0.10, minus 0.20, 0.30, minus 0.10 and 0.25 QALYs. The drug has the higher mean, 0.07 QALYs, so it is chosen, and it loses 0.20 and 0.10 QALYs in draws 2 and 4 where standard care is better. The mean loss is 0.30 / 5 = 0.06 QALYs per patient, the same EVPI as the mean of the maxima less the maximum of the means. This example is for reading, as its draw-by-draw lists may not run in the site calculator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's five draws at GBP 25,000 per QALY as opportunity losses" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S = 5; NBmax_s = [0.10,0,0.30,0,0.25]; NBcur_s = [0.10,-0.20,0.30,-0.10,0.25]; L_s = [0,0.20,0,0.10,0]; EVPI = 0.06" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-five-draws-at-gbp-25-000-per-qaly-as-opportunity-losses" .

hemo:7003868 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "S in the test Article's five draws at GBP 25,000 per QALY as opportunity losses"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002812 ;
    rheo:2000001 5.0 .

