    rheo:2000001 0.0 .

hemo:7003885 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Exactly two options with the comparator as the zero reference"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The decision is between one new option and one comparator, so the comparator's net benefit is zero in every draw. With three or more options the positive-part form no longer applies, and HE-FM-EVPI-001 or the computational function below is used instead." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exactly two options with the comparator as the zero reference" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exactly-two-options-with-the-comparator-as-the-zero-reference" .

hemo:7003886 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-option EVPI reported at stated thresholds"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "EVPI depends on the threshold through INHB_s, so it is reported for explicit thresholds or plotted against the threshold, as the ISPOR methods report advises. For NICE the expected net health benefits are presented, when appropriate, at GBP 25,000 and GBP 35,000 per QALY (PMG36, section 4.10.8)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-option EVPI reported at stated thresholds" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPI-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-option-evpi-reported-at-stated-thresholds" .

hemo:7003887 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Same draws and threshold for the health and money forms of EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "EVPI_M equals lambda times EVPI_H only when both use the same draws and the same lambda. A money value of EVPI belongs to one threshold and is not rescaled to another." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Same draws and threshold for the health and money forms of EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPI-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "same-draws-and-threshold-for-the-health-and-money-forms-of-evpi" .

hemo:7003888 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-option EVPI in QALYs from incremental QALY and cost columns"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000652 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the incremental QALYs of each draw in a range named IncQALY, the incremental costs in IncCost and the threshold in Threshold, SUMPRODUCT averages the positive INHB values and MAX takes the positive part of the mean INHB. Multiplying the result by Threshold gives EVPI in money." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-option EVPI in QALYs from incremental QALY and cost columns" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVPI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-option-evpi-in-qalys-from-incremental-qaly-and-cost-columns" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT((IncQALY-IncCost/Threshold>0)*(IncQALY-IncCost/Threshold))/ROWS(IncQALY)-MAX(0,AVERAGE(IncQALY)-AVERAGE(IncCost)/Threshold)" .

hemo:7003889 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's two-option EVPI of 0.06 QALYs reproduced at GBP 25,000"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The five draws with an incremental cost worth 0.40 QALYs give 0.06 QALYs when rounded to two decimals. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the positive part taken of the mean only, or of each draw only." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's two-option EVPI of 0.06 QALYs reproduced at GBP 25,000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-two-option-evpi-of-0-06-qalys-reproduced-at-gbp-25-000" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(SUMPRODUCT(({0.5;0.2;0.7;0.3;0.65}-0.4>0)*({0.5;0.2;0.7;0.3;0.65}-0.4))/5-MAX(0,AVERAGE({0.5;0.2;0.7;0.3;0.65})-0.4),2)=0.06" .

hemo:7003890 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's two-option EVPI of 0.017 QALYs reproduced at GBP 35,000"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the incremental cost worth 10,000 / 35,000 QALYs, the same draws give 0.017 QALYs when rounded to three decimals. Expected result TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's two-option EVPI of 0.017 QALYs reproduced at GBP 35,000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPI-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-two-option-evpi-of-0-017-qalys-reproduced-at-gbp-35-000" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(SUMPRODUCT(({0.5;0.2;0.7;0.3;0.65}-10000/35000>0)*({0.5;0.2;0.7;0.3;0.65}-10000/35000))/5-MAX(0,AVERAGE({0.5;0.2;0.7;0.3;0.65})-10000/35000),3)=0.017" .

hemo:7003891 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Money EVPI equals the threshold times health EVPI for two options"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The money value in a cell named EVPIMoney equals Threshold times the QALY value in EVPIHealth. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a money value computed at a different threshold from the health value." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Money EVPI equals the threshold times health EVPI for two options" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPI-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "money-evpi-equals-the-threshold-times-health-evpi-for-two-options" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(EVPIMoney-Threshold*EVPIHealth)<0.01" .

hemo:7003892 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's two-option EVPI at GBP 25,000 per QALY in QALYs and money"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative example the incremental cost is GBP 10,000 in every draw and the incremental QALYs are 0.50, 0.20, 0.70, 0.30 and 0.65. At GBP 25,000 per QALY the cost is worth 0.40 QALYs, the mean of the positive parts is 0.65 / 5 = 0.13 QALYs and the mean INHB is 0.07 QALYs, so EVPI is 0.06 QALYs per patient, or GBP 1,500 at the same threshold. This example is for reading, as its draw-by-draw lists may not run in the site calculator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's two-option EVPI at GBP 25,000 per QALY in QALYs and money" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S = 5; dQ_s = [0.50,0.20,0.70,0.30,0.65]; dC_s = [10000,10000,10000,10000,10000]; lambda = 25000; INHB_s = [0.10,-0.20,0.30,-0.10,0.25]; EVPI_H = 0.06; EVPI_M = 1500" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-two-option-evpi-at-gbp-25-000-per-qaly-in-qalys-and-money" .

hemo:7003893 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's two-option EVPI at GBP 35,000 per QALY in QALYs and money"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At GBP 35,000 per QALY the same cost is worth about 0.2857 QALYs, only draw 2 has a negative INHB and EVPI falls to about 0.0171 QALYs per patient, or about GBP 600 at that threshold. A higher threshold moves the mean INHB further from zero and lowers EVPI. This example is for reading, as its draw-by-draw lists may not run in the site calculator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's two-option EVPI at GBP 35,000 per QALY in QALYs and money" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S = 5; dQ_s = [0.50,0.20,0.70,0.30,0.65]; dC_s = [10000,10000,10000,10000,10000]; lambda = 35000; INHB_s = [0.2143,-0.0857,0.4143,0.0143,0.3643]; EVPI_H = 0.0171429; EVPI_M = 600" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPI-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-two-option-evpi-at-gbp-35-000-per-qaly-in-qalys-and-money" .

hemo:7003894 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two-option EVPI of zero at an illustrative GBP 60,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At an illustrative threshold of GBP 60,000 per QALY, above the values in PMG36, the cost is worth about 0.1667 QALYs and the drug's INHB is positive in all five draws. The drug is best in every draw, so EVPI is zero, a limiting case of the formula. This example is for reading, as its draw-by-draw lists may not run in the site calculator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Two-option EVPI of zero at an illustrative GBP 60,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S = 5; dQ_s = [0.50,0.20,0.70,0.30,0.65]; dC_s = [10000,10000,10000,10000,10000]; lambda = 60000; INHB_s = [0.3333,0.0333,0.5333,0.1333,0.4833]; EVPI_H = 0; EVPI_M = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPI-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "two-option-evpi-of-zero-at-an-illustrative-gbp-60-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7003895 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Ties counted as correct decisions in the EVPI error split"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A draw in which the chosen option ties with the best has no loss and is not counted as an error, in line with the acceptability curve's treatment of ties in HE-FM-CEAC-002. Counting ties as errors raises P_err and lowers L_wrong but leaves their product unchanged." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Ties counted as correct decisions in the EVPI error split" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPI-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "ties-counted-as-correct-decisions-in-the-evpi-error-split" .

hemo:7003896 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Error probability and loss from the same draws and threshold as EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "P_err and L_wrong come from the same draws, the same threshold and the same current choice as EVPI. An error probability read from an acceptability curve at another threshold cannot be combined with a loss computed at this one." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Error probability and loss from the same draws and threshold as EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPI-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "error-probability-and-loss-from-the-same-draws-and-threshold-as-evpi" .

hemo:7003897 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Error probability and loss when wrong from an opportunity-loss column"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000653 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the opportunity loss of each draw in a range named Loss, COUNTIF gives the share of draws with a positive loss and AVERAGEIF the mean loss over those draws. IFERROR returns zero for the loss when no draw has one." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Error probability and loss when wrong from an opportunity-loss column" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVPI-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "error-probability-and-loss-when-wrong-from-an-opportunity-loss-column" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=COUNTIF(Loss,\">0\")/COUNT(Loss)*IFERROR(AVERAGEIF(Loss,\">0\"),0)" .

hemo:7003898 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Error probability times loss when wrong equals the mean opportunity loss"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The product from the Loss column equals the plain mean of the column. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows that the loss when wrong was averaged over all draws or that P_err was read from a different set of draws." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Error probability times loss when wrong equals the mean opportunity loss" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPI-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "error-probability-times-loss-when-wrong-equals-the-mean-opportunity-loss" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(COUNTIF(Loss,\">0\")/COUNT(Loss)*IFERROR(AVERAGEIF(Loss,\">0\"),0)-AVERAGE(Loss))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003899 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's EVPI of 0.06 QALYs reproduced from its error split"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Two wrong draws out of five with losses of 0.20 and 0.10 QALYs give 0.06 QALYs when rounded to two decimals. Expected result TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's EVPI of 0.06 QALYs reproduced from its error split" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPI-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-evpi-of-0-06-qalys-reproduced-from-its-error-split" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(2/5*AVERAGE(0.2,0.1),2)=0.06" .

hemo:7003900 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's error probability and loss when wrong at GBP 25,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The drug is the wrong choice in two of the five illustrative draws, so P_err is 0.4, and the losses there are 0.20 and 0.10 QALYs, a mean of 0.15. The product is 0.06 QALYs per patient, the article's EVPI." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's error probability and loss when wrong at GBP 25,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P_err = 0.4; L_wrong = 0.15; EVPI = 0.06" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPI-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-error-probability-and-loss-when-wrong-at-gbp-25-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7003901 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's error probability and loss when wrong at GBP 35,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At GBP 35,000 per QALY only draw 2 favours standard care, so P_err is 0.2 and the loss when wrong is about 0.0857 QALYs. The product is about 0.0171 QALYs per patient. The error probability halves but EVPI falls by more than two thirds, because the loss when wrong also shrinks." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's error probability and loss when wrong at GBP 35,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P_err = 0.2; L_wrong = 0.0857143; EVPI = 0.0171" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPI-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-error-probability-and-loss-when-wrong-at-gbp-35-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7003902 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Rare but costly error giving a larger EVPI than a frequent small one"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An illustrative current choice that is wrong in only 5% of draws but loses 2 QALYs per patient when wrong has an EVPI of 0.1 QALYs. That is more than an illustrative choice wrong in 45% of draws with a mean loss of 0.1 QALYs, whose EVPI is 0.045 QALYs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Rare but costly error giving a larger EVPI than a frequent small one" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P_err = 0.05; L_wrong = 2; EVPI = 0.1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPI-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "rare-but-costly-error-giving-a-larger-evpi-than-a-frequent-small-one" .

hemo:7003903 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal distribution of incremental net benefit for closed-form EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The incremental net benefit is normally distributed. For a mean estimated from trial data this rests on the central limit theorem, while a model's net benefit across draws can be skewed, in which case the closed form is an approximation to EVPI from the draws." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal distribution of incremental net benefit for closed-form EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPI-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-distribution-of-incremental-net-benefit-for-closed-form-evpi" .

hemo:7003904 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Exactly two options for the one-dimensional normal EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The closed form applies to one incremental net benefit, so to two options. Three options need the two-dimensional loss integral of Lee and colleagues or the draws themselves (HE-FM-EVPI-001)." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Exactly two options for the one-dimensional normal EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPI-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "exactly-two-options-for-the-one-dimensional-normal-evpi" .

hemo:7003905 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Mean and standard deviation of incremental net benefit at one threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "mu_INB and sigma_INB are in the same units and at the same threshold. Both change with the threshold, so the closed form is evaluated again for each threshold, and the threshold at which mu_INB is zero need not be where EVPI peaks if sigma_INB also changes." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Mean and standard deviation of incremental net benefit at one threshold" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPI-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "mean-and-standard-deviation-of-incremental-net-benefit-at-one-threshold" .

hemo:7003906 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal two-option EVPI with NORM.S.DIST from named cells"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000654 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the mean incremental net benefit in a cell named MuINB and its standard deviation in SigmaINB, NORM.S.DIST with FALSE returns the density and with TRUE the cumulative probability at z." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal two-option EVPI with NORM.S.DIST from named cells" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVPI-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-two-option-evpi-with-norm-s-dist-from-named-cells" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SigmaINB*(NORM.S.DIST(ABS(MuINB)/SigmaINB,FALSE)-ABS(MuINB)/SigmaINB*(1-NORM.S.DIST(ABS(MuINB)/SigmaINB,TRUE)))" .

hemo:7003907 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal EVPI equals the loss integral less the positive part of the mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The value in a cell named EVPINormal equals Lee and colleagues' unit normal loss integral, the expected positive part of the incremental net benefit, less the positive part of its mean. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a signed z or a density and cumulative probability swapped." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal EVPI equals the loss integral less the positive part of the mean" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPI-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-evpi-equals-the-loss-integral-less-the-positive-part-of-the-mean" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(EVPINormal-(MuINB*(1-NORM.S.DIST(-MuINB/SigmaINB,TRUE))+SigmaINB*NORM.S.DIST(-MuINB/SigmaINB,FALSE)-MAX(MuINB,0)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7003908 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal EVPI at a zero mean is 0.3989 times the standard deviation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a standard deviation of 1 and a mean of zero the closed form returns 0.3989 when rounded to four decimals. Expected result TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal EVPI at a zero mean is 0.3989 times the standard deviation" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPI-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-evpi-at-a-zero-mean-is-0-3989-times-the-standard-deviation" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(1*(NORM.S.DIST(0,FALSE)-0*(1-NORM.S.DIST(0,TRUE))),4)=0.3989" .

hemo:7003909 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal EVPI unchanged by the sign of the mean incremental net benefit"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A mean of minus GBP 1,000 with a standard deviation of GBP 2,000 gives GBP 395.59 from the loss integral form, the same as a mean of plus GBP 1,000. Expected result TRUE." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal EVPI unchanged by the sign of the mean incremental net benefit" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPI-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-evpi-unchanged-by-the-sign-of-the-mean-incremental-net-benefit" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(-1000*(1-NORM.S.DIST(1000/2000,TRUE))+2000*NORM.S.DIST(1000/2000,FALSE)-MAX(-1000,0),2)=395.59" .

hemo:7003910 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal approximation to the article's five draws at GBP 25,000 per QALY"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A normal distribution with the mean and sample standard deviation of the article's five illustrative INHB values, 0.07 and about 0.2168 QALYs, gives z of about 0.3229 and an EVPI of about 0.0560 QALYs per patient, against 0.06 from the draws themselves. The gap reflects the five draws not being normal." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal approximation to the article's five draws at GBP 25,000 per QALY" ;
    hemo:9000014 "mu_INB = 0.07; sigma_INB = 0.2168; cdf_z = 0.62661; z = 0.3229; pdf_z = 0.3787; EVPI_N = 0.0560" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPI-010" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-approximation-to-the-article-s-five-draws-at-gbp-25-000-per-qaly" .

hemo:7003911 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal EVPI when the mean incremental net benefit is zero"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With mu_INB equal to zero and the same standard deviation of 0.2168 QALYs, z is zero, cdf_z is 0.5 and EVPI is about 0.3989 times 0.2168, or about 0.0865 QALYs per patient. This limiting case is the largest normal EVPI for that standard deviation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal EVPI when the mean incremental net benefit is zero" ;
    hemo:9000014 "mu_INB = 0; sigma_INB = 0.2168; cdf_z = 0.5; z = 0; pdf_z = 0.398942; EVPI_N = 0.0865" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPI-011" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-evpi-when-the-mean-incremental-net-benefit-is-zero" .

hemo:7003912 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Normal EVPI for an illustrative GBP 1,000 mean and GBP 2,000 spread"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An illustrative incremental net monetary benefit with a mean of GBP 1,000 and a standard deviation of GBP 2,000 gives z of 0.5, a density of about 0.3521 and a cumulative probability of about 0.6915, so EVPI is about GBP 395.59 per person." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Normal EVPI for an illustrative GBP 1,000 mean and GBP 2,000 spread" ;
    hemo:9000014 "mu_INB = 1000; sigma_INB = 2000; cdf_z = 0.69146; z = 0.5; pdf_z = 0.352065; EVPI_N = 395.59" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPI-012" ;
    hemo:9000023 "normal-evpi-for-an-illustrative-gbp-1-000-mean-and-gbp-2-000-spread" .

hemo:7003913 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Inner draws from the conditional distribution of the remaining parameters"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "For each outer draw the J values of theta_c come from their distribution conditional on theta_i at that draw, as step 2 of Algorithm 2 in the second ISPOR report requires. Only when theta_i and theta_c are independent may the inner draws come from the marginal distribution of theta_c. Strong, Oakley and Brennan note that sampling the conditional distribution can require Markov chain Monte Carlo when parameters are correlated, which adds substantially to the computation." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Inner draws from the conditional distribution of the remaining parameters" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPP-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "inner-draws-from-the-conditional-distribution-of-the-remaining-parameters" .

hemo:7003914 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Inner and outer loop sizes chosen for bias and precision of nested EVPPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The maximum of a Monte Carlo mean is biased upwards, so a small inner loop J biases the estimate, and good practice recommendation 5 of the second ISPOR report asks for inner and outer loop sizes chosen to give acceptable bias and precision. Brennan and colleagues found in their case studies that fewer samples on the outer level and more on the inner level could be efficient." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Inner and outer loop sizes chosen for bias and precision of nested EVPPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPP-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "inner-and-outer-loop-sizes-chosen-for-bias-and-precision-of-nested-evppi" .

hemo:7003915 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Incremental net benefit at a stated threshold for nested EVPPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each INB_kj is the net monetary benefit of the new option less that of standard care at one stated cost-effectiveness threshold, computed from the same parameter values for both options. EVPPI changes with the threshold, so the loops are rerun for every threshold reported and the results are not rescaled." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Incremental net benefit at a stated threshold for nested EVPPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPP-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "incremental-net-benefit-at-a-stated-threshold-for-nested-evppi" .

hemo:7003916 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Nested EVPPI from a grid of inner-loop results"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000655 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the incremental net benefits in a range named INBGrid, one row for each outer draw and one column for each inner draw, the first formula returns the estimate in Excel 365, where BYROW and LAMBDA are available. In older versions a column named InnerMean holding the AVERAGE of each row feeds the second formula. Both use the mean of the inner means for the current decision, as in step 7 of Algorithm 2." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Nested EVPPI from a grid of inner-loop results" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVPP-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "nested-evppi-from-a-grid-of-inner-loop-results" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LET(m,BYROW(INBGrid,LAMBDA(x,AVERAGE(x))),AVERAGE(IF(m>0,m,0))-MAX(AVERAGE(m),0)); =SUMPRODUCT((InnerMean>0)*InnerMean)/COUNT(InnerMean)-MAX(AVERAGE(InnerMean),0)" .

hemo:7003917 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Nested EVPPI estimate no larger than the EVPI from the same runs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the estimate in a cell named EVPPIest, the per-person EVPI from the same model runs (HE-FM-VOI-001) in EVPIest and a stated Monte Carlo tolerance in MCTol, the estimate is at least zero and no more than the EVPI plus the tolerance. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows an inner loop too small, which biases the estimate upwards, or a maximum taken inside the inner average." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Nested EVPPI estimate no larger than the EVPI from the same runs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPP-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "nested-evppi-estimate-no-larger-than-the-evpi-from-the-same-runs" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(EVPPIest>=0,EVPPIest<=EVPIest+MCTol)" .

hemo:7003918 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect reproduced by the nested estimator"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The inner means of GBP 1,500 and GBP -1,100 return the article's EVPPI for A of GBP 550. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the current decision valued at the mean of the kept values instead of the larger of zero and the mean of the inner means." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect reproduced by the nested estimator" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPP-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-evppi-for-the-treatment-effect-reproduced-by-the-nested-estimator" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(MAX(1500,0)+MAX(-1100,0))/2-MAX((1500-1100)/2,0)=550" .

hemo:7003919 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Nested estimator with one run per outer draw equals the EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the four combinations of the article's example as outer draws and a single run each, the estimator returns the EVPI of GBP 600. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the zero value of standard care left out of the maximum." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Nested estimator with one run per outer draw equals the EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPP-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "nested-estimator-with-one-run-per-outer-draw-equals-the-evpi" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(MAX(2000,0)+MAX(1000,0)+MAX(200,0)+MAX(-2400,0))/4-MAX((2000+1000+200-2400)/4,0)=600" .

hemo:7003920 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with exact inner means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003921,
        hemo:7003922,
        hemo:7003923,
        hemo:7003924,
        hemo:7003925,
        hemo:7003926 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003927,
        hemo:7003928,
        hemo:7003929 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "All values are illustrative and come from the article's example. The two equally likely values of the treatment effect A are the outer draws and the two equally likely values of the utility B the inner draws, so the inner means are GBP 1,500 when A is high and GBP -1,100 when A is low. Standard care is chosen when A is low, the average of the kept values is GBP 750, and subtracting the current-decision value of GBP 200 leaves GBP 550, the article's EVPPI for A." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with exact inner means" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K = 2; J = 2; INB_11 = 2000; INB_12 = 1000; INB_21 = 200; INB_22 = -2400; ibar_1 = 1500; ibar_2 = -1100; EVPPI_2L = 550" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPP-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-evppi-for-the-treatment-effect-with-exact-inner-means" .

hemo:7003921 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "K in the test Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with exact inner means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002836 ;
    rheo:2000001 2.0 .

hemo:7003922 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "J in the test Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with exact inner means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002837 ;
    rheo:2000001 2.0 .

hemo:7003923 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "INB_11 in the test Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with exact inner means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002830 ;
    rheo:2000001 2000.0 .

hemo:7003924 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "INB_12 in the test Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with exact inner means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002831 ;
    rheo:2000001 1000.0 .

hemo:7003925 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "INB_21 in the test Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with exact inner means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002832 ;
    rheo:2000001 200.0 .

hemo:7003926 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "INB_22 in the test Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with exact inner means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002833 ;
    rheo:2000001 -2400.0 .

hemo:7003927 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "ibar_1 in the test Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with exact inner means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002834 ;
    rheo:2000001 1500.0 .

hemo:7003928 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "ibar_2 in the test Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with exact inner means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002835 ;
    rheo:2000001 -1100.0 .

hemo:7003929 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "EVPPI_2L in the test Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with exact inner means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002829 ;
    rheo:2000001 550.0 .

hemo:7003930 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's EVPPI for the utility with exact inner means"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003931,
        hemo:7003932,
        hemo:7003933,
        hemo:7003934,
        hemo:7003935,
        hemo:7003936 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003937,
        hemo:7003938,
        hemo:7003939 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the utility B in the outer loop and the treatment effect A in the inner loop, the inner means are GBP 1,100 when B is high and GBP -700 when B is low, and the estimate is GBP 350, the article's EVPPI for B. The two values sum to GBP 900, more than the EVPI of GBP 600, because EVPPIs are not additive." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's EVPPI for the utility with exact inner means" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K = 2; J = 2; INB_11 = 2000; INB_12 = 200; INB_21 = 1000; INB_22 = -2400; ibar_1 = 1100; ibar_2 = -700; EVPPI_2L = 350" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPP-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-evppi-for-the-utility-with-exact-inner-means" .

