    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002833 ;
    rheo:2000001 -1100.0 .

hemo:7003947 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "ibar_1 in the test Nested estimator with every parameter of interest returns the EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002834 ;
    rheo:2000001 1500.0 .

hemo:7003948 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "ibar_2 in the test Nested estimator with every parameter of interest returns the EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002835 ;
    rheo:2000001 -1100.0 .

hemo:7003949 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "EVPPI_2L in the test Nested estimator with every parameter of interest returns the EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002829 ;
    rheo:2000001 550.0 .

hemo:7003950 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Net benefit linear in the remaining parameters given theta_i"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "For each value of theta_i the incremental net benefit is a straight-line function of theta_c, or a sum of products of complementary parameters that are not correlated where they are multiplied together, so its expectation over theta_c equals the model evaluated at their means. A parameter that enters squared or inside an exponential breaks the shortcut." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Net benefit linear in the remaining parameters given theta_i" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPP-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "net-benefit-linear-in-the-remaining-parameters-given-theta-i" .

hemo:7003951 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Remaining parameters independent of the parameters of interest for the shortcut"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "One mean mu_c applies at every draw of theta_i only when theta_c is independent of theta_i. Under correlation the mean of theta_c given each value of theta_i is required, and Brennan and colleagues report that the shortcut with a single set of means can then be substantially inaccurate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Remaining parameters independent of the parameters of interest for the shortcut" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPP-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "remaining-parameters-independent-of-the-parameters-of-interest-for-the-shortcut" .

hemo:7003952 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Single-loop EVPPI from intercept and slope columns"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000656 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha_k and beta_k for each draw of theta_i in ranges named Alpha and Beta and the mean of theta_c in a cell named MuC, the formula returns the estimate. In practice the model is run once per draw with theta_c set at its mean, and that column of incremental net benefits takes the place of Alpha+Beta*MuC in the same formula." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Single-loop EVPPI from intercept and slope columns" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVPP-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "single-loop-evppi-from-intercept-and-slope-columns" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(((Alpha+Beta*MuC)>0)*(Alpha+Beta*MuC))/COUNT(Alpha)-MAX(AVERAGE(Alpha)+AVERAGE(Beta)*MuC,0)" .

hemo:7003953 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Linearity check before using the single-loop EVPPI shortcut"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For one draw of theta_i, a short inner loop gives incremental net benefits in a range named INBInner, and one run with theta_c at the mean of those inner values gives a cell named INBAtMean. The two agree within a tolerance in LinTol. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows curvature in theta_c, so the shortcut does not apply and the nested or regression estimator is needed." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Linearity check before using the single-loop EVPPI shortcut" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPP-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "linearity-check-before-using-the-single-loop-evppi-shortcut" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AVERAGE(INBInner)-INBAtMean)<=LinTol" .

hemo:7003954 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's EVPPI for the utility reproduced by the single-loop shortcut"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The intercepts, slopes and mean of the second worked example return GBP 350. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the slope applied to the wrong draw or the mean of the indicator entered as 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's EVPPI for the utility reproduced by the single-loop shortcut" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPP-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-evppi-for-the-utility-reproduced-by-the-single-loop-shortcut" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(MAX(200+1800*0.5,0)+MAX(-2400+3400*0.5,0))/2-MAX((200+1800*0.5-2400+3400*0.5)/2,0)=350" .

hemo:7003955 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with the utility at its mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Illustrative, from the article's example, with the utility B coded as an indicator that is 1 when high and has a mean of 0.5. Given high A the incremental net benefit is GBP 1,000 plus GBP 1,000 times the indicator, and given low A it is GBP -2,400 plus GBP 2,600 times the indicator. At the mean these give GBP 1,500 and GBP -1,100, and the shortcut returns GBP 550, the same as the nested estimator, because the model is linear in the indicator." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's EVPPI for the treatment effect with the utility at its mean" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K = 2; alpha_k = [1000,-2400]; beta_k = [1000,2600]; mu_c = 0.5; ibar_k = [1500,-1100]; EVPPI_1L = 550" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPP-004" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-evppi-for-the-treatment-effect-with-the-utility-at-its-mean" .

hemo:7003956 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's EVPPI for the utility with the treatment effect at its mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the treatment effect A coded as an indicator with a mean of 0.5, the incremental net benefit is GBP 200 plus GBP 1,800 times the indicator given high B and GBP -2,400 plus GBP 3,400 times the indicator given low B. At the mean these give GBP 1,100 and GBP -700, and the shortcut returns the article's EVPPI for B of GBP 350." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's EVPPI for the utility with the treatment effect at its mean" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K = 2; alpha_k = [200,-2400]; beta_k = [1800,3400]; mu_c = 0.5; ibar_k = [1100,-700]; EVPPI_1L = 350" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPP-005" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-evppi-for-the-utility-with-the-treatment-effect-at-its-mean" .

hemo:7003957 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's adverse-event cost that never changes the decision"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Limiting case. The article's third parameter moves incremental net benefit by GBP 100 up or down and adds to the part that depends on A and B, whose mean is GBP 200. Both plug-in values, GBP 300 and GBP 100, favour the new treatment, so the decision never changes and the EVPPI is zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's adverse-event cost that never changes the decision" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K = 2; alpha_k = [100,-100]; beta_k = [1,1]; mu_c = 200; ibar_k = [300,100]; EVPPI_1L = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPP-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-adverse-event-cost-that-never-changes-the-decision" .

hemo:7003958 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Regression captures the conditional mean of net benefit given theta_i"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The fitted value at each run estimates the expectation of incremental net benefit over theta_c given theta_i at that run. The regression must therefore be flexible enough for the shape of that relationship, including interactions within theta_i, and Strong, Oakley and Brennan inspect residual plots for each fit." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Regression captures the conditional mean of net benefit given theta_i" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPP-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "regression-captures-the-conditional-mean-of-net-benefit-given-theta-i" .

hemo:7003959 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "One probabilistic sample from the joint distribution for regression EVPPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The N runs are draws from the joint distribution of all parameters, correlated or not, with the net benefit of every option computed at each run, and the same runs give the EVPI used as the upper bound. Strong, Oakley and Brennan note that only the joint distribution is required, even when inputs are correlated." ;
    hemo:9000009 "One probabilistic sample from the joint distribution for regression EVPPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-EVPP-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "one-probabilistic-sample-from-the-joint-distribution-for-regression-evppi" .

hemo:7003960 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "Regression-based EVPPI from columns of fitted values"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000657 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the fitted incremental net benefits of options 2 and 3 against option 1 in ranges named FitInc2 and FitInc3, the first formula returns the estimate in Excel 365. A linear least squares regression on the columns of theta_i in a range named ThetaI gives the fitted values of the raw incremental net benefits in RawInc2 with TREND, as in the second formula, entered as a spill range. A flexible regression such as a generalised additive model is fitted outside Excel and its fitted values pasted in." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Regression-based EVPPI from columns of fitted values" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-EVPP-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "regression-based-evppi-from-columns-of-fitted-values" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LET(m,BYROW(HSTACK(FitInc2,FitInc3),LAMBDA(x,MAX(0,x))),AVERAGE(m)-MAX(0,AVERAGE(FitInc2),AVERAGE(FitInc3))); =TREND(RawInc2,ThetaI)" .

hemo:7003961 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Regression-based EVPPI estimate no larger than the EVPI from the same sample"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the estimate in a cell named EVPPIreg, the EVPI from the raw net benefits of the same runs (HE-FM-VOI-001) in EVPIraw and a stated tolerance in MCTol, the estimate is at least zero and no more than the EVPI plus the tolerance. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows fitted values out of row order with the sample or a regression that overfits the noise." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Regression-based EVPPI estimate no larger than the EVPI from the same sample" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPP-006" ;
    hemo:9000023 "regression-based-evppi-estimate-no-larger-than-the-evpi-from-the-same-sample" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(EVPPIreg>=0,EVPPIreg<=EVPIraw+MCTol)" .

hemo:7003962 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fitted incremental net benefits keep the sample mean"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a least squares regression, or a Gaussian additive model with an identity link, that includes an intercept, the mean of the fitted values equals the mean of the raw incremental net benefits in RawInc2. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows a regression fitted without an intercept or fitted values taken from another sample." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fitted incremental net benefits keep the sample mean" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPP-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fitted-incremental-net-benefits-keep-the-sample-mean" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AVERAGE(FitInc2)-AVERAGE(RawInc2))<1E-6" .

hemo:7003963 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Illustrative three-option regression EVPPI reproduced"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The fitted values of the first worked example return GBP 325. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows zero for the baseline left out of the maximum for each run." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Illustrative three-option regression EVPPI reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-EVPP-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "illustrative-three-option-regression-evppi-reproduced" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=(MAX(0,900,400)+MAX(0,300,700)+MAX(0,-200,100)+MAX(0,-600,-900))/4-MAX(0,(900+300-200-600)/4,(400+700+100-900)/4)=325" .

hemo:7003964 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Illustrative three-option regression EVPPI from four fitted runs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "All values are illustrative. Over four equally weighted runs the fitted incremental net benefits are GBP 900, 300, -200 and -600 for option 2 and GBP 400, 700, 100 and -900 for option 3. The largest of zero and the two fitted values averages GBP 425, the best mean is option 2's GBP 100, and the estimate is GBP 325." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Illustrative three-option regression EVPPI from four fitted runs" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N = 4; g_2n = [900,300,-200,-600]; g_3n = [400,700,100,-900]; EVPPI_R = 325" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPP-007" ;
    hemo:9000023 "illustrative-three-option-regression-evppi-from-four-fitted-runs" .

hemo:7003965 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fitted values equal to the model outputs return the EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Limiting case, illustrative. If the regression reproduces every model output, as a regression on all parameters can, the fitted values are the raw incremental net benefits, here GBP 1,300, 500, -600 and -800 for option 2 and GBP 100, 1,100, 300 and -1,200 for option 3, with the same means as in the first example. The estimate is then the EVPI from these runs, GBP 575." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Fitted values equal to the model outputs return the EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N = 4; g_2n = [1300,500,-600,-800]; g_3n = [100,1100,300,-1200]; EVPPI_R = 575" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPP-008" ;
    hemo:9000023 "fitted-values-equal-to-the-model-outputs-return-the-evpi" .

hemo:7003966 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Parameters of interest unrelated to net benefit give zero regression EVPPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Limiting case. When the regression finds no relationship, every fitted value equals the mean of its option, GBP 100 for option 2 and GBP 75 for option 3, the same option is best at every run and the estimate is zero." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Parameters of interest unrelated to net benefit give zero regression EVPPI" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N = 4; g_2n = [100,100,100,100]; g_3n = [75,75,75,75]; EVPPI_R = 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-EVPP-009" ;
    hemo:9000023 "parameters-of-interest-unrelated-to-net-benefit-give-zero-regression-evppi" .

hemo:7003967 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Study result informs only the decision being modelled"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Rothery and colleagues state that ENBS of zero or more is a necessary condition for conducting a study only under the assumption that the study is relevant to this decision alone and has no wider value. A study that would also inform other decisions or jurisdictions can be worth more than its ENBS for this decision." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Study result informs only the decision being modelled" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ENBS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "study-result-informs-only-the-decision-being-modelled" .

hemo:7003968 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Beneficiary population counted once the study reports"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The population behind EVSI_pop, N people a year for Y years in HE-FM-EVSI-004, counts only the people whose treatment follows the result, adjusted for the time the study takes to finish, as Fenwick and colleagues recommend. Eckermann and Willan show that time for accrual, follow-up and analysis lowers EVSI and the expected net gain at any trial size. The article holds the discounted population at 8,000 for every design, a simplification since larger trials take longer." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Beneficiary population counted once the study reports" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ENBS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "beneficiary-population-counted-once-the-study-reports" .

hemo:7003969 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "EVSI and study cost on one net benefit scale at a stated threshold"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "EVSI_pop and C_n are both in net monetary benefit or both in net health benefit, valued at the same cost-effectiveness threshold. Rothery and colleagues ask for value of information results at explicit thresholds or as a function of the threshold, so ENBS is reported in the same way." ;
    hemo:9000009 "EVSI and study cost on one net benefit scale at a stated threshold" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-AS-ENBS-003" ;
    hemo:9000023 "evsi-and-study-cost-on-one-net-benefit-scale-at-a-stated-threshold" .

hemo:7003970 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "ENBS of one design from population EVSI in Excel"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000004 hemo:5000658 ;
    hemo:1000040 hemo:4000019 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the design's population EVSI from HE-FM-EVSI-004 in PopulationEVSI and its expected total cost from HE-FM-ENBS-002 in StudyCost, the cell subtracts the cost from the population value." ;
    hemo:9000009 "ENBS of one design from population EVSI in Excel" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-IM-ENBS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "enbs-of-one-design-from-population-evsi-in-excel" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PopulationEVSI-StudyCost" .

hemo:7003971 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's 600-patient ENBS rebuilt from its inputs"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000010 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Rebuilding the 600-patient row of the article's table from its per-person EVSI, its discounted population and its three cost components returns GBP 940,000. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a cost component dropped or the participant loss charged to every participant." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Article's 600-patient ENBS rebuilt from its inputs" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ENBS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "article-s-600-patient-enbs-rebuilt-from-its-inputs" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(300*8000-(200000+2000*600+0.5*600*200)-940000)<0.5" .

hemo:7003972 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Per-person EVSI of a design not above per-person EVPI"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "No finite study yields perfect information, so the per-person EVSI of any design is at most the per-person EVPI of HE-FM-VOI-001 at the same threshold, GBP 300 against GBP 400 in the article. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows simulation error in the EVSI estimate or the two values computed at different thresholds or on different scales." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Per-person EVSI of a design not above per-person EVPI" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-VT-ENBS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "per-person-evsi-of-a-design-not-above-per-person-evpi" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PerPersonEVSI<=PerPersonEVPI" .

hemo:7003973 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "ENBS of the article's 600-patient trial with a discounted population of 8,000"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:1000037 hemo:7003974,
        hemo:7003975 ;
    hemo:1000038 hemo:7003976 ;
    hemo:2000008 0.5 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In the article's illustrative example the 600-patient trial has a per-person EVSI of GBP 300 and a discounted population of 8,000, so its population EVSI is GBP 2,400,000 (HE-FM-EVSI-004). The study costs GBP 1,460,000, so ENBS is GBP 940,000, the largest of the article's four designs." ;
    hemo:9000009 "ENBS of the article's 600-patient trial with a discounted population of 8,000" ;
    hemo:9000014 "EVSI_pop = 2400000; C_n = 1460000; ENBS = 940000" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-EX-ENBS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "enbs-of-the-article-s-600-patient-trial-with-a-discounted-population-of-8-000" .

hemo:7003974 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "EVSI_pop in the test ENBS of the article's 600-patient trial with a discounted population of 8,000"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000039 hemo:6002849 ;
    rheo:2000001 2400000.0 .

