hemo:7007062 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Start-of-year factor sum equals the end-of-year sum times one plus the rate (HE-CF-DISC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Moving every year one period earlier multiplies each factor by (1 + r). The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(SUM((1+DiscRate)^-(SEQUENCE(Years)-1))-(1+DiscRate)*SUM((1+DiscRate)^-SEQUENCE(Years)))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUM((1+DiscRate)^-(SEQUENCE(Years)-1))-(1+DiscRate)*SUM((1+DiscRate)^-SEQUENCE(Years)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007063 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Common rate on a spread cost leaves the ratio unchanged (HE-CF-DISC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When a yearly cost falls in the same years as the gain, discounting both at one rate leaves the ratio at the undiscounted value, as the article notes for a lifelong drug. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(PV(DiscRate,Years,-YearlyCost)/PV(DiscRate,Years,-YearlyQALYs)-YearlyCost/YearlyQALYs)<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(PV(DiscRate,Years,-YearlyCost)/PV(DiscRate,Years,-YearlyQALYs)-YearlyCost/YearlyQALYs)<1E-9" .

hemo:7007064 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Retinal camera and screener training over 2,500 screens (HE-CF-ANLS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The camera at GBP 50,000 with a GBP 5,000 resale value over 5 years and training at GBP 12,000 repeated every 4 years give annual charges of about GBP 10,142 and GBP 3,267 at 3.5%, or about GBP 5.36 per screen over 2,500 screens, against GBP 4.80 per screen on a straight-line basis, about 12% higher. `K_1 = 50000; S_1 = 5000; n_1 = 5; K_2 = 12000; S_2 = 0; n_2 = 4; r = 0.035; Q = 2500; A_1 = 4.51505; A_2 = 3.67308; E_1 = 10141.66; E_2 = 3267.01; E_total = 13408.68; c_unit = 5.3635; c_SL = 4.80`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K_1 = 50000; S_1 = 5000; n_1 = 5; K_2 = 12000; S_2 = 0; n_2 = 4; r = 0.035; Q = 2500; A_1 = 4.51505; A_2 = 3.67308; E_1 = 10141.66; E_2 = 3267.01; E_total = 13408.68; c_unit = 5.3635; c_SL = 4.80" .

hemo:7007065 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Camera alone with no training cost (HE-CF-ANLS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Setting the training price to zero leaves only the camera's charge of about GBP 10,142 a year, or about GBP 4.06 per screen, a limiting case that checks that each input is annualised separately. `K_1 = 50000; S_1 = 5000; n_1 = 5; K_2 = 0; S_2 = 0; n_2 = 4; r = 0.035; Q = 2500; A_1 = 4.51505; A_2 = 3.67308; E_1 = 10141.66; E_2 = 0; E_total = 10141.66; c_unit = 4.0567; c_SL = 3.60`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K_1 = 50000; S_1 = 5000; n_1 = 5; K_2 = 0; S_2 = 0; n_2 = 4; r = 0.035; Q = 2500; A_1 = 4.51505; A_2 = 3.67308; E_1 = 10141.66; E_2 = 0; E_total = 10141.66; c_unit = 4.0567; c_SL = 3.60" .

hemo:7007066 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Economic cost per unit exceeds the straight-line cost per unit (HE-CF-ANLS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At a rate above zero the annualised charges sum to more than the straight-line charges for any inputs with a positive price. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=SUMPRODUCT((Price-Resale*(1+Rate)^-Life)/((1-(1+Rate)^-Life)/Rate))>SUMPRODUCT((Price-Resale)/Life)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT((Price-Resale*(1+Rate)^-Life)/((1-(1+Rate)^-Life)/Rate))>SUMPRODUCT((Price-Resale)/Life)" .

hemo:7007067 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's capital cost per screen reproduced (HE-CF-ANLS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The camera and training inputs return GBP 5.36 per screen when rounded to the penny. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ROUND(SUMPRODUCT(({50000;12000}-{5000;0}*1.035^-{5;4})/((1-1.035^-{5;4})/0.035))/2500,2)=5.36`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(SUMPRODUCT(({50000;12000}-{5000;0}*1.035^-{5;4})/((1-1.035^-{5;4})/0.035))/2500,2)=5.36" .

hemo:7007068 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Camera in its first year (HE-CF-ANLS-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In year 1 the full GBP 50,000 is tied up, so the return at 3.5% is GBP 1,750 and the remaining GBP 9,324 of the GBP 11,074 charge recovers part of the price. `K = 50000; r = 0.035; n = 5; t = 1; A = 4.51505; E = 11074.07; B_t = 50000; R_t = 1750; P_t = 9324.07`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K = 50000; r = 0.035; n = 5; t = 1; A = 4.51505; E = 11074.07; B_t = 50000; R_t = 1750; P_t = 9324.07" .

hemo:7007069 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Camera in its final year (HE-CF-ANLS-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In year 5 about GBP 10,700 is still tied up, the return is about GBP 374 and the recovered part, about GBP 10,700, clears the balance, as in the article's table. `K = 50000; r = 0.035; n = 5; t = 5; A = 4.51505; E = 11074.07; B_t = 10699.58; R_t = 374.49; P_t = 10699.58`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "K = 50000; r = 0.035; n = 5; t = 5; A = 4.51505; E = 11074.07; B_t = 10699.58; R_t = 374.49; P_t = 10699.58" .

hemo:7007070 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Recovered parts sum to the price (HE-CF-ANLS-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Over the useful life the recovered parts add up to the purchase price. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(-CUMPRINC(DiscountRate,UsefulLife,CapitalPrice,1,UsefulLife,0)-CapitalPrice)<0.01`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(-CUMPRINC(DiscountRate,UsefulLife,CapitalPrice,1,UsefulLife,0)-CapitalPrice)<0.01" .

hemo:7007071 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Returns sum to the total charges less the price (HE-CF-ANLS-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Over 5 years the camera's returns sum to about GBP 5,370, five charges of GBP 11,074 less the GBP 50,000 price. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(-CUMIPMT(DiscountRate,UsefulLife,CapitalPrice,1,UsefulLife,0)-(UsefulLife*PMT(DiscountRate,UsefulLife,-CapitalPrice)-CapitalPrice))<0.01`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(-CUMIPMT(DiscountRate,UsefulLife,CapitalPrice,1,UsefulLife,0)-(UsefulLife*PMT(DiscountRate,UsefulLife,-CapitalPrice)-CapitalPrice))<0.01" .

hemo:7007072 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's 5% baseline risk population (HE-CF-MREG-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With d of -0.40, b of 0.30 and x_bar of -1.70, a 5% baseline risk gives an odds ratio of about 0.462 and 26.3 events avoided per 1,000. At GBP 300 per person, GBP 2,000 saved and 0.5 QALYs gained per event avoided, the ICER is about GBP 18,800 per QALY, as in the article. `p_0 = 0.05; d = -0.40; b = 0.30; x_bar = -1.70; c_tx = 300; s_ev = 2000; q_ev = 0.5; z = -2.9444; theta_z = -0.7733; OR_z = 0.4615; p_1 = 0.02371; N_av = 26.29; C_net = 247424; Q_gain = 13.144; ICER = 18824`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_0 = 0.05; d = -0.40; b = 0.30; x_bar = -1.70; c_tx = 300; s_ev = 2000; q_ev = 0.5; z = -2.9444; theta_z = -0.7733; OR_z = 0.4615; p_1 = 0.02371; N_av = 26.29; C_net = 247424; Q_gain = 13.144; ICER = 18824" .

hemo:7007073 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Zero interaction returns the unadjusted result (HE-CF-MREG-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With b set to 0 the odds ratio stays at about 0.670 whatever the baseline risk, giving 15.9 events avoided per 1,000 and an ICER of about GBP 33,700 per QALY, the article's result with the unadjusted effect. `p_0 = 0.05; d = -0.40; b = 0; x_bar = -1.70; c_tx = 300; s_ev = 2000; q_ev = 0.5; z = -2.9444; theta_z = -0.40; OR_z = 0.6703; p_1 = 0.03408; N_av = 15.92; C_net = 268155; Q_gain = 7.961; ICER = 33683`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "p_0 = 0.05; d = -0.40; b = 0; x_bar = -1.70; c_tx = 300; s_ev = 2000; q_ev = 0.5; z = -2.9444; theta_z = -0.40; OR_z = 0.6703; p_1 = 0.03408; N_av = 15.92; C_net = 268155; Q_gain = 7.961; ICER = 33683" .

hemo:7007074 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Effect at the trials' mean risk equals d (HE-CF-MREG-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Setting the baseline risk to the risk whose log-odds is x_bar returns an adjusted log odds ratio equal to d. Expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(B2+B3*(LN((1/(1+EXP(-B4)))/(1-1/(1+EXP(-B4))))-B4)-B2)<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(B2+B3*(LN((1/(1+EXP(-B4)))/(1-1/(1+EXP(-B4))))-B4)-B2)<1E-9" .

hemo:7007075 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Protective adjusted effect lowers the treated risk (HE-CF-MREG-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When the adjusted log odds ratio is negative, the treated risk is below the baseline risk and the events avoided are positive. Expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=IF(B10<0,AND(B12<B1,B13>0),TRUE)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=IF(B10<0,AND(B12<B1,B13>0),TRUE)" .

hemo:7007076 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's 0.8 QALYs a year for 30 years with alpha of 0.035 (HE-CF-HYPD-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The hyperbolic total is about 16.20 QALYs against 14.71 under constant discounting at 3.5%, the HE-FM-DISC-001 value, about 10% more (computed here for illustration). `q = 0.8; T = 30; alpha = 0.035; S_H = 20.255833; S_E = 18.392045; Q_H = 16.204666; Q_E = 14.713636; ratio = 1.101337`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q = 0.8; T = 30; alpha = 0.035; S_H = 20.255833; S_E = 18.392045; Q_H = 16.204666; Q_E = 14.713636; ratio = 1.101337" .

hemo:7007077 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Twelve months of 1 unit with alpha of 0.4 a month (HE-CF-HYPD-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At the steep monthly parameter of the article's smoker, a year of monthly gains is worth about 4.01 units under the hyperbola against 2.46 under the constant rate (computed here for illustration). `q = 1; T = 12; alpha = 0.4; S_H = 4.012697; S_E = 2.455904; Q_H = 4.012697; Q_E = 2.455904; ratio = 1.633898`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q = 1; T = 12; alpha = 0.4; S_H = 4.012697; S_E = 2.455904; Q_H = 4.012697; Q_E = 2.455904; ratio = 1.633898" .

hemo:7007078 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Zero parameter returns the undiscounted total (HE-CF-HYPD-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha = 0 every weight is 1, so both totals equal q times T, a limiting case that checks the implementation. `q = 0.8; T = 30; alpha = 0; S_H = 30; S_E = 30; Q_H = 24; Q_E = 24; ratio = 1`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q = 0.8; T = 30; alpha = 0; S_H = 30; S_E = 30; Q_H = 24; Q_E = 24; ratio = 1" .

hemo:7007079 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Hyperbolic total never below the constant-rate total (HE-CF-HYPD-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Each hyperbolic weight is at least the constant-rate factor for whole periods, so the ratio is 1 or more. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=SUM(1/(1+HypAlpha*SEQUENCE(Years)))>=SUM((1+HypAlpha)^-SEQUENCE(Years))-1E-12`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUM(1/(1+HypAlpha*SEQUENCE(Years)))>=SUM((1+HypAlpha)^-SEQUENCE(Years))-1E-12" .

hemo:7007080 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant-rate sum matches Excel PV (HE-CF-HYPD-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The sum of the constant-rate factors equals the end-of-period annuity of HE-FM-DISC-001. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(SUM((1+HypAlpha)^-SEQUENCE(Years))-PV(HypAlpha,Years,-1))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUM((1+HypAlpha)^-SEQUENCE(Years))-PV(HypAlpha,Years,-1))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007081 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's quasi-hyperbolic smoker (HE-CF-HYPD-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Smoking wins today by 0.991, quitting wins for next month, and the penalty and reward thresholds are 0.991 and about 1.430, as in the article. `a = 10; b = 13; beta = 0.7; delta = 0.99; w_1 = 0.693; w_2 = 0.68607; M_0 = -0.991; M_1 = 1.98891; P = 0.991; R = 1.430014`. The first delay at which waiting wins is 1." ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 10; b = 13; beta = 0.7; delta = 0.99; w_1 = 0.693; w_2 = 0.68607; M_0 = -0.991; M_1 = 1.98891; P = 0.991; R = 1.430014" .

hemo:7007082 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's simple hyperbolic smoker (HE-CF-HYPD-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With alpha = 0.4 the plan also reverses, and the reward needed is exactly 1 unit, 10 divided by 0.714286 minus 13 (computed here for illustration). The values come from the R and Python code, since the calculator line follows the quasi-hyperbolic path. `a = 10; b = 13; alpha = 0.4; w_1 = 0.714286; w_2 = 0.555556; M_0 = -0.714286; M_1 = 0.079365; P = 0.714286; R = 1`. The first delay at which waiting wins is 1." ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 10; b = 13; alpha = 0.4; w_1 = 0.714286; w_2 = 0.555556; M_0 = -0.714286; M_1 = 0.079365; P = 0.714286; R = 1" .

hemo:7007083 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Impatient exponential smoker with delta of 0.75 (HE-CF-HYPD-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Waiting never wins at any delay, so no plan to quit is formed and there is nothing to reverse. `a = 10; b = 13; beta = 1; delta = 0.75; w_1 = 0.75; w_2 = 0.5625; M_0 = -0.25; M_1 = -0.1875; P = 0.25; R = 0.333333`." ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 10; b = 13; beta = 1; delta = 0.75; w_1 = 0.75; w_2 = 0.5625; M_0 = -0.25; M_1 = -0.1875; P = 0.25; R = 0.333333" .

hemo:7007084 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Patient exponential smoker with delta of 0.99 (HE-CF-HYPD-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Waiting wins today, so both thresholds are zero, a limiting case. `a = 10; b = 13; beta = 1; delta = 0.99; w_1 = 0.99; w_2 = 0.9801; M_0 = 2.87; M_1 = 2.8413; P = 0; R = 0`." ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 10; b = 13; beta = 1; delta = 0.99; w_1 = 0.99; w_2 = 0.9801; M_0 = 2.87; M_1 = 2.8413; P = 0; R = 0" .

hemo:7007085 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reward threshold equals the penalty divided by the one-period weight (HE-CF-HYPD-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The timing premium 1/w_1 links the two thresholds, 1.443 for the article's quasi-hyperbolic smoker. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=ABS((10/(0.7*0.99)-13)-(10-13*0.7*0.99)/(0.7*0.99))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((10/(0.7*0.99)-13)-(10-13*0.7*0.99)/(0.7*0.99))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007086 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Constant-rate weights never reverse (HE-CF-HYPD-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For delta = 0.75 and 0.99 the two margins share a sign. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=AND((13*0.75-10)*(13*0.75^2-10*0.75)>0,(13*0.99-10)*(13*0.99^2-10*0.99)>0)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND((13*0.75-10)*(13*0.75^2-10*0.75)>0,(13*0.99-10)*(13*0.99^2-10*0.99)>0)" .

hemo:7007087 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Trial of 100 patients per arm (HE-CF-EVSI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the illustrative prior mean of GBP 500 and standard deviation of GBP 1,000, arm standard deviations of GBP 10,000, and 2,000 patients a year for five years at an illustrative 3.5%, the trial is worth about GBP 61.68 per patient, about 31% of EVPI, and about GBP 576,507 across the population. `m0 = 500; sd0 = 1000; sd_A = 10000; sd_B = 10000; n = 100; N = 2000; Y = 5; r = 0.035; Q_s = 0.19323812; Q_0 = 0.30853754; v0 = 1000000; sigma2 = 200000000; n0 = 200; nu = 0.333333; s2 = 333333.33; s = 577.350269; z_s = 0.866025; phi_s = 0.274189; EVSI = 61.68; z_0 = 0.5; phi_0 = 0.352065; EVPI = 197.8; share = 0.3119; D = 4.673079; EVSI_pop = 576507.41`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m0 = 500; sd0 = 1000; sd_A = 10000; sd_B = 10000; n = 100; N = 2000; Y = 5; r = 0.035; Q_s = 0.19323812; Q_0 = 0.30853754; v0 = 1000000; sigma2 = 200000000; n0 = 200; nu = 0.333333; s2 = 333333.33; s = 577.350269; z_s = 0.866025; phi_s = 0.274189; EVSI = 61.68; z_0 = 0.5; phi_0 = 0.352065; EVPI = 197.8; share = 0.3119; D = 4.673079; EVSI_pop = 576507.41" .

hemo:7007088 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Trial of 400 patients per arm (HE-CF-EVSI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Quadrupling the trial raises EVSI to about GBP 134.97 per patient, about 68% of EVPI, and population EVSI to about GBP 1.26 million, so value rises with n but less than in proportion. `m0 = 500; sd0 = 1000; sd_A = 10000; sd_B = 10000; n = 400; N = 2000; Y = 5; r = 0.035; Q_s = 0.27014569; Q_0 = 0.30853754; v0 = 1000000; sigma2 = 200000000; n0 = 200; nu = 0.666667; s2 = 666666.67; s = 816.496581; z_s = 0.612372; phi_s = 0.330735; EVSI = 134.97; z_0 = 0.5; phi_0 = 0.352065; EVPI = 197.8; share = 0.6824; D = 4.673079; EVSI_pop = 1261460`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m0 = 500; sd0 = 1000; sd_A = 10000; sd_B = 10000; n = 400; N = 2000; Y = 5; r = 0.035; Q_s = 0.27014569; Q_0 = 0.30853754; v0 = 1000000; sigma2 = 200000000; n0 = 200; nu = 0.666667; s2 = 666666.67; s = 816.496581; z_s = 0.612372; phi_s = 0.330735; EVSI = 134.97; z_0 = 0.5; phi_0 = 0.352065; EVPI = 197.8; share = 0.6824; D = 4.673079; EVSI_pop = 1261460" .

hemo:7007089 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Options equally preferred now (HE-CF-EVSI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a prior mean of zero, EVSI is about GBP 230.33 and EVPI about GBP 398.94 per patient, and the share equals the square root of the variance fraction, about 0.5774, a limiting case that checks the implementation. `m0 = 0; sd0 = 1000; sd_A = 10000; sd_B = 10000; n = 100; N = 2000; Y = 5; r = 0.035; Q_s = 0.5; Q_0 = 0.5; v0 = 1000000; sigma2 = 200000000; n0 = 200; nu = 0.333333; s2 = 333333.33; s = 577.350269; z_s = 0; phi_s = 0.398942; EVSI = 230.33; z_0 = 0; phi_0 = 0.398942; EVPI = 398.94; share = 0.5774; D = 4.673079; EVSI_pop = 2152695.37`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "m0 = 0; sd0 = 1000; sd_A = 10000; sd_B = 10000; n = 100; N = 2000; Y = 5; r = 0.035; Q_s = 0.5; Q_0 = 0.5; v0 = 1000000; sigma2 = 200000000; n0 = 200; nu = 0.333333; s2 = 333333.33; s = 577.350269; z_s = 0; phi_s = 0.398942; EVSI = 230.33; z_0 = 0; phi_0 = 0.398942; EVPI = 398.94; share = 0.5774; D = 4.673079; EVSI_pop = 2152695.37" .

hemo:7007090 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Share of EVPI equals the square root of the variance fraction at a zero prior mean (HE-CF-EVSI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the options equally preferred now, EVSI divided by EVPI equals the square root of n over n plus n0, about 0.5774 for 100 per arm. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(SQRT(1E6*100/(100+2E8/1E6))*NORM.S.DIST(0,FALSE)/(1000*NORM.S.DIST(0,FALSE))-SQRT(100/300))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SQRT(1E6*100/(100+2E8/1E6))*NORM.S.DIST(0,FALSE)/(1000*NORM.S.DIST(0,FALSE))-SQRT(100/300))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007091 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Single-loop Monte Carlo agrees with the closed form (HE-CF-EVSI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 100,000 simulated trials of 100 per arm, the average shortfall of the posterior mean below zero is within GBP 3 of the closed-form GBP 61.68, a margin of more than five Monte Carlo standard errors. Expected result TRUE in Microsoft 365, recalculated with new random numbers each time. Excel check `=LET(k,100000,t,500+1000*NORM.S.INV(RANDARRAY(k)),x,t+SQRT(2E8/100)*NORM.S.INV(RANDARRAY(k)),pm,(200*500+100*x)/300,ABS(AVERAGE(IF(pm<0,-pm,0))-61.68)<3)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LET(k,100000,t,500+1000*NORM.S.INV(RANDARRAY(k)),x,t+SQRT(2E8/100)*NORM.S.INV(RANDARRAY(k)),pm,(200*500+100*x)/300,ABS(AVERAGE(IF(pm<0,-pm,0))-61.68)<3)" .

hemo:7007092 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's two subgroups at GBP 35,000 per QALY (HE-CF-EQWA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Subgroup A has 300 patients at a weight of 1.7 gaining 0.6 QALYs each for GBP 30,000, and subgroup B 700 patients at a weight of 1 gaining 0.8 QALYs for GBP 24,000, all illustrative. The total cost of GBP 25.8 million displaces about 737.1 QALYs, so the population net health benefit is about 2.9 QALYs unweighted and 128.9 weighted, the sums of the article's subgroup values. `N_1 = 300; w_1 = 1.7; dE_1 = 0.6; dC_1 = 30000; N_2 = 700; w_2 = 1; dE_2 = 0.8; dC_2 = 24000; lambda = 35000; E_u = 740; E_w = 866; C_tot = 25800000; H_d = 737.1429; NHB_u = 2.8571; NHB_w = 128.8571; ICER_u = 34864.86; ICER_w = 29792.15`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_1 = 300; w_1 = 1.7; dE_1 = 0.6; dC_1 = 30000; N_2 = 700; w_2 = 1; dE_2 = 0.8; dC_2 = 24000; lambda = 35000; E_u = 740; E_w = 866; C_tot = 25800000; H_d = 737.1429; NHB_u = 2.8571; NHB_w = 128.8571; ICER_u = 34864.86; ICER_w = 29792.15" .

hemo:7007093 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same subgroups at GBP 25,000 per QALY (HE-CF-EQWA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The displaced health rises to 1,032 QALYs, and the population net health benefit falls to minus 292 QALYs unweighted and minus 166 weighted, so the programme lowers health on both measures. `N_1 = 300; w_1 = 1.7; dE_1 = 0.6; dC_1 = 30000; N_2 = 700; w_2 = 1; dE_2 = 0.8; dC_2 = 24000; lambda = 25000; E_u = 740; E_w = 866; C_tot = 25800000; H_d = 1032; NHB_u = -292; NHB_w = -166; ICER_u = 34864.86; ICER_w = 29792.15`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_1 = 300; w_1 = 1.7; dE_1 = 0.6; dC_1 = 30000; N_2 = 700; w_2 = 1; dE_2 = 0.8; dC_2 = 24000; lambda = 25000; E_u = 740; E_w = 866; C_tot = 25800000; H_d = 1032; NHB_u = -292; NHB_w = -166; ICER_u = 34864.86; ICER_w = 29792.15" .

hemo:7007094 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Both weights set to 1 (HE-CF-EQWA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With no priority weight the weighted and unweighted results are identical, about 2.9 QALYs at GBP 35,000 per QALY, the limiting case that checks the weighting step. `N_1 = 300; w_1 = 1; dE_1 = 0.6; dC_1 = 30000; N_2 = 700; w_2 = 1; dE_2 = 0.8; dC_2 = 24000; lambda = 35000; E_u = 740; E_w = 740; C_tot = 25800000; H_d = 737.1429; NHB_u = 2.8571; NHB_w = 2.8571; ICER_u = 34864.86; ICER_w = 34864.86`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_1 = 300; w_1 = 1; dE_1 = 0.6; dC_1 = 30000; N_2 = 700; w_2 = 1; dE_2 = 0.8; dC_2 = 24000; lambda = 35000; E_u = 740; E_w = 740; C_tot = 25800000; H_d = 737.1429; NHB_u = 2.8571; NHB_w = 2.8571; ICER_u = 34864.86; ICER_w = 34864.86" .

hemo:7007095 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted minus unweighted net health benefit equals the extra weighted gain (HE-CF-EQWA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The difference is the sum over groups of patients times weight minus 1 times QALY gain, 300 × 0.7 × 0.6 = 126 QALYs in the article's example, at any value of a QALY. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ABS((SUMPRODUCT(GroupSize,EquityWeight,QALYGainPerPatient)-SUMPRODUCT(GroupSize,QALYGainPerPatient))-SUMPRODUCT(GroupSize,EquityWeight-1,QALYGainPerPatient))<0.000001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((SUMPRODUCT(GroupSize,EquityWeight,QALYGainPerPatient)-SUMPRODUCT(GroupSize,QALYGainPerPatient))-SUMPRODUCT(GroupSize,EquityWeight-1,QALYGainPerPatient))<0.000001" .

hemo:7007096 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's weighted population net health benefit reproduced (HE-CF-EQWA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The two subgroups give 128.9 weighted QALYs at GBP 35,000 per QALY when rounded to one decimal place. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ROUND(SUMPRODUCT({300;700},{1.7;1},{0.6;0.8})-SUMPRODUCT({300;700},{30000;24000})/35000,1)=128.9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(SUMPRODUCT({300;700},{1.7;1},{0.6;0.8})-SUMPRODUCT({300;700},{30000;24000})/35000,1)=128.9" .

hemo:7007097 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's programme discounted at 3 per cent (HE-CF-DALY-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The cohort of 200 incurs 960.37 DALYs without and 363.41 with the programme, so the programme averts 596.95 DALYs at about USD 744 each, and deaths prevented supply about 50% of the gain. The article shows 960.35 and 596.94 because it multiplies factors rounded to 24.692 and 8.639. `N = 200; D_0 = 20; D_1 = 8; DW_0 = 0.3; DW_1 = 0.1; T = 10; L = 45; r = 0.03; dC = 444000; f_L = 24.691991; f_T = 8.639393; DALY_0 = 960.37; DALY_1 = 363.41; DALY_av = 596.95; share_YLL = 0.4964; CPD = 743.77`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N = 200; D_0 = 20; D_1 = 8; DW_0 = 0.3; DW_1 = 0.1; T = 10; L = 45; r = 0.03; dC = 444000; f_L = 24.691991; f_T = 8.639393; DALY_0 = 960.37; DALY_1 = 363.41; DALY_av = 596.95; share_YLL = 0.4964; CPD = 743.77" .

hemo:7007098 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same programme at a rate close to zero (HE-CF-DALY-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A rate of 0.0000001 stands in for zero, which the calculator text cannot take because it divides by r. The results return the article's undiscounted 1,440 and 552 DALYs, 888 DALYs averted with 61% from deaths prevented, and USD 500 per DALY averted, a limiting case that checks the implementation. `N = 200; D_0 = 20; D_1 = 8; DW_0 = 0.3; DW_1 = 0.1; T = 10; L = 45; r = 0.0000001; dC = 444000; f_L = 44.999899; f_T = 9.999995; DALY_0 = 1440.00; DALY_1 = 552.00; DALY_av = 888.00; share_YLL = 0.6081; CPD = 500.00`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N = 200; D_0 = 20; D_1 = 8; DW_0 = 0.3; DW_1 = 0.1; T = 10; L = 45; r = 0.0000001; dC = 444000; f_L = 44.999899; f_T = 9.999995; DALY_0 = 1440.00; DALY_1 = 552.00; DALY_av = 888.00; share_YLL = 0.6081; CPD = 500.00" .

hemo:7007099 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's undiscounted cost per DALY averted (HE-CF-DALY-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Deaths prevented give 540 DALYs averted and the change in weighted years of illness 348, so 444,000 divided by 888 returns USD 500. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(444000/((20-8)*45+(180*0.3-192*0.1)*10)-500)<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(444000/((20-8)*45+(180*0.3-192*0.1)*10)-500)<1E-9" .

hemo:7007100 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's discounted cost per DALY averted (HE-CF-DALY-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With continuous factors at 3% the ratio is USD 743.77 to the cent. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows discrete annual factors or the rate entered as 3. Excel check `=ABS(444000/((20-8)*(1-EXP(-0.03*45))/0.03+(180*0.3-192*0.1)*(1-EXP(-0.03*10))/0.03)-743.77)<0.005`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(444000/((20-8)*(1-EXP(-0.03*45))/0.03+(180*0.3-192*0.1)*(1-EXP(-0.03*10))/0.03)-743.77)<0.005" .

hemo:7007101 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK tariff, state 11223 (HE-CF-EQ3L-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The UK coefficients give 0.255, the value worked in the MVH discussion paper. `l_MO = 1; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 2; l_PD = 2; l_AD = 3; c_0 = 0.081; b_MO2 = 0.069; b_MO3 = 0.314; b_SC2 = 0.104; b_SC3 = 0.214; b_UA2 = 0.036; b_UA3 = 0.094; b_PD2 = 0.123; b_PD3 = 0.386; b_AD2 = 0.071; b_AD3 = 0.236; c_N3 = 0.269; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U = 0.255`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 1; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 2; l_PD = 2; l_AD = 3; c_0 = 0.081; b_MO2 = 0.069; b_MO3 = 0.314; b_SC2 = 0.104; b_SC3 = 0.214; b_UA2 = 0.036; b_UA3 = 0.094; b_PD2 = 0.123; b_PD3 = 0.386; b_AD2 = 0.071; b_AD3 = 0.236; c_N3 = 0.269; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U = 0.255" .

hemo:7007102 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Dutch coefficients, state 33333 (HE-CF-EQ3L-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The Dutch time trade-off coefficients of Lamers and colleagues 2006, as tabulated in the EuroQol reference volume, give minus 0.329 for the worst state, against minus 0.594 under the UK tariff. `l_MO = 3; l_SC = 3; l_UA = 3; l_PD = 3; l_AD = 3; c_0 = 0.071; b_MO2 = 0.036; b_MO3 = 0.161; b_SC2 = 0.082; b_SC3 = 0.152; b_UA2 = 0.032; b_UA3 = 0.057; b_PD2 = 0.086; b_PD3 = 0.329; b_AD2 = 0.124; b_AD3 = 0.325; c_N3 = 0.234; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U = -0.329`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 3; l_SC = 3; l_UA = 3; l_PD = 3; l_AD = 3; c_0 = 0.071; b_MO2 = 0.036; b_MO3 = 0.161; b_SC2 = 0.082; b_SC3 = 0.152; b_UA2 = 0.032; b_UA3 = 0.057; b_PD2 = 0.086; b_PD3 = 0.329; b_AD2 = 0.124; b_AD3 = 0.325; c_N3 = 0.234; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U = -0.329" .

hemo:7007103 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Full health under the UK coefficients (HE-CF-EQ3L-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "State 11111 sets both indicators to zero and scores 1, a limiting case for any coefficient set. `l_MO = 1; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 1; l_PD = 1; l_AD = 1; c_0 = 0.081; b_MO2 = 0.069; b_MO3 = 0.314; b_SC2 = 0.104; b_SC3 = 0.214; b_UA2 = 0.036; b_UA3 = 0.094; b_PD2 = 0.123; b_PD3 = 0.386; b_AD2 = 0.071; b_AD3 = 0.236; c_N3 = 0.269; D = 0; N_3 = 0; U = 1`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 1; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 1; l_PD = 1; l_AD = 1; c_0 = 0.081; b_MO2 = 0.069; b_MO3 = 0.314; b_SC2 = 0.104; b_SC3 = 0.214; b_UA2 = 0.036; b_UA3 = 0.094; b_PD2 = 0.123; b_PD3 = 0.386; b_AD2 = 0.071; b_AD3 = 0.236; c_N3 = 0.269; D = 0; N_3 = 0; U = 1" .

hemo:7007104 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "UK minimum and states below zero (HE-CF-EQ3L-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Scoring all 243 states with the UK coefficients gives a minimum of minus 0.594 at 33333 and 84 states below zero, about a third, matching the negative values printed in the tariff appendix. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=AND(ROUND(1-(0.081+0.314+0.214+0.094+0.386+0.236+0.269),3)=-0.594,ROUND(1-(0.081+0.036+0.123+0.236+0.269),3)=0.255)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(1-(0.081+0.314+0.214+0.094+0.386+0.236+0.269),3)=-0.594,ROUND(1-(0.081+0.036+0.123+0.236+0.269),3)=0.255)" .

hemo:7007105 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "N3 charged once (HE-CF-EQ3L-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For 33333 the UK utility equals 1 less the constant, the five level 3 decrements and one N3 decrement, and differs from the five-fold N3 version by four times 0.269, 1.076. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ROUND((1-1.325-0.269)-(1-1.325-5*0.269),3)=1.076`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND((1-1.325-0.269)-(1-1.325-5*0.269),3)=1.076" .

hemo:7007106 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three options at GBP 25,000 per QALY over 10 years (HE-CF-EVPI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The article's drug, with INHB values 0.10, minus 0.20, 0.30, minus 0.10 and 0.25 QALYs, is joined by an illustrative lower-dose regimen with 0.05, 0.05, 0.10, 0 and 0.10. The drug keeps the highest mean, 0.07 against 0.06, the mean of the best values is 0.14, and EVPI is 0.07 QALYs per patient, with an error probability of 0.4. For 2,000 patients a year over 10 years at 3.5% the discounted population is about 17,215, population EVPI about 1,205 QALYs and its money value about GBP 30.1 million. `B_1 = 0.10; B_2 = -0.20; B_3 = 0.30; B_4 = -0.10; B_5 = 0.25; C_1 = 0.05; C_2 = 0.05; C_3 = 0.10; C_4 = 0; C_5 = 0.10; I = 2000; Y = 10; r = 0.035; lambda = 25000; M_1 = 0.10; M_2 = 0.05; M_3 = 0.30; M_4 = 0; M_5 = 0.25; EVPI = 0.07; N_disc = 17215.37; EVPI_pop = 1205.08; EVPI_popM = 30126902.78`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "B_1 = 0.10; B_2 = -0.20; B_3 = 0.30; B_4 = -0.10; B_5 = 0.25; C_1 = 0.05; C_2 = 0.05; C_3 = 0.10; C_4 = 0; C_5 = 0.10; I = 2000; Y = 10; r = 0.035; lambda = 25000; M_1 = 0.10; M_2 = 0.05; M_3 = 0.30; M_4 = 0; M_5 = 0.25; EVPI = 0.07; N_disc = 17215.37; EVPI_pop = 1205.08; EVPI_popM = 30126902.78" .

hemo:7007107 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Dominated third option reproduces the article (HE-CF-EVPI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Giving option C a net benefit of minus 1 QALY in every draw leaves the two-option problem of the article, with EVPI of 0.06 QALYs per patient, population EVPI of about 1,033 QALYs and about GBP 25.8 million, a limiting case that checks the third option is handled correctly. `B_1 = 0.10; B_2 = -0.20; B_3 = 0.30; B_4 = -0.10; B_5 = 0.25; C_1 = -1; C_2 = -1; C_3 = -1; C_4 = -1; C_5 = -1; I = 2000; Y = 10; r = 0.035; lambda = 25000; M_1 = 0.10; M_2 = 0; M_3 = 0.30; M_4 = 0; M_5 = 0.25; EVPI = 0.06; N_disc = 17215.37; EVPI_pop = 1032.92; EVPI_popM = 25823059.53`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "B_1 = 0.10; B_2 = -0.20; B_3 = 0.30; B_4 = -0.10; B_5 = 0.25; C_1 = -1; C_2 = -1; C_3 = -1; C_4 = -1; C_5 = -1; I = 2000; Y = 10; r = 0.035; lambda = 25000; M_1 = 0.10; M_2 = 0; M_3 = 0.30; M_4 = 0; M_5 = 0.25; EVPI = 0.06; N_disc = 17215.37; EVPI_pop = 1032.92; EVPI_popM = 25823059.53" .

hemo:7007108 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Opportunity-loss and maxima forms agree (HE-CF-EVPI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For any table the mean loss of the highest-mean option equals the mean of the row maxima less the largest column mean. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(RowMax-INDEX(NB,0,MATCH(MAX(ColMeans),ColMeans,0)))/ROWS(NB)-(AVERAGE(RowMax)-MAX(ColMeans)))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(RowMax-INDEX(NB,0,MATCH(MAX(ColMeans),ColMeans,0)))/ROWS(NB)-(AVERAGE(RowMax)-MAX(ColMeans)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007109 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's population EVPI reproduced (HE-CF-EVPI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Per-person EVPI of 0.06 QALYs for 2,000 patients a year over 10 years at 3.5% gives 1,033 QALYs when rounded to the nearest QALY. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ROUND(0.06*2000*(1-1.035^-10)*1.035/0.035,0)=1033`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(0.06*2000*(1-1.035^-10)*1.035/0.035,0)=1033" .

hemo:7007110 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's treatment effect A from the four equally likely combinations (HE-CF-EVPP-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With an indicator of high A as the only column of `X` and standard care as the baseline, the fitted values are the conditional means GBP 1,500 and GBP -1,100 and the estimate is the article's GBP 550, with an EVPI of GBP 600. `X = [[1],[1],[0],[0]]; NB = [[0,2000],[0,1000],[0,200],[0,-2400]]; EVPPI = 550; EVPI = 600; ok = 1` For the Math / Code line `g_1 = 1500; g_2 = 1500; g_3 = -1100; g_4 = -1100; b_1 = 2000; b_2 = 1000; b_3 = 200; b_4 = -2400; EVPPI = 550; EVPI = 600; ok = 1`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "g_1 = 1500; g_2 = 1500; g_3 = -1100; g_4 = -1100; b_1 = 2000; b_2 = 1000; b_3 = 200; b_4 = -2400; EVPPI = 550; EVPI = 600; ok = 1" .

hemo:7007111 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's utility B (HE-CF-EVPP-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An indicator of high B returns the article's GBP 350. `X = [[1],[0],[1],[0]]; NB = [[0,2000],[0,1000],[0,200],[0,-2400]]; EVPPI = 350; EVPI = 600; ok = 1` For the Math / Code line `g_1 = 1100; g_2 = -700; g_3 = 1100; g_4 = -700; b_1 = 2000; b_2 = 1000; b_3 = 200; b_4 = -2400; EVPPI = 350; EVPI = 600; ok = 1`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "g_1 = 1100; g_2 = -700; g_3 = 1100; g_4 = -700; b_1 = 2000; b_2 = 1000; b_3 = 200; b_4 = -2400; EVPPI = 350; EVPI = 600; ok = 1" .

hemo:7007112 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "A and B together with their interaction (HE-CF-EVPP-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Columns for A, B and their product fit every output exactly, so the estimate equals the EVPI, as the article states for the pair. `X = [[1,1,1],[1,0,0],[0,1,0],[0,0,0]]; NB = [[0,2000],[0,1000],[0,200],[0,-2400]]; EVPPI = 600; EVPI = 600; ok = 1` For the Math / Code line `g_1 = 2000; g_2 = 1000; g_3 = 200; g_4 = -2400; b_1 = 2000; b_2 = 1000; b_3 = 200; b_4 = -2400; EVPPI = 600; EVPI = 600; ok = 1`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "g_1 = 2000; g_2 = 1000; g_3 = 200; g_4 = -2400; b_1 = 2000; b_2 = 1000; b_3 = 200; b_4 = -2400; EVPPI = 600; EVPI = 600; ok = 1" .

hemo:7007113 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Parameter that never changes the decision (HE-CF-EVPP-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Adding the article's adverse-event cost, which moves incremental net benefit by GBP 100 up or down, to the four combinations gives eight equally likely runs. A regression on an indicator of the adverse-event cost value alone returns an EVPPI of zero and an EVPI of GBP 600, as in the article. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=LET(g,TREND({2100;1900;1100;900;300;100;-2300;-2500},{1;0;1;0;1;0;1;0}),ROUND(AVERAGE(IF(g>0,g,0))-MAX(AVERAGE(g),0),6)=0)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LET(g,TREND({2100;1900;1100;900;300;100;-2300;-2500},{1;0;1;0;1;0;1;0}),ROUND(AVERAGE(IF(g>0,g,0))-MAX(AVERAGE(g),0),6)=0)" .

hemo:7007114 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's EVPPI for A from TREND (HE-CF-EVPP-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The four combinations with an indicator of high A return GBP 550. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=LET(g,TREND({2000;1000;200;-2400},{1;1;0;0}),ROUND(AVERAGE(IF(g>0,g,0))-MAX(AVERAGE(g),0),6)=550)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=LET(g,TREND({2000;1000;200;-2400},{1;1;0;0}),ROUND(AVERAGE(IF(g>0,g,0))-MAX(AVERAGE(g),0),6)=550)" .

hemo:7007115 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's 600-patient trial with approval with research (HE-CF-ENBS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The article's discounted population of 8,000 is entered as N of 8,000 for one year, which gives a factor of 1, and the ENBS is GBP 940,000. The 100, 300 and 1,000-patient designs give GBP 390,000, GBP 770,000 and GBP 500,000, so every design is worthwhile and 600 is the efficient size, as in the article's table. `EVSI = 300; N = 8000; Y = 1; r = 0.035; C_F = 200000; c_V = 2000; n = 600; s_inf = 0.5; INB = 200; N_w = 0; D = 1; EVSI_pop = 2400000; C_n = 1460000; ENBS = 940000`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "EVSI = 300; N = 8000; Y = 1; r = 0.035; C_F = 200000; c_V = 2000; n = 600; s_inf = 0.5; INB = 200; N_w = 0; D = 1; EVSI_pop = 2400000; C_n = 1460000; ENBS = 940000" .

hemo:7007116 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's 300-patient trial under only in research (HE-CF-ENBS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 1,000 people waiting, each forgoing GBP 200, the ENBS is GBP 570,000, against GBP 540,000 for the 600-patient trial with 2,000 waiting, so the smaller trial becomes efficient, as in the article. `EVSI = 200; N = 8000; Y = 1; r = 0.035; C_F = 200000; c_V = 2000; n = 300; s_inf = 0.5; INB = 200; N_w = 1000; D = 1; EVSI_pop = 1600000; C_n = 830000; ENBS = 570000`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "EVSI = 200; N = 8000; Y = 1; r = 0.035; C_F = 200000; c_V = 2000; n = 300; s_inf = 0.5; INB = 200; N_w = 1000; D = 1; EVSI_pop = 1600000; C_n = 830000; ENBS = 570000" .

hemo:7007117 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "600-patient trial with 2,000 people a year for five years at 3.5 per cent (HE-CF-ENBS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The factor is about 4.6731 and the ENBS about GBP 1,343,848. The 100, 300 and 1,000-patient designs give about GBP 524,616, GBP 1,039,232 and GBP 971,155, so the 600-patient trial stays efficient (computed here for illustration). `EVSI = 300; N = 2000; Y = 5; r = 0.035; C_F = 200000; c_V = 2000; n = 600; s_inf = 0.5; INB = 200; N_w = 0; D = 4.673079; EVSI_pop = 2803847.53; C_n = 1460000; ENBS = 1343847.53`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "EVSI = 300; N = 2000; Y = 5; r = 0.035; C_F = 200000; c_V = 2000; n = 600; s_inf = 0.5; INB = 200; N_w = 0; D = 4.673079; EVSI_pop = 2803847.53; C_n = 1460000; ENBS = 1343847.53" .

hemo:7007118 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "No design worthwhile for a discounted population of 1,000 (HE-CF-ENBS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The 100-patient trial has an ENBS of minus GBP 310,000 and the 300, 600 and 1,000-patient designs minus GBP 630,000, minus GBP 1,160,000 and minus GBP 1,950,000, so no sample size is returned and, in the words of Fenwick and colleagues, the current evidence should be considered sufficient for decision making (illustrative population). `EVSI = 100; N = 1000; Y = 1; r = 0.035; C_F = 200000; c_V = 2000; n = 100; s_inf = 0.5; INB = 200; N_w = 0; D = 1; EVSI_pop = 100000; C_n = 410000; ENBS = -310000`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "EVSI = 100; N = 1000; Y = 1; r = 0.035; C_F = 200000; c_V = 2000; n = 100; s_inf = 0.5; INB = 200; N_w = 0; D = 1; EVSI_pop = 100000; C_n = 410000; ENBS = -310000" .

hemo:7007119 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Efficient design has the largest ENBS on the grid (HE-CF-ENBS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the ENBS of each design in ENBSRange and the returned size in OptimalSize, the ENBS of the returned design equals the largest value. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=MAX(ENBSRange)=INDEX(ENBSRange,MATCH(OptimalSize,SampleSize,0))`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MAX(ENBSRange)=INDEX(ENBSRange,MATCH(OptimalSize,SampleSize,0))" .

hemo:7007120 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Largest ENBS within the population EVPI ceiling (HE-CF-ENBS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "No design can be worth more than population EVPI less the cost of the cheapest design, GBP 3,200,000 less GBP 410,000 in the article, with population EVPI from HE-FM-VOI-002 in PopulationEVPI and the cost of each design in StudyCostRange. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=MAX(ENBSRange)<=PopulationEVPI-MIN(StudyCostRange)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MAX(ENBSRange)<=PopulationEVPI-MIN(StudyCostRange)" .

hemo:7007121 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Illustrative trial at GBP 25,000 per QALY (HE-CF-NBA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The trial of HE-EX-NBA-001 gives INMB of GBP 1,000 per patient with a 95% interval of about minus GBP 394 to GBP 2,394, INHB of 0.04 QALYs with about minus 0.0158 to 0.0958, and a probability of about 0.920 that net benefit is positive. `E_1 = 0.80; E_0 = 0.70; C_1 = 6000; C_0 = 4500; s_E1 = 0.25; s_C1 = 3000; r_1 = 0.3; n_1 = 150; s_E0 = 0.25; s_C0 = 2500; r_0 = 0.2; n_0 = 150; lambda = 25000; z = 1.96; Delta_E = 0.10; Delta_C = 1500; R = 15000; V_E = 0.00083333; V_C = 101666.67; Cov_EC = 2.3333; INMB = 1000; SE_INMB = 711.22; M_L = -393.99; M_U = 2393.99; INHB = 0.04; SE_INHB = 0.028449; H_L = -0.015760; H_U = 0.095760; z_NB = 1.4060`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_1 = 0.80; E_0 = 0.70; C_1 = 6000; C_0 = 4500; s_E1 = 0.25; s_C1 = 3000; r_1 = 0.3; n_1 = 150; s_E0 = 0.25; s_C0 = 2500; r_0 = 0.2; n_0 = 150; lambda = 25000; z = 1.96; Delta_E = 0.10; Delta_C = 1500; R = 15000; V_E = 0.00083333; V_C = 101666.67; Cov_EC = 2.3333; INMB = 1000; SE_INMB = 711.22; M_L = -393.99; M_U = 2393.99; INHB = 0.04; SE_INHB = 0.028449; H_L = -0.015760; H_U = 0.095760; z_NB = 1.4060" .

hemo:7007122 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same trial at GBP 35,000 per QALY (HE-CF-NBA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "INMB rises to GBP 2,000 with an interval of about GBP 80 to GBP 3,920, INHB is about 0.0571 QALYs with about 0.0023 to 0.1120, and the probability that net benefit is positive is about 0.979. `E_1 = 0.80; E_0 = 0.70; C_1 = 6000; C_0 = 4500; s_E1 = 0.25; s_C1 = 3000; r_1 = 0.3; n_1 = 150; s_E0 = 0.25; s_C0 = 2500; r_0 = 0.2; n_0 = 150; lambda = 35000; z = 1.96; Delta_E = 0.10; Delta_C = 1500; R = 15000; V_E = 0.00083333; V_C = 101666.67; Cov_EC = 2.3333; INMB = 2000; SE_INMB = 979.37; M_L = 80.43; M_U = 3919.57; INHB = 0.057143; SE_INHB = 0.027982; H_L = 0.002298; H_U = 0.111988; z_NB = 2.0421`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_1 = 0.80; E_0 = 0.70; C_1 = 6000; C_0 = 4500; s_E1 = 0.25; s_C1 = 3000; r_1 = 0.3; n_1 = 150; s_E0 = 0.25; s_C0 = 2500; r_0 = 0.2; n_0 = 150; lambda = 35000; z = 1.96; Delta_E = 0.10; Delta_C = 1500; R = 15000; V_E = 0.00083333; V_C = 101666.67; Cov_EC = 2.3333; INMB = 2000; SE_INMB = 979.37; M_L = 80.43; M_U = 3919.57; INHB = 0.057143; SE_INHB = 0.027982; H_L = 0.002298; H_U = 0.111988; z_NB = 2.0421" .

hemo:7007123 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Money-scale standard error over lambda equals equation 7 (HE-CF-NBA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "SE_INMB divided by lambda equals the standard error of HE-FM-NBA-001 from the same arm summaries. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(SQRT(Threshold^2*(SdEffect1^2/ArmSize1+SdEffect0^2/ArmSize0)+SdCost1^2/ArmSize1+SdCost0^2/ArmSize0-2*Threshold*(Corr1*SdEffect1*SdCost1/ArmSize1+Corr0*SdEffect0*SdCost0/ArmSize0))/Threshold-SeINHB)<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SQRT(Threshold^2*(SdEffect1^2/ArmSize1+SdEffect0^2/ArmSize0)+SdCost1^2/ArmSize1+SdCost0^2/ArmSize0-2*Threshold*(Corr1*SdEffect1*SdCost1/ArmSize1+Corr0*SdEffect0*SdCost0/ArmSize0))/Threshold-SeINHB)<1E-9" .

hemo:7007124 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Probability at GBP 35,000 per QALY (HE-CF-NBA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The z statistic of the second worked example converts to a probability of 0.9794 that net benefit is positive. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(NORM.S.DIST(2000/979.3705,TRUE)-0.9794)<0.0001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(NORM.S.DIST(2000/979.3705,TRUE)-0.9794)<0.0001" .

hemo:7007125 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Four options A to D of the live dominance records (HE-CF-CEF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A at GBP 10,000 and 4.0 QALYs, B at GBP 13,000 and 4.3, C at GBP 18,000 and 4.5 and D at GBP 22,000 and 4.8 give ratios of GBP 10,000, 25,000 and about 13,333 per QALY. C's ratio is higher than D's, so C is removed, and D against B is GBP 18,000, which leaves A, B and D, as in HE-EX-EXD-002. At GBP 20,000 per QALY the choice is D, as in HE-EX-NMB-004. The figures are illustrative. `C_1 = 10000; Q_1 = 4.0; C_2 = 13000; Q_2 = 4.3; C_3 = 18000; Q_3 = 4.5; C_4 = 22000; Q_4 = 4.8; r_2 = 10000; r_3 = 25000; r_4 = 13333.33; exd_2 = 0; exd_3 = 1; r_42 = 18000`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_1 = 10000; Q_1 = 4.0; C_2 = 13000; Q_2 = 4.3; C_3 = 18000; Q_3 = 4.5; C_4 = 22000; Q_4 = 4.8; r_2 = 10000; r_3 = 25000; r_4 = 13333.33; exd_2 = 0; exd_3 = 1; r_42 = 18000" .

hemo:7007126 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's six rehabilitation options (HE-CF-CEF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "R2 is strictly dominated by R1, R3 is removed in the first pass of extended dominance, and R4 against R1 gives GBP 30,000 per QALY, so the frontier is R0, R1, R4 and R5. `frontier = R0, R1, R4, R5; ICER_F = 20000, 30000, 60000`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "frontier = R0, R1, R4, R5; ICER_F = 20000, 30000, 60000" .

hemo:7007127 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Four strategies on one straight line (HE-CF-CEF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Strategies at GBP 1,000, 2,000, 3,000 and 4,000 with 1.00, 1.25, 1.50 and 1.75 QALYs all have ratios of GBP 4,000 per QALY, so none is removed, a limiting case for the equal-ratio rule. `C_1 = 1000; Q_1 = 1.00; C_2 = 2000; Q_2 = 1.25; C_3 = 3000; Q_3 = 1.50; C_4 = 4000; Q_4 = 1.75; r_2 = 4000; r_3 = 4000; r_4 = 4000; exd_2 = 0; exd_3 = 0; r_42 = 4000`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_1 = 1000; Q_1 = 1.00; C_2 = 2000; Q_2 = 1.25; C_3 = 3000; Q_3 = 1.50; C_4 = 4000; Q_4 = 1.75; r_2 = 4000; r_3 = 4000; r_4 = 4000; exd_2 = 0; exd_3 = 0; r_42 = 4000" .

hemo:7007128 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Both ends of the frontier kept (HE-CF-CEF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The cheapest strategy and the strategy with the most QALYs are always on the frontier. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=AND(INDEX(FrontierCosts,1)=MIN(Costs),INDEX(FrontierQALYs,ROWS(FrontierQALYs))=MAX(QALYs))`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(INDEX(FrontierCosts,1)=MIN(Costs),INDEX(FrontierQALYs,ROWS(FrontierQALYs))=MAX(QALYs))" .

hemo:7007129 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Four-option example returns the ratio of D against B (HE-CF-CEF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "After C is removed, D against B gives GBP 18,000 per QALY, and C's ratio was higher than D's. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=AND(ROUND((22000-13000)/(4.8-4.3),0)=18000,(18000-13000)/(4.5-4.3)>(22000-18000)/(4.8-4.5))`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND((22000-13000)/(4.8-4.3),0)=18000,(18000-13000)/(4.5-4.3)>(22000-18000)/(4.8-4.5))" .

hemo:7007130 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Options A to D at GBP 20,000 per QALY (HE-CF-CEF-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The net monetary benefits are GBP 70,000, 73,000, 72,000 and 74,000, so D is chosen, as in HE-EX-NMB-004, and A, B and C give up GBP 4,000, 1,000 and 2,000 per person. `C_1 = 10000; Q_1 = 4.0; C_2 = 13000; Q_2 = 4.3; C_3 = 18000; Q_3 = 4.5; C_4 = 22000; Q_4 = 4.8; lambda = 20000; N_1 = 70000; N_2 = 73000; N_3 = 72000; N_4 = 74000; N_max = 74000; L_1 = 4000; L_2 = 1000; L_3 = 2000; L_4 = 0`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_1 = 10000; Q_1 = 4.0; C_2 = 13000; Q_2 = 4.3; C_3 = 18000; Q_3 = 4.5; C_4 = 22000; Q_4 = 4.8; lambda = 20000; N_1 = 70000; N_2 = 73000; N_3 = 72000; N_4 = 74000; N_max = 74000; L_1 = 4000; L_2 = 1000; L_3 = 2000; L_4 = 0" .

hemo:7007131 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Options A to D at the GBP 18,000 switching value (HE-CF-CEF-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "B and D tie at GBP 64,400, and C gives up GBP 1,400, the blend saving of HE-EX-EXD-003. `C_1 = 10000; Q_1 = 4.0; C_2 = 13000; Q_2 = 4.3; C_3 = 18000; Q_3 = 4.5; C_4 = 22000; Q_4 = 4.8; lambda = 18000; N_1 = 62000; N_2 = 64400; N_3 = 63000; N_4 = 64400; N_max = 64400; L_1 = 2400; L_2 = 0; L_3 = 1400; L_4 = 0`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_1 = 10000; Q_1 = 4.0; C_2 = 13000; Q_2 = 4.3; C_3 = 18000; Q_3 = 4.5; C_4 = 22000; Q_4 = 4.8; lambda = 18000; N_1 = 62000; N_2 = 64400; N_3 = 63000; N_4 = 64400; N_max = 64400; L_1 = 2400; L_2 = 0; L_3 = 1400; L_4 = 0" .

hemo:7007132 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Options A to D at a value of zero (HE-CF-CEF-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With no value placed on health the cheapest strategy has the highest net monetary benefit, a limiting case. `C_1 = 10000; Q_1 = 4.0; C_2 = 13000; Q_2 = 4.3; C_3 = 18000; Q_3 = 4.5; C_4 = 22000; Q_4 = 4.8; lambda = 0; N_1 = -10000; N_2 = -13000; N_3 = -18000; N_4 = -22000; N_max = -10000; L_1 = 0; L_2 = 3000; L_3 = 8000; L_4 = 12000`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_1 = 10000; Q_1 = 4.0; C_2 = 13000; Q_2 = 4.3; C_3 = 18000; Q_3 = 4.5; C_4 = 22000; Q_4 = 4.8; lambda = 0; N_1 = -10000; N_2 = -13000; N_3 = -18000; N_4 = -22000; N_max = -10000; L_1 = 0; L_2 = 3000; L_3 = 8000; L_4 = 12000" .

hemo:7007133 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's six options with two largest values (HE-CF-CEF-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a largest value of GBP 100,000 per QALY the search returns R0, R1, R4 and R5, the same frontier as the elimination. With GBP 35,000 it returns R0, R1 and R4, since R5 is chosen only above GBP 60,000. `lambda_max = 100000; frontier = R0, R1, R4, R5` and `lambda_max = 35000; frontier = R0, R1, R4`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "lambda_max = 35000; frontier = R0, R1, R4" .

hemo:7007134 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's choices at the two NICE values (HE-CF-CEF-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At GBP 25,000 per QALY the second option, R1, has the highest net monetary benefit and at GBP 35,000 the fifth, R4. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=AND(MATCH(MAX(25000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000}),25000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000},0)=2,MATCH(MAX(35000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000}),35000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000},0)=5)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(MATCH(MAX(25000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000}),25000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000},0)=2,MATCH(MAX(35000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000}),35000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000},0)=5)" .

hemo:7007135 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Most effective option found once the value passes its ratio (HE-CF-CEF-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At GBP 100,000 per QALY the sixth option, R5, has the highest net monetary benefit. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=MATCH(MAX(100000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000}),100000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000},0)=6`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MATCH(MAX(100000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000}),100000*{5;5.1;5.08;5.2;5.3;5.45}-{2000;4000;5500;9000;10000;19000},0)=6" .

hemo:7007136 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Programmes E and F and doing nothing (HE-CF-EET-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's illustrative shares of 0.4 and 0.6 and net gains of 0.10 and 0.60 under E, 0.50 and 0.25 under F and zero under doing nothing, the mean gains are 0.40, 0.35 and 0, E is health-maximising, F forgoes 0.05 years per person and doing nothing 0.40. `s_worse = 0.4; s_better = 0.6; g_worse_1 = 0.10; g_better_1 = 0.60; g_worse_2 = 0.50; g_better_2 = 0.25; g_worse_3 = 0; g_better_3 = 0; H_1 = 0.4; H_2 = 0.35; H_3 = 0; H_top = 0.4; F_1 = 0; F_2 = 0.05; F_3 = 0.4`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "s_worse = 0.4; s_better = 0.6; g_worse_1 = 0.10; g_better_1 = 0.60; g_worse_2 = 0.50; g_better_2 = 0.25; g_worse_3 = 0; g_better_3 = 0; H_1 = 0.4; H_2 = 0.35; H_3 = 0; H_top = 0.4; F_1 = 0; F_2 = 0.05; F_3 = 0.4" .

hemo:7007137 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "A tie at the top (HE-CF-EET-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Replacing doing nothing with an illustrative option giving 0.40 years to both groups ties it with E at a mean gain of 0.40, so both forgo zero health. `s_worse = 0.4; s_better = 0.6; g_worse_1 = 0.10; g_better_1 = 0.60; g_worse_2 = 0.50; g_better_2 = 0.25; g_worse_3 = 0.40; g_better_3 = 0.40; H_1 = 0.4; H_2 = 0.35; H_3 = 0.4; H_top = 0.4; F_1 = 0; F_2 = 0.05; F_3 = 0`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "s_worse = 0.4; s_better = 0.6; g_worse_1 = 0.10; g_better_1 = 0.60; g_worse_2 = 0.50; g_better_2 = 0.25; g_worse_3 = 0.40; g_better_3 = 0.40; H_1 = 0.4; H_2 = 0.35; H_3 = 0.4; H_top = 0.4; F_1 = 0; F_2 = 0.05; F_3 = 0" .

hemo:7007138 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's health forgone by F reproduced (HE-CF-EET-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The health forgone by F against the best of the three options is 0.05 years per person. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(MAX(SUMPRODUCT({0.4;0.6},{0.1;0.6}),SUMPRODUCT({0.4;0.6},{0.5;0.25}),0)-SUMPRODUCT({0.4;0.6},{0.5;0.25})-0.05)<0.000001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(MAX(SUMPRODUCT({0.4;0.6},{0.1;0.6}),SUMPRODUCT({0.4;0.6},{0.5;0.25}),0)-SUMPRODUCT({0.4;0.6},{0.5;0.25})-0.05)<0.000001" .

hemo:7007139 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "No option forgoes negative health (HE-CF-EET-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the forgone values held in a helper row named ForgoneRow, every value is zero or above because each is measured against the highest mean gain. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows forgone health measured against a comparator such as doing nothing, which gives minus 0.40 for E and minus 0.35 for F. Excel check `=MIN(ForgoneRow)>=0`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=MIN(ForgoneRow)>=0" .

hemo:7007140 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's tunnel model for the year after an event (HE-CF-MKA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Survival of 0.75 after one year and 0.95 a year after that gives per-cycle exit probabilities of 0.25 and then 0.05, while the constant fitted to five-year survival of 0.61088 is 0.093869, the article's 0.09387. The largest gap is about 0.156, and the fitted state's mean stay of 10.653 cycles is the article's 10.653 post-event years against 16 with the tunnel. `S_1 = 0.75; S_2 = 0.7125; S_3 = 0.676875; S_4 = 0.643031; S_5 = 0.61088; h_1 = 0.25; h_2 = 0.05; h_3 = 0.05; h_4 = 0.05; h_5 = 0.05; q_c = 0.093869; dev = 0.156131; D_c = 10.6532`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_1 = 0.75; S_2 = 0.7125; S_3 = 0.676875; S_4 = 0.643031; S_5 = 0.61088; h_1 = 0.25; h_2 = 0.05; h_3 = 0.05; h_4 = 0.05; h_5 = 0.05; q_c = 0.093869; dev = 0.156131; D_c = 10.6532" .

hemo:7007141 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's memoryless model (HE-CF-MKA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The trace of the single post-event state, 0.90613 to the powers 1 to 5 rounded to six decimals, gives per-cycle values within 0.000001 of the constant (computed here for illustration). `S_1 = 0.90613; S_2 = 0.821072; S_3 = 0.743998; S_4 = 0.674159; S_5 = 0.610875; h_1 = 0.09387; h_2 = 0.09387; h_3 = 0.09387; h_4 = 0.09387; h_5 = 0.09387; q_c = 0.09387; dev = 0.000001; D_c = 10.653`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_1 = 0.90613; S_2 = 0.821072; S_3 = 0.743998; S_4 = 0.674159; S_5 = 0.610875; h_1 = 0.09387; h_2 = 0.09387; h_3 = 0.09387; h_4 = 0.09387; h_5 = 0.09387; q_c = 0.09387; dev = 0.000001; D_c = 10.653" .

hemo:7007142 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal survival steps of 0.9 (HE-CF-MKA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Survival falling by the same factor 0.9 each cycle is geometric, so every per-cycle value is 0.1, the gap is zero and the mean stay is 10 cycles, a limiting case that checks an implementation. `S_1 = 0.9; S_2 = 0.81; S_3 = 0.729; S_4 = 0.6561; S_5 = 0.59049; h_1 = 0.1; h_2 = 0.1; h_3 = 0.1; h_4 = 0.1; h_5 = 0.1; q_c = 0.1; dev = 0; D_c = 10`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_1 = 0.9; S_2 = 0.81; S_3 = 0.729; S_4 = 0.6561; S_5 = 0.59049; h_1 = 0.1; h_2 = 0.1; h_3 = 0.1; h_4 = 0.1; h_5 = 0.1; q_c = 0.1; dev = 0; D_c = 10" .

hemo:7007143 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Geometric survival returns per-cycle values equal to the constant (HE-CF-MKA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For survival of 0.9 to the power k the second per-cycle value equals the constant fitted at five cycles. Expected result TRUE. Entering the tunnel model's 0.7125 and 0.75 in place of 0.81 and 0.9 gives 0.05 against 0.1 and FALSE. Excel check `=ABS((1-0.81/0.9)-(1-0.59049^(1/5)))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((1-0.81/0.9)-(1-0.59049^(1/5)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007144 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Fitted constant reproduces survival at the last cycle (HE-CF-MKA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Five cycles at 1 minus 0.093869 return the tunnel model's survival of 0.61088 to five decimal places. Expected result TRUE. Fitting the constant as one fifth of the five-year death probability, about 0.07782, gives 0.6669 and FALSE. Excel check `=ABS((1-0.093869)^5-0.61088)<0.00001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((1-0.093869)^5-0.61088)<0.00001" .

hemo:7007145 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's programme with equal sharing (HE-CF-DCEA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With funding giving 63.996 and 72.016 years and not funding 64 and 72, in two equal groups of an area of 100,000 people, bisection on a bracket with ends 0 and 30 returns about 11.7557. At that value, shown to four decimals, the two EDEs differ by about 0.0003 EDE QALYs across the area, against 600 at epsilon of 0. `s_1 = 0.5; s_2 = 0.5; hA_1 = 63.996; hA_2 = 72.016; hB_1 = 64; hB_2 = 72; epsilon = 11.7557; N_pop = 100000; E_A = 66.703089; E_B = 66.703089; D = -0.000000003; D_pop = -0.0003`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "s_1 = 0.5; s_2 = 0.5; hA_1 = 63.996; hA_2 = 72.016; hB_1 = 64; hB_2 = 72; epsilon = 11.7557; N_pop = 100000; E_A = 66.703089; E_B = 66.703089; D = -0.000000003; D_pop = -0.0003" .

hemo:7007146 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's programme with the 60% gradient (HE-CF-DCEA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With funding giving 63.9936 and 72.0184 years, the same search returns about 8.9526, against about 8.97 from the two-group approximation. `s_1 = 0.5; s_2 = 0.5; hA_1 = 63.9936; hA_2 = 72.0184; hB_1 = 64; hB_2 = 72; epsilon = 8.9526; N_pop = 100000; E_A = 66.984446; E_B = 66.984446; D = -0.000000015; D_pop = -0.0015`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "s_1 = 0.5; s_2 = 0.5; hA_1 = 63.9936; hA_2 = 72.0184; hB_1 = 64; hB_2 = 72; epsilon = 8.9526; N_pop = 100000; E_A = 66.984446; E_B = 66.984446; D = -0.000000015; D_pop = -0.0015" .

hemo:7007147 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "No inequality aversion at the lower end of the bracket (HE-CF-DCEA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At epsilon of 0 each EDE is the mean, and the difference is the 600 QALYs of total net health benefit, positive, while at the upper end of 30 it is negative, so the bracket contains the root. `s_1 = 0.5; s_2 = 0.5; hA_1 = 63.996; hA_2 = 72.016; hB_1 = 64; hB_2 = 72; epsilon = 0; N_pop = 100000; E_A = 68.006; E_B = 68; D = 0.006; D_pop = 600`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "s_1 = 0.5; s_2 = 0.5; hA_1 = 63.996; hA_2 = 72.016; hB_1 = 64; hB_2 = 72; epsilon = 0; N_pop = 100000; E_A = 68.006; E_B = 68; D = 0.006; D_pop = 600" .

hemo:7007148 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Critical aversion gives equal EDE health (HE-CF-DCEA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Entering the returned value in the difference formula gives a difference within 1E-9 years per person. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a search stopped after too few halvings, about 3E-6 years after 10, or a reversed sign test, which in the article's example settles at 15, where the difference is about minus 111 EDE QALYs. Excel check `=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(GroupShare,HealthOptionA^(1-CritEpsilon))^(1/(1-CritEpsilon))-SUMPRODUCT(GroupShare,HealthOptionB^(1-CritEpsilon))^(1/(1-CritEpsilon)))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(GroupShare,HealthOptionA^(1-CritEpsilon))^(1/(1-CritEpsilon))-SUMPRODUCT(GroupShare,HealthOptionB^(1-CritEpsilon))^(1/(1-CritEpsilon)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007149 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's switching values reproduced (HE-CF-DCEA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the results for equal sharing in CritEpsilonEqual and for the gradient in CritEpsilonGradient, both round to the article's 11.76 and 8.95. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the two-group approximations of 11.77 and 8.97 entered in place of the solved values. Excel check `=AND(ROUND(CritEpsilonEqual,2)=11.76,ROUND(CritEpsilonGradient,2)=8.95)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(CritEpsilonEqual,2)=11.76,ROUND(CritEpsilonGradient,2)=8.95)" .

hemo:7007150 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "GBP 1,000 a year for 100 years (HE-CF-TPR-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The standard schedule gives about GBP 28,863 and the reduced schedule GBP 33,040, so about GBP 4,176 of present value is lost to pure time preference (illustrative stream, computed here for illustration). `q = 1000; T = 100; r_1 = 0.035; r_2 = 0.03; r_3 = 0.025; z_1 = 0.03; z_2 = 0.0257; z_3 = 0.0214; n_1 = 30; n_2 = 45; n_3 = 25; A_S = 28.863363; A_Z = 33.03971; PV_S = 28863.363; PV_Z = 33039.71; W = 4176.346`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q = 1000; T = 100; r_1 = 0.035; r_2 = 0.03; r_3 = 0.025; z_1 = 0.03; z_2 = 0.0257; z_3 = 0.0214; n_1 = 30; n_2 = 45; n_3 = 25; A_S = 28.863363; A_Z = 33.03971; PV_S = 28863.363; PV_Z = 33039.71; W = 4176.346" .

hemo:7007151 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "One unit a year for 60 years (HE-CF-TPR-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Just past the 50-year trigger for the extra sensitivity analysis, the standard sum is about 25.375 and the reduced sum 28.144 (computed here for illustration). `q = 1; T = 60; r_1 = 0.035; r_2 = 0.03; r_3 = 0.025; z_1 = 0.03; z_2 = 0.0257; z_3 = 0.0214; n_1 = 30; n_2 = 30; n_3 = 0; A_S = 25.37526; A_Z = 28.143509; PV_S = 25.37526; PV_Z = 28.143509; W = 2.76825`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q = 1; T = 60; r_1 = 0.035; r_2 = 0.03; r_3 = 0.025; z_1 = 0.03; z_2 = 0.0257; z_3 = 0.0214; n_1 = 30; n_2 = 30; n_3 = 0; A_S = 25.37526; A_Z = 28.143509; PV_S = 25.37526; PV_Z = 28.143509; W = 2.76825" .

hemo:7007152 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Thirty-year horizon inside the first band (HE-CF-TPR-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "No step is reached, and the standard sum of 18.392045 is the HE-FM-DISC-001 annuity at 3.5%, a limiting case that checks the implementation. `q = 1000; T = 30; r_1 = 0.035; r_2 = 0.03; r_3 = 0.025; z_1 = 0.03; z_2 = 0.0257; z_3 = 0.0214; n_1 = 30; n_2 = 0; n_3 = 0; A_S = 18.392045; A_Z = 19.600441; PV_S = 18392.045; PV_Z = 19600.441; W = 1208.396`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q = 1000; T = 30; r_1 = 0.035; r_2 = 0.03; r_3 = 0.025; z_1 = 0.03; z_2 = 0.0257; z_3 = 0.0214; n_1 = 30; n_2 = 0; n_3 = 0; A_S = 18.392045; A_Z = 19.600441; PV_S = 18392.045; PV_Z = 19600.441; W = 1208.396" .

hemo:7007153 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Thirty-year standard sum equals the Excel PV annuity (HE-CF-TPR-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Horizon = 30 and RateNear = 0.035 the closed-form sum in a cell named SumStd equals the annuity factor of HE-FM-DISC-001. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(SumStd-PV(RateNear,30,-1))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SumStd-PV(RateNear,30,-1))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007154 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Reduced schedule gives the larger present value (HE-CF-TPR-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a positive amount and a horizon of at least one year, the present value in PVReduced exceeds that in PVStd, because every reduced rate is lower. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the two schedules swapped. Excel check `=PVReduced>PVStd`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=PVReduced>PVStd" .

hemo:7007155 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's three options at epsilon of 2 (HE-CF-SWF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's illustrative QALE values, P ranks first on the total, T on the isoelastic welfare and R on the maximin, the result of the article's steps 1 to 3. `h_P1 = 60.3; h_P2 = 68.5; h_P3 = 76.7; h_T1 = 61; h_T2 = 68.3; h_T3 = 76; h_R1 = 61.2; h_R2 = 67.6; h_R3 = 75.6; epsilon = 2; U_P = 205.5; U_T = 205.3; U_R = 204.4; W_P = -0.0442201; W_T = -0.0441926; W_R = -0.0443603; M_P = 60.3; M_T = 61; M_R = 61.2`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "h_P1 = 60.3; h_P2 = 68.5; h_P3 = 76.7; h_T1 = 61; h_T2 = 68.3; h_T3 = 76; h_R1 = 61.2; h_R2 = 67.6; h_R3 = 75.6; epsilon = 2; U_P = 205.5; U_T = 205.3; U_R = 204.4; W_P = -0.0442201; W_T = -0.0441926; W_R = -0.0443603; M_P = 60.3; M_T = 61; M_R = 61.2" .

hemo:7007156 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same options at epsilon of 0.5 (HE-CF-SWF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At low aversion P also ranks first on the isoelastic welfare, about 49.5993 against 49.5849 for T and 49.4796 for R. `h_P1 = 60.3; h_P2 = 68.5; h_P3 = 76.7; h_T1 = 61; h_T2 = 68.3; h_T3 = 76; h_R1 = 61.2; h_R2 = 67.6; h_R3 = 75.6; epsilon = 0.5; U_P = 205.5; U_T = 205.3; U_R = 204.4; W_P = 49.5993; W_T = 49.5849; W_R = 49.4796; M_P = 60.3; M_T = 61; M_R = 61.2`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "h_P1 = 60.3; h_P2 = 68.5; h_P3 = 76.7; h_T1 = 61; h_T2 = 68.3; h_T3 = 76; h_R1 = 61.2; h_R2 = 67.6; h_R3 = 75.6; epsilon = 0.5; U_P = 205.5; U_T = 205.3; U_R = 204.4; W_P = 49.5993; W_T = 49.5849; W_R = 49.4796; M_P = 60.3; M_T = 61; M_R = 61.2" .

hemo:7007157 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Epsilon of 0 returns the totals (HE-CF-SWF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With no inequality aversion each isoelastic value equals the option's total, the limiting case that checks the implementation. `h_P1 = 60.3; h_P2 = 68.5; h_P3 = 76.7; h_T1 = 61; h_T2 = 68.3; h_T3 = 76; h_R1 = 61.2; h_R2 = 67.6; h_R3 = 75.6; epsilon = 0; U_P = 205.5; U_T = 205.3; U_R = 204.4; W_P = 205.5; W_T = 205.3; W_R = 204.4; M_P = 60.3; M_T = 61; M_R = 61.2`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "h_P1 = 60.3; h_P2 = 68.5; h_P3 = 76.7; h_T1 = 61; h_T2 = 68.3; h_T3 = 76; h_R1 = 61.2; h_R2 = 67.6; h_R3 = 75.6; epsilon = 0; U_P = 205.5; U_T = 205.3; U_R = 204.4; W_P = 205.5; W_T = 205.3; W_R = 204.4; M_P = 60.3; M_T = 61; M_R = 61.2" .

hemo:7007158 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Epsilon of 0 gives the totals (HE-CF-SWF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With InequalityAversion at 0 every isoelastic value equals the option's total. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the exponent written as minus epsilon, which gives 3 for every option. Excel check `=OR(InequalityAversion<>0,SUMPRODUCT(ABS(IsoelasticByOption-TotalByOption))<1E-9)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=OR(InequalityAversion<>0,SUMPRODUCT(ABS(IsoelasticByOption-TotalByOption))<1E-9)" .

hemo:7007159 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's isoelastic ranking at epsilon of 2 (HE-CF-SWF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's options in rows ordered P, T and R and InequalityAversion at 2, T is above P and P above R in IsoelasticByOption. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the divisor 1 minus epsilon left out of the isoelastic column, which reverses the order. Excel check `=AND(InequalityAversion=2,INDEX(IsoelasticByOption,2)>INDEX(IsoelasticByOption,1),INDEX(IsoelasticByOption,1)>INDEX(IsoelasticByOption,3))`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(InequalityAversion=2,INDEX(IsoelasticByOption,2)>INDEX(IsoelasticByOption,1),INDEX(IsoelasticByOption,1)>INDEX(IsoelasticByOption,3))" .

hemo:7007160 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard constants (HE-CF-AGW-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weight exceeds 1 between about 8.46 and 55.47 years, the article's roughly 8.5 and 55.5. `C = 0.1658; beta = 0.04; x_lo = 8.4603; x_hi = 55.4732; x_peak = 25; W_lo = 1; W_hi = 1`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C = 0.1658; beta = 0.04; x_lo = 8.4603; x_hi = 55.4732; x_peak = 25; W_lo = 1; W_hi = 1" .

hemo:7007161 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Murray's 1994 constant (HE-CF-AGW-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With C = 0.16243 the span is about 8.73 to 54.53 years, which matches the 9 to 54 years that Barendregt and colleagues report for these values. `C = 0.16243; beta = 0.04; x_lo = 8.7292; x_hi = 54.532; x_peak = 25; W_lo = 1; W_hi = 1`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C = 0.16243; beta = 0.04; x_lo = 8.7292; x_hi = 54.532; x_peak = 25; W_lo = 1; W_hi = 1" .

hemo:7007162 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Crossings either side of the peak (HE-CF-AGW-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The lower crossing is below 25 and the upper above it, and the weight at each is 1 to four decimal places. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=AND(8.4603<25,55.4732>25,ABS(0.1658*8.4603*EXP(-0.04*8.4603)-1)<0.0001,ABS(0.1658*55.4732*EXP(-0.04*55.4732)-1)<0.0001)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(8.4603<25,55.4732>25,ABS(0.1658*8.4603*EXP(-0.04*8.4603)-1)<0.0001,ABS(0.1658*55.4732*EXP(-0.04*55.4732)-1)<0.0001)" .

hemo:7007163 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "No crossing above the peak weight (HE-CF-AGW-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A level of 1.6 is above the peak weight 1.525, so the function returns no ages. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=0.1658/(0.04*EXP(1))<1.6`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=0.1658/(0.04*EXP(1))<1.6" .

hemo:7007164 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's death at 5 with weights and 3% discounting (HE-CF-AGW-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The closed form and the integral both give 36.4398 years, and age weighting raises the discounted loss by about 22% (computed here for illustration). `a = 5; L = 75; r = 0.03; K = 1; C = 0.1658; beta = 0.04; DW = 1; s = 0.07; G = 36.439825; G_0 = 29.820026; Y = 36.439825; effect = 1.221992`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 5; L = 75; r = 0.03; K = 1; C = 0.1658; beta = 0.04; DW = 1; s = 0.07; G = 36.439825; G_0 = 29.820026; Y = 36.439825; effect = 1.221992" .

hemo:7007165 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's death at 40 with weights and 3% discounting (HE-CF-AGW-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both give 23.2180 years, about 0.3% below the unweighted discounted value. `a = 40; L = 40; r = 0.03; K = 1; C = 0.1658; beta = 0.04; DW = 1; s = 0.07; G = 23.217966; G_0 = 23.293526; Y = 23.217966; effect = 0.996756`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 40; L = 40; r = 0.03; K = 1; C = 0.1658; beta = 0.04; DW = 1; s = 0.07; G = 23.217966; G_0 = 23.293526; Y = 23.217966; effect = 0.996756" .

hemo:7007166 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Illustrative case with onset at 35, 10 years at a weight of 0.6 (HE-CF-AGW-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The case counts about 6.955 age-weighted discounted years against 5.184 without age weights, Larson's discounted value for the same case (computed here for illustration). `a = 35; L = 10; r = 0.03; K = 1; C = 0.1658; beta = 0.04; DW = 0.6; s = 0.07; G = 11.591293; G_0 = 8.639393; Y = 6.954776; effect = 1.341679`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a = 35; L = 10; r = 0.03; K = 1; C = 0.1658; beta = 0.04; DW = 0.6; s = 0.07; G = 11.591293; G_0 = 8.639393; Y = 6.954776; effect = 1.341679" .

hemo:7007167 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Zero rate, read from the code (HE-CF-AGW-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "At r = 0 the code returns the undiscounted 84.0684 years of HE-FM-AGW-002 for the death at 5, matched by the integral; the calculator line is not used at r = 0." .

hemo:7007168 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Closed form agrees with the integral (HE-CF-AGW-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For the article's death at 5 the closed form and the 1,000-panel integral differ by less than 0.0001 years. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(ClosedFormYears-SimpsonYears)<0.0001` with the two Excel results in cells named ClosedFormYears and SimpsonYears." ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ClosedFormYears-SimpsonYears)<0.0001" .

hemo:7007169 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Modulation constant enters linearly (HE-CF-AGW-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The value at K = 0.5 is the mean of the values at K = 0 and K = 1, 33.1299 for the death at 5. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=ABS((29.820026+36.439825)/2-33.129926)<0.00001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((29.820026+36.439825)/2-33.129926)<0.00001" .

hemo:7007170 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's interim look with a favourable signal (HE-CF-AVOI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "After 100 pairs with an illustrative mean of GBP 125, the design-stage prior of GBP 500 worth 25 pairs updates to a posterior mean of GBP 200 worth 125 pairs, the article's interim case. The remaining 100 pairs are worth about GBP 3.02 million, and after GBP 400,000 of sampling and GBP 20,000 for participants the net gain is about GBP 2.60 million, so the trial continues. The article's GBP 2.62 million is G_off, the offline gain that leaves the participants' loss out. `mu_0 = 500; n_0 = 25; m_1 = 100; xbar_1 = 125; m = 100; sigma_X = 10000; P = 20000; c = 4000; C_a = 0; Q_z = 0.3686578386; n_t = 125; mu_t = 200; sd_t = 894.427191; s_m = 596.284794; z = 0.33541; phi_z = 0.377121; EVSI = 151.14; EVSI_pop = 3022802; G_off = 2622802; NG = 2602802; go = 1`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "mu_0 = 500; n_0 = 25; m_1 = 100; xbar_1 = 125; m = 100; sigma_X = 10000; P = 20000; c = 4000; C_a = 0; Q_z = 0.3686578386; n_t = 125; mu_t = 200; sd_t = 894.427191; s_m = 596.284794; z = 0.33541; phi_z = 0.377121; EVSI = 151.14; EVSI_pop = 3022802; G_off = 2622802; NG = 2602802; go = 1" .

hemo:7007171 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's interim look with an unfavourable signal (HE-CF-AVOI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "An illustrative interim mean of minus GBP 2,000 over 100 pairs gives the article's posterior mean of minus GBP 1,500. The remaining pairs are worth about GBP 22,772 in all and the net gain is about minus GBP 527,228; the scan in the code finds no smaller plan with a positive gain (the best, one pair, gives minus GBP 5,500), so the trial stops. `mu_0 = 500; n_0 = 25; m_1 = 100; xbar_1 = -2000; m = 100; sigma_X = 10000; P = 20000; c = 4000; C_a = 0; Q_z = 0.0059418946; n_t = 125; mu_t = -1500; sd_t = 894.427191; s_m = 596.284794; z = 2.515576; phi_z = 0.016857; EVSI = 1.14; EVSI_pop = 22772; G_off = -377228; NG = -527228; go = 0`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "mu_0 = 500; n_0 = 25; m_1 = 100; xbar_1 = -2000; m = 100; sigma_X = 10000; P = 20000; c = 4000; C_a = 0; Q_z = 0.0059418946; n_t = 125; mu_t = -1500; sd_t = 894.427191; s_m = 596.284794; z = 2.515576; phi_z = 0.016857; EVSI = 1.14; EVSI_pop = 22772; G_off = -377228; NG = -527228; go = 0" .

hemo:7007172 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "No pairs observed yet, the article's design stage (HE-CF-AVOI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With no data the interim posterior is the prior, and for 200 pairs the offline gain is about GBP 9.77 million, the article's design-stage ENBS, while the participants' loss of GBP 500 a pair lowers it to about GBP 9.67 million, a limiting case that checks the implementation. `mu_0 = 500; n_0 = 25; m_1 = 0; xbar_1 = 0; m = 200; sigma_X = 10000; P = 20000; c = 4000; C_a = 0; Q_z = 0.3954411615; n_t = 25; mu_t = 500; sd_t = 2000; s_m = 1885.618083; z = 0.265165; phi_z = 0.385161; EVSI = 528.55; EVSI_pop = 10570906; G_off = 9770906; NG = 9670906; go = 1`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "mu_0 = 500; n_0 = 25; m_1 = 0; xbar_1 = 0; m = 200; sigma_X = 10000; P = 20000; c = 4000; C_a = 0; Q_z = 0.3954411615; n_t = 25; mu_t = 500; sd_t = 2000; s_m = 1885.618083; z = 0.265165; phi_z = 0.385161; EVSI = 528.55; EVSI_pop = 10570906; G_off = 9770906; NG = 9670906; go = 1" .

hemo:7007173 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Effective sample size update equals the precision form of HE-FM-BAD-001 (HE-CF-AVOI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The interim mean from 25 prior pairs at GBP 500 and 100 observed pairs at GBP 125 equals the precision-weighted mean with prior variance 10,000 squared over 25 and data variance 10,000 squared over 100, GBP 200. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ABS((25*500+100*125)/125-(1/(1/(1E8/25)+1/(1E8/100)))*(500/(1E8/25)+125/(1E8/100)))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((25*500+100*125)/125-(1/(1/(1E8/25)+1/(1E8/100)))*(500/(1E8/25)+125/(1E8/100)))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007174 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Design-stage limiting case reproduces the article (HE-CF-AVOI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With no pairs observed and 200 pairs planned, the offline gain equals the article's design-stage ENBS of about GBP 9,770,906. Expected result TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(20000*(SQRT(1E8*200/(25*225))*NORM.S.DIST(500/SQRT(1E8*200/(25*225)),FALSE)-500*(1-NORM.S.DIST(500/SQRT(1E8*200/(25*225)),TRUE)))-200*4000-9770906)<1`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(20000*(SQRT(1E8*200/(25*225))*NORM.S.DIST(500/SQRT(1E8*200/(25*225)),FALSE)-500*(1-NORM.S.DIST(500/SQRT(1E8*200/(25*225)),TRUE)))-200*4000-9770906)<1" .

hemo:7007175 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's three and two contacts, 10,000 agents, seed 2026 in R (HE-CF-ABM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The R code below returns 2,675 infected agents with three contacts and 1,867 with two. The simulated share 0.2675 is 0.79 standard errors below the analytic 0.271, so the test passes, and the simulated share averted, 0.0808, is close to the analytic 0.081. Python's generator gives different draws for the same seeds, 2,784 and 1,935 infected, 1.66 standard errors above 0.271, and also passes. `N_agents = 10000; p = 0.10; k_3 = 3; k_2 = 2; n_3 = 2675; n_2 = 1867; P_3 = 0.271; P_2 = 0.19; Phat_3 = 0.2675; Phat_2 = 0.1867; MCSE_3 = 0.00444; ok = 1; D_hat = 0.0808`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_agents = 10000; p = 0.10; k_3 = 3; k_2 = 2; n_3 = 2675; n_2 = 1867; P_3 = 0.271; P_2 = 0.19; Phat_3 = 0.2675; Phat_2 = 0.1867; MCSE_3 = 0.00444; ok = 1; D_hat = 0.0808" .

hemo:7007176 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Single contact limiting case (HE-CF-ABM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With one contact under both strategies the analytic share is the per-contact probability 0.10, the R run gives 980 infected agents out of 10,000, 0.67 standard errors below it, and no infection is averted. `N_agents = 10000; p = 0.10; k_3 = 1; k_2 = 1; n_3 = 980; n_2 = 980; P_3 = 0.1; P_2 = 0.1; Phat_3 = 0.098; Phat_2 = 0.098; MCSE_3 = 0.003; ok = 1; D_hat = 0`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "N_agents = 10000; p = 0.10; k_3 = 1; k_2 = 1; n_3 = 980; n_2 = 980; P_3 = 0.1; P_2 = 0.1; Phat_3 = 0.098; Phat_2 = 0.098; MCSE_3 = 0.003; ok = 1; D_hat = 0" .

hemo:7007177 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Simulated share within three standard errors of the analytic probability (HE-CF-ABM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The share infected with three contacts lies within three binomial standard errors of the analytic value. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a simulation that infects an agent when one draw falls below k times p, which with the per-agent seeds of the R code and base seed 2026 gives a share of 0.2897, about 4.2 standard errors above 0.271. Excel check `=ABS(AVERAGE(InfectedThree)-(1-(1-ContactTransProb)^3))<=3*SQRT((1-(1-ContactTransProb)^3)*(1-ContactTransProb)^3/ROWS(InfectedThree))`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AVERAGE(InfectedThree)-(1-(1-ContactTransProb)^3))<=3*SQRT((1-(1-ContactTransProb)^3)*(1-ContactTransProb)^3/ROWS(InfectedThree))" .

hemo:7007178 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Common random numbers across strategies (HE-CF-ABM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "No agent is infected with two contacts and not with three. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows that the programme column drew its own RAND values. Excel check `=SUMPRODUCT(--(InfectedTwo>InfectedThree))=0`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=SUMPRODUCT(--(InfectedTwo>InfectedThree))=0" .

hemo:7007179 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Half-year cycles from age 63 across two bands (HE-CF-BGM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Illustrative annual probabilities of 0.010 for ages 60 to 64 and 0.016 for ages 65 to 69, and six half-year cycles starting at age 63. The first four cycles fall in the first band and the last two in the second, so background survival after three years is 0.964418, the same as (1 minus 0.010) squared times (1 minus 0.016). `a_0 = 63; a_edge = 65; Delta = 0.5; n_cyc = 6; q_A = 0.010; q_B = 0.016; n_A = 4; n_B = 2; p_A = 0.005013; p_B = 0.008032; S_bg = 0.964418`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_0 = 63; a_edge = 65; Delta = 0.5; n_cyc = 6; q_A = 0.010; q_B = 0.016; n_A = 4; n_B = 2; p_A = 0.005013; p_B = 0.008032; S_bg = 0.964418" .

hemo:7007180 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Cohort starting at the band edge (HE-CF-BGM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Starting at 65, every cycle uses the second band, so background survival after three years is 0.984 cubed, 0.952764, a limiting case. `a_0 = 65; a_edge = 65; Delta = 0.5; n_cyc = 6; q_A = 0.010; q_B = 0.016; n_A = 0; n_B = 6; p_A = 0.005013; p_B = 0.008032; S_bg = 0.952764`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_0 = 65; a_edge = 65; Delta = 0.5; n_cyc = 6; q_A = 0.010; q_B = 0.016; n_A = 0; n_B = 6; p_A = 0.005013; p_B = 0.008032; S_bg = 0.952764" .

hemo:7007181 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Annual cycles return the table's probabilities (HE-CF-BGM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With one-year cycles each cycle probability equals its band's annual probability, a second limiting case. `a_0 = 63; a_edge = 65; Delta = 1; n_cyc = 4; q_A = 0.010; q_B = 0.016; n_A = 2; n_B = 2; p_A = 0.01; p_B = 0.016; S_bg = 0.948988`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_0 = 63; a_edge = 65; Delta = 1; n_cyc = 4; q_A = 0.010; q_B = 0.016; n_A = 2; n_B = 2; p_A = 0.01; p_B = 0.016; S_bg = 0.948988" .

hemo:7007182 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Two half-year cycles compound to the annual probability (HE-CF-BGM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the first worked example's inputs, D2 holds the first cycle probability, for age 63 from the annual 0.010 and half-year cycles, and two such cycles compound back to the annual probability. Expected result TRUE. Halving the annual probability in column D instead of rescaling it puts 0.005 in D2, which compounds to 0.009975 and makes the check FALSE. Excel check `=ABS(1-(1-D2)^2-0.010)<1E-12`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(1-(1-D2)^2-0.010)<1E-12" .

hemo:7007183 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Final background survival reflects the move to the older band (HE-CF-BGM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the first worked example's inputs the last cell of column E, named FinalBgSurvival, equals (1 minus 0.010) squared times (1 minus 0.016). Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the lookup fixed at the starting band, which gives 0.970299. Excel check `=ABS(FinalBgSurvival-(1-0.010)^2*(1-0.016))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(FinalBgSurvival-(1-0.010)^2*(1-0.016))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007184 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's two-group matrix (HE-CF-BRN-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Three generations from one case in each group give 2.8, 3.56 and 4.516 cases in total, so the one-generation ratio is about 1.2685 and the two-generation ratio about 1.270, against the exact R_0 of about 1.2685 (computed here for illustration). `k_11 = 0.8; k_12 = 1.2; k_21 = 0.3; k_22 = 0.5; a_1 = 2; a_2 = 0.8; b_1 = 2.56; b_2 = 1; c_1 = 3.248; c_2 = 1.268; R_pow = 1.2685; R_two = 1.27; T_K = 1.3; D_K = 0.04; R_0 = 1.2685`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "k_11 = 0.8; k_12 = 1.2; k_21 = 0.3; k_22 = 0.5; a_1 = 2; a_2 = 0.8; b_1 = 2.56; b_2 = 1; c_1 = 3.248; c_2 = 1.268; R_pow = 1.2685; R_two = 1.27; T_K = 1.3; D_K = 0.04; R_0 = 1.2685" .

hemo:7007185 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Host and vector matrix with a zero diagonal (HE-CF-BRN-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The one-generation ratio is 2.25 here and about 0.889 one generation later, while the two-generation ratio gives the exact 1.4142, the square root of 2 (computed here for illustration). `k_11 = 0; k_12 = 4; k_21 = 0.5; k_22 = 0; a_1 = 4; a_2 = 0.5; b_1 = 2; b_2 = 2; c_1 = 8; c_2 = 1; R_pow = 2.25; R_two = 1.4142; T_K = 0; D_K = -2; R_0 = 1.4142`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "k_11 = 0; k_12 = 4; k_21 = 0.5; k_22 = 0; a_1 = 4; a_2 = 0.5; b_1 = 2; b_2 = 2; c_1 = 8; c_2 = 1; R_pow = 2.25; R_two = 1.4142; T_K = 0; D_K = -2; R_0 = 1.4142" .

hemo:7007186 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Three illustrative age groups, R and Python (HE-CF-BRN-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For an illustrative matrix with rows (1.2, 0.4, 0.1), (0.6, 0.8, 0.2) and (0.1, 0.3, 0.4) the routines return R_0 of about 1.5726, with about 46.3%, 39.6% and 14.1% of cases in the three groups once the generations settle, and the Excel power iteration returns the same R_0 to six decimals after 100 helper columns. The calculator line does not apply to three groups. `ngm_r0(matrix(c(1.2, 0.6, 0.1, 0.4, 0.8, 0.3, 0.1, 0.2, 0.4), 3))` returns `R0 = 1.572561`." ;
    hemo:9000014 "R0 = 1.572561" .

hemo:7007187 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "SEIR model built from F and V, R and Python (HE-CF-BRN-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For van den Driessche's SEIR model with an illustrative beta S_0 of 0.5 per day, kappa of 0.2 per day, gamma of 0.25 per day and a natural death rate d of 1/25,550 per day, a 70-year lifespan, F has the single entry beta S_0 in row 1, column 2, and V has d + kappa and d + gamma on the diagonal with minus kappa in row 2, column 1. The routines return about 1.9993, the closed form kappa beta S_0/((d + kappa)(d + gamma)) of section 3." .

hemo:7007188 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Excel power iteration agrees with the two-group closed form (HE-CF-BRN-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "For a two-group matrix the power-iteration result matches HE-FM-BRN-005 to six decimals. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(MMULT(NextGenMatrix,LastVector))/SUM(LastVector)-(INDEX(NextGenMatrix,1,1)+INDEX(NextGenMatrix,2,2)+SQRT((INDEX(NextGenMatrix,1,1)-INDEX(NextGenMatrix,2,2))^2+4*INDEX(NextGenMatrix,1,2)*INDEX(NextGenMatrix,2,1)))/2)<1E-6`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(MMULT(NextGenMatrix,LastVector))/SUM(LastVector)-(INDEX(NextGenMatrix,1,1)+INDEX(NextGenMatrix,2,2)+SQRT((INDEX(NextGenMatrix,1,1)-INDEX(NextGenMatrix,2,2))^2+4*INDEX(NextGenMatrix,1,2)*INDEX(NextGenMatrix,2,1)))/2)<1E-6" .

hemo:7007189 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "SEIR route matches the closed form (HE-CF-BRN-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The R check `abs(ngm_r0(Fm = matrix(c(0, 0, 0.5, 0), 2), Vm = matrix(c(0.2+1/25550, -0.2, 0, 0.25+1/25550), 2))$R0-0.2*0.5/((0.2+1/25550)*(0.25+1/25550))) < 1e-12` returns TRUE. A FALSE result shows the entry minus kappa left out of V, which returns 0 because no exposed case then moves on to the infectious stage." ;
    hemo:9000024 "abs(ngm_r0(Fm = matrix(c(0, 0, 0.5, 0), 2), Vm = matrix(c(0.2+1/25550, -0.2, 0, 0.25+1/25550), 2))$R0-0.2*0.5/((0.2+1/25550)*(0.25+1/25550))) < 1e-12" .

hemo:7007190 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Turner and colleagues' Vietnamese cost, 2006 to 2016 (HE-CF-BOC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "VND1,000,000 in 2006 prices. The factor 2.360037 is the Vietnamese inflation implied by their Figure 1B and 1.1684 the US inflation implied by the abstract's US$116.84 for US$100; the rates are 15,994 dong per US dollar in 2006 and 21,935 in 2016. Method 1 gives US$73.05 and method 2 US$107.59, as in Figure 1, so method 2 is about 47% higher. `C_a = 1000000; I_a = 1; I_b = 2.360037; e_a = 0.0000625234; e_b = 0.0000455893; J_a = 1; J_b = 1.1684; C_m1 = 73.05; C_m2 = 107.59; gap = 1.4728`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_a = 1000000; I_a = 1; I_b = 2.360037; e_a = 0.0000625234; e_b = 0.0000455893; J_a = 1; J_b = 1.1684; C_m1 = 73.05; C_m2 = 107.59; gap = 1.4728" .

hemo:7007191 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Illustrative purchasing power parity conversion (HE-CF-BOC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A cost of 1,000 with illustrative source and target indices rising by 10% and 4%, and a PPP cross rate of 0.875, 0.7 over 0.8, in both years (illustrative values). `C_a = 1000; I_a = 100; I_b = 110; e_a = 0.875; e_b = 0.875; J_a = 100; J_b = 104; C_m1 = 910; C_m2 = 962.5; gap = 1.0577`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_a = 1000; I_a = 100; I_b = 110; e_a = 0.875; e_b = 0.875; J_a = 100; J_b = 104; C_m1 = 910; C_m2 = 962.5; gap = 1.0577" .

hemo:7007192 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal inflation and an unchanged rate (HE-CF-BOC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the same index in both countries and the same rate in both years the two orders agree, a limiting case. `C_a = 1000; I_a = 100; I_b = 110; e_a = 0.5; e_b = 0.5; J_a = 100; J_b = 110; C_m1 = 550; C_m2 = 550; gap = 1`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "C_a = 1000; I_a = 100; I_b = 110; e_a = 0.5; e_b = 0.5; J_a = 100; J_b = 110; C_m1 = 550; C_m2 = 550; gap = 1" .

hemo:7007193 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Turner and colleagues' method 2 reproduced (HE-CF-BOC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the first worked example's inputs CostMethodTwo is within 0.01 of US$107.59. Expected result TRUE. Converting at the costing-year rate instead, which is equivalent to the incorrect route of their Figure 4 (derived here), gives about 147.56 and makes it FALSE. Excel check `=ABS(CostMethodTwo-107.59)<0.01`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(CostMethodTwo-107.59)<0.01" .

hemo:7007194 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Orders agree under equal inflation and an unchanged rate (HE-CF-BOC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the third worked example's inputs CostMethodOne equals CostMethodTwo. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the rate divided into the cost in one cell; dividing by 0.5 in method 1 gives 2200 against 550. Excel check `=ABS(CostMethodOne-CostMethodTwo)<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(CostMethodOne-CostMethodTwo)<1E-9" .

hemo:7007195 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Basket B before the country priced at 70 launches (HE-CF-BOC-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "As in the article, the four observed prices give a mean of 96.25 and a ceiling of 120.3125, and the proposed price of 130 is 9.6875 above it. The median of the four is 97.5 (computed here for illustration). `d_1 = 0; c_1 = 70; d_2 = 1; c_2 = 80; d_3 = 1; c_3 = 95; d_4 = 1; c_4 = 100; d_5 = 1; c_5 = 110; k = 1.25; P_prop = 130; n = 4; P_mean = 96.25; T = 120.3125; D = 9.6875`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_1 = 0; c_1 = 70; d_2 = 1; c_2 = 80; d_3 = 1; c_3 = 95; d_4 = 1; c_4 = 100; d_5 = 1; c_5 = 110; k = 1.25; P_prop = 130; n = 4; P_mean = 96.25; T = 120.3125; D = 9.6875" .

hemo:7007196 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Basket B after launch (HE-CF-BOC-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With all five prices observed the ceiling falls to 113.75 and the margin rises to 16.25; the median is 95. `d_1 = 1; c_1 = 70; d_2 = 1; c_2 = 80; d_3 = 1; c_3 = 95; d_4 = 1; c_4 = 100; d_5 = 1; c_5 = 110; k = 1.25; P_prop = 130; n = 5; P_mean = 91; T = 113.75; D = 16.25`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_1 = 1; c_1 = 70; d_2 = 1; c_2 = 80; d_3 = 1; c_3 = 95; d_4 = 1; c_4 = 100; d_5 = 1; c_5 = 110; k = 1.25; P_prop = 130; n = 5; P_mean = 91; T = 113.75; D = 16.25" .

hemo:7007197 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Basket A (HE-CF-BOC-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The proposed price is 1.25 below the ceiling and is accepted; the median is 100. `d_1 = 1; c_1 = 80; d_2 = 1; c_2 = 95; d_3 = 1; c_3 = 100; d_4 = 1; c_4 = 110; d_5 = 1; c_5 = 140; k = 1.25; P_prop = 130; n = 5; P_mean = 105; T = 131.25; D = -1.25`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "d_1 = 1; c_1 = 80; d_2 = 1; c_2 = 95; d_3 = 1; c_3 = 100; d_4 = 1; c_4 = 110; d_5 = 1; c_5 = 140; k = 1.25; P_prop = 130; n = 5; P_mean = 105; T = 131.25; D = -1.25" .

hemo:7007198 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Launch-sequencing ceiling reproduced (HE-CF-BOC-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the first worked example's inputs BasketCeilingObserved is 120.3125. Expected result TRUE. Flagging the unlaunched country as observed with a price of 0 gives a mean of 77 and a ceiling of 96.25, and keeping its price of 70 gives 113.75; either makes it FALSE. Excel check `=ABS(BasketCeilingObserved-120.3125)<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(BasketCeilingObserved-120.3125)<1E-9" .

hemo:7007199 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Median of the priced countries (HE-CF-BOC-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the same inputs BasketMedianObserved is 97.5. Expected result TRUE. Leaving the unlaunched country's 70 in the helper column gives 95 and makes it FALSE. Excel check `=ABS(BasketMedianObserved-97.5)<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(BasketMedianObserved-97.5)<1E-9" .

hemo:7007200 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's two equal risk groups (HE-CF-COHM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The stratified runs give a QALY gain of 2.4 and an ICER of GBP 8,333 per QALY; the averaged cohort gives 1.33 QALYs and GBP 15,000, understating life expectancy without treatment by 46% and the QALY gain by 44% and overstating the ICER by 80%, as in the article. `w = 0.5; q_low = 0.05; q_high = 0.25; e = 0.2; u = 0.8; c = 20000; q_bar = 0.15; L_low_0 = 19.5; L_low_1 = 24.5; L_high_0 = 3.5; L_high_1 = 4.5; L_avg_0 = 6.1667; L_avg_1 = 7.8333; dQ_strat = 2.4; dQ_avg = 1.3333; ICER_strat = 8333.33; ICER_avg = 15000; LE_strat_0 = 11.5; under_LE = 0.4638; under_dQ = 0.4444; over_ICER = 0.8`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w = 0.5; q_low = 0.05; q_high = 0.25; e = 0.2; u = 0.8; c = 20000; q_bar = 0.15; L_low_0 = 19.5; L_low_1 = 24.5; L_high_0 = 3.5; L_high_1 = 4.5; L_avg_0 = 6.1667; L_avg_1 = 7.8333; dQ_strat = 2.4; dQ_avg = 1.3333; ICER_strat = 8333.33; ICER_avg = 15000; LE_strat_0 = 11.5; under_LE = 0.4638; under_dQ = 0.4444; over_ICER = 0.8" .

hemo:7007201 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "80% of the population at low risk (HE-CF-COHM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With illustrative shares of 80% and 20% the stratified ICER is about GBP 5,952 per QALY and the averaged cohort's GBP 9,000, about 51% too high (computed here for illustration). `w = 0.8; q_low = 0.05; q_high = 0.25; e = 0.2; u = 0.8; c = 20000; q_bar = 0.09; L_low_0 = 19.5; L_low_1 = 24.5; L_high_0 = 3.5; L_high_1 = 4.5; L_avg_0 = 10.6111; L_avg_1 = 13.3889; dQ_strat = 3.36; dQ_avg = 2.2222; ICER_strat = 5952.38; ICER_avg = 9000; LE_strat_0 = 16.3; under_LE = 0.349; under_dQ = 0.3386; over_ICER = 0.512`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w = 0.8; q_low = 0.05; q_high = 0.25; e = 0.2; u = 0.8; c = 20000; q_bar = 0.09; L_low_0 = 19.5; L_low_1 = 24.5; L_high_0 = 3.5; L_high_1 = 4.5; L_avg_0 = 10.6111; L_avg_1 = 13.3889; dQ_strat = 3.36; dQ_avg = 2.2222; ICER_strat = 5952.38; ICER_avg = 9000; LE_strat_0 = 16.3; under_LE = 0.349; under_dQ = 0.3386; over_ICER = 0.512" .

hemo:7007202 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Equal stratum probabilities (HE-CF-COHM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When both strata have a probability of 0.15 the averaged cohort reproduces the stratified results and all three relative errors are zero, a limiting case. `w = 0.5; q_low = 0.15; q_high = 0.15; e = 0.2; u = 0.8; c = 20000; q_bar = 0.15; L_low_0 = 6.1667; L_low_1 = 7.8333; L_high_0 = 6.1667; L_high_1 = 7.8333; L_avg_0 = 6.1667; L_avg_1 = 7.8333; dQ_strat = 1.3333; dQ_avg = 1.3333; ICER_strat = 15000; ICER_avg = 15000; LE_strat_0 = 6.1667; under_LE = 0; under_dQ = 0; over_ICER = 0`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w = 0.5; q_low = 0.15; q_high = 0.15; e = 0.2; u = 0.8; c = 20000; q_bar = 0.15; L_low_0 = 6.1667; L_low_1 = 7.8333; L_high_0 = 6.1667; L_high_1 = 7.8333; L_avg_0 = 6.1667; L_avg_1 = 7.8333; dQ_strat = 1.3333; dQ_avg = 1.3333; ICER_strat = 15000; ICER_avg = 15000; LE_strat_0 = 6.1667; under_LE = 0; under_dQ = 0; over_ICER = 0" .

hemo:7007203 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Trace life expectancy of the low-risk stratum (HE-CF-COHM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With DeathProbLow at 0.05 the cell LifeExpLowStd is 19.5 years to six decimal places. Expected result TRUE. Starting CycleIndex at 1, which counts at the end of each cycle, gives 18.5 and FALSE, and leaving out the half cycle gives 20 and FALSE. Excel check `=ABS(LifeExpLowStd-19.5)<0.000001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(LifeExpLowStd-19.5)<0.000001" .

hemo:7007204 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Stratified ICER of the article's example (HE-CF-COHM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's inputs ICERStrat is 20,000 divided by 2.4. Expected result TRUE. An ICERStrat cell that takes the averaged cohort's QALY gain, or the simple mean of the two stratum ICERs, returns GBP 15,000 and FALSE. Excel check `=ABS(ICERStrat-20000/2.4)<0.01`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ICERStrat-20000/2.4)<0.01" .

hemo:7007205 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Low-risk stratum gain against its closed form (HE-CF-COHM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The traced gain LifeExpLowTreat minus LifeExpLowStd is compared with RiskCut divided by the product of 1 minus RiskCut and DeathProbLow, the closed form derived here, which is 5 years at the article's inputs. Expected result TRUE. A LifeExpLowTreat cell that leaves out the half cycle while LifeExpLowStd keeps it gives 5.5 and FALSE. Excel check `=ABS((LifeExpLowTreat-LifeExpLowStd)-RiskCut/((1-RiskCut)*DeathProbLow))<0.000001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS((LifeExpLowTreat-LifeExpLowStd)-RiskCut/((1-RiskCut)*DeathProbLow))<0.000001" .

hemo:7007206 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's two one-day steps (HE-CF-CMPM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Day-1 infections are 29.7 without and 23.7 with the programme. On day 2 they are about 35.44 without the programme, 28.28 under the static force and 26.87 under the dynamic force, so over two days the static count averts about 13.16 infections and the dynamic count about 14.58, and at GBP 40 per infection the averted costs are about GBP 526 and GBP 583, the article's figures. `beta = 0.3; gamma = 0.1; N = 10000; dt = 1; S_0 = 9900; I_0 = 100; V = 2000; c_inf = 40; F1b = 29.7; S1b = 9870.3; I1b = 119.7; S0p = 7900; F1p = 23.7; S1p = 7876.3; I1p = 113.7; F2b = 35.4442; F2s = 28.2838; F2d = 26.8661; A_s = 13.1605; A_d = 14.5782; A_i = 1.4177; C_s = 526.42; C_d = 583.13`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "beta = 0.3; gamma = 0.1; N = 10000; dt = 1; S_0 = 9900; I_0 = 100; V = 2000; c_inf = 40; F1b = 29.7; S1b = 9870.3; I1b = 119.7; S0p = 7900; F1p = 23.7; S1p = 7876.3; I1p = 113.7; F2b = 35.4442; F2s = 28.2838; F2d = 26.8661; A_s = 13.1605; A_d = 14.5782; A_i = 1.4177; C_s = 526.42; C_d = 583.13" .

hemo:7007207 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Whole epidemic over 200 days, R and Python (HE-CF-CMPM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the same illustrative inputs run for 200 one-day steps, by which time the epidemic has ended in both runs, the static count averts about 1,893.7 infections and the dynamic count about 2,376.4, of which about 482.6 are indirect, about a fifth of the dynamic total (computed here for illustration). `sir_avert(0.3, 0.1, 10000, 9900, 100, 2000, 200)` returns `A_s = 1893.75, A_d = 2376.37, A_i = 482.62`." ;
    hemo:9000014 "A_s = 1893.75, A_d = 2376.37, A_i = 482.62" .

hemo:7007208 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's two-day counts in Excel (HE-CF-CMPM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's inputs and two steps, so that the sums run over rows 2 and 3, AvertStaticTotal and AvertDynamicTotal hold about 13.1605 and 14.5782. The expected result is TRUE. Excel check `=AND(ABS(AvertStaticTotal-13.1605)<1E-4,ABS(AvertDynamicTotal-14.5782)<1E-4)`. A FALSE result shows the static column L computed from the programme run's infectious count in column H, which makes AvertStaticTotal 14.5782." ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ABS(AvertStaticTotal-13.1605)<1E-4,ABS(AvertDynamicTotal-14.5782)<1E-4)" .

hemo:7007209 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Static count no larger than the dynamic count (HE-CF-CMPM-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With these inputs the dynamic count is at least the static count at every horizon from 1 to 300 steps, although the gap narrows after day 29, because the static run's own susceptible pool is used up faster than the programme run's and its daily infections then fall below those of the dynamic run (computed here for illustration; the one-step result of HE-FM-CMPM-005 does not carry over to a run in which the static susceptible count differs from S_p). The R check `r <- sir_avert(0.3, 0.1, 10000, 9900, 100, 2000, 200); r[\"A_d\"] >= r[\"A_s\"] && abs(r[\"A_s\"]-1893.748) < 1e-3` returns TRUE. A FALSE result shows the static and dynamic streams swapped in the code." ;
    hemo:9000024 "r <- sir_avert(0.3, 0.1, 10000, 9900, 100, 2000, 200); r[\"A_d\"] >= r[\"A_s\"] && abs(r[\"A_s\"]-1893.748) < 1e-3" .

hemo:7007210 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Illustrative three-item basket (HE-CF-CPI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Expenditure of 500, 300 and 200 at period b prices of 2, 5 and 10, base prices of 2.10, 5 and 11 and current prices of 2.31, 5.25 and 11 give weights of 0.5024, 0.2871 and 0.2105 and an index of 106.4593 (illustrative inputs, computed here for illustration). `V_1 = 500; V_2 = 300; V_3 = 200; p1_b = 2; p2_b = 5; p3_b = 10; p1_0 = 2.1; p2_0 = 5; p3_0 = 11; p1_t = 2.31; p2_t = 5.25; p3_t = 11; u_1 = 525; u_2 = 300; u_3 = 220; w_1 = 0.502392; w_2 = 0.287081; w_3 = 0.210526; I_0t = 106.4593`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "V_1 = 500; V_2 = 300; V_3 = 200; p1_b = 2; p2_b = 5; p3_b = 10; p1_0 = 2.1; p2_0 = 5; p3_0 = 11; p1_t = 2.31; p2_t = 5.25; p3_t = 11; u_1 = 525; u_2 = 300; u_3 = 220; w_1 = 0.502392; w_2 = 0.287081; w_3 = 0.210526; I_0t = 106.4593" .

hemo:7007211 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Weight reference prices equal to base prices (HE-CF-CPI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "When period b prices equal base prices, price-updating changes nothing, the weights are the expenditure shares 0.5, 0.3 and 0.2 and the index is the Laspeyres case of section 3.3 with b equal to 0, 106.5 here (computed here for illustration). `V_1 = 500; V_2 = 300; V_3 = 200; p1_b = 2.1; p2_b = 5; p3_b = 11; p1_0 = 2.1; p2_0 = 5; p3_0 = 11; p1_t = 2.31; p2_t = 5.25; p3_t = 11; u_1 = 500; u_2 = 300; u_3 = 200; w_1 = 0.5; w_2 = 0.3; w_3 = 0.2; I_0t = 106.5`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "V_1 = 500; V_2 = 300; V_3 = 200; p1_b = 2.1; p2_b = 5; p3_b = 11; p1_0 = 2.1; p2_0 = 5; p3_0 = 11; p1_t = 2.31; p2_t = 5.25; p3_t = 11; u_1 = 500; u_2 = 300; u_3 = 200; w_1 = 0.5; w_2 = 0.3; w_3 = 0.2; I_0t = 106.5" .

hemo:7007212 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Expenditure route agrees with the basket of HE-FM-CPI-001 (HE-CF-CPI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Dividing each expenditure by its period b price gives the quantities, and the basket ratio built from them equals the result cell. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows weights taken as expenditure shares without price-updating, which gives 106.5 in place of 106.4593 for the first worked example. Excel check `=ABS(CFIndexOut-100*SUMPRODUCT(ItemExpenditure/ItemPriceWeightRef,ItemPriceCurrent)/SUMPRODUCT(ItemExpenditure/ItemPriceWeightRef,ItemPriceBase))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(CFIndexOut-100*SUMPRODUCT(ItemExpenditure/ItemPriceWeightRef,ItemPriceCurrent)/SUMPRODUCT(ItemExpenditure/ItemPriceWeightRef,ItemPriceBase))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007213 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Illustrative three-item basket reproduced (HE-CF-CPI-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the first worked example in the input ranges, the result cell holds 106.4593 to four decimal places. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the relatives inverted to base over current price, which gives 94.0657, or weights without price-updating, which gives 106.5. Excel check `=ABS(CFIndexOut-106.4593)<0.00005`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(CFIndexOut-106.4593)<0.00005" .

hemo:7007214 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "D7BT financial years 2019/20 and 2023/24 from the article (HE-CF-CPI-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The monthly values sum to 1,298.9 and 1,580.1, so the averages are 108.2417 and 131.675, the ratio is 1.2165 and the average annual rate is 0.0502. The ratio 1.2165 applied to GBP 2,500 through HE-FM-COST-002 gives GBP 3,041.25, as in the article. `a_01 = 107.6; a_02 = 107.9; a_03 = 107.9; a_04 = 107.9; a_05 = 108.4; a_06 = 108.5; a_07 = 108.3; a_08 = 108.5; a_09 = 108.5; a_10 = 108.2; a_11 = 108.6; a_12 = 108.6; b_01 = 130.4; b_02 = 131.3; b_03 = 131.5; b_04 = 130.9; b_05 = 131.3; b_06 = 132; b_07 = 132; b_08 = 131.7; b_09 = 132.2; b_10 = 131.5; b_11 = 132.3; b_12 = 133; Y = 4; A_1 = 108.2417; A_2 = 131.675; R = 1.2165; n = 48; g = 0.0502`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_01 = 107.6; a_02 = 107.9; a_03 = 107.9; a_04 = 107.9; a_05 = 108.4; a_06 = 108.5; a_07 = 108.3; a_08 = 108.5; a_09 = 108.5; a_10 = 108.2; a_11 = 108.6; a_12 = 108.6; b_01 = 130.4; b_02 = 131.3; b_03 = 131.5; b_04 = 130.9; b_05 = 131.3; b_06 = 132; b_07 = 132; b_08 = 131.7; b_09 = 132.2; b_10 = 131.5; b_11 = 132.3; b_12 = 133; Y = 4; A_1 = 108.2417; A_2 = 131.675; R = 1.2165; n = 48; g = 0.0502" .

hemo:7007215 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Calendar years 2015 and 2019 as a check on the averaging (HE-CF-CPI-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Entering January to December blocks instead gives 100.0083 for 2015, which rounds to the reference value of 100.0, and 107.8 for 2019, the published D7BT annual value, with a ratio of 1.0779 and an average annual rate of 0.0189 (computed here for illustration). `a_01 = 99.3; a_02 = 99.5; a_03 = 99.7; a_04 = 99.9; a_05 = 100.1; a_06 = 100.2; a_07 = 100; a_08 = 100.3; a_09 = 100.2; a_10 = 100.3; a_11 = 100.3; a_12 = 100.3; b_01 = 106.3; b_02 = 106.8; b_03 = 107; b_04 = 107.6; b_05 = 107.9; b_06 = 107.9; b_07 = 107.9; b_08 = 108.4; b_09 = 108.5; b_10 = 108.3; b_11 = 108.5; b_12 = 108.5; Y = 4; A_1 = 100.0083; A_2 = 107.8; R = 1.0779; n = 48; g = 0.0189`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "a_01 = 99.3; a_02 = 99.5; a_03 = 99.7; a_04 = 99.9; a_05 = 100.1; a_06 = 100.2; a_07 = 100; a_08 = 100.3; a_09 = 100.2; a_10 = 100.3; a_11 = 100.3; a_12 = 100.3; b_01 = 106.3; b_02 = 106.8; b_03 = 107; b_04 = 107.6; b_05 = 107.9; b_06 = 107.9; b_07 = 107.9; b_08 = 108.4; b_09 = 108.5; b_10 = 108.3; b_11 = 108.5; b_12 = 108.5; Y = 4; A_1 = 100.0083; A_2 = 107.8; R = 1.0779; n = 48; g = 0.0189" .

hemo:7007216 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Earlier financial-year average matches the article (HE-CF-CPI-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the April 2019 to March 2020 D7BT values in MonthsEarlier, FYAverageEarlier equals 108.2417 to four decimal places. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the calendar year 2019 entered instead, which gives 107.8. Excel check `=ABS(FYAverageEarlier-108.2417)<0.00005`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(FYAverageEarlier-108.2417)<0.00005" .

hemo:7007217 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Average rate compounds back to the later average (HE-CF-CPI-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The earlier average compounded at the result over YearsApart years equals the later average. The expected result is TRUE. FALSE shows the simple average rate of 0.0541 in AvgRateCFOut, which reaches 133.65 against 131.675. Excel check `=ABS(FYAverageEarlier*(1+AvgRateCFOut)^YearsApart-FYAverageLater)<1E-6`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(FYAverageEarlier*(1+AvgRateCFOut)^YearsApart-FYAverageLater)<1E-6" .

hemo:7007218 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's four programmes and GBP 900,000 (HE-CF-CELT-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A, B and C are funded in full and 0.375 of D, giving 97.5 QALYs for the whole budget, with a critical ratio of GBP 20,000 per QALY, as in step 1 of the article. `B = 900000; Delta_C_1 = 200000; Delta_E_1 = 40; Delta_C_2 = 300000; Delta_E_2 = 30; Delta_C_3 = 250000; Delta_E_3 = 20; Delta_C_4 = 400000; Delta_E_4 = 20; S_1 = 200000; S_2 = 500000; S_3 = 750000; x_1 = 1; x_2 = 1; x_3 = 1; x_4 = 0.375; H = 97.5; spend = 900000`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "B = 900000; Delta_C_1 = 200000; Delta_E_1 = 40; Delta_C_2 = 300000; Delta_E_2 = 30; Delta_C_3 = 250000; Delta_E_3 = 20; Delta_C_4 = 400000; Delta_E_4 = 20; S_1 = 200000; S_2 = 500000; S_3 = 750000; x_1 = 1; x_2 = 1; x_3 = 1; x_4 = 0.375; H = 97.5; spend = 900000" .

hemo:7007219 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Budget of GBP 700,000 (HE-CF-CELT-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With an illustrative smaller budget C receives 0.8 of its cost and D nothing, giving 86 QALYs and a critical ratio of GBP 12,500 per QALY. `B = 700000; Delta_C_1 = 200000; Delta_E_1 = 40; Delta_C_2 = 300000; Delta_E_2 = 30; Delta_C_3 = 250000; Delta_E_3 = 20; Delta_C_4 = 400000; Delta_E_4 = 20; S_1 = 200000; S_2 = 500000; S_3 = 750000; x_1 = 1; x_2 = 1; x_3 = 0.8; x_4 = 0; H = 86; spend = 700000`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "B = 700000; Delta_C_1 = 200000; Delta_E_1 = 40; Delta_C_2 = 300000; Delta_E_2 = 30; Delta_C_3 = 250000; Delta_E_3 = 20; Delta_C_4 = 400000; Delta_E_4 = 20; S_1 = 200000; S_2 = 500000; S_3 = 750000; x_1 = 1; x_2 = 1; x_3 = 0.8; x_4 = 0; H = 86; spend = 700000" .

hemo:7007220 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Budget above the cost of the whole table (HE-CF-CELT-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With an illustrative GBP 1,200,000 every programme is funded in full for 110 QALYs and GBP 50,000 is left, a limiting case in which the budget does not bind. `B = 1200000; Delta_C_1 = 200000; Delta_E_1 = 40; Delta_C_2 = 300000; Delta_E_2 = 30; Delta_C_3 = 250000; Delta_E_3 = 20; Delta_C_4 = 400000; Delta_E_4 = 20; S_1 = 200000; S_2 = 500000; S_3 = 750000; x_1 = 1; x_2 = 1; x_3 = 1; x_4 = 1; H = 110; spend = 1150000`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "B = 1200000; Delta_C_1 = 200000; Delta_E_1 = 40; Delta_C_2 = 300000; Delta_E_2 = 30; Delta_C_3 = 250000; Delta_E_3 = 20; Delta_C_4 = 400000; Delta_E_4 = 20; S_1 = 200000; S_2 = 500000; S_3 = 750000; x_1 = 1; x_2 = 1; x_3 = 1; x_4 = 1; H = 110; spend = 1150000" .

hemo:7007221 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's whole programmes P, Q and R, for the R and Python code (HE-CF-CELT-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "In whole mode with GBP 1,000,000, P is funded and neither Q nor R fits, giving 60 QALYs with GBP 400,000 left, as in step 3 of the article. The Math / Code line covers divisible programmes only, so this example is for reading against the R and Python versions, and its calculator form is HE-EX-CELT-007 under HE-FM-CELT-003. `celt_fill(c(\"P\", \"Q\", \"R\"), c(600000, 500000, 500000), c(60, 40, 40), 1000000, whole = TRUE)` returns health 60, spend 600000 and unspent 400000." ;
    hemo:9000014 "celt_fill(c(\"P\", \"Q\", \"R\"), c(600000, 500000, 500000), c(60, 40, 40), 1000000, whole = TRUE)" .

hemo:7007222 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Spending equals the budget or the cost of the whole table (HE-CF-CELT-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the shares in F2 to F5 and the costs in B2 to B5, the spending on divisible programmes equals the budget when the budget binds and the cost of every programme when it does not. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a share formula without the floor at zero, which at GBP 700,000 gives D a share of minus 0.125 and spending of GBP 650,000, or one without the cap at 1, which at GBP 1,200,000 gives spending of GBP 3,350,000. Excel check `=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(F2:F5,B2:B5)-MIN(Budget,SUM(B2:B5)))<0.01`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(F2:F5,B2:B5)-MIN(Budget,SUM(B2:B5)))<0.01" .

hemo:7007223 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's 97.5 QALYs reproduced (HE-CF-CELT-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's four programmes and GBP 900,000 the health in the fill is 97.5 QALYs. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows rows left sorted by incremental cost with the dearest first, D, B, C and A, which buy 66 QALYs. Excel check `=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(F2:F5,C2:C5)-97.5)<0.000001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(F2:F5,C2:C5)-97.5)<0.000001" .

hemo:7007224 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article state 21232 (HE-CF-CSVS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The UK tariff gives 0.088 and the Zimbabwe set 0.453, so the UK value is 0.365 lower. `l_MO = 2; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 2; l_PD = 3; l_AD = 2; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U_UK = 0.088; U_ZW = 0.453; dU = -0.365`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 2; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 2; l_PD = 3; l_AD = 2; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U_UK = 0.088; U_ZW = 0.453; dU = -0.365" .

hemo:7007225 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Jelsma and colleagues' state 22331 (HE-CF-CSVS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The Zimbabwe set gives 0.315, the value worked in the paper, and the UK tariff minus 0.003. `l_MO = 2; l_SC = 2; l_UA = 3; l_PD = 3; l_AD = 1; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U_UK = -0.003; U_ZW = 0.315; dU = -0.318`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 2; l_SC = 2; l_UA = 3; l_PD = 3; l_AD = 1; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U_UK = -0.003; U_ZW = 0.315; dU = -0.318" .

hemo:7007226 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Worst state 33333 (HE-CF-CSVS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The UK tariff gives minus 0.594 and the Zimbabwe set minus 0.145. `l_MO = 3; l_SC = 3; l_UA = 3; l_PD = 3; l_AD = 3; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U_UK = -0.594; U_ZW = -0.145; dU = -0.449`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 3; l_SC = 3; l_UA = 3; l_PD = 3; l_AD = 3; D = 1; N_3 = 1; U_UK = -0.594; U_ZW = -0.145; dU = -0.449" .

hemo:7007227 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Full health 11111 (HE-CF-CSVS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Both sets give 1, a limiting case. `l_MO = 1; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 1; l_PD = 1; l_AD = 1; D = 0; N_3 = 0; U_UK = 1; U_ZW = 1; dU = 0`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 1; l_SC = 1; l_UA = 1; l_PD = 1; l_AD = 1; D = 0; N_3 = 0; U_UK = 1; U_ZW = 1; dU = 0" .

hemo:7007228 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "State 33333 gap (HE-CF-CSVS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Levels at 33333 the cell CrossSetGap is minus 0.449, the UK minimum minus 0.594 less the Zimbabwe value minus 0.145. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the UK N3 decrement charged to the Zimbabwe set as well, which gives minus 0.180. Excel check `=ABS(CrossSetGap-(-0.594-(-0.145)))<0.0005`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(CrossSetGap-(-0.594-(-0.145)))<0.0005" .

hemo:7007229 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Jelsma and colleagues' state 22331 (HE-CF-CSVS-001) (HE-CF-CSVS-001 test 332f53137ce7)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Levels at 22331 the cell ZimUtility rounds to 0.315, the value worked in the paper. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the Zimbabwe constant left out, which gives 0.415. Excel check `=ROUND(ZimUtility,3)=0.315`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ROUND(ZimUtility,3)=0.315" .

hemo:7007230 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's five draws reproduced as a limiting case (HE-CF-PSA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With s_b0 equal to zero, rho equal to zero, s_b1 equal to 1 and the second standard normal values set to the logs of the article's rate ratios 0.4, 0.8, 0.8, 1 and 1, the five draws are the article's mortality rates 0.10, 0.20, 0.20, 0.25 and 0.25 against 0.25 on usual care. The function returns the article's incremental net health benefits, an expected value of 0.2 QALYs, a probability of 0.2 and expected losses of 0.28 and 0.48. The Monte Carlo standard error of about 0.561 QALYs is larger than the mean itself, and about 15,750 draws would be needed for a standard error of 0.01 if the spread of these five draws held. `mu_b0 = -1.3862944; s_b0 = 0; mu_b1 = 0; s_b1 = 1; rho = 0; z1_1 = 0; z1_2 = 0; z1_3 = 0; z1_4 = 0; z1_5 = 0; z2_1 = -0.9162907; z2_2 = -0.2231436; z2_3 = -0.2231436; z2_4 = 0; z2_5 = 0; q = 0.5; dC = 15000; lambda = 25000; e_target = 0.01; INHB_1 = 2.4; INHB_2 = -0.1; INHB_3 = -0.1; INHB_4 = -0.6; INHB_5 = -0.6; ENHB = 0.2; P_CE = 0.2; EL_new = 0.28; EL_comp = 0.48; SD_INHB = 1.25499; MCSE = 0.56125; N_req = 15750`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "mu_b0 = -1.3862944; s_b0 = 0; mu_b1 = 0; s_b1 = 1; rho = 0; z1_1 = 0; z1_2 = 0; z1_3 = 0; z1_4 = 0; z1_5 = 0; z2_1 = -0.9162907; z2_2 = -0.2231436; z2_3 = -0.2231436; z2_4 = 0; z2_5 = 0; q = 0.5; dC = 15000; lambda = 25000; e_target = 0.01; INHB_1 = 2.4; INHB_2 = -0.1; INHB_3 = -0.1; INHB_4 = -0.6; INHB_5 = -0.6; ENHB = 0.2; P_CE = 0.2; EL_new = 0.28; EL_comp = 0.48; SD_INHB = 1.25499; MCSE = 0.56125; N_req = 15750" .

hemo:7007231 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Five illustrative correlated draws (HE-CF-PSA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the illustrative log rate and log hazard ratio of HE-EX-PSA-001 (means minus 1.3862944 and minus 0.2231436, standard deviations 0.10 and 0.20, correlation minus 0.5), an incremental cost of GBP 15,000, a threshold of GBP 25,000 per QALY and five illustrative pairs of standard normal values, the expected incremental net health benefit is about minus 0.1009 QALYs, two draws in five favour the new option and the expected losses are about 0.2426 from adopting and 0.1417 from keeping the comparator. Five draws give a Monte Carlo standard error of about 0.205, so the result says nothing reliable about the sign. `mu_b0 = -1.3862944; s_b0 = 0.1; mu_b1 = -0.2231436; s_b1 = 0.2; rho = -0.5; z1_1 = 0.5; z1_2 = -1.0; z1_3 = 1.3; z1_4 = -0.2; z1_5 = 0.8; z2_1 = -1.2; z2_2 = 0.4; z2_3 = 0.9; z2_4 = -0.6; z2_5 = 1.5; q = 0.5; dC = 15000; lambda = 25000; e_target = 0.01; INHB_1 = 0.5751; INHB_2 = -0.47768; INHB_3 = -0.21705; INHB_4 = 0.13339; INHB_5 = -0.51823; ENHB = -0.10090; P_CE = 0.4; EL_new = 0.24259; EL_comp = 0.14170; SD_INHB = 0.45866; MCSE = 0.20512; N_req = 2103.72`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "mu_b0 = -1.3862944; s_b0 = 0.1; mu_b1 = -0.2231436; s_b1 = 0.2; rho = -0.5; z1_1 = 0.5; z1_2 = -1.0; z1_3 = 1.3; z1_4 = -0.2; z1_5 = 0.8; z2_1 = -1.2; z2_2 = 0.4; z2_3 = 0.9; z2_4 = -0.6; z2_5 = 1.5; q = 0.5; dC = 15000; lambda = 25000; e_target = 0.01; INHB_1 = 0.5751; INHB_2 = -0.47768; INHB_3 = -0.21705; INHB_4 = 0.13339; INHB_5 = -0.51823; ENHB = -0.10090; P_CE = 0.4; EL_new = 0.24259; EL_comp = 0.14170; SD_INHB = 0.45866; MCSE = 0.20512; N_req = 2103.72" .

hemo:7007232 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's expected value and probability reproduced (HE-CF-PSA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the inputs of the first worked example in the Excel columns, the mean of DrawIncNHB rounds to 0.2 and the share of positive draws is 0.2. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the hazard ratio applied by division, so that survival is 4 times the hazard ratio, which gives a mean of minus 1.0 and no positive draw. Excel check `=AND(ROUND(AVERAGE(DrawIncNHB),4)=0.2,COUNTIF(DrawIncNHB,\">0\")/COUNT(DrawIncNHB)=0.2)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(AVERAGE(DrawIncNHB),4)=0.2,COUNTIF(DrawIncNHB,\">0\")/COUNT(DrawIncNHB)=0.2)" .

hemo:7007233 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Five frozen correlated draws reproduced (HE-CF-PSA-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the inputs of HE-EX-PSA-001 in the named cells, QALYPerLifeYear at 0.5, IncCost at 15000, Threshold at 25000 and the five standard normal pairs of the second worked example frozen in columns A and B, the mean of DrawIncNHB rounds to minus 0.1009 and two of the five draws are positive. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the correlation left out of the draws, CholOffDiag at zero and CholDiagSecond equal to SDLogHR, which gives a mean of about minus 0.1526, or the upper triangular factor used without transposing, which gives about minus 0.1817. Excel check `=AND(ROUND(AVERAGE(DrawIncNHB),4)=-0.1009,COUNTIF(DrawIncNHB,\">0\")/COUNT(DrawIncNHB)=0.4)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(AVERAGE(DrawIncNHB),4)=-0.1009,COUNTIF(DrawIncNHB,\">0\")/COUNT(DrawIncNHB)=0.4)" .

hemo:7007234 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Office visits, chemotherapy and one three-night stay (HE-CF-PTC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Illustrative counts of 4 office visits, 6 chemotherapy visits and one stay of 3 nights give 4,486.4 minutes, 74.7733 hours and an annual patient time cost of USD 1,238.99. `n_off = 4; n_chemo = 6; n_stay = 1; n_night = 3; m_off = 51.6; m_chemo = 168.8; m_trav = 35.2; m_night = 960; w = 16.57; h_T = 74.7733; C_T = 1238.99`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_off = 4; n_chemo = 6; n_stay = 1; n_night = 3; m_off = 51.6; m_chemo = 168.8; m_trav = 35.2; m_night = 960; w = 16.57; h_T = 74.7733; C_T = 1238.99" .

hemo:7007235 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Hospital nights counted as 24 hours (HE-CF-PTC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Yabroff and colleagues tested 24 hours per hospital day in a sensitivity analysis. With 1,440 minutes per night the same counts give 98.7733 hours and USD 1,636.67. `n_off = 4; n_chemo = 6; n_stay = 1; n_night = 3; m_off = 51.6; m_chemo = 168.8; m_trav = 35.2; m_night = 1440; w = 16.57; h_T = 98.7733; C_T = 1636.67`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_off = 4; n_chemo = 6; n_stay = 1; n_night = 3; m_off = 51.6; m_chemo = 168.8; m_trav = 35.2; m_night = 1440; w = 16.57; h_T = 98.7733; C_T = 1636.67" .

hemo:7007236 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "No service use (HE-CF-PTC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With no uses of any service the hours and the time cost are zero, a limiting case. `n_off = 0; n_chemo = 0; n_stay = 0; n_night = 0; m_off = 51.6; m_chemo = 168.8; m_trav = 35.2; m_night = 960; w = 16.57; h_T = 0; C_T = 0`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_off = 0; n_chemo = 0; n_stay = 0; n_night = 0; m_off = 51.6; m_chemo = 168.8; m_trav = 35.2; m_night = 960; w = 16.57; h_T = 0; C_T = 0" .

hemo:7007237 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "One office visit with travel (HE-CF-PTC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a count of 1 in the office row and 0 elsewhere, AnnualPatientTimeCost equals 51.6 plus 35.2 minutes at USD 16.57 an hour, USD 23.97. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows travel left out of the office row, which gives 14.25, or the minutes not divided by 60, which gives 1,438.28. Excel check `=ABS(AnnualPatientTimeCost-(51.6+35.2)/60*16.57)<0.005`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AnnualPatientTimeCost-(51.6+35.2)/60*16.57)<0.005" .

hemo:7007238 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Hospital nights at 16 waking hours (HE-CF-PTC-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With one stay of 3 nights and no other use, AnnualPatientTimeCost equals 35.2 plus 2,880 minutes at USD 16.57 an hour, USD 805.08. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the nights counted at 24 hours, which gives USD 1,202.76, or travel added to every night as well as the stay, which gives USD 834.24. Excel check `=ABS(AnnualPatientTimeCost-(35.2+3*960)/60*16.57)<0.005`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(AnnualPatientTimeCost-(35.2+3*960)/60*16.57)<0.005" .

hemo:7007239 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "England set, state 23245 (HE-CF-EQ5L-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The England coefficients give 0.247, the value worked in Table 2 of Devlin and colleagues. `l_MO = 2; l_SC = 3; l_UA = 2; l_PD = 4; l_AD = 5; c_0 = 0; b_MO2 = 0.058; b_MO3 = 0.076; b_MO4 = 0.207; b_MO5 = 0.274; b_SC2 = 0.050; b_SC3 = 0.080; b_SC4 = 0.164; b_SC5 = 0.203; b_UA2 = 0.050; b_UA3 = 0.063; b_UA4 = 0.162; b_UA5 = 0.184; b_PD2 = 0.063; b_PD3 = 0.084; b_PD4 = 0.276; b_PD5 = 0.335; b_AD2 = 0.078; b_AD3 = 0.104; b_AD4 = 0.285; b_AD5 = 0.289; D = 1; U = 0.247`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_MO = 2; l_SC = 3; l_UA = 2; l_PD = 4; l_AD = 5; c_0 = 0; b_MO2 = 0.058; b_MO3 = 0.076; b_MO4 = 0.207; b_MO5 = 0.274; b_SC2 = 0.050; b_SC3 = 0.080; b_SC4 = 0.164; b_SC5 = 0.203; b_UA2 = 0.050; b_UA3 = 0.063; b_UA4 = 0.162; b_UA5 = 0.184; b_PD2 = 0.063; b_PD3 = 0.084; b_PD4 = 0.276; b_PD5 = 0.335; b_AD2 = 0.078; b_AD3 = 0.104; b_AD4 = 0.285; b_AD5 = 0.289; D = 1; U = 0.247" .

