hemo:7007242 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Implementation cell against the Table 2 example (HE-CF-EQ5L-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Levels set to 2, 3, 2, 4 and 5, the England decrements in the four ranges and Const at 0, ProfileUtility equals 1 minus the five Table 2 decrements for 23245. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows misaligned ranges, for example DecSlight and DecModerate swapped, which gives 0.246. Excel check `=ABS(ProfileUtility-(1-0.058-0.080-0.050-0.276-0.289))<0.000001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(ProfileUtility-(1-0.058-0.080-0.050-0.276-0.289))<0.000001" .

hemo:7007243 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "England worst state and states below zero (HE-CF-EQ5L-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With Levels set to 5, 5, 5, 5 and 5, the England decrements in the four ranges and Const at 0, ProfileUtility rounds to minus 0.285 and lies below zero, the minimum given in section 3.4 of Devlin and colleagues. Scoring all 3,125 states with the R or Python code gives 159 below zero, 5.1%, as in Table 3, and a minimum other than minus 0.285 or a count other than 159 there shows a coefficient mistyped or a level misread. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a level 5 decrement entered wrongly, for example the anxiety or depression severe value 0.285 entered in DecWorst in place of 0.289, which gives minus 0.281. Excel check `=AND(ROUND(ProfileUtility,3)=-0.285,ProfileUtility<0)`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=AND(ROUND(ProfileUtility,3)=-0.285,ProfileUtility<0)" .

hemo:7007244 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Older person holding the stock at 100 (HE-CF-HPF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With a stock of 100, depreciation of 0.25 and a target of 100, the gross investment required is 25, the outlay 1,000 GBP and the mix 12.5 units of care and 50 hours, as in the article. `H_t = 100; delta_t = 0.25; H_target = 100; P = 40; W = 10; K = 0.5; rho_H = 0.03; E = 0; I_req = 25; pi = 40; C = 1000; M = 12.5; TH = 50`" ;
