hemo:7007245 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Younger person raising the stock to 105 (HE-CF-HPF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With depreciation of 0.15 the article's 20 units of gross investment raise the stock of 100 to 105, so a target of 105 needs 800 GBP, 10 units of care and 40 hours. `H_t = 100; delta_t = 0.15; H_target = 105; P = 40; W = 10; K = 0.5; rho_H = 0.03; E = 0; I_req = 20; pi = 40; C = 800; M = 10; TH = 40`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "H_t = 100; delta_t = 0.15; H_target = 105; P = 40; W = 10; K = 0.5; rho_H = 0.03; E = 0; I_req = 20; pi = 40; C = 800; M = 10; TH = 40" .

hemo:7007246 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Target below the depreciated stock (HE-CF-HPF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "A target of 80 with depreciation of 0.15 is below the 85 units left after depreciation, so no gross investment is required, the outlay is zero and the stock ends at 85, above the target, a limiting case (computed here for illustration). `H_t = 100; delta_t = 0.15; H_target = 80; P = 40; W = 10; K = 0.5; rho_H = 0.03; E = 0; I_req = 0; pi = 40; C = 0; M = 0; TH = 0`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "H_t = 100; delta_t = 0.15; H_target = 80; P = 40; W = 10; K = 0.5; rho_H = 0.03; E = 0; I_req = 0; pi = 40; C = 0; M = 0; TH = 0" .

hemo:7007247 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Older person holding the stock (HE-CF-HPF-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With HealthStock 100, DeprRate 0.25, TargetStock 100, PriceCare 40, Wage 10, TimeShare 0.5 and SchoolingYears 0, HoldOutlay equals 25 units at 40 GBP, 1,000 GBP. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the depreciation rate used in place of one minus the rate, which requires 75 units and gives 3,000, or only the net change in the stock financed, which gives 0. Excel check `=ABS(HoldOutlay-25*40)<0.005`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(HoldOutlay-25*40)<0.005" .

hemo:7007248 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Younger person raising the stock to 105 (HE-CF-HPF-001) (HE-CF-HPF-001 test 73ecc0ac4b81)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With HealthStock 100, DeprRate 0.15 and TargetStock 105 and the same prices, HoldOutlay equals the article's 800 GBP. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows only the net change of 5 units financed, which gives 200, or depreciation charged on the target stock in place of the starting stock, which requires 20.75 units and gives 830. Excel check `=ABS(HoldOutlay-800)<0.005`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(HoldOutlay-800)<0.005" .

hemo:7007249 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's USD 50,000 specific attachment point (HE-CF-ATTP-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Ten members are expected above the attachment point, expected reimbursement is USD 900,000 with a standard deviation of about USD 485,222, and the illustrative premium at a 30% loading is USD 1,170,000. `c = 1; p_1 = 0.006; C_1 = 75000; p_2 = 0.003; C_2 = 150000; p_3 = 0.001; C_3 = 500000; n = 1000; theta = 0.3; A = 50000; U = 500000; E_R = 900; M2_R = 236250000; V_R = 235440000; SD_R = 15344.05; N_A = 10; E_T = 900000; SD_T = 485221.6; P_T = 1170000; CV_T = 0.5391`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "c = 1; p_1 = 0.006; C_1 = 75000; p_2 = 0.003; C_2 = 150000; p_3 = 0.001; C_3 = 500000; n = 1000; theta = 0.3; A = 50000; U = 500000; E_R = 900; M2_R = 236250000; V_R = 235440000; SD_R = 15344.05; N_A = 10; E_T = 900000; SD_T = 485221.6; P_T = 1170000; CV_T = 0.5391" .

