    hemo:9000008 "The scores are 2.667, 4.205 and 1.538 per 10,000, the mean 3.333 and the variance 1.083 (GPs per 10,000, squared), as in the article. `S_X = 8; S_Y = 4; P_1 = 10000; P_2 = 20000; P_3 = 6000; d_1X = 10; d_1Y = 40; d_2X = 20; d_2Y = 25; d_3X = 45; d_3Y = 15; d_0 = 30; k = 10000; R_X = 0.000266667; R_Y = 0.000153846; A_1 = 0.000266667; A_2 = 0.000420513; A_3 = 0.000153846; M = 3.3333; V = 1.0826`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_X = 8; S_Y = 4; P_1 = 10000; P_2 = 20000; P_3 = 6000; d_1X = 10; d_1Y = 40; d_2X = 20; d_2Y = 25; d_3X = 45; d_3Y = 15; d_0 = 30; k = 10000; R_X = 0.000266667; R_Y = 0.000153846; A_1 = 0.000266667; A_2 = 0.000420513; A_3 = 0.000153846; M = 3.3333; V = 1.0826" .

hemo:7007313 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's consolidation at practice X (HE-CF-ACCS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With all 12 GPs at X the mean stays at 3.333 and the variance rises to 2.222, as in the article. `S_X = 12; S_Y = 0; P_1 = 10000; P_2 = 20000; P_3 = 6000; d_1X = 10; d_1Y = 40; d_2X = 20; d_2Y = 25; d_3X = 45; d_3Y = 15; d_0 = 30; k = 10000; R_X = 0.0004; R_Y = 0; A_1 = 0.0004; A_2 = 0.0004; A_3 = 0; M = 3.3333; V = 2.2222`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_X = 12; S_Y = 0; P_1 = 10000; P_2 = 20000; P_3 = 6000; d_1X = 10; d_1Y = 40; d_2X = 20; d_2Y = 25; d_3X = 45; d_3Y = 15; d_0 = 30; k = 10000; R_X = 0.0004; R_Y = 0; A_1 = 0.0004; A_2 = 0.0004; A_3 = 0; M = 3.3333; V = 2.2222" .

hemo:7007314 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Supply conserved over any number of sites (HE-CF-ACCS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The population-weighted sum of AccessColumn equals the total of SupplyRow when every provider has someone within the threshold. Expected result TRUE. With the article's inputs, a doubled AccessColumn gives 24 against 12, a halved one 6, and a RatioRow divided by each provider's own neighbourhood only 41.33, all FALSE. Excel check `=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(PopColumn,AccessColumn)-SUM(SupplyRow))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(PopColumn,AccessColumn)-SUM(SupplyRow))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007315 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's consolidation variance (HE-CF-ACCS-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With SupplyRow 12 and 0 and the article's populations and times, VarAccessCF times 10,000 squared is 2.2222 within 0.0001. Expected result TRUE. The base inputs give 1.0826 and FALSE, an unweighted variance of the three scores gives 3.5556 and FALSE, and doubling (4.4444) or halving (1.1111) the cell also gives FALSE. Excel check `=ABS(VarAccessCF*10000^2-2.2222)<0.0001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(VarAccessCF*10000^2-2.2222)<0.0001" .

hemo:7007316 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's inputs at beta of 1 (HE-CF-ACCS-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The scores are 4.440, 2.978 and 2.672 per 10,000, the mean 3.333 and the variance 0.483 (computed here). `S_X = 8; S_Y = 4; P_1 = 10000; P_2 = 20000; P_3 = 6000; d_1X = 10; d_1Y = 40; d_2X = 20; d_2Y = 25; d_3X = 45; d_3Y = 15; beta = 1; k = 10000; V_X = 2133.333; V_Y = 1450; A_1 = 0.000443966; A_2 = 0.000297845; A_3 = 0.000267241; M = 3.3333; V = 0.4828`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_X = 8; S_Y = 4; P_1 = 10000; P_2 = 20000; P_3 = 6000; d_1X = 10; d_1Y = 40; d_2X = 20; d_2Y = 25; d_3X = 45; d_3Y = 15; beta = 1; k = 10000; V_X = 2133.333; V_Y = 1450; A_1 = 0.000443966; A_2 = 0.000297845; A_3 = 0.000267241; M = 3.3333; V = 0.4828" .

hemo:7007317 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's inputs at beta of 2 (HE-CF-ACCS-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The scores are 5.615, 2.293 and 2.997 per 10,000 and the variance 2.066 (computed here). `S_X = 8; S_Y = 4; P_1 = 10000; P_2 = 20000; P_3 = 6000; d_1X = 10; d_1Y = 40; d_2X = 20; d_2Y = 25; d_3X = 45; d_3Y = 15; beta = 2; k = 10000; V_X = 152.963; V_Y = 64.917; A_1 = 0.000561513; A_2 = 0.000229339; A_3 = 0.000299683; M = 3.3333; V = 2.066`" ;
