hemo:7007318 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Supply conserved under gravity decay (HE-CF-ACCS-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The population-weighted sum of AccessColumnG equals the total of SupplyRow for any BetaCF. Expected result TRUE. With the article's inputs at BetaCF 1, a doubled AccessColumnG gives 24 against 12, a halved one 6, and scores without the division by DemandRow 22,866.7, all FALSE. Excel check `=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(PopColumn,AccessColumnG)-SUM(SupplyRow))<1E-9`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SUMPRODUCT(PopColumn,AccessColumnG)-SUM(SupplyRow))<1E-9" .

hemo:7007319 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article's neighbourhood B at beta of 1 (HE-CF-ACCS-002)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "The second cell of AccessColumnG times 10,000 is 2.9784 within 0.0001 for the article's inputs at BetaCF 1. Expected result TRUE. BetaCF entered as minus 1 gives 3.0880 and FALSE, and doubling (5.9569) or halving (1.4892) the cell also gives FALSE. Excel check `=ABS(INDEX(AccessColumnG,2)*10000-2.9784)<0.0001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(INDEX(AccessColumnG,2)*10000-2.9784)<0.0001" .

hemo:7007320 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Article baseline with illustrative survey sizes (HE-CF-ALE-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the article's baseline life table and prevalence and illustrative samples of 2,000, 1,500 and 800 respondents, active life expectancy is 14.475 years with a standard error of 0.1083 and a 95% interval of 14.2626 to 14.6874 years (computed here). The 85 and over band, with the smallest sample and a prevalence of one half, contributes 24% of the variance (derived). `l_x = 100000; L_1 = 900000; L_2 = 650000; L_3 = 300000; pi_1 = 0.1; pi_2 = 0.25; pi_3 = 0.5; N_1 = 2000; N_2 = 1500; N_3 = 800; w_1 = 9; w_2 = 6.5; w_3 = 3; ALE_x = 14.475; V_ALE = 0.0117; SE_ALE = 0.1083; lo_ALE = 14.2626; hi_ALE = 14.6874`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_x = 100000; L_1 = 900000; L_2 = 650000; L_3 = 300000; pi_1 = 0.1; pi_2 = 0.25; pi_3 = 0.5; N_1 = 2000; N_2 = 1500; N_3 = 800; w_1 = 9; w_2 = 6.5; w_3 = 3; ALE_x = 14.475; V_ALE = 0.0117; SE_ALE = 0.1083; lo_ALE = 14.2626; hi_ALE = 14.6874" .

hemo:7007321 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Same table with four times the respondents (HE-CF-ALE-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000007 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With 8,000, 6,000 and 3,200 respondents the variance falls to a quarter and the standard error halves to 0.0542 years, an interval of 14.3688 to 14.5812 (computed here). `l_x = 100000; L_1 = 900000; L_2 = 650000; L_3 = 300000; pi_1 = 0.1; pi_2 = 0.25; pi_3 = 0.5; N_1 = 8000; N_2 = 6000; N_3 = 3200; w_1 = 9; w_2 = 6.5; w_3 = 3; ALE_x = 14.475; V_ALE = 0.0029; SE_ALE = 0.0542; lo_ALE = 14.3688; hi_ALE = 14.5812`" ;
    hemo:9000014 "l_x = 100000; L_1 = 900000; L_2 = 650000; L_3 = 300000; pi_1 = 0.1; pi_2 = 0.25; pi_3 = 0.5; N_1 = 8000; N_2 = 6000; N_3 = 3200; w_1 = 9; w_2 = 6.5; w_3 = 3; ALE_x = 14.475; V_ALE = 0.0029; SE_ALE = 0.0542; lo_ALE = 14.3688; hi_ALE = 14.5812" .

hemo:7007322 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Standard error at the article baseline (HE-CF-ALE-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the inputs of the first worked example, SullivanSE is compared with the hand value 0.1083. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a variance that uses the weights unsquared, which gives 0.0464, and a doubled (0.2167) or halved (0.0542) cell. Excel check `=ABS(SullivanSE-0.1083)<0.0001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SullivanSE-0.1083)<0.0001" .

hemo:7007323 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Four times the respondents halve the standard error (HE-CF-ALE-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With SurveyRespondentsBandCF set to 8,000, 6,000 and 3,200, SullivanSE is compared with 0.0542, half the baseline value. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows the baseline respondents left in place (0.1083), and a doubled (0.1083) or halved (0.0271) cell. Excel check `=ABS(SullivanSE-0.0542)<0.0001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SullivanSE-0.0542)<0.0001" .

hemo:7007324 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000015 ;
    rdfs:label "Lower limit of the 95% interval at the article baseline (HE-CF-ALE-001)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000036 hemo:4000009 ;
    hemo:9000008 "With the inputs of the first worked example, SullivanLower is compared with 14.2626. Expected result TRUE. FALSE shows a limit built from the variance in place of the standard error, 14.4520, and a doubled (28.5253) or halved (7.1313) cell. Excel check `=ABS(SullivanLower-14.2626)<0.0001`" ;
    hemo:9000024 "=ABS(SullivanLower-14.2626)<0.0001" .

hemo:7007325 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Strictly better on both"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Strict dominance needs a lower cost and a greater effect, each beyond its tolerance." .

hemo:7007326 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Mirror of the dominance rule"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "An option is dominated exactly when its comparator dominates it, so the rule is HE-FM-DOM-001 with both differences reversed." .

hemo:7007327 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Four exclusive outcomes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "Exactly one of the four outcomes holds for every pair of differences, so they sum to 1." .

hemo:7007328 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "A duplicate is merged"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "An option with the cost and effect of its comparator is a duplicate to merge with it, as module assumption HE-AS-DOM-004 says, and is neither dominant nor dominated." .

hemo:7007329 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Two options"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The decision is between two options, so the net benefit of the best option is the larger of 0 and the incremental net benefit." .

hemo:7007330 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Inner loop large enough"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "A small inner loop biases the estimate upwards, because the maximum of a noisy mean exceeds the maximum of the true mean on average." .

hemo:7007331 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "Weight on the gain only"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:9000008 "The weight multiplies the QALY gain of the option and not the health forgone through its cost." .

