    hemo:1000008 hemo:6005243,
        hemo:6005244,
        hemo:6005245,
        hemo:6005246,
        hemo:6005247,
        hemo:6005248 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Maps the payoffs of two players, each with two pure strategies, over the four strategy pairs to the game's Nash equilibria, the pairs in which each player's strategy is a best reply to the other's, u_i(s_i*, s_-i*) >= u_i(s_i, s_-i*) for every strategy s_i of every player i, as in the article's display. The general condition over any finite strategy sets has no calculator form. For a 2 x 2 game HE-FM-NASH-001 tests each of the four cells as a pure-strategy equilibrium and classifies it as strict or weak, HE-FM-NASH-002 gives the mixed equilibrium in which each player randomises so as to leave the other indifferent, and HE-CF-NASH-001 lists every equilibrium of a game without payoff ties and values the outcome of mixed play. Each player's expected payoff at the mixed equilibrium and the expected value of an outcome measure such as total surplus are probability-weighted sums, the form of HE-FM-CHN-001, and the probability of each cell under independent mixing is the product of HE-FM-CHN-002, so neither is restated. Dominance between interventions in cost-effectiveness analysis (HE-FM-DOM-001) compares the incremental cost and effect of options for one decision maker and is a different test. The Nash bargaining solution (HE-FN-BARG-001, with the negotiated price of HE-FM-BARG-001) divides a surplus between parties who can make a binding agreement, Rubinstein's first proposer's share (HE-FM-BARG-003) comes from the perfect equilibrium of a sequential alternating-offers game, and the voluntary vaccination coverage of HE-FM-VEXT-003 is the equilibrium of a population game solved through an infection risk; all are separate records. Notation follows the Nash Equilibrium article, with u_jk and v_jk for the row and column players' payoffs when the row player chooses its strategy j and the column player its strategy k." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Nash equilibria of a two-player game with two strategies each" ;
    hemo:9000014 "e(u_11, u_12, u_21, u_22, v_11, v_12, v_21, v_22) = (NE_11, NE_12, NE_21, NE_22, p_star, q_star)" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-FN-NASH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "nash-equilibria-of-a-two-player-game-with-two-strategies-each" .

