        hemo:6003874,
        hemo:6003875 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005601 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007076,
        hemo:7007077,
        hemo:7007078,
        hemo:7007079,
        hemo:7007080 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes a level yearly amount, the number of periods and one parameter used both as the hyperbolic alpha and as the constant rate, and returns the sum of the simple hyperbolic weights, the sum of the constant-rate factors, the two weighted totals and their ratio. It builds one weight for each period, because the hyperbolic sum has no simple closed form, and so shows how much more weight the hyperbola gives to later periods than HE-FM-DISC-001 does at the same first-period rate. The inputs therefore differ from the formula's variables, which describe one delay." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for a yearly stream weighted by the simple hyperbola against constant-rate discounting" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Frederick S, Loewenstein G, O'Donoghue T. Time discounting and time preference: a critical review. Journal of Economic Literature. 2002;40(2) 351-401. Page 360 and footnote 13 for the simple hyperbola D(t) = 1/(1 + alpha t). National Institute for Health and Care Excellence. NICE technology appraisal and highly specialised technologies guidance, the manual (PMG36). Chapter 4, economic evaluation. Published 31 January 2022, last updated 13 October 2026. Section 4.5.1 for the constant 3.5% rate of the reference case." ;
    hemo:9000011 "Reading the hyperbolic total as a reference-case result. Reporting 16.20 QALYs in place of 14.71 would raise the discounted gain by about 10% through a weighting that NICE does not use for the reference case; the hyperbolic total belongs in a description of how individuals value the stream" ;
    hemo:9000014 "S_H = sum_(t=1)^T [1 / (1 + alpha * t)]; S_E = sum_(t=1)^T [(1 + alpha)^(-t)]; Q_H = q * S_H; Q_E = q * S_E; ratio = Q_H / Q_E" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-HYPD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-a-yearly-stream-weighted-by-the-simple-hyperbola-against-constant-rate-discounting" .

hemo:5000842 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "Computational function for a smaller-sooner against larger-later plan check with commitment thresholds under a chosen discount form"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-CF-HYPD-002" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000002 hemo:5000634 ;
    hemo:1000005 hemo:7005615,
        hemo:7005616,
        hemo:7005617 ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6003528,
        hemo:6003529,
        hemo:6003530,
        hemo:6003531,
        hemo:6003532,
        hemo:6003533,
        hemo:6003534,
        hemo:6003535,
        hemo:6003536,
        hemo:6003876,
        hemo:6003877,
        hemo:6004769,
        hemo:6004770 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6003528,
        hemo:6003529,
        hemo:6003530,
        hemo:6003531,
        hemo:6003536,
        hemo:6003876,
        hemo:6004770 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6003532,
        hemo:6003533,
        hemo:6003534,
        hemo:6003535,
        hemo:6003877,
        hemo:6004769 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005610 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007081,
        hemo:7007082,
        hemo:7007083,
        hemo:7007084,
        hemo:7007085,
        hemo:7007086 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the two amounts, a choice of discount form and its parameters, builds the weights at delays 0, 1 and 2, and returns the two margins of HE-FM-HYPD-005, whether the plan reverses, the penalty on the sooner outcome felt now that would tip today's choice, the reward paid with the later outcome that would do the same, and the first whole delay at which waiting is preferred. The penalty is minus M_0 and the reward minus M_0 divided by w_1, so their ratio is the timing premium 1/w_1 in step 4 of the article's example. The inputs therefore differ from the formula's variables, which take the weights as given." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for a smaller-sooner against larger-later plan check with commitment thresholds under a chosen discount form" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Frederick S, Loewenstein G, O'Donoghue T. Time discounting and time preference: a critical review. Journal of Economic Literature. 2002;40(2) 351-401. Section 5.1, pages 366 to 368, on time-inconsistent preferences under non-exponential discounting, precommitment, and commitment devices for sophisticated and naive people. Attema AE, Brouwer WBF, Claxton K. Discounting in economic evaluations. PharmacoEconomics. 2018;36(7) 745-758. Section on discount models, on a preference between two programmes reversing within a year with nothing changed." ;
    hemo:9000011 "Reward sized as if paid now. Offering the 0.991 penalty threshold as a reward paid with next month's health gain leaves today's choice unchanged, since 13.991 times 0.693 is about 9.70, still below 10; a reward paid then needs to exceed about 1.430 (computed here for illustration)" ;
    hemo:9000014 "w_1 = beta * delta; w_2 = beta * delta^2; M_0 = b * w_1 - a; M_1 = b * w_2 - a * w_1; P = max(a - b * w_1, 0); R = max(a / w_1 - b, 0)" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-HYPD-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-a-smaller-sooner-against-larger-later-plan-check-with-commitment-thresholds-under-a-chosen-discount-form" .

