    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005629 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007092,
        hemo:7007093,
        hemo:7007094,
        hemo:7007095,
        hemo:7007096 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the number of patients, the equity weight, the incremental QALYs and the incremental cost per patient in each group, and one value of a QALY, and returns the programme's population QALY gain unweighted and weighted, its total incremental cost, the health displaced, the unweighted and weighted net health benefit and the unweighted and weighted ICER. It applies HE-FM-EQWA-001 to the group totals and HE-FM-EQWA-003 to the whole programme, and it is run once at GBP 25,000 and once at GBP 35,000 per QALY to give the four net health benefits PMG36 asks for. The Math / Code line shows two groups, and the R and Python versions take any number." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for weighted and unweighted population net health benefit across several groups" ;
    hemo:9000010 "National Institute for Health and Care Excellence. NICE technology appraisal and highly specialised technologies guidance: the manual (PMG36). Published 31 January 2022, last updated 13 October 2026. Chapter 6 Committee recommendations, section 6.3.2, which asks for net health benefit at GBP 25,000 and GBP 35,000 per QALY, both with and without the QALY weighting applied, and chapter 4 Economic evaluation, section 4.9.1, which asks for clinical and cost-effectiveness estimates separately for each relevant subgroup of patients. Cookson R, Mirelman AJ, Griffin S, Asaria M, Dawkins B, Norheim OF, Verguet S, Culyer AJ. Using cost-effectiveness analysis to address health equity concerns. Value in Health. 2017;20(2):206-212. Section on equity-weighting analysis, on weights applied to the health benefits of people with different characteristics. https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Reading a positive pooled result as a gain in every group. At GBP 35,000 per QALY the pooled unweighted net health benefit is about 2.9 QALYs, yet subgroup A alone loses about 77.1 QALYs and subgroup B gains 80.0. PMG36 asks for cost-effectiveness estimates separately for each relevant subgroup (section 4.9.1), so pooled figures are reported beside the subgroup values, not in place of them" ;
    hemo:9000014 "E_u = N_1 * dE_1 + N_2 * dE_2; E_w = N_1 * w_1 * dE_1 + N_2 * w_2 * dE_2; C_tot = N_1 * dC_1 + N_2 * dC_2; H_d = C_tot / lambda; NHB_u = E_u - H_d; NHB_w = E_w - H_d; ICER_u = C_tot / E_u; ICER_w = C_tot / E_w" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-EQWA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-weighted-and-unweighted-population-net-health-benefit-across-several-groups" .

hemo:5000845 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "Computational function for DALYs averted and cost per DALY averted from deaths, disability and duration in two scenarios"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-CF-DALY-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000002 hemo:5000644,
        hemo:5000645,
        hemo:5000646 ;
    hemo:1000005 hemo:7005641,
        hemo:7005642,
        hemo:7005643 ;
