        hemo:6003548 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6003549,
        hemo:6003550,
        hemo:6003551,
        hemo:6003552,
        hemo:6003553,
        hemo:6003554,
        hemo:6004781 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005638 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007097,
        hemo:7007098,
        hemo:7007099,
        hemo:7007100 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the size of a cohort, its deaths and the survivors' disability weight with and without a programme, the duration of the condition, the standard remaining life expectancy at the age of death, an optional continuous discount rate and the extra cost, and returns each scenario's DALYs, the DALYs averted, the share of them that comes from deaths prevented and the cost per DALY averted. It sets the survivors in each scenario to the cohort less its deaths, so the people saved by the programme are counted as living with the condition, and it chains HE-FM-DALY-002 or HE-FM-DALY-004 with HE-FM-DALY-003. The inputs therefore differ from the formulas' variables, which take survivors and DALY totals as given." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for DALYs averted and cost per DALY averted from deaths, disability and duration in two scenarios" ;
    hemo:9000010 "World Health Organization. WHO methods and data sources for global burden of disease estimates 2000-2019. Global Health Estimates Technical Paper WHO/DDI/DNA/GHE/2020.3. Geneva, WHO, 2020 (full text read). Section 2 on DALYs as YLLs plus YLDs and on the YLL and YLD formulas. Larson BA. Calculating disability-adjusted-life-years lost (DALYs) in discrete-time. Cost Effectiveness and Resource Allocation. 2013;11 article 18 (full text read). Equations 1 and 2 on continuously discounted years of life lost and years lived with disability. Bertram MY, Lauer JA, Stenberg K, Tan Torres Edejer T. Methods for the economic evaluation of health care interventions for priority setting in the health system, an update from WHO CHOICE. International Journal of Health Policy and Management. 2021;10(11) 673-677 (full text read). Cost per DALY as the WHO-CHOICE outcome, with health benefits undiscounted and at 3%. https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/gho-documents/global-health-estimates/ghe2019_daly-methods.pdf" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Survivors held fixed when deaths fall. Entering the survivors directly and leaving them at 180 in the programme scenario credits 900 DALYs averted in place of 888 undiscounted and lowers the cost per DALY averted to about USD 493 (computed here for illustration). Setting survivors to the cohort less its deaths avoids this" ;
    hemo:9000014 "f_L = (1 - exp(-r * L)) / r; f_T = (1 - exp(-r * T)) / r; DALY_0 = D_0 * f_L + (N - D_0) * DW_0 * f_T; DALY_1 = D_1 * f_L + (N - D_1) * DW_1 * f_T; DALY_av = DALY_0 - DALY_1; share_YLL = (D_0 - D_1) * f_L / DALY_av; CPD = dC / DALY_av" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-DALY-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-dalys-averted-and-cost-per-daly-averted-from-deaths-disability-and-duration-in-two-scenarios" .

hemo:5000846 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "Computational function for scoring an EQ-5D-3L profile under any constant and N3 coefficient set"@en ;
