    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005682 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007121,
        hemo:7007122,
        hemo:7007123,
        hemo:7007124 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the per-arm summaries a trial report gives, the mean effect and cost in each arm, their standard deviations, the within-arm correlation and the arm size, together with a threshold, and returns incremental net benefit on the money and health scales with its standard error, interval and z statistic, plus the ICER. It first builds the variances and covariance of the two mean differences from the arm summaries, the inputs that HE-FM-AN-004 and HE-CF-AN-001 start from, then forms incremental net monetary benefit and divides by lambda to return the net health benefit of HE-FM-NBA-001, Stinnett and Mullahy's equation 7. The ICER is returned for reading with the quadrant rule of HE-FM-NBA-002, and the Excel, R and Python versions add the probability that net benefit is positive." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for incremental net benefit on the money and health scales from per-arm trial summaries" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Stinnett AA, Mullahy J. Net health benefits: a new framework for the analysis of uncertainty in cost-effectiveness analysis. Medical Decision Making. 1998;18(2 Suppl):S68-S80. Equations 6 to 8, checked in NBER Technical Working Paper 227 (1998). Tambour M, Zethraeus N, Johannesson M. A note on confidence intervals in cost-effectiveness analysis. International Journal of Technology Assessment in Health Care. 1998;14(3):467-471. Abstract, which multiplies effects by the price per unit of effectiveness so that standard statistical techniques give a confidence interval for net benefit in money. https://doi.org/10.1177/0272989X98018002S09" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Covariance of the differences set to zero. At GBP 35,000 per QALY, dropping Cov_EC raises SE_INMB from about GBP 979 to GBP 1,059 and moves the interval to about minus GBP 77 to GBP 4,077, which now includes zero, with the probability falling to about 0.970 (computed here for illustration). Resampling or summarising costs and effects separately loses the within-arm correlation that the trial data carry" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Delta_E = E_1 - E_0; Delta_C = C_1 - C_0; R = Delta_C / Delta_E; V_E = s_E1^2 / n_1 + s_E0^2 / n_0; V_C = s_C1^2 / n_1 + s_C0^2 / n_0; Cov_EC = r_1 * s_E1 * s_C1 / n_1 + r_0 * s_E0 * s_C0 / n_0; INMB = lambda * Delta_E - Delta_C; SE_INMB = sqrt(lambda^2 * V_E + V_C - 2 * lambda * Cov_EC); M_L = INMB - z * SE_INMB; M_U = INMB + z * SE_INMB; INHB = INMB / lambda; SE_INHB = SE_INMB / lambda; H_L = INHB - z * SE_INHB; H_U = INHB + z * SE_INHB; z_NB = INMB / SE_INMB" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-NBA-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-incremental-net-benefit-on-the-money-and-health-scales-from-per-arm-trial-summaries" .

