        hemo:6003612,
        hemo:6003613,
        hemo:6003614 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6003615,
        hemo:6003616,
        hemo:6003617,
        hemo:6003618,
        hemo:6003619 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005761 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007164,
        hemo:7007165,
        hemo:7007166,
        hemo:7007167,
        hemo:7007168,
        hemo:7007169 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the age at death or onset, the years lost or duration, the discount rate, the modulation constant, the age-weight constants and a disability weight, and returns the closed-form age-weighted discounted years (HE-FM-AGW-003, or HE-FM-AGW-002 when the rate is zero), the same quantity from a numerical integral of the weighted, discounted integrand over the span, their difference, the result times the disability weight for a case (HE-FM-AGW-004), and the ratio to the unweighted discounted years of HE-FM-YLL-003. The integral is a Simpson's rule sum over 1,000 panels in Excel and Python and adaptive quadrature in R, so a typing error in the closed form shows as a difference. The inputs therefore differ from the formula's variables." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for age-weighted discounted years lost per death or case with a numerical integral check" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Prüss-Üstün A, Mathers C, Corvalán C, Woodward A. Introduction and methods, assessing the environmental burden of disease at national and local levels. Environmental Burden of Disease Series No. 1. Geneva, World Health Organization, 2003. Section 3.5, pages 32 to 34, for the YLL and YLD formulas with K, C, beta and r. Murray CJ. Quantifying the burden of disease, the technical basis for disability-adjusted life years. Bulletin of the World Health Organization. 1994;72(3) 429-445. Page 441 for the integral from a to a + L and its closed-form solution. Larson BA. Calculating disability-adjusted-life-years lost (DALYs) in discrete-time. Cost Effectiveness and Resource Allocation. 2013;11 article 18. Equation 2 for 5.1836 discounted YLDs in the same case without age weighting." ;
    hemo:9000011 "Integral started at birth or at the reference year. Discounting from age 0 instead of from the age at death or onset shrinks every result by e to the minus ra, the error of HE-ER-AGW-005, and for a death at 40 the integral then returns about 7.0 years instead of 23.22" ;
    hemo:9000014 "s = r + beta; G = K * C * exp(r * a) / s^2 * (exp(-s * (L + a)) * (-s * (L + a) - 1) - exp(-s * a) * (-s * a - 1)) + (1 - K) / r * (1 - exp(-r * L)); G_0 = (1 - exp(-r * L)) / r; Y = DW * G; effect = G / G_0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-AGW-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-age-weighted-discounted-years-lost-per-death-or-case-with-a-numerical-integral-check" .

hemo:5000860 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "Computational function for the stop or continue decision at one interim look of a two-arm trial"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-CF-AVOI-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000002 hemo:5000484,
        hemo:5000636,
