        hemo:6003980,
        hemo:6003981,
        hemo:6003982,
        hemo:6003983,
        hemo:6003984,
        hemo:6003985,
        hemo:6003986,
        hemo:6004892,
        hemo:6004893,
        hemo:6004894 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005771 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007170,
        hemo:7007171,
        hemo:7007172,
        hemo:7007173,
        hemo:7007174 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the design-stage prior for incremental net monetary benefit, the pairs observed and their mean at the interim look, the remaining pairs, the sampling standard deviation per pair, the patients informed and the costs, and returns the interim posterior, the per-patient and population EVSI of the remaining pairs, the offline gain of HE-FM-AVOI-001 with no switching cost, the net gain with the participants' loss and the decision. It chains the normal update of HE-FM-BAD-001 in effective sample size form, the preposterior variance of HE-FM-EVSI-002 with n_t in place of n0, the closed-form EVSI of HE-FM-EVSI-003 at the interim mean, HE-FM-AVOI-001, and HE-FM-ENBS-001 with the cost of HE-FM-ENBS-002 for the remaining pairs (n equal to 2m, a variable cost of c/2 per participant, a share of one half on the arm expected to be inferior and the analysis cost C_a in place of the fixed cost), so its inputs differ from the symbols of any one formula. The calculator takes Q_z from 1-NORM.S.DIST(z,TRUE) because it has no normal distribution function. The Excel, R and Python versions compute it and also scan every remaining size up to the maximum, continuing if any one-stage plan has a positive net gain, the KG* rule of Chick and colleagues." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for the stop or continue decision at one interim look of a two-arm trial" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Chick SE, Forster M, Pertile P. A Bayesian decision theoretic model of sequential experimentation with delayed response. Journal of the Royal Statistical Society Series B. 2017;79(5):1439-1462. Equations 2 and 3 for the interim posterior, equation 6 for the preposterior variance and equations 17 and 18 for the KG* rule. Flight L, Julious S, Brennan A, Todd S. Expected value of sample information to guide the design of group sequential clinical trials. Medical Decision Making. 2022;42(4):461-473. Methods, step 6, stage 5, equation 8 for the cost of sampling with analysis costs and the opportunity cost per participant on n/2 participants, and the discussion on when that cost holds. Fenwick E, Steuten L, Knies S, et al. Value of information analysis for research decisions, an introduction. Report 1 of the ISPOR Value of Information Analysis Emerging Good Practices Task Force. Value in Health. 2020;23(2):139-150. Section on estimating the value of specific research, for the opportunity cost of participants on the technology expected to be inferior. Forster M, Brealey S, Chick S, Keding A, Corbacho B, Alban A, Pertile P, Rangan A. Cost-effective clinical trial design, application of a Bayesian sequential model to the ProFHER pragmatic trial. Clinical Trials. 2021;18(6):647-656. Methods, implementation of the model, for fixed costs committed once the trial was commissioned. https://doi.org/10.1111/rssb.12225" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Interim effective sample size left at the prior value. Keeping n_0 of 25 for the preposterior variance at the favourable interim look prices the remaining 100 pairs at about GBP 12.36 million instead of GBP 3.02 million and the net gain at about GBP 11.94 million instead of GBP 2.60 million, about four times the value of the remaining pairs, because the 100 pairs already observed are ignored (computed here for illustration)",
        "Signed interim mean used for the participants' loss. At a posterior mean of minus GBP 1,500 the signed term adds GBP 150,000 to the gain instead of charging it, giving about minus GBP 227,228 instead of minus GBP 527,228, as if the participants on the new technology gained from it (computed here for illustration)" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_t = n_0 + m_1; mu_t = (n_0 * mu_0 + m_1 * xbar_1) / n_t; sd_t = sigma_X / sqrt(n_t); s_m = sigma_X * sqrt(m / (n_t * (n_t + m))); z = abs(mu_t) / s_m; phi_z = exp(-z * z / 2) / sqrt(2 * 3.14159265); EVSI = s_m * (phi_z - z * Q_z); EVSI_pop = P * EVSI; G_off = EVSI_pop - m * c; NG = EVSI_pop - m * c - C_a - m * abs(mu_t); go = NG > 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-AVOI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-the-stop-or-continue-decision-at-one-interim-look-of-a-two-arm-trial" .

hemo:5000861 a owl:NamedIndividual,
