        hemo:6003993,
        hemo:6003994,
        hemo:6003995,
        hemo:6003996,
        hemo:6003997,
        hemo:6003998 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005780 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007175,
        hemo:7007176,
        hemo:7007177,
        hemo:7007178 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Runs a small seeded agent simulation of one step and checks it against the analytic infection probability HE-FM-ABM-001. It takes a number of susceptible agents, a per-contact transmission probability, the number of infectious contacts per agent under a comparator and under a programme, and a base seed, and returns the simulated and analytic shares infected under each, the Monte Carlo standard error of the simulated share, a pass flag and the simulated infections averted per agent. Each agent i draws one uniform number per contact from its own stream, seeded with seed + i, and is infected when any draw is below p, so the simulation works contact by contact and never uses the formula itself. The programme removes each agent's last contact and keeps the draws for the others, so the two strategies share common random numbers." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function: seeded one-step agent simulation checked against the analytic infection probability" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Britton T. Basic stochastic transmission models and their inference. arXiv preprint 1801.09594, 2018. Section 2.3, which gives the probability of infection as the complement of (1 minus p) raised to the number of infectives when contacts are independent. Chhatwal J, He T. Economic evaluations with agent-based modelling, an introduction. PharmacoEconomics. 2015;33(5):423-433. Section 3.1, which assigns a unique random seed to each agent to implement common random numbers. https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.09594" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Fresh seeds for the programme. Drawing new numbers for the programme leaves the expected share averted at 0.081 but raises the variance of the per-agent difference about 4.7 fold (HE-ER-ABM-003), so for 10,000 agents the standard error of the share averted rises from about 0.0027 to about 0.0059" ;
    hemo:9000014 "P_3 = 1 - (1 - p)^k_3; P_2 = 1 - (1 - p)^k_2; Phat_3 = n_3 / N_agents; Phat_2 = n_2 / N_agents; MCSE_3 = sqrt(P_3 * (1 - P_3) / N_agents); ok = abs(Phat_3 - P_3) <= 3 * MCSE_3; D_hat = Phat_3 - Phat_2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-ABM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-seeded-one-step-agent-simulation-checked-against-the-analytic-infection-probability" .

hemo:5000862 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "Computational function for cycle-by-cycle background death probabilities from an age-banded life table"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-CF-BGM-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000002 hemo:5000216,
        hemo:5000695 ;
    hemo:1000005 hemo:7005792,
        hemo:7005793,
        hemo:7005794 ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6003622,
        hemo:6003623,
        hemo:6003624,
        hemo:6003999,
        hemo:6004000,
        hemo:6004001,
        hemo:6004896,
        hemo:6004897,
        hemo:6004898,
        hemo:6004899,
        hemo:6004900 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6003622,
        hemo:6003623,
        hemo:6003624,
        hemo:6003999,
        hemo:6004000,
        hemo:6004001 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6004896,
        hemo:6004897,
        hemo:6004898,
        hemo:6004899,
        hemo:6004900 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005788 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007179,
        hemo:7007180,
        hemo:7007181,
        hemo:7007182,
        hemo:7007183 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes a starting age, a cycle length, a number of cycles and a life table that gives an annual probability of death for each age band, and returns the background death probability p_bg for every cycle and the share of the cohort still alive when background causes alone act. For each cycle it finds the band that contains the attained age at the start of the cycle, starting age plus elapsed time, and rescales that band's annual probability to the cycle length with HE-FM-TP-003, so the probabilities rise as the cohort moves into older bands. The vector then feeds HE-FM-BGM-002 cycle by cycle. The inputs therefore differ from the formula's variables, which describe a single cycle." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for cycle-by-cycle background death probabilities from an age-banded life table" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Office for National Statistics. National life tables QMI. Last revised 10 December 2025. Section 6, methods used to produce the national life tables data, which defines the mortality rate between age x and x + 1 as the probability that a person aged x exactly will die before reaching age x + 1. Sonnenberg FA, Beck JR. Markov models in medical decision making: a practical guide. Medical Decision Making. 1993;13(4):322-338. Section on time dependence of probabilities (page 333), which stores mortality rates that change with age in a table indexed by cycle number, and section on assignment of probabilities (pages 335 and 336), which looks up the age-specific rate for each cycle and describes the corrections to the lookup age." ;
    hemo:9000011 "Background probability fixed at the starting age. Holding the band of age 63 for all six cycles gives background survival of 0.970299 against 0.964418, so background deaths over three years are 29.7 per 1,000 instead of 35.6, about 17% too few (computed here for illustration). Sonnenberg and Beck note that the probability of death increases as the cohort ages and must change with each cycle" ;
    hemo:9000014 "n_A = (a_edge - a_0) / Delta; n_B = n_cyc - n_A; p_A = 1 - (1 - q_A)^Delta; p_B = 1 - (1 - q_B)^Delta; S_bg = (1 - p_A)^n_A * (1 - p_B)^n_B" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-BGM-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-cycle-by-cycle-background-death-probabilities-from-an-age-banded-life-table" .

hemo:5000863 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "Computational function for R_0 as the spectral radius of a next-generation matrix of any size"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-CF-BRN-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000002 hemo:5000701 ;
    hemo:1000005 hemo:7005802,
