    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005843 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007210,
        hemo:7007211,
        hemo:7007212,
        hemo:7007213 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the household expenditure on each item in the weight reference period b, the form in which the national accounts supply weights, with item prices in period b, in the base period 0 and at time t. It price-updates each expenditure to the base period, turns the updated amounts into weights and averages the price relatives with them, the steps of sections 3.3 and 3.5 of the ONS technical manual. The result equals the basket form of HE-FM-CPI-001 with quantities V_b / p_b, so the inputs differ from the formula's variables, which are quantities." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for a Lowe CPI from weight-reference expenditure with price-updated weights for a three-item basket" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Office for National Statistics. Consumer Prices Indices Technical Manual, 2019. Newport, Office for National Statistics, 2019, page last revised 26 March 2025. Section 3.3, index calculation, for the Laspeyres-type and Lowe-type index and its weighted-average form, and section 3.5, aggregation, which states that the weight for January is calculated by price updating the expenditure V in the weight reference period to the December of the previous year and the weight for February to December by price updating January's weight. https://www.ons.gov.uk/economy/inflationandpriceindices/methodologies/consumerpricesindicestechnicalmanual2019" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Weight reference shares used without price-updating. The manual's Lowe index takes weights from period b and price-updates them to the base period (section 3.3). Using the raw shares 0.5, 0.3 and 0.2 in the first worked example gives 106.5 in place of 106.4593 (computed here for illustration), a gap that depends on how far relative prices moved between period b and the base period" ;
    hemo:9000014 "u_1 = V_1 * p1_0 / p1_b; u_2 = V_2 * p2_0 / p2_b; u_3 = V_3 * p3_0 / p3_b; w_1 = u_1 / (u_1 + u_2 + u_3); w_2 = u_2 / (u_1 + u_2 + u_3); w_3 = u_3 / (u_1 + u_2 + u_3); I_0t = 100 * (w_1 * p1_t / p1_0 + w_2 * p2_t / p2_0 + w_3 * p3_t / p3_0)" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-CPI-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-a-lowe-cpi-from-weight-reference-expenditure-with-price-updated-weights-for-a-three-item-basket" .

