    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005851 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007214,
        hemo:7007215,
        hemo:7007216,
        hemo:7007217 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes twelve monthly index values for each of two financial years, April to March, and returns the two financial-year averages as arithmetic means of the twelve months, their ratio, which is the I_b / I_a input of HE-FM-COST-002, and the average annual rate of HE-FM-CPI-004 between them. Section 11.3 of the ONS technical manual defines the annual average as the arithmetic mean of the 12 monthly values and quarters in the same way; applying it to April to March is the article's step for costs priced in a financial year. The inputs are monthly values, so they differ from the formula's variables, which are two index values." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for monthly D7BT values to financial-year CPI averages, their ratio and the average annual rate" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Office for National Statistics. Consumer Prices Indices Technical Manual, 2019. Newport, Office for National Statistics, 2019, page last revised 26 March 2025. Section 11.3, annual and quarterly averages, which defines the annual average as the arithmetic mean of the 12 monthly values and gives the annual average inflation rate equation. Office for National Statistics. CPI index 00, all items, 2015=100 (series D7BT, dataset MM23), release of 16 September 2026, for the monthly values and the 2019 annual value of 107.8. https://www.ons.gov.uk/economy/inflationandpriceindices/methodologies/consumerpricesindicestechnicalmanual2019" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Calendar-year index paired with a financial-year cost. For a cost priced in 2019/20, the calendar 2019 average of 107.8 in place of 108.2417 raises the ratio to 2023/24 to 1.2215 from 1.2165 (computed here for illustration), about 0.4% more on every uprated cost",
        "Rounded averages re-averaged. Averaging four quarterly averages that were each rounded to one decimal place can move the annual average away from the mean of the twelve months; the manual computes CPI averages at maximum precision from unrounded monthly indices (section 11.3)" ;
    hemo:9000014 "A_1 = (a_01 + a_02 + a_03 + a_04 + a_05 + a_06 + a_07 + a_08 + a_09 + a_10 + a_11 + a_12) / 12; A_2 = (b_01 + b_02 + b_03 + b_04 + b_05 + b_06 + b_07 + b_08 + b_09 + b_10 + b_11 + b_12) / 12; R = A_2 / A_1; n = 12 * Y; g = R^(12 / n) - 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-CPI-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-monthly-d7bt-values-to-financial-year-cpi-averages-their-ratio-and-the-average-annual-rate" .

