        hemo:6005045,
        hemo:6005046,
        hemo:6005047 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6005048,
        hemo:6005049 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005887 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007234,
        hemo:7007235,
        hemo:7007236,
        hemo:7007237,
        hemo:7007238 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes a patient's yearly counts of uses of each service category, the minutes each use takes, a flag for whether round-trip travel is added and an hourly value of time, and returns the annual patient hours and the annual patient time cost, the article's sum over K service types. It follows the service-based method of Yabroff and colleagues, in which the time estimate for a category already contains the waiting time where waiting applies, round-trip travel is added to the services, and each night in hospital counts as 16 waking hours. The inputs therefore differ from the single-type variables of HE-FM-PTC-001." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for annual patient time cost from service counts with the Yabroff time estimates" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Yabroff KR, Guy GP Jr, Ekwueme DU, McNeel T, Rozjabek HM, Dowling E, Li C, Virgo KS. Annual patient time costs associated with medical care among cancer survivors in the United States. Medical Care. 2014;52(7):594-601. Methods, Measures subsection, which measures service frequency for the year in each category, adds travel time to all service time estimates and waiting time to office-based or hospital outpatient visits, chemotherapy and radiation therapy but not to emergency visits, hospitalisations or ambulatory surgery, and multiplies hospital days by 16 hours, an estimate of waking hours; the Analyses subsection, which applies the time estimates for each type of service, summarises patient time and applies the hourly value; Table 1, which gives the minutes per service category including wait time and 35.2 minutes of urban round-trip travel per visit; and Table 4, which reports the sensitivity analysis with 24 hours per hospital day. https://doi.org/10.1097/MLR.0000000000000151" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Waiting added to emergency and hospital time. Yabroff and colleagues timed emergency visits, hospital stays and ambulatory surgery by the interval between arrival or admission and discharge, so waiting is already inside them. Adding the 30.19-minute wait to an urban emergency visit at ages 18 to 64, 203.3 minutes, plus 35.2 minutes of travel raises its time to 268.69 minutes against 238.5, 12.7% too much (computed here for illustration)" ;
    hemo:9000014 "h_T = (n_off * (m_off + m_trav) + n_chemo * (m_chemo + m_trav) + n_stay * m_trav + n_night * m_night) / 60; C_T = w * h_T" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-PTC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-annual-patient-time-cost-from-service-counts-with-the-yabroff-time-estimates" .

