    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes an EQ-5D-5L profile, as a five-digit string such as 23245 or as five level inputs, and a five-level value set given as a constant and a table of 20 decrements, and returns the utility. It applies HE-FM-EQ5L-001 on each dimension and subtracts the five decrements, and the constant where the set has one, from 1, so with the England coefficients it reproduces HE-FM-EQ5L-002. The R and Python versions also score all 3,125 states, which is how the count of states below zero is checked." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for scoring an EQ-5D-5L profile under any 20-decrement value set" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Devlin NJ, Shah KK, Feng Y, Mulhern B, van Hout B. Valuing health-related quality of life: an EQ-5D-5L value set for England. Health Economics. 2018;27(1):7-22. Table 2, which prints the England decrements for levels 2 to 5 of each dimension and works the value of 23245 as 0.247 by subtracting one decrement per dimension from the constant; section 3.4 and Table 3, which give the minimum minus 0.285 and 159 of 3,125 states worse than dead. https://doi.org/10.1002/hec.3564" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Constant row read as a decrement. Table 2 prints a constant of 1.000, the value the decrements are subtracted from. Entering it as c_0 subtracts 1 from every state with any problem, so 23245 scores minus 0.753 instead of 0.247. For England c_0 is 0" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = min(l_MO + l_SC + l_UA + l_PD + l_AD - 5, 1); U = 1 - c_0 * D - (b_MO2 * (min(l_MO - 1, 1) - min(max(l_MO - 2, 0), 1)) + b_MO3 * (min(max(l_MO - 2, 0), 1) - min(max(l_MO - 3, 0), 1)) + b_MO4 * (min(max(l_MO - 3, 0), 1) - max(l_MO - 4, 0)) + b_MO5 * max(l_MO - 4, 0)) - (b_SC2 * (min(l_SC - 1, 1) - min(max(l_SC - 2, 0), 1)) + b_SC3 * (min(max(l_SC - 2, 0), 1) - min(max(l_SC - 3, 0), 1)) + b_SC4 * (min(max(l_SC - 3, 0), 1) - max(l_SC - 4, 0)) + b_SC5 * max(l_SC - 4, 0)) - (b_UA2 * (min(l_UA - 1, 1) - min(max(l_UA - 2, 0), 1)) + b_UA3 * (min(max(l_UA - 2, 0), 1) - min(max(l_UA - 3, 0), 1)) + b_UA4 * (min(max(l_UA - 3, 0), 1) - max(l_UA - 4, 0)) + b_UA5 * max(l_UA - 4, 0)) - (b_PD2 * (min(l_PD - 1, 1) - min(max(l_PD - 2, 0), 1)) + b_PD3 * (min(max(l_PD - 2, 0), 1) - min(max(l_PD - 3, 0), 1)) + b_PD4 * (min(max(l_PD - 3, 0), 1) - max(l_PD - 4, 0)) + b_PD5 * max(l_PD - 4, 0)) - (b_AD2 * (min(l_AD - 1, 1) - min(max(l_AD - 2, 0), 1)) + b_AD3 * (min(max(l_AD - 2, 0), 1) - min(max(l_AD - 3, 0), 1)) + b_AD4 * (min(max(l_AD - 3, 0), 1) - max(l_AD - 4, 0)) + b_AD5 * max(l_AD - 4, 0))" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-EQ5L-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-scoring-an-eq-5d-5l-profile-under-any-20-decrement-value-set" .

hemo:5000875 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "Computational function for the outlay and least-cost inputs that hold the health stock on a target path"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-CF-HPF-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000002 hemo:5000258,
        hemo:5000259,
        hemo:5000735,
