    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005941 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007264,
        hemo:7007265,
        hemo:7007266,
        hemo:7007267 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the national mean unit cost of each case group and, for each provider, its cases and its unit cost in each group, and returns each provider's actual cost, expected cost, crude cost per case, cost index and directly standardised cost per case on the pooled mix of all providers, with the number of provider pairs whose crude ranking the index reverses and the number the direct standardisation reverses. It carries out steps 1 to 4 of the article's worked example. With the weights of HE-FM-CWT-001 the expected cost and index follow HE-FM-CWT-003 multiplied by 100, the direct standardisation is the weighted sum of HE-FM-INEQ-001 with the pooled case shares as the standard, and each pair is classified with the reversal rule of HE-FM-CMAD-001. The calculator line writes out two providers and two groups; the Excel, R and Python code take any number of each, so the inputs differ from the formula's symbols." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function: provider cost indices, direct standardisation check and reversed pairs from group tables" ;
    hemo:9000010 "NHS England and NHS Improvement. User guide: National Cost Collection 2018/19. A guide to using the data. 2020. Chapter 3, Table 9 (p. 23), expected cost as activity multiplied by the national mean unit cost, and Chapter 2, Table 7 (p. 15), the index as actual over expected cost multiplied by 100. Shahian DM, Normand SL. Comparison of \"risk-adjusted\" hospital outcomes. Circulation. 2008;117(15):1955-1963. Abstract, Conclusions, on indirectly standardised outcomes not being used to compare one institution directly with another without reasonable case-mix overlap. https://www.england.nhs.uk/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/National_Cost_Collection_2018-19_A_Guide_to_using_the_data.pdf" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Standardising each provider to its own mix. Weighting each provider's unit costs by its own case shares returns its crude cost per case, 3,360 GBP and 5,890 GBP in the article, so the check repeats the crude comparison it was meant to correct; the standard is the pooled mix, 55% simple and 45% complex" ;
    hemo:9000014 "A_A = n_A1 * u_A1 + n_A2 * u_A2; A_B = n_B1 * u_B1 + n_B2 * u_B2; E_A = n_A1 * cbar_1 + n_A2 * cbar_2; E_B = n_B1 * cbar_1 + n_B2 * cbar_2; crude_A = A_A / (n_A1 + n_A2); crude_B = A_B / (n_B1 + n_B2); I_A = 100 * A_A / E_A; I_B = 100 * A_B / E_B; s_1 = (n_A1 + n_B1) / (n_A1 + n_A2 + n_B1 + n_B2); D_A = s_1 * u_A1 + (1 - s_1) * u_A2; D_B = s_1 * u_B1 + (1 - s_1) * u_B2; rev_I = (crude_A - crude_B) * (I_A - I_B) < 0; rev_D = (crude_A - crude_B) * (D_A - D_B) < 0" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-CMAD-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-provider-cost-indices-direct-standardisation-check-and-reversed-pairs-from-group-tables" .

hemo:5000880 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "Computational function for conditional covariances and the joint negative likelihood ratio of two tests from cross-classified counts"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-CF-NLR-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000002 hemo:5000749 ;
    hemo:1000005 hemo:7005952,
        hemo:7005953,
        hemo:7005954 ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6003639,
        hemo:6003640,
        hemo:6003641,
        hemo:6003642,
        hemo:6003643,
        hemo:6003644,
        hemo:6004091,
        hemo:6004092,
        hemo:6005131,
        hemo:6005132,
        hemo:6005133,
        hemo:6005134,
        hemo:6005135,
        hemo:6005136,
        hemo:6005137,
        hemo:6005138 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6003639,
        hemo:6003640,
        hemo:6003641,
        hemo:6003642,
        hemo:6003643,
        hemo:6003644,
        hemo:6005131,
        hemo:6005132 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6004091,
        hemo:6004092,
        hemo:6005133,
        hemo:6005134,
        hemo:6005135,
        hemo:6005136,
        hemo:6005137,
        hemo:6005138 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005949 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007268,
        hemo:7007269,
        hemo:7007270,
        hemo:7007271 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the counts from a study in which every person had both tests and the reference standard and returns the single-test sensitivities and specificities, the conditional covariances C_pos and C_neg, the joint negative likelihood ratio LR_neg_12 of HE-FM-NLR-002 and the product LR_prod of the single-test ratios for comparison. The inputs are counts, not the formula's accuracy values. With the plug-in covariances the joint ratio equals the observed both-negative proportion among people with the condition divided by that among people without it (derived), so the procedure shows how much of that ratio the independence product misses." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for conditional covariances and the joint negative likelihood ratio of two tests from cross-classified counts" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Wang C, Lin X, Nelson KP. Bayesian hierarchical latent class models for estimating diagnostic accuracy. Statistical Methods in Medical Research. 2020;29(4):1112-1128, section 2.2 (joint probabilities of two tests with conditional covariances). Gardner IA, Stryhn H, Lind P, Collins MT. Preventive Veterinary Medicine. 2000;45(1-2):107-122, abstract (conditional covariances calculated as a measure of dependence between binary tests)." ;
    hemo:9000011 "Independence product used when covariances can be estimated. With the illustrative counts the joint ratio of about 0.0667 leaves a residual risk of about 2.78% at a 30% pre-test probability, above the article's 2.73% threshold, while the product of 0.0125 suggests about 0.53%, well below it" ;
    hemo:9000014 "Se_1 = 1 - x_1D / n_D; Se_2 = 1 - x_2D / n_D; Sp_1 = y_1N / n_N; Sp_2 = y_2N / n_N; C_pos = x_12D / n_D - (1 - Se_1) * (1 - Se_2); C_neg = y_12N / n_N - Sp_1 * Sp_2; LR_neg_12 = ((1 - Se_1) * (1 - Se_2) + C_pos) / (Sp_1 * Sp_2 + C_neg); LR_prod = (1 - Se_1) / Sp_1 * (1 - Se_2) / Sp_2" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-NLR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-conditional-covariances-and-the-joint-negative-likelihood-ratio-of-two-tests-from-cross-classified-counts" .

hemo:5000885 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "MCDA weighted sum of three criterion values"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "Gives the overall value of an option in a multiple criteria decision analysis as the sum of its partial values on each criterion times the criterion weights, which add to 1."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "A HEMO-native record, for a formula the Functions and Formulae module does not yet hold. It is listed in module-backlog.md for the module curator."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Thokala et al. 2016" ;
    dcterms:identifier "HEMO-FM-MCDA-001" ;
