hemo:5000890 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "Cost per DALY averted converted at a market exchange rate"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "Gives a programme's cost per DALY averted in another currency, converting the cost at a market exchange rate and dividing by the DALYs without the programme less the DALYs with it."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "A HEMO-native record, for a formula the Functions and Formulae module does not yet hold. It is listed in module-backlog.md for the module curator."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Murray 1994; Turner et al. 2019" ;
    dcterms:identifier "HEMO-FM-CPDA-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6003685,
        hemo:6003686,
        hemo:6003687,
        hemo:6003688,
        hemo:6003689,
        hemo:6003690,
        hemo:6003691 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6003686,
        hemo:6003687,
        hemo:6003688,
        hemo:6003689 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6003691 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005966 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7006074 ;
    hemo:1000011 hemo:8001272 ;
    hemo:1000018 hemo:8001254,
        hemo:8001260,
        hemo:8001266 ;
    hemo:1000030 hemo:5000645 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000017 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000003 "rheo 0.3.0 cq27-cost-per-daly-averted.rq" ;
    hemo:9000014 "DALY_av = D_0 - D_1; C_x = C * e; c_D = C_x / DALY_av" ;
    hemo:9000015 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><apply><csymbol cd=\"logic1\">and</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>DALY_av</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><ci>D_0</ci><ci>D_1</ci></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>C_x</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><ci>C</ci><ci>e</ci></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>c_D</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">divide</csymbol><ci>C_x</ci><ci>DALY_av</ci></apply></apply></apply></math>" ;
    hemo:9000016 "\\mathrm{DALY}_{\\mathrm{av}} = D_{0} - D_{1} ;\\quad C_{x} = C \\, e ;\\quad c_{D} = \\frac{C_{x}}{\\mathrm{DALY}_{\\mathrm{av}}}" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HEMO-FM-CPDA-001" .

hemo:5000894 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000023 ;
    rdfs:label "Flagship three-state Markov cohort model structure"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "The equations of the three-state Stable, Progressed and Dead cohort model of the Build demonstrator, version 1.1, for one arm. Transition probabilities come from a progression probability, a relative risk of progression and death probabilities. The cohort trace is updated once a cycle, the trapezoidal half-cycle correction gives the occupancy of each cycle, and costs and QALYs are weighted by the cycle length and discounted at the start of each cycle."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "A HEMO-native record, for a formula the Functions and Formulae module does not yet hold. It is listed in module-backlog.md for the module curator."@en,
        "The structure corrects the occupancy of each cycle by the trapezoid rule and discounts each cycle at its start, the Build demonstrator's choices. Mid-cycle discounting is the usual pairing with the trapezoid. A uniform shift of the discount timing scales costs and QALYs alike and leaves the ICER at GBP 29,359.56, while dropping the correction moves it to GBP 31,832.90, as reviewer B recomputed on 19 October 2026. The QALY sum applies the trapezoid to occupancy at constant utility in each state, the form of HE-FM-QALY-001 discounted, not the trapezoid in utility of HE-FM-QALY-002."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Sonnenberg and Beck 1993; Siebert et al. 2012; Naimark et al. 2008; Elbasha and Chhatwal 2016; Drummond et al. 2015" ;
    dcterms:identifier "HEMO-MS-FLAG-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
