    hemo:9000001 rheo:0000028 ;
    hemo:9000002 heto:4200503 ;
    hemo:9000014 "pSP = tpS2P * RR; pSD = tpS2D; pSS = 1 - pSP - pSD; pPD = tpP2D; pPP = 1 - pPD; S_(0) = 1; P_(0) = 0; D_(0) = 0; S_(t+1) = S_(t) * pSS; P_(t+1) = S_(t) * pSP + P_(t) * pPP; D_(t+1) = S_(t) * pSD + P_(t) * pPD + D_(t); mS_(t) = (S_(t) + S_(t+1)) / 2; mP_(t) = (P_(t) + P_(t+1)) / 2; C_tot = sum_(t=0)^(H-1) [(mS_(t) * c_S + mP_(t) * c_P) * L / (1 + disc_c)^(t * L)]; Q_tot = sum_(t=0)^(H-1) [(mS_(t) * u_S + mP_(t) * u_P) * L / (1 + disc_q)^(t * L)]" ;
    hemo:9000015 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><apply><csymbol cd=\"logic1\">and</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>pSP</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><ci>tpS2P</ci><ci>RR</ci></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>pSD</ci><ci>tpS2D</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>pSS</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn><ci>pSP</ci></apply><ci>pSD</ci></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>pPD</ci><ci>tpP2D</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>pPP</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn><ci>pPD</ci></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>S</ci><cn type=\"integer\">0</cn></apply><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>P</ci><cn type=\"integer\">0</cn></apply><cn type=\"integer\">0</cn></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>D</ci><cn type=\"integer\">0</cn></apply><cn type=\"integer\">0</cn></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>S</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><ci>t</ci><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>S</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><ci>pSS</ci></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>P</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><ci>t</ci><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>S</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><ci>pSP</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>P</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><ci>pPP</ci></apply></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>D</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><ci>t</ci><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>S</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><ci>pSD</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>P</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><ci>pPD</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>D</ci><ci>t</ci></apply></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>mS</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">divide</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>S</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>S</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><ci>t</ci><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn></apply></apply></apply><cn type=\"integer\">2</cn></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>mP</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">divide</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>P</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>P</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><ci>t</ci><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn></apply></apply></apply><cn type=\"integer\">2</cn></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>C_tot</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">sum</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"interval1\">integer_interval</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">0</cn><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><ci>H</ci><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn></apply></apply><bind><csymbol cd=\"fns1\">lambda</csymbol><bvar><ci>t</ci></bvar><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">divide</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>mS</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><ci>c_S</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>mP</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><ci>c_P</ci></apply></apply><ci>L</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">power</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn><ci>disc_c</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><ci>t</ci><ci>L</ci></apply></apply></apply></bind></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>Q_tot</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">sum</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"interval1\">integer_interval</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">0</cn><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><ci>H</ci><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn></apply></apply><bind><csymbol cd=\"fns1\">lambda</csymbol><bvar><ci>t</ci></bvar><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">divide</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>mS</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><ci>u_S</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>mP</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><ci>u_P</ci></apply></apply><ci>L</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">power</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn><ci>disc_q</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><ci>t</ci><ci>L</ci></apply></apply></apply></bind></apply></apply></apply></math>" ;
    hemo:9000016 "\\mathrm{pSP} = \\mathrm{tpS2P} \\, \\mathrm{RR} ;\\quad \\mathrm{pSD} = \\mathrm{tpS2D} ;\\quad \\mathrm{pSS} = 1 - \\mathrm{pSP} - \\mathrm{pSD} ;\\quad \\mathrm{pPD} = \\mathrm{tpP2D} ;\\quad \\mathrm{pPP} = 1 - \\mathrm{pPD} ;\\quad S_{0} = 1 ;\\quad P_{0} = 0 ;\\quad D_{0} = 0 ;\\quad S_{t + 1} = S_{t} \\, \\mathrm{pSS} ;\\quad P_{t + 1} = S_{t} \\, \\mathrm{pSP} + P_{t} \\, \\mathrm{pPP} ;\\quad D_{t + 1} = S_{t} \\, \\mathrm{pSD} + P_{t} \\, \\mathrm{pPD} + D_{t} ;\\quad \\mathrm{mS}_{t} = \\frac{S_{t} + S_{t + 1}}{2} ;\\quad \\mathrm{mP}_{t} = \\frac{P_{t} + P_{t + 1}}{2} ;\\quad C_{\\mathrm{tot}} = \\sum_{t=0}^{H - 1} \\left[\\frac{\\left(\\mathrm{mS}_{t} \\, c_{S} + \\mathrm{mP}_{t} \\, c_{P}\\right) \\, L}{\\left(1 + \\mathrm{disc}_{c}\\right)^{t \\, L}}\\right] ;\\quad Q_{\\mathrm{tot}} = \\sum_{t=0}^{H - 1} \\left[\\frac{\\left(\\mathrm{mS}_{t} \\, u_{S} + \\mathrm{mP}_{t} \\, u_{P}\\right) \\, L}{\\left(1 + \\mathrm{disc}_{q}\\right)^{t \\, L}}\\right]" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HEMO-MS-FLAG-001" ;
    hemo:9000026 rheo:0000134 .

hemo:5000909 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "Copas selection parameters and implied unpublished studies from two assumed publication probabilities"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-CF-COPAS-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000002 hemo:5000901,
        hemo:5000902 ;
    hemo:1000005 hemo:7006251,
        hemo:7006252,
        hemo:7006253 ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6004093,
        hemo:6004094,
        hemo:6004095,
        hemo:6004096,
        hemo:6004097,
        hemo:6004098,
        hemo:6005139,
        hemo:6005140,
        hemo:6005141,
        hemo:6005142,
        hemo:6005143 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6004093,
        hemo:6004094,
        hemo:6004095,
        hemo:6004096,
        hemo:6004097,
        hemo:6004098,
        hemo:6005139,
        hemo:6005140 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6005141,
        hemo:6005142,
        hemo:6005143 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7006247 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007272,
        hemo:7007273,
        hemo:7007274,
        hemo:7007275,
        hemo:7007276 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the publication probabilities assumed for studies at two standard errors, the way the article sets each scenario, solves the selection equation of HE-FM-COPAS-001 at both for gamma_1 and gamma_0, and returns them with the implied number of unpublished studies of HE-FM-COPAS-002 for the published studies at those standard errors. With quantiles z_a = Phi^-1(P_a) and z_b = Phi^-1(P_b), gamma_1 = (z_a minus z_b) / (1 / s_a minus 1 / s_b) and gamma_0 = z_b minus gamma_1 / s_b. Huang and colleagues set the selection parameters of their simulation the same way, by solving two publication probability equations for studies of 20 and 500 patients in a selection equation written on the square root of the sample size; the closed form above, for the equation in 1 / s, is derived. The copas function of metasens chooses its grid of gamma_0 and gamma_1 to cover a range of publication probabilities for the study with the largest standard error, and repeating the calculation over pairs of probabilities builds the selection columns of the article's scenario table. The adjusted effect at each pair needs the conditional maximum likelihood fit of the copas software and is not computed here." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function: Copas selection parameters and implied unpublished studies from two assumed publication probabilities" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Huang A, Komukai S, Friede T, Hattori S. Using clinical trial registries to inform Copas selection model for publication bias in meta-analysis. Research Synthesis Methods. 2021;12(5):658-673 (preprint arXiv:2005.14396 full text read; journal abstract read). Preprint section 3.1, on fixing the selection parameters for sensitivity analysis and translating them into the expected number of unpublished studies, and preprint section 4.2, Data generation, which derives (alpha_0, alpha_1) by solving P20 = Phi(alpha_0 + alpha_1 sqrt(20)) and P500 = Phi(alpha_0 + alpha_1 sqrt(500)). Carpenter J, Rücker G, Schwarzer G. copas: an R package for fitting the Copas selection model. The R Journal. 2009;1(2):31-36 (full text read). Equation (4), Pr(Z_i > 0) = Phi(gamma_0 + gamma_1 / s_i), which the two-point solution inverts. Schwarzer G, Carpenter JR, Rücker G. metasens R package version 1.5-3 reference manual, function copas, Details, on the grid of gamma0 and gamma1 values corresponding to a range of publication probabilities for the study with the largest standard error. https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.14396" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Standard errors in place of precisions. Dividing the difference in quantiles by s_a minus s_b, which is -0.30, instead of 1 / s_a minus 1 / s_b, which is 7.5, gives gamma_1 = -6.767 in the moderate scenario, a selection equation in which the most precise studies are the least likely to be published (computed here for illustration)" ;
    hemo:9000014 "gamma_1 = (z_a - z_b) / (1 / s_a - 1 / s_b); gamma_0 = z_b - gamma_1 / s_b; M = n_a * (1 - P_a) / P_a + n_b * (1 - P_b) / P_b" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-COPAS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-copas-selection-parameters-and-implied-unpublished-studies-from-two-assumed-publication-probabilities" .

hemo:5000910 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "HFMA net days in accounts receivable from three monthly net revenues and their calendar days"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-CF-DAR-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000002 hemo:5000905 ;
    hemo:1000005 hemo:7006259,
        hemo:7006260,
        hemo:7006261 ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6004099,
        hemo:6004100,
        hemo:6004101,
        hemo:6004102,
        hemo:6004103,
        hemo:6004104,
        hemo:6004105,
        hemo:6004106,
        hemo:6004107,
        hemo:6005144,
        hemo:6005145 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6004099,
        hemo:6004100,
        hemo:6004101,
        hemo:6004102,
        hemo:6004103,
        hemo:6005144,
        hemo:6005145 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6004104,
        hemo:6004105,
        hemo:6004106,
        hemo:6004107 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7006256 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007277,
        hemo:7007278,
        hemo:7007279,
        hemo:7007280 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the net patient receivables at the end of a quarter, the net patient service revenue of each of its three months and the months themselves, and returns the calendar days of the quarter, its revenue, average daily net revenue and net days in accounts receivable. It counts the actual days of the three months, as HFMA MAP Key FM-1 requires, and then applies HE-FM-DAR-001, so its inputs are monthly ledger figures rather than the single R and D of the formula. The R and Python code take the last month reported and find the month lengths themselves, leap years included." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function: HFMA net days in accounts receivable from three monthly net revenues and their calendar days" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Healthcare Financial Management Association. MAP Keys, industry-standard revenue cycle KPIs. HFMA MAP Initiative web page, accessed 18 October 2026. FM-1, Average Daily Net Patient Service Revenue, the most recent three-month daily average using the number of days in the three months including the last month reported (91 days for the three months ending June 30). https://www.hfma.org/data-and-insights/map-initiative/map-keys/" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Dividing by the days of the last month only. Taking June's revenue of 32.0 over its 30 days as the daily rate gives 51.56 days in place of 55.0, 3.44 days lower, because a rising month is treated as the whole quarter (computed here for illustration)" ;
    hemo:9000014 "D = d_1 + d_2 + d_3; R = R_1 + R_2 + R_3; r_bar = R / D; DAR = AR / r_bar" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-DAR-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-hfma-net-days-in-accounts-receivable-from-three-monthly-net-revenues-and-their-calendar-days" .

hemo:5000911 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "Computational function for HTMT ratios of every construct pair from an indicator correlation matrix"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-CF-DISV-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000002 hemo:5000906 ;
    hemo:1000005 hemo:7006267,
        hemo:7006268,
        hemo:7006269 ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6004108,
        hemo:6004109,
        hemo:6004110,
        hemo:6004111,
        hemo:6004112,
        hemo:6004113,
        hemo:6005146,
        hemo:6005147,
        hemo:6005148,
        hemo:6005149,
        hemo:6005150,
        hemo:6005151,
        hemo:6005152,
        hemo:6005153,
        hemo:6005154 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6004108,
        hemo:6004109,
        hemo:6004110,
        hemo:6005146,
        hemo:6005147,
        hemo:6005148,
        hemo:6005149,
        hemo:6005150,
        hemo:6005151,
        hemo:6005152,
        hemo:6005153 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6004111,
        hemo:6004112,
        hemo:6004113,
        hemo:6005154 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7006264 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007281,
        hemo:7007282,
        hemo:7007283,
        hemo:7007284 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Computes the heterotrait-monotrait ratio of Eq. 6 of Henseler, Ringle and Sarstedt for every pair of constructs from a full indicator correlation matrix with any number of indicators per construct, and flags the pairs above 0.85 and above 0.90. For each pair it divides the mean of the block of correlations between the two constructs' indicators by the geometric mean of the two within-construct means of the off-diagonal correlations; the two-indicator case is HE-FM-DISV-001. The site calculator has no matrices, so the Math / Code line writes the case of three indicators against two term by term, and the loops over pairs are in the Excel, R and Python code. The bootstrap test of the ratio against 1 that the authors also propose needs respondent-level data and is not implemented here." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for HTMT ratios of every construct pair from an indicator correlation matrix" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Henseler J, Ringle CM, Sarstedt M. Journal of the Academy of Marketing Science. 2015;43(1):115-135. Eq. 6 in the section on the heterotrait-monotrait ratio, and the section Empirical example with Table 5, the item correlation matrix of the reduced ACSI model (N = 10,417), Table 6 with the six HTMT values, and the text reporting values between 0.53 for CUEX and PERV and 0.95 for ACSI and PERQ, with two of the six pairs above 0.85 and one above 0.90. https://doi.org/10.1007/s11747-014-0403-8" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Lower triangle only. Published correlation tables such as Table 5 print only the lower triangle. Pasted as it stands, the OFFSET blocks find nothing above the diagonal, so every ratio with StartI below StartJ returns #DIV/0! (0 if the empty cells hold zeros), because AVERAGE has no numbers in the block between the constructs, and every ratio the other way round is exactly doubled, because SUM skips the empty cells and both within-construct means are halved (derived here). For customer expectations and perceived value the result is #DIV/0! (or 0) or 1.0652 against 0.5326 (computed here). Filling the upper triangle by symmetry first avoids it" ;
    hemo:9000014 "rbar_ij = (r_i1j1 + r_i1j2 + r_i2j1 + r_i2j2 + r_i3j1 + r_i3j2) / 6; rbar_ii = (r_i1i2 + r_i1i3 + r_i2i3) / 3; rbar_jj = r_j1j2; HTMT_ij = rbar_ij / sqrt(rbar_ii * rbar_jj)" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-DISV-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-htmt-ratios-of-every-construct-pair-from-an-indicator-correlation-matrix" .

hemo:5000916 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000012 ;
    rdfs:label "Endemic vaccination externality function from coverage at birth to infection risk, benefit split and voluntary uptake"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-FN-VEXT-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6004136,
        hemo:6004137,
        hemo:6004138,
        hemo:6004139,
        hemo:6004140,
        hemo:6004141,
        hemo:6004142,
        hemo:6004143,
        hemo:6004144 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6004136,
        hemo:6004137,
        hemo:6004138,
        hemo:6004139 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6004140,
        hemo:6004141,
        hemo:6004142,
        hemo:6004143,
        hemo:6004144 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Maps the basic reproduction number R_0 of an endemic infection, the share v of each birth cohort vaccinated at birth, the loss L per infection and the private cost c of one vaccination to the lifetime infection risk of an unvaccinated child and the infections per birth (HE-FM-VEXT-001), the private and external benefit of one more vaccination (HE-FM-VEXT-002) and the coverage that voluntary uptake reaches (HE-FM-VEXT-003), all in the long-run steady state of an SIR model with births and deaths. The marginal social benefit as marginal private plus marginal external benefit is HE-FM-EXT-001, the herd immunity threshold H = 1 minus 1/R_0 is HE-FM-BRN-003 and the effective reproduction number is HE-FM-BRN-002, so none of them is restated here; the Pigouvian vaccination subsidy with linear curves is HE-FM-EXT-002, with its bill and net welfare under HE-FN-PIGS-001. The article's social cost per 1,000 births, GBP 250,000 under voluntary uptake, GBP 212,500 under free provision and GBP 200,000 at the threshold, is 1,000 times the expected cost per birth at a chance node, HE-FM-CHN-001, with a vaccinated branch of probability v costing the full resource cost of a vaccination whoever pays it and an unvaccinated branch of probability 1 minus v costing the expected loss L times pi from HE-FM-VEXT-001, so it is not drafted as a formula. The lifetime chance lambda/(lambda + mu) of infection before death is the long-horizon limit of the competing-hazards record HE-FM-TP-004, the final size of a closed epidemic is HE-CF-ATR-001 and vaccine effectiveness from attack rates is HE-FM-ATR-004. Notation follows the Vaccination Externalities article." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Endemic vaccination externality function from coverage at birth to infection risk, benefit split and voluntary uptake" ;
    hemo:9000014 "e(R_0, v, L, c) = (pi, n, MPB, MEB, v_vol)" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-FN-VEXT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "endemic-vaccination-externality-function-from-coverage-at-birth-to-infection-risk-benefit-split-and-voluntary-uptake" .

hemo:5000933 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
