    hemo:1000009 hemo:7006442 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007300,
        hemo:7007301,
        hemo:7007302,
        hemo:7007303 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Compares three policies for a purchaser buying from a supplier whose unit cost is theta_L with probability nu or theta_H otherwise, when both types have an outside option U_0 at least zero. Under complete information each type produces its first-best output and is paid its cost plus U_0. The second-best menu of HE-FM-MECH-002 pays the high-cost type its cost plus U_0 and the low-cost type its cost plus U_0 plus the rent (theta_H minus theta_L) q_H. Shutting out the high-cost type serves only the low-cost type at first-best output with no information rent. The purchaser takes the better of the two incentive-feasible policies, which is (2.32) of Laffont and Martimort, and the gap to the complete-information payoff measures what the hidden cost costs the purchaser (derived). The second-best output does not depend on U_0, so a large outside option makes shut-down optimal even when (2.28) has a positive solution." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for the second-best menu against shut-down and complete information with an outside option" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Laffont JJ, Martimort D. The Theory of Incentives I. The Principal-Agent Model. Authors' manuscript dated 6 February 2001, Toulouse Capitole Publications, record 14941 (full text read); published by Princeton University Press, 2002, doi:10.1515/9781400829453, whose section numbers differ (see HE-SR-MECH-004). Manuscript chapter 2, section 2.7.3 (Shut-Down Policy), (2.30) to (2.32) and the remark on the status quo utility level U_0; section 2.7.1, Proposition 2.1. https://publications.ut-capitole.fr/id/eprint/14941/1/Laffont_14941.pdf" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Outside option ignored. With a zero status quo and a positive solution of (2.28), serving the high-cost type is always better here, because S(q) less S'(q) q equals b q^2 / 2, which is above zero (derived, the argument of the remark in section 2.7.3 of Laffont and Martimort). Leaving U_0 out therefore always keeps the high-cost type in. With U_0 = 200 the menu of HE-EX-MECH-004 leaves the high-cost type 0 and the low-cost type 80 (GBP thousand), both below the outside option, so neither type accepts and nothing is bought (computed here)" ;
    hemo:9000014 "q_L = (a - theta_L) / b; q_FB = (a - theta_H) / b; theta_v = theta_H + nu / (1 - nu) * (theta_H - theta_L); q_SB = max(0, (a - theta_v) / b); S_L = a * q_L - b * q_L^2 / 2; S_FB = a * q_FB - b * q_FB^2 / 2; S_SB = a * q_SB - b * q_SB^2 / 2; V_FB = nu * (S_L - theta_L * q_L - U_0) + (1 - nu) * (S_FB - theta_H * q_FB - U_0); V_SB = nu * (S_L - theta_L * q_L - U_0 - (theta_H - theta_L) * q_SB) + (1 - nu) * (S_SB - theta_H * q_SB - U_0); V_shut = nu * (S_L - theta_L * q_L - U_0); V_star = max(V_SB, V_shut); shut = (V_shut >= V_SB); loss = V_FB - V_star" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-MECH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-the-second-best-menu-against-shut-down-and-complete-information-with-an-outside-option" .

