    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007304,
        hemo:7007305,
        hemo:7007306,
        hemo:7007307 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Lists every equilibrium of a two-player game with two strategies each and values the outcome of mixed play, the procedure Slantchev sets out for finding all Nash equilibria, checking first for pure-strategy solutions and then for mixed ones. The pure cells come from HE-FM-NASH-001 and the completely mixed equilibrium from HE-FM-NASH-002. Under independent mixing each cell's probability is the product of the two players' probabilities, the pathway probability of HE-FM-CHN-002, and the expected payoffs and the expected value of an outcome measure W over the four cells are probability-weighted sums, the form of HE-FM-CHN-001. At the mixed equilibrium each player's expected payoff can be read from its first strategy alone, because both of its strategies pay the same (derived from the indifference condition). The probabilities, payoffs and E_W apply only when interior is 1." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for every equilibrium of a 2 x 2 game with the outcome probabilities and expected welfare of mixed play" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Slantchev BL. Game theory: dominance, Nash equilibrium, symmetry. Lecture notes, Department of Political Science, University of California, San Diego; 23 May 2008 (full text read). Section 2.4.2 (Another Simple Game), the algorithm for finding all Nash equilibria by checking for solutions in pure strategies and then in mixed strategies; section 2.3.1 (Battle of the Sexes), the outcome probabilities as products of the equilibrium probabilities and each player's expected payoff of 2/3; section 2.4, Remark 4, a player's payoff to a mixed profile as the probability-weighted average of its payoffs to its pure strategies. https://slantchev.ucsd.edu/courses/gt/04-strategic-form.pdf" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Equal weights on the four cells. Averaging the cell values as if each outcome were equally likely gives (7 + 14 + 14 + 0) / 4 = 8.75 for the angioplasty game in place of 9.3333 (computed here), and reports a value that no equilibrium produces" ;
    hemo:9000014 "NE_11 = (u_11 >= u_21) and (v_11 >= v_12); NE_12 = (u_12 >= u_22) and (v_12 >= v_11); NE_21 = (u_21 >= u_11) and (v_21 >= v_22); NE_22 = (u_22 >= u_12) and (v_22 >= v_21); a_1 = u_11 - u_21; a_2 = u_22 - u_12; q_star = a_2 / (a_1 + a_2); b_1 = v_11 - v_12; b_2 = v_22 - v_21; p_star = b_2 / (b_1 + b_2); interior = (q_star > 0) and (q_star < 1) and (p_star > 0) and (p_star < 1); P_11 = p_star * q_star; P_12 = p_star * (1 - q_star); P_21 = (1 - p_star) * q_star; P_22 = (1 - p_star) * (1 - q_star); U_A = q_star * u_11 + (1 - q_star) * u_12; U_B = p_star * v_11 + (1 - p_star) * v_21; E_W = P_11 * W_11 + P_12 * W_12 + P_21 * W_21 + P_22 * W_22" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-NASH-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-every-equilibrium-of-a-2-x-2-game-with-the-outcome-probabilities-and-expected-welfare-of-mixed-play" .

