        hemo:6005493 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7006612 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007308,
        hemo:7007309,
        hemo:7007310,
        hemo:7007311 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Runs one tender under both pricing rules and checks the closed forms of HE-FM-AUCT-001 and HE-FM-AUCT-002 by simulating many tenders with a fixed seed. In one tender the second-price rule pays the winner the second-lowest cost, since every supplier bids its cost, and the first-price rule pays the lowest equilibrium bid. The lowest of the bids is the min form used for observed prices in HE-FM-BOC-003, and the scalar line writes the second-lowest of three costs as the median of three. The simulation draws N uniform costs per tender, sorts them, and averages the lowest cost, the second-lowest cost and the winning first-price bid, which converge to E_c1, E_p and E_b." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for one tender under both pricing rules and a seeded check of the uniform-cost closed forms" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Klemperer P. Auction theory: a guide to the literature. Author's copy dated May 1999, posted on the author's Nuffield College page (full text read), which states that it is published in Journal of Economic Surveys 1999;13(3):227-286, doi:10.1111/1467-6419.00083 (journal version not seen; page numbers below are the author's copy's). Appendix D, page 57, for the expected order statistics and the bids; Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences. Improvements to auction theory and inventions of new auction formats. Scientific background on the Sveriges Riksbank Prize in Economic Sciences in Memory of Alfred Nobel 2020. 12 October 2020 (full text read). Section 2.2 (Private Values) for the second-price and first-price rules. https://www.nuff.ox.ac.uk/users/klemperer/survey.pdf" ;
    hemo:9000011 "fresh random draws in the check. Using live RAND() in the draw table changes the simulated means at every recalculation, and with a 4 standard error band a correct sheet then fails about 6 times in 100,000 recalculations (normal approximation, derived), so the table is pasted as values or the seed is fixed in R and Python" ;
    hemo:9000014 "b_1 = c_1 + (c_high - c_1) / N; b_2 = c_2 + (c_high - c_2) / N; b_3 = c_3 + (c_high - c_3) / N; p_FP = min(min(b_1, b_2), b_3); p_SP = max(min(c_1, c_2), min(max(c_1, c_2), c_3)); d = p_FP - p_SP" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-AUCT-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-one-tender-under-both-pricing-rules-and-a-seeded-check-of-the-uniform-cost-closed-forms" .

