        hemo:6005516 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7006620 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007312,
        hemo:7007313,
        hemo:7007314,
        hemo:7007315 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the GPs or other capacity of any number of provider locations, the populations of any number of residential locations, the matrix of travel times between them and a threshold, and returns each provider's supply ratio, each location's 2SFCA score, the population-weighted mean of the scores and their population-weighted variance, scaled to a stated number of people. It applies HE-FM-ACCS-001 to every provider and location at once, with SUMPRODUCT over a travel-time block in Excel and matrix operations in R, so its inputs are a matrix and two lists rather than the formula's named scalars. The mean is the check that the scores conserve total supply, and the variance, the population-weighted second moment that HE-VR-HINQ-007 takes over ranks, here taken over scores, is Wang 2012's equation 4, the inequality objective of Wang and Tang, divided by the total population (derived). The calculator line repeats the chain for the article's two practices and three neighbourhoods and adds the mean and variance; any other size is in the Excel, R and Python code." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for two-step floating catchment area scores, mean and spread for any number of sites" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Luo W, Wang F. Measures of spatial accessibility to healthcare in a GIS environment: synthesis and a case study in Chicago region. Environment and Planning B: Planning and Design. 2003;30(6):865-884. Author manuscript read (HHS Author Manuscripts, PMC8238135); the published version, doi 10.1068/b29120, not seen. Section The Evolvement of Floating Catchment Area Methods, equations (3) and (4), and section The Gravity-Based Method and a Synthesis on the population-weighted average. Wang F. Measurement, optimization, and impact of health care accessibility: a methodological review. Annals of the Association of American Geographers. 2012;102(5):1104-1112. Author manuscript read (NIHPA Author Manuscripts, PMC3547595); the published version, doi 10.1080/00045608.2012.657146, not seen. Section Optimization Models in Health Care Accessibility, the weighted mean property and equation (4), the Wang and Tang objective of minimising the population-weighted sum of squared gaps between each score and the ratio of total supply to total demand. https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8238135/" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Provider location with nobody in reach. A provider whose catchment is empty gives a zero denominator; without the IF guard Excel returns #DIV/0! in RatioRow, and SUMPRODUCT then returns #DIV/0! for every location, including those that cannot reach that provider",
        "Unweighted mean of the scores. The simple mean of the article's three scores is 2.803 per 10,000 against the population-weighted 3.333 (computed here), so the supply check fails and a neighbourhood of 6,000 people counts as much as one of 20,000" ;
    hemo:9000014 "R_X = S_X / ((d_1X <= d_0) * P_1 + (d_2X <= d_0) * P_2 + (d_3X <= d_0) * P_3); R_Y = S_Y / ((d_1Y <= d_0) * P_1 + (d_2Y <= d_0) * P_2 + (d_3Y <= d_0) * P_3); A_1 = (d_1X <= d_0) * R_X + (d_1Y <= d_0) * R_Y; A_2 = (d_2X <= d_0) * R_X + (d_2Y <= d_0) * R_Y; A_3 = (d_3X <= d_0) * R_X + (d_3Y <= d_0) * R_Y; M = k * (P_1 * A_1 + P_2 * A_2 + P_3 * A_3) / (P_1 + P_2 + P_3); V = (P_1 * (k * A_1 - M)^2 + P_2 * (k * A_2 - M)^2 + P_3 * (k * A_3 - M)^2) / (P_1 + P_2 + P_3)" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-ACCS-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-two-step-floating-catchment-area-scores-mean-and-spread-for-any-number-of-sites" .

