        hemo:6005538 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7006628 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007316,
        hemo:7007317,
        hemo:7007318,
        hemo:7007319 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000018 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the capacities of any number of provider locations, the populations of any number of residential locations, the matrix of travel times between them and a friction coefficient, and returns each provider's demand potential, each location's gravity score and the population-weighted mean and variance of the scores, scaled to a stated number of people. It applies HE-FM-ACCS-002 to every provider and location at once, so its inputs are a matrix and two lists rather than the formula's named scalars; the mean and variance are as in HE-CF-ACCS-001. The calculator line repeats the chain for the article's two practices and three neighbourhoods; any other size is in the Excel, R and Python code." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for gravity accessibility scores, mean and spread for any number of sites" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Luo W, Wang F. Measures of spatial accessibility to healthcare in a GIS environment: synthesis and a case study in Chicago region. Environment and Planning B: Planning and Design. 2003;30(6):865-884. Author manuscript read (HHS Author Manuscripts, PMC8238135); the published version, doi 10.1068/b29120, not seen. Section The Gravity-Based Method and a Synthesis, equation (6). Wang F. Measurement, optimization, and impact of health care accessibility: a methodological review. Annals of the Association of American Geographers. 2012;102(5):1104-1112. Author manuscript read (NIHPA Author Manuscripts, PMC3547595); the published version, doi 10.1080/00045608.2012.657146, not seen. Section Health Care Accessibility Measures Synthesized, equation (1). https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8238135/" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Friction coefficient entered with its sign. Typing minus 1 for beta raises travel time to a positive power, so farther practices count more; for the article's inputs C, the neighbourhood farthest from the larger practice, then scores highest at 5.281 per 10,000 (computed here)" ;
    hemo:9000014 "V_X = P_1 * d_1X^(-beta) + P_2 * d_2X^(-beta) + P_3 * d_3X^(-beta); V_Y = P_1 * d_1Y^(-beta) + P_2 * d_2Y^(-beta) + P_3 * d_3Y^(-beta); A_1 = S_X * d_1X^(-beta) / V_X + S_Y * d_1Y^(-beta) / V_Y; A_2 = S_X * d_2X^(-beta) / V_X + S_Y * d_2Y^(-beta) / V_Y; A_3 = S_X * d_3X^(-beta) / V_X + S_Y * d_3Y^(-beta) / V_Y; M = k * (P_1 * A_1 + P_2 * A_2 + P_3 * A_3) / (P_1 + P_2 + P_3); V = (P_1 * (k * A_1 - M)^2 + P_2 * (k * A_2 - M)^2 + P_3 * (k * A_3 - M)^2) / (P_1 + P_2 + P_3)" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-ACCS-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-gravity-accessibility-scores-mean-and-spread-for-any-number-of-sites" .

