        hemo:7003781 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7003783,
        hemo:7003784,
        hemo:7003785,
        hemo:7003796,
        hemo:7003807,
        hemo:7003818,
        hemo:7003829 ;
    hemo:1000011 hemo:8000835 ;
    hemo:1000018 hemo:8000813 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000017 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000001 heao:0000003,
        heao:0000055,
        oheo:0000105 ;
    hemo:9000004 "HEMO-HOOK-03" ;
    hemo:9000008 "Subtracts from full health a constant for any problem at all, the decrement attached to the level reported on each of the five dimensions and a single N3 decrement when any dimension is at level 3. The decrements are zero at level 1, so state 11111 scores 1, and the constant and N3 term are each charged once whatever the number of dimensions with problems. Any value set of this form can be scored by entering its own coefficients, and HE-FM-EQ3L-002 fixes them at the UK tariff." ;
    hemo:9000009 "EQ-5D-3L utility as one minus a constant, level decrements and an N3 term" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Dolan P, Gudex C, Kind P, Williams A. A social tariff for EuroQol. Results from a UK general population survey. Centre for Health Economics Discussion Paper 138. York, University of York, 1995. Pages 10 and 11, which report that none of the models with interactions between dimensions improved the model significantly and many introduced inconsistencies, that without the N3 intercept for any dimension at level 3 the model underestimated less severe and overestimated more severe states, and that TTO scores are explained by an intercept for any move away from full health, two variables for each dimension and N3. Scanned text, read from the page images. https://www.york.ac.uk/media/che/documents/papers/discussionpapers/CHE%20Discussion%20Paper%20138.pdf",
        "Dolan P. Modeling valuations for EuroQol health states. Medical Care. 1997;35(11):1095-1108. Abstract, which reports that valuations of 42 states elicited by time trade-off from a representative UK sample were modelled in terms of the level of severity on each dimension, an intercept for any move away from full health and a term for whether any dimension is at its most severe level, to interpolate values for all 243 states. https://doi.org/10.1097/00005650-199711000-00002",
        "Janssen B, Szende A, Ramos-Goñi JM. Data and methods. In Szende A, Janssen B, Cabases J, editors. Self-reported population health. An international perspective based on EQ-5D. Dordrecht, Springer, 2014, chapter 2. Table 2.2, which gives the time trade-off value set coefficients of 13 countries as a constant, dummies for level 2 and level 3 on each dimension and N3, defined as 1 if any dimension is at level 3, and shows the US set of Shaw 2005 with D1 and count terms in place of the constant and N3. Open access. https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-007-7596-1_2" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Charging the EQ-5D-3L N3 decrement once for each dimension at level 3. N3 is a single indicator. Subtracting the illustrative 0.27 for both level 3 dimensions of 31131 gives minus 0.30 instead of minus 0.03, and under the UK tariff charging it five times for 33333 gives minus 1.670 instead of minus 0.594, so the most severe states are understated.",
        "Reading the minus 0.594 floor as a property of the EQ-5D-3L instrument. The lowest value belongs to the value set and not to the questionnaire. Scoring 33333 with the Dutch time trade-off coefficients of Lamers and colleagues 2006 tabulated in the EuroQol reference volume gives minus 0.329, against minus 0.594 with the UK tariff, so a negative mean utility partly reflects the set used." ;
    hemo:9000014 "U = 1 - alpha * D - (beta_MO + beta_SC + beta_UA + beta_PD + beta_AD) - gamma * N_3" ;
    hemo:9000015 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>U</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><ci>alpha</ci><ci>D</ci></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><ci>beta_MO</ci><ci>beta_SC</ci><ci>beta_UA</ci><ci>beta_PD</ci><ci>beta_AD</ci></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><ci>gamma</ci><ci>N_3</ci></apply></apply></apply></math>" ;
    hemo:9000016 "U = 1 - \\alpha \\, D - \\left(\\beta_{\\mathrm{MO}} + \\beta_{\\mathrm{SC}} + \\beta_{\\mathrm{UA}} + \\beta_{\\mathrm{PD}} + \\beta_{\\mathrm{AD}}\\right) - \\gamma \\, N_{3}" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-FM-EQ3L-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "eq-5d-3l-utility-as-one-minus-a-constant-level-decrements-and-an-n3-term" .

hemo:5000837 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000013 ;
    rdfs:label "Computational function for discounted QALYs and cost per QALY of a one-off treatment under a chosen timing convention"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "The timing convention is the named input s, 0 for end-of-year and 1 for start-of-year counting (decision on timing). Years are counted as periods of one year, so q is the QALY gain of each year and T the number of years."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "the Source rows of the Functions and Formulae module record HE-CF-DISC-001" ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-CF-DISC-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000002 hemo:5000618,
        hemo:5000619,
        hemo:5000621 ;
    hemo:1000005 hemo:7005572,
        hemo:7005573,
        hemo:7005574 ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6003513,
        hemo:6003514,
        hemo:6003515,
        hemo:6003516,
        hemo:6003517,
        hemo:6003518,
        hemo:6003519,
        hemo:6003520,
        hemo:6003521,
        hemo:6003736,
        hemo:6003737 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6003513,
        hemo:6003514,
        hemo:6003515,
        hemo:6003516,
        hemo:6003517 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6003518,
        hemo:6003519,
        hemo:6003520,
        hemo:6003521,
        hemo:6003737 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7005531 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7007018,
        hemo:7007029,
        hemo:7007040,
        hemo:7007051,
        hemo:7007062,
        hemo:7007063 ;
    hemo:1000011 hemo:8001055 ;
    hemo:1000018 hemo:8001013,
        hemo:8001027,
        hemo:8001033,
        hemo:8001039,
        hemo:8001047 ;
    hemo:1000034 hemo:4000012,
        hemo:4000013 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000017 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000002 heto:4201002 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Takes the inputs a one-off treatment analysis usually holds, an incremental cost paid at the start, a yearly QALY gain, the number of years it lasts, an annual rate and a flag for counting each year at its start or its end, and returns the sum of the discount factors, the discounted QALYs, the discounted and undiscounted cost per QALY and the rise caused by discounting. It builds one factor for each year, so it also works at a zero rate where the closed form fails, and chains HE-FM-DISC-001 or HE-FM-DISC-002 with HE-FM-DISC-004. The inputs therefore differ from the formulas' variables, which assume one timing convention and a positive rate." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Computational function for discounted QALYs and cost per QALY of a one-off treatment under a chosen timing convention" ;
    hemo:9000010 "National Institute for Health and Care Excellence. NICE technology appraisal and highly specialised technologies guidance, the manual (PMG36). Chapter 4, economic evaluation. Published 31 January 2022, last updated 13 October 2026. Section 4.5.1 on the present value of the stream of costs and benefits over the time horizon at 3.5% a year, and section 4.5.3 on the 1.5% non-reference-case rate. Larson BA. Calculating disability-adjusted-life-years lost (DALYs) in discrete-time. Cost Effectiveness and Resource Allocation. 2013;11 article 18. Table 1, which counts each year at the beginning of the year, the same as a stream of payments made at the start of each year. https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Discounting the year 0 cost. Dividing the GBP 300,000 paid at the start by 1.035 lowers the ratio at 3.5% to about GBP 19,700 instead of GBP 20,389. An amount paid in year 0 has a factor of 1, so the timing flag applies to the QALY stream only" ;
    hemo:9000014 "A = sum_(t=1)^T [(1 + r)^(-(t - s))]; Q_d = q * A; ICER_d = C_0 / Q_d; ICER_0 = C_0 / (q * T); rise = ICER_d / ICER_0 - 1" ;
    hemo:9000015 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><apply><csymbol cd=\"logic1\">and</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>A</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">sum</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"interval1\">integer_interval</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn><ci>T</ci></apply><bind><csymbol cd=\"fns1\">lambda</csymbol><bvar><ci>t</ci></bvar><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">power</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn><ci>r</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">unary_minus</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><ci>t</ci><ci>s</ci></apply></apply></apply></bind></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>Q_d</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><ci>q</ci><ci>A</ci></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>ICER_d</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">divide</csymbol><ci>C_0</ci><ci>Q_d</ci></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>ICER_0</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">divide</csymbol><ci>C_0</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><ci>q</ci><ci>T</ci></apply></apply></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>rise</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">divide</csymbol><ci>ICER_d</ci><ci>ICER_0</ci></apply><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn></apply></apply></apply></math>" ;
    hemo:9000016 "A = \\sum_{t=1}^{T} \\left[\\left(1 + r\\right)^{-\\left(t - s\\right)}\\right] ;\\quad Q_{d} = q \\, A ;\\quad \\mathrm{ICER}_{d} = \\frac{C_{0}}{Q_{d}} ;\\quad \\mathrm{ICER}_{0} = \\frac{C_{0}}{q \\, T} ;\\quad \\mathrm{rise} = \\frac{\\mathrm{ICER}_{d}}{\\mathrm{ICER}_{0}} - 1" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-CF-DISC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "computational-function-for-discounted-qalys-and-cost-per-qaly-of-a-one-off-treatment-under-a-chosen-timing-convention" .

hemo:6000544 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000018 ;
    rdfs:label "Annual discount rate"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000013 hemo:4000121 ;
    hemo:1000014 hemo:4000093 ;
    hemo:1000016 hemo:4000001 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Annual discount rate expressed as a decimal." ;
