hemo:5000190 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "Total present value of a stream"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "The year index runs from 0, so the first amount is not discounted, the convention RHEO 0.4.0, OHEO 0.3.0 and the HEAO worked examples use."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "the Source rows of the Functions and Formulae module record HE-FM-DR-002" ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-FM-DR-002" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000001 hemo:5000010 ;
    hemo:1000005 hemo:7000125 ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6000546,
        hemo:6000547,
        hemo:6000548,
        hemo:6000549,
        hemo:6000550 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6000547,
        hemo:6000548,
        hemo:6000550 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6000546 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7000123,
        hemo:7000124 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7000126,
        hemo:7000127,
        hemo:7000128 ;
    hemo:1000011 hemo:8000051 ;
    hemo:1000018 hemo:8000036 ;
    hemo:1000030 hemo:5000189 ;
    hemo:1000034 hemo:4000013 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000017 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000001 heao:0000010,
        rheo:0000152 ;
    hemo:9000002 heto:4201002 ;
    hemo:9000004 "HEMO-HOOK-06" ;
    hemo:9000008 "Sums discounted values occurring across the selected time horizon." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Total present value of a stream" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Sanders GD, Neumann PJ, Basu A, Brock DW, Feeny D, Krahn M, et al. Recommendations for conduct, methodological practices, and reporting of cost-effectiveness analyses: Second Panel on Cost-Effectiveness in Health and Medicine. JAMA. 2016;316(10):1093-1103. https://doi.org/10.1001/jama.2016.12195" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Treating Excel NPV as beginning at time zero. Including a time-zero value inside the NPV range discounts it by one period and shifts every cash flow's timing." ;
    hemo:9000014 "PV_total = sum_(t=0)^T [V_t/(1+r)^t]" ;
    hemo:9000015 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>PV_total</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">sum</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"interval1\">integer_interval</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">0</cn><ci>T</ci></apply><bind><csymbol cd=\"fns1\">lambda</csymbol><bvar><ci>t</ci></bvar><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">divide</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"hemo1\" cdbase=\"https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/cd\">element</csymbol><ci>V_t</ci><ci>t</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">power</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn><ci>r</ci></apply><ci>t</ci></apply></apply></bind></apply></apply></math>" ;
    hemo:9000016 "\\mathrm{PV}_{\\mathrm{total}} = \\sum_{t=0}^{T} \\left[\\frac{V_{t}_{t}}{\\left(1 + r\\right)^{t}}\\right]" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-FM-DR-002" ;
    hemo:9000023 "total-present-value-of-a-stream" .

hemo:5000618 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        hemo:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "Discounted total of a level yearly amount counted at the end of each year"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "the Source rows of the Functions and Formulae module record HE-FM-DISC-001" ;
    dcterms:identifier "HE-FM-DISC-001" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/hemo/hemo-formulae.owl> ;
    hemo:1000001 hemo:5000133 ;
    hemo:1000005 hemo:7003424 ;
    hemo:1000006 hemo:6002621,
        hemo:6002622,
        hemo:6002623,
        hemo:6002624 ;
    hemo:1000007 hemo:6002622,
        hemo:6002623,
        hemo:6002624 ;
    hemo:1000008 hemo:6002621 ;
    hemo:1000009 hemo:7003421,
        hemo:7003422,
        hemo:7003423 ;
    hemo:1000010 hemo:7003425,
        hemo:7003426,
        hemo:7003427,
        hemo:7003432,
        hemo:7005994 ;
    hemo:1000011 hemo:8000567 ;
    hemo:1000018 hemo:8000552 ;
    hemo:1000029 hemo:5000620 ;
    hemo:1000030 hemo:5000190 ;
    hemo:1000034 hemo:4000012 ;
    hemo:1000035 hemo:4000017 ;
    hemo:2000019 true ;
    hemo:9000001 heao:0000027 ;
    hemo:9000002 heto:4201002 ;
    hemo:9000008 "Gives the present value of the same amount q in each of T years when each year's amount is counted at the end of that year, so the first year carries the factor 1/(1 + r) and the last 1/(1 + r)^T. The fraction (1 minus (1 + r) to the power minus T) divided by r is the sum of the T yearly discount factors, the annuity form in the article's worked example. It tends to T as r falls towards zero, where the closed form itself cannot be evaluated." ;
    hemo:9000009 "Discounted total of a level yearly amount counted at the end of each year" ;
    hemo:9000010 "Attema AE, Brouwer WBF, Claxton K. Discounting in economic evaluations. PharmacoEconomics. 2018;36(7) 745-758. Section on discount models, which describes the constant discounting model as the one most often used by social planners, with costs or utilities in each period multiplied by the discount factor 1/(1 + D)^t of that period. https://doi.org/10.1007/s40273-018-0672-z",
        "National Institute for Health and Care Excellence. NICE technology appraisal and highly specialised technologies guidance, the manual (PMG36). Chapter 4, economic evaluation. Published 31 January 2022, last updated 13 October 2026. Section 4.5.1, results reflect the present value of the stream of costs and benefits over the time horizon, with costs and health effects discounted at the same rate of 3.5% a year. https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation" ;
    hemo:9000011 "Inflation added to the discount rate for a real cost stream. Discounting real costs of GBP 1,000 a year for 30 years at 5.5%, the 3.5% rate plus 2% inflation, gives about GBP 14,534 instead of GBP 18,392 at 3.5% (computed here for illustration). The Green Book states that the two rates should not be added together.",
        "Year 0 included in an end-of-year discounted stream. Running the year index from 0 to 30 adds a 31st year. For 0.8 QALYs at 3.5% the total becomes about 15.51 instead of 14.71 discounted QALYs (computed here for illustration). A stream of T years counted at the end runs from year 1 to year T.",
        "Zero rate entered in the closed-form discounted annuity. The closed form divides by r, so a rate of zero returns #DIV/0! in Excel instead of the undiscounted total q times T. An undiscounted result, which PMG36 asks for in its disaggregated table and the Dutch guideline as a scenario, uses q times T, the factor-by-factor sum or Excel PV, which accepts a zero rate." ;
    hemo:9000014 "Q = q * (1 - (1 + r)^(-T)) / r" ;
    hemo:9000015 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><apply><csymbol cd=\"relation1\">eq</csymbol><ci>Q</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">divide</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">times</csymbol><ci>q</ci><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">minus</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">power</csymbol><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">plus</csymbol><cn type=\"integer\">1</cn><ci>r</ci></apply><apply><csymbol cd=\"arith1\">unary_minus</csymbol><ci>T</ci></apply></apply></apply></apply><ci>r</ci></apply></apply></math>" ;
    hemo:9000016 "Q = \\frac{q \\, \\left(1 - \\left(1 + r\\right)^{-T}\\right)}{r}" ;
    hemo:9000018 "HE-FM-DISC-001" ;
    hemo:9000023 "discounted-total-of-a-level-yearly-amount-counted-at-the-end-of-each-year" .

